   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_27_7_10","title":"Echoes of the Forgotten City","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Underground Worlds","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Sam, Lily, and Alex stood at the edge of a dark tunnel. They had just discovered the entrance to the forgotten city. The air felt cool, and strange sounds echoed from deep inside.\n\n\u201cThis is it! This is where the map leads!\u201d Sam exclaimed, his eyes wide with excitement.\n\n\u201cAre we really going to go in there?\u201d Alex asked, peering into the tunnel. \u201cIt looks a bit spooky.\u201d\n\n\u201cSpooky? More like mysterious!\u201d Lily said, adjusting her backpack. \u201cPlus, I have my tablet. I can use it to help us navigate.\u201d\n\nAs they stepped inside, the light from Lily's tablet lit up the walls. The walls were covered in strange symbols. Sam traced one with his finger. \u201cWhat do you think these mean?\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe they\u2019re clues!\u201d Lily suggested. \u201cWe should look for more.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud noise behind them. \u201cHey! Wait up!\u201d shouted a voice. It was Gerald, the rival treasure hunter! He was catching up fast.\n\n\u201cQuick! We have to solve these riddles before he finds the artifact!\u201d Sam urged, his heart racing.\n\nThey moved deeper into the city, the sounds of their footsteps echoing. The tunnel opened into a large chamber filled with crumbling buildings. Vines draped over the stone like green curtains. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cThis place is amazing!\u201d Alex said, looking around. \u201cBut where do we start?\u201d\n\nLily scanned the room with her tablet. \u201cLook! There\u2019s a stone pedestal over there. It might have something important on it.\u201d\n\nAs they approached the pedestal, they saw a large stone tablet. It was covered in more symbols. \u201cThese look like the ones from the tunnel!\u201d Sam pointed out.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see if we can figure it out!\u201d Lily said excitedly, pulling out her notebook. They worked together, trying to decode the symbols.\n\nBut just then, Gerald barged into the chamber. \u201cLooks like I found you!\u201d he sneered. \u201cAnd I\u2019m going to take that artifact first!\u201d\n\n\u201cWe won\u2019t let you!\u201d Sam shouted bravely. \n\nThe tension filled the air as they faced Gerald. The race for the artifact was on!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWe need to work quickly!\u201d Lily whispered. \u201cHe\u2019s not going to wait for us.\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s solve this riddle!\u201d Alex said firmly. \u201cWe can beat him!\u201d\n\nWith a newfound determination, the trio leaned over the stone tablet, ready to decipher the secrets of the forgotten city.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam, Lily, and Alex find at the entrance?","options":["A treasure chest","A dark tunnel","A giant door","A hidden cave"],"correct_answer":"A dark tunnel"},{"question":"What does Lily use to help navigate?","options":["A flashlight","A map","A tablet","A compass"],"correct_answer":"A tablet"},{"question":"Who is the rival treasure hunter?","options":["Alex","Sam","Gerald","Lily"],"correct_answer":"Gerald"},{"question":"What do they find on the stone pedestal?","options":["A magical artifact","A stone tablet","A treasure map","A key"],"correct_answer":"A stone tablet"},{"question":"What do they need to do before Gerald finds the artifact?","options":["Run away","Solve the riddle","Climb a tower","Eat a snack"],"correct_answer":"Solve the riddle"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_27_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_27_ch2_img1.png","plot_27_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":393,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
