   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_27_7_10","title":"Echoes of the Forgotten City","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Underground Worlds","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Chapter 4: The Riddle of the Shadows\n\nThe underground city felt alive. Sam, Lily, and Alex stood in awe. Bright green vines hung from the crumbling stone walls. Soft echoes whispered secrets around them. \n\n\"Can you believe this place?\" Sam said, his eyes sparkling. \n\n\"It\u2019s amazing!\" Lily replied, adjusting her glasses. \"Look at those symbols! They might be clues!\"\n\nThey gathered around a large stone pillar covered in strange drawings. Each symbol looked like a shadow dancing. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see if we can figure this out,\u201d Alex said, pointing to a symbol that looked like a key. \"Maybe it unlocks something!\"\n\nLily pulled out her notebook. \"Okay! The riddle we solved led us here. We need to solve another one to find the artifact!\"\n\nSuddenly, they heard footsteps behind them. It was Gerald, the rival treasure hunter! He smirked and said, \u201cI\u2019m here for the artifact, and I\u2019ll get it first!\u201d\n\n\u201cNot if we can help it!\u201d Sam shouted back, feeling brave. \n\nGerald\u2019s eyes narrowed. \u201cYou kids can\u2019t outsmart me!\u201d\n\nThe trio huddled together. \u201cWe need to focus,\u201d Lily whispered. \u201cLet\u2019s solve the riddle before he can catch us!\u201d\n\nThey examined the symbols closely. Sam traced his finger over the key symbol. \u201cWhat if it means we have to find something that opens a door?\u201d\n\n\u201cOr a treasure chest!\u201d Alex added with excitement.\n\nLily flipped through her notebook. \u201cLook! There\u2019s a drawing of a door and a riddle underneath. It says, \u2018To find the treasure that you seek, unlock the path where shadows speak.\u2019\u201d\n\n\u201cShadows speak?\u201d Sam repeated. \u201cWhat does that mean?\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe we have to speak to the shadows!\u201d Alex exclaimed. \n\nSuddenly, they noticed the sun\u2019s light shining through a crack above, casting shadows on the wall. \u201cLook!\u201d Lily said. \u201cThe shadows are moving!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s follow them!\u201d Sam suggested.\n\nAs they moved closer to the dancing shadows, they felt a spark of hope. They were on the right path!\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed. Gerald had knocked over a stone! \u201cYou won\u2019t win!\u201d he yelled, scrambling to get back up. \n\nThe trio shared worried glances. \u201cWe have to hurry!\u201d Sam said.\n\nWith determination, they followed the shadows deeper into the city. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWait!\u201d Lily cried. \u201cThe shadows lead to that wall! Maybe there\u2019s a hidden door!\u201d\n\nExcited, they reached the wall. Sam found a small stone that looked different. \u201cShould I push it?\u201d\n\n\u201cYes!\u201d both Alex and Lily urged.\n\nWith a firm push, the stone clicked, and a door creaked open. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Sam shouted, leading the way into the unknown. \n\nWhat did they find behind the door? \n\nAs they stepped inside, a bright light filled the room. The echoes of the past welcomed them. \n\nCould this be the treasure they were looking for?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do the kids discover in the underground city?","options":["A hidden door","A treasure chest","A map","A monster"],"correct_answer":"A hidden door"},{"question":"Who is the rival treasure hunter?","options":["Alex","Sam","Lily","Gerald"],"correct_answer":"Gerald"},{"question":"What does the riddle they find mention?","options":["Shadows","Treasure chests","Monsters","Magic"],"correct_answer":"Shadows"},{"question":"What do the shadows lead the trio to?","options":["A treasure map","A hidden door","A giant monster","The exit"],"correct_answer":"A hidden door"},{"question":"How do Sam, Lily, and Alex feel about their discovery?","options":["Scared","Excited","Bored","Confused"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_27_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_27_ch4_img1.png","plot_27_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":469,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
