   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_27_11_14","title":"Echoes of the Forgotten City","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Underground Worlds","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Sam had always been the kind of kid who found adventure in the most unexpected places. Today, as he rummaged through the dusty attic of their old house, he stumbled upon a wooden trunk. Its aged surface was adorned with intricate carvings that looked like tangled vines and strange symbols. He wiped off the dust and pried it open, revealing a collection of yellowed papers, old toys, and\u2014most importantly\u2014a crumpled map.\n\n\"Hey, Sam! What did you find?\" called Lily, his twelve-year-old sister, who was busy tinkering with a disassembled gadget at the far end of the attic.\n\n\"Check this out!\" Sam shouted, holding the map up triumphantly. The faded lines twisted and turned, leading to a spot marked with an ominous 'X.' Curiosity sparked in his hazel eyes. \"It looks like a treasure map!\"\n\nLily abandoned her project and rushed over, her dark hair bouncing with excitement. \"Let me see! What does it say?\"\n\nAs she studied the map, Sam felt a thrill of anticipation. He could already picture the adventure ahead. The map hinted at a city long forgotten, buried deep underground. \"It says something about the Echoes of the Forgotten City. We have to check it out!\"\n\nJust then, Alex, their cousin and the bravest of their trio, burst through the attic door, breathless and ready for action. \"What\u2019s going on? I heard treasure!\"\n\nSam grinned and waved the map. \"We found a way to an ancient city! It could be full of secrets and artifacts! But we have to hurry. Someone else might be looking for this too.\"\n\nAlex raised an eyebrow, his adventurous spirit igniting. \"You mean like treasure hunters? This is going to be epic!\"\n\nLily squinted at the map, tracing its path with her finger. \"We\u2019ll need to gather supplies. We can\u2019t just rush in blindly.\"\n\nAs they descended the attic stairs, Sam felt a mix of excitement and nervousness. What if they weren\u2019t the only ones seeking the treasure? The whispers of the past echoed in his mind, filling him with both dread and determination.\n\nOnce they were outside, the sun warmed their faces as they gathered their gear. Sam could hardly believe they were about to embark on a journey that could change their lives forever. His heart raced as they made their way to the nearby woods, each step echoing with the promise of adventure.\n\nSuddenly, a rustle in the bushes caught their attention. Sam and Lily exchanged worried glances, while Alex stepped forward, eyeing the sound with a mix of curiosity and caution. \"What was that?\" he asked, his voice low.\n\nBefore they could react, a shadow darted between the trees. It was quick and silent, like a whisper of wind. Sam's heart pounded. \"Do you think it\u2019s another treasure hunter?\"\n\nLily pulled out her tablet, tapping at the screen. \"We should record this! If there's someone else out there, we need to know who they are.\"\n\nAs they moved deeper into the woods, following the winding path depicted on the map, the air grew thick with tension. Sam couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that they were being watched. The thrill of discovery mixed with the fear of danger\u2014a perfect recipe for adventure.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nJust as they reached a clearing, Sam caught sight of a crumbling stone wall, partially hidden beneath vines and moss. The air around it felt electric, as if the very stones held memories of an ancient world. His pulse quickened. \"This has to be it! The entrance to the city!\"\n\nLily raised her tablet, capturing the moment. \"This is incredible! But we need to figure out how to get inside before anyone else finds it.\"\n\nBefore Sam could respond, a loud crack echoed through the clearing, causing them all to jump. The ground trembled slightly beneath their feet. \"What was that?\" Alex whispered, glancing nervously behind them.\n\n\"Only one way to find out,\" Sam replied, determination igniting within him. They had come too far to turn back now.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they approached the stone wall, the shadows around them deepened, and with it came the realization that the adventure had only just begun.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam, Lily, and Alex find in the attic?","options":["An old toy","A treasure map","A dusty book","A photograph"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"What is the name of the city mentioned in the map?","options":["The Lost City","Echoes of the Forgotten City","Ancient Ruins","Buried Secrets"],"correct_answer":"Echoes of the Forgotten City"},{"question":"How does Sam feel about their adventure?","options":["Bored","Scared","Excited and nervous","Confused"],"correct_answer":"Excited and nervous"},{"question":"What mysterious event occurs as they approach the stone wall?","options":["A bird flies away","The ground trembles","A fog rolls in","A lightning bolt strikes"],"correct_answer":"The ground trembles"},{"question":"Who is the bravest member of the trio?","options":["Sam","Lily","Alex","None of them"],"correct_answer":"Alex"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_27_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_27_ch1_img1.png","plot_27_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":698,"reading_level":"Builder"}
