   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_27_11_14","title":"Echoes of the Forgotten City","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Underground Worlds","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As Sam, Lily, and Alex ventured deeper into the dark woods, the trees loomed above them like ancient guardians, their gnarled branches twisted and tangled. Sam held the map tightly, its edges frayed and yellowed with age. \"This way,\" he said, pointing toward a cluster of rocks that looked like they might hide a secret entrance.\n\nLily whipped out her tablet, the screen glowing faintly against the encroaching dusk. \"I can use the GPS to track our location,\" she said, her fingers dancing over the screen. \"It should help us find the entrance to the city.\"\n\nAlex peered over her shoulder, his excitement palpable. \"What if we find treasure? Or ancient artifacts? Maybe we\u2019ll solve the mystery of the city!\" His blue eyes sparkled with the thrill of adventure.\n\nSuddenly, a rustle in the underbrush stopped them in their tracks. Sam glanced at his sister and cousin, his heart pounding like a drum. \"Did you hear that?\"\n\nLily nodded, lowering her tablet. \"It could be an animal, but\u2026\"\n\nBefore she could finish, the rustling grew louder, and a shadow darted between the trees. Sam felt a chill race down his spine. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s that treasure hunter?\u201d he whispered, recalling the strange man he had glimpsed in town. They had to move quickly.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s hurry,\u201d Alex urged, taking the lead. They pressed on, urgency fueling their steps until they finally reached the rocky entrance. It was partially hidden by thick vines, creating a natural curtain that seemed to guard the forgotten city. \n\nSam pushed aside the foliage, revealing a dark tunnel that beckoned them forward. \u201cThis is it,\u201d he breathed, the air cool and damp against his skin. He could almost hear the echoes of history whispering from within.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWith a shared glance of determination, they stepped inside. The tunnel opened to a vast underground chamber, illuminated only by the light of their flashlights. Crumbling buildings encircled them, draped in vibrant green vines that hung like curtains of emerald. Strange symbols adorned the walls, and the air was thick with the scent of earth and mystery.\n\n\u201cWhat do you think those symbols mean?\u201d Lily asked, her curiosity piqued. She shone her light on one of the markings, a swirling pattern that seemed to pulse with energy.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Sam replied, tracing the air above it with his fingers. \u201cBut I feel like they\u2019re important. We should take pictures of everything.\u201d\n\nAs they explored the chamber, a sudden noise echoed from the tunnel behind them, sending a wave of panic through Sam's chest. Footsteps\u2014heavy and purposeful\u2014were approaching. They had to act fast.\n\n\u201cHide!\u201d Alex hissed, yanking Sam and Lily behind a crumbling wall just as a figure appeared in the entrance. The shadowy outline of a man loomed large, his face obscured by a wide-brimmed hat. Sam's breath hitched in his throat as he recognized the rival treasure hunter from town.\n\n\u201cWhat does he want?\u201d Sam whispered, his heart racing. \n\nThe man stepped further into the chamber, pulling out a flashlight that sliced through the darkness. \u201cI know you\u2019re here,\u201d he called, his voice low and menacing. \u201cI can hear you.\u201d\n\nLily shivered, gripping Sam\u2019s arm tightly. \u201cHe\u2019s looking for the artifact! We need to find it first,\u201d she whispered urgently.\n\nJust then, the ground trembled beneath them, and dust cascaded from the ceiling like a warning. Sam\u2019s mind raced\u2014this was no longer just a treasure hunt; they were in a race against time, and the stakes had never been higher.\n\n\u201cOn three, we run for it!\u201d Alex whispered, his eyes fierce with determination. \u201cOne\u2026 two\u2026\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey burst from their hiding spot, sprinting past the startled treasure hunter as the walls shuddered. The echoes of the forgotten city seemed to scream in protest, urging them forward into the unknown.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam, Lily, and Alex discover at the beginning of Chapter 2?","options":["A treasure chest","An ancient map","A hidden tunnel","A rival treasure hunter"],"correct_answer":"A hidden tunnel"},{"question":"What symbolizes the urgency of their situation?","options":["The symbols on the walls","The rustling in the bushes","The dark tunnel","The crumbling buildings"],"correct_answer":"The rustling in the bushes"},{"question":"How does Lily plan to assist the team as they explore?","options":["By leading them with a map","By using her tablet for GPS","By taking pictures","By reading the symbols"],"correct_answer":"By using her tablet for GPS"},{"question":"What does the rival treasure hunter want?","options":["To help them","To find the artifact","To read the symbols","To scare them away"],"correct_answer":"To find the artifact"},{"question":"What happens as the characters are hiding?","options":["They discover treasure","The ground trembles","They find a way out","They fall asleep"],"correct_answer":"The ground trembles"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_27_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_27_ch2_img1.png","plot_27_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":645,"reading_level":"Builder"}
