   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_27_11_14","title":"Echoes of the Forgotten City","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Underground Worlds","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the flickering light from their flashlights cut through the thick darkness, Sam, Lily, and Alex stepped into the heart of the forgotten city. The air was cool and filled with the scent of damp earth and ancient stone. Towering structures loomed above them, their surfaces covered in a tapestry of green vines and colorful moss, as if nature were reclaiming what once belonged to it. Each step echoed eerily, as if the city itself were whispering secrets long buried in time.\n\n\u201cWow,\u201d Alex breathed, eyes wide with wonder. \u201cThis is amazing!\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, like something out of a movie,\u201d Lily agreed, her fingers tapping furiously on her tablet as she scanned for any signals or clues. \u201cIf only we could find a signal down here.\u201d\n\nSam ran his fingers along a crumbling wall, tracing the strange symbols etched into the stone. \u201cThese must be the markings from the map. It feels like we're walking through history.\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from deeper within the city, making them all jump. Sam\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d\n\n\u201cProbably just the wind. Or maybe\u2026,\u201d Alex started, but he was interrupted by the sudden sound of footsteps approaching swiftly. The trio exchanged worried glances. They weren\u2019t alone.\n\nLily quickly hid behind a broken pillar, her eyes darting nervously as she whispered, \u201cWhat if it\u2019s the rival treasure hunter?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe can\u2019t let him find the artifact before we do,\u201d Sam said, determination lighting his features. \u201cWe have to move\u2014now!\u201d\n\nAs they crept forward, the sound of footsteps grew louder, echoing ominously in the cavernous space. The trio rounded a corner, and there it was\u2014a massive archway leading into an even darker area of the city, the entrance adorned with the same mysterious symbols they had seen earlier.\n\n\u201cDo you think this is where the artifact is?\u201d Alex asked, his voice barely a whisper.\n\n\u201cIt must be,\u201d Sam replied, squinting into the shadows. Just then, a figure stepped into the light\u2014a tall man with a dark coat and a menacing grin. It was Victor, the rival treasure hunter they had heard about.\n\n\u201cWell, well, what do we have here?\u201d he said, his voice low and mocking. \u201cA little scavenger hunt? I\u2019ve been waiting for you, kids.\u201d\n\nPanic surged through Sam. \u201cRun!\u201d he shouted, and they dashed toward the archway, adrenaline fueling their movements.\n\nThey slipped inside just as Victor lunged forward, his hand outstretched. The darkness engulfed them, and they found themselves in a narrow tunnel, the walls damp and glistening.\n\n\u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d Lily gasped, her breath coming in quick bursts.\n\n\u201cWe have to find a way to outsmart him,\u201d Sam said, his mind racing. \u201cIf we can reach the artifact first, we can protect it from him.\u201d\n\nBut as they pressed deeper into the tunnel, whispers echoed around them, growing louder and more urgent. The walls seemed to pulse, and Sam felt a strange sensation, as if the city itself were alive and aware of their presence. \n\n\u201cDo you hear that?\u201d Alex said, his eyes wide with fear. \u201cIt\u2019s like\u2026 someone is guiding us.\u201d\n\n\u201cThe echoes of the past,\u201d Sam whispered, a chill running down his spine. \u201cWe have to listen closely. They might be trying to tell us something important.\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud clang resonated behind them, and the entrance to the tunnel began to close. \u201cWe don\u2019t have much time!\u201d Lily shouted, shoving her tablet into her backpack.\n\nAs they pressed on, their hearts pounded in unison, fueled by the urgency of their quest. They had a choice to make: follow the mysterious whispers or risk facing Victor again. \n\nWhich way would they choose? The echoes of the city seemed to beckon them forward, but they knew danger lurked just behind.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam, Lily, and Alex find in the underground city?","options":["A treasure chest","A lost artifact","An ancient map","A treasure hunter"],"correct_answer":"A lost artifact"},{"question":"Who do the children encounter in the city?","options":["A friendly explorer","A lost traveler","Victor, the rival treasure hunter","An ancient spirit"],"correct_answer":"Victor, the rival treasure hunter"},{"question":"What does Sam feel when he hears the echoes in the city?","options":["Curiosity","Fear","Excitement","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Curiosity"},{"question":"What important decision do the children face at the end of the chapter?","options":["To climb out of the city","To follow the whispers or face Victor","To split up","To call for help"],"correct_answer":"To follow the whispers or face Victor"},{"question":"How does the city react as they explore deeper?","options":["It becomes brighter","It feels alive and aware","It collapses","It remains silent"],"correct_answer":"It feels alive and aware"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_27_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_27_ch3_img1.png","plot_27_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":638,"reading_level":"Builder"}
