   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_29_11_14","title":"The Forgotten Train of Wonderland","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Underground Worlds","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the train rumbled through the dark tunnel, Ella and Max exchanged nervous glances. The air in the carriage crackled with excitement, but there was also an undercurrent of uncertainty. Max leaned forward, his brow furrowed. \u201cDo you think the conductor will explain how we\u2019re supposed to get home?\u201d \n\nElla, her eyes sparkling with wonder, shrugged. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s like a fairy tale! We just have to follow the signs.\u201d Just then, the train screeched to a halt, sending a jolt through their seats. A sign above the door lit up, shimmering with gold letters that read \u201cMystical Marshlands.\u201d \n\n\u201cLooks like this is our stop!\u201d Ella exclaimed, her heart racing. She could already envision shimmering waters and glowing creatures. But Max hesitated, gripping the edge of his seat. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s dangerous? We don\u2019t know anything about this place.\u201d\n\nWith a deep breath, Ella stood up. \u201cWe can handle it together, like we always do.\u201d She stepped toward the door, which opened with a soft hiss, revealing a misty, enchanting landscape. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe moment they set foot outside, the siblings were enveloped in a vibrant world. Lush green plants with bioluminescent petals swayed gently in the breeze. A chorus of strange creatures sang from the shadows, their voices like tinkling bells. \n\n\u201cWow,\u201d Max breathed, taking in the beauty around them. \u201cThis is incredible.\u201d \n\nBut just as they took their first steps into the Marshlands, a loud croaking echoed through the air. A giant, green frog-like creature appeared, blocking their path. Its bulging eyes glimmered with mischief. \u201cTo pass through my domain, you must answer my riddle!\u201d it croaked, a toothy grin spreading across its face. \n\nElla\u2019s heart raced as she exchanged worried looks with Max. \u201cWhat if we can\u2019t solve it?\u201d she whispered. \n\n\u201cStay calm,\u201d Max replied, determination flickering in his eyes. \u201cWe\u2019ll figure it out.\u201d \n\nThe frog cleared its throat dramatically. \u201cWhat has keys but can\u2019t open locks?\u201d \n\nElla\u2019s mind raced like a whirlwind. \u201cA piano!\u201d she shouted, her voice echoing in the still air. But the frog shook its head, still grinning. \n\n\u201cNo, no! Think deeper!\u201d It shifted its weight, making the ground tremble beneath them. \n\nMax bit his lip, his mind whirring. \u201cWait! A map has keys!\u201d he exclaimed, recalling how they had once used a treasure map that had key symbols. \n\nThe frog\u2019s grin faltered. \u201cCorrect! You may pass!\u201d it croaked, stepping aside with a flourish. \n\nAs they continued deeper into the Marshlands, Ella felt a blend of relief and anxiety. \u201cWhat if there\u2019s more to come?\u201d \n\n\u201cThen we solve it together,\u201d Max said, a fierce determination lighting his eyes. \u201cNo matter what.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, Ella's foot slipped on the slick green ground, and she tumbled forward, nearly losing her balance. For a split second, her heart raced in panic. Just as she steadied herself, a soft glow began to flicker in the distance, illuminating a path that wound through the marsh. \u201cLook!\u201d she exclaimed, pointing ahead. \n\nBut just as they approached the glowing path, the ground trembled again, and a loud roar echoed through the Marshlands. The siblings froze, their hearts pounding. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Max whispered, fear creeping into his voice. \n\nElla\u2019s eyes widened as a shadow loomed over them from the trees. Just then, the conductor\u2019s voice echoed in their minds, \u201cRemember, challenges are the key to your growth!\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep moving!\u201d Ella urged, grabbing Max\u2019s hand. They sprinted toward the glowing path, not knowing what lay ahead.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the first challenge Ella and Max face in the Marshlands?","options":["A riddle from a giant frog","A maze of glowing plants","A race against time","A battle with a dragon"],"correct_answer":"A riddle from a giant frog"},{"question":"What does Max suggest they do when faced with the frog's riddle?","options":["Give up","Think deeper","Run away","Ask for help"],"correct_answer":"Think deeper"},{"question":"What key does Max suggest in response to the riddle?","options":["A treasure chest","A piano","A map","A door"],"correct_answer":"A map"},{"question":"What does Ella feel after solving the riddle?","options":["Relief and anxiety","Anger and frustration","Happiness and joy","Boredom"],"correct_answer":"Relief and anxiety"},{"question":"What threatens Ella and Max as they move deeper into the Marshlands?","options":["A giant wave","A mysterious roar","A flood","A storm"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious roar"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_29_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_29_ch2_img1.png","plot_29_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":591,"reading_level":"Builder"}
