   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_29_11_14","title":"The Forgotten Train of Wonderland","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Underground Worlds","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The air inside the Enchanted Forest was thick with tension as Ella and Max stood frozen, the walls of vines and branches inching closer around them. The Keeper of the Forest, a tall figure cloaked in emerald green, watched them with a knowing smile. \u201cTo escape, you must answer my riddle,\u201d he intoned, his voice echoing like wind through the trees. \n\nMax glanced at Ella, her wide eyes reflecting both fear and determination. \u201cWhat if we can\u2019t figure it out in time?\u201d he whispered. Ella took a deep breath, trying to quell the fluttering in her stomach. \u201cWe have to try, Max. We can\u2019t give up!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, the Keeper raised his hands, and the walls halted, frozen in place. \u201cThe riddle is simple. What has roots as nobody sees, is taller than trees, up, up it goes, and yet never grows?\u201d The words hung in the air like a spell, and Ella\u2019s heart raced. She had read about riddles in books, but this one felt different\u2014there was an urgency to it. \n\n\u201cThink, Ella!\u201d Max urged. Ella\u2019s imagination raced as she pictured tall mountains and deep valleys. \u201cIt\u2019s not something we can see right away,\u201d she murmured, \u201cbut it\u2019s still there...\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s a mountain?\u201d Max suggested, his brow furrowed as he wrestled with the answer.\n\n\u201cYes! A mountain!\u201d Ella exclaimed. \u201cThey have roots in the ground, and they\u2019re taller than trees.\u201d The Keeper nodded, but his smile remained enigmatic. \n\n\u201cCorrect, young adventurers,\u201d he said, his voice now softer. \u201cBut remember, you have a task to complete. The train is not just a ride; it holds secrets.\u201d With a wave of his hand, the walls receded, revealing a shimmering pathway leading them onward. \n\nAs they stepped through, the forest transformed into a dazzling landscape filled with floating lanterns illuminating colors they had never seen before. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] The shimmering lights danced above a river that sparkled like diamonds, and the air was filled with a sweet scent of blooming flowers. Ella and Max exchanged glances, hearts pounding with hope. \n\n\u201cDo you think we can find a way back home?\u201d Max asked, his voice barely above a whisper.\n\nElla nodded, her imagination ignited by the beauty surrounding them. \u201cIf we keep solving the riddles and working together, we can do it!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a loud crack echoed through the air, and the ground trembled beneath their feet. The siblings stumbled, clutching each other\u2019s hands as a figure appeared from the shadows. It was the train conductor, his wide-brimmed hat obscuring his face. \u201cAh, you\u2019ve come this far, but the journey is not yet over!\u201d he boomed, his voice booming like thunder. \n\n\u201cWhat do you want from us?\u201d Max demanded, trying to sound brave despite his racing heart.\n\n\u201cI want to see if you are truly worthy of the train\u2019s magic,\u201d the conductor replied, his eyes glinting with mischief. \u201cSolve my next riddle, and I will guide you home. Fail, and the magic will fade, taking you with it.\u201d\n\nElla felt a wave of determination wash over her. \u201cWe can do this together!\u201d she said, squeezing Max\u2019s hand tighter. \u201cWhat\u2019s the riddle?\u201d\n\n\u201cHere it is,\u201d the conductor said, his voice dripping with amusement. \u201cI speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with the wind. What am I?\u201d \n\nAs the conductor\u2019s words hung like a cloud of mystery, Ella closed her eyes, envisioning the train, the adventures, and the promise of returning home. They had come so far, and she wasn\u2019t about to give up now. \n\n\u201cMax, think!\u201d she urged, her heart pounding as they faced this new challenge together. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] The tension mounted as the seconds ticked away, the conductor watching them with an eager grin. Would they find the answer in time? \n\n\u201cAn echo!\u201d Max shouted suddenly, his face lighting up with realization. \n\nThe conductor\u2019s grin widened. \u201cCorrect! But remember, the train will soon vanish into the fog if you do not hurry.\u201d \n\nTogether, with renewed hope, Ella and Max prepared to board the train once more, ready to unravel the next mystery that awaited them.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does the Keeper of the Forest ask Ella and Max to do?","options":["Solve a riddle","Find a treasure","Escape a trap","Help a creature"],"correct_answer":"Solve a riddle"},{"question":"What is the answer to the first riddle posed by the Keeper?","options":["A tree","A mountain","A river","An echo"],"correct_answer":"A mountain"},{"question":"What magical landscape do Ella and Max enter after escaping the forest?","options":["A snowy village","A desert oasis","A flower-filled riverbank","A dark cave"],"correct_answer":"A flower-filled riverbank"},{"question":"What does the conductor demand from Ella and Max in order to guide them home?","options":["A treasure","Another riddle","Their friendship","A magical artifact"],"correct_answer":"Another riddle"},{"question":"What is the riddle presented by the conductor?","options":["What has roots nobody sees?","I speak without a mouth?","What flies without wings?","What is always coming but never arrives?"],"correct_answer":"I speak without a mouth?"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_29_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_29_ch4_img1.png","plot_29_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":700,"reading_level":"Builder"}
