   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_21_11_14","title":"The Starlit Path","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Quest or Journey","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Mira stood at the edge of the Whispering Woods, her heart racing with excitement and fear. The ancient trees loomed above her like guardians of a forgotten secret. Sunlight filtered through the leaves, casting dappled shadows on the ground, while Jasper sniffed the air, his tail wagging like a fluffy metronome. She glanced down at the map clutched in her hands, its edges worn and frayed, as if it had waited centuries for her touch.\n\n\u201cAre you ready for this, buddy?\u201d she asked, looking at Jasper, whose big brown eyes sparkled with enthusiasm. He barked happily, and Mira felt a surge of courage. Together, they would reclaim the lost stars.\n\nAs they ventured deeper into the woods, the atmosphere shifted. The rustling leaves whispered secrets, and the air grew cooler. Mira traced her finger over the map, which glimmered faintly in the shade. \u201cThe first star,\u201d she murmured, squinting at the runic symbols. \u201cIt\u2019s near the Old Oak.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a shadow darted across her path, and a familiar voice called out behind her. \u201cWell, well, if it isn\u2019t Mira and her mutt!\u201d Zane stepped out from behind a tree, a cocky grin on his face. \u201cI hope you\u2019re not thinking you can solve those riddles before me.\u201d\n\nMira clenched her fists, anger bubbling beneath her skin. \u201cThis isn\u2019t a game, Zane. Those stars belong to our village!\u201d\n\n\u201cOh, I\u2019m well aware. But I\u2019m going to be the one who finds them first,\u201d he taunted, his eyes glinting like shards of ice. \u201cI\u2019ll take that map off your hands, and all the glory will be mine.\u201d\n\nBefore she could respond, Zane lunged forward, trying to snatch the map from her grip. Mira instinctively pulled back, but in the struggle, the map slipped from her fingers and fluttered to the ground. Zane scooped it up with a triumphant laugh. \u201cToo easy!\u201d \n\nPanic surged through Mira. \u201cGive it back!\u201d she shouted, reaching out. Jasper barked, his playful demeanor shifting to protectiveness. With a sudden burst of speed, he dashed toward Zane, barking loudly. Zane stumbled back, surprised.\n\n\u201cGet him, Jasper!\u201d Mira yelled, determination flooding her veins. Jasper leaped, his paws landing right at Zane\u2019s feet. The map slipped from Zane\u2019s grasp, landing face-up on the forest floor, revealing a new riddle that had appeared as he dropped it.\n\nMira gasped, reading the riddle aloud: \u201cTo find the first star, you must seek the tree, where sun meets shadow, and roots hold the key.\u201d \n\nThe air felt electric with tension, and Zane\u2019s cocky expression faltered. \u201cYou\u2019re lucky this time, but I won\u2019t let you win again.\u201d With a last glare, he spun on his heel and dashed into the woods.\n\nMira\u2019s heart pounded as she bent to pick up the map, her mind racing with the riddle\u2019s meaning. \u201cJasper, we have to find that Old Oak! It\u2019s our only chance!\u201d \n\nThey turned towards the direction of the Old Oak, but doubt gnawed at her insides. Could she solve the riddle in time? What if Zane came back?\n\nJasper trotted beside her, his presence a steady reminder of friendship and loyalty. \u201cOkay, boy. Let\u2019s do this together,\u201d she whispered, determination igniting within her.\n\nAs they ventured deeper into the woods, the trees twisted into strange shapes, and the paths narrowed. Mira could almost hear the stars whispering to her, urging her forward. \n\nBut as they approached an ancient clearing, Mira\u2019s breath hitched. There, looming before them, was the Old Oak, its gnarled roots sprawling like fingers reaching into the earth. The sunlight broke through the thick canopy above, bathing the tree in a warm glow.\n\n\u201cHere it is!\u201d Mira exclaimed, excitement bubbling up. But as she stepped forward, she felt a chill, her instincts warning her that this was only the beginning of their adventure.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMira stood before the massive Old Oak, its thick trunk twisted and its roots sprawling across the ground. Sunlight filters through the leaves, illuminating her excited and determined expression as Jasper playfully sniffs around the base of the tree.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nZane is caught off guard as Jasper lunges towards him, barking fiercely. The map slips from Zane's grasp, fluttering to the ground. The tension in the scene is palpable, with Mira looking fiercely determined while Zane wears a surprised expression.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mira discover about the map in this chapter?","options":["It has new riddles","It is a fake","It leads to a treasure chest","It is cursed"],"correct_answer":"It has new riddles"},{"question":"What does Zane attempt to do during their encounter?","options":["Help Mira solve the riddle","Steal the map","Hide from Mira","Join Mira and Jasper"],"correct_answer":"Steal the map"},{"question":"How does Mira feel about Zane's challenge?","options":["Excited","Scared","Angry","Indifferent"],"correct_answer":"Angry"},{"question":"What does Jasper do when Zane tries to take the map?","options":["Runs away","Barks and lunges","Sits quietly","Lies down"],"correct_answer":"Barks and lunges"},{"question":"What is the first riddle about?","options":["Finding a treasure chest","The Old Oak tree","A hidden cave","Shooting stars"],"correct_answer":"The Old Oak tree"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_21_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_21_ch2_img1.png","plot_21_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":730,"reading_level":"Builder"}
