   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_21_11_14","title":"The Starlit Path","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Quest or Journey","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Mira stood at the foot of the Old Oak, its gnarled branches stretching high into the twilight sky like ancient fingers grasping for the stars. She brushed her fingers against the rough bark, feeling the pulse of magic beneath its surface. Beside her, Jasper wagged his tail, his ears perked up as if he could sense the adventure just around the corner.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s just a tree, right?\u201d Mira whispered, though her own words faltered under the weight of expectation. The map crinkled in her pocket, a reminder of the riddle that awaited her. She pulled it out and scanned the delicate lines that hinted at the first hidden constellation.\n\n\u201cWe need to solve this riddle, Jasper,\u201d she said, determination igniting in her chest. \u201cThe stars won\u2019t find themselves.\u201d\n\nAs dusk deepened, Mira read the riddle aloud: \u201cAt the heart of the woods, where silence whispers low, find the spark of the stars, in the shadows they glow.\u201d Mira furrowed her brow, glancing around. \u201cWhat could that mean?\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a rustling sound broke the silence. Mira\u2019s heart raced as she turned to see Zane emerging from behind a cluster of bushes, a smug grin plastered across his face. \u201cWell, well, if it isn\u2019t my favorite rival,\u201d he sneered. \u201cYou think you can solve that riddle before I do?\u201d\n\n\u201cZane!\u201d Mira bristled, anger bubbling up. \u201cThis is my chance to help our village. You can\u2019t just steal it.\u201d\n\n\u201cYou think you\u2019re the only one who cares about the stars?\u201d Zane shot back, his voice like ice. \u201cI want them too. And I\u2019m not leaving without that map.\u201d\n\nMira took a step back, her mind racing. Zane had always been competitive, but this felt different. It felt dangerous. \u201cYou can\u2019t\u2014\u201d\n\nBefore she could finish, Zane lunged forward, trying to grab the map. Mira instinctively turned to run, but not before feeling the rough tug of Zane\u2019s hand against her arm. She stumbled but regained her balance, her heart pounding like a drum.\n\n\u201cLet go of me!\u201d she shouted, pulling the map close to her chest. Jasper barked fiercely, his protective instincts kicking in. He darted between Mira and Zane, teeth bared and growling.\n\nZane hesitated, momentarily taken aback by the fierce dog. \u201cYou think that mutt can stop me?\u201d he laughed, regaining his composure. \u201cYou\u2019re wasting time, Mira. The stars won\u2019t wait forever!\u201d\n\nJust then, a bright twinkle caught Mira\u2019s eye from the branches above. \u201cLook!\u201d she pointed, momentarily distracted. \u201cThe spark of the stars!\u201d \n\nZane\u2019s gaze shot upwards, and Mira seized the moment. \u201cWe have to find the spark before it disappears!\u201d She dashed toward the Old Oak, her legs pumping with adrenaline.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe bark of the tree shimmered as she reached out, tracing the path of light that glimmered like a beacon. \u201cIt\u2019s here! It\u2019s really here!\u201d Mira exclaimed, her heart swelling with hope.\n\nBut Zane wasn\u2019t far behind. \u201cYou won\u2019t figure it out, Mira. You never could!\u201d he taunted, lunging again in a desperate attempt to snatch the map. \n\nIn that critical moment, with Zane so close, Mira felt the weight of the riddle pressing down on her. The spark flickered above her, beckoning her closer, but the risk of losing the map was looming larger than ever. She had to decide: protect the map or reach for the constellation that could lead them to the stars.\n\n\u201cMira!\u201d Jasper barked, urging her to focus. She took a deep breath, realizing that this was the moment her bravery would be truly tested.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cOkay, Zane,\u201d she said, turning to face him with newfound confidence. \u201cLet\u2019s see who can solve the riddle first.\u201d\n\nMira knew that whatever happened next would change everything.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the riddle that Mira must solve?","options":["At the heart of the woods, where silence whispers low, find the spark of the stars, in the shadows they glow.","In the darkest night, when the moon is high, the stars reveal secrets, if you only try.","When the sun sets low, and the sky turns blue, follow the light to find what's true.","The stars hide deep in the forest's embrace, find them quickly or lose the race."],"correct_answer":"At the heart of the woods, where silence whispers low, find the spark of the stars, in the shadows they glow."},{"question":"What does Zane want from Mira?","options":["To join her on her adventure","The magical map","Her dog, Jasper","A treasure chest"],"correct_answer":"The magical map"},{"question":"How does Mira feel when Zane confronts her?","options":["Excited","Angry and fearful","Happy","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Angry and fearful"},{"question":"What does Jasper do during Zane's confrontation?","options":["Runs away","Barks protectively","Sits quietly","Tries to attack Zane"],"correct_answer":"Barks protectively"},{"question":"What major decision does Mira face at the end of the chapter?","options":["Whether to leave the map behind","Whether to challenge Zane to a riddle race","Whether to run away from Zane","Whether to trust Zane"],"correct_answer":"Whether to challenge Zane to a riddle race"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_21_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_21_ch3_img1.png","plot_21_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":631,"reading_level":"Builder"}
