   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_22_7_10","title":"The Secret Compass","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Quest or Journey","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Leo stood in his dusty attic, the light from the small window barely reaching him. Boxes were piled high, filled with forgotten toys and old clothes. \u201cWhat a mess!\u201d he exclaimed, brushing away a spiderweb. Suddenly, something shiny caught his eye.\n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d Leo said, reaching into a box. He pulled out a strange compass. It was round and sparkled like the stars. \u201cHello, Leo!\u201d said the compass in a cheerful voice.\n\nLeo jumped back. \u201cDid that compass just talk?\u201d he asked, blinking in disbelief. \u201cYes, I did!\u201d the compass replied with a giggle. \u201cI\u2019m your guide to adventure!\u201d\n\nLeo's heart raced. \u201cWhat kind of adventure?\u201d he wondered aloud. The compass spun around, its needle pointing toward the attic door. \u201cFollow me to the Island of Whimsy!\u201d it said. \u201cBut beware of the Gnome King!\u201d\n\n\u201cGnome King?\u201d Leo scratched his head. \u201cIs he scary?\u201d The compass chuckled. \u201cHe\u2019s more silly than scary. But he doesn\u2019t want you to find the island!\u201d\n\nJust then, Leo heard a voice coming from the stairs. \u201cLeo!\u201d It was Ms. Tilly, his quirky neighbor. She wore a bright purple hat covered in feathers. \u201cWhat are you up to in there?\u201d \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Leo exclaimed, holding up the talking compass. \u201cIt wants to take me on an adventure!\u201d \n\nMs. Tilly\u2019s eyes sparkled. \u201cAn adventure? Count me in! I have my trusty parrot, Pippin!\u201d she said, pulling the feathery parrot from her shoulder.\n\n\u201cSquawk! Adventure!\u201d Pippin cried, flapping his wings wildly. Leo smiled. \u201cOkay, let\u2019s go!\u201d \n\nThey stepped out of the attic, the compass guiding them. The world outside looked normal, but Leo felt something magical in the air. Leaves rustled, and the sun shone brightly. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, the compass whirled faster. \u201cWe\u2019re getting closer!\u201d it chirped. Just then, they arrived at the edge of an enchanted forest. Towering trees with candy-colored trunks loomed over them, and flowers danced in the soft breeze.\n\n\u201cWow!\u201d Leo gasped. \u201cThis is incredible!\u201d But then, a tiny voice piped up from the bushes. \u201cWell, well, well! What do we have here?\u201d A small gnome with a pointy hat poked his head out. \n\n\u201cHello!\u201d Leo greeted, but the gnome frowned. \u201cYou\u2019re not supposed to be here! The Gnome King will keep you from finding the island!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhy would he do that?\u201d Ms. Tilly asked, crossing her arms. \n\n\u201cBecause the Island of Whimsy is a secret!\u201d the gnome said, grinning. \u201cAnd I\u2019m going to make sure you don\u2019t find it!\u201d \n\nLeo felt a shiver of excitement. \u201cOh no! We have to hurry!\u201d [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] \n\nWith the compass spinning wildly, Leo, Ms. Tilly, and Pippin raced into the forest. They had a secret to find, and a silly gnome to outsmart!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does the compass do?","options":["It tells the time","It talks","It gives directions","It is broken"],"correct_answer":"It talks"},{"question":"Who joins Leo on his adventure?","options":["His dog","Ms. Tilly and Pippin","His sister","His friend"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Tilly and Pippin"},{"question":"What does the Gnome King want?","options":["To help Leo","To keep the island a secret","To be friends","To find treasure"],"correct_answer":"To keep the island a secret"},{"question":"What colors describe the enchanted forest?","options":["Gray and dull","Bright and colorful","Black and white","Brown and green"],"correct_answer":"Bright and colorful"},{"question":"What does the compass point towards?","options":["The attic","The island","The ground","The city"],"correct_answer":"The island"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_22_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_22_ch1_img1.png","plot_22_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":457,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
