   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_22_11_14","title":"The Secret Compass","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Quest or Journey","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Leo Wilson had always believed that adventures were meant for brave knights and daring explorers\u2014not for twelve-year-old boys who found themselves trapped in boring suburban life. But on one particularly rainy Saturday afternoon, Leo\u2019s dull world was about to change forever. He was rummaging through his attic, searching for anything remotely interesting when he stumbled upon an old, dusty box. \n\nCuriosity piqued, he brushed away the cobwebs and opened the box, revealing a shiny, bronze compass nestled amongst a collection of forgotten trinkets. It looked ordinary enough, but as he picked it up and examined it closer, the needle spun wildly before settling, pointing toward him. \n\n\u201cHello there!\u201d said a cheerful voice. \n\nLeo nearly dropped the compass. \u201cDid that compass just talk?\u201d he exclaimed, his heart racing. He blinked, half-expecting the voice to disappear like a mirage. \n\n\u201cOf course I did! Name\u2019s Caden, and I\u2019m your guide to adventure!\u201d The compass winked, its needle now steady and pointing straight ahead. \n\n\u201cWhat kind of adventure?\u201d Leo asked, his excitement mingling with skepticism. \n\n\u201cThat\u2019s for you to discover, but it involves the legendary Island of Whimsy!\u201d Caden declared. \n\nLeo\u2019s mind raced. The Island of Whimsy was a place filled with magic, talking animals, and endless possibilities\u2014at least, that\u2019s what the stories said. \u201cBut how do I get there?\u201d \n\n\u201cFollow me,\u201d Caden instructed, and with a quick twist of the compass, the attic around Leo began to shimmer like a mirage in the desert. \n\nSuddenly, the walls of his attic melted away, revealing a vibrant, enchanted forest filled with colorful trees and flowers that seemed to sing. Leo stood there, mouth agape, but then he remembered his neighbor, Ms. Tilly, and her outrageous stories about the forest behind their houses. \n\n\u201cWait! I need to tell Ms. Tilly!\u201d Leo shouted, turning on his heel and racing down the stairs. He dashed across the yard, where the familiar sight of Ms. Tilly\u2019s whimsical cottage came into view. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nLeo knocked on her door, and it swung open to reveal Ms. Tilly in her characteristic oversized glasses and a bright green apron with pockets stuffed full of oddities. \u201cLeo, dear! What\u2019s the matter?\u201d she asked, her pet parrot, Nimbus, perched on her shoulder, bobbing his head.\n\n\u201cI found a talking compass! It says it can take us to the Island of Whimsy!\u201d Leo panted, excitement bubbling in his chest.\n\n\u201cOh, how marvelous!\u201d Ms. Tilly exclaimed, her eyes twinkling with mischief. \u201cI\u2019ve always believed there was more to this world than what meets the eye!\u201d\n\nTogether, they followed Caden, who led them deeper into the forest. However, the path soon twisted and turned, becoming more complicated with every step. Suddenly, a giggling sound erupted from behind a bush. \n\nOut popped a gnome, wearing a bright red hat that seemed almost too large for his head. \u201cWell, well, well! What do we have here? Two adventurers lost in my woods?\u201d His eyes sparkled with mischief.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re not lost!\u201d Leo declared, trying to sound braver than he felt. \u201cWe\u2019re on our way to the Island of Whimsy!\u201d\n\n\u201cAh, the Island of Whimsy!\u201d the gnome chuckled. \u201cBut you\u2019ll never get there without my help!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Ms. Tilly asked, her brow furrowing. \n\nThe Gnome King leaned closer, a sly smile on his face. \u201cI could show you the way\u2026 for a price!\u201d\n\nA chill ran down Leo\u2019s spine. Something felt off, and he glanced at Ms. Tilly, who seemed equally wary. Who was this gnome, really? And could they trust him?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nLeo heard Caden whisper, \u201cBe careful, Leo. The Gnome King is known for his tricks!\u201d\n\nAs they stood there, the gnome\u2019s laughter echoed in the air, blending with the enchanted sounds of the forest. Leo knew they were at a crossroads\u2014would they follow the gnome's lead or trust their instincts?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the name of the talking compass?","options":["Nimbus","Caden","Leo","Tilly"],"correct_answer":"Caden"},{"question":"Who is Leo's neighbor?","options":["The Gnome King","Nimbus","Ms. Tilly","Caden"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Tilly"},{"question":"Where does Caden promise to take Leo?","options":["The Island of Mysteries","The Island of Whimsy","The Land of Giants","The Gnome King's Castle"],"correct_answer":"The Island of Whimsy"},{"question":"What does the Gnome King offer Leo and Ms. Tilly?","options":["A treasure map","A magical potion","To show them the way to the island","A pet parrot"],"correct_answer":"To show them the way to the island"},{"question":"What does Leo feel about the Gnome King's offer?","options":["Excited","Curious","Wary","Confident"],"correct_answer":"Wary"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_22_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_22_ch1_img1.png","plot_22_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":653,"reading_level":"Builder"}
