   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_25_7_10","title":"Journey to the Edge of the World","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Quest or Journey","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Sara stared at the old, dusty journal. It was hidden in her attic, just under a pile of boxes. It looked ancient and mysterious. \n\n\u201cMax, come look at this!\u201d she shouted. Max, her best friend, shuffled into the attic, rubbing his eyes. \n\n\u201cWhat is it?\u201d he asked, leaning closer. \n\n\u201cIt\u2019s a navigator\u2019s journal!\u201d Sara exclaimed, flipping the pages. They were filled with maps and stories about a place called the Edge of the World. \n\n\u201cSounds boring,\u201d Max said with a shrug. \n\n\u201cNo way! It says here that the Edge has answers to all of life\u2019s questions!\u201d Sara\u2019s eyes sparkled with excitement. \n\nMax\u2019s eyebrows furrowed. \u201cBut what if it\u2019s dangerous?\u201d \n\nSara smiled. \u201cThat\u2019s what makes it an adventure! We could be explorers!\u201d \n\nMax chewed on his lip. \u201cI guess... but what if we get lost?\u201d \n\nJust then, a soft voice spoke from the shadows. \u201cYou won\u2019t get lost if you have a guide.\u201d \n\nSara and Max turned to see a wise old turtle, with a shell covered in seaweed. \n\n\u201cWho are you?\u201d Max whispered, his eyes wide. \n\n\u201cI am Tully,\u201d the turtle said, smiling gently. \u201cAnd I know the way to the Edge of the World.\u201d \n\nSara jumped up, clapping her hands. \u201cCan you take us there?\u201d \n\nTully nodded slowly. \u201cBut first, you must be brave. The journey will test you.\u201d \n\nSara felt a flutter in her stomach. \u201cWhat kind of tests?\u201d \n\n\u201cStormy seas, wild creatures, and your own fears,\u201d Tully replied. \n\nMax took a deep breath. \u201cOkay, maybe we should think about this\u2026\u201d \n\nBut Sara was already dreaming of the ocean. \u201cWe can do this, Max! We can find the answers!\u201d \n\nMax glanced at Tully, then back at Sara. \u201cAlright, let\u2019s go!\u201d \n\nWith a laugh, Sara tucked the journal under her arm. They were ready. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they stepped out of the attic, Sara felt a mix of excitement and nervousness. The sun shone bright outside, but she had no idea what awaited them. \n\nSara looked back at Tully. \u201cWhat do we do first?\u201d \n\n\u201cGather supplies and meet me at the shore,\u201d Tully said, his voice steady. \u201cThen, our adventure begins!\u201d \n\nNow, more excited than ever, Sara dashed down the street. Max followed, still a little hesitant. \n\n\u201cWait up!\u201d he called. \n\nThey gathered food, water, and a small tent. Sara could hardly contain her excitement. \n\n\u201cThis is it!\u201d she cheered. \u201cWe\u2019re going on an adventure!\u201d \n\nAs they reached the shore, they saw a small boat waiting for them. Tully was already on board, waving a flipper. \n\n\u201cCome aboard, my brave friends!\u201d he called. \n\nSara and Max exchanged glances. This was it! They would sail into the unknown. \n\nAs the boat rocked gently in the waves, Sara felt a rush of courage. She looked at Max, who smiled back. \n\n\u201cReady?\u201d he asked. \n\n\u201cReady!\u201d Sara shouted. \n\nTogether, they climbed aboard, ready to embark on their journey to the Edge of the World. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Sara find in the attic?","options":["A map","A journal","A toy","A book"],"correct_answer":"A journal"},{"question":"Who is Tully?","options":["A bird","A wise old turtle","A pirate","A fish"],"correct_answer":"A wise old turtle"},{"question":"What does the Edge of the World promise?","options":["Danger","Adventure","Answers","Treasure"],"correct_answer":"Answers"},{"question":"What do Max and Sara need to gather?","options":["Friends","Supplies","Toys","Bags"],"correct_answer":"Supplies"},{"question":"How does Sara feel about the adventure?","options":["Scared","Bored","Excited","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_25_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_25_ch1_img1.png","plot_25_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":493,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
