   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_25_7_10","title":"Journey to the Edge of the World","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Quest or Journey","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Sara and Max stood at the beach, with the sun shining bright. The ocean sparkled, and the waves danced playfully. They were ready for an adventure!\n\n\u201cLook! There\u2019s Tully!\u201d said Sara, pointing to the wise old turtle swimming toward them. Tully surfaced, his big eyes twinkling. \u201cAre you ready for your journey?\u201d he asked with a slow, gentle voice.\n\n\u201cYes!\u201d shouted Max, though he felt butterflies in his stomach. \u201cUm, I mean\u2026 Yes!\u201d \n\nTully smiled. \u201cGood! Remember, the path to the Edge of the World is not easy. There will be storms and challenges.\u201d\n\nSara\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat kind of challenges?\u201d she asked, her eyes wide with curiosity.\n\n\u201cYou will face your fears,\u201d Tully said, dipping his big head into the water. \u201cBut together, you can conquer anything!\u201d\n\nJust then, dark clouds appeared on the horizon. Sara frowned. \u201cIs that a storm?\u201d \n\n\u201cYes,\u201d Tully replied, narrowing his eyes. \u201cWe must sail quickly.\u201d\n\nThey hopped onto a small boat, and Tully led the way. The wind picked up, and the waves grew larger. \u201cHold on tight!\u201d cried Sara, gripping the sides of the boat.\n\nMax\u2019s face turned pale. \u201cI don\u2019t like storms!\u201d he shouted over the wind. \u201cWhat if we capsized?\u201d\n\nTully turned to Max, his eyes kind. \u201cBravery is not the absence of fear. It\u2019s sailing through it.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a giant wave crashed over the boat! Water splashed everywhere, soaking Sara and Max. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cWhoa! This is wild!\u201d Sara laughed, splashing back at Max, who was now giggling despite his worries.\n\n\u201cOkay, okay! I can do this!\u201d he yelled, grinning wide. \n\nAs they sailed on, the storm began to calm. The clouds parted, revealing a beautiful island. \u201cLook!\u201d Sara pointed. \u201cIs that one of the magical islands from the journal?\u201d\n\nTully nodded. \u201cYes, but be careful. Each island has its own mysteries.\u201d\n\nJust then, they heard a loud roar! Max jumped up. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d\n\nTully\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cStay close! We must face what\u2019s ahead together.\u201d\n\nThe boat drifted closer to the island. Sara felt a mix of excitement and fear. What would they find? \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d she cheered, ready for whatever was next.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMax took a deep breath. \u201cOkay, I\u2019m with you, Sara. Together, we can do anything!\u201d\n\nBut as they approached the shore, shadows moved in the trees. What could it be? \n\nThe adventure was just beginning.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who do Sara and Max meet at the beach?","options":["A giant bird","A wise old turtle","A friendly dolphin","A magical mermaid"],"correct_answer":"A wise old turtle"},{"question":"What do Sara and Max sail through?","options":["A sunny day","A heavy storm","A calm sea","A magical fog"],"correct_answer":"A heavy storm"},{"question":"What is revealed after the storm?","options":["A treasure map","A magical island","A secret cave","A friendly whale"],"correct_answer":"A magical island"},{"question":"What does Tully say about bravery?","options":["It's easy to be brave.","It's sailing through fear.","Bravery means no fear.","It's running away."],"correct_answer":"It's sailing through fear."},{"question":"What do Sara and Max sense on the island?","options":["A friendly creature","A hidden treasure","Danger lurking in the shadows","A party"],"correct_answer":"Danger lurking in the shadows"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_25_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_25_ch2_img1.png","plot_25_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":401,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
