   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_25_11_14","title":"Journey to the Edge of the World","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Quest or Journey","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The salty breeze swept through the small coastal town of Seaview, where the waves crashed against the rocks like a thousand secrets waiting to be uncovered. Thirteen-year-old Sara stood at the edge of the pier, her heart racing with excitement and curiosity. Today was different; today would change everything.\n\n\"Are you sure about this, Sara?\" Max asked, his voice tinged with hesitation as he fidgeted with the compass he had borrowed from his grandfather. He had always been the logical one, the one who preferred the safety of predictability over the unknown. Yet, there was something about Sara's enthusiasm that drew him in.\n\n\"Come on, Max! We can't let this chance slip away. The journal says the Edge of the World is real!\" Sara\u2019s eyes sparkled with determination as she clutched the worn navigator's journal in her hands. It had been hidden away in her attic for years, filled with sketches of mysterious islands, maps marked with strange symbols, and notes about the adventures of a long-gone explorer.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs she flipped through its yellowed pages, the illustrations seemed to leap to life. She could almost hear the whispers of the ocean calling her name, urging her to embark on this journey. \"Imagine all the answers we could find, Max! What if the Edge holds the key to our future?\"\n\nMax sighed, his brow furrowing. \"But what if it\u2019s dangerous? What if we get lost?\"\n\nSara shook her head, a smile playing on her lips. \"That\u2019s the thrill of adventure! Besides, we\u2019ll have Tully to guide us.\"\n\nTully was no ordinary turtle; he was a wise creature who had lived for decades in the sea, with stories that spanned generations. Just as Sara spoke his name, the gentle swish of water caught their attention, and Tully surfaced, his shell glistening in the sunlight.\n\n\"Ready for an adventure, young explorers?\" Tully asked, his voice deep and soothing like the ocean itself. \"The sea is full of wonders, but it also demands respect.\"\n\nMax nodded slowly, his fear mingled with awe as Tully\u2019s eyes twinkled with wisdom. \u201cWe\u2019ll be careful, I promise.\u201d\n\nWith Tully leading the way, they climbed onto the small boat that Sara\u2019s father had used for fishing. As they set sail, clouds began to gather on the horizon. The wind picked up, tossing the boat slightly, and Sara felt her stomach flutter with a mix of excitement and anxiety.\n\n\"Look!\" Sara shouted, pointing at the waves cresting in the distance. \"It\u2019s beautiful!\"\n\nBut Tully\u2019s expression grew serious. \"Remember, the journey to the Edge of the World is not just about what you will see, but what you will learn. Be prepared to face your fears.\"\n\nJust as he finished speaking, a sharp crack of thunder echoed across the sky, darkening the once bright blue. The first drops of rain began to fall, and the boat rocked violently. Max grabbed the edge of the boat, his knuckles white.\n\n\"Sara! I don\u2019t think we should go any further!\" he yelled, his voice barely audible over the roaring wind.\n\nSara\u2019s heart raced, but she knew they couldn\u2019t turn back now. \"We can do this, Max! We have to make it to the Edge!\u201d \n\nBut doubt flickered in her mind like the lightning splitting the sky. Could they really face the wild waters ahead, or would they be swept away by the storm?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith the waves crashing against the boat, they prepared for whatever lay ahead. Would they make it to the Edge of the World, or would they find themselves lost in the depths of their own fears?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What motivates Sara to go on the journey?","options":["Curiosity for adventure","A school project","To impress her friends","To escape her town"],"correct_answer":"Curiosity for adventure"},{"question":"Who is Tully?","options":["A wise turtle","A fisherman","Sara's father","A sailor"],"correct_answer":"A wise turtle"},{"question":"What does Max express concern about?","options":["The weather","Their parents' approval","Getting lost","The boat's condition"],"correct_answer":"Getting lost"},{"question":"What happens when they set sail?","options":["The sun shines brightly","A storm begins to brew","They find treasure","They see dolphins"],"correct_answer":"A storm begins to brew"},{"question":"What lesson does Tully mention about the journey?","options":["It\u2019s easy to navigate","They will find treasure","It\u2019s about facing fears","They should never turn back"],"correct_answer":"It\u2019s about facing fears"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_25_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_25_ch1_img1.png","plot_25_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":611,"reading_level":"Builder"}
