   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_16_7_10","title":"The Clock Tower Conundrum","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The clock tower echoed with strange sounds. Max, Ava, Leo, and Mia huddled together. \u201cWhat just happened?\u201d Mia whispered, her eyes wide. \n\n\u201cI think we\u2019re locked in!\u201d Max said, trying to hide his worry. He pulled on the heavy door, but it wouldn\u2019t budge. \u201cWe need to find a way out!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s look for clues,\u201d Ava suggested, her eyebrows raised. She loved puzzles. \u201cThere must be something in here.\u201d \n\nThe friends walked deeper into the tower. They passed tall, wooden beams and dusty old gears. \u201cIt\u2019s like a giant clock factory!\u201d Leo joked, trying to lighten the mood. \u201cMaybe we\u2019ll find a giant hamster running the show!\u201d\n\n\u201cStop it, Leo!\u201d Mia said, giggling despite her fear. \u201cThis is serious!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, they spotted a flickering light from a hidden corner. \u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d Max pointed. The friends rushed to the light. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nIn the corner, they found a small chest. It was covered in cobwebs. \u201cLet\u2019s open it!\u201d Ava said, her eyes sparkling. They all gathered around as Max lifted the lid. Inside, they discovered a riddle written on a piece of parchment.\n\n\u201cTo escape this tower, you must be wise. Solve this riddle, and you\u2019ll see the prize. I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with the years. What am I?\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat does that mean?\u201d Mia asked, biting her lip. \n\n\u201cIt sounds like\u2026 a ghost!\u201d Leo exclaimed with a dramatic shiver. \n\n\u201cA ghost? Really, Leo?\u201d Max chuckled. \u201cLet\u2019s think. It\u2019s something that doesn\u2019t have a body. It must be something else.\u201d\n\n\u201cI know!\u201d Ava shouted. \u201cIt\u2019s an echo!\u201d \n\n\u201cAn echo?\u201d Mia repeated, unsure. \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Ava beamed. \u201cThat\u2019s it! Let\u2019s say it together.\u201d\n\nThe friends took a deep breath. \u201cAn echo!\u201d they shouted. Suddenly, the chest creaked and opened wider. Inside, they found a key! \n\n\u201cWe did it!\u201d Leo cheered, jumping up and down. \u201cNow we can unlock the door!\u201d\n\nBut before they could leave, the clock began to chime. \u201cOh no! We need to hurry!\u201d Max said, clutching the key tightly. \n\nWhat if the only way out was to solve more riddles? They looked at each other, determination in their eyes. The clock was ticking, and time was running out!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do the friends find in the clock tower?","options":["A treasure map","A riddle","A giant hamster","A clock"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What is the answer to the riddle?","options":["A ghost","An echo","A shadow","A whisper"],"correct_answer":"An echo"},{"question":"How does Mia feel when they find out they are locked in?","options":["Excited","Worried","Angry","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Worried"},{"question":"Who finds the riddle first?","options":["Max","Leo","Ava","Mia"],"correct_answer":"Ava"},{"question":"What happens when they shout the answer to the riddle?","options":["The clock stops","The chest opens wider","They hear a ghost","The door unlocks"],"correct_answer":"The chest opens wider"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_16_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_16_ch2_img1.png","plot_16_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":384,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
