   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_16_7_10","title":"The Clock Tower Conundrum","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The clock tower was dark and dusty. Max, Ava, Leo, and Mia stood close together. They could hear the soft ticking of the giant clock above them. \n\n\u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d asked Mia, nervously biting her lip.\n\nMax took a deep breath. \u201cWe keep solving the riddles. We\u2019re getting closer!\u201d\n\nAva pointed at the wall. \u201cLook! There\u2019s another riddle!\u201d She read it aloud:\n\n\u201cTo move ahead, find the gears that spin,  \nTurn them right, and let the fun begin!  \nBut beware, one wrong move\u2014  \nYou\u2019ll have to start over; that\u2019s the groove!\u201d\n\nLeo laughed, \u201cSounds like a dance party! Let\u2019s spin those gears!\u201d\n\nThey walked over to the giant gears on the wall. The gears were rusty and big, each one a different color. Max examined them closely. \n\n\u201cWhich one do we turn first?\u201d he asked.\n\nAva glanced at the riddle again. \u201cIt says to turn them right. But which one?\u201d\n\nMia pointed to a blue gear. \u201cWhat if we start with that one? It\u2019s the brightest.\u201d\n\nMax nodded. \u201cGood idea! On three, we turn it together!\u201d \n\n\u201cOne, two, three!\u201d they shouted and turned the blue gear.\n\nSuddenly, there was a loud *clunk*! The floor shook, and a hidden door opened in the wall. \n\n\u201cWow! Look at that!\u201d cheered Leo, jumping up and down. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe door revealed a staircase that spiraled down into darkness. Mia hesitated, her eyes wide. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s scary?\u201d\n\nMax smiled reassuringly. \u201cWe\u2019ll be together. We can do this!\u201d\n\nAva added, \u201cAnd we\u2019re getting closer to escaping!\u201d\n\nThey all took a deep breath and decided to go down the stairs. Each step creaked beneath their feet. As they reached the bottom, they found themselves in a small room filled with colorful lights.\n\n\u201cWhoa! This is amazing!\u201d Leo exclaimed. He pointed to the wall, where another riddle glowed.\n\n\u201cRead it, Ava!\u201d shouted Max, bouncing with excitement.\n\nAva read:\n\n\u201cTo find the way out, you must work as a team,  \nCount the colors of the lights that gleam.  \nWhen you know the number, shout it loud,  \nOnly then will the door open proud!\u201d\n\nMia whispered, \u201cThere are so many colors. How will we count them?\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s do it together!\u201d Max encouraged. They began counting.\n\n\u201cThere\u2019s red, blue, green\u2026\u201d Ava started.\n\n\u201cYellow!\u201d Leo added. \n\nSoon, they counted all the colors together. \u201cSeven!\u201d they shouted in unison. \n\nThe door creaked open slowly, revealing a tunnel. \u201cWe did it!\u201d cheered Mia, her face lighting up with hope.\n\n\u201cI can\u2019t believe we\u2019re making progress!\u201d Ava grinned, feeling more confident now.\n\nMax grinned as they lined up to enter the tunnel. \u201cLet\u2019s go before time runs out!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey stepped into the tunnel, the excitement bubbling inside them. What other secrets did the clock tower hold?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did the friends find on the wall?","options":["A treasure map","Another riddle","A painting","A clock"],"correct_answer":"Another riddle"},{"question":"What color gear did they turn first?","options":["Red","Green","Blue","Yellow"],"correct_answer":"Blue"},{"question":"How many colors did they count in the colorful room?","options":["Five","Six","Seven","Eight"],"correct_answer":"Seven"},{"question":"What did Mia feel about going down the stairs?","options":["Excited","Scared","Angry","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Scared"},{"question":"What did Max encourage his friends to do?","options":["Run away","Work as a team","Take a nap","Leave the tower"],"correct_answer":"Work as a team"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_16_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_16_ch4_img1.png","plot_16_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":471,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
