   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_16_7_10","title":"The Clock Tower Conundrum","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The clock tower creaked and groaned as Max, Ava, Leo, and Mia stood together in the colorful room. \u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d Mia asked, biting her nails. \n\n\u201cWe need to find the last riddle!\u201d Max encouraged. \u201cAva, do you think you can figure it out?\u201d \n\nAva nodded. \u201cLet\u2019s look at the patterns on the walls. There might be clues.\u201d\n\nThe friends spread out, their eyes searching every corner. The walls were painted bright colors, with swirls and shapes. They saw a big clock that looked like it was smiling at them. \n\n\u201cLook at this!\u201d Leo shouted, pointing to a circle of lights above. \u201cThere are five red lights and three blue lights!\u201d\n\n\u201cCount them again, Leo!\u201d Mia said, trembling. \u201cWe can\u2019t make mistakes!\u201d \n\n\u201cFive red lights!\u201d Leo laughed. \u201cAnd three blue lights! Counting is easy!\u201d \n\n\u201cWait!\u201d Ava said, her eyes sparkling. \u201cThe riddle about gears said something about colors and numbers. Maybe we need to use this information!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe friends gathered around Ava. They put their heads together and whispered, \u201cFive plus three equals eight. Let\u2019s see what happens if we press the lights in order!\u201d \n\nMia pressed the first red light. Nothing happened. \n\n\u201cTry the next one!\u201d Max said, feeling excited.\n\nOne by one, they pressed the lights. Finally, when Mia pressed the last blue light, the room filled with a soft humming sound. The floor beneath them shook slightly. \n\n\u201cDid you feel that?\u201d Mia squeaked.\n\n\u201cI did!\u201d Ava exclaimed, bouncing on her toes. \u201cLook! The wall is moving!\u201d \n\nThe wall slid open to reveal a hidden passageway. The group cheered and jumped up and down. \n\n\u201cThis is it! We are getting out!\u201d Leo shouted with glee. \n\nAs they entered the passage, the air felt cooler, and the walls were dark. Max led the way, his heart pounding. \u201cStay close, everyone!\u201d he called out. \n\nSuddenly, they heard a ticking noise. \u201cIs that the clock?\u201d Mia gasped. \n\n\u201cYeah!\u201d Leo replied, grinning. \u201cBut let\u2019s hurry before it ticks us into a time warp!\u201d \n\nThey ran through the passage, laughter echoing off the walls. Each step they took felt lighter as they worked together. They were not just friends now; they were a team. \n\nAs they burst into the light outside, they felt the sunshine on their faces. They had solved the riddle and escaped the clock tower! \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s never stop being brave together!\u201d Max declared. \n\nAva smiled, \u201cAnd let\u2019s never forget our adventure!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do the friends find in the colorful room?","options":["A big clock","A treasure chest","A giant door","A magic carpet"],"correct_answer":"A big clock"},{"question":"How many red lights do the friends count?","options":["Three","Five","Eight","Six"],"correct_answer":"Five"},{"question":"What do the friends need to do with the lights?","options":["Sing a song","Press them in order","Color them","Count them again"],"correct_answer":"Press them in order"},{"question":"What feeling do the friends have when they escape?","options":["Nervous","Sad","Excited","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What important lesson do the friends learn?","options":["To be quick","To work together","To be silly","To stay quiet"],"correct_answer":"To work together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_16_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_16_ch5_img1.png","plot_16_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":411,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
