   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_16_11_14","title":"The Clock Tower Conundrum","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun hung low in the sky, casting a golden hue over the town of Eldridge as Max, Ava, Leo, and Mia stepped off the bus. Their school trip to the old clock tower had been the talk of the week, and the excitement buzzed in the air like static before a storm. Max, the group\u2019s natural leader, scanned the towering structure with wide eyes. \n\n\u201cThere it is! The clock tower of Eldridge!\u201d he exclaimed, his voice a mix of awe and determination. The ancient stone fa\u00e7ade loomed before them, covered in creeping vines and mysterious carvings. Its clockface, cracked and faded, ticked lazily. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLooks like something out of a movie,\u201d Ava said, pushing her glasses up her nose. As the puzzle expert of the group, she was both curious and cautious about what lay ahead. \u201cI wonder if there are any hidden rooms inside.\u201d \n\n\u201cOr ghosts!\u201d Leo chimed in, his wide grin breaking the tension. He loved to joke around, but deep down, he was just as intrigued. \u201cWhat if the clock is cursed? Tick-tock, you're trapped!\u201d\n\nMia, who often felt nervous in unfamiliar situations, looked up at the tower and swallowed hard. \u201cI hope it\u2019s just a regular old tower,\u201d she muttered, her fingers fidgeting with the strap of her backpack. \n\nThey ventured inside, the heavy door creaking ominously as it swung open. Dust motes danced in the sunlight filtering through the stained glass, casting colorful patterns on the stone floor. The interior was a labyrinth of twisting staircases, ancient gears, and shadows that seemed to whisper secrets. \n\nAs the group moved deeper, they stumbled upon a massive clock face, its hands frozen at midnight. \u201cWhy is it stopped?\u201d Ava wondered aloud, her brow furrowed in thought. Suddenly, a loud clank echoed through the tower, making Mia jump. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d she gasped, peering into the dim light. \n\nBefore anyone could answer, the floor beneath them trembled, and a series of gears began to whir and grind. Max felt a rush of adrenaline as the door they had entered through slammed shut, echoing like a thunderclap. \n\n\u201cUh-oh,\u201d Leo said, his joking tone replaced by concern. \u201cI think we\u2019ve just entered a real-life escape room!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d Mia asked, her voice a blend of fear and resolve. \n\n\u201cFirst, we need to stay calm,\u201d Max said, taking charge. \u201cAva, you\u2019re our puzzle expert. Can you find any clues?\u201d \n\n\u201cI see something over there!\u201d Ava pointed towards an ancient inscription etched into the stone wall. \u201cIt looks like a riddle.\u201d \n\nAs they gathered closer, the inscription began to glow faintly. \u201cWhat has hands but cannot clap?\u201d it read. The air was thick with tension as they realized they needed to solve this riddle to escape. \n\n\u201cIs it\u2026a clock?\u201d Mia suggested hesitantly. \n\n\u201cOf course! It\u2019s a clock!\u201d Leo shouted, his earlier humor returning as he bounced on his heels. \u201cWe need to find a way to unlock it!\u201d \n\nAs they began to search for more clues, an eerie silence enveloped them. The sound of ticking grew louder, a countdown that echoed in their hearts. They were running out of time. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s split up and look for more answers,\u201d Max proposed, though doubt flickered in his mind. Could they find a way out before it was too late? \n\nThe clock tower held its secrets tightly, and with each tick of the clock, the challenge ahead loomed larger than ever. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMax's heart raced as he glanced around for anything that could help. The walls seemed to close in, but deep down, he felt the bond of friendship strengthen. They would face this together, and whether they succeeded or failed, they would emerge changed.\n\nCould they unravel the mysteries of the clock tower before time ran out?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Max, Ava, Leo, and Mia discover when they first enter the clock tower?","options":["A treasure map","A hidden door","A massive clock face","A ghost"],"correct_answer":"A massive clock face"},{"question":"What happens to the door they entered through?","options":["It disappears","It locks shut","It opens wider","It breaks"],"correct_answer":"It locks shut"},{"question":"What does the riddle in the inscription say?","options":["What has hands but cannot clap?","What is lost but never found?","What is silent but can shout?","What runs but never walks?"],"correct_answer":"What has hands but cannot clap?"},{"question":"Who is the puzzle expert in the group?","options":["Max","Leo","Ava","Mia"],"correct_answer":"Ava"},{"question":"What is the main theme of the chapter?","options":["Adventure and exploration","Fear and isolation","Friendship and teamwork","Mystery and danger"],"correct_answer":"Friendship and teamwork"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_16_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_16_ch1_img1.png","plot_16_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":638,"reading_level":"Builder"}
