   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_16_11_14","title":"The Clock Tower Conundrum","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The clock tower loomed over Max and his friends like a giant guardian of secrets. Inside, the air was thick with dust and the scent of old wood. As they stood in the dimly lit chamber, the massive clock face ticked steadily, each tick echoing like a heartbeat in the silence. \n\n\u201cAlright, team,\u201d Max said, his voice steady despite the unease creeping into his gut. \u201cWe need to figure out how to get out of here.\u201d He glanced at his watch, the hands of which mocked him with their relentless march. \n\nLeo leaned against the wall, a smirk on his face. \u201cMaybe we just need to ask the clock nicely. \u2018Please unlock this door, Mr. Clock!\u2019\u201d He burst into laughter, but the sound bounced off the stone walls, drawing furrowed brows from the others.\n\n\u201cVery funny, Leo,\u201d Ava interjected, her eyes scanning the intricate gears and levers surrounding them. \u201cLet\u2019s focus. There has to be a clue somewhere.\u201d She stepped closer to a dusty old book lying on a pedestal, its pages yellowed with age. \n\nMia shifted anxiously. \u201cWhat if we can\u2019t solve whatever is in there? What if we\u2019re stuck forever?\u201d Her voice trembled, and Max could see her biting her lip, worry etched across her face. \n\n\u201cHey, we\u2019ll be fine,\u201d Max reassured, placing a hand on her shoulder. \u201cWe just have to stick together. Let\u2019s see what this book has to say.\u201d \n\nWith a nod, Ava flipped the book open. The pages crackled with age, and the friends leaned in closer. Words jumped out at them: \u201cTo escape the tower\u2019s hold, the heart of the time must be told.\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat does that even mean?\u201d Leo asked, scratching his head. \n\nAva\u2019s brow furrowed in concentration. \u201cIt could be a riddle. \u2018The heart of the time\u2019? Maybe it\u2019s referring to something specific in the tower.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, an ominous clang echoed from above. The friends jumped back, fear lacing the air. Max\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we need to hurry,\u201d Ava urged, her fingers tapping nervously on the book. \u201cWe don\u2019t have much time before... well, before something bad happens.\u201d \n\nJust then, a loud *click* echoed through the chamber. The sound made Mia scream, while Max instinctively moved closer to her. The clock\u2019s face shifted, revealing a hidden compartment. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Leo exclaimed, pointing. \u201cThere\u2019s something in there!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMax took a deep breath. \u201cAlright, let\u2019s check it out.\u201d He reached into the compartment, pulling out something shiny. It was an old key, glinting in the minimal light. \n\n\u201cDo you think it could unlock one of the doors?\u201d Max asked, his hopes rising with each word. \n\n\u201cOnly one way to find out,\u201d Ava said, her pulse quickening with anticipation. \n\nAs they turned towards the towering door marked \u2018EXIT\u2019, Mia hesitated, a frown creasing her forehead. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s a trap?\u201d \n\n\u201cThen we\u2019ll face it together,\u201d Max replied firmly, gripping the key tightly. The ticking clock felt louder now, each tick a reminder that they were racing against time.\n\nJust as he approached the door, another rumble shook the tower, this one more intense. It felt as if the very walls were alive. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?\u201d Mia gasped, her voice barely above a whisper.\n\nMax turned toward his friends. \u201cWe need to decide. Do we try the key or find another clue?\u201d \n\nAva\u2019s eyes sparkled with determination. \u201cI say we go for it! We can\u2019t let fear hold us back.\u201d \n\nLeo nodded, his usual joking demeanor replaced with seriousness. \u201cYeah, let\u2019s do this!\u201d\n\nWith a deep breath, Max inserted the key into the lock, ready to face whatever lay behind the door. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe clock ticked ominously as they waited with bated breath, the sound echoing their racing hearts.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ava find in the dusty old book?","options":["A riddle","A map","A poem","A story"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What does Max reassure Mia about?","options":["That they will never escape","That they need to split up","That they will be fine if they stick together","That they should stop searching"],"correct_answer":"That they will be fine if they stick together"},{"question":"What do the friends find inside the hidden compartment?","options":["A treasure map","An old key","A diary","A compass"],"correct_answer":"An old key"},{"question":"How does Mia feel about the situation?","options":["Excited","Nervous","Indifferent","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What happens when Max tries the key in the lock?","options":["Nothing happens","The door opens","The clock stops","The tower shakes"],"correct_answer":"Nothing happens"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_16_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_16_ch2_img1.png","plot_16_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":642,"reading_level":"Builder"}
