   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_16_11_14","title":"The Clock Tower Conundrum","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The clock\u2019s relentless ticking echoed through the dimly lit chamber, wrapping around Max, Ava, Leo, and Mia like a tightening noose. With their hearts racing, they huddled closer together, their breaths misting in the cold air. \u201cWe have to find the next riddle!\u201d Max declared, steadying his voice despite the panic bubbling inside him. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check the wall over there,\u201d Ava suggested, pointing to a section adorned with intricate carvings of gears and clocks. \u201cThe book said something about a hidden message behind the symbols.\u201d \n\nAs they approached, Leo, always the jokester, quipped, \u201cWhat if the message says, \u2018Keep calm and panic on\u2019?\u201d Despite the nervous atmosphere, Mia cracked a smile, grateful for Leo\u2019s humor amidst their precarious situation.\n\nAva brushed her fingers over the carvings, her eyes narrowing with concentration. \u201cHere! This gear looks different.\u201d She pressed it, and with a soft click, another hidden compartment swung open, revealing a scroll. \n\nThe four friends crowded around as Ava unrolled it. The riddle was inscribed in elegant, flowing script:\n\n*\"In shadows deep where secrets dwell,  \nA guardian waits to cast his spell.  \nFind the heart that beats in the night,  \nAnd face your fear to find the light.\"*\n\n\u201cWhat does that even mean?\u201d Leo asked, scratching his head. \n\nMia\u2019s voice trembled slightly, \u201cMaybe it\u2019s about the clock? It has a heart, right?\u201d \n\n\u201cNo, not a literal heart,\u201d Max responded, looking around the chamber. \u201cIt\u2019s like\u2026 finding courage, I guess? But what\u2019s the \u2018guardian\u2019?\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the clock\u2019s hands began to move faster, a low rumble vibrating through the tower. Each tick felt like a countdown to calamity. \u201cWe need to hurry!\u201d Max urged, panic creeping into his tone. \n\nThey exchanged worried glances, each friend grappling with their own fears. For Mia, it was the anxiety of failing, while Leo felt the sting of being serious in such an overwhelming moment. Ava\u2019s confidence faltered as she realized this riddle was more than just a puzzle; it was a test of their very spirits.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s split up,\u201d Max suggested, though uncertainty edged his words. \u201cAva, you check the walls for any clues. Leo and I will look upstairs.\u201d \n\n\u201cNo! We shouldn\u2019t separate,\u201d Mia protested, her eyes wide. \u201cWhat if something happens?\u201d \n\n\u201cWe\u2019ll be fine,\u201d Max assured her, masking his own trepidation. \u201cWe\u2019re stronger together, right?\u201d \n\nReluctantly, Mia nodded, though doubt weighed heavily on her. \n\nAs they made their way to the staircase, a loud creak echoed above them, followed by a thud. The friends froze, hearts pounding in their chests. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Ava whispered, her bravado slipping away. \n\n\u201cJust the tower settling,\u201d Leo said, but his voice lacked conviction. \n\nMax turned to lead the way, but before he could take a step, the clock chimed ominously, the sound echoing like thunder in the confined space. \u201cWe don\u2019t have much time!\u201d he shouted, determination igniting within him. \n\nThey climbed the winding staircase, the air growing colder with each step. At the top, they stepped into a vast room illuminated by the moonlight streaming through a cracked window. In the center stood a massive clock, its intricate gears whirring with an otherworldly hum. \n\n\u201cThis must be it!\u201d Ava exclaimed, scanning for the heart of the clock. Suddenly, a shadow flickered in the corner of the room. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d \n\nBefore they could react, a figure emerged from the shadows, cloaked in darkness. \u201cYou dare disturb the guardian of time?\u201d it intoned, its voice echoing like a haunting melody through the chamber. \n\nMax\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWe just want to escape!\u201d\n\nThe figure\u2019s laughter was chilling. \u201cTo escape, you must first confront that which you fear most.\u201d \n\nAs the clock chimed again, a wave of panic swept over the friends. They stood frozen, staring into the abyss of the guardian\u2019s gaze\u2014a moment that would test their friendship, their courage, and their very identities.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe clock tower's interior with Max, Ava, Leo, and Mia standing before an enormous clock. Shadows loom around them, and the expressions of the friends reflect their mix of fear and determination.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nA dark, cloaked figure standing in the shadows of the room, illuminated by the eerie glow of the clock. Their face is obscured, and the air feels tense as the friends confront the unknown.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did the friends find in the hidden compartment?","options":["A key","A scroll","A map","A clock"],"correct_answer":"A scroll"},{"question":"What does Mia fear the most?","options":["Failing","The dark","Being alone","Climbing stairs"],"correct_answer":"Failing"},{"question":"What is the riddle about?","options":["Finding courage","The clock's gears","The tower's history","A hidden treasure"],"correct_answer":"Finding courage"},{"question":"What creature do they encounter at the top of the staircase?","options":["A ghost","A guardian","A robot","A clockmaker"],"correct_answer":"A guardian"},{"question":"What does the figure challenge them to confront?","options":["Their fears","The clock","Each other","Time itself"],"correct_answer":"Their fears"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_16_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_16_ch3_img1.png","plot_16_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":725,"reading_level":"Builder"}
