   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_17_11_14","title":"Escape from Dragon\u2019s Cave","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the echo of the trap\u2019s clang faded into the cavern\u2019s depths, Emma and Jake stood frozen, hearts pounding in unison. The cave, once enchanting with its shimmering gems, now felt like a dark, ominous prison. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Jake whispered, his eyes wide as saucers. \n\nEmma narrowed her gaze, trying to listen over the frantic thumping of their hearts. \u201cYeah, we need to move\u2014now!\u201d \n\nThey dashed deeper into the cave, the walls glistening like stars in a night sky. Each step felt heavier as the reality of their situation pressed down on them. What if the dragon returned before they found a way out? \n\nSuddenly, they stumbled upon a clearing where a massive stone statue of a dragon loomed, its eyes sparkling with the same gems that adorned the walls. \u201cLook at this! It\u2019s beautiful!\u201d Jake exclaimed, momentarily distracted.\n\n\u201cBeautiful doesn\u2019t help us escape,\u201d Emma said, her voice sharp. \u201cWe need to focus!\u201d \n\nJust then, the ground rumbled beneath their feet, sending a shiver up Emma\u2019s spine. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Jake asked, his voice barely above a whisper. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep moving. If we get caught\u2014\u201d \n\nThey hadn\u2019t taken more than a few steps when Jake spotted something on the ground. \u201cWait! What\u2019s this?\u201d He picked up a small, glimmering stone, its surface shimmering like a tiny galaxy. \n\n\u201cPut it down!\u201d Emma insisted. \u201cIt could be a trap!\u201d\n\nBut Jake\u2019s curiosity had already grabbed him. \u201cNo, look! It\u2019s glowing. Maybe it\u2019s magic!\u201d \n\nEmma sighed, torn between her instinct to keep them safe and Jake\u2019s adventurous spirit. \u201cJust be careful with it. We can\u2019t afford to attract any more trouble.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWith the stone in hand, Jake glanced up at Emma, his eyes shining with excitement. \u201cWhat if this can help us? What if it\u2019s a key or something?\u201d\n\n\u201cOr it could alert the dragon,\u201d Emma replied, scanning the shadows that danced around them. \u201cWe don\u2019t have time for this!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a low growl echoed through the cave, vibrating through the walls. Both siblings froze. \u201cThat\u2019s not good,\u201d Jake muttered, his face paling.\n\n\u201cWhat do we do?\u201d Emma asked, her voice trembling slightly. \n\n\u201cRun!\u201d Jake shouted, and they sprinted away from the clearing, hearts racing. \n\nAs they fled through twisting corridors adorned with more sparkling gems, they heard the unmistakable sound of claws scraping against stone. \u201cIt\u2019s getting closer!\u201d Emma gasped, adrenaline fueling her speed. \n\n\u201cWe need to hide!\u201d Jake yelled, spotting a narrow crevice in the wall. They squeezed into the tight space just as the dragon\u2019s shadow loomed large in front of them. Emma held her breath, their bodies pressed together as they waited in silence.\n\nFrom their hiding spot, they watched as Drago, the dragon, entered the clearing. His scales shimmered like the jewels that surrounded him, and his golden eyes scanned the area. \u201cWhere are you, intruders?\u201d his deep voice rumbled, sending a chill down Emma\u2019s spine. \n\nEmma exchanged a glance with Jake, who looked more frightened than ever. \u201cWhat if he finds us?\u201d he whispered.\n\n\u201cWe have to be brave,\u201d Emma murmured, gripping his hand tightly. \u201cWe\u2019ll think of something. We always do.\u201d\n\nAs they watched Drago\u2019s massive form, Emma couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that there was more to the dragon than met the eye. But figuring that out meant surviving this encounter first.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWhat if we can\u2019t escape?\u201d Jake whimpered, tears glistening in his eyes. \n\nEmma squeezed her brother\u2019s hand reassuringly. \u201cWe will, I promise. But we need to stay quiet and think.\u201d \n\nJust then, the glimmering stone in Jake\u2019s hand began to pulse with a soft light, illuminating their hiding place. They exchanged panicked looks. \u201cUh-oh,\u201d Jake said, \u201cI think it\u2019s trying to help\u2026\u201d\n\nAs the light brightened, Emma realized that their next move would be crucial. They had to outsmart the dragon before it was too late.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Emma and Jake find that might help them escape?","options":["A map","A glowing stone","A magical creature","A key"],"correct_answer":"A glowing stone"},{"question":"How does Emma react to Jake\u2019s discovery of the stone?","options":["She is excited","She is angry","She is cautious","She ignores him"],"correct_answer":"She is cautious"},{"question":"What sound indicates that the dragon is nearby?","options":["A roar","A growl","A hiss","A flap"],"correct_answer":"A growl"},{"question":"What is Drago doing when Emma and Jake hide?","options":["Sleeping","Flying","Scouring the area","Eating"],"correct_answer":"Scouring the area"},{"question":"What does Emma promise Jake?","options":["That they will find treasure","That they will escape","That they will meet the dragon","That they will go home"],"correct_answer":"That they will escape"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_17_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_17_ch2_img1.png","plot_17_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":665,"reading_level":"Builder"}
