   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_17_11_14","title":"Escape from Dragon\u2019s Cave","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The cave was alive with shimmering lights and the sound of distant dripping water, echoing like whispers of long-lost treasures. Emma and Jake stood at the edge of an enormous cavern, the glowing stone clutched tightly in Emma's hand. She glanced at her brother, his eyes wide with a mix of fear and excitement. \u201cThis is it, Jake. We can\u2019t turn back now,\u201d she said, her voice steady but her heart racing.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe cave's walls sparkled with an array of colorful gems, lighting their path like a starry night sky. But it was the feeling of dread that hung in the air that sent shivers down their spines. They had to find a way out before Drago returned. \u201cWhat if he comes back and finds us?\u201d Jake whispered, glancing over his shoulder as if expecting the dragon to burst through the shadows.\n\nEmma's determination flickered like the light from the glowing stone. \u201cWe\u2019ll think of something. We have to. Just remember, he\u2019s not here to hurt us... I think.\u201d As they moved deeper into the cave, they encountered a series of strange symbols etched into the walls. Each symbol seemed to pulse with magic, and Emma felt a strange energy radiating from them.\n\n\u201cThis one looks like a map!\u201d Jake pointed excitedly, tracing the lines with his finger. \u201cI think it shows a path out of here.\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s follow it,\u201d Emma said, glancing around anxiously. They stepped forward, but as they did, the ground beneath them trembled. Suddenly, a trapdoor swung open beneath Jake\u2019s feet! He gasped and scrambled to grab hold of the edge, Emma lunging forward to help him.\n\n\u201cHang on!\u201d Emma shouted, her heart pounding as she pulled him back up just in time. They landed in a heap on the ground, breathless and wide-eyed. \u201cThat was too close,\u201d Jake said, trying to catch his breath.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m starting to think this cave has a mind of its own,\u201d Emma replied, brushing dirt from her clothes. \u201cBut look! The map continues this way.\u201d \n\nTaking deep breaths to steady themselves, they pressed on, following the glowing symbols. As they moved, Jake started to feel a flicker of confidence. \u201cEmma, I think I can do this. We can do this!\u201d he said, a spark of hope igniting in his voice.\n\nSuddenly, a loud roar echoed through the cave, silencing their conversation. The air grew thick with tension as they both froze. \u201cThat\u2019s Drago!\u201d Emma exclaimed. \u201cWe don\u2019t have much time!\u201d\n\nThey rushed forward, adrenaline pumping as they navigated through the winding paths of the cave. Each corner they turned revealed more traps and illusions\u2014a shifting wall of shadows here, a sudden burst of colorful mist there. Yet with every challenge, Jake\u2019s imagination sparked ideas. \u201cWhat if we use the mist to hide?\u201d he suggested, glancing back nervously towards the sound of the dragon.\n\n\u201cThat could work!\u201d Emma replied, her heart racing but her spirit soaring. They ducked behind a rock formation just as Drago\u2019s massive shadow passed above them, casting an ominous darkness over the cave. \u201cWe have to keep moving,\u201d she breathed, taking Jake\u2019s hand.\n\nAs they crept forward, they found themselves in a small chamber, the walls adorned with a tapestry of faintly glowing scenes depicting a dragon, a treasure, and a pair of siblings. Emma felt a connection to the story woven in front of them. \u201cLook, Jake! This tapestry\u2026 it shows a dragon protecting something valuable. Maybe Drago isn\u2019t the villain after all!\u201d\n\nJake nodded, wide-eyed. \u201cMaybe he just wants a friend!\u201d\n\nAs they pondered this revelation, they spotted an exit shimmering in the distance. Hope swelled in their hearts. \u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Emma shouted, bolting toward the light. Together, they raced forward, their laughter echoing through the cave. \n\nBut as they reached the entrance, a loud crash sounded behind them. They turned to see Drago emerging from the shadows, his eyes glimmering with curiosity rather than rage. Emma and Jake exchanged glances, and in that moment, they realized that their adventure was just beginning.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Jake discover on the wall of the cave?","options":["A glowing stone","A map","A treasure chest","A dragon's lair"],"correct_answer":"A map"},{"question":"How does Emma feel about Drago at the end of the chapter?","options":["She fears him","She wants to be his friend","She thinks he is dangerous","She wants to escape"],"correct_answer":"She wants to be his friend"},{"question":"What dangerous event occurs while Jake and Emma are exploring?","options":["They find treasure","They trigger a trapdoor","They meet magical creatures","They find an exit"],"correct_answer":"They trigger a trapdoor"},{"question":"What do Emma and Jake decide to do when they hear Drago's roar?","options":["Hide","Run away","Fight him","Call for help"],"correct_answer":"Hide"},{"question":"What is the atmosphere of the cave described as?","options":["Dark and spooky","Lively and colorful","Boring and plain","Hot and uncomfortable"],"correct_answer":"Lively and colorful"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_17_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_17_ch4_img1.png","plot_17_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":684,"reading_level":"Builder"}
