   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_18_11_14","title":"The Abandoned Amusement Park","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: The Maze of Mirrors\n\nAs soon as the door slammed shut behind them, a chill swept over the group. The musty air of the funhouse clung to their skin like a damp blanket, and all around them, the faint sounds of laughter echoed, twisting into a haunting melody. Sara stepped forward, her heart racing but her determination stronger. \"We can do this, guys. Just stick together.\"\n\nBen, his skepticism bubbling just beneath the surface, crossed his arms. \"Are we really going to explore a place that could have ghosts lurking in every corner?\" He glanced nervously at the warped mirrors lining the walls, each reflecting a distorted version of his friends. \"This is just a bunch of old junk.\"\n\n\"Come on, Ben!\" Lily said, her eyes gleaming with excitement. \"Think of it as a puzzle. If we stick together, we can find our way out. Besides, it\u2019s just an old park\u2014there\u2019s nothing to be afraid of!\" She approached a mirror, peering into it as if it might reveal a hidden clue.\n\nTom, always ready with a joke, flexed his arms dramatically and grinned. \"I\u2019m not scared of a few ghosts. I\u2019m more worried about getting lost in here and ending up at the nearest candy shop instead!\" He wiggled his fingers playfully, trying to lighten the mood.\n\nJust then, a loud creak echoed through the funhouse, sending shivers racing down Sara\u2019s spine. \"Did you hear that?\" she whispered, her voice trembling slightly. The group fell silent, straining to listen. The silence was thick, as if the funhouse itself was holding its breath.\n\nThen, without warning, the floor beneath them shifted. The walls seemed to close in, and the mirrors flickered like candle flames. The cheerful laughter morphed into a sinister cackle, bouncing around the enclosed space. \"What is happening?!\" Ben shouted, panicking.\n\nBefore they could react, the mirrors began to swirl, creating a dizzying effect. The reflections of Sara and her friends rippled like water, distorting their faces into grotesque figures. \"Stay close!\" Sara commanded, grabbing Ben's arm. Lily was a step ahead, moving toward the only apparent exit\u2014a narrow hallway that appeared at the end of the room.\n\nAs they raced toward it, Tom stumbled, his foot catching on a loose floorboard. \"Whoa!\" he yelped, flailing his arms. The laughter echoed louder, almost mocking their fear. Sara reached back just in time to catch him, pulling him upright before he fell into a pile of broken mirrors.\n\n\"Thanks!\" Tom said, his face pale but cracking a smile. \"Thought I was going to become a ghost myself!\"\n\nLily's eyes sparkled with determination as she pointed down the hallway. \"We\u2019ve got to keep moving! It looks like there's a way out!\" But as they moved closer, the hallway began to shift as well, twisting like a serpent, adding an unexpected layer of difficulty to their escape.\n\nJust then, Sara hesitated, her heart pounding. \"Wait, what if we get lost? What if\u2014\"\n\nSuddenly, the laughter returned, echoing around them. \"Face your fears!\" it taunted. It was as if the funhouse was alive, challenging each of them to confront their deepest anxieties. Sara felt a shiver run down her spine. \"We can\u2019t let it win!\" she yelled back defiantly.\n\nBen took a deep breath, finally releasing his doubts. \"Alright, let\u2019s do this together. On three, we run!\" They formed a tight circle, each friend holding on to a part of the next, ready to charge down the winding hallway.\n\n\"One, two, three!\" Sara shouted, and together they dashed into the swirling darkness, their hearts pounding with fear and exhilaration as the funhouse closed in around them.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[The image depicts the four friends standing in the eerie funhouse, surrounded by warped mirrors. Sara is leading the group confidently, with Ben looking skeptical, Lily examining the mirrors curiously, and Tom striking a comical pose to lighten the mood. The background shows the dimly lit, chaotic atmosphere of the funhouse, with distorted reflections of their faces.]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n[The image captures the moment when the floor shifts beneath their feet. The friends are in mid-action, with expressions of surprise and determination. The mirrors around them reflect their distorted images, creating a sense of disorientation. The eerie laughter echoes in the background, enhancing the suspenseful atmosphere.]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do the friends encounter that makes them feel trapped?","options":["A locked door","Shifting mirrors","A ghost","A maze"],"correct_answer":"Shifting mirrors"},{"question":"Who is the most skeptical about exploring the funhouse?","options":["Sara","Ben","Lily","Tom"],"correct_answer":"Ben"},{"question":"What challenge do the friends face as they move through the funhouse?","options":["Finding a way out","Overcoming their fears","Building a bridge","Rescuing someone"],"correct_answer":"Overcoming their fears"},{"question":"What does Tom do to lighten the mood?","options":["Tells a joke","Starts singing","Makes funny faces","Acts brave"],"correct_answer":"Tells a joke"},{"question":"What do the friends decide to do when faced with a challenge in the funhouse?","options":["Split up","Run together","Wait for help","Go back"],"correct_answer":"Run together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_18_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_18_ch2_img1.png","plot_18_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":722,"reading_level":"Builder"}
