   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_18_11_14","title":"The Abandoned Amusement Park","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The funhouse loomed before them, its twisted entrance a gaping mouth that seemed to swallow the light. Sara led the way, her heart racing with excitement, while Ben trailed behind, glancing nervously at the peeling paint and broken mirrors. \u201cI can\u2019t believe we actually came in here,\u201d he muttered, hands shoved deep into his pockets.\n\n\u201cCome on, Ben! Where\u2019s your sense of adventure?\u201d Tom chuckled, trying to lighten the mood. \u201cBesides, it\u2019s just a bunch of old mirrors and dusty floorboards. What\u2019s the worst that could happen?\u201d\n\n\u201cFamous last words,\u201d Ben grumbled, but the corners of his mouth turned up slightly. Lily was already peering into one of the warped mirrors, her eyes wide with curiosity. \u201cLook at this one! It\u2019s like I\u2019m in a funhouse of weirdness!\u201d she exclaimed, her voice echoing slightly in the empty space.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they stepped deeper inside, the atmosphere shifted, the air growing thick and heavy, almost as if the funhouse was alive. The walls began to shimmer, reflecting their faces in strange, exaggerated ways. Sara felt a shiver travel down her spine. \u201cGuys, we need to stick together,\u201d she said, trying to sound brave even though uncertainty gnawed at her.\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed from one of the adjoining rooms, and they all jumped. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Tom whispered, his previous bravado gone. \u201cIt\u2019s probably just the wind,\u201d Ben suggested, but his tone lacked confidence. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out,\u201d Sara declared, her voice firm. \u201cWe can\u2019t just sit here. We have to find a way out.\u201d \n\nWith hesitant footsteps, they approached the source of the noise. As they rounded the corner, they stumbled into a room filled with spinning wheels and flashing lights, but something was off. The colors swirled together, creating an overwhelming spectacle that made Lily's head spin. \u201cThis doesn\u2019t feel right,\u201d she said, pressing her hand to her forehead.\n\n\u201cMaybe we should turn back,\u201d Ben suggested, a hint of panic creeping into his voice. Just then, the room began to shift again, the walls bending and warping like a funhouse mirage. \n\n\u201cRun!\u201d shouted Sara, as the floor beneath them started to tilt, threatening to throw them off balance. They sprinted toward the exit, but as they reached it, the doorway vanished, replaced by a solid wall. \u201cNo! We\u2019re trapped!\u201d Tom shouted, his playful demeanor replaced by fear.\n\nSara took a deep breath, forcing her mind to focus. \u201cWe need to remember the way we came in. There must be a pattern to this madness,\u201d she said, her voice strong despite the fluttering in her stomach. Just then, a glimmer caught her eye. \u201cLook! There\u2019s something written on the wall!\u201d \n\nThey gathered around, deciphering the faint, glowing letters. \u201cTo escape the shifting walls, face your fears and heed the call,\u201d Sara read aloud, her voice echoing in the eerie silence. \u201cWhat does that even mean?\u201d Ben asked, anxiety evident in his eyes.\n\nAs they stood there, contemplating the message, the walls began to pulse ominously, and the lights flickered. Lily\u2019s eyes widened with realization. \u201cIt\u2019s about us! We have to confront our fears to find our way out!\u201d \n\n\u201cNo way! I don\u2019t want to face my fears!\u201d Tom protested, his voice shaking. \n\nBut before they could argue, the walls surged forward, and the room shifted once more, trapping them in darkness. \u201cWe have to decide now!\u201d Sara said urgently. \u201cWe can\u2019t let fear win!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nFear and determination battled within each of them as they prepared to confront whatever lay ahead. They needed to face their challenges and work together. \u201cLet\u2019s do this!\u201d Sara commanded, feeling the weight of leadership on her shoulders.\n\nBut just as they formed a plan, a low growl echoed through the darkness, and the floor trembled beneath them. Something was lurking in the shadows, ready to test their courage.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What mysterious message do the characters find on the wall?","options":["To escape, be brave and follow the path","Face your fears and heed the call","Stay calm and find the hidden door","Help each other to find the exit"],"correct_answer":"Face your fears and heed the call"},{"question":"What initially causes the characters to panic in the funhouse?","options":["A loud crash","A flickering light","A strange smell","A sudden darkness"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash"},{"question":"Who suggests they should check out the source of the noise?","options":["Lily","Tom","Ben","Sara"],"correct_answer":"Sara"},{"question":"How do the walls of the funhouse react as the characters move through it?","options":["They stay still","They shift and warp","They glow brightly","They break apart"],"correct_answer":"They shift and warp"},{"question":"What does Tom initially feel about facing his fears?","options":["Excited","Indifferent","Reluctant","Eager"],"correct_answer":"Reluctant"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_18_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_18_ch3_img1.png","plot_18_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":654,"reading_level":"Builder"}
