   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_19_7_10","title":"The Secret of the Ancient Library","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Leo and Zoe stood in the magical library, their eyes wide with wonder. Rows of books sparkled like stars. \u201cLook at all these stories!\u201d Zoe exclaimed, bouncing on her toes. \n\n\u201cWhich one should we explore first?\u201d Leo asked, curious.\n\nBefore Zoe could answer, an old librarian appeared. She wore round glasses and a warm smile. \u201cWelcome, young adventurers!\u201d she said. \u201cI\u2019m Ms. Page. You must solve puzzles to return home. Time is running out!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat kind of puzzles?\u201d Leo asked nervously.\n\n\u201cLiterary puzzles,\u201d Ms. Page replied. \u201cEach story has a challenge. Complete them to unlock the door back to your world.\u201d She pointed to a large, glowing book at the center of the library. \n\nZoe stepped closer. \u201cLet\u2019s start there!\u201d She grabbed Leo\u2019s hand and raced toward the book. As they opened it, colorful words swirled around them. Suddenly, they found themselves in an enchanted forest, filled with towering trees and singing birds. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cWow! We\u2019re inside a book!\u201d Leo shouted, spinning around. \n\n\u201cBut how do we find the puzzle?\u201d Zoe asked, her eyes darting around. \n\nJust then, a friendly squirrel appeared. \u201cTo find the puzzle, you must listen to the trees,\u201d the squirrel chattered. \u201cThey will tell you a secret!\u201d\n\nLeo and Zoe exchanged glances. \u201cLet\u2019s listen!\u201d they said together. \n\nThey closed their eyes and focused. The trees began to whisper softly. \u201cIn the forest, there lies a key. Find the heart of the old oak tree!\u201d \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Zoe asked, her voice full of excitement. \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Leo replied, his mind racing. \u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d\n\nThey rushed through the forest. Suddenly, they heard a loud rustling. A big shadow loomed overhead. \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Zoe whispered, her heart racing. \n\n\u201cOnly one way to find out!\u201d Leo said bravely. \n\nThey peeked around a tree. A giant talking troll sat on a rock, scratching his head. \u201cWho\u2019s stealing my treasure?\u201d he grumbled. \n\n\u201cOh no!\u201d Zoe gasped. \u201cWe need to get past him!\u201d\n\n\u201cBut how?\u201d Leo wondered. \n\nJust then, the squirrel appeared again. \u201cYou must solve his riddle!\u201d it squeaked. \n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s the riddle?\u201d they both asked.\n\nThe troll grinned. \u201cI am tall when I\u2019m young and short when I\u2019m old. What am I?\u201d \n\n\u201cUgh! Think, Leo!\u201d Zoe urged. \n\nLeo thought hard. \u201cI know! It\u2019s a candle!\u201d\n\nThe troll laughed. \u201cVery clever! You may pass!\u201d \n\nLeo and Zoe cheered. \u201cWe\u2019re getting closer to the old oak!\u201d Zoe said. \n\nBut just as they turned to run, the ground shook. \u201cOh no! A storm is coming!\u201d Leo shouted. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey had to hurry! Would they find the old oak tree before it was too late?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who guides Leo and Zoe in the magical library?","options":["A wise owl","Ms. Page","A talking squirrel","The troll"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Page"},{"question":"What must Leo and Zoe solve to find their way home?","options":["A treasure map","Literary puzzles","A riddle from a troll","A secret code"],"correct_answer":"Literary puzzles"},{"question":"What kind of environment do Leo and Zoe enter first?","options":["A castle","An enchanted forest","A spaceship","A dragon's cave"],"correct_answer":"An enchanted forest"},{"question":"What does the troll want to know?","options":["Who stole his treasure","Where the library is","How to get home","What time it is"],"correct_answer":"Who stole his treasure"},{"question":"What is the answer to the troll's riddle?","options":["A tree","A shadow","A candle","A mountain"],"correct_answer":"A candle"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_19_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_19_ch2_img1.png","plot_19_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":445,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
