   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_19_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Ancient Library","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As Leo and Zoe stepped through the hidden door, the air shimmered around them like a warm summer breeze. The library had transformed into a breathtaking landscape, with towering trees that glimmered with golden leaves and books floating like clouds in a brilliant blue sky. Leo's eyes widened, taking in the wonder. \"This... is amazing!\" he exclaimed, his voice echoing off the verdant canopy.\n\n\"Where do you think we are?\" Zoe asked, bouncing on her toes, excitement sparkling in her eyes. \"It feels like we\u2019ve stepped into a storybook!\"\n\nBefore Leo could respond, a figure emerged from behind a gigantic oak tree. It was the wise librarian they had met earlier, her spectacles perched precariously on her nose, a knowing smile spreading across her face. \"Welcome back, young adventurers! You\u2019ve entered the Realm of Stories, but time is a tricky thing here. You must solve the riddles of the stories to navigate your way back.\"\n\nLeo nodded, trying to mask the flutter of uncertainty in his stomach. \"What kind of riddles?\"\n\n\"The kind that will test not only your knowledge of the tales but also your courage,\" she said cryptically, then gestured toward a path winding deeper into the enchanted forest. \"Follow the markers; they will lead you to your first challenge.\"\n\nAs they walked, the whispers of the stories floated through the air, intertwining with the rustling leaves. Zoe pointed eagerly at a glowing sign that read, \"The Forest of Fables.\" \"Leo, this is where we\u2019ll find the first riddle! I can almost hear the characters calling us!\"\n\nThey stepped into the forest, where trees twisted into fantastical shapes and colorful flowers bloomed, each petal shimmering like a page from a book. Suddenly, a shadow darted across their path, and Leo felt a chill run down his spine. \"Did you see that?\" he asked, his voice barely above a whisper.\n\nZoe nodded, her eyes wide. \"What do you think it was?\"\n\nBefore Leo could respond, the shadow materialized into a tiny, mischievous creature with bright eyes and a wide grin. \"Welcome, welcome! I am Wisp, the guardian of this forest! To pass through, you must answer my riddle!\" \n\nLeo felt a mix of apprehension and curiosity. \"What\u2019s the riddle?\"\n\nWisp clapped his tiny hands, and a shimmering scroll appeared in the air. \"Here it goes! 'I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with the wind. What am I?'\"\n\nThe words echoed around them, and Leo\u2019s heart raced. He could feel the weight of the challenge pressing down. \"It\u2019s... it\u2019s something to do with sound, right?\" Zoe offered, her brow furrowed in concentration.\n\nAs they debated, the trees seemed to lean in, their branches straining to hear. The pressure of time loomed over them like storm clouds, and Leo knew they had to hurry. \u201cWait! I remember reading something about echoes!\u201d Leo exclaimed. \u201cThat\u2019s it! The answer is an echo!\u201d\n\nWisp\u2019s eyes sparkled with intrigue. \"Is that your final answer?\" he asked, his grin stretching wider.\n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Leo declared, his heart pounding. \n\nThe creature's laughter filled the air. \"Correct! But be warned, your journey has only just begun.\" With a dramatic flourish, Wisp waved his hand, and a path opened before them, leading to a shimmering portal. \n\nBut just as they stepped forward, the ground beneath them trembled. \"What now?\" Zoe gasped, grabbing Leo's arm as the trees around them began to sway ominously.\n\n\u201cSomething isn\u2019t right,\u201d Leo murmured, feeling a surge of fear. \u201cWe need to keep moving!\u201d\n\nWith a determined nod, they took off down the path, their hearts racing. The forest began to shift around them, the stories they loved twisting and turning into something darker. What awaited them on the other side of the portal felt much more dangerous than they\u2019d anticipated.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the name of the guardian in the Forest of Fables?","options":["Wisp","Leo","Zoe","The Librarian"],"correct_answer":"Wisp"},{"question":"What riddle does Wisp ask Leo and Zoe?","options":["What has hands but cannot clap?","I speak without a mouth and hear without ears.","What can run but never walks?","I have keys but open no locks."],"correct_answer":"I speak without a mouth and hear without ears."},{"question":"How do Leo and Zoe feel when they first enter the Realm of Stories?","options":["Scared","Excited","Bored","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What does Leo remember to solve Wisp's riddle?","options":["A story about trees","A fact about echoes","A poem he read","A song he heard"],"correct_answer":"A fact about echoes"},{"question":"What happens at the end of the chapter?","options":["They find a way home","The ground trembles","They meet a dragon","They fall asleep"],"correct_answer":"The ground trembles"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_19_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_19_ch2_img1.png","plot_19_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":652,"reading_level":"Builder"}
