   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_19_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Ancient Library","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The air in the Forest of Fables started to thicken with anticipation, as Leo and Zoe stepped deeper into the magical woods. Sunlight filtered through the leaves, casting enchanting patterns on the forest floor. The whispers of stories long forgotten beckoned them forward. \"This place is amazing!\" Zoe exclaimed, her eyes sparkling with excitement. Leo, still processing their previous encounter with Wisp, nodded in agreement, though his heart raced with the weight of their mission.\n\nJust as they wandered further, the trees began to shift, their trunks twisting and bending as if alive. \"We need to solve the next riddle before time runs out,\" Leo reminded, glancing at the large clock face that hovered in the air above them, ticking steadily. Each tick echoed like a drum, reminding them that the library was closing soon.\n\nSuddenly, a loud rustling sound startled them. Out from behind a giant fern leaped a character Leo recognized immediately\u2014a mischievous wolf from one of his favorite fairy tales! Its fur bristled, and eyes glinted with mischief. \u201cI hear you\u2019re looking for a riddle,\u201d the wolf grinned, showing sharp teeth. \u201cBut beware, young adventurers! Not all riddles are as they seem.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\"Wait! We don't want any trouble!\" Zoe exclaimed, stepping protectively in front of Leo. The wolf laughed, a sound echoing hauntingly through the forest. \u201cNo trouble here, just a game! Solve my riddle, and you may continue on your way. Fail, and\u2026\u201d The wolf's smile faded slightly, replaced by a shadow of something darker. \u201cYou\u2019ll become part of my story.\u201d\n\nLeo felt his palms sweat. \u201cWhat\u2019s the riddle?\u201d he asked, trying to sound braver than he felt. The wolf circled them, eyes gleaming with mischief. \u201cHere it is: I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with the wind. What am I?\u201d\n\nZoe furrowed her brow, tapping her fingers against her jeans. \u201cWe can\u2019t let him trick us. Think, Leo!\u201d The clock ticked louder in his ears, drowning out the sounds of the forest. Leo\u2019s mind raced through their recent adventures. \u201cAn echo!\u201d he shouted suddenly.\n\nThe wolf stopped, surprised. \u201cCorrect, clever boy! But beware\u2014an echo can also lead you astray.\u201d He vanished into the underbrush, leaving behind a shimmering path that forked into two directions. \u201cWhich way should we go?\u201d Zoe asked, glancing anxiously from one path to the other.\n\nLeo pointed toward the right path, where the light seemed to dance with energy. \u201cThat one feels right,\u201d he said. But as they stepped forward, a sudden shudder rippled through the ground. The trees turned into shadows, and thick mist enveloped them. \u201cLeo! What\u2019s happening?\u201d Zoe screamed, but her voice seemed to get lost in the swirling fog.\n\nThen, from the depths of the mist, shapes began to materialize\u2014figures from stories they knew well, each bearing a haunting expression. They were trapped, just like Leo and Zoe. \u201cWe need to escape!\u201d Leo shouted, panic rising in his chest. Zoe grasped his arm tightly. \u201cWhat do we do?\u201d\n\nAs the figures drew closer, Leo noticed one of them\u2014an old character he had read about, the wise Owl from a beloved fable. \u201cTo leave this place, you must face your fears,\u201d the Owl hooted, eyes piercing through the fog. \u201cOnly then will you find your way back.\u201d\n\nLeo\u2019s heart sank. \u201cFace our fears? But what does that mean?\u201d he wondered, looking at Zoe, whose face was pale with worry. Just then, the mist began to swirl furiously, pulling them down a dark path. \u201cWe don\u2019t have time to think!\u201d Zoe yelled, and Leo nodded, adrenaline pumping through his veins as they ran, not knowing what awaited them ahead.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What creature do Leo and Zoe encounter in the Forest of Fables?","options":["A dragon","A wolf","A fairy","A giant"],"correct_answer":"A wolf"},{"question":"What riddle does the wolf present to Leo and Zoe?","options":["What has keys but can't open locks?","What comes once in a minute, twice in a moment, but never in a thousand years?","I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. What am I?","What has to be broken before you can use it?"],"correct_answer":"I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. What am I?"},{"question":"What do Leo and Zoe need to do to escape the library?","options":["Solve literary puzzles","Face their fears","Find hidden treasures","Make new friends"],"correct_answer":"Face their fears"},{"question":"What happens when they solve the wolf's riddle?","options":["They receive a treasure","They find a hidden door","The wolf disappears","They are granted special powers"],"correct_answer":"The wolf disappears"},{"question":"What do Leo and Zoe see as they are pulled into the mist?","options":["Treasure chests","Figures from stories","A castle","A library"],"correct_answer":"Figures from stories"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_19_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_19_ch3_img1.png","plot_19_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":627,"reading_level":"Builder"}
