   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_20_11_14","title":"Rescue Mission: The Island of Shadows","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The storm raged like a wild beast, thrashing against the small boat that Sophie, Ethan, Chloe, and Kai had boarded for their weekend adventure. Waves crashed against the hull, sending sprays of saltwater into the air. A sharp crack of lightning illuminated the dark sky, revealing the terrified faces of the friends huddled together. \u201cWe need to head back!\u201d Ethan shouted over the roar of the wind, his voice shaky. \n\n\u201cJust a little further!\u201d Sophie insisted, gripping the steering wheel tightly. \u201cWe\u2019re almost to the island! We can make it!\u201d \n\n\u201cLook out!\u201d Chloe shrieked as another wave slammed into the boat, tipping it sideways. With a thunderous crash, the boat spun and capsized, sending the friends tumbling into the churning sea.\n\nWhen Sophie finally gasped for air and swam to the surface, she found herself alone. Panic coursed through her. \u201cEthan? Chloe? Kai?\u201d she called, her voice trembling. Just as despair began to settle in, she spotted them struggling to reach the shore of a nearby island. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey crawled onto the sand, gasping for breath. The island was lush and vibrant, with palm trees swaying gently in the breeze despite the remnants of the storm. \u201cIs everyone okay?\u201d Sophie asked, brushing sand from her hair. \n\n\u201cI think so,\u201d Kai replied, propping himself up on his elbows. \u201cBut where are we?\u201d \n\n\u201cLooks like we\u2019re stuck here for now,\u201d Ethan said, glancing at the darkening sky. \u201cWhat do we do next?\u201d\n\nChloe stood, her eyes wide with wonder. \u201cLook at all the plants! I\u2019ve never seen anything like this!\u201d She wandered a few steps, fingers brushing against the strange foliage. \u201cThis place is amazing!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s amazing is that we\u2019re alive,\u201d Ethan said, standing up and surveying their surroundings. \u201cBut we need to find a way off this island before it gets dark. There\u2019s no telling what else is out there.\u201d\n\nAs the sun dipped behind the trees, casting eerie shadows across the ground, Sophie felt a chill creep up her spine. \u201cLet\u2019s stick together,\u201d she urged, trying to mask her fear. \u201cIf we explore, maybe we can find a way to signal for help.\u201d\n\nThe friends formed a loose circle, their faces illuminated by the fading light. As they ventured deeper into the island, the air grew thick with the sounds of rustling leaves and whispers of the wind. Suddenly, a low growl echoed from the shadows, freezing them in place. \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Chloe whispered, eyes wide with fright. \n\n\u201cShh!\u201d Kai hissed, his heart racing. \u201cDid you hear it?\u201d\n\nSophie felt a knot of dread twist in her stomach. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s just an animal\u2026 or maybe\u2026 something else.\u201d The shadows around them seemed to grow darker, as if alive and creeping closer. \n\nJust then, something darted past them, a shadow flickering between the trees. The friends jumped back, their breaths quickening. Ethan squinted into the darkness. \u201cWe need to move. Now!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe group dashed through the underbrush, branches snagging at their clothes. The growling came again, louder this time, sending a wave of adrenaline through them. They stumbled toward a clearing, searching for a way to escape the unseen terror. \n\nAs they burst into the open, the moonlight bathed the area in silvery glow, revealing ancient ruins that spiraled up toward the sky. \u201cLook!\u201d Sophie gasped, pointing at the crumbling stone structures. \u201cMaybe we can find shelter there.\u201d\n\n\u201cOr maybe it\u2019s where our pursuer lives,\u201d Kai countered, eyes darting back toward the dark forest. \u201cWe need to decide quickly!\u201d\n\nThe shadows loomed closer, and with every heartbeat, the urgency surged. Would they uncover the secrets of the island, or would they fall victim to the darkness that awaited them?\n\n---","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event causes the friends to end up on the island?","options":["A boat capsizing","A plane crash","A hiking accident","A camping trip gone wrong"],"correct_answer":"A boat capsizing"},{"question":"Which character is described as the determined explorer?","options":["Ethan","Chloe","Sophie","Kai"],"correct_answer":"Sophie"},{"question":"What do the friends hear that makes them feel scared?","options":["The sound of waves","A low growl","The thunder of the storm","Birds singing"],"correct_answer":"A low growl"},{"question":"Where do the friends decide to find shelter?","options":["In a cave","In the forest","In the ancient ruins","On the beach"],"correct_answer":"In the ancient ruins"},{"question":"What is the main feeling among the friends as they explore the island?","options":["Excitement","Boredom","Fear","Happiness"],"correct_answer":"Fear"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_20_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_20_ch1_img1.png","plot_20_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":622,"reading_level":"Builder"}
