   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_20_11_14","title":"Rescue Mission: The Island of Shadows","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The island loomed ahead, a vast expanse of greenery and mystery. Lush trees swayed gently in the warm breeze, their leaves glistening like emeralds under the sun. Sophie stood at the edge of a rocky cliff, the salty sea spray kissing her face as she gazed at the horizon. \u201cWe need a plan,\u201d she declared, her voice steady despite the uncertainty swirling inside her. \n\nEthan, ever the cautious planner, paced behind her, his brow furrowed. \u201cWe don\u2019t even know what dangers are lurking here. The creature from last night\u2014what if it comes back?\u201d \n\nChloe plucked a vibrant flower from a nearby bush, her eyes sparkling with curiosity. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s just a shadow of our fears. Look at this place! It\u2019s beautiful, not scary!\u201d \n\nKai, leaning against a palm tree, grinned. \u201cOr it could be hiding treasures! Let\u2019s see what else this island has to offer!\u201d \n\nJust then, a rustle in the nearby trees made them all freeze. Shadows danced along the ground, stretching unnaturally as if alive. Sophie\u2019s heart raced. \u201cDid anyone else hear that?\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they exchanged worried glances, a strange howl echoed from the depths of the forest, sending chills down their spines. \u201cWe should stick together,\u201d Ethan urged, his earlier confidence waning. \n\nThey moved cautiously toward the sound, the thick underbrush crunching beneath their feet. Chloe stepped ahead, her keen eye spotting a narrow path leading deeper into the woods. \u201cLook! It\u2019s a trail. We might find something useful!\u201d \n\nThe group hesitated, the air thick with tension. \u201cOr we could get lost,\u201d Ethan countered, glancing back at the cliffs where they had come from. \n\nKai stepped forward, determination lighting up his face. \u201cWe can\u2019t just stand here. Let\u2019s find out what\u2019s making that sound. It could lead us to safety\u2014or at least some answers.\u201d \n\nSophie nodded, her adventurous spirit igniting. \u201cAlright, let\u2019s do it. Together.\u201d \n\nThey ventured down the path, the foliage closing in around them. The sounds of the island muffled their footsteps, and the shadows grew longer, whispering secrets as they journeyed deeper. Suddenly, the ground beneath them shifted, revealing a hidden cave entrance, its mouth dark and foreboding. \n\n\u201cShould we go in?\u201d Chloe asked, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\nBefore anyone could respond, a gust of wind blew through the cave, sending a shiver down their spines. \u201cWe\u2019re running out of time, guys!\u201d Kai urged, glancing back at the dark trees. \u201cThat creature is still out there!\u201d \n\nWith a deep breath, Sophie stepped inside the cave, her heart pounding. The air was cool and damp, and the walls glistened with moisture. As they moved farther in, a soft glow illuminated the chamber. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Ethan exclaimed, pointing to ancient drawings carved into the stone. \u201cThese must tell the story of the island!\u201d \n\nBut just as they began to decipher the images, a low growl erupted from the shadows behind them, echoing ominously. The ground trembled as the dark creature emerged, its eyes glinting like shards of glass. \n\n\u201cRun!\u201d Sophie shouted, adrenaline surging. They dashed deeper into the cave, the sound of their hearts pounding in their ears. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they sprinted, the cave walls closed in, the shadows twisting around them like phantoms. Sophie turned to see the creature gaining on them, its breath hot and heavy. \u201cWe can\u2019t let it catch us!\u201d \n\nThey raced to an opening at the far end of the cave, but the shadows were relentless. Just when they thought they\u2019d found an escape, Sophie spotted something glimmering on the ground\u2014a strange artifact that pulsed with light. \n\nShould they stop to grab it or keep running? The decision weighed heavily on them as the creature lunged closer, ready to strike.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do the friends discover inside the cave?","options":["A treasure chest","Ancient drawings","A hidden village","A magical creature"],"correct_answer":"Ancient drawings"},{"question":"What does Kai suggest they do when they hear the creature?","options":["Hide in the cave","Run deeper into the cave","Climb a tree","Stay where they are"],"correct_answer":"Run deeper into the cave"},{"question":"Why does Ethan hesitate as they approach the cave?","options":["He is afraid of the dark","He's worried about getting lost","He thinks they should go back","He doesn't like caves"],"correct_answer":"He's worried about getting lost"},{"question":"What is the artifact that Sophie sees in the cave?","options":["A weapon","A glowing treasure","A magical map","An ancient scroll"],"correct_answer":"A glowing treasure"},{"question":"What emotion does Sophie feel when they encounter the creature?","options":["Excitement","Fear","Joy","Confusion"],"correct_answer":"Fear"}]},"images":null,"word_count":629,"reading_level":"Builder"}
