   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_20_11_14","title":"Rescue Mission: The Island of Shadows","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the sun crept higher in the sky, casting dappled patterns of light through the lush leaves, Sophie gathered her friends near the ancient stone altar they had discovered the day before. The air was thick with the sweet scent of blooming flowers and the distant call of exotic birds. \"We need a plan,\" she said, her eyes glimmering with determination. \n\nEthan, ever the cautious planner, bit his lip as he surveyed their surroundings. \"What about using the drawings from the cave? They might tell us how to get off this island,\" he suggested, his voice steady but laced with uncertainty. \n\nChloe plucked a leaf from a nearby fern, running her fingers over its edges. \"But what if the creature is drawn to the drawings? We can't risk getting caught,\" she cautioned, her brow furrowing. \n\nKai, bouncing on his heels, leaned closer to Sophie. \"We can't just sit here! Maybe the altar is a clue. It looks like it was used for something important.\" His excitement was infectious, but Sophie couldn\u2019t help but feel a knot of worry tighten in her stomach.\n\n\u201cOkay, let\u2019s check out the altar,\u201d Sophie decided, hoping that her confidence would lift the group. They moved closer, the stones worn and weathered, whispering secrets of a time long past. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they examined the altar, Chloe noticed something glinting in the sunlight. \u201cLook!\u201d She pointed to the ground, where a small, circular object lay half-buried in the sand. Ethan crouched down and brushed the dirt away, revealing an old compass, its needle spinning wildly. \n\n\u201cThis could help us find our way,\u201d he declared, excitement bubbling in his voice. \u201cBut it\u2019s broken. I don\u2019t know which direction is which.\u201d \n\nJust then, the shadows around them deepened, and a chilling wind swept through the clearing. Kai\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cWe need to hurry! The creature could be close!\u201d \n\nWith a sudden burst of urgency, they began to circle the altar, searching for any more clues. As they moved, Sophie felt the hairs on the back of her neck stand up. She glanced back toward the forest, half-expecting to see the dark shape looming behind the trees. \n\n\u201cI think I saw something!\u201d Chloe exclaimed, pointing toward the underbrush. Before she could say more, a rustling sound echoed through the trees, and the four friends froze. \n\n\u201cWhat if it\u2019s the creature?\u201d Ethan whispered, his voice shaking. \n\n\u201cWe have to stick together,\u201d Sophie urged, her heart racing. They all nodded, forming a tight circle around the altar. Suddenly, a figure darted out from the shadows\u2014a small monkey, its wide eyes sparkling with mischief. \n\nThey all laughed, releasing the tension that had gripped them. \u201cSee? Nothing to worry about,\u201d Kai said, though the fear lingered in his eyes. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep searching,\u201d Sophie said, her voice firm again. \u201cWe\u2019ve come this far. We can\u2019t turn back now.\u201d \n\nAs they continued their exploration, hope blossomed within the group. They were learning to rely on one another, to trust their instincts, and to face the unknown together. \n\nBut as they moved deeper into the forest, shadows danced just beyond their sight, reminding them that danger was always lurking. \n\nThey found another ancient carving on a tree trunk, depicting a boat sailing away from the island. \u201cMaybe this is a map!\u201d Chloe exclaimed, her voice filled with wonder. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nEthan traced the carving with his finger, frowning. \u201cWe need to figure out the route it shows. It could lead us out of here.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a chilling howl echoed through the trees. The shadows seemed to pulse, and the breeze turned cold. \u201cWe need to move!\u201d Sophie shouted, her heart pounding. \n\nWith new determination, they raced towards the direction the carving indicated, their fears momentarily forgotten as they focused on the adventure ahead.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sophie and her friends discover at the altar?","options":["A treasure chest","A broken compass","A map to escape","A shadowy creature"],"correct_answer":"A broken compass"},{"question":"What does the ancient carving on the tree depict?","options":["A ship sinking","A boat sailing away","A shadowy creature","A treasure map"],"correct_answer":"A boat sailing away"},{"question":"How do the friends respond when they hear a rustling in the trees?","options":["They run away","They laugh","They freeze in fear","They ignore it"],"correct_answer":"They freeze in fear"},{"question":"What does Sophie suggest they need to do?","options":["Turn back","Keep searching","Build a raft","Climb a tree"],"correct_answer":"Keep searching"},{"question":"How do the friends feel as they continue to explore the island?","options":["Confident and hopeful","Scared and alone","Angry and frustrated","Bored and tired"],"correct_answer":"Confident and hopeful"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_20_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_20_ch4_img1.png","plot_20_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":637,"reading_level":"Builder"}
