   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_20_15_18","title":"Rescue Mission: The Island of Shadows","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Escape Mission","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The wind howled like a lost spirit as the storm raged overhead, tossing their small boat like a discarded toy on the furious waves. Sophie gripped the railing, her knuckles white against the salt-stained wood. \u201cWe have to head towards the island! It\u2019s our only chance!\u201d she shouted over the roar of thunder. Beside her, Ethan was pale, his mind racing through the possibilities.\n\n\u201cAre you sure about this?\u201d he questioned, glancing back at the darkening skies. \u201cIt could be dangerous.\u201d His caution often tempered Sophie\u2019s adventurous spirit, but at this moment, there was no room for discussion.\n\n\u201cDanger? We\u2019re surrounded by it!\u201d Kai chimed in, his voice brimming with reckless enthusiasm. He was always the one to jump first and ask questions later, his eyes sparkling with a thrill for the unknown. \u201cCome on! What\u2019s the worst that could happen?\u201d\n\nChloe, sitting cross-legged at the back of the boat, raised her eyes from the deck, her hands clutching a small pocket field guide. \u201cWe could get stranded,\u201d she offered, her voice calm yet tinged with worry. \u201cBut the island could also be a place of discovery. Look!\u201d She pointed to the silhouette of land emerging through the torrent, a dark mass against the raging sky.\n\nWith one final wave crashing down, the boat lurched forward, and they were thrown into the waters, the roar of the storm eclipsing everything. Moments later, consciousness slipped away.\n\nWhen Sophie awoke, it was to the gentle rustling of palm fronds and the distant call of exotic birds. She tried to sit up but winced at a sharp pain in her side. \u201cEthan?\u201d she croaked, her voice hoarse. \u201cWhere are you?\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2019m here,\u201d he replied, emerging from behind a cluster of bushes, his shirt torn and his brow furrowed with concern. \u201cThe others are scattered along the beach. You took quite a hit.\u201d\n\nAs she stood, Sophie brushed sand from her hair and surveyed their surroundings. It was a lush, tropical paradise, vibrant and alive, yet there was an unsettling stillness in the air. The shadows cast by the trees seemed unusually long, as if they were stretching toward them. \n\n\u201cWhere are we?\u201d Chloe\u2019s voice broke through her thoughts, and Sophie turned to see her friend, still clutching her field guide, scanning the horizon. \u201cThere\u2019s something strange about this place. It\u2019s too quiet.\u201d\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s not just quiet,\u201d Kai said, joining them, his face lit with excitement. \u201cIt feels... charged. Like this island is alive.\u201d He glanced back at the dense thicket behind them, a flicker of unease passing across his features. \u201cWe should find a way to signal for help, but not before we explore a bit. There's an adventure waiting for us!\u201d\n\nSophie exchanged a look with Ethan, who remained skeptical. \u201cWe need to be careful, Kai. If we go wandering off, who knows what we might encounter?\u201d\n\n\u201cCome on, what\u2019s the fun in playing it safe?\u201d Kai challenged, his bravado palpable. Chloe caught Sophie\u2019s gaze, her eyes wide with curiosity. For a moment, the decision hung in the air, heavy with the weight of uncertainty.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s explore,\u201d Sophie decided, the explorer within her ignited. \u201cBut we stick together. No one goes off alone.\u201d\n\nAs they ventured deeper into the island, the air thickened with humidity, and the scent of damp earth enveloped them. Ancient trees loomed above, their twisted branches forming a natural canopy that filtered the sunlight into dappled patterns on the ground. With each step, Sophie felt the thrill of discovery, but a lingering thought nagged at the back of her mind\u2014the shadows were growing longer, and the silence more profound.\n\nSuddenly, a rustling erupted from the underbrush, freezing them in their tracks. Chloe\u2019s eyes widened, anxiety flashing across her face. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d she whispered, her tone barely audible.\n\n\u201cProbably just a bird or some other animal,\u201d Ethan muttered, but his voice lacked conviction. Just then, a dark shape slipped between the trees, a fleeting glimpse of something sinister. It was gone before they could discern what it was, leaving behind an oppressive stillness. \n\nSophie\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWe should go back,\u201d she urged, her voice trembling slightly. \n\nBut Kai, ever the instigator, grinned. \u201cAnd miss out on what\u2019s waiting for us? No way!\u201d\n\nBefore Sophie could protest, he darted forward, disappearing into the thick foliage. \u201cKai!\u201d she called, but her voice was swallowed by the forest. A deep-seated fear gripped her\u2014a feeling that they had awoken something dark and ancient on this island.\n\nAs twilight descended, shadows stretched like fingers across the ground, and they could feel the island watching, waiting. They needed to escape before the true nature of the island revealed itself. But first, they had to find Kai.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What storm event led to the group's situation on the island?","options":["A hurricane","A thunderstorm","A blizzard","A tornado"],"correct_answer":"A thunderstorm"},{"question":"Which character is described as the cautious planner?","options":["Sophie","Ethan","Chloe","Kai"],"correct_answer":"Ethan"},{"question":"What does Kai suggest they do on the island?","options":["Search for food","Find a way to signal for help","Explore the island","Build a shelter"],"correct_answer":"Explore the island"},{"question":"What unsettling aspect of the island is mentioned?","options":["It is deserted","There are hostile creatures","The shadows seem alive","It is covered in fog"],"correct_answer":"The shadows seem alive"},{"question":"What causes tension among the group as they explore?","options":["An argument","A strange noise","Wild animals","A storm"],"correct_answer":"A strange noise"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_20_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_20_ch1_img1.png","plot_20_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":804,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
