   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_12_7_10","title":"The Cave of Lost Treasures","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Sam and Olivia stood in the dim cave, their hearts racing. Glowing rocks sparkled all around them. \u201cThis place is amazing!\u201d Sam said, his eyes wide. \n\n\u201cI know! But we need to find a way out before it gets dark,\u201d Olivia replied, pulling out the map they had found. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLook at this!\u201d Sam pointed at a large stone with strange markings. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s a clue!\u201d \n\nOlivia studied the map. \u201cIt looks like the symbol matches this one. It might lead us to the next puzzle!\u201d \n\nThey approached the stone. It had a riddle carved into it. \u201cTo find the way, you must first know, what has roots that nobody sees, is taller than trees, up, up it goes, and yet never grows?\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat could it be?\u201d Olivia thought aloud. \n\n\u201cHmm,\u201d Sam pondered, scratching his head. \u201cI know! It\u2019s a mountain!\u201d \n\n\u201cGreat job, Sam!\u201d Olivia clapped her hands. \u201cLet\u2019s see what happens when we say the answer.\u201d \n\nThey stood together and shouted, \u201cA mountain!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the stone began to glow! A small opening formed in the wall, revealing a narrow path. \u201cLook, it worked!\u201d Sam cheered. \n\nBut just then, they heard a rustling sound. A tiny creature peeked out from behind a rock, its big eyes shining. \u201cAre you treasure hunters?\u201d it squeaked. \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Olivia said excitedly. \u201cWe are trying to find our way out.\u201d \n\n\u201cFollow me! I know the way!\u201d the creature chirped, bouncing with energy. \n\nAs they followed the creature, it led them through twisting tunnels. They walked past shimmering crystals and sparkling waterfalls. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cI can\u2019t believe all this treasure!\u201d Sam exclaimed, eyes wide with wonder. \n\n\u201cJust remember, we\u2019re not here to collect it. We need to go home,\u201d Olivia reminded him gently. \n\nThey reached a large chamber filled with more treasures than they had ever seen. Golden coins, shiny jewels, and ancient artifacts filled the room. But in the center was an enormous door, locked tight. \n\n\u201cUh oh,\u201d Sam said, looking worried. \u201cHow do we open it?\u201d \n\nThe creature grinned. \u201cYou need another riddle! Are you ready?\u201d \n\n\u201cAbsolutely!\u201d they said in unison, feeling hopeful. \n\n\u201cHere it goes! I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with the wind. What am I?\u201d \n\nSam and Olivia exchanged glances. \u201cWe can do this!\u201d Olivia said, her spirit lifting. \n\n\u201cI think it\u2019s an echo!\u201d Sam shouted, his voice bouncing off the cave walls. \n\nThe creature nodded, excited. \u201cSay it out loud!\u201d \n\n\u201cEcho!\u201d they yelled together. \n\nWith a rumble, the door began to open. Light poured in, and they could see the way ahead. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s hurry!\u201d Olivia urged, feeling the thrill of adventure. They stepped through the door, ready for whatever came next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What riddle do Sam and Olivia solve?","options":["What has roots that nobody sees?","What is very tall?","What is a treasure?","What is a cave?"],"correct_answer":"What has roots that nobody sees?"},{"question":"Who helps Sam and Olivia in the cave?","options":["A strange creature","A big monster","Their classmates","A talking map"],"correct_answer":"A strange creature"},{"question":"What do Sam and Olivia see in the large chamber?","options":["A big door","A treasure map","Their hiking group","A waterfall"],"correct_answer":"A big door"},{"question":"What is the answer to the second riddle?","options":["An echo","A shadow","A cave","A treasure"],"correct_answer":"An echo"},{"question":"What feeling do Sam and Olivia have as they explore the cave?","options":["Boredom","Fear","Hope","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Hope"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_12_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_12_ch4_img1.png","plot_12_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":460,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
