   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_12_7_10","title":"The Cave of Lost Treasures","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As Sam and Olivia stepped through the door they had unlocked, they found themselves in a large, bright chamber. Glimmering stones sparkled on the walls, and the air smelled sweet, like fresh berries. \n\n\u201cWow! Look at all this treasure!\u201d Sam exclaimed, his eyes wide. \n\n\u201cYes, but we need to be careful,\u201d Olivia said, glancing around. \u201cWe don\u2019t know what\u2019s in here.\u201d \n\nJust then, they heard a soft, fluttering sound. It came from a corner of the room. Curiosity bubbled in Sam\u2019s chest. \u201cWhat is that?\u201d \n\n\u201cI\u2019m not sure,\u201d Olivia replied, her voice low. \u201cLet\u2019s stay together.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey cautiously approached the sound. To their surprise, they discovered a tiny, sparkling creature! It looked like a mix between a butterfly and a fairy. Its wings glimmered in shades of blue and green. \n\n\u201cHello!\u201d it squeaked, its voice high and cheerful. \u201cI\u2019m Luma! Are you here for the treasure?\u201d \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Sam shouted, excited. \u201cBut we need to find a way out before dark.\u201d \n\nLuma fluttered closer, her wings humming. \u201cI can help! But first, you must solve my riddle.\u201d \n\nOlivia nodded. \u201cWe love riddles! What is it?\u201d\n\nLuma smiled. \u201cI have keys, but no locks. I have space, but no room. What am I?\u201d\n\nSam scratched his head. \u201cHmm. That sounds tricky.\u201d \n\nOlivia thought for a moment. \u201cI know! It\u2019s a computer! A computer has keys, but no locks!\u201d \n\nLuma clapped her tiny hands. \u201cCorrect! You\u2019re clever! Follow me!\u201d \n\nAs they followed Luma, the cave became brighter. They passed piles of gold coins and ancient vases covered in jewels. Sam felt a thrill of adventure. \u201cLook at all this treasure!\u201d he said, but Olivia kept her focus. \n\n\u201cRemember, we need to find the exit,\u201d she reminded him. \n\nSuddenly, Luma stopped. \u201cHere it is! The way out!\u201d She pointed to a shimmering archway. \n\nBut before they could step through, a loud rumble echoed through the cave. Rocks began to fall! \n\n\u201cQuick! We must run!\u201d Olivia shouted. \n\nThe three of them dashed toward the archway, heart pounding with excitement. Sam and Olivia reached it just in time, slipping through as the last rock fell behind them. \n\nPanting and giggling, they found themselves outside, bathed in warm sunlight. \n\n\u201cWe did it!\u201d Sam cheered. \n\nOlivia smiled, relieved. \u201cWe worked together, just like we always do!\u201d \n\nAs they headed back to their hiking group, Sam felt proud. They had faced challenges and solved puzzles. Most importantly, they had each other. \n\n\u201cNext time, let\u2019s bring a map!\u201d Sam joked. \n\nOlivia laughed. \u201cOr maybe just stick closer to the group!\u201d \n\nWith that, they walked home, treasures from the cave sparkling in their minds, ready for the next adventure.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What type of creature do Sam and Olivia meet?","options":["A dragon","A fairy","A cat","A bird"],"correct_answer":"A fairy"},{"question":"What was Luma's riddle about?","options":["A treasure","A map","A computer","A cave"],"correct_answer":"A computer"},{"question":"What do Sam and Olivia need to find?","options":["A treasure","An exit","A friend","A secret"],"correct_answer":"An exit"},{"question":"What happens when they try to leave the cave?","options":["They find more treasure","Rocks start to fall","They meet more creatures","They get lost"],"correct_answer":"Rocks start to fall"},{"question":"What lesson do Sam and Olivia learn?","options":["To explore alone","To always bring snacks","The importance of teamwork","To never enter caves"],"correct_answer":"The importance of teamwork"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_12_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_12_ch5_img1.png","plot_12_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":449,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
