   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_12_11_14","title":"The Cave of Lost Treasures","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The air in the cave was cool and damp, a stark contrast to the warm sunlight they had left behind on the mountain trail. Shadows danced across the jagged walls, and Olivia felt a shiver run down her spine. \"This place is amazing, but also a little creepy,\" she whispered, her voice barely rising above the echoing drip of water from the stalactites overhead.\n\nSam grinned, his eyes sparkling with excitement. \"It\u2019s like a treasure hunt! Just think of all the stories hidden in here.\" He stepped cautiously forward, his boots crunching on the gravelly floor as they ventured deeper into the cave.\n\nSuddenly, the darkness seemed to swallow them. \u201cDo you have your flashlight?\u201d Olivia asked, pulling out her own with a hint of anxiety in her voice. Sam nodded and flicked his on, illuminating a path of glimmering rocks that sparkled like stars against the cave's damp walls. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cWow, look at that!\u201d Sam exclaimed, pointing to a large, shimmering object partially obscured by the shadows. They approached it cautiously, revealing a beautifully carved stone tablet engraved with intricate symbols and a riddle that seemed to pulse with energy.\n\n\u201c\u2018To find the way, answer with care; the secret lies where none can dare. What runs but never walks, has a bed but never sleeps?\u2019\u201d Olivia read aloud, her brow furrowing in concentration. \n\n\u201cWater,\u201d Sam replied confidently. \u201cIt runs in rivers and streams but doesn\u2019t walk. It also has a riverbed.\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see if that\u2019s right!\u201d Olivia said with anticipation, but just as she stepped closer to touch the tablet, a low growl echoed through the cave, sending a jolt of fear through them both. \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Sam asked, his voice trembling slightly.\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s just an echo?\u201d Olivia suggested weakly, but they both knew it sounded far too close for comfort. The growl repeated, closer this time, along with the rustling of what sounded like feathers. \n\nA shadow flitted across the beam of Sam\u2019s flashlight, and a creature emerged from the darkness\u2014a creature with gleaming eyes and luminous feathers. It looked like a cross between a hawk and a dragon, its wings folded tightly against its body.\n\n\u201cDon\u2019t move!\u201d Olivia whispered urgently. The creature stared at them, its head tilting to one side, as if pondering whether they were friend or foe. \n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s guarding the treasure?\u201d Sam suggested, his adventurous spirit now tinged with nervousness. \n\n\u201cOr it\u2019s angry we\u2019re here,\u201d Olivia replied, her heart racing. They had to think quickly. \u201cWe need to answer the riddle before it decides to attack!\u201d\n\nIn that tense moment, Sam felt the weight of the adventure settle on his shoulders. \u201cOkay! Water is the answer, so let\u2019s say it together!\u201d \n\nThey both shouted, \u201cWater!\u201d The creature\u2019s eyes widened, and a low rumble echoed through the cave as it spread its wings, revealing a hidden path illuminated by the glow of bioluminescent moss.\n\n\u201cLook! It\u2019s moving!\u201d Olivia gasped in awe as the creature stepped aside, revealing an opening leading deeper into the cave. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Sam urged, adrenaline pumping through him. But just as they took a step forward, they heard a loud rumble\u2014rocks cascaded from above, blocking the way they had just come.\n\n\u201cNow what?\u201d Olivia said, panic rising in her voice as the echoes of the growl returned, mixing with the sound of falling stones. \u201cWe need to find another way out before it gets dark!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam and Olivia find engraved on the stone tablet?","options":["A treasure map","A riddle","A warning","A drawing"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What creature do Sam and Olivia encounter in the cave?","options":["A bear","A dragon","A hawk","A mythical bird"],"correct_answer":"A mythical bird"},{"question":"What is the answer to the riddle they read?","options":["Fire","Wind","Water","Light"],"correct_answer":"Water"},{"question":"What happens to block their way back?","options":["A flood occurs","Rocks fall","The creature attacks","They get lost"],"correct_answer":"Rocks fall"},{"question":"What do Sam and Olivia feel as they continue their adventure?","options":["Excitement","Boredom","Disinterest","Fearlessness"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_12_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_12_ch2_img1.png","plot_12_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":584,"reading_level":"Builder"}
