   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_12_11_14","title":"The Cave of Lost Treasures","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the echoes of their footsteps faded into the shadows, Sam and Olivia found themselves deeper in the cave than they had ever imagined. The walls glimmered with crystals that sparkled like stars, and the air was cool and damp, filled with the scent of ancient earth. Sam ran his fingers along a particularly large crystal, its surface smooth and cold. \n\n\u201cLook at this! It\u2019s like something out of a fairy tale,\u201d he exclaimed, eyes wide with wonder. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nOlivia squinted into the dim light, her practical side taking over. \u201cSam, remember what we came here for. We need to find a way out before it gets dark.\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, right. But how cool would it be to explore just a bit more?\u201d Sam bit his lip, torn between curiosity and caution.\n\nJust then, they heard a faint sound, like the rustling of leaves. Olivia\u2019s eyes darted around the cave. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Sam whispered, a shiver running down his spine. \u201cLet\u2019s check it out.\u201d\n\nAs they cautiously stepped forward, the sound grew louder, echoing off the walls. Suddenly, a pair of glowing eyes appeared from behind a rock formation. A small creature, with fur as white as snow and a long, twitching tail, emerged cautiously.\n\n\u201cDon\u2019t be scared! I\u2019m just a cave dweller,\u201d it squeaked. \u201cI\u2019ve seen many adventurers come and go, but never two like you!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Olivia asked, her heart racing.\n\nThe creature hopped closer, curiosity twinkling in its eyes. \u201cYou\u2019re not looking for treasure, are you? Many have tried, but only a few have escaped!\u201d\n\nSam frowned. \u201cWe\u2019re not here for treasure. We\u2019re just trying to find our way back to our friends.\u201d\n\n\u201cThen you\u2019ll need to answer a riddle,\u201d the creature replied, its voice echoing with a hint of mischief. \u201cThis cave has its secrets. Solve the riddle, and I shall guide you out.\u201d\n\n\u201cI love riddles!\u201d Sam said, a grin spreading across his face. \n\nThe creature tilted its head. \u201cVery well. Here it is: I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with wind. What am I?\u201d\n\nThey exchanged glances, deep in thought. Olivia\u2019s brow furrowed as she pondered the words. \u201cIt sounds like\u2026 an echo!\u201d she exclaimed.\n\n\u201cIs it just me, or is this cave full of echoes?\u201d Sam added, excitement bubbling in his voice.\n\nThe creature clapped its tiny paws together. \u201cCorrect! But you must hurry. The cave is alive, and it\u2019s awakening. Dark creatures lie in wait to trap those who linger too long.\u201d\n\nA low growl echoed through the cavern as the ground trembled slightly beneath them. Sam felt a surge of panic. \u201cWe need to move!\u201d\n\n\u201cFollow me!\u201d the cave dweller squeaked, darting down a narrow passageway. They raced after it, the flickering light of the crystals dimming behind them as shadows stretched across the walls.\n\nSuddenly, Olivia stumbled, scraping her knee on the jagged rocks. \u201cOw! Sam, I can\u2019t keep going like this!\u201d\n\nSam turned back, worry clouding his face. \u201cWe can\u2019t stop now! We have to find the exit before the cave gets too dark!\u201d\n\nThe creature paused, looking back. \u201cIf you\u2019re going to make it out, you must decide: press forward, or turn back to find shelter! Time is running out!\u201d\n\nSam\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat do we do, Olivia?\u201d\n\nShe looked at the darkening passage behind them, the shadows growing thicker. \u201cWe go forward. I can climb if you help me.\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2019ll help you!\u201d Sam gripped her hand tightly, determination flooding his veins. \u201cTogether, we can do this!\u201d\n\nWith one last glance at the creature, they forged ahead, deeper into the cave\u2019s labyrinth, their breaths quickening in the thick air. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut just as they turned a corner, they found themselves face-to-face with yet another guardian, its eyes gleaming ominously in the dark. They stood frozen, realization dawning: this was more than just a cave\u2014it was a test of their friendship, courage, and wit.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What riddle does the cave dweller ask Sam and Olivia?","options":["What has keys but can't open locks?","I speak without a mouth and hear without ears.","What is always hungry and must be fed?","What can travel around the world while staying in a corner?"],"correct_answer":"I speak without a mouth and hear without ears."},{"question":"What happens when they answer the riddle correctly?","options":["The cave dweller disappears.","They are given treasure.","The cave dweller offers to guide them out.","They find a map."],"correct_answer":"The cave dweller offers to guide them out."},{"question":"What does Olivia scrape when she stumbles?","options":["Her arm","Her knee","Her foot","Her hand"],"correct_answer":"Her knee"},{"question":"What does Sam suggest when Olivia is hurt?","options":["To find shelter","To go back","To keep going","To wait for help"],"correct_answer":"To keep going"},{"question":"What is the main conflict Sam and Olivia face in this chapter?","options":["Finding treasure","Solving a riddle","Deciding whether to move forward or find shelter","Getting lost in the cave"],"correct_answer":"Deciding whether to move forward or find shelter"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_12_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_12_ch3_img1.png","plot_12_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":684,"reading_level":"Builder"}
