   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_12_11_14","title":"The Cave of Lost Treasures","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As Sam and Olivia stood at the entrance of the cave, an eerie stillness surrounded them. The air was cool and damp, swirling with the faint scent of moss and something metallic. Stalactites hung from the ceiling like sharp teeth ready to snap. Sam\u2019s eyes sparkled with excitement, while Olivia, ever the pragmatist, scanned their surroundings warily.\n\n\u201cAre you sure we should go in?\u201d Olivia asked, her voice echoing slightly. \u201cWhat if we get lost?\u201d\n\n\u201cCome on, Liv! This is our chance for an adventure!\u201d Sam replied, taking a brave step forward. \u201cBesides, look at those shiny rocks!\u201d He pointed to a glimmering pile of crystals nestled against the cave wall. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they ventured deeper, the cave opened up into a vast chamber illuminated by the glow of bioluminescent fungi. The walls were adorned with ancient markings, telling stories of explorers long gone. Sam traced the carvings with his finger, igniting his curiosity. \u201cThese could be clues! Maybe they\u2019ll help us find our way out,\u201d he mused, his mind racing with possibilities.\n\n\u201cOr they could just be drawings,\u201d Olivia countered, crossing her arms. \u201cWe don\u2019t have time to be distracted. We need to focus on getting out before it gets dark.\u201d She glanced back at the narrow passage they had come from, the light slowly fading.\n\nBut Sam was already drawn to another part of the cave. \u201cLook over here!\u201d he shouted, rushing towards a stone pedestal at the center of the chamber. On it lay a sparkling jewel, a massive sapphire that gleamed like the sky on a clear day. \u201cThis must be part of the lost treasures!\u201d\n\n\u201cSam, wait! What if it\u2019s a trap?\u201d Olivia exclaimed, her heart racing. Just then, the ground shook slightly beneath their feet. \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Sam asked, stepping back. \u201cDid you feel that?\u201d\n\nOlivia nodded, her eyes wide. \u201cWe should really think this through.\u201d But before Sam could respond, a low growl echoed from the shadows, making them both freeze. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nEmerging from the darkness was a creature that looked part lizard, part bear, with glimmering scales and sharp claws. It eyed the jewel hungrily, its nostrils flaring. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be here!\u201d it growled, its voice gravelly and deep. \n\n\u201cUh, we were just\u2014\u201d Sam began, but Olivia quickly interrupted, \u201cWe don\u2019t want any trouble! We just want to find our way out!\u201d Her voice trembled, but she stood firm, knowing they had to work together if they wanted to escape.\n\nThe creature tilted its head, considering their words. \u201cSolve my riddle,\u201d it said, its eyes narrowing. \u201cOnly then will I let you pass.\u201d \n\nSam exchanged a glance with Olivia, both nervous but determined. \u201cWhat\u2019s the riddle?\u201d Sam asked, his mind racing back to his favorite puzzle books. \n\nThe creature growled again, \u201cI speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have nobody, but I come alive with the wind. What am I?\u201d\n\nOlivia\u2019s eyes lit up. \u201cIt\u2019s an echo!\u201d she shouted, relief washing over her. \n\n\u201cCorrect,\u201d the creature said, stepping aside. \u201cBut hurry! Darkness creeps closer, and you don\u2019t want to be here when it does.\u201d \n\nWith a mix of relief and renewed determination, Sam and Olivia dashed past the creature, deeper into the cave, where the next challenge awaited. They could feel the tension in the air, a sense of urgency pushing them forward. \n\nWhat lay ahead could be the key to unlocking their way home\u2014or it could lead them into even greater peril.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Sam find in the cave that excites him?","options":["A treasure map","A sparkling jewel","A magical creature","A hidden door"],"correct_answer":"A sparkling jewel"},{"question":"What is Olivia's main concern about exploring the cave?","options":["They might get lost","They could find treasure","They will meet other explorers","The cave is too dark"],"correct_answer":"They might get lost"},{"question":"What riddle does the creature present to Sam and Olivia?","options":["What has keys but can't open locks?","What comes down but never goes up?","I speak without a mouth and hear without ears","What has a heart that doesn't beat?"],"correct_answer":"I speak without a mouth and hear without ears"},{"question":"How does Olivia respond when the creature appears?","options":["She runs away","She stays quiet","She confronts it bravely","She tries to negotiate"],"correct_answer":"She confronts it bravely"},{"question":"What do Sam and Olivia need to do before it gets dark?","options":["Find the treasure","Solve puzzles","Escape the cave","Make friends with the creature"],"correct_answer":"Escape the cave"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_12_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_12_ch4_img1.png","plot_12_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":588,"reading_level":"Builder"}
