   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_13_7_10","title":"The Island of Whispers","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Jess and Mark were excited. They were on a boat trip with their dad. The sun shone bright, and the water sparkled like diamonds. Jess loved stories, and she imagined all the adventures they might have. \n\n\u201cDo you think we\u2019ll see any dolphins?\u201d Mark asked. He leaned over the side of the boat, eyes wide with wonder.\n\n\u201cMaybe! Or treasure islands!\u201d Jess replied, her smile big.\n\nSuddenly, dark clouds rolled in. The wind howled. The boat rocked back and forth. \n\n\u201cHold on!\u201d their dad shouted. The boat tipped, and then\u2014splash! The world turned upside down. \n\nJess and Mark found themselves in the water. Jess gasped as she felt the cold waves. \u201cMark! Swim!\u201d she called. They kicked and paddled, trying to reach the shore. \n\nWhen they finally reached land, they crawled onto the sandy beach. They looked around, panting and wet. \n\n\u201cThis place is strange,\u201d Mark said. The trees towered high, their leaves whispering softly. Jess noticed something magical about them. \n\n\u201cDo you hear that?\u201d she asked. \n\n\u201cHear what?\u201d Mark replied, shaking water from his hair.\n\n\u201cThe trees,\u201d Jess whispered. \u201cThey\u2019re talking!\u201d \n\nThe trees rustled, and Mark frowned. \u201cYou\u2019re just tired. Trees can\u2019t talk!\u201d \n\nBut Jess smiled. \u201cLet\u2019s explore! We need to find help.\u201d \n\nThey walked into the island. The air smelled sweet, like fruit. Bright flowers bloomed everywhere, and colorful birds flew above. \n\nAfter a few steps, they came across a cave. The entrance was dark and inviting. \u201cShould we go in?\u201d Mark asked, glancing back at Jess. \n\n\u201cOf course! What if there\u2019s treasure?\u201d she exclaimed, her eyes sparkling.\n\nAs they entered the cave, the air felt cooler. Suddenly, a loud crack echoed. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Mark jumped, gripping Jess\u2019s arm.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know!\u201d Jess whispered, her heart racing. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe cave opened up to a beautiful underground waterfall. It sparkled like stars in the night. \n\n\u201cWow!\u201d Mark said, his fear forgotten. \u201cThis is amazing!\u201d \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Jess pointed. \u201cThere\u2019s something shining near the water!\u201d \n\nBut before they could get closer, the ground shook. They stumbled back. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?\u201d Mark shouted. \n\n\u201cWe need to get out of here!\u201d Jess yelled, pulling him toward the cave entrance. \n\nAs they raced back outside, they heard the trees whispering again. \u201cListen!\u201d Jess said. \u201cMaybe they can help us!\u201d \n\nMark frowned but nodded. \u201cOkay. But how do we talk to trees?\u201d \n\nJess thought hard. \u201cI guess we\u2019ll have to find out!\u201d \n\nThe sun was setting, casting shadows. Their adventure was just beginning. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s figure out what the island is saying!\u201d Jess said, determination in her voice. \n\nMark grinned. \u201cI\u2019m ready. Let\u2019s do this!\u201d \n\nThey stood together, ready to unlock the secrets of the Island of Whispers.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What happened to Jess and Mark's boat?","options":["It sailed smoothly.","It capsized in a storm.","It floated away.","It was lost in the ocean."],"correct_answer":"It capsized in a storm."},{"question":"What do the trees seem to do on the island?","options":["Whisper secrets","Dance in the wind","Play music","Hide treasures"],"correct_answer":"Whisper secrets"},{"question":"What do Jess and Mark find in the cave?","options":["A treasure chest","A beautiful waterfall","A scary creature","A map"],"correct_answer":"A beautiful waterfall"},{"question":"How does Mark feel when they see the cave?","options":["Scared","Excited","Bored","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What do Jess and Mark plan to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Leave the island","Talk to the trees","Find their dad","Go to sleep"],"correct_answer":"Talk to the trees"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_13_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_13_ch1_img1.png","plot_13_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":460,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
