   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_14_7_10","title":"The Wildflower Trail","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"It was a sunny Thursday morning when the school bus rolled into the beautiful Wildflower Trail. Mia peered out of the window, her heart racing with excitement. She loved nature, especially flowers. \u201cLook at those daisies!\u201d she exclaimed, pointing to the golden blooms.  \n\nEthan, sitting beside her, grinned. \u201cI can\u2019t wait to find the biggest one! Let\u2019s go!\u201d  \n\nAs they stepped off the bus, their teacher, Mrs. Thompson, clapped her hands. \u201cOkay, everyone! Stay close and follow me!\u201d The students cheered, their voices echoing in the fresh air.  \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]  \n\nThe trail was alive with colors. Bright red poppies danced in the breeze, and bluebells swayed happily. Mia took a deep breath, smelling the sweet scent of flowers. \u201cThis place is magical,\u201d she whispered.  \n\nEthan nodded, already wandering ahead. \u201cCome on, Mia! Let\u2019s explore!\u201d He dashed down the path, while Mia hesitated. She felt shy and unsure. What if she got lost?  \n\nAs they walked, the other students chatted and laughed. \u201cLook at that butterfly!\u201d shouted Lily, a girl with curly hair. The butterfly fluttered past Mia and Ethan, leading them deeper into the forest.  \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s follow it!\u201d Ethan said, his eyes sparkling with adventure.  \n\nMia bit her lip. \u201cI don\u2019t know. What if we lose the group?\u201d  \n\nBut Ethan waved his hand. \u201cIt\u2019ll be fun! Don\u2019t worry!\u201d And with that, he raced after the butterfly. Mia took a deep breath, then followed him, hoping to keep up.  \n\nSuddenly, they reached a clearing. It was a sea of wildflowers! Mia\u2019s eyes widened in wonder. \u201cWow, look at all the colors!\u201d  \n\nThey frolicked among the flowers, giggling and running. But when they looked around, the group was nowhere in sight.  \n\n\u201cMia,\u201d Ethan said, his voice suddenly serious. \u201cWhere did everyone go?\u201d  \n\nPanic gripped Mia\u2019s heart. \u201cOh no! We\u2019re lost!\u201d  \n\nEthan took a deep breath. \u201cOkay, we can find them. We just need to stick together.\u201d  \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]  \n\nMia nodded, feeling a little braver. \u201cBut how do we get back?\u201d  \n\nEthan pointed to the sun. \u201cThe sun is over there. If we go that way, we might find the trail!\u201d  \n\nTogether, they set off, determined to lead their classmates back to safety. Mia felt her fear start to fade. Maybe, just maybe, she could be brave like Ethan.  \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go, Mia! Adventure awaits!\u201d he cheered, and with that, they walked forward into the wildflower wonderland.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia love about nature?","options":["Flowers","Trees","Birds","Rocks"],"correct_answer":"Flowers"},{"question":"Who is the adventurous student?","options":["Mia","Ethan","Lily","Mrs. Thompson"],"correct_answer":"Ethan"},{"question":"What happens when they follow the butterfly?","options":["They find the bus","They meet a bear","They get lost","They see a stream"],"correct_answer":"They get lost"},{"question":"What does Ethan suggest when they realize they are lost?","options":["Stay where they are","Ask for help","Look for flowers","Stick together"],"correct_answer":"Stick together"},{"question":"What is the main setting of the story?","options":["A school","A city","A national park","A beach"],"correct_answer":"A national park"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_14_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_14_ch1_img1.png","plot_14_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":404,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
