   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_14_7_10","title":"The Wildflower Trail","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The sun shone bright over the Wildflower Trail. Mia and Ethan stood at the edge of a meadow full of colorful flowers. The air smelled sweet and fresh. \u201cLook at all the flowers!\u201d Mia said, her eyes wide. \u201cI\u2019ve never seen so many!\u201d\n\nEthan grinned. \u201cLet\u2019s explore! Maybe we can find a shortcut back!\u201d They took their first steps into the sea of colors. Butterflies danced around them, and bees buzzed happily. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they walked, their classmates followed closely. Suddenly, they heard a loud rustle in the bushes. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Ethan asked, his voice a mix of excitement and fear. \n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s a bear!\u201d someone shouted. The group froze. Mia\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWe should get back to the path,\u201d she whispered.\n\n\u201cI think it was just a rabbit,\u201d said Ethan, trying to sound brave. \u201cLet\u2019s go check it out!\u201d He stepped closer to the bushes. \n\nMia followed, though her legs felt wobbly. They peeked through the leaves together. A small rabbit hopped away, its fluffy tail bouncing. Everyone laughed, relieved. \u201cSee? Nothing to worry about!\u201d Ethan said, smiling.\n\nBut just as they turned to leave, they realized their classmates were not behind them anymore. \u201cWhere did they go?\u201d Mia asked. Panic bubbled in her stomach. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. We have to find them!\u201d Ethan said. \u201cLet\u2019s call their names.\u201d They shouted, \u201cGuys! Where are you?\u201d\n\nNo answer came. The woods felt bigger and darker now. \u201cWhat if we\u2019re really lost?\u201d Mia said, her voice trembling. \u201cWhat if we never get back?\u201d\n\nEthan put a hand on her shoulder. \u201cWe will! We just need to think.\u201d He looked around. \u201cHow about we follow the river? It might lead us back to the trail!\u201d\n\nMia nodded, trying to feel brave. They hurried to the sound of flowing water. The river sparkled in the sunlight, twisting through the trees. But as they reached the edge, they saw something strange. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Ethan pointed. There was a sparkling stone half-buried in the mud. It glinted like a star. \u201cWhat is that?\u201d Mia asked, bending down to see. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but it looks special!\u201d Ethan said, reaching for it. Suddenly, the ground shook a little. \u201cUh-oh, what\u2019s happening?\u201d Mia cried, stepping back.\n\nJust then, a loud crash came from the thicket. A big branch fell, blocking their path! Now, they were trapped! \n\n\u201cMia! What do we do?\u201d Ethan shouted, panic in his eyes.\n\n\u201cI\u2026 I don\u2019t know!\u201d she replied, feeling that same fear again. \n\nBut then she remembered the rabbit. \u201cWhat if we dig around it? We might find a way through or under!\u201d \n\nEthan nodded, feeling hopeful again. \u201cGreat idea! Let\u2019s do it!\u201d They both got to work, digging with their hands, hoping to uncover a way back to safety.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nJust as they were about to give up, they heard a noise behind them. Was it their classmates? Or something else? \n\nMia and Ethan paused, their hearts racing. \n\n\u201cShould we turn around?\u201d Ethan asked.\n\n\u201cWe have to,\u201d Mia said, feeling braver now. \u201cIt might be a chance to get back!\u201d \n\nBut what if it was something scary?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia and Ethan find in the mud?","options":["A bear","A rabbit","A sparkling stone","A flower"],"correct_answer":"A sparkling stone"},{"question":"What blocked Mia and Ethan's path?","options":["A stream","A fallen branch","A big rock","A bush"],"correct_answer":"A fallen branch"},{"question":"What suggestion did Mia have to escape?","options":["Climb the branch","Dig around it","Yell for help","Run away"],"correct_answer":"Dig around it"},{"question":"Who is feeling brave by the end of the chapter?","options":["Ethan","Mia","Both","Neither"],"correct_answer":"Mia"},{"question":"What noise do Mia and Ethan hear?","options":["A bird","Someone calling their names","A mysterious noise","A waterfall"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious noise"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_14_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_14_ch3_img1.png","plot_14_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":530,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
