   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_14_7_10","title":"The Wildflower Trail","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Chapter 4: The Way Forward\n\nThe sun peeked through the tall trees, making the wildflowers sparkle. Mia and Ethan stood at the fallen branch. They looked at each other, determination shining in their eyes.\n\n\u201cDo you think we can move it?\u201d asked Mia. Her heart raced, but she felt brave.\n\nEthan nodded. \u201cWe have to try! Let\u2019s do it together.\u201d\n\nThey pushed against the heavy branch. It creaked and groaned, but slowly it shifted. With one big effort, they rolled it off the path! \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cYay! We did it!\u201d cheered Mia, smiling brightly. She felt proud. \n\nEthan grinned. \u201cNow we can move on! Let\u2019s see what else is out there.\u201d\n\nThey walked further down the trail, surrounded by a sea of colorful wildflowers. Bees buzzed happily, and butterflies danced through the air. It felt magical.\n\n\u201cLook at that!\u201d Mia pointed to a big, bright blue flower. \u201cI\u2019ve never seen one like it before!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s take a closer look.\u201d Ethan knelt down, examining the petals.\n\nSuddenly, they heard a rustling sound nearby. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Mia whispered, her eyes wide.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out!\u201d Ethan said, full of excitement.\n\nThey tiptoed toward the noise. To their surprise, they found a small group of their classmates! They were huddled around a sparkling stream, splashing water at each other.\n\n\u201cMia! Ethan!\u201d called Sophie, waving her hand. \u201cWe were so worried about you!\u201d\n\n\u201cWe got lost!\u201d Mia replied. \u201cBut we figured some things out!\u201d\n\nEthan added, \u201cWe moved a big branch!\u201d\n\n\u201cWow! You guys are heroes!\u201d said Sam, grinning from ear to ear.\n\nMia's face turned a little red. \u201cWe just did what we had to do.\u201d\n\n\u201cWe should stick together now,\u201d Ethan suggested. \u201cLet\u2019s head back as a team!\u201d\n\nEveryone agreed, feeling stronger together. They formed a line, with Mia and Ethan in front. As they walked, they talked and laughed, forgetting their worries.\n\nHope filled the air as they made their way through the wildflowers. They couldn\u2019t wait to share their adventure with the class.\n\nAs they approached a fork in the trail, Mia stopped. \u201cWhich way should we go?\u201d\n\nEthan looked left, then right. \u201cMaybe we should split up and see if we can find the main path!\u201d\n\n\u201cGreat idea!\u201d Mia exclaimed.\n\nWith renewed excitement, they prepared to find their way back home.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe adventure was far from over!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia and Ethan move to get past the path?","options":["A big rock","A fallen branch","A tree","A log"],"correct_answer":"A fallen branch"},{"question":"What color was the flower Mia pointed out?","options":["Red","Blue","Yellow","Pink"],"correct_answer":"Blue"},{"question":"What did they hear that surprised them?","options":["A bird singing","A rustling sound","A dog barking","A waterfall"],"correct_answer":"A rustling sound"},{"question":"Where did they find their classmates?","options":["By a waterfall","At a picnic","Near a stream","In a cave"],"correct_answer":"Near a stream"},{"question":"What did Ethan suggest they do at the fork in the trail?","options":["Sit and rest","Go home","Split up","Take a nap"],"correct_answer":"Split up"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_14_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_14_ch4_img1.png","plot_14_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":397,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
