   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_14_11_14","title":"The Wildflower Trail","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun peeked over the tall pine trees, painting the sky with hues of orange and pink. Mia sat on the bus, her fingers nervously tracing the outline of a wildflower sticker on her backpack. Today was the day! A field trip to Green Meadow National Park, a place she had only read about in books. It was a chance to learn about nature, her favorite subject, and escape the buzz of middle school for just a little while.\n\n\u201cHey, Mia! You ready for our great adventure?\u201d Ethan, with his bright blue baseball cap and an infectious grin, plopped down beside her. He was the kind of boy who thrived on excitement and never seemed to shy away from anything.\n\n\u201cUh, I guess,\u201d Mia replied, her voice barely above a whisper. She watched as he leaned forward, eyes sparkling with anticipation. \u201cI just hope we don\u2019t get lost.\u201d\n\nEthan laughed, his carefree nature lighting up the cramped space of the bus. \u201cLost? Not a chance! I have a great sense of direction.\u201d He paused, casting a sideways glance out the window. \u201cBesides, we\u2019ll have our whole class with us. How could we possibly get lost?\u201d\n\nAs the bus rumbled along the winding road, Mia felt a mix of excitement and apprehension. She looked out the window, where wildflowers danced like colorful confetti in the gentle breeze. Soon, they arrived. The students piled off the bus, chattering and laughing, their footsteps crunching on the gravel as they formed a line behind their teacher, Ms. Johnson.\n\n\u201cWelcome to Green Meadow National Park,\u201d Ms. Johnson announced, her voice full of enthusiasm. \u201cToday, we\u2019ll explore the Wildflower Trail, learn about the local ecosystem, and hopefully discover some interesting creatures along the way!\u201d\n\nWith that, the group set off, the air filled with the sweet scent of blooming flowers. Mia took a deep breath, letting the fresh air fill her lungs. She loved the outdoors, but the thought of being away from the group made her stomach twist into knots. \n\nAbout an hour into their hike, they stopped at a clearing. Vibrant wildflowers stretched endlessly in front of them, a kaleidoscope of colors. Mia couldn\u2019t help but smile. She recognized daisies, buttercups, and even some elusive orchids nestled in the grass. This was her happy place.\n\n\u201cLook at that butterfly!\u201d Ethan shouted, pointing excitedly. \u201cLet\u2019s see who can catch it first!\u201d Without waiting for a response, he darted off, his laughter echoing through the meadow.\n\n\u201cWait, Ethan!\u201d Mia called, but he was already too far ahead. Her heart raced\u2014not from the thrill of the chase, but from fear. She had never been very fast, and the thought of running after him made her feel small.\n\nSuddenly, Mia heard a commotion behind her. \u201cWhere\u2019s Ethan?\u201d one of their classmates yelled. The group had noticed his absence, and panic began to ripple among them. The sunny day suddenly felt more ominous; shadows loomed as the realization hit: they had wandered off the main trail.\n\n\u201cEveryone, stay calm!\u201d Ms. Johnson instructed, but her voice trembled ever so slightly. Mia felt a knot tightening in her stomach as she turned to see Ethan was nowhere in sight.\n\n\u201cMaybe we should look for him?\u201d Mia suggested, her voice steadier than she felt. She glanced at the others, her heart racing. Ethan might be lost, but they needed to find him. She looked at the path ahead, a sea of wildflowers obscuring the way. This was their chance\u2014together, they had to be brave.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s split into two groups,\u201d Ethan\u2019s friend, Sarah, suggested. \u201cMia, you and I can go this way. It\u2019s the last place we saw him.\u201d \n\nMia nodded, swallowing her fear. \u201cOkay, let\u2019s go.\u201d With each step, her determination grew. She was no longer just the shy girl; she had to be a leader now.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe vibrant wildflower meadow stretched before them, a stunning sea of colors under the bright blue sky. Mia and Sarah stood at the edge, their expressions a mix of determination and concern as they prepared to venture off the trail.\n\nAs they walked through the woods, shadows danced among the trees, and the sounds of nature surrounded them. Suddenly, a rustle came from a nearby bush, halting them in their tracks.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia\u2019s heart raced as she turned, her eyes wide. A flash of movement caught her attention, revealing a small creature peeking out\u2014a fox! Its bright eyes watched them curiously before it darted deeper into the underbrush.\n\n\u201cDid you see that?\u201d Sarah whispered, excitement bubbling in her voice. \u201cWe\u2019re on the right path, Mia. This adventure is just beginning!\u201d\n\nBut as they continued on, the woods grew thicker, and the sunlight dimmed, casting eerie shadows around them. Mia felt the weight of responsibility pressing down on her shoulders\u2014what if they didn\u2019t find Ethan? What if they were lost forever?\n\nShe glanced at Sarah, who was now scanning the area, determination etched in her features. Mia took a deep breath, reminding herself that they had to trust each other. They could do this. They had to.\n\nThe thrill of adventure intertwined with the fear of the unknown. Little did they know, the wildflower trail was more than just a path through nature; it was a journey into the heart of themselves.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What was Mia's initial feeling about the field trip?","options":["Excitement","Fear","Boredom","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"},{"question":"Who is the confident classmate that encourages Mia to have fun?","options":["Sarah","Ethan","Ms. Johnson","Jake"],"correct_answer":"Ethan"},{"question":"What happens when the group realizes Ethan is missing?","options":["They continue on their hike","They panic","They take a break","They call for help"],"correct_answer":"They panic"},{"question":"How does Mia feel about leading the search for Ethan?","options":["Excited","Nervous","Angry","Disinterested"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What creature do Mia and Sarah encounter in the woods?","options":["A deer","A bear","A fox","A rabbit"],"correct_answer":"A fox"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_14_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_14_ch1_img1.png","plot_14_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":896,"reading_level":"Builder"}
