   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_14_11_14","title":"The Wildflower Trail","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The sun filtered through the trees, creating a patchwork of light on the forest floor as Mia and her classmates stood at a crossroads in the Wildflower Trail. Anxiety buzzed in the air like a swarm of bees. \u201cWhich way do we go now?\u201d Mia whispered, her heart thumping like a drum. She glanced at Ethan, who was scanning their surroundings.\n\n\u201cI think we should follow the stream,\u201d Ethan suggested, his voice brimming with confidence. \u201cIt\u2019ll lead us back to the main path for sure.\u201d \n\nMia nodded, though uncertainty clung to her like the morning mist. The group agreed, their footsteps echoing as they followed the gentle gurgle of the water. Wildflowers danced in the breeze, their colors vivid against the backdrop of green. Mia felt a small thrill at the beauty surrounding her, but that was quickly eclipsed by worry for their missing friend. \n\n\u201cDo you think Ethan\u2019s okay?\u201d Mia asked, her voice barely a whisper. \n\n\u201cHe\u2019s fine! He\u2019s probably climbing a tree or something,\u201d Chloe, a classmate with a penchant for drama, scoffed. \u201cHe always thinks he\u2019s invincible.\u201d \n\nThe group continued walking, tension building with each step. Suddenly, they heard a crunching noise in the bushes. Mia\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d \n\n\u201cProbably just a squirrel,\u201d Liam said. \u201cOr maybe a deer. Don\u2019t freak out.\u201d He laughed, but his voice trembled slightly, betraying his own fears. The others shared nervous glances, the uncertainty of their situation weighing heavily.\n\nAs they rounded a bend, the stream widened into a small, sparkling pool. Sunlight sparkled on the water like diamonds scattered across a blue velvet cloth. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s take a quick break!\u201d Ethan suggested, plopping down on a rock. \u201cWe deserve it after all this wandering.\u201d \n\nMia hesitated. \u201cBut what if we get more lost?\u201d \n\n\u201cRelax, Mia! We\u2019ll only stop for a minute.\u201d Ethan smiled, but there was a flicker of concern in his eyes. \n\nAs the group settled, they began to chat, their laughter breaking the tension. Mia found herself smiling, feeling a bit more at ease. But then, like a cloud blocking the sun, doubt crept back in. What if they couldn\u2019t find their way back? \n\nJust then, a rustling sound erupted from the bushes. Everyone froze, eyes wide. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Chloe shrieked, her hands clenching her backpack. \n\nBefore anyone could answer, a small figure burst from the underbrush\u2014a raccoon! It stumbled into the clearing, its shiny eyes surveying the group as if they were the intruders in its domain. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Ethan exclaimed, pointing. \u201cIt\u2019s just a raccoon! How cute!\u201d\n\nThe raccoon sniffed the air, cautiously edging closer to them. For a moment, all fear evaporated as the students giggled and leaned forward to watch. But in the midst of their laughter, the raccoon suddenly darted back into the bushes. The group\u2019s laughter faded, an unspoken concern hanging in the air like the scent of wildflowers.\n\n\u201cMaybe we should keep moving,\u201d Mia suggested, her voice steady despite the fluttering in her stomach. \u201cWe can\u2019t stay here forever.\u201d \n\nAs they stood to leave, Mia noticed a faint trail leading into the woods, obscured by tall grass and wildflowers. \u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d she pointed. \n\n\u201cIt looks like it could lead somewhere,\u201d Ethan said, his adventurous spirit ignited. \u201cWhat do you think, should we check it out?\u201d \n\nMia hesitated, but the determination in Ethan\u2019s eyes ignited a spark within her. \u201cLet\u2019s do it,\u201d she said, her voice stronger than before. They stepped onto the hidden path, ready to uncover whatever secrets lay ahead, unaware of the challenges waiting just around the bend.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Mia and her classmates decide to follow to find their way back?","options":["The trail of wildflowers","The sound of the stream","The sound of the wind","The path of sunlight"],"correct_answer":"The sound of the stream"},{"question":"How does Mia feel when they spot the raccoon?","options":["Terrified","Excited","Indifferent","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What does Mia suggest after they encounter the raccoon?","options":["To stay there longer","To keep moving","To go back the way they came","To climb a tree"],"correct_answer":"To keep moving"},{"question":"What does Ethan\u2019s character represent in the story?","options":["Caution and fear","Adventure and confidence","Shy and reserved nature","Insecurity and doubt"],"correct_answer":"Adventure and confidence"},{"question":"What new challenge do Mia and her classmates face at the end of the chapter?","options":["Finding Ethan","Deciding whether to take a hidden path","Getting lost in the woods","Encountering other wild animals"],"correct_answer":"Deciding whether to take a hidden path"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_14_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_14_ch2_img1.png","plot_14_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":609,"reading_level":"Builder"}
