   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_14_11_14","title":"The Wildflower Trail","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Chapter 3: The Heart of the Wildflower Trail\n\nAs the sun climbed higher in the sky, the vibrant colors of the wildflowers seemed to pulse with life. Mia looked around, her heart racing with a mix of excitement and trepidation. \u201cDo you think we\u2019re close?\u201d she asked Ethan, who was momentarily distracted, trying to catch a glimpse of a butterfly flitting about.\n\n\u201cClose to what? Getting lost? We\u2019ve been wandering for hours!\u201d Ethan chuckled, his adventurous spirit undeterred by the growing tension in Mia's voice. The scent of clover and blooming daisies filled the air, but the thrill of their expedition was starting to wear thin. \n\nSuddenly, a rustling noise erupted from the nearby bushes. All eyes turned as a sleek deer emerged, its big, curious eyes studying the group. \u201cWow, look at that!\u201d whispered Jamie, one of their classmates, her eyes wide with amazement. Mia watched in awe as the deer gracefully bounded away, but the moment was short-lived. The sound of their surroundings shifted, replaced by an unsettling silence.\n\n\u201cWe should keep moving,\u201d Ethan urged, scanning the thick undergrowth for any sign of the trail. \u201cWe can\u2019t stay here forever.\u201d\n\nAs they continued deeper into the trail, the blooming flowers began to thin out, replaced by tall thickets that loomed like sentinels. Mia could feel the weight of uncertainty pressing down on her. \u201cWhat if we don\u2019t find our way back? What if we\u2019re out here all night?\u201d she whispered, her voice shaky.\n\nEthan placed a comforting hand on her shoulder. \u201cWe\u2019ll find a way. We have each other, remember? And besides,\u201d he added, grinning, \u201cyou\u2019re the one who knows all about nature. You can help us figure this out.\u201d\n\nMia felt a glimmer of confidence stir within her. \u201cOkay, let\u2019s look for something familiar,\u201d she suggested, her voice steadier now. \u201cThe stream! If we follow it, maybe it\u2019ll lead us back to the path.\u201d \n\nThe group nodded enthusiastically, and they began to retrace their steps toward the sound of flowing water. As they approached the stream, the sunlight shimmered on the surface, creating a pathway of sparkles. \u201cThere it is!\u201d shouted Ethan, pointing ahead. But just then, a loud crack echoed through the trees, making everyone jump.\n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Jamie gasped, her eyes darting around.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Ethan replied, staring into the thick woods, his bravado faltering. \u201cWe need to be careful.\u201d \n\nMia\u2019s stomach twisted as the noise repeated, closer this time. \u201cMaybe we should go the other way,\u201d she suggested, her voice barely above a whisper.\n\nBefore they could react, a massive figure burst through the bushes\u2014an enormous bear! It stood on its hind legs, surveying them with curious yet cautious eyes, its fur glistening in the sun. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cEveryone, stay calm!\u201d Ethan commanded, his previous confidence replaced by urgency. The bear let out a low growl, and Mia\u2019s heart raced faster than a hummingbird\u2019s wings. \u201cWe need a plan,\u201d Ethan continued, his voice steady. \u201cWe can\u2019t just run.\u201d\n\nMia felt her mind racing. \u201cMaybe if we back away slowly, we can get to the trees! Bears don\u2019t chase unless they feel threatened!\u201d\n\n\u201cOkay, on the count of three,\u201d Ethan said, his gaze never leaving the bear.\n\n\u201cThree\u2026 two\u2026 one\u2026 go!\u201d they all whispered, slowly inching backward, hearts pounding in unison. But as they moved, the bear shifted, its eyes narrowing. \n\nIn that pivotal moment, Mia realized they had to confront their fears together. \u201cWe can do this!\u201d she shouted, surprising herself with her own courage. \u201cIf we work as a team!\u201d\n\nThe bear let out another growl as if testing their resolve. \n\n\u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d Jamie whimpered, clinging to Mia\u2019s arm. \n\nMia took a deep breath, feeling her pulse steady. \u201cWe stick together. On my count, we make a break for the trees.\u201d \n\nAnd just at that moment, a loud snap resonated nearby. The bear\u2019s ears perked up, and it turned, its attention drawn away from them.\n\n\u201cNow!\u201d Ethan shouted, and they all sprinted toward the cover of the trees, the wildflower trail fading behind them.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they reached the trees, Mia glanced back, her heart still racing. They were safe, for now, but she knew they had to make another decision\u2014should they follow the now-trembling stream to safety, or attempt to find a different path altogether?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What creature do Mia and her classmates encounter in this chapter?","options":["A deer","A bear","A raccoon","A fox"],"correct_answer":"A bear"},{"question":"What strategy does Mia suggest to the group when they see the bear?","options":["To run away","To stand still","To back away slowly","To climb a tree"],"correct_answer":"To back away slowly"},{"question":"How does Mia feel about the adventure at the beginning of this chapter?","options":["Excited and carefree","Nervous and anxious","Angry and frustrated","Indifferent"],"correct_answer":"Nervous and anxious"},{"question":"What does Ethan encourage Mia to do during their adventure?","options":["To give up","To trust herself","To lead the group","To go back"],"correct_answer":"To trust herself"},{"question":"What important decision do the characters have to make at the end of the chapter?","options":["Whether to go to bed","Whether to follow the stream or find another path","Whether to leave the park","Whether to climb a mountain"],"correct_answer":"Whether to follow the stream or find another path"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_14_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_14_ch3_img1.png","plot_14_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":737,"reading_level":"Builder"}
