   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_14_11_14","title":"The Wildflower Trail","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the sun peeked through the trees, casting golden rays on the Wildflower Trail, Mia and Ethan gathered their classmates near a bubbling stream. The air was sweet with the scent of blooming flowers, and the vibrant colors around them made it feel as if they had stepped into a living painting. \u201cLook at those daisies!\u201d Mia exclaimed, her eyes sparkling. \u201cThey remind me of the ones in my grandmother\u2019s garden.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nEthan, ever the adventurer, grinned. \u201cLet\u2019s see if we can find more flowers along the path. Who\u2019s with us?\u201d With renewed enthusiasm, the group followed him, eager to discover new sights despite their earlier scare with the bear.\n\nAs they walked deeper into the woods, the atmosphere shifted. The cheerful chirping of birds was replaced by an eerie silence, and the trail narrowed. A sense of unease hovered like a fog, but Mia took a deep breath, reminding herself that they were on an adventure. \n\nSuddenly, Ethan stopped in his tracks. \u201cGuys, do you hear that?\u201d he whispered, a frown creasing his forehead. The group fell silent, straining their ears. It sounded like someone\u2014no, something\u2014was rustling in the bushes nearby. \n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s just a squirrel,\u201d suggested Jamie, one of their classmates, though her voice trembled slightly. \n\nMia\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s something else?\u201d she said, glancing at Ethan. She could feel her doubts creeping in again, but Ethan\u2019s steady gaze reassured her. \u201cWe can handle it. Let\u2019s check it out together.\u201d \n\nGathering their courage, they approached the bushes cautiously. Mia reached out, her fingers trembling as she pulled aside a low-hanging branch. To their surprise, they found a small, abandoned campsite, with a broken tent and scattered supplies. Ethan\u2019s eyes lit up with excitement. \u201cLook! This might belong to someone who got lost here too!\u201d\n\nBut as they explored, Mia noticed a glint of something shiny beneath the leaves. She knelt down, brushing away the dirt. \u201cWhat\u2019s this?\u201d she asked, revealing an old compass. It was tarnished but still functional. \n\n\u201cMaybe it could help us find our way back!\u201d Ethan exclaimed. \n\nJust then, a loud snap echoed through the trees, making them all jump. They turned to see a large branch fall from a nearby tree, crashing to the ground. The rumble of the earth seemed to mirror their racing hearts. \u201cWe need to get out of here,\u201d Mia urged, her voice rising. \n\n\u201cWe can\u2019t let fear take over,\u201d Ethan reminded her. \u201cWe have the compass now. Let\u2019s use it!\u201d \n\nWith a newfound sense of purpose, they huddled together, deciding to follow the compass north. As they walked, whispers of fear and uncertainty began to fade, replaced by a bond strengthened through shared struggles. \n\nMia felt a surge of hope. \u201cWe can do this. Together.\u201d \n\nThey pressed on, each step filling them with determination. In that moment, the shadows of doubt seemed to lift, and for the first time in a long while, Mia truly believed they would find their way home.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith the compass in hand, they walked side by side. Their laughter began to echo through the trees, a melody of friendship and bravery woven into the wilderness. But as they rounded a bend, they came face to face with a steep cliff dropping into a rushing river below.\n\n\u201cWhat now?\u201d Mia whispered, her heart thumping in her chest. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s figure it out, just like we always have,\u201d Ethan replied, his voice steady but laced with urgency. \u201cTogether.\u201d \n\nAs they stood at the edge, the journey back to safety hung in the balance, and uncertainty loomed ahead. But with the compass guiding them and their friendship unwavering, they were ready to face whatever came next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia find underneath the leaves?","options":["A broken tent","A shiny compass","A wildflower","A map"],"correct_answer":"A shiny compass"},{"question":"What does Ethan suggest they do when they hear a rustling noise?","options":["Run away","Check it out together","Ignore it","Climb a tree"],"correct_answer":"Check it out together"},{"question":"How does Mia feel when they find the compass?","options":["Scared","Hopeful","Angry","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Hopeful"},{"question":"What happens when they approach the cliff?","options":["They find a way to cross","They discover more wildflowers","They are faced with uncertainty","They meet more hikers"],"correct_answer":"They are faced with uncertainty"},{"question":"What key theme is highlighted in this chapter?","options":["Friendship and teamwork","Fear of the dark","Adventure in the city","Cooking together"],"correct_answer":"Friendship and teamwork"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_14_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_14_ch4_img1.png","plot_14_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":628,"reading_level":"Builder"}
