   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_15_7_10","title":"The Secret of Timberwood","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Tyler and Bella stood at the edge of the two glowing paths, their hearts racing. The forest was thick with trees that seemed to whisper secrets. \u201cWhich way do you think we should go, Bella?\u201d Tyler asked, scratching his dog\u2019s ears.\n\nBella wagged her tail, sniffing the air. \u201cI wish you could talk and tell me!\u201d Tyler laughed. He looked down the left path. It shimmered with a bright, golden light. The right path glowed a soft, calming blue.\n\n\u201cGolden means treasure!\u201d Tyler said, pointing excitedly. \u201cBut the blue path looks safe.\u201d He rubbed his chin, trying to decide. Just then, a low growl echoed from the blue path. \n\nTyler\u2019s stomach dropped. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d \n\nBella\u2019s ears perked up. \u201cWe should be careful!\u201d she barked.\n\nSuddenly, out of the shadows, a giant wolf stepped into view! It had sparkling fur and glowing eyes that seemed to see right through them. \n\n\u201cWhat do you want?\u201d Tyler asked, trying to sound brave. \n\n\u201cI guard the heart of Timberwood,\u201d the wolf said in a deep voice. \u201cYou must answer my question to pass.\u201d \n\nTyler nodded, feeling nervous but excited. \u201cOkay, what\u2019s the question?\u201d\n\n\u201cThe wish you seek is tied to those you love. What would you sacrifice for their happiness?\u201d the wolf challenged.\n\nTyler gasped. He thought of his mom, his friends, and, of course, Bella. \u201cI would give up anything, even my wishes!\u201d\n\nThe wolf\u2019s eyes softened. \u201cVery well. But remember, wishes can come with great responsibility.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nBella looked up at Tyler, her tail wagging. \u201cYou\u2019re so brave, Tyler!\u201d she said, giving him a nudge.\n\n\u201cThanks, Bella! But we still need to choose a path.\u201d Tyler knew he had to make a decision. The golden path sparkled invitingly, but the blue path felt safer. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go blue,\u201d he said, taking a deep breath. \u201cI think it might lead us to the Wishing Tree.\u201d \n\nAs they stepped onto the blue path, the woods became quieter. Suddenly, a flicker of light danced ahead. Tyler and Bella hurried toward it. \n\n\u201cCome on, Bella! Let\u2019s see what it is!\u201d Tyler exclaimed.\n\nThey reached a clearing where a beautiful blue flower glowed softly. The air shimmered, and out popped a tiny forest sprite. \u201cYou\u2019ve chosen wisely!\u201d she chirped with a smile. \u201cBut you must hurry! The path is closing soon!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nTyler\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat do we do?\u201d he asked. \n\n\u201cFollow me!\u201d the sprite said, leading them deeper into the woods.\n\nTyler looked back and felt a rush of excitement mixed with fear. \u201cThis is it, Bella! We\u2019re really going to find the Wishing Tree!\u201d\n\nBut just then, a loud crack sounded above them. Tyler looked up. A large branch was falling! \n\n\u201cRun!\u201d he shouted, and they sprinted forward, the branch crashing down right where they had just been standing. \n\nWhat would happen next?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does the giant wolf guard?","options":["A treasure","The heart of Timberwood","A magical spell","A hidden cave"],"correct_answer":"The heart of Timberwood"},{"question":"What color is the path that Tyler and Bella choose?","options":["Red","Blue","Green","Yellow"],"correct_answer":"Blue"},{"question":"What does Tyler say he would sacrifice?","options":["His wishes","His dog","His map","His backpack"],"correct_answer":"His wishes"},{"question":"What does the forest sprite tell Tyler and Bella?","options":["To go back","To hurry","To rest","To fly"],"correct_answer":"To hurry"},{"question":"What happens at the end of the chapter?","options":["They find the Wishing Tree","A branch falls","They meet another creature","They take a break"],"correct_answer":"A branch falls"}]},"images":null,"word_count":481,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
