   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_15_11_14","title":"The Secret of Timberwood","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Tyler sat cross-legged on the dusty wooden floor of his attic, the smell of old books and forgotten treasures enveloping him like a warm blanket. Sunlight streamed through a small window, illuminating the cobwebs in the corners and casting a golden glow on the objects piled around him. He rummaged through an old trunk, his fingers brushing against faded photographs and rusty toys, when something shiny caught his eye. It was a crumpled piece of parchment, yellowed with age.\n\n\u201cBella! Come here!\u201d he called, a grin spreading across his face as his loyal golden retriever bounded up the attic stairs, her tail wagging like a flag. The dog sniffed curiously at the parchment as Tyler unfolded it, revealing a map. His eyes widened. \u201cLook at this, Bella! It\u2019s a treasure map!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe map was covered in swirling lines and strange symbols, marking a path that led to a place called Timberwood. Tyler recalled the stories his grandfather used to tell about a magical forest where wishes came true. His heart raced with excitement. Could it be real? \u201cC\u2019mon, girl! We have to go find this place!\u201d \n\nAfter a quick breakfast, Tyler packed a small backpack with essentials\u2014water, snacks, a flashlight, and the map\u2014while Bella sat patiently, ears perked. They stepped outside into the crisp morning air, the sun shining brightly against a clear blue sky. \u201cToday\u2019s the day!\u201d Tyler declared, determination bubbling inside him. \n\nAs they walked through the familiar streets of their quiet town, Tyler felt a mix of thrill and trepidation. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s just a fairy tale?\u201d he murmured, glancing down at Bella, who seemed to sense his uncertainty. She wagged her tail and nudged him with her nose, as if saying, \u201cLet\u2019s do this!\u201d\n\nAfter an hour of walking, the town faded behind them and the trees began to grow taller and denser. Tyler could hear the distant sound of a bubbling stream and the rustling of leaves in the wind. \u201cWe\u2019re getting close,\u201d he whispered, his heart pounding. But then, as they stepped into the shade of a particularly large oak tree, a chill ran down his spine. He could have sworn he heard a whisper, soft and fleeting, like the rustling of leaves.\n\n\u201cDid you hear that, Bella?\u201d he asked, looking around. But Bella only tilted her head curiously, her golden eyes wide. Ignoring the feeling of unease, Tyler pressed on, the map clutched tightly in his hands. They soon reached a narrow path, overgrown with vines and flowers that seemed to glow subtly in the dim light. \n\n\u201cIt\u2019s beautiful,\u201d he breathed, but his excitement was laced with apprehension. What lay ahead? As they ventured deeper, the trees began to close in, their branches twisting together like gnarled hands. Shadows danced across the ground, and the air felt electric with mystery. \n\nSuddenly, Bella halted, her ears perked up, and she growled softly. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, girl?\u201d Tyler whispered, scanning the area. Then, from behind a thicket, a figure emerged\u2014a tall, cloaked figure with a face obscured by a hood. Tyler\u2019s heart raced. Was this the guardian of Timberwood?\n\n\u201cWho dares to enter the realm of Timberwood?\u201d the figure asked, voice deep and resonant. \n\n\u201cUh, I\u2014I\u2019m Tyler, and this is Bella,\u201d he stammered, feeling small and vulnerable. \u201cWe\u2019re looking for Timberwood. I found a map.\u201d \n\nThe guardian stepped closer, the shadows shifting around him. \u201cMany seek the wishes of Timberwood, but few understand the cost,\u201d he warned. Tyler swallowed hard. He had heard the stories, but they had never felt so real until now. Perhaps this adventure was more than just a quest for wishes. It was about facing fears and discovering who he truly was.\n\n\u201cAre you brave enough to continue?\u201d the guardian asked, his voice challenging. Tyler glanced at Bella, who stared back at him with unwavering loyalty. \u201cYes,\u201d he replied, determination hardening in his chest. \u201cWe\u2019re ready.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith that, the guardian stepped aside, revealing a path that shimmered as if lit from within. Tyler took a deep breath, steeling himself for whatever challenges lay ahead. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go, Bella,\u201d he said, taking his first step into Timberwood. The adventure had just begun.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Tyler find in the attic?","options":["A treasure chest","An old map","A dusty book","A photograph"],"correct_answer":"An old map"},{"question":"Who accompanies Tyler on his adventure?","options":["His sister","His best friend","His dog Bella","His grandfather"],"correct_answer":"His dog Bella"},{"question":"What warning does the guardian give Tyler?","options":["The forest is dangerous","Wishes come at a cost","He must leave Bella behind","He needs a special key"],"correct_answer":"Wishes come at a cost"},{"question":"What emotion does Tyler feel when entering the forest?","options":["Excitement","Boredom","Fear","Confusion"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"},{"question":"What is the main theme introduced in this chapter?","options":["Friendship and loyalty","The importance of school","Adventure and exploration","The power of technology"],"correct_answer":"Friendship and loyalty"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_15_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_15_ch1_img1.png","plot_15_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":709,"reading_level":"Builder"}
