   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_15_15_18","title":"The Secret of Timberwood","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Lost in the Wild","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The forest was alive with an electric hum as Tyler and Bella forged deeper into Timberwood. Towering trees loomed above, their leaves filtering the sunlight into a kaleidoscope of greens and golds. Tyler's heart raced, not only from excitement but from the gnawing doubts that had settled in his mind since confronting the wolf. What if the wish he sought was too great a price? Tyler absently stroked Bella's fur as they walked, the warm comfort of his dog grounding him in the moment. \n\n\u201cDo you think it\u2019s true?\u201d he asked Bella, who looked up at him with her big, trusting eyes. \u201cDo you think wishes can really come true?\u201d\n\nBella tilted her head, and Tyler couldn\u2019t help but smile. \u201cMaybe we\u2019ll find out soon enough.\u201d \n\nAs they ventured further, the path twisted and turned, leading them to a glistening stream. The water sparkled like diamonds, and Tyler knelt down to splash his fingers in it. He felt a sense of peace wash over him, but it was short-lived. \n\n\u201cHey, Bella, come look at this!\u201d he called, but the dog remained on high alert, sniffing the air as if she sensed something he could not. \n\nSuddenly, a rustling sound broke through the tranquility, and Tyler straightened, heart pounding. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d \n\nBefore he could register his fear, a figure emerged from the shadows. It was a tall man with long hair and wise, piercing eyes, dressed in earthy tones that mirrored the forest. A guardian. \n\n\u201cWelcome, seeker of wishes,\u201d the man said, his voice like the rustle of leaves in a gentle breeze. \u201cI am the Guardian of Timberwood.\u201d\n\nTyler swallowed hard. \u201cAre you\u2026 are you the one who grants wishes?\u201d \n\nThe guardian smiled knowingly. \u201cWishes can only be granted if the heart is true and the sacrifice is genuine.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Tyler asked, a chill running down his spine. \n\n\u201cEvery wish has a cost. What you seek, young one, may come with a price you\u2019re not yet prepared to pay.\u201d \n\nTyler's thoughts raced. Was he willing to sacrifice everything for a fleeting wish? He thought of his mother\u2019s smile, and his heart clenched. \u201cI want to save my mom. She\u2019s sick. If I can wish for her to be better\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cBut at what cost?\u201d the guardian interrupted. Tyler saw a flicker of concern in the guardian\u2019s eyes, a hint that the price might be steep. \n\nBefore he could respond, the forest shuddered. The ground beneath them trembled, and Tyler stumbled, reaching for Bella. She barked fiercely, her instincts sharpening as a figure emerged from the thick underbrush. \n\nIt was the wolf again, but this time it was not just a beast\u2014its eyes glowed a deep crimson, and a low growl emanated from its throat. Tyler felt a wave of terror wash over him, but beneath it flickered a spark of determination. He would not let fear dictate his actions.\n\nThe guardian stepped forward. \u201cThis is the true test of courage, Tyler. Face your fear, or it will consume you.\u201d \n\nWith Bella at his side, Tyler squared his shoulders, ready to confront the threat. \u201cI won\u2019t back down!\u201d he shouted, his voice trembling but strong. \n\nThe wolf lunged, snapping its jaws, but Tyler stood his ground, heart racing. Time seemed to slow as he focused on the creature, thoughts swirling in his mind\u2014he thought of his mother, of the wish he might make, and of the sacrifice it could demand. \n\nA brilliant light erupted from the guardian\u2019s hands, illuminating the clearing. \u201cFace it, Tyler! You must confront the truth of your heart!\u201d\n\nIn that moment, Tyler saw images flash before him: his mother smiling, him standing alone, and then something darker\u2014a void where his dreams should be. \n\n\u201cChoose wisely!\u201d the guardian\u2019s voice rang out, echoing in the chaos. \n\nWith his heart pounding, Tyler had to make a decision. Would he fight for his wish, or would he turn and run? The wolf charged, and as Tyler braced for impact, a decision loomed heavy in the air.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does the Guardian of Timberwood warn Tyler about wishes?","options":["They can be granted freely","There is always a cost","They are easy to achieve","Only good wishes are granted"],"correct_answer":"There is always a cost"},{"question":"What is Tyler's primary motivation for seeking a wish?","options":["To become famous","To save his mother","To gain wealth","To escape reality"],"correct_answer":"To save his mother"},{"question":"What does the wolf symbolize in this chapter?","options":["Fear and danger","Friendship","Wisdom","Joy"],"correct_answer":"Fear and danger"},{"question":"What internal conflict is Tyler facing in this chapter?","options":["Wanting to give up","Choosing between fear and bravery","Desiring a different life","Losing his friendship"],"correct_answer":"Choosing between fear and bravery"},{"question":"How does the chapter end?","options":["With Tyler running away","With a clear resolution","With a cliffhanger involving the wolf","With a wish granted"],"correct_answer":"With a cliffhanger involving the wolf"}]},"images":null,"word_count":685,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
