   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_6_7_10","title":"The Map of Forgotten Dreams","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Treasure Hunt","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Mia climbed the old wooden stairs to her grandmother's attic. Dust danced in the sunlight that peeked through the small window. The attic was a treasure chest of memories. Boxes were piled high, and old toys sat in the corners. Mia loved exploring this magical place.\n\n\u201cWow, look at all this stuff!\u201d Mia exclaimed. She brushed off a dusty box and opened it. Inside, she found a faded blanket, some old photos, and a shiny object. \n\n\u201cWhat did you find, Mia?\u201d asked Sam, her best friend, who followed her up the stairs. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know yet!\u201d Mia replied, holding up the shiny object. It was a compass, spinning wildly. \n\nToby, Mia\u2019s playful dog, sniffed around the attic. He barked happily, excited to be with his friends. \n\nSuddenly, Mia spotted something unusual sticking out from under an old trunk. She pulled it out carefully. It was a rolled-up map! \n\n\u201cLook at this!\u201d she shouted. \n\nSam leaned in closer, squinting at the parchment. \u201cIt looks really old! What does it say?\u201d\n\nMia unfolded the map. It was covered in strange symbols and colorful drawings of mountains and trees. \u201cI think it leads to a treasure in the Enchanted Forest!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMia and Sam shared wide-eyed looks. \u201cA treasure hunt? This is going to be amazing!\u201d said Sam, already imagining magical adventures. \n\nToby wagged his tail, as if he also wanted to join the fun. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Mia declared. \u201cWe need to find this treasure before Mr. Grizzle does!\u201d\n\n\u201cWho\u2019s Mr. Grizzle?\u201d Sam asked, eyebrows raised.\n\n\u201cHe\u2019s a treasure hunter! I heard my grandma talking about him. He\u2019s always looking for lost treasure and he\u2019s really sneaky.\u201d \n\n\u201cThen we have to be extra careful!\u201d Sam said. \n\nWith the map tucked under her arm, Mia felt brave. \u201cDon\u2019t worry! We can solve any riddle and face any danger together!\u201d \n\nJust as they were about to leave the attic, a loud crash came from below. It sounded like something heavy had fallen. They exchanged worried glances.\n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Sam whispered. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we should be careful,\u201d Mia replied. \n\nWith Toby leading the way, they tiptoed down the stairs, heartbeats racing. What if Mr. Grizzle was already here?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia clutched the map tightly. This was just the beginning of their adventure. \n\n\u201cAre you ready, Toby?\u201d she asked. Toby barked, his tail wagging. \u201cLet\u2019s find that treasure!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia find in her grandmother's attic?","options":["A compass","A treasure chest","A book","A painting"],"correct_answer":"A compass"},{"question":"Who is Mia's best friend?","options":["Toby","Mr. Grizzle","Sam","Her grandmother"],"correct_answer":"Sam"},{"question":"What does the map lead to?","options":["A hidden cave","A treasure","A castle","A garden"],"correct_answer":"A treasure"},{"question":"Who is Mr. Grizzle?","options":["A friendly dog","A treasure hunter","Mia's father","A magical creature"],"correct_answer":"A treasure hunter"},{"question":"What did they hear before leaving the attic?","options":["A music box","A loud crash","Someone calling","A bird singing"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_6_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_6_ch1_img1.png","plot_6_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":406,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
