   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_6_7_10","title":"The Map of Forgotten Dreams","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Treasure Hunt","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Mia, Sam, and Toby stood at the mouth of the dark cave. The air was cool and smelled of damp earth. \u201cAre we really going in there?\u201d Sam asked, peeking into the shadows.\n\n\u201cOf course!\u201d Mia replied, determination shining in her eyes. \u201cWe have to find the treasure before Mr. Grizzle does!\u201d\n\nToby barked happily, ready for another adventure. They took a deep breath and stepped inside. The cave was darker than they expected, but Mia pulled out her flashlight. The beam danced across the walls, revealing sparkling stones.\n\n\u201cThis looks magical!\u201d Sam exclaimed. \u201cLook at all the colors!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they walked deeper, they saw strange markings on the walls. \u201cThese look like more riddles!\u201d Mia said, pointing. \u201cLet\u2019s figure them out!\u201d\n\nThe first riddle read, \u201cWhat has roots as nobody sees, is taller than trees.\u201d \n\nMia thought hard. \u201cI know! It\u2019s a mountain!\u201d\n\nToby wagged his tail, as if cheering for Mia. \u201cYes! Now let\u2019s find the next one!\u201d They searched the cave until Sam shouted, \u201cOver here!\u201d\n\nHe found another riddle. \u201cWhat runs but never walks, has a mouth but never talks.\u201d\n\nMia giggled. \u201cThat\u2019s a river!\u201d \n\nJust then, they heard footsteps. Mr. Grizzle was close! \u201cHurry!\u201d Sam whispered, and they raced further into the cave.\n\nSuddenly, they stumbled upon a hidden chamber filled with glowing crystals. \u201cWow!\u201d Mia gasped. \u201cLook at this place!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut before they could admire it, Mr. Grizzle appeared, a greedy grin on his face. \u201cYou\u2019ll never find the treasure! It\u2019s mine!\u201d\n\n\u201cWe\u2019ll see about that!\u201d Mia shouted, feeling brave. \n\nWith Toby by her side, they darted past him, hearts pounding. \u201cWe have to find a way out!\u201d Sam urged, and they sprinted toward the exit, the cave alive with their laughter and shouts. \n\nThey could hear Mr. Grizzle behind them, but Mia felt a spark of hope. They were close to understanding the treasure\u2019s true meaning. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s get to the forest!\u201d Mia cried. \u201cThe adventure isn\u2019t over yet!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia, Sam, and Toby find in the cave?","options":["A treasure chest","Glowing crystals","A waterfall","A treasure map"],"correct_answer":"Glowing crystals"},{"question":"What was the first riddle they solved?","options":["What runs but never walks?","What has roots as nobody sees?","What is taller than trees?","What has a mouth but never talks?"],"correct_answer":"What has roots as nobody sees?"},{"question":"Who is chasing Mia, Sam, and Toby?","options":["A friendly wizard","Mr. Grizzle","A magical creature","A forest ranger"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Grizzle"},{"question":"How did Mia feel while solving the riddles?","options":["Scared","Bored","Brave","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Brave"},{"question":"What did Mia shout as they escaped the cave?","options":["The adventure is over!","Let\u2019s get to the forest!","We found the treasure!","I\u2019m scared!"],"correct_answer":"Let\u2019s get to the forest!"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_6_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_6_ch4_img1.png","plot_6_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":339,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
