   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_6_11_14","title":"The Map of Forgotten Dreams","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Treasure Hunt","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The sun peeked through the canopy of leaves as Mia, Sam, and Toby ventured deeper into the enchanted forest. Shafts of golden light danced on the ground, illuminating a tapestry of vibrant plants and flowers that swayed gently in the breeze. The air was fragrant with the scent of pine and wildflowers, creating a magical atmosphere that made Mia\u2019s heart race with excitement. \n\n\u201cLook at this place! It\u2019s like something out of a dream!\u201d Sam exclaimed, his eyes wide with wonder. He bent down to examine a cluster of blue blossoms that sparkled like jewels. \n\nToby barked happily, darting ahead to chase a fluttering butterfly. Mia chuckled at her dog\u2019s playful antics, but as the laughter faded, a knot of worry twisted in her stomach. They had to find the treasure before Mr. Grizzle did, and time was running out.\n\n\u201cOkay, according to the map,\u201d Mia said, spreading the parchment on a moss-covered rock, \u201cwe should head towards the Silver Stream. The next clue is supposed to be hidden near a waterfall.\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Sam urged, pulling the map closer to him. But just as they were about to set off, a rustling noise caught their attention. They turned to see Mr. Grizzle emerging from the shadows, a sly grin on his face.\n\n\u201cLooking for something?\u201d he taunted, his voice dripping with mockery. \u201cYou really think you can outsmart me? I\u2019ve been searching for that treasure for years!\u201d \n\nMia felt her heart pound loudly in her chest. \u201cWe can\u2019t let him scare us, Mia,\u201d Sam whispered, clenching his fists. \u201cWe have to keep going!\u201d\n\nWith a determined nod, Mia squared her shoulders. \u201cYou\u2019re right. We won\u2019t let him win.\u201d She held up the map, pointing to the next destination. \u201cLet\u2019s find that waterfall!\u201d\n\nAs they turned to leave, Mr. Grizzle stepped forward, blocking their path. \u201cNot so fast, kids. You\u2019ll need to solve my riddle first.\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat? A riddle?\u201d Sam asked, his face scrunching in confusion. \n\n\u201cIndeed,\u201d Mr. Grizzle chuckled, his eyes glinting mischievously. \u201cWhat has roots as nobody sees, is taller than trees, up, up it goes, and yet never grows?\u201d \n\nMia\u2019s mind raced. She\u2019d heard this riddle before. \u201cIt\u2019s a mountain!\u201d she shouted, feeling a surge of confidence. \n\nMr. Grizzle narrowed his eyes, but before he could respond, a loud growl echoed from the trees. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, a massive creature with shimmering scales and fierce, glowing eyes leaped into view. It was a dragon! The ground trembled beneath its weight, and Mia felt a rush of fear. \u201cWhat are we going to do?\u201d she whispered, her heart racing.\n\n\u201cBack away slowly,\u201d Sam suggested, but the dragon let out a fearsome roar that made the air vibrate. \n\nWith no time to think, Mia grabbed Toby\u2019s collar and yelled, \u201cRun!\u201d They darted into the underbrush, branches slapping against their arms as they fled. Behind them, they could hear Mr. Grizzle\u2019s frustrated shouts as he too scrambled away from the beast.\n\nBreathless, they stumbled into a clearing, the waterfall glimmering in the distance. \u201cWe have to get to the waterfall!\u201d Mia shouted, adrenaline pumping through her veins. \u201cThat\u2019s where the next clue is!\u201d\n\nBut just as they were about to move forward, Sam stopped. \u201cMia, wait! What if the treasure isn\u2019t what we think? What if we find something much more important?\u201d\n\nMia looked into her friend\u2019s earnest eyes. \u201cMaybe the true treasure is the journey we\u2019re on and the dreams we\u2019ve almost forgotten,\u201d she replied, her heart swelling with resolve. \n\nThey stood at the edge of the clearing, the sound of rushing water echoing in their ears, when suddenly, the dragon appeared again, blocking their path to the waterfall. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia took a deep breath. \u201cWe can\u2019t turn back now. This is our chance to find out what really lies ahead.\u201d\n\nWith a glance at Sam and a nod to Toby, they prepared to face the dragon together, knowing that their journey was only just beginning.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mr. Grizzle challenge Mia and Sam to solve?","options":["A puzzle","A riddle","A maze","A mystery"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What creature unexpectedly appears in the forest?","options":["A unicorn","A dragon","A troll","A wolf"],"correct_answer":"A dragon"},{"question":"What is the first clue that Mia finds on the map?","options":["A waterfall","A mountain","A cave","A tree"],"correct_answer":"A waterfall"},{"question":"How does Mia feel about their journey as they reach the waterfall?","options":["Afraid","Excited","Indifferent","Disappointed"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What does Sam suggest about the treasure?","options":["It might be dangerous","It could be a dream","It might be gold","It could be something more important"],"correct_answer":"It could be something more important"}]},"images":null,"word_count":679,"reading_level":"Builder"}
