   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_7_11_14","title":"Pirates of Maplewood Cove","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Treasure Hunt","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun dipped low over Maplewood Cove, casting a golden glow on the quaint seaside town. Jake stood on the weathered dock, his heart racing with excitement. \"This is it, Lily! I can feel it!\" he exclaimed, his eyes sparkling like the waves lapping at the shore. Beside him, Lily, his younger sister, rolled her eyes but couldn't suppress a grin. She loved how adventurous Jake always was.\n\n\"Are you sure it's really a pirate's journal?\" she asked, adjusting her cap with a determined tilt. The two siblings had spent the last few days rummaging through their attic, and there, tucked away beneath a pile of dusty books, they found it\u2014an old, tattered journal with mysterious scribbles and drawings of treasure maps. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they traced the worn pages, one particular entry caught their eye. \"Buried treasure lies on Midnight Isle, where the tides whisper secrets of the past,\" it read. Jake\u2019s adventurous spirit ignited. \u201cWe have to go find it! Just imagine the stories we could tell!\u201d \n\nLily chewed her lip, feeling a flutter of nerves. \u201cBut what if it\u2019s dangerous? What if we run into real pirates?\u201d \n\nJake shrugged, his enthusiasm unyielding. \u201cThat\u2019s the fun part! Besides, we\u2019ll have Captain Finn to help us.\u201d \n\nCaptain Finn, their quirky neighbor, was a retired sailor who claimed to have sailed with pirates in his youth. He was always full of wild tales, and the kids adored him. They rushed to his house, their hearts pounding with anticipation.\n\n\u201cCaptain Finn! Captain Finn!\u201d Jake called as they pounded on the old wooden door. Moments later, the door creaked open, revealing a disheveled old man with a twinkle in his eyes. His beard was long and white, resembling a wispy cloud.\n\n\u201cAhoy, young adventurers!\u201d he boomed, a grin spreading across his face. \u201cWhat brings ye to my humble abode?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe found a pirate's journal!\u201d Lily exclaimed, nearly bouncing on her toes. \u201cIt says there\u2019s treasure on Midnight Isle!\u201d\n\nFinn\u2019s eyes widened, and he rubbed his chin thoughtfully. \u201cTreasure, you say? Aye, I\u2019ve heard whispers of that isle. It\u2019s mysterious and dangerous, filled with legends of ghosts and treacherous tides.\u201d \n\n\u201cThen we have to go, Captain!\u201d Jake insisted. \u201cWe need your help to build a raft and find it before anyone else does.\u201d\n\nFinn chuckled, his laugh like the soft rumble of thunder. \u201cAlright, I\u2019m in! But we\u2019ll need proper supplies. Meet me at the cove before dawn. We\u2019ll show those treasure hunters what we\u2019re made of!\u201d\n\nAs they left Finn\u2019s house, Lily felt a mix of excitement and fear. \u201cWhat if we don\u2019t find it? What if Bella gets there first?\u201d Bella was a girl from school, smart and sly, always ready to best Jake and Lily at everything. The thought of losing to her sent a shiver down her spine.\n\nJake placed a comforting hand on her shoulder. \u201cWe\u2019ll find it, Lily. Together.\u201d \n\nAs night fell, the siblings lay in their beds, the moonlight painting the room in silver. Jake stared at the ceiling, dreaming of adventures while Lily snuggled under the covers, the pirate journal clutched tightly in her arms. \n\nThe next morning, they rose with the sun, the prospect of adventure bubbling in their hearts. They quickly made their way to the cove, the salty breeze filling their lungs with possibilities. Little did they know, a rival crew was already hot on their trail.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cOkay, let\u2019s get to work!\u201d Jake shouted, excitement bubbling over. They set about gathering materials for a raft, unaware of the challenges that awaited them on the tides of fate.\n\nWith every board they nailed, the thrill of the treasure grew stronger, and the shadow of Bella and her crew loomed ever closer. \n\nWould they discover the secrets hidden within Midnight Isle? Only time would tell.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What discovery do Jake and Lily make in the attic?","options":["A map of the town","An old pirate's journal","A treasure chest","A photo album"],"correct_answer":"An old pirate's journal"},{"question":"Who do Jake and Lily ask for help in finding the treasure?","options":["Their parents","Their friends","Captain Finn","Bella"],"correct_answer":"Captain Finn"},{"question":"What is the main conflict introduced in this chapter?","options":["Jake and Lily want a pet","There is a storm coming","A rival crew led by Bella is after the treasure","Captain Finn forgets his map"],"correct_answer":"A rival crew led by Bella is after the treasure"},{"question":"What emotion does Lily express about the adventure?","options":["Excitement","Fear","Anger","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Fear"},{"question":"What time do Jake and Lily plan to meet Captain Finn?","options":["Midnight","At sunset","Before dawn","In the afternoon"],"correct_answer":"Before dawn"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_7_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_7_ch1_img1.png","plot_7_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":650,"reading_level":"Builder"}
