   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_7_11_14","title":"Pirates of Maplewood Cove","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Treasure Hunt","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: Tides of Trouble\n\nAs the sun peeked over the horizon, its golden rays danced upon the waves of Maplewood Cove, casting flickering lights that seemed to whisper secrets. Jake and Lily stood at the edge of the dock, their hearts thumping in rhythm with the gentle lapping of the water. With Captain Finn bustling around, attaching makeshift sails to their homemade raft, the siblings exchanged excited glances.\n\n\u201cDo you think the treasure is really out there, Jake?\u201d Lily asked, her voice bubbling with anticipation. She twirled a strand of her hair, her blue eyes wide with wonder.\n\n\u201cAbsolutely! This is no ordinary treasure hunt!\u201d Jake replied, puffing out his chest like a pirate captain. \u201cBut we need to be careful. That journal mentioned treacherous tides. We can\u2019t underestimate the sea.\u201d\n\nJust then, Captain Finn, with his scruffy beard and twinkling eyes, interrupted their conversation. \u201cAye, my hearties! Are ye ready to brave the waves? The sea has a mind of its own, and it won\u2019t give up its secrets easily.\u201d He pointed dramatically toward the horizon, where the mysterious outline of Midnight Isle loomed like a dark giant.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe raft bobbed eagerly against the dock, as if it too could sense the adventure ahead. With a final check of their supplies\u2014an old compass, some snacks, and the pirate journal\u2014the trio set sail, their spirits soaring like the gulls above.\n\nAs they paddled into deeper waters, the gentle rhythm of their strokes began to match the pulse of the ocean. But soon, the cheerful breeze turned ominous. Dark clouds gathered, swirling overhead, and the waves began to slap against the raft with a growing intensity. Jake strained to keep the raft steady, while Lily clutched the journal to her chest.\n\n\u201cHold on tight!\u201d Jake shouted, his voice rising above the growing roar of the wind. Suddenly, a sharp splash broke the surface, and a rival ship emerged from behind a curtain of rain. A sleek, well-crafted boat with a crew of determined-looking kids was heading straight for them. At the helm stood Bella, the self-proclaimed treasure hunter who had a knack for getting what she wanted.\n\n\u201cLook who we have here,\u201d Bella sneered, her eyes glinting like daggers. \u201cA couple of wannabe pirates and an old sea dog. I hope you\u2019re not too attached to your little raft. It\u2019ll be at the bottom of the cove soon enough!\u201d\n\nJake clenched his fists, feeling a rush of anger. \u201cWe\u2019re not afraid of you, Bella! We\u2019ll find that treasure before you do!\u201d\n\nBut the wind howled louder, and a wave crashed against their raft, nearly sending them tumbling into the churning sea. Lily squealed, her heart racing. \u201cJake! What do we do?\u201d\n\n\u201cSteer away! We need to get to the island before she does!\u201d Jake shouted, his voice steady despite the fear bubbling inside him. As they fought to control the raft, Jake realized that this was more than just about treasure. It was about proving to himself\u2014and to Lily\u2014that they could face any storm together.\n\nWith renewed determination, the siblings paddled harder, their eyes locked on the island in the distance. But with Bella\u2019s crew gaining speed behind them, the race for the treasure had truly begun.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nJust as they neared the island's rocky shore, another wave surged forward, sending a shudder through the raft. Jake and Lily braced themselves, knowing that their adventure was only just beginning, and the tides of trouble were far from over.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Jake and Lily discover at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["A rival treasure map","An old pirate's journal","A hidden cave","A storm warning"],"correct_answer":"An old pirate's journal"},{"question":"Who is the rival treasure hunter that they encounter?","options":["Captain Finn","Bella","A mysterious stranger","Their father"],"correct_answer":"Bella"},{"question":"What happens when they encounter a storm?","options":["The raft sinks","They find the treasure","They almost fall into the sea","They turn back home"],"correct_answer":"They almost fall into the sea"},{"question":"What are Jake's feelings as they face the storm?","options":["Fearful but determined","Excited and careless","Indifferent","Angry and rebellious"],"correct_answer":"Fearful but determined"},{"question":"What do they need to do to reach Midnight Isle first?","options":["Steer away from the storm","Paddle faster","Call for help","Turn back home"],"correct_answer":"Paddle faster"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_7_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_7_ch2_img1.png","plot_7_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":591,"reading_level":"Builder"}
