   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_9_7_10","title":"Hidden Treasures of Harmony Hill","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Treasure Hunt","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the sun rose over Harmony Hill, Sophie gathered her friends. \u201cWe need to find the cave today!\u201d she said, excitement bubbling in her voice. Leo adjusted his glasses. \u201cI\u2019ve been studying the map. It shows a path through the wildflower field.\u201d\n\nEmma painted a picture in her mind. \u201cLet\u2019s imagine finding the treasure! It will be sparkly, and we can share it!\u201d Max felt nervous. \u201cWhat if those older kids come back? They\u2019ll try to ruin everything again.\u201d\n\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry, Max. We\u2019re stronger together!\u201d Sophie cheered. They set off, walking through the sunny park. Bright flowers danced in the breeze. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, they heard laughter behind them. The older kids were back! \u201cWhat are you losers doing?\u201d one of them shouted. They threw a stick onto the path, trying to trip the friends.\n\n\u201cStay calm!\u201d Sophie whispered. \u201cLet\u2019s stick to the plan.\u201d The friends stepped carefully around the stick. Leo pointed to a big rock. \u201cLook! The map indicates we should go that way!\u201d \n\nAs they walked, Emma spotted something shiny in the grass. \u201cWhat is that?\u201d she asked. She bent down and picked up a small silver key. \u201cThis could be important!\u201d she exclaimed.\n\nJust then, the older kids caught up. \u201cYou think you can outsmart us?\u201d one of them sneered. Sophie took a deep breath. \u201cWe can solve this challenge. Let\u2019s work together!\u201d\n\nMax spoke up, surprising everyone. \u201cWe can trap them!\u201d he suggested, grinning. The friends quickly made a plan with Leo\u2019s tech skills to create a distraction. They hid behind tall flowers, waiting.\n\nJust as the older kids approached, Leo pressed a button on his invention. A flock of colorful butterflies flew out, swirling around the older kids. \u201cWhoa!\u201d they shouted, surprised. This was their chance! \n\nThe friends dashed toward the wildflower field, laughing and running. \u201cWe did it!\u201d Emma squealed. Max felt happy. \u201cI didn\u2019t know I could help,\u201d he said, smiling. \n\nThey reached the cave entrance, where the map signaled the treasure was hidden. \u201cAre you ready?\u201d Sophie asked. Everyone nodded excitedly. They were a team now, ready for whatever lay ahead. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find that treasure!\u201d Sophie cheered. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe cave loomed before them, its dark opening filled with mystery. Hope surged in their hearts. They were one step closer to uncovering the hidden treasures of Harmony Hill.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Emma find in the grass?","options":["A silver key","A gold coin","A treasure map","A butterfly"],"correct_answer":"A silver key"},{"question":"What did the friends use to distract the older kids?","options":["A loud noise","A flock of butterflies","A bright light","A funny dance"],"correct_answer":"A flock of butterflies"},{"question":"How did Max feel during the adventure?","options":["Confident","Nervous","Angry","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What do the friends plan to find next?","options":["A treasure","A friend","A cave","A flower"],"correct_answer":"A treasure"},{"question":"What does Sophie encourage the group to do?","options":["Give up","Work together","Play a game","Go home"],"correct_answer":"Work together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_9_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_9_ch4_img1.png","plot_9_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":397,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
