   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_9_11_14","title":"Hidden Treasures of Harmony Hill","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Treasure Hunt","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the sun rose over Harmony Hill, the golden rays spilled across the lush green fields, making the wildflowers shimmer like tiny jewels. Sophie stood at the base of the hill, her heart racing with excitement. \u201cToday\u2019s the day!\u201d she exclaimed, turning to her friends. Leo adjusted his glasses, his mind already whirring with ideas. \u201cWe should start at the old oak tree. The legend says the first clue is hidden there.\u201d \n\nEmma, sketchbook in hand, added, \u201cAnd I can draw a map as we go! It\u2019ll help us track our steps.\u201d Her artistic spirit shone as brightly as the morning sun, and Max, the newcomer, felt a mix of admiration and anxiety. He was still trying to find his place among them, feeling like a missing puzzle piece that didn\u2019t quite fit.\n\nAs they made their way up the hill, the sound of laughter and chatter caught their attention. A group of older kids from school lounged on a nearby bench, eyeing the younger friends with a mix of amusement and disdain. \u201cLook at those losers,\u201d one of them sneered, his arms crossed over his chest. \u201cWhat makes them think they can find anything?\u201d\n\nSophie took a deep breath, trying to ignore the taunts. \u201cLet\u2019s just focus on our adventure. They can\u2019t stop us,\u201d she said, her voice steady. But Leo\u2019s brow furrowed. \u201cI don\u2019t like the way they\u2019re looking at us. They might try to ruin our hunt.\u201d\n\n\u201cThen we\u2019ll have to be smart,\u201d Sophie replied, her determination like a shield. The group reached the old oak tree, its gnarled branches stretching out like welcoming arms. Emma pulled out her sketchbook and began to draw the tree, while Leo set up his gadget to scan the area for any hidden clues. \n\nJust as they were getting started, a loud crash startled them. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] A large rock tumbled down from above, narrowly missing Max, who jumped back in fright. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d he exclaimed, eyes wide with panic. The laughter from the older kids echoed ominously in the background. \n\n\u201cJust a coincidence,\u201d Sophie said, though her voice wavered slightly. But Leo was already analyzing the gadget\u2019s readings. \u201cI think there\u2019s something behind the tree! It might be a clue!\u201d \n\nThey hurried to the tree, excitement bubbling within them. As they pushed aside the roots and dirt, Emma's fingers brushed against something cold and metallic. \u201cI found something!\u201d she called out, her heart racing. \n\nA rusted old box emerged from its earthy prison, covered in moss and forgotten by time. Max\u2019s eyes sparkled with wonder. This was it\u2014the first step toward their treasure! But just as they were about to open the box, the older kids approached, blocking their way. \n\n\u201cLet me guess, you think you\u2019ve found a treasure?\u201d one of them mocked, stepping forward with a smug grin. \u201cYou\u2019re just wasting your time.\u201d The group\u2019s tension surged, and Sophie felt the weight of the moment. This was more than a treasure hunt now; it was about standing their ground. \n\n\u201cLet us through,\u201d Sophie said firmly, her heart pounding. \u201cWe\u2019re not afraid of you.\u201d Max stood taller beside her, feeling the support of his friends. This was a turning point. \n\nAs the older kids laughed, Sophie knew they had to act fast. \u201cLet\u2019s open the box. If it\u2019s treasure, they\u2019ll back off,\u201d she whispered urgently. With one swift motion, Emma lifted the lid, and they all leaned in, eager to discover what lay within. \n\nThe moment hung in the air, thick with suspense. What would they find?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Sophie suggest they do first in their treasure hunt?","options":["Start at the old oak tree","Go to the river","Visit the nearby park","Look for clues in town"],"correct_answer":"Start at the old oak tree"},{"question":"How does Max feel at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["Confident","Out of place","Angry","Excited"],"correct_answer":"Out of place"},{"question":"What do the older kids do when they see the group of friends?","options":["Join in on the treasure hunt","Laugh and mock them","Help them find clues","Ignore them completely"],"correct_answer":"Laugh and mock them"},{"question":"What do the friends discover at the base of the oak tree?","options":["A treasure map","An ancient box","A pile of rocks","A hidden cave"],"correct_answer":"An ancient box"},{"question":"How does Sophie handle the confrontation with the older kids?","options":["Runs away","Stands firm with her friends","Cries","Laughs with them"],"correct_answer":"Stands firm with her friends"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_9_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_9_ch2_img1.png","plot_9_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":608,"reading_level":"Builder"}
