   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"adventure_9_11_14","title":"Hidden Treasures of Harmony Hill","genre":"Adventure","sub_genre":"Treasure Hunt","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The afternoon sun bathed Harmony Hill in a warm glow as Sophie, Leo, Emma, and Max gathered beneath the gnarled branches of the old oak tree. The ancient box they had discovered earlier was nestled in the roots, its surface covered in a thick layer of dust. Sophie knelt beside it, her heart racing with excitement. \u201cWhat do you think is inside?\u201d she asked, her eyes sparkling.\n\n\u201cI bet it\u2019s treasure!\u201d Leo exclaimed, adjusting his glasses and pulling out his trusty toolkit. \u201cMaybe a map or ancient coins.\u201d Emma\u2019s face lit up with a smile, her imagination swirling with colorful images of long-lost riches. Max, however, shifted nervously at the back of the group. He had felt like an outsider since joining, unsure of how to contribute.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s open it together,\u201d Emma suggested, her artistic flair making the moment feel even more special. The group leaned in closely, their breaths held in anticipation. Sophie lifted the lid, and a cloud of dust erupted into the air like a burst of confetti.\n\nInside, they found an assortment of old photographs and a beautifully ornate compass, its needle spinning wildly. \u201cLook at this!\u201d Leo shouted, thrusting the compass into the sunlight. \u201cIt\u2019s not just a compass; it looks like it has a riddle on it!\u201d \n\nAs they examined the compass closely, a shadow fell over them, and the familiar laughter of the older kids echoed through the trees. \u201cWhat are you losers doing?\u201d Jake, the leader of the older kids, sneered. \u201cYou really think you can find anything hidden here? You might as well give up now!\u201d\n\nSophie\u2019s heart sank as Jake and his friends stepped forward, their menacing grins making her pulse quicken. \u201cWe\u2019re not afraid of you!\u201d she shot back, her voice stronger than she felt. \u201cWe\u2019re not giving up!\u201d\n\nJust then, Leo noticed something odd about the compass. \u201cWait! The needle is pointing towards the hilltop!\u201d he exclaimed, excitement bubbling in his voice. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s trying to tell us where to go next!\u201d \n\n\u201cWe should follow it!\u201d Emma added, her excitement overshadowing her fear. But Max hesitated, glancing back at the older kids, who were now closing in around them. \u201cWhat if they try to sabotage us?\u201d \n\n\u201cThey will,\u201d Sophie replied with determination. \u201cBut we can\u2019t let them stop us. This is our chance to find the treasure!\u201d \n\nJust as they decided to follow the compass, Jake and his crew lunged forward, trying to snatch the box from Sophie\u2019s hands. \u201cLet\u2019s get out of here!\u201d Max shouted, panic rising in his chest. \n\nWith their hearts pounding, the friends dashed away from the tree, the compass clutched tightly in Leo\u2019s hand. The older kids chased them, their shouts echoing in the woods. The thicket of wildflowers blurred around them as they sprinted, adrenaline fueling their flight. \n\n\u201cWe need to split up!\u201d Sophie shouted, glancing back to see how close the older kids were. \u201cLeo, Emma, head towards the trail! Max, come with me!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhy me?\u201d Max protested, but there was no time for debate. Sophie grabbed his hand, pulling him along as they veered off the main path, hoping to lose their pursuers in the maze of trees.\n\nA sudden rustle in the bushes startled them, and a shadow darted past. Max\u2019s heart raced even faster. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d he gasped, feeling the weight of uncertainty settle on his shoulders. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we have to keep moving!\u201d Sophie urged, her determination shining through her fear. They pushed through the underbrush, every snap of a twig sending shivers down their spines. \n\nJust as they reached a clearing, they paused to catch their breath. The compass still spun, seemingly agitated, and Sophie looked at Max, determination etched on her face. \u201cNo matter what happens, we stick together, right?\u201d\n\nMax nodded, feeling a flicker of belonging amidst the chaos. But suddenly, a loud shout echoed behind them, and their hearts sank. They risked a glance back, only to see Jake appearing at the edge of the clearing, a triumphant smile on his face. \u201cYou can\u2019t run forever!\u201d \n\nIt was a moment that hung heavy in the air\u2014one choice, one decision, that could change everything. As Sophie looked around, she realized they were at a crossroads, not just in their adventure, but in their friendships.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nThe image shows the four friends gathered around the old oak tree, their expressions a mix of excitement and determination. The ancient box is open, revealing its contents, with dust particles floating in the sunlight that filters through the branches. The warm glow of the afternoon sun creates an atmosphere of adventure and hope.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] \n\nThe image captures the tense moment as the older kids approach, with Jake leading the charge. Sophie stands defiantly in front of her friends, her face showing both fear and courage. The woods around them are vibrant, but the looming threat of Jake and his friends casts a shadow over the scene, heightening the suspense.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do the friends find inside the ancient box?","options":["A treasure map","An old compass and photographs","A pile of gold coins","A diary"],"correct_answer":"An old compass and photographs"},{"question":"What does the compass do when they examine it?","options":["It shows them a map","It starts spinning wildly","It leads them to gold","It points to the oak tree"],"correct_answer":"It starts spinning wildly"},{"question":"How does Jake, the older kid, react to the friends' discovery?","options":["He helps them","He mocks them","He is scared","He joins their group"],"correct_answer":"He mocks them"},{"question":"What decision do the friends make when chased by the older kids?","options":["They fight back","They split up","They hide","They give up"],"correct_answer":"They split up"},{"question":"What does Sophie ask Max when they reach a clearing?","options":["If he feels scared","If he wants to go home","If they should keep moving","If they will stick together"],"correct_answer":"If they will stick together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_9_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_9_ch3_img1.png","plot_9_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":842,"reading_level":"Builder"}
