   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_276_15_18","title":"The Enigma Club","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Secret Societies","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the afternoon sun poured through the massive stained-glass windows of Harlow High School\u2019s library, Mia, Leo, and Ava huddled around the flickering candlelight of their makeshift meeting spot\u2014a dusty old table in the corner, obscured from prying eyes. The sense of adventure crackled in the air, but an undercurrent of tension buzzed among them. They had entered the Enigma Club, but with that title came expectations, and the weight of the mystery loomed like the shelves of ancient books surrounding them.\n\n\u201cWhat if we actually find something?\u201d Leo broke the silence, his fingers dancing over the latest gadget he had crafted\u2014a small device that could decode basic ciphers. His eyes sparkled with a mix of excitement and anxiety. \u201cI mean, what if it\u2019s something incredible?\u201d\n\nAva, her nose buried in a tattered volume about local legends, looked up. \u201cOr it could be a myth. Remember the last time we got our hopes up about a treasure hunt? We ended up searching the playground for a week over a rumor.\u201d\n\nMia felt the familiar tug of ambition in her chest. \u201cBut this is different! The whispers about the treasure hidden in the school are decades old. We\u2019ve found the secret door. We can\u2019t just let it fade away like another ghost story.\u201d Her determination was palpable, igniting an emboldening energy among her friends.\n\nSuddenly, Mia\u2019s thoughts spiraled. What if they weren\u2019t the only ones after the treasure? The rival club, the Knights of the Lost Key, had been lurking in the shadows since the Enigma Club\u2019s inception. They were older and had a reputation for being ruthless. Would they sabotage their efforts? \n\nJust then, a faint noise echoed from behind the bookshelf behind them, drawing their attention. The three exchanged wary glances, their hearts thudding in unison. Was it just the creaking of an old building, or was someone else listening in?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMia took a deep breath. \u201cWe need to move fast. If the Knights are onto us, we don\u2019t have much time before they beat us to the prize.\u201d She glanced around the library, her mind racing. \u201cLet\u2019s split up. Leo, you and I will search the history section. Ava, you check the reference books. We need to gather as many clues as possible.\u201d\n\nAs they set off in their respective directions, the library's atmosphere shifted. The long shadows cast by the waning sunlight seemed to stretch ominously, and the air thickened with the weight of uncertainty. Mia flipped through dusty tomes, her fingers trailing over faded titles like \u201cSecrets of the Ancients\u201d and \u201cThe Lost Chronicles of Harlow.\u201d \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Leo\u2019s voice broke through Mia\u2019s concentration, tinged with an unsettling mix of excitement and fear. \n\n\u201cWhat?\u201d she asked, her heartbeat quickening.\n\n\u201cSounds like footsteps. Quick, hide!\u201d \n\nMia ducked behind a towering bookshelf, her heart racing. The footsteps grew louder, and she could see the outline of a figure\u2014one of the Knights, she was certain. Holding her breath, she peered through the narrow space between the books. There, in the dim light, stood Eric, the leader of the rival club, his expression smug as he rifled through a stack of old newspapers.\n\nMia\u2019s mind raced; they were onto them, and she needed to warn Ava. But as she turned to leave her hiding spot, she stumbled over a loose floorboard, sending a cascade of books tumbling to the floor. \n\n\u201cWho\u2019s there?\u201d Eric\u2019s voice sliced through the silence like a knife.\n\nMia\u2019s heart fell. Panic surged as she realized the moment she had dreaded had come. She had to act fast. \u201cLeo! Ava!\u201d she whispered urgently, praying they were close enough to hear.\n\nSuddenly, Eric\u2019s face twisted into a predatory grin. \u201cI knew you\u2019d be snooping around, Mia. But it\u2019s too late now. The treasure is ours.\u201d\n\nThe challenge was clear. The tension in the library reached a breaking point; Mia felt the pulse of adrenaline in her veins. She would not let them win.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see about that,\u201d Mia replied, her voice steadier than she felt. She could almost hear the ticking clock of their quest echoing in her mind.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia\u2019s thoughts raced as she prepared to confront Eric. The stakes had never been higher, and she could feel the weight of her friends' hopes resting on her shoulders. \n\nWith every ounce of courage, she stepped forward into the dim light, ready to face whatever came next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mia discover in the library that leads to the formation of the Enigma Club?","options":["A hidden compartment","A series of puzzles","A hidden door","A secret book"],"correct_answer":"A hidden door"},{"question":"Who is the leader of the rival club?","options":["Leo","Ava","Eric","Mia"],"correct_answer":"Eric"},{"question":"What is the main challenge Mia and her friends face in this chapter?","options":["Finding the treasure","Competing against the rival club","Decoding clues","Avoiding school staff"],"correct_answer":"Competing against the rival club"},{"question":"How does Mia feel when she sees Eric in the library?","options":["Relieved","Excited","Panic-stricken","Joyful"],"correct_answer":"Panic-stricken"},{"question":"What does Mia plan to do when she confronts Eric?","options":["Run away","Make a deal","Face him","Call for help"],"correct_answer":"Face him"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_276_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_276_ch2_img1.png","plot_276_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":757,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
