   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_276_15_18","title":"The Enigma Club","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Secret Societies","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The afternoon sun filtered through the dusty windows of the library, casting golden patterns on the worn wooden floor. Mia stood in front of the hidden door, heart racing as she glanced at Ava and Leo, who shared her mounting excitement. The Enigma Club was set to meet again, and today, they had a new lead\u2014a crumpled piece of parchment recovered from a section of the library that smelled of mothballs and mystery.\n\n\u201cDo you think it could be the clue we\u2019ve been waiting for?\u201d Ava asked, her voice barely above a whisper. Her eyes gleamed with curiosity, the usual calm demeanor replaced by an eagerness that made Mia smile. \n\n\u201cOnly one way to find out,\u201d Leo said, adjusting his glasses, his fingers itching to get to work. He always loved these moments, the thrill of discovery. \u201cLet\u2019s spread it out on the table.\u201d\n\nThey gathered around an old oak table in the corner, the wood smooth from years of use. As they unfolded the parchment, Mia noticed a series of strange symbols sketched alongside a faded map of the school. Her heart raced. \u201cThis must be a code!\u201d \n\n\u201cOr an elaborate joke,\u201d Ava replied, glancing over her shoulder, as if the Knights of the Lost Key might be lurking nearby. \n\n\u201cNo way. Look at the detail,\u201d Leo pointed out, tapping his finger on a distinct marking. \u201cThis part here matches the old clock tower where they used to hide the keys!\u201d \n\nMia leaned in closer, breath hitching. \u201cIf we decode this, we might find the treasure before they do,\u201d she murmured. \n\nRealizing the weight of their mission, she felt a surge of determination. Their previous run-ins with the rival club had been unsettling, and their latest encounter had ended in a near confrontation near the gymnasium, tempers flaring as they each accused the other of cheating.\n\n\u201cThis could be our biggest challenge yet,\u201d said Ava, adjusting her glasses. \u201cBut we have to work together. No secrets, no shortcuts.\u201d \n\nMia nodded. They understood the stakes now; this wasn\u2019t just a game. As they delved deeper into deciphering the symbols, a sudden crash echoed through the library. The door swung open, revealing Max, the leader of the Knights of the Lost Key, flanked by his smug cohorts.\n\n\u201cWhat are you doing in here?\u201d Max sneered, arms crossed defiantly. \u201cYou really think you can outsmart us?\u201d\n\nMia felt the blood rush to her face. \u201cWe\u2019re not afraid of you, Max. We\u2019re closer than ever to solving the mystery.\u201d\n\nMax smirked, stepping forward. \u201cI\u2019ll tell you what\u2019s really close\u2014your defeat. You think you\u2019re clever? All you\u2019re doing is digging your own graves.\u201d The threat hung heavy in the air, charging the already tense atmosphere.\n\nLeo\u2019s fingers danced nervously on the parchment. \u201cLet\u2019s just ignore them. We have more important work to do.\u201d \n\n\u201cWork? You mean, trying to claim what\u2019s rightfully ours?\u201d Max retorted, stepping even closer, eyes glinting with mischief. \n\nMia, fueled by anger and indignation, took a step forward herself. \u201cYou think you can intimidate us? We\u2019re not going to let you steal this from us. We have a right to this treasure too.\u201d \n\n\u201cRight?\u201d Max scoffed. \u201cLife isn\u2019t fair, Mia. It\u2019s about who\u2019s willing to take it first.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, Leo\u2019s voice broke through the tension, desperate but determined. \u201cMia, look!\u201d He pointed at the parchment, where a small symbol had begun to glow faintly. \n\nBefore Mia could process what she was seeing, Max lunged for the parchment. \u201cNo!\u201d she shouted, throwing herself forward. In that moment of chaos, the parchment ripped in half, and a surge of energy pulsed through the library, casting shadows that danced wildly across the walls. \n\nAva gasped, clutching her notebook as fear etched itself across her face. \u201cWhat did we just do?\u201d\n\nMia looked into Max's eyes, now filled with uncertainty and rage. \u201cWe need to get out of here!\u201d \n\nThey ran past the stunned Knights, hearts pounding, the glow of the parchment still pulsating in their minds. As they burst through the hidden door and into the corridor beyond, Mia knew they had crossed a line. The treasure was no longer just a mystery; it had become a challenge that could change everything.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia glanced back at the library, the door now ominously closed. \u201cThis is just the beginning,\u201d she said, her voice steady despite the uncertainty swirling in her mind. \u201cWe have to regroup and figure out what this really means.\u201d \n\nAs they escaped into the twilight, an unsettling thought lingered in Mia\u2019s mind. What had they unleashed?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the main discovery Mia and her friends make in this chapter?","options":["A hidden treasure","A coded map","A new rival club","A secret passageway"],"correct_answer":"A coded map"},{"question":"Who confronts Mia and her friends in the library?","options":["A teacher","Max from the Knights of the Lost Key","The librarian","A ghost"],"correct_answer":"Max from the Knights of the Lost Key"},{"question":"What happens to the parchment during the encounter with Max?","options":["It is thrown away","It glows brightly","It is ripped in half","It disappears"],"correct_answer":"It is ripped in half"},{"question":"What internal conflict does Mia face in this chapter?","options":["Fear of failing","Jealousy of Leo and Ava","Doubt about the treasure's existence","Confusion about her feelings for Max"],"correct_answer":"Fear of failing"},{"question":"What does Mia suggest at the end of the chapter?","options":["To abandon the quest","To regroup and figure out the implications of the parchment","To confront the Knights of the Lost Key again","To leave the library for good"],"correct_answer":"To regroup and figure out the implications of the parchment"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_276_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_276_ch3_img1.png","plot_276_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":778,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
