   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_277_7_10","title":"The Midnight Guardians","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Secret Societies","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Jake took a deep breath as he stepped into the old church. The air was cool and smelled like dusty books. Emma stood beside him, eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cThis is it, Jake! Our training starts now!\u201d\n\nMr. Whiskers paced back and forth in front of them. \u201cWelcome, new Guardians! Tonight, we face the shadow creature. But first, we must prepare!\u201d He flicked his tail, and a small book appeared from nowhere. It floated in the air, glowing softly.\n\n\u201cWow!\u201d Jake exclaimed, his skepticism melting away. \u201cWhat\u2019s that book?\u201d\n\n\u201cIt holds the secrets of the Guardians!\u201d Mr. Whiskers replied. \u201cNow, listen closely.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cEach Guardian has a special skill,\u201d Mr. Whiskers continued. \u201cEmma, you\u2019ll use your bravery. Jake, you must find your courage. You both need to trust in yourselves.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat if I can\u2019t?\u201d Jake asked, doubt creeping back in his voice.\n\n\u201cThen you\u2019ll let the shadow win!\u201d Mr. Whiskers said firmly. \u201cBut if you believe in yourselves, you can defeat it!\u201d\n\nThe words echoed in Jake\u2019s mind. He wanted to believe, but fear bubbled in his stomach. \u201cLet\u2019s just try our best,\u201d he said, his voice shaky.\n\n\u201cExactly!\u201d Emma cheered, clenching her fists. \u201cWe can do this!\u201d\n\nAs they practiced, shadows danced like wiggly worms across the walls. Jake swung a toy sword. \u201cHa! Take that, shadow!\u201d He laughed, but inside, his heart raced.\n\nThen, a chilling howl echoed through the church. It made Jake freeze. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d he whispered.\n\n\u201cJust the wind,\u201d Emma said, but her own voice trembled.\n\nSuddenly, the door creaked open. A dark figure slipped inside. It was the shadow creature! It loomed tall, with eyes like glowing embers. Jake's heart pounded. \n\n\u201cStay back!\u201d Emma shouted, stepping in front of Jake. \u201cWe\u2019re the Midnight Guardians!\u201d\n\nJake's mind raced. He remembered Mr. Whiskers' words. Find your courage. He took a deep breath and stepped forward. \u201cWe won\u2019t let you take our town!\u201d\n\nThe creature laughed, a deep, rumbling sound. \u201cYou think two children and a cat can stop me?\u201d\n\nJake felt his knees shake. But then he looked at Emma, and she nodded. \n\n\u201cTogether,\u201d he whispered.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nJust then, bright light burst from the book in Mr. Whiskers\u2019 paws. \u201cNow!\u201d he yelled. \u201cUse the light to banish the shadow!\u201d\n\nJake and Emma raised their hands, channeling their energy into the light. Would it be enough? The shadow creature hissed, retreating.\n\n\u201cKeep going!\u201d shouted Emma. \u201cWe can do this!\u201d\n\nJake felt a rush of strength. \u201cOur town is worth fighting for!\u201d he cried, pouring all his courage into the light.\n\nBut as the darkness swirled around them, Jake wondered. Would he truly be worthy of being a Guardian?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Jake and Emma start to do in this chapter?","options":["Fight the shadow creature","Train to be Guardians","Go home","Play a game"],"correct_answer":"Train to be Guardians"},{"question":"Who is the unofficial mascot of the Midnight Guardians?","options":["Jake","Mr. Whiskers","Emma","The shadow"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Whiskers"},{"question":"What does Jake struggle with during the chapter?","options":["Hunger","Self-doubt","Boredom","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Self-doubt"},{"question":"What does the shadow creature do when it appears?","options":["Laughs and threatens Jake and Emma","Runs away","Sings a song","Gives them a gift"],"correct_answer":"Laughs and threatens Jake and Emma"},{"question":"What do Jake and Emma use to banish the shadow?","options":["A sword","Their voices","The light from the book","A magic spell"],"correct_answer":"The light from the book"}]},"images":null,"word_count":452,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
