   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_280_7_10","title":"The Phantom Collectors","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Secret Societies","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Chapter 4: Clues and Confusion\n\nNia sat on the edge of the museum\u2019s ancient stone fountain. The moonlight sparkled on the water, making it look magical. Max was sketching the strange symbols they had found in the enchanted room. Zara stood nearby, her eyes focused on the shadows.\n\n\u201cWhat if we don\u2019t find the amulet?\u201d Nia asked, biting her lip. \u201cWhat if the Dark Society gets it first?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe have to believe we can!\" Max said, glancing up. \"The symbols might help us.\u201d\n\nZara nodded. \u201cThe symbols are a map. They guide us to the amulet\u2019s last known location.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhere is that?\u201d Nia asked, feeling a spark of hope.\n\n\u201cDownstairs, in the old exhibit!\u201d Zara exclaimed. \u201cBut we have to move quickly.\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed through the museum. Nia\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find out!\u201d Max said, his eyes full of determination. They hurried down the dimly lit hallway.\n\nThey reached the old exhibit room. The door creaked open slowly. Inside, the darkness felt heavy. Nia took a deep breath. \u201cStay close.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, there was a gust of wind, and the lights flickered. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] In the glow of the flickering light, strange shadows danced on the wall. \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Nia whispered, clutching Max\u2019s arm.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Max replied, his voice shaking a little. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s the spirit of the museum!\u201d\n\nZara moved toward the center of the room. \u201cLook! Over there!\u201d She pointed to a dusty old chest in the corner. \u201cIt might have clues about the amulet!\u201d\n\nNia and Max followed her to the chest. They opened it slowly, and inside, they found a rolled-up piece of parchment. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see what it says,\u201d Nia said, unfolding it carefully.\n\nThe parchment was covered in more symbols. \u201cThese look like the ones we saw before!\u201d Max exclaimed. \u201cMaybe they can help us.\u201d\n\nAs Nia studied the symbols, she noticed something. \u201cWait! This symbol means \u2018trust.\u2019 If we find it, we can figure out who to trust in the Phantom Collectors!\u201d\n\n\u201cBut how do we find it?\u201d Zara asked, looking worried.\n\nNia smiled. \u201cI think we just did! We have to follow the map!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Max shouted. They all felt a rush of excitement.\n\nNia knew they were closer to uncovering the truth. But something still felt off. Could they really trust everyone in the Phantom Collectors? \n\nThe adventure was just beginning.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Nia, Max, and Zara find in the old exhibit room?","options":["A magical amulet","A rolled-up parchment","A treasure map","A dark shadow"],"correct_answer":"A rolled-up parchment"},{"question":"What do the symbols on the parchment help the characters with?","options":["Finding food","Solving a riddle","Finding the amulet","Making a wish"],"correct_answer":"Finding the amulet"},{"question":"How does Nia feel about trusting the Phantom Collectors?","options":["Very sure","Confused","Excited","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Confused"},{"question":"What does Nia suggest they need to find?","options":["A treasure","A secret","The trust symbol","A magic spell"],"correct_answer":"The trust symbol"},{"question":"What does Max think the gust of wind might be?","options":["A ghost","A friend","The Dark Society","A cat"],"correct_answer":"A ghost"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_280_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_280_ch4_img1.png","plot_280_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":410,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
