   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_280_15_18","title":"The Phantom Collectors","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Secret Societies","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The air in the museum was thick with a sense of foreboding as Nia and Max stepped through the tall, arched doorway. Shadows flickered across the wall, cast by the dim light of the old sconces that lined the hallway. Nia's heart raced; the deeper they ventured into the museum's labyrinthine halls, the more she felt the weight of the secrets hidden within its walls. This place was not just a repository of artifacts but a vault of magic and mystery, each item a whisper from the past.\n\n\u201cStay close, Max,\u201d Nia whispered, her voice barely audible over the creaking wooden floor. Max nodded, adjusting his glasses, his hands twitching nervously\u2014the telltale sign of a mind that was always at work, concocting inventions and solutions. \"Do you think we can really trust Zara?\" he asked, glancing back the way they had come. \"She knows things about magic that even the Phantom Collectors might not understand.\"\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Nia admitted, her thoughts spiraling. \u201cBut if the Shadow Society is as dangerous as she says, we need all the help we can get.\u201d As they turned a corner, Nia's breath caught in her throat. They stood before the artifact room, its door slightly ajar, a sliver of light spilling out into the hallway. \n\n\u201cDo you think it\u2019s safe?\u201d Max asked, his voice trembling slightly. Nia took a deep breath and pushed the door open. The room was filled with artifacts glowing softly under glass cases, but it was the empty pedestal at the center that drew her eye. \u201cThe artifact!\u201d she gasped, rushing inside. \u201cIt\u2019s gone!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe moment was surreal; the empty space where the artifact had once stood felt like an abyss. Nia\u2019s mind raced to the warnings Zara had given them. Had someone betrayed them? Was one of the Collectors in league with the Shadow Society? She could feel the panic rising in her chest but forced herself to calm down. \u201cWe need to find out who was here last,\u201d she stated, her voice steadier than her heart felt. \n\nAs she searched for clues, she heard a faint sound\u2014shuffling footsteps echoing from the hallway. \u201cMax, hide!\u201d she hissed, ducking behind the nearest display case. Max followed her lead, his eyes wide with fear. They peered around the edge just as Zara entered the room, her expression unreadable. \n\n\u201cWhat are you doing here?\u201d Nia demanded, stepping out from her hiding spot. Zara\u2019s eyes widened, but she quickly masked her surprise. \u201cI could ask you the same thing. You shouldn't be here. It's dangerous.\u201d \n\n\u201cDangerous?\u201d Max scoffed. \u201cYou\u2019re the one who came here when you knew something was amiss!\u201d \n\nBefore Zara could respond, another figure stepped into the light\u2014a tall boy with a familiar face, one that sent chills down Nia\u2019s spine. It was Ethan, a member of the Phantom Collectors known for his quick smile and charming demeanor. But now, his eyes glinted with a predatory gleam that made Nia\u2019s stomach twist. \n\n\u201cLooks like the little Collectors have stumbled into something they can\u2019t handle,\u201d he taunted, stepping closer. \u201cAnd I\u2019d say you're in over your heads.\u201d \n\n\u201cEthan, what do you want?\u201d Nia demanded, trying to keep her voice steady despite the fear coursing through her veins. \u201cWhere is the artifact?\u201d \n\n\u201cOh, you\u2019ll find out soon enough,\u201d Ethan replied, a smirk playing on his lips. \u201cThe Shadow Society will have it, and the Phantom Collectors will be nothing but a whisper in the wind.\u201d \n\nJust then, the room began to tremble, the lights flickering ominously. Nia's thoughts raced; she needed a plan, and fast. But as she glanced at Max and Zara, uncertainty clouded her mind. Could she trust either of them? The weight of betrayal hung thick in the air. It was clear that her only choice was to confront the truth about her companions and the growing threat surrounding them.\n\n\u201cRun!\u201d Nia shouted, her instincts kicking in as a shadow flitted across the wall, growing larger by the second. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe three sprinted toward the exit, hearts pounding and adrenaline surging. Nia could hear Ethan's mocking laughter following them, mingling with the ominous sounds of the museum coming alive. As they burst through the door and into the cool night air, Nia turned to her friends, desperation in her eyes. \u201cWe need to figure out who we can trust, and fast. The Shadow Society is coming for us.\u201d\n\nMax nodded, determination flickering in his gaze. Zara, though visibly shaken, made a decision that surprised Nia. \u201cThen we have to split up. It\u2019s the only way to gather more information. I\u2019ll go to the library. Nia, you and Max take the streets.\u201d\n\nNia hesitated, the gravity of their choices settling in. \u201cAre you sure?\u201d\n\n\u201cTrust me,\u201d Zara said, and with that, she disappeared into the darkness.\n\nNia and Max exchanged a glance, the weight of uncertainty pressing down on them. They had to move quickly, but as they stepped into the night, Nia could feel the shadows closing in around them. The game had begun.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What artifact do Nia and Max discover is missing?","options":["A magical sword","An ancient book","A powerful artifact","A cursed jewel"],"correct_answer":"A powerful artifact"},{"question":"Who does Nia confront in the artifact room?","options":["Max","Zara","Ethan","The Shadow Society"],"correct_answer":"Ethan"},{"question":"What major decision do Nia, Max, and Zara make at the end of the chapter?","options":["To leave the museum","To split up","To confront the Shadow Society","To call for help"],"correct_answer":"To split up"},{"question":"What is the primary emotion Nia feels when she discovers the artifact is gone?","options":["Joy","Fear","Relief","Boredom"],"correct_answer":"Fear"},{"question":"What does Zara suggest they do to gather information?","options":["Go to the police","Split up","Search the museum","Contact other collectors"],"correct_answer":"Split up"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_280_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_280_ch3_img1.png","plot_280_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":854,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
