   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_271_7_10","title":"The Case of the Missing Goldfish","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Mia stood by the big window in her classroom. The sun shined brightly on Riverview Middle School. Today was a special day. The big game was just hours away! Everyone was buzzing with excitement. \n\n\u201cDid you see the mascot?\u201d Mia asked her best friend, Theo. \n\nTheo was busy doodling a fish on his notebook. \u201cYou mean Bubbles? I hope he\u2019s safe!\u201d He looked up with wide eyes. \u201cBubbles is our lucky goldfish!\u201d\n\nJust then, Mr. Hargrove, the science teacher, walked in. He wore a lab coat covered in colorful fish stickers. \u201cGood morning, class!\u201d he said cheerfully. \u201cHave you all seen Bubbles?\u201d\n\n\u201cNo!\u201d Mia exclaimed. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\n\nMr. Hargrove scratched his head. \u201cBubbles is missing. He was in his bowl this morning. Now, poof! Gone!\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat? We need to find him! The game is tonight!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry, Mr. Hargrove,\u201d said Theo, jumping to his feet. \u201cWe\u2019ll find Bubbles! Right, Mia?\u201d\n\n\u201cRight!\u201d Mia agreed. \u201cBut where should we start looking?\u201d\n\n\u201cWell,\u201d Mr. Hargrove said, \u201cBubbles loves to swim. Maybe he swam somewhere interesting... Maybe even the gym?\u201d\n\n\u201cGood idea!\u201d Mia replied. The two friends dashed out of the classroom. \n\nAs they ran, they passed the gym door. Inside, players were practicing basketball. \u201cHold on!\u201d shouted a boy named Jake, one of the star players. \u201cDid you see the fish? Everyone thinks you took him!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat? No!\u201d Mia shouted back. \u201cWe\u2019re trying to find him!\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, right!\u201d Jake laughed. \u201cYou\u2019ll see. We\u2019re all counting on you two!\u201d\n\nTheo frowned. \u201cThis isn\u2019t good. We need to hurry.\u201d \n\nThey rushed to the janitor's closet. It was dark inside and smelled funny. Mia opened the door slowly. \u201cDo you think Bubbles is in here?\u201d\n\nSuddenly, they heard a splash! \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Theo whispered, eyes wide. \n\nMia gulped. \u201cLet\u2019s find out!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey stepped inside, hearts pounding. What would they find?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the name of the school mascot?","options":["Bubbles","Goldie","Flipper","Fishy"],"correct_answer":"Bubbles"},{"question":"Who is Mr. Hargrove?","options":["The janitor","The science teacher","The gym coach","The principal"],"correct_answer":"The science teacher"},{"question":"What did Mia and Theo hear in the janitor's closet?","options":["A voice","A splash","A laugh","A whisper"],"correct_answer":"A splash"},{"question":"What did everyone think Mia and Theo did?","options":["Took the mascot","Found a treasure","Played basketball","Went to the library"],"correct_answer":"Took the mascot"},{"question":"What is the main problem in this chapter?","options":["A game is canceled","The goldfish went missing","It's raining outside","The school is closed"],"correct_answer":"The goldfish went missing"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_271_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_271_ch1_img1.png","plot_271_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":323,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
