   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_271_7_10","title":"The Case of the Missing Goldfish","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Mia and Theo rushed down the bustling hallways of Riverview Middle School. Their hearts raced with excitement and worry. Where could Bubbles be? \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check the gym first!\u201d Mia suggested, her eyes sparkling with determination. \n\n\u201cGreat idea!\u201d Theo replied. \u201cMaybe someone saw him.\u201d \n\nAs they entered the gym, the smell of popcorn filled the air. Students were cheering, practicing for the big game. But Mia and Theo had only one thing on their minds. They scanned the room, looking for clues. \n\n\u201cDo you see anything?\u201d Theo asked, peering behind the bleachers. \n\n\u201cNo, just a lot of basketballs,\u201d Mia said, shaking her head. \n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud crash. They turned to see Mr. Hargrove, their science teacher, juggling three basketballs! \n\n\u201cOops!\u201d he exclaimed, dropping one. It bounced and rolled toward Mia and Theo. \n\n\u201cMr. Hargrove!\u201d Mia called. \u201cHave you seen Bubbles?\u201d \n\nMr. Hargrove scratched his head. \u201cBubbles? No, but I did see something shiny near the art room!\u201d He winked playfully, then continued juggling. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Theo said, his excitement bubbling. They raced out of the gym, not wanting to waste a second.\n\nAs they approached the art room, they noticed the door was slightly ajar. Mia peeked inside. \u201cDo you think we should go in?\u201d \n\n\u201cDefinitely!\u201d Theo said, pushing the door open. \n\nInside, the room was filled with colorful paintings and messy tables. But where was the shiny thing Mr. Hargrove mentioned? Suddenly, Mia spotted it\u2014a sparkling object on the floor near the paint supplies! \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d she exclaimed, pointing. \n\nThey rushed over and found a glittering goldfish bowl. \n\n\u201cWhat? Is this Bubbles?\u201d Theo asked, his eyes wide. \n\n\u201cNo, it\u2019s empty!\u201d Mia said, frowning. \u201cBut there\u2019s something here.\u201d She picked up a note next to the bowl. \n\n\u201cIt says, \u2018Find me before the game or lose the prize!\u2019\u201d \n\n\u201cWho would leave such a message?\u201d Theo wondered, scratching his head. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Mia replied, \u201cbut we have to keep searching!\u201d \n\nJust then, they heard footsteps outside the room. They froze, hearts pounding. \n\n\u201cQuick! Hide!\u201d Mia whispered. \n\nThey ducked behind a large painting, their breaths held tight. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMoments later, the door swung open. It was two kids from the rival school, laughing and pointing at their own school\u2019s mascot. \n\n\u201cHa! Your fish is gone! You\u2019re in big trouble!\u201d one of them sneered. \n\n\u201cThey\u2019ll never find it!\u201d the other giggled. \n\nMia glanced at Theo. \u201cThis is worse than I thought. They might know something!\u201d \n\nThey waited until the rivals left before creeping back out into the hallway. \n\n\u201cNow what?\u201d Theo asked, looking worried. \n\n\u201cWe have to confront them,\u201d Mia said, determination returning to her voice. \u201cThey might be hiding something!\u201d \n\nAs they stepped into the hallway, they felt the pressure of time. The game was starting soon, and they had to find Bubbles!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Mia said, her spirit high. \n\nWith a new plan in mind, they rushed to find the rivals.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mr. Hargrove say about Bubbles?","options":["He saw Bubbles in the gym.","He saw something shiny near the art room.","He lost Bubbles himself.","He didn\u2019t know anything about Bubbles."],"correct_answer":"He saw something shiny near the art room."},{"question":"What did Mia and Theo find in the art room?","options":["A painting of Bubbles.","An empty goldfish bowl.","A treasure chest.","A note about the game."],"correct_answer":"An empty goldfish bowl."},{"question":"What does the note say?","options":["Find me before the game or lose the prize!","Bubbles is at the gym!","Your goldfish is safe!","You will never find Bubbles!"],"correct_answer":"Find me before the game or lose the prize!"},{"question":"Who did Mia and Theo overhear in the hallway?","options":["Mr. Hargrove and a teacher.","Two kids from the rival school.","Other students cheering.","The janitor."],"correct_answer":"Two kids from the rival school."},{"question":"What do Mia and Theo plan to do next?","options":["Leave school.","Confront the rival students.","Check the gym again.","Go home."],"correct_answer":"Confront the rival students."}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_271_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_271_ch2_img1.png","plot_271_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":494,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
