   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_271_7_10","title":"The Case of the Missing Goldfish","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Mia and Theo stood in the bustling hallway of Riverview Middle School. Students rushed past them, excited for the big game. Mia frowned. \u201cWe have to find Bubbles before it\u2019s too late!\u201d\n\nTheo nodded, his eyes wide. \u201cBut where do we look next? We\u2019ve checked the gym and the art room!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud crash. Mia and Theo exchanged worried glances. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Mia whispered.\n\n\u201cI think it came from the janitor's closet!\u201d Theo replied, pointing down the hall.\n\nThey hesitated. The janitor's closet was dark and mysterious. \u201cWhat if there\u2019s something scary in there?\u201d Mia asked, biting her lip.\n\n\u201cOr what if Bubbles is in there?\u201d Theo said, his voice brightening.\n\nWith determination, they tiptoed to the closet. Mia opened the door. It creaked loudly. Inside, it was cluttered with cleaning supplies and boxes. They peered inside, searching for clues.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cMia! Look at this!\u201d Theo exclaimed, holding up a bright orange ball. \u201cIt has Bubbles\u2019 name on it!\u201d\n\n\u201cBubbles was here!\u201d Mia said, her heart racing. \u201cBut where did he go?\u201d\n\nJust then, they heard a voice behind them. \u201cWhat are you two doing in my closet?\u201d\n\nIt was Mr. Hargrove, the science teacher! He wore a puzzled look. \u201cYou\u2019re not supposed to be in here.\u201d\n\n\u201cMr. Hargrove! We\u2019re looking for Bubbles!\u201d Mia said. \u201cHe\u2019s missing!\u201d\n\n\u201cMissing, you say?\u201d Mr. Hargrove raised an eyebrow. \u201cThat\u2019s quite the mystery. I may have seen something... unusual.\u201d\n\nMia stepped closer. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\n\nMr. Hargrove leaned in, whispering. \u201cI saw one of the rival team members sneaking towards the aquarium this morning.\u201d\n\nTheo gasped. \u201cDo you think they took Bubbles?\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe,\u201d said Mr. Hargrove, \u201cbut you must hurry. The game is about to start!\u201d\n\nMia felt a rush of determination. \u201cWe have to find that rival before the game!\u201d \n\nThey rushed out of the closet, ready for action. But who could they trust? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia and Theo raced down the hall, hearts pounding. \u201cWe have to split up,\u201d Mia said. \u201cYou check the cafeteria. I\u2019ll look outside by the field.\u201d\n\n\u201cOkay, but be careful!\u201d Theo called as they dashed in different directions.\n\nMia took a deep breath. She felt nervous but excited. Could they really solve the mystery in time?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia and Theo find in the janitor's closet?","options":["A goldfish bowl","A bright orange ball","A cleaning spray","A note"],"correct_answer":"A bright orange ball"},{"question":"Who did Mia and Theo hear in the janitor's closet?","options":["The janitor","Mr. Hargrove","Their teacher","A rival student"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Hargrove"},{"question":"What did Mr. Hargrove say he saw?","options":["Bubbles swimming","A rival team member","Theo hiding","A cleaning cart"],"correct_answer":"A rival team member"},{"question":"What decision did Mia and Theo make to find Bubbles?","options":["To ask the principal","To split up","To call the police","To go home"],"correct_answer":"To split up"},{"question":"How did Mia feel at the end of the chapter?","options":["Nervous but excited","Scared","Bored","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Nervous but excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_271_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_271_ch3_img1.png","plot_271_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":383,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
