   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_271_11_14","title":"The Case of the Missing Goldfish","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The bell rang loudly, echoing through the bustling hallways of Riverview Middle School. Mia adjusted her glasses, the frames slipping down her nose as she scanned the crowded corridor. \u201cCan you believe it, Theo? Tonight\u2019s the big game against Crestview! Everyone\u2019s talking about it,\u201d she said, her eyes sparkling with excitement.\n\nTheo, her best friend since kindergarten, rolled his eyes playfully. \u201cYeah, and I bet half of them will forget about it when they realize they don\u2019t have a ticket.\u201d He jostled Mia lightly, causing her to giggle. \n\nAs they moved through the throngs of students, Mia caught a glimpse of the school\u2019s prized goldfish, Bubbles, swimming in his tank near the entrance. He was the mascot of their team, a small but vibrant orange fish that had become a symbol of school spirit. \u201cLook! There\u2019s Bubbles! I hope Mr. Hargrove has him all ready for the game,\u201d she said.\n\nJust then, Mr. Hargrove, with his wild hair and oversized glasses, emerged from the science lab, holding a clipboard like a treasure map. \u201cMia! Theo! Perfect timing! I need your help!\u201d His voice was a strange mix of excitement and worry. \n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s up, Mr. Hargrove?\u201d Theo asked, curiosity piqued.\n\n\u201cThe game is tonight, and I need to prepare Bubbles for his big moment,\u201d he replied. But as he reached for the tank, his expression turned grave. \u201cOh no! Where is he?\u201d \n\nMia\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat do you mean? Bubbles is missing?\u201d \n\n\u201cExactly! I had just fed him, and now\u2026 he\u2019s not here!\u201d The teacher\u2019s voice trembled slightly. \u201cIf we can\u2019t find Bubbles, the game will be ruined!\u201d\n\nMia and Theo exchanged worried glances. \u201cWe\u2019ll help you find him, Mr. Hargrove!\u201d Mia declared, her mind already racing with possibilities. \u201cWhere did you last see him?\u201d\n\n\u201cRight here, before lunch. I was just organizing the supplies, and when I turned back\u2014poof! He was gone!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe image would capture the chaotic scene of the hallway with students milling about, Mr. Hargrove looking frantic near the empty tank, and Mia and Theo looking determined, their expressions showing a mix of concern and excitement.\n\nAs they began their search, Mia felt the adrenaline kicking in. \u201cWe need to split up. I\u2019ll check the gym; maybe someone moved him there for good luck,\u201d she suggested, already strategizing. \n\n\u201cWhat if he\u2019s in the janitor\u2019s closet?\u201d Theo added, his adventurous spirit shining through. \u201cIt\u2019s always filled with surprises!\u201d\n\n\u201cGood idea! I\u2019ll meet you there in ten minutes,\u201d Mia replied, setting off towards the gym. The smell of sweat and popcorn hung in the air as she stepped inside, glancing around at the teams practicing for the game. \n\nSuddenly, she spotted a group of students from Crestview snickering on the bleachers. \u201cHey, Mia! Looking for your little fishy? Heard he swam away!\u201d one taunted, laughter bubbling around them. Mia\u2019s heart sank. She had no time for rivalries right now. \n\n\u201cLeave me alone!\u201d she shouted back, but doubt crept in. What if they were right? \n\nJust then, a flash of orange caught her eye near the bleachers. \u201cBubbles?\u201d Mia whispered, racing toward it. \n\nHowever, as she reached the spot, her heart fell. It was just a bright orange ball. \u201cNo, no, no! Where are you, Bubbles?\u201d she muttered, frustration bubbling inside her. She needed to find him before the game started, or they would all be in trouble.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe second image could show Mia in the gym, looking determined and slightly frustrated as she searches amidst the bleachers, with students whispering and pointing at her in the background, capturing the tension of the moment.\n\nThe time was ticking down, and the game was only hours away. Mia knew that finding Bubbles was more than just about keeping the mascot; it was about proving that she could solve this mystery\u2014and that she could trust her instincts. \n\n\u201cHang on, Bubbles! I\u2019m coming!\u201d she whispered, determination flooding through her veins. \n\nThe adventure was just beginning, and there was no turning back now.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the name of the school's prized goldfish?","options":["Goldy","Bubbles","Finny","Nemo"],"correct_answer":"Bubbles"},{"question":"Who is Mr. Hargrove?","options":["The janitor","The math teacher","The science teacher","The principal"],"correct_answer":"The science teacher"},{"question":"What do Mia and Theo plan to do?","options":["Ignore the problem","Help find Bubbles","Talk to other students","Prepare for the game"],"correct_answer":"Help find Bubbles"},{"question":"What does Mia find instead of the goldfish?","options":["A toy","A ball","A piece of paper","A book"],"correct_answer":"A ball"},{"question":"What does Mia feel as she searches for Bubbles?","options":["Excitement","Fear","Frustration","Joy"],"correct_answer":"Frustration"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_271_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_271_ch1_img1.png","plot_271_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":683,"reading_level":"Builder"}
