   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_271_11_14","title":"The Case of the Missing Goldfish","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Mia paced nervously in front of the fish tank, her heart racing like a drum as she replayed the frantic message from Mr. Hargrove in her mind. \"Bubbles is missing! We need to find him before the game!\" she could still hear his worried voice echoing. The bright fluorescent lights of Riverview Middle School reflected off the tank, illuminating the last remnants of Bubbles' home. \n\n\"Why would anyone want to take Bubbles?\" Theo asked, scratching his head, his expression a mix of confusion and concern. He leaned against the wall, his brown eyes darting across the room, trying to piece together the mystery. \"I mean, he\u2019s just a fish, right?\"\n\n\"Just a fish?\" Mia countered, crossing her arms. \"Bubbles is our mascot! Without him, the team is going to lose morale.\" She could feel the weight of the situation pressing down on her. The upcoming game against Crestview wasn\u2019t just about winning; it was about pride.\n\nJust then, the sound of laughter erupted outside the classroom door. Mia and Theo exchanged glances. \"Sounds like the Crestview team,\" Theo muttered under his breath. \"You think they could be behind this?\"\n\nBefore Mia could respond, a loud clang echoed from down the hall. Intrigued, they hurried out of the classroom, following the sound. As they rounded the corner, they stumbled upon a group of Crestview students gathered around the janitor's closet, snickering and whispering. \n\nMia shot Theo a look, determination sparking in her eyes. \"We have to check it out!\"\n\nThey approached cautiously, and Theo whispered, \u201cWhat if they\u2019re hiding Bubbles in there?\u201d\n\nJust as Mia reached for the doorknob, the door swung open, revealing Mr. Hargrove, his wild hair sticking out in all directions like a frenzied cloud. \"What are you two doing here?\" he asked, his voice a mix of surprise and irritation. \n\n\u201cMr. Hargrove! We\u2019re trying to find Bubbles!\u201d Mia exclaimed. \u201cDo you know where he might be?\u201d\n\nThe teacher's eyes darted to the group of rival students, and he lowered his voice. \u201cI don\u2019t know. But I do know that the janitor\u2019s closet can hold some surprising secrets.\u201d \n\nAs he spoke, a shriek erupted from behind them. A Crestview student pointed toward the end of the hallway. \u201cLook! There\u2019s Bubbles!\u201d \n\nMia and Theo turned, hearts in their throats, only to see a blond student holding a bowl, but no goldfish inside. It was an empty bowl! \n\n\"Hey!\" Mia shouted, sprinting toward the student. \u201cWhat do you have there?\u201d\n\nThe rival student smirked, holding the bowl high. \u201cNothing you need. Just a dirty old bowl.\u201d \n\nTheo, sensing the rising tension, tugged at Mia's shirt. \u201cWe can\u2019t let them get away with this,\u201d he urged. \u201cWe need to find out what\u2019s really going on.\u201d\n\nMia nodded, her mind racing with possibilities. This wasn\u2019t just a mystery; it was a challenge. They needed a plan. A deep breath steadied her resolve as she fixed her gaze on the Crestview students, who were now laughing and whispering among themselves.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s follow them,\u201d Mia declared, her heart pounding with a mix of fear and excitement. \u201cThey might lead us to Bubbles!\u201d\n\nAs they began to tail the Crestview group, the stakes felt higher than ever. The game was drawing near, and every second counted. What if they failed? The thought made her shiver. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nJust then, an idea struck Mia like a bolt of lightning. \u201cTheo, we need to split up. I\u2019ll follow from behind, and you take the front. If they notice you, it\u2019ll be easier for me to slip in unnoticed. We need to figure out who\u2019s behind this!\u201d\n\nTheo nodded, determination shining in his eyes. \u201cBe careful, Mia,\u201d he warned. \u201cI\u2019ll meet you back at the gym in ten.\u201d\n\nWith that, they parted ways, each charged with a sense of urgency. The bustling hallways felt a little more menacing now, and Mia couldn\u2019t help but feel that someone was watching her. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs she crept closer to the group of Crestview students, she overheard snippets of conversation. \u201cYou think they suspect us?\u201d one of them whispered. \n\nMia's heart raced. What if they were involved? Could they be the ones who had taken Bubbles? The mystery deepened, and Mia felt a thrill coursing through her. This was going to be even more complicated than she had imagined, and the clock was ticking.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is Mia and Theo's main goal in this chapter?","options":["To play in the game","To find Bubbles","To prank Crestview","To make new friends"],"correct_answer":"To find Bubbles"},{"question":"Who is the eccentric teacher assisting Mia and Theo?","options":["Mr. Hargrove","Mr. Smith","Ms. Jensen","Coach Taylor"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Hargrove"},{"question":"What does Mia suggest they do to find Bubbles?","options":["Ask the principal","Follow the Crestview students","Search the library","Go home"],"correct_answer":"Follow the Crestview students"},{"question":"How does Mia feel about the situation?","options":["Excited and carefree","Nervous and determined","Bored and uninterested","Angry and frustrated"],"correct_answer":"Nervous and determined"},{"question":"What complicates Mia and Theo's search?","options":["They get lost","The game is about to start","Crestview students are suspicious","Mr. Hargrove takes them away"],"correct_answer":"Crestview students are suspicious"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_271_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_271_ch2_img1.png","plot_271_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":739,"reading_level":"Builder"}
