   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_271_11_14","title":"The Case of the Missing Goldfish","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Chapter 3: The Hidden Truth\n\nMia paced in front of the gym doors, glancing anxiously at her watch. The game against Crestview was in less than an hour, and the absence of Bubbles, the beloved goldfish mascot, felt like a weight pressing down on her chest. The halls of Riverview Middle School buzzed with excitement, kids wearing their team colors and chanting cheers, but all Mia could think about was the missing fish and the suspect list that seemed to grow longer by the minute.\n\n\u201cMaybe we should check the art room again,\u201d Theo suggested, trying to keep his voice light despite the tension. His brown curls bounced as he spoke, and his eyes sparkled with determination. \u201cMrs. Palmer mentioned something about a new display. What if it\u2019s hidden in there?\u201d\n\nMia nodded, her mind racing through the clues they had gathered. \u201cOr it could still be in the janitor\u2019s closet. You remember how Mr. Hargrove said he\u2019d seen some strange stuff coming out of there?\u201d She shook her head, trying to ignore the creeping doubt. What if they didn\u2019t find Bubbles in time?\n\nAs they turned the corner, they spotted a group of Crestview students loitering by the lockers. Their laughter echoed down the hall like a warning bell. Mia\u2019s heart sank. \u201cWhy do I have the feeling they know more than they\u2019re letting on?\u201d she whispered to Theo, who frowned in agreement.\n\nSuddenly, one of the Crestview boys, Jake, caught sight of them. \u201cHey, look! It\u2019s Mia and her little sidekick!\u201d he jeered, a smug smile spreading across his face. \u201cStill looking for your fish? Shouldn\u2019t you be practicing your cheerleading instead?\u201d\n\nTheo stepped in front of Mia, his jaw set. \u201cWe\u2019re not afraid of you, Jake. We\u2019ll find Bubbles, and you\u2019ll be sorry!\u201d But inside, Mia could feel the knot of fear tightening in her stomach. What if they couldn\u2019t find Bubbles? What if they were too late?\n\nWith renewed determination, they slipped past the Crestview group, their footsteps quickening. Just as they reached the art room, Mia\u2019s phone buzzed with a message from Mr. Hargrove.\n\n**\"Check the aquarium in my room. Important.\"**\n\nMia exchanged a glance with Theo, her pulse racing. \u201cDo you think he knows something?\u201d\n\n\u201cThere\u2019s only one way to find out,\u201d Theo replied, glancing back nervously at the Crestview students. They took off toward the science lab, the halls now feeling like a maze of shadows.\n\nInside the lab, Mr. Hargrove stood by his aquarium, peering closely at the bubbling water. \u201cMia! Theo! Just in time!\u201d His glasses slid down his nose as he gestured for them to approach. \u201cI found something unusual!\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s heart raced as she and Theo approached. But the moment they got close, they froze. Inside the aquarium, in the place where Bubbles should have been, a flash of orange scales darted away, but it wasn\u2019t Bubbles. It was a different fish entirely.\n\n\u201cWhat is going on, Mr. Hargrove?\u201d Mia asked, her voice trembling slightly. \n\nAt that moment, the lights flickered, and a loud crash echoed from the janitor\u2019s closet. Fear gripped Mia\u2019s heart. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d she gasped.\n\n\u201cWe need to check it out,\u201d Theo urged, his eyes wide with excitement and dread.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Mia yelled, adrenaline surging through her veins. They rushed to the closet, the door ajar and shadows dancing ominously inside. The mystery was deepening, and time was running out.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What message do Mia and Theo receive from Mr. Hargrove?","options":["Check the library for clues","Check the aquarium in his room","Meet him in the gym","Go to the art room"],"correct_answer":"Check the aquarium in his room"},{"question":"What was the reaction of the Crestview students when they saw Mia and Theo?","options":["They ignored them","They cheered them on","They mocked them","They offered to help"],"correct_answer":"They mocked them"},{"question":"What unusual thing did Mia and Theo find in the aquarium?","options":["A treasure chest","Another fish","Bubbles the goldfish","A pair of sunglasses"],"correct_answer":"Another fish"},{"question":"What happens at the janitor's closet at the end of the chapter?","options":["It opens slowly","There\u2019s a crash from inside","A janitor appears","Mia finds a clue"],"correct_answer":"There\u2019s a crash from inside"},{"question":"How do Mia and Theo feel during their investigation?","options":["Excited and carefree","Nervous and determined","Bored and uninterested","Confused and lost"],"correct_answer":"Nervous and determined"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_271_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_271_ch3_img1.png","plot_271_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":588,"reading_level":"Builder"}
