   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_271_11_14","title":"The Case of the Missing Goldfish","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Mia peered into the dimly lit hallway of Riverview Middle School, her heart racing with a mixture of excitement and nerves. The air was thick with anticipation as students rushed past her, their voices blending into a cacophony of chatter. \u201cThis is it, Theo!\u201d she exclaimed, glancing back at her best friend, who was busy adjusting his backpack. \u201cWe need to find Bubbles before the game! We only have a couple of hours left!\u201d\n\n\u201cRight!\u201d Theo replied, his face lighting up with determination. \u201cBut where do we even begin? We\u2019ve searched everywhere!\u201d \n\nMia thought for a moment, tapping her chin. \u201cMr. Hargrove mentioned something about a secret compartment in his classroom. Maybe we should check there again?\u201d \n\nTheo nodded, and the duo hurried toward the science lab, their footsteps echoing in the empty corridor. They reached the door, its glass panel fogged from the warmth inside. Opening it, they were greeted by the familiar scent of fish food and the sight of bubbling aquariums. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nIn the center of the room, Mr. Hargrove stood, examining a tank full of colorful fish. His wild hair was even wilder today, sticking out in every direction. \u201cAh, Mia! Theo! I was just about to call you!\u201d he said, his eyes twinkling with enthusiasm. \u201cHave you found any leads on Bubbles?\u201d\n\n\u201cNot yet, but we were hoping to check out that secret compartment you mentioned. Do you think it could hold a clue?\u201d Mia asked, her voice laced with curiosity.\n\n\u201cAbsolutely! But be careful. It\u2019s a bit\u2026 tricky,\u201d Mr. Hargrove warned, gesturing toward a large cabinet in the corner. \u201cIt requires a special code to open it.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat kind of code?\u201d Theo wondered, peering at the cabinet with intrigue.\n\n\u201cA puzzle of sorts, much like a riddle,\u201d Mr. Hargrove replied, his eyebrows raised in delight. \u201cI\u2019ve been meaning to change it, but\u2026 I guess it could help you!\u201d \n\nMia\u2019s eyes brightened. \u201cWe can solve it! What\u2019s the riddle?\u201d\n\nMr. Hargrove cleared his throat dramatically. \u201cTo find what\u2019s lost, you must first know, the color of the sky when the sun\u2019s aglow. The number of fingers on a hand you see, plus the number of seasons, tell the key.\u201d\n\nTheo furrowed his brow. \u201cOkay, so\u2026 the sky is blue, right? That\u2019s one. And there are five fingers on a hand. Then there are four seasons, so one plus five plus four equals ten?\u201d\n\n\u201cCorrect!\u201d Mr. Hargrove beamed. \u201cNow, let\u2019s see if the code works.\u201d \n\nWith bated breath, Mia stepped forward and pressed the buttons labeled with numbers. \u201cOne, five, four,\u201d she whispered, pressing the final digit. The cabinet creaked open, revealing a jumble of papers and\u2026 a small treasure chest!\n\n\u201cWow!\u201d Theo exclaimed, lifting the chest carefully. \u201cWhat do you think is inside?\u201d\n\nAs he opened it, a loud crash echoed from the back of the room\u2014a stack of books had toppled over! Startled, they turned to find a shadow lurking in the doorway. It was Casey, the school\u2019s rival, her arms crossed defiantly.\n\n\u201cWhat are you two doing in here?\u201d she sneered. \u201cLooking for trouble, I see.\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s heart pounded. \u201cCasey, we\u2019re just trying to find Bubbles! Have you seen him?\u201d\n\nCasey smirked, her eyes glinting with mischief. \u201cMaybe. Maybe not. But I wouldn\u2019t count on it.\u201d With a final glare, she disappeared down the hall as quickly as she\u2019d come, leaving Mia and Theo frozen in place.\n\n\u201cWhat was that about?\u201d Theo breathed, glancing at Mia, who was now even more determined. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we need to figure this out\u2014quickly!\u201d Mia replied, clenching her fists in resolve. \n\nAs they returned their attention to the treasure chest, they realized this might be the breakthrough they needed. \n\n\u201cWhatever happens, we\u2019ll find Bubbles,\u201d Theo said, a spark of hope igniting in his eyes. \n\nMia nodded. \u201cAbsolutely. We\u2019re not giving up yet!\u201d \n\nWith their mission renewed, they each reached into the chest to see what secrets awaited them, ready to dive deeper into the mystery.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What riddle does Mr. Hargrove give to Mia and Theo?","options":["The color of the sky at night","The number of fingers on a hand plus the number of seasons","The weight of a goldfish","The height of a classroom window"],"correct_answer":"The number of fingers on a hand plus the number of seasons"},{"question":"What does Theo find in the treasure chest?","options":["A goldfish","A map","A stack of papers","A trophy"],"correct_answer":"A stack of papers"},{"question":"Who interrupts Mia and Theo in the science lab?","options":["Mr. Hargrove","Casey","The janitor","Their classmates"],"correct_answer":"Casey"},{"question":"How do Mia and Theo feel after solving the riddle?","options":["Frustrated","Bored","Determined","Scared"],"correct_answer":"Determined"},{"question":"What does Mia suggest they do after Casey leaves?","options":["Give up","Keep searching","Tell the teacher","Go to the gym"],"correct_answer":"Keep searching"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_271_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_271_ch4_img1.png","plot_271_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":680,"reading_level":"Builder"}
