   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_271_11_14","title":"The Case of the Missing Goldfish","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The buzzing hallways of Riverview Middle School felt different today. The air was charged with excitement, yet the weight of worry hung over Mia and Theo as they stood outside Mr. Hargrove's classroom. Their hearts raced\u2014Bubbles, the school\u2019s beloved goldfish, was still missing. With only hours left before the big game, time was not on their side.\n\n\u201cOkay, let\u2019s think this through,\u201d Mia said, her brow furrowed in concentration. \u201cIf we can figure out how Casey got involved, it might lead us to Bubbles.\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah. I still don\u2019t trust her,\u201d Theo replied, crossing his arms. \u201cBut we need to focus. What's our next move?\u201d\n\nBefore Mia could respond, a loud clang echoed from the janitor\u2019s closet down the hall. She exchanged a glance with Theo, her eyes sparkling with curiosity. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Without waiting for an answer, she started toward the closet, her heart pounding in her chest.\n\nAs they neared the dark, wooden door, Theo hesitated. \u201cMia, what if it\u2019s a trap?\u201d\n\n\u201cIt could be a clue,\u201d Mia countered, undeterred. The door creaked open, revealing shadows and the faint smell of cleaning supplies. The light from the hall illuminated a messy assortment of mops, buckets, and\u2026 a small, shimmering object in the corner.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Theo exclaimed, pointing towards the glinting item. \u201cWhat is that?\u201d\n\nMia cautiously stepped into the closet, her heart racing with excitement. She reached down, brushing aside a pile of rags, and uncovered what appeared to be a shiny, gold fishbowl. \u201cThis has to be it!\u201d she said, her voice barely above a whisper.\n\nSuddenly, they heard footsteps approaching. Panic surged through Mia. \u201cHide!\u201d She quickly ducked behind a stack of boxes, pulling Theo down with her. They held their breath as the door swung open, revealing Mr. Hargrove, his glasses perched atop his nose and his wild hair sticking up like a bird\u2019s nest.\n\n\u201cWhere is that fish?\u201d he muttered to himself, rummaging through the closet. Mia and Theo exchanged worried glances. What if he found them? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMia watched as Mr. Hargrove pulled out various items, seemingly oblivious to the two students hiding just a few feet away. His hands moved swiftly, like a conductor orchestrating a chaotic symphony. She could see the worry etched on his face, and suddenly, a thought struck her. \u201cWhat if Mr. Hargrove knows more than he\u2019s letting on?\u201d she whispered to Theo.\n\nAs Mr. Hargrove turned to leave, Theo nudged Mia. \u201cWe can\u2019t let him see us! We need to follow him,\u201d he whispered, his eyes wide with a mix of fear and determination.\n\nWith a silent agreement, they slipped out of the closet and followed at a safe distance. The school felt like a maze as they navigated through hallways bustling with students, their laughter ringing in the air. They finally caught up to Mr. Hargrove, just as he entered the gym.\n\nInside, the bright lights glared down, illuminating the excited crowd gathering for the game. But to Mia\u2019s surprise, Mr. Hargrove wasn\u2019t preparing for the game; he was standing at a table filled with fish-themed decorations. \u201cThis is where it all happens,\u201d he announced, \u201cand I need someone to help!\u201d\n\nMia exchanged a glance with Theo. \u201cThis is our chance,\u201d she said, excitement bubbling inside her. \n\nJust then, Casey appeared from the crowd, a smirk plastered on her face. \u201cWhat are you two doing here? Shouldn\u2019t you be looking for your missing fish?\u201d \n\nMia felt a rush of determination. \u201cActually, we might just be about to find him.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe tension in the air thickened like fog. Casey\u2019s eyes narrowed. \u201cYou\u2019re on the wrong track. Why does it matter to you? You\u2019re not even on the team.\u201d \n\nMia took a deep breath, her voice steady. \u201cBecause Bubbles is more than just a fish. He represents our school spirit. And we can\u2019t let anyone ruin that.\u201d\n\nA stunned silence fell between them. Casey\u2019s expression softened slightly, and for a moment, Mia saw a flicker of understanding in her eyes. Perhaps they weren\u2019t so different after all.\n\nAs they stood there, each girl pondering the importance of friendship and loyalty, Mia knew that they were on the brink of solving the mystery. And together, they would uncover what really happened to Bubbles before the game began.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What item do Mia and Theo find in the janitor's closet?","options":["A fishbowl","A mop","A trophy","A book"],"correct_answer":"A fishbowl"},{"question":"Where do Mia and Theo follow Mr. Hargrove?","options":["The cafeteria","The gym","The library","The playground"],"correct_answer":"The gym"},{"question":"What does Mia realize about the rivalry with Casey?","options":["It's unimportant","They are the same","It's fun","It's dangerous"],"correct_answer":"They are the same"},{"question":"How does Mia feel when they discover the goldfish bowl?","options":["Excited","Angry","Indifferent","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What does Mia express is important about Bubbles?","options":["He is just a fish","He represents school spirit","He is her pet","He is lucky"],"correct_answer":"He represents school spirit"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_271_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_271_ch5_img1.png","plot_271_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":729,"reading_level":"Builder"}
