   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_272_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Spooky Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The town of Willow Creek was home to many secrets, but none were as mysterious as the old library nestled between the bakery and the town square. Its wooden sign creaked in the wind, swinging gently like a pendulum, while the ivy climbed its brick walls like a curious cat. Sam and Lily Thompson stood at the entrance, staring at the worn green door, their hearts racing with anticipation.\n\n\u201cAre you sure we should be here?\u201d Lily asked, her wide brown eyes darting around as if the very shadows might whisper secrets to her.\n\n\u201cOf course! We\u2019re here to solve the mystery of the disappearing books!\u201d Sam replied with enthusiasm, puffing out his chest. He was twelve, brave and confident, often playing the part of the hero in their little adventures. At ten, Lily was his loyal sidekick, imaginative and full of wonder, always looking for magic in the mundane.\n\nAs they pushed the door open, it groaned loudly, echoing through the musty air. The inside of the library was just as old as its exterior. Dust danced in the sunlight that filtered through the high windows, illuminating rows upon rows of towering shelves filled with books. Their spines, some faded and others vibrant, called out to them like old friends.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLook at this place!\u201d Lily exclaimed, taking a deep breath that smelled of old paper and adventure. \u201cIt\u2019s like a treasure chest!\u201d\n\nSam nodded, moving deeper into the library, where he noticed a faint glow coming from the far corner. \u201cOver there! Let\u2019s check it out!\u201d He led the way, dodging a few chairs that looked ready to topple at any moment.\n\nWhen they reached the corner, they found Mrs. Knott, the librarian, hunched over a table stacked with books. Her silver hair was tied up in a bun, and her round glasses perched on her nose. She looked up, her eyes narrowing suspiciously.\n\n\u201cAh, Sam, Lily. What brings you here?\u201d she asked, her voice low and gravelly.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re investigating the missing books!\u201d Sam declared, feeling a surge of excitement. \u201cDo you know anything about it?\u201d\n\nMrs. Knott\u2019s expression shifted slightly, as if she were weighing her words. \u201cThere are stories, children. Stories that might interest you. But be careful what you wish for. Not all mysteries are meant to be solved.\u201d\n\n\u201cBut we can handle it!\u201d Lily insisted, her imagination already racing with possibilities.\n\n\u201cVery well.\u201d Mrs. Knott nodded, then gestured toward a dusty book on the shelf behind her. \u201cThis one might hold a clue. But remember, adventure comes with challenges.\u201d\n\nCuriosity piqued, Sam reached for the book, brushing away the dust. As he opened it, a small, crinkled piece of paper fluttered out and landed on the table. \u201cWhat\u2019s this?\u201d he murmured, unfolding it carefully.\n\nLily leaned closer, gasping as she recognized the strange symbols and lines. \u201cA treasure map!\u201d she squealed, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cWe have to find it!\u201d\n\nBut just as Sam was about to respond, they heard a loud thud, echoing from the attic above. The noise sent a shiver down their spines. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Lily whispered, her voice trembling.\n\n\u201cYes,\u201d Sam replied, glancing at Mrs. Knott, who now looked pale. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe must be cautious,\u201d Mrs. Knott warned, her voice barely above a whisper. \u201cThere are secrets in this library that should remain hidden.\u201d\n\nSam felt a thrill of determination surge within him. \u201cWe\u2019ll uncover the truth!\u201d he vowed, looking at Lily. They had a mystery to solve and a treasure to find, but a shadow loomed over them, and they were not alone.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go,\u201d Sam urged, taking Lily\u2019s hand as they moved toward the attic staircase. The adventure was just beginning, and they had no idea what lay ahead.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam and Lily discover in the library?","options":["A magical book","A treasure map","A hidden room","A ghost"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"Who is the librarian in the story?","options":["Mrs. Knott","Ms. Smith","Mr. Brown","Old Man Jenkins"],"correct_answer":"Mrs. Knott"},{"question":"What sound do Sam and Lily hear from the attic?","options":["A cat meowing","A book falling","A loud thud","Someone crying"],"correct_answer":"A loud thud"},{"question":"What is Sam\u2019s attitude towards the mystery?","options":["Scared","Indifferent","Brave","Disinterested"],"correct_answer":"Brave"},{"question":"How does Lily feel about the adventure they are about to embark on?","options":["Bored","Excited","Nervous","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_272_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_272_ch1_img1.png","plot_272_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":638,"reading_level":"Builder"}
