   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_272_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Spooky Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting long shadows through the dusty windows of Willow Creek Library, Sam and Lily huddled over the treasure map they had discovered. The old oak table creaked beneath them, as if it were sharing in their excitement and trepidation. \n\n\u201cI can\u2019t believe Mrs. Knott let us take this map,\u201d Lily whispered, her eyes sparkling like stars in the twilight. \u201cWhat if it really leads to the Whispering Bookshelf?\u201d \n\n\u201cThen we\u2019d be famous!\u201d Sam grinned, brushing his tousled hair back. He felt a thrill course through him\u2014this was the adventure he had always dreamed of. \u201cLet\u2019s check the map again. I think we\u2019re supposed to head to the Fiction section next.\u201d\n\nAs they made their way through the labyrinth of bookshelves, the dim, flickering overhead lights added an air of mystery. Sam felt a shiver crawl up his spine. The atmosphere was thick with secrets, and the library\u2019s creaks echoed like whispers of the past. Just then, a loud thud reverberated from the attic above. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Lily\u2019s voice trembled. \n\n\u201cProbably just the wind,\u201d Sam replied, though he wasn\u2019t sure. They reached the Fiction section, where towering shelves seemed to guard the treasures hidden within. \u201cHere it is,\u201d he said, pointing to the section marked with a faint, faded symbol on the map.\n\nTo their surprise, a thin layer of dust covered the books, undisturbed by eager hands. Sam pulled out a thick book with a cracked spine titled \"The Secrets of the Shadows.\" As he flipped through the pages, an unusual piece of parchment slipped out, fluttering to the floor. \n\nLily picked it up, her heart racing. \u201cThis looks like another clue!\u201d She unfolded it, revealing an intricate riddle: \n\n*\"In shadows deep, where tales unwind,  \nA secret waits, for hearts aligned.  \nFind the book with tales of fright,  \nAnd there you'll see the truth in light.\"*\n\nBefore Sam could respond, the dark figure they had sensed earlier appeared at the end of the aisle. Cloaked in shadow, it stood motionless, watching them with cold eyes. \n\n\u201cSam, we need to go!\u201d Lily urged, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\n\u201cNo, wait!\u201d Sam said, gripping her arm. \u201cWe have to figure this out.\u201d\n\nBut just as he spoke, the figure began to move toward them, the floorboards groaning beneath its weight. The tension in the air was palpable, like the moment before a storm breaks. \n\n\u201cI\u2014 I think it\u2019s after the map!\u201d Lily gasped, clutching the parchment tightly. \n\nThey darted towards the back of the aisle, hearts pounding like drums. Sam felt a mix of fear and determination. \u201cWe won\u2019t let it scare us away. We have to find that book!\u201d \n\nWith the riddle echoing in his mind, they sprinted through the stacks, weaving through rows of dusty novels. The figure followed, silent and relentless. Sam could feel Lily\u2019s breath quickening beside him. \n\nJust as they reached the end of a corridor, a sudden realization struck him. \u201cThe book of fright! It must be\u2014\u201d\n\nBut before he could finish, the figure closed in, and a gloved hand shot out, grasping the corner of the map. \n\n\u201cLet go!\u201d Sam shouted, yanking the map back. \n\nLily\u2019s eyes were wide with fear. \u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d \n\nThey faced a choice: run back toward the unknown attic or confront the dark figure. \n\n\u201cTogether?\u201d Sam asked, his voice steady despite the chaos.\n\n\u201cTogether,\u201d Lily replied, determination igniting her spirit.\n\nAnd in that moment, they prepared to face whatever lay ahead.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1: The dimly lit interior of the Willow Creek Library, filled with towering bookshelves, a large wooden table where Sam and Lily examine the treasure map, with flickering lights casting shadows across their eager faces. Dust motes float in the air, enhancing the atmosphere of mystery.]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2: Sam and Lily standing at the end of a narrow aisle, looking back at the cloaked figure emerging from the shadows. Their expressions reflect a mix of fear and determination, with the ominous presence of the figure looming behind them, surrounded by towering stacks of books that seem to close in on them.]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What clue do Sam and Lily discover in the Fiction section?","options":["A hidden passage","A riddle on a piece of parchment","A rare book about magic","An old map"],"correct_answer":"A riddle on a piece of parchment"},{"question":"What does the figure they encounter seem to be after?","options":["The treasure map","Sam and Lily","The Whispering Bookshelf","The book of fright"],"correct_answer":"The treasure map"},{"question":"How do Sam and Lily feel when they hear the thud from the attic?","options":["Curious","Excited","Scared","Indifferent"],"correct_answer":"Scared"},{"question":"What is the main conflict in this chapter?","options":["Finding the Whispering Bookshelf","Deciding whether to run or confront the figure","Reading the riddle","Leaving the library"],"correct_answer":"Deciding whether to run or confront the figure"},{"question":"What does the riddle hint at for Sam and Lily?","options":["A location in the library","A new friend","A secret passage","A way to escape"],"correct_answer":"A location in the library"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_272_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_272_ch3_img1.png","plot_272_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":701,"reading_level":"Builder"}
