   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_272_15_18","title":"The Secret of the Spooky Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting a golden hue through the grimy windows of the library, Sam and Lily huddled next to the old trunk they had discovered in the attic. Dust motes danced in the fading light, creating an almost ethereal atmosphere that felt both magical and foreboding. Sam's heart raced with excitement, but a shadow of doubt flickered in his mind. \u201cWhat if we don\u2019t find anything? What if we\u2019re just chasing ghosts?\u201d he said, his voice barely above a whisper.\n\nLily, ever the optimist, brushed aside his concerns. \u201cBut what if we do find something amazing, Sam? Something that could change everything?\u201d Her eyes sparkled with the possibilities, a stark contrast to Sam\u2019s cautious demeanor. He admired her unwavering belief in magic, even when reality often contradicted it.\n\nThey pried open the trunk, releasing a cloud of musty air that seemed to have been trapped for decades. Inside, they found a collection of aged maps, yellowed and fragile, along with an assortment of intricately designed keys. \u201cThese look like... treasure maps?\u201d Lily exclaimed, her voice a blend of excitement and disbelief.\n\n\u201cYeah, but they\u2019re probably just old city maps,\u201d Sam replied, though he couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that they were onto something significant. He picked up one of the maps, tracing the faded lines with his finger. There were strange symbols and annotations that made his skin prickle with curiosity. \u201cWait, look at this,\u201d he said, holding the map closer to the dim light. \u201cIt seems to lead to... the library?\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s a clue to where the missing books are!\u201d Lily suggested, her imagination taking flight. \u201cOr maybe it\u2019s a treasure hidden within the library itself. What if the library is more than just a place for books?\u201d\n\nJust then, the floor creaked ominously, and both siblings froze. A chill raced up Sam\u2019s spine. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d he whispered.\n\nLily nodded, her face pale. \u201cWe should get out of here. Now.\u201d Just as they turned to leave, a faint rustle echoed from the corner of the attic, sending their hearts pounding. Sam instinctively stepped between Lily and the noise, his protective instincts kicking in. \u201cStay behind me,\u201d he whispered fiercely.\n\nBut before they could react, the attic door swung open, revealing Mrs. Knott, the librarian. Her expression was unreadable as she stepped into the dim light. \u201cWhat are you two doing up here?\u201d she asked, her voice steady, though an undercurrent of something unspoken lingered in the air.\n\nCaught off guard, Sam stammered, \u201cWe were just... exploring.\u201d He felt the weight of her gaze, an unsettling mixture of concern and curiosity. \u201cWe found this trunk.\u201d\n\nMrs. Knott\u2019s eyebrows knit together. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be up here. This part of the library holds secrets not meant for everyone.\u201d There was an edge to her words, a hint of warning that sent a shiver down Sam\u2019s spine.\n\n\u201cBut we think we found something important,\u201d Lily interjected, her courage flaring. \u201cThese maps could lead us to something\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cEnough!\u201d Mrs. Knott\u2019s voice cut through the air, sharp and commanding. \u201cYou must understand, some secrets are best left buried.\u201d There was something in her eyes, a flicker of fear that made Sam wonder if she knew more than she was letting on. \n\nAs if sensing the tension, the light flickered, casting eerie shadows that danced around them. Sam could feel the air crackling with unspoken truths. \u201cWe\u2019re not afraid of the secrets,\u201d he declared, his voice steadying with resolve. \u201cWe have to know what\u2019s going on.\u201d\n\nMrs. Knott sighed, her shoulders slumping as if a heavy burden rested on them. \u201cVery well. But you must be careful. There are forces at play that you cannot begin to understand.\u201d She paused, her gaze piercing into Sam and Lily. \u201cAnd you\u2019re not the only ones searching. There\u2019s someone else interested in those maps.\u201d\n\nSam\u2019s heart dropped. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\n\nBefore she could answer, a loud crash echoed from downstairs, reverberating through the wooden beams of the library. Panic surged through Sam. \u201cWe have to go!\u201d he shouted, pulling Lily toward the attic stairs. \n\nAs they hurried down, dread settled in Sam\u2019s stomach. Who else was after the treasure? And what were they willing to do to get it?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam and Lily find in the trunk?","options":["Old photographs","Maps and keys","Rare books","A diary"],"correct_answer":"Maps and keys"},{"question":"How does Mrs. Knott react to the siblings being in the attic?","options":["She encourages them","She is angry","She is indifferent","She is supportive"],"correct_answer":"She is angry"},{"question":"What does Sam feel as they explore the attic?","options":["Excitement and doubt","Fear and anxiety","Happiness and joy","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Excitement and doubt"},{"question":"What event disrupts their exploration in the attic?","options":["The lights go out","A loud crash from downstairs","Mrs. Knott leaves","They find a hidden passage"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash from downstairs"},{"question":"What warning does Mrs. Knott give to Sam and Lily?","options":["To leave immediately","About other treasure hunters","Not to tell anyone","To stop reading books"],"correct_answer":"About other treasure hunters"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_272_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_272_ch2_img1.png","plot_272_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":730,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
