   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_272_15_18","title":"The Secret of the Spooky Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting long shadows across the creaky floorboards of the old library, Sam and Lily gathered in the small reading nook nestled between towering shelves. The fading light filtered through the dusty stained glass, creating a rainbow of colors on the worn carpet. The atmosphere was heavy with the scent of old books, but it was a comfort they had grown to cherish. They were not just looking for answers anymore; they felt they were on the brink of uncovering something monumental.\n\n\u201cDo you think Mrs. Knott knows more than she\u2019s telling us?\u201d Sam asked, his brow furrowed in thought as he traced his finger along the edge of the treasure map they had discovered in the attic. The parchment crinkled under his touch, and the faded ink seemed to pulse with secrets. \n\nLily, her imagination ignited, nodded. \u201cMaybe she\u2019s guarding the library\u2019s magic,\u201d she said dreamily, her wide eyes sparkling. \u201cOr maybe she knows about the treasure and is just waiting for us to figure it out!\u201d\n\nSam chuckled softly, appreciating his sister's whimsical outlook. \u201cMagic or not, we need to focus on the clues. The next stop is the hidden alcove near the poetry section. The map pointed there for a reason.\u201d \n\nWith a sense of purpose, they ventured further into the library, past the ancient wooden counters and rows of tomes that seemed to whisper their own stories. Every creak of the floorboards heightened their senses, as if the library itself was alive and watching them. They reached the poetry section, where the shelves loomed like silent sentinels. \n\n\u201cHere!\u201d Lily exclaimed, her finger hovering over a dusty spine labeled \u2018Lost Verses\u2019. \u201cIt\u2019s the book we need!\u201d \n\nSam pulled the volume from the shelf, and as he did, he felt a rush of excitement. The map had led them this far, but something felt off. The shadows deepened, and an eerie silence enveloped the library, dampening the usual rustle of pages and distant whispers. \n\nSuddenly, from behind a stack of encyclopedias, a figure slipped into view\u2014a shadowy silhouette that sent chills racing down their spines. \n\n\u201cWho\u2019s there?\u201d Sam called, his voice steadier than he felt. \n\nThe figure froze for a moment, then turned and dashed towards the exit. Sam and Lily exchanged panicked glances. \u201cWe can\u2019t let them get away!\u201d Sam shouted, launching into a sprint, with Lily close behind. The thrill of the chase fueled their adrenaline as they rushed past the rows of books, the heavy atmosphere now charged with urgency.\n\nJust as they reached the doors, the mysterious figure stumbled, knocking over a nearby lamp. The light flickered precariously before crashing to the ground, shattering the silence. In that brief moment, Sam caught a glimpse of a familiar scarf swirling around the figure's neck, a scarf he had seen before\u2014on Mrs. Knott.\n\n\u201cWait!\u201d he shouted, skidding to a stop. \u201cIt\u2019s Mrs. Knott!\u201d \n\nLily halted beside him, panting. \u201cWhat is she doing?\u201d \n\nBefore they could think further, Mrs. Knott turned, revealing a look of surprise mixed with apprehension. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be here!\u201d she said, her voice low but intense. \u201cYou don\u2019t understand what you\u2019re getting into!\u201d \n\n\u201cThen help us understand!\u201d Sam demanded, his heart racing. \u201cWe found the map, we know something is hidden here. What\u2019s the secret?\u201d \n\nMrs. Knott\u2019s expression softened momentarily, and a flicker of vulnerability crossed her face. \u201cThere are forces at play far beyond your understanding. But if you\u2019re determined to uncover the truth, you must promise to tread carefully.\u201d \n\nWith that, she handed Sam a small, intricately carved key. \u201cThis will unlock a chamber in the attic. But you must be ready for what you find.\u201d \n\nFeeling a surge of hope and determination, Sam took the key, its cold metal warm against his palm. \u201cWe will be ready,\u201d he vowed, exchanging a glance with Lily that spoke volumes. \n\nThe path ahead was fraught with danger and uncertainty, but they had taken a pivotal step forward. The attic held the promise of revelation, and with it, the hope of solving the mystery that had ensnared their town.\n\nAs they prepared to return to the attic, the air crackled with anticipation, their hearts beating in sync with the rhythm of unfolding secrets. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam and Lily discover in this chapter?","options":["A new book","A key to a hidden chamber","A note from Mrs. Knott","A treasure map"],"correct_answer":"A key to a hidden chamber"},{"question":"Who do Sam and Lily chase in the library?","options":["A mysterious figure","Mrs. Knott","A librarian","A lost book"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious figure"},{"question":"What does Mrs. Knott warn Sam and Lily about?","options":["The magic of the library","The dangers of their investigation","The importance of reading","The history of the town"],"correct_answer":"The dangers of their investigation"},{"question":"What emotion does Sam feel when holding the key?","options":["Fear","Determination","Confusion","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Determination"},{"question":"What is the setting of this chapter?","options":["A park","An attic","A library","A school"],"correct_answer":"A library"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_272_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_272_ch4_img1.png","plot_272_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":724,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
