   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_273_7_10","title":"The Vanishing Pet Mystery","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Chapter 1: The Missing Pets\n\nOn a sunny day in Maplewood, Alex Parker stood in his front yard. He loved solving mysteries. He wore his favorite green detective hat. It was tilted to one side, making him look extra cool. \n\n\u201cHey, Alex!\u201d called his best friend, Jenna. She raced over with her backpack bouncing. \u201cDid you hear about the missing pets?\u201d \n\nAlex\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\n\n\u201cFive pets have disappeared in just one week!\u201d Jenna exclaimed, adjusting her glasses. \u201cFirst Mr. Wilson\u2019s cat, then Mrs. Lee\u2019s dog, and now even Timmy\u2019s turtle!\u201d \n\n\u201cThat\u2019s strange.\u201d Alex scratched his head. \u201cWe should investigate!\u201d \n\nJenna grinned. \u201cLet\u2019s start at the park! Maybe someone saw something.\u201d \n\nThe park was colorful and filled with laughter. Kids played, and dogs chased frisbees. Alex and Jenna walked down the path, scanning for clues. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey spotted Mr. Davis, the new neighbor. He was sitting on a bench, staring at the pet show flyer. \u201cWhat a shame about all those missing pets,\u201d he said, his voice low. \n\n\u201cDo you know anything?\u201d Alex asked, tilting his head.\n\nMr. Davis smiled mysteriously. \u201cI might know a thing or two.\u201d \n\nBefore Alex could ask more, Mr. Davis stood up and walked away. \u201cCome on, Jenna!\u201d Alex said. \u201cWe need to follow him!\u201d \n\nThey quietly trailed Mr. Davis. He led them to a shady spot behind the big oak tree. Suddenly, they heard barking! \n\n\u201cDo you hear that?\u201d Jenna whispered. \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Alex\u2019s heart raced. \u201cIt sounds like a dog!\u201d \n\nThey peeked around the tree. To their surprise, they found a small group of kids. They were holding pets: a fluffy bunny, a kitten, and even a parrot! \n\n\u201cWhat are they doing?\u201d Jenna asked, eyes wide.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Alex replied. \u201cBut we need to find out!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nJust then, one of the kids noticed them. \u201cWho are you?\u201d he shouted. \n\nAlex and Jenna exchanged worried glances. They had to be brave. \u201cWe\u2019re detectives!\u201d Alex declared. \u201cAnd we want to know about the missing pets!\u201d \n\nThe kids giggled. \u201cYou\u2019re too late! We have a secret pet-swap club!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat?\u201d Alex and Jenna exclaimed together. \n\nThe chase for the truth had begun!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Alex want to be?","options":["A detective","A teacher","A firefighter","A chef"],"correct_answer":"A detective"},{"question":"How many pets have disappeared?","options":["Three","Four","Five","Six"],"correct_answer":"Five"},{"question":"Who is the new neighbor?","options":["Mr. Wilson","Mr. Davis","Mrs. Lee","Timmy"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Davis"},{"question":"What are Alex and Jenna looking for in the park?","options":["Clues","Food","Friends","Toys"],"correct_answer":"Clues"},{"question":"What do the kids have behind the oak tree?","options":["Toys","Snacks","Pets","Books"],"correct_answer":"Pets"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_273_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_273_ch1_img1.png","plot_273_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":370,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
