   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_274_7_10","title":"The Mystery of the Haunted Skate Park","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Ella, Max, and Zoe stood in front of the skate park. The sun was shining, and the ramps looked inviting. \u201cThis place is awesome!\u201d Ella exclaimed, rolling her skateboard back and forth. \n\n\u201cYeah, but what about the ghost?\u201d Max said, biting his lip. \u201cWhat if it jumps out at us?\u201d \n\nZoe laughed. \u201cGhosts don\u2019t skateboard! Come on, let\u2019s check out that abandoned building!\u201d \n\nTogether, they skated towards the old building next door. It was dark and quiet, with broken windows and peeling paint. The air felt cool, and a strange sound echoed from inside. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Max whispered. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s investigate!\u201d Ella said, her eyes bright with excitement. They entered the building, and the floor creaked beneath them. A flash of light flickered in the corner. \n\n\u201cDid you see that?\u201d Zoe gasped. \u201cWhat was it?\u201d \n\nElla grinned. \u201cOnly one way to find out!\u201d \n\nThey moved closer to the light. Suddenly, a shadow darted past. Max jumped back, but Ella moved forward. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, Max! I\u2019m right here!\u201d \n\nBut just then, a gust of wind blew through the room. Papers flew everywhere, swirling like leaves in a storm. \n\n\u201cWhoa! This is spooky!\u201d Max shouted, trying to catch his balance. \n\n\u201cLook! Over there!\u201d Zoe pointed. In the corner, they saw an old skateboard half-hidden under a pile of dust. Ella rushed over to it. \u201cIt looks just like mine!\u201d \n\nAs Ella picked up the skateboard, a soft voice echoed, \"Please... help me.\" \n\nElla froze. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d \n\nMax nodded, wide-eyed. \u201cWhat does it mean?\u201d \n\n\u201cI think that ghost really needs our help!\u201d Ella said, her heart racing. \u201cWe have to figure out what it wants!\u201d \n\nThe three friends exchanged worried glances. But then, Ella smiled. \u201cWe can do this! We just need clues.\u201d \n\n\u201cYeah! Clues,\u201d Max said, feeling braver. \n\nJust then, they heard footsteps outside. \u201cQuick! Hide!\u201d Zoe whispered. They ducked behind the old skateboard as the door creaked open. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nIn the doorway stood Mr. Grayson, the city councilman. He looked grumpy, but then he saw the skateboard in Ella\u2019s hands. \u201cWhat are you kids doing here?\u201d he asked, crossing his arms. \n\n\u201cUh, we were just\u2026 um\u2026 looking for the ghost?\u201d Ella stammered. \n\nMr. Grayson raised an eyebrow. \u201cGhosts? Pfft. They don\u2019t exist.\u201d But then, he glanced at the skateboard with a hint of nostalgia. \u201cThat skateboard... it looks familiar.\u201d \n\nMax couldn\u2019t hold back. \u201cBut what if the ghost really wants to help the skate park?\u201d \n\nMr. Grayson rolled his eyes but didn\u2019t walk away. \u201cListen, kids. If you\u2019re really serious about this ghost, you might want to learn the park\u2019s history.\u201d \n\n\u201cLike how?\u201d Zoe asked. \n\n\u201cYou\u2019ll need to dig deeper. But be careful! There are some things even I can\u2019t explain.\u201d \n\nElla smiled bright. \u201cWe will! Let\u2019s do this, team!\u201d \n\nBut as they prepared to leave, the wind howled again. The mystery was only just beginning.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ella and her friends hear in the abandoned building?","options":["A ghostly voice","A dog barking","Music playing","A train passing"],"correct_answer":"A ghostly voice"},{"question":"Who do they meet in the doorway?","options":["Mr. Grayson","A ghost","A skater","A dog"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Grayson"},{"question":"What do the kids find in the dusty corner?","options":["A treasure chest","An old skateboard","A ghost","A bicycle"],"correct_answer":"An old skateboard"},{"question":"How does Max feel about investigating the ghost?","options":["Excited","Nervous","Angry","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What does Mr. Grayson suggest they learn about?","options":["The skateboard tricks","The park's history","His favorite food","Skateboard safety"],"correct_answer":"The park's history"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_274_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_274_ch2_img1.png","plot_274_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":495,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
