   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_274_7_10","title":"The Mystery of the Haunted Skate Park","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ella, Max, and their friends gathered at the skate park. The sun was shining, and the air was filled with the sound of wheels rolling on ramps. But today felt different. A chill ran down Ella\u2019s spine. \"Do you think the ghost will show up?\" she asked, biting her lip.\n\nMax looked nervous. \"Maybe we should just stick to skating,\" he replied. \"Ghosts are scary!\"\n\n\"But what if it's not scary? What if it\u2019s just lonely?\" Ella said. \"We need to find out.\" She pointed toward the abandoned building next door. \"That\u2019s where we\u2019ll start.\"\n\nAs they skated over to the building, they heard a loud crash. Everyone froze. \"What was that?\" whispered Max. Ella gripped her skateboard tightly. \"Let\u2019s check it out!\"\n\nWhen they reached the door of the building, it creaked open. Inside, dust floated in the air, and old skateboards were scattered everywhere. There was an eerie glow coming from the back of the room. \"What\u2019s that?\" Ella whispered.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMax gulped. \"Maybe it\u2019s the ghost!\" he squeaked. Ella shook her head. \"We can\u2019t turn back now!\" She bravely stepped forward. The glow got brighter. Suddenly, a skateboard rolled out from the darkness. Ella jumped back. \"Whoa! Did you see that?\"\n\nJust then, a figure appeared. \"Hey! What are you doing in my skate park?\" It was a boy, wearing a hoodie and a baseball cap. \"I\u2019m just trying to fix it up!\"\n\nElla and her friends exchanged glances. \"You\u2019re not a ghost?\" Ella asked, confused.\n\nThe boy laughed. \"No! I\u2019m Sam. The park is in trouble. I\u2019m trying to save it!\"\n\nElla felt a spark of hope. \"Really? We want to help!\" she exclaimed. \"What do we need to do?\"\n\nSam looked serious. \"We need proof that the ghost people see is just a rumor. If we don\u2019t, Mr. Grayson will close the park for good!\"\n\nMax frowned. \"How do we prove it?\"\n\n\"We need to skate at night,\" Sam said with a smirk. \"That\u2019s when the ghost appears!\"\n\nElla\u2019s heart raced. \"Okay! Let\u2019s do it!\" she shouted. Her friends cheered, but doubt crept into Max\u2019s eyes. \"But what if it really is a ghost?\"\n\nElla smiled. \"Then we\u2019ll just have to skate faster than the ghost!\" \n\nSuddenly, the lights flickered, and the room went dark. A loud bang echoed from the back. \"What was that?\" they all gasped, looking toward the noise. \n\n\"Only one way to find out!\" Ella said, her voice steady. But her heart raced. Would they really face the ghost tonight? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith courage, they stepped deeper into the darkness, ready to solve the mystery.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ella and her friends decide to do to uncover the truth?","options":["They skate at night","They leave the park","They call the police","They tell their parents"],"correct_answer":"They skate at night"},{"question":"Who do Ella and her friends meet in the abandoned building?","options":["Mr. Grayson","A ghost","Sam","Max's brother"],"correct_answer":"Sam"},{"question":"What does Ella say about the ghost?","options":["It is scary","It is lonely","It is funny","It is angry"],"correct_answer":"It is lonely"},{"question":"What noise do they hear in the abandoned building?","options":["A dog barking","A skateboard rolling","Thunder","A door slamming"],"correct_answer":"A skateboard rolling"},{"question":"Why is the skate park in danger of closing?","options":["It is too small","Mr. Grayson wants to close it","It is haunted","There are too many skaters"],"correct_answer":"It is haunted"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_274_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_274_ch3_img1.png","plot_274_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":453,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
