   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_274_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Haunted Skate Park","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Ella leaned against the fence surrounding the vibrant skate park, her skateboard resting at her feet. The sun dipped low in the sky, casting golden rays on the ramps slick with graffiti. It was the kind of place where dreams took flight\u2014if you could just stick the landing. \"So, what do you think, Max?\" she asked, glancing at her best friend who fidgeted nervously beside her.\n\nMax adjusted his glasses and frowned. \u201cI think it\u2019s a bad idea to skate so close to the old building. You know, the one they say is haunted?\u201d His voice trembled slightly, making Ella grin. \n\n\u201cC\u2019mon! It\u2019s just a story. Besides, what if the ghost has some cool skating tricks?\u201d Ella laughed, pushing off the ground and gliding effortlessly across the concrete, her heart racing with excitement. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe skate park was alive with the sounds of wheels on wood and the laughter of her friends. Ella relished every moment, the thrill of the wind in her hair invigorating her spirit. Just then, a loud bang echoed from the abandoned building next door, freezing everyone in their tracks. \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Max\u2019s eyes widened in fear. \n\nElla shrugged off the chill creeping up her spine. \u201cIt\u2019s probably just something falling. Or maybe\u2026\u201d she leaned in closer, a mischievous glint in her eye, \u201cit\u2019s the ghost! We should investigate!\u201d\n\n\u201cSeriously?\u201d Max asked, incredulous. \u201cYou want to go near a haunted building?\u201d\n\nThe other skaters turned to them, interest piqued. \u201cElla\u2019s right! It could be fun!\u201d chimed in Leo, a skater known for his wild stunts. The group nodded in agreement, rallying around Ella\u2019s boldness.\n\nWith a determined nod, Ella led the charge toward the old building, a once-vibrant structure now draped in vines and shadow. As they approached, the setting sun cast long, eerie shadows against the walls, each creak of the building echoing their fears. \n\nSuddenly, a figure appeared in the doorway, silhouetted against the dim light. Ella and her friends froze. \u201cWhat are you kids doing here?\u201d barked Mr. Grayson, the grumpy city councilman who had always seemed to have a grudge against the skate park.\n\nElla stepped forward, heart pounding but resolved. \u201cWe\u2019re just checking out the ghost rumors, Mr. Grayson! What about you?\u201d\n\n\u201cGhosts?\u201d he scoffed, but there was a hint of something softer behind his gruff demeanor. \u201cI\u2019m here to make sure this place doesn\u2019t fall apart before the city shuts it down for good.\u201d\n\n\u201cShuts it down?\u201d Ella repeated, disappointment washing over her. \u201cWe can\u2019t let that happen!\u201d \n\nMax looked at Ella, anxiety etched on his face. \u201cHow can we stop it?\u201d\n\nMr. Grayson sighed, rubbing the back of his neck as if the weight of the park's fate rested heavily on him. \u201cYou want to help? Then find out if the ghost is real. If it scares everyone away, we might have to close it for good.\u201d\n\nElla felt a spark of determination. \u201cWe will!\u201d she declared, the thrill of the mystery igniting her spirit. \u201cWe\u2019ll uncover the truth!\u201d\n\nAs the sun set, casting the park into twilight, Ella and her friends exchanged determined looks. They were ready for the adventure ahead\u2014whatever it took to save the skate park they loved.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut deep down, as shadows danced around them, Ella couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that this ghost might be hiding secrets that were more than just spooky tales.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ella want to investigate?","options":["The skate park's ramps","The ghost rumors","Mr. Grayson's past","Max's fears"],"correct_answer":"The ghost rumors"},{"question":"What is Max's initial reaction to the ghost rumors?","options":["Excited","Indifferent","Nervous","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What is the city councilman's concern?","options":["The skate park is too noisy","The park might be shut down","He doesn't like skaters","There are too many ghosts"],"correct_answer":"The park might be shut down"},{"question":"What motivates Ella to confront the ghost rumors?","options":["Her love for skating","Her friends' encouragement","Her desire to save the skate park","Her bravery"],"correct_answer":"Her desire to save the skate park"},{"question":"How does the chapter end?","options":["With the group running away","With Ella feeling scared","With a sense of determination to investigate","With Max giving up"],"correct_answer":"With a sense of determination to investigate"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_274_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_274_ch1_img1.png","plot_274_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":579,"reading_level":"Builder"}
