   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_274_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Haunted Skate Park","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Ella stood at the entrance of the skate park, her heart racing with excitement. The sun dipped low in the sky, casting long shadows over the vibrant graffiti that decorated the ramps. She could hear the distant thumping of music from the nearby snack shack, a familiar soundtrack that felt like home. \u201cThis place is amazing!\u201d she said, spinning her skateboard beneath her feet. \n\nMax stood beside her, his brow furrowed as he adjusted his helmet. \u201cI don\u2019t know, Ella. What if the ghost really is out there? What if it\u2019s dangerous?\u201d His voice was a whisper, barely audible over the echoing laughter and clatter of skaters practicing tricks.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019ll be fine! Just a few ghost stories and some cool tricks. Plus, we\u2019ve got each other,\u201d Ella reassured him, her voice bright and confident. She flicked her hair back, ready to gather her friends. \u201cLet\u2019s find Ben and Mia!\u201d\n\nAs they searched the park, Ella felt a surge of determination. The skate park was more than just a place to ride; it was where she felt alive. It was where she had first landed her biggest trick\u2014a backflip off the highest ramp. And now, the thought of losing it to a ghostly legend was unacceptable.\n\nBy the time they spotted Ben and Mia at the half-pipe, Ella\u2019s excitement was infectious. \u201cGuys! We need to talk!\u201d she called, her voice ringing clear. The two skaters paused, curious looks on their faces. \n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d Ben asked, leaning against his board.\n\n\u201cThere\u2019s a ghost haunting that old building over there,\u201d Ella said, pointing dramatically to the crumbling structure next to the park, its windows like hollow eyes watching them. \u201cWe need to figure out what\u2019s going on before they shut this place down!\u201d \n\nMia crossed her arms, skepticism flickering in her dark eyes. \u201cIsn\u2019t that just a story? Ghosts aren\u2019t real, Ella.\u201d\n\n\u201cAre you sure?\u201d Max chimed in, glancing nervously toward the abandoned building. \u201cWhat if it really is?\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed from the direction of the old building, sending a shiver down their spines. The four friends exchanged glances, the thrill of mystery hanging thick in the air. \n\n\u201cOkay, let\u2019s check it out!\u201d Ben said, his adventurous spirit ignited. \n\nWith hearts pounding, they skated toward the building. The closer they got, the more they noticed the eerie quiet. The vibrant sounds of the skate park faded, leaving only the echo of their boards on the cracked pavement. Just as they reached the building, a streak of white flickered past one of the windows, vanishing before they could register what they\u2019d seen. \n\n\u201cDid you guys see that?\u201d Ella exclaimed, eyes wide. \n\nBefore anyone could answer, a voice came from behind them. \u201cWhat are you kids doing here?\u201d It was Mr. Grayson, the notoriously grumpy city councilman, appearing from the shadows with an intense glare. \n\nElla gulped. \u201cUh, just... investigating.\u201d \n\nMr. Grayson eyed them suspiciously, his arms crossed. \u201cYou know that place is dangerous. You should stay away.\u201d\n\n\u201cBut what if there\u2019s a ghost?\u201d Max interjected, his voice shaky but filled with a hint of courage. \n\nMr. Grayson\u2019s expression softened for a moment, as if a spark of a forgotten memory flickered in his eyes. \u201cGhosts aren\u2019t the real danger. The real danger is what\u2019ll happen if the city decides to close this place for good.\u201d \n\nElla felt a knot tighten in her stomach. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d \n\n\u201cI know things,\u201d Mr. Grayson said, his voice low. \u201cAnd you\u2019d be surprised how much this park means to me.\u201d \n\nJust then, a loud bang echoed from inside the building, startling them all. \u201cWe need to go in. Now!\u201d Ella said, her heart racing once again. \n\nWith a nod of agreement, the group pushed forward, ready to face whatever awaited them inside.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] shows the vibrant skate park during sunset, with Ella confidently riding her skateboard and Max looking a bit apprehensive. The graffiti-covered ramps and the eerie old building loom in the background, capturing the contrasting energy of excitement and mystery.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] depicts the moment the friends stand outside the abandoned building. Ella looks determined, while Max appears nervous. Mr. Grayson stands nearby, looking conflicted as he reveals his hidden connection to the park. Shadows and a vague ghostly shape can be seen through the window, adding to the suspense of the scene.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What motivates Ella to investigate the ghost rumors?","options":["To scare her friends","To save the skate park","To prove a point","To find treasure"],"correct_answer":"To save the skate park"},{"question":"What does Mr. Grayson hint at regarding the skate park?","options":["He wants it to close","He has a secret love for skating","He owns the park","He knows the ghost personally"],"correct_answer":"He has a secret love for skating"},{"question":"How does Max feel about the ghost rumors?","options":["Excited","Nervous","Angry","Indifferent"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What happens when they get closer to the abandoned building?","options":["They see a friendly ghost","A loud bang echoes from inside","They find a treasure map","They decide to leave"],"correct_answer":"A loud bang echoes from inside"},{"question":"What is one theme explored in this chapter?","options":["Friendship","Cooking","Sports","Space travel"],"correct_answer":"Friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_274_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_274_ch2_img1.png","plot_274_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":745,"reading_level":"Builder"}
