   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_274_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Haunted Skate Park","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ella stood at the edge of the skate park, the sun dipping low in the sky, casting long shadows over the half-pipe. Her vibrant skateboard, adorned with stickers, felt solid beneath her feet. She glanced back at Max, Ben, and Mia, who were all huddled together, their faces a mix of excitement and apprehension.\n\n\u201cAre we really doing this?\u201d Max asked, biting his lip. \u201cI mean, what if the ghost actually shows up?\u201d\n\nElla shrugged, determination sparking in her eyes. \u201cIf the ghost is real, we\u2019ll find out what it wants. And if it\u2019s not, we\u2019ll have a story to tell.\u201d \n\nWith that, she rolled forward, weaving through the scattered ramps and graffiti-covered walls, the thrill of the skate park urging her on. The sound of wheels clacking against concrete filled the air, but something unsettling nagged at her. The abandoned building loomed in the background, its broken windows like empty eyes watching their every move. \n\nAs they approached the building, a chill breeze swept through, causing Mia to shiver. \u201cIt feels like the air is charged with\u2026 I don\u2019t know, something spooky,\u201d she murmured.\n\n\u201cOr maybe it\u2019s just your imagination,\u201d Ben teased, nudging her playfully. The tension broke slightly, but Ella couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that they were being watched.\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed from the building, making them all jump. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Max whispered, his eyes wide. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out,\u201d Ella said, her voice steady. \u201cWe\u2019ve come too far to back down now.\u201d \n\nCautiously, they crept closer, the wooden planks creaking underfoot. Ella led the charge, her heart racing but her resolve strong. They peered into the dark interior, the light from the setting sun barely illuminating the dusty space. \n\nThen, out of the corner of her eye, Ella spotted something moving. \u201cDid you see that?\u201d she gasped, pointing toward a flicker of light that danced near the far wall. \n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s the ghost!\u201d Mia squeaked, her voice barely a whisper. \n\n\u201cOr a raccoon,\u201d Max countered, trying to sound brave. \n\nThey edged forward, the tension thick enough to cut. As they entered the building, the air felt electric. The flickering light bobbed and weaved, drawing them deeper into the shadows. Uncertainty gnawed at Ella, but curiosity pushed her forward. What if this ghost was real? \n\nJust as they reached the source of the light, it suddenly vanished, plunging them into darkness. Ella\u2019s heart pounded in her chest. \u201cGuys, stay close,\u201d she whispered, her voice trembling slightly. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Ben said, his voice barely above a whisper. \n\nA low groan echoed from the back of the building, and the ground trembled beneath their feet. Panic surged through Ella, but she couldn\u2019t turn back now. \u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d she shouted, leading the way.\n\nThey rushed toward the noise, only to find a tattered old skateboard lying on the ground, glowing faintly in the dim light. Ella knelt to pick it up, the words \u201cSave the Park\u201d etched into the deck. \n\n\u201cWhat does this mean?\u201d Max asked, his brow furrowed. Just then, a shadow loomed behind them, and the air grew colder. Ella\u2019s heart raced as she turned to face whatever was coming, her mind swirling with questions.\n\n\u201cElla, look out!\u201d Mia screamed.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe room exploded with noise as the figure emerged from the darkness. \n\n\u201cWho dares to enter my domain?\u201d the voice boomed, sending chills down Ella\u2019s spine. \n\nShe had a choice to make: confront the ghost and discover the truth, or run away and let the park\u2019s future slip through their fingers.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ella and her friends find inside the abandoned building?","options":["A ghost","A skateboard","A treasure map","A dog"],"correct_answer":"A skateboard"},{"question":"Who expresses concern about the ghost's appearance?","options":["Ella","Max","Ben","Mr. Grayson"],"correct_answer":"Max"},{"question":"What message is written on the skateboard they find?","options":["Help us","Save the Park","Leave now","Keep skating"],"correct_answer":"Save the Park"},{"question":"What feeling do the friends experience as they approach the abandoned building?","options":["Excitement","Happiness","Apprehension","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Apprehension"},{"question":"What does Ella decide to do when faced with the ghostly figure?","options":["Run away","Confront the ghost","Call for help","Ignore it"],"correct_answer":"Confront the ghost"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_274_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_274_ch3_img1.png","plot_274_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":606,"reading_level":"Builder"}
