   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_274_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Haunted Skate Park","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The sun dipped low in the sky, casting long shadows over the cracked pavement of the skate park. Ella stood at the edge, her heart pounding with excitement and a hint of trepidation. The abandoned building loomed nearby, its broken windows resembling vacant eyes watching their every move. \"This is it,\" she said, glancing back at Max, who was adjusting his helmet nervously.\n\n\"Are you sure we should even be here?\" Max asked, eyeing the graffiti-covered walls. \"What if the ghost really is haunting this place?\"\n\n\"That\u2019s exactly why we need to investigate,\" Ella replied, determination igniting her spirit like a flame. \"We can\u2019t let some silly rumors shut down the park. Plus, we need to find out what Mr. Grayson was hiding.\"\n\nAs they approached the building, Mia and Ben joined them, their faces painted with a mix of excitement and fear. \"If we stick together, we can face anything,\" Mia said, her usual confidence shining through as she flicked her skateboard back and forth.\n\nThey pushed through the creaky door, the air inside heavy with dust and the scent of old wood. Shadows danced across the walls, stretching and shrinking with every movement. The sight of old skateboards leaning against the walls and half-rotted ramps sent shivers down Ella's spine. She felt like they had stepped back in time.\n\nSuddenly, a clatter echoed from the corner of the room. The group froze, exchanging anxious looks. \"Did you hear that?\" Ben whispered, his voice barely audible.\n\n\"It\u2019s probably just a raccoon,\" Max suggested, though he didn\u2019t sound convinced.\n\nBut Ella shook her head. \"We need to check it out.\" She led the way toward the noise, her heart racing. As they moved closer, they spotted something glinting under a pile of debris. With a swift motion, Ella cleared the mess, revealing an old skateboard, its surface covered in dust but still shining beneath the grime.\n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d Mia asked, her eyes wide as she pointed at a peculiar marking on the skateboard.\n\nElla knelt down, brushing off more dirt. \"It looks like\u2026 a message?\" she murmured, tracing her fingers over the lettering. \"It says, \u2018Save the park and find me.\u2019\u201d\n\nMax\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cThat has to be a clue! But what does it mean?\u201d\n\nTheir discussion was interrupted by a sudden noise\u2014a shrill, ghostly laugh echoed through the room. The friends jumped, their hearts racing. Out of the shadows emerged a figure, shimmering and translucent. It wore a tattered skateboard shirt and a mischievous grin.\n\n\"Not here to scare you, kids,\" the ghost said, his voice a gentle whisper. \"I want to help.\"\n\nElla's breath caught in her throat. This ghost was nothing like they had imagined. He seemed more like an old friend than a haunting spirit. \"Who are you?\" she asked, trying to steady her voice.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m Tony,\u201d he replied, gliding closer. \u201cI used to skate here before the park fell into disrepair. I can\u2019t let it close down, not when there\u2019s still hope!\u201d\n\nJust as hope filled the air, a loud crash sounded from outside, making everyone jump. The ghost flickered nervously. \u201cThey\u2019re coming for the building! You need to hurry!\u201d\n\nElla exchanged glances with her friends, determination building in her chest. \"We won\u2019t let them take it. We can save the skate park together!\"\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe scene was set: Ella standing boldly in front of the abandoned building, her skateboard in hand while Max, Ben, and Mia gathered closely. The sunset painted the sky in hues of orange and purple, casting an adventurous glow on their determined faces.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe moment of suspense: The ghost, Tony, revealing himself to the stunned group amidst the dusty surroundings of the old building. His translucent form glows faintly, illuminating Ella\u2019s awestruck expression as she faces the spirit with newfound courage.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What message is found on the skateboard?","options":["Find the ghost","Save the park and find me","Close the park","Help the ghost"],"correct_answer":"Save the park and find me"},{"question":"What does the ghost reveal about himself?","options":["He wants to scare them","He used to skate at the park","He wants to close the park","He is a famous skater"],"correct_answer":"He used to skate at the park"},{"question":"How do the friends feel when they first hear the ghost's laugh?","options":["Excited","Terrified","Indifferent","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Terrified"},{"question":"What is the main goal of Ella and her friends in this chapter?","options":["To find a hidden treasure","To uncover the truth about the ghost","To skate the best tricks","To find out about Mr. Grayson's past"],"correct_answer":"To uncover the truth about the ghost"},{"question":"What emotion does Ella feel when she meets the ghost?","options":["Fear","Joy","Confusion","Courage"],"correct_answer":"Courage"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_274_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_274_ch4_img1.png","plot_274_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":647,"reading_level":"Builder"}
