   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_274_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Haunted Skate Park","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the echo of their footsteps bounced off the crumbling walls of the abandoned building, Ella, Max, Mia, and Ben felt a chill crawl down their spines. The air was thick with dust, and it smelled of stale memories, like the forgotten corners of a long-lost skate park. Tony, the ghost, floated beside them, his ethereal form shimmering like a mirage in the afternoon light.\n\n\u201cAre you all okay?\u201d Tony asked, his voice smooth yet faint, like a breeze rustling through leaves. \u201cI know this place can be a bit\u2026 intimidating.\u201d\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re fine!\u201d Ella replied with a brave grin, though her heart raced. It was strange, speaking to a ghost, but there was something comforting about Tony\u2019s presence. \u201cWhat do you want to help us with?\u201d\n\n\u201cI want to show you the truth about the park,\u201d Tony said, glancing toward a dusty window. \u201cAnd the reason it\u2019s in danger.\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed outside. The friends exchanged nervous glances, their excitement turning to dread. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Mia whispered, her eyes wide.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out!\u201d Ella said, her adventurous spirit igniting. They raced back toward the entrance, adrenaline pushing them forward. The skate park was only a few steps away, and they needed to find out what was happening.\n\nAs they burst out of the building, they were met with a scene of chaos. A group of city workers was shoving equipment into a truck. Mr. Grayson stood nearby, his face a mask of frustration, arms crossed tightly over his chest.\n\n\u201cHey! What are you doing?\u201d Ella shouted, her voice cutting through the clamor.\n\nOne worker turned, a smirk on his face. \u201cJust clearing out this place. It\u2019s done for! No one wants to skate here with all those ghost stories floating around.\u201d He laughed, tossing a shovel into the back of the truck.\n\n\u201cWait!\u201d Max called out, a plan forming in his mind. \u201cYou can\u2019t just take it away without proof!\u201d\n\nMr. Grayson\u2019s expression softened for a moment. \u201cI know some of you kids love this park, but it\u2019s too dangerous. There have been too many accidents.\u201d His voice was gruff, but there was a hint of regret.\n\n\u201cMr. Grayson\u2014\u201d Ella started, her heart pounding, \u201cwe can prove that nothing\u2019s wrong! We\u2019ve discovered that the ghost is trying to help!\u201d\n\nLaughter erupted from the workers, but Mr. Grayson\u2019s gaze turned serious. \u201cYou think a ghost can help? It\u2019s time to grow up, kids.\u201d\n\nElla took a deep breath, her resolve hardening. \u201cNo, really! Tony, the ghost, is trying to save the park from being demolished! He wants to show you the truth!\u201d\n\nWith a wave of his hand, Tony appeared in front of them, glowing slightly. The workers gasped, stepping back in disbelief. \u201cI\u2019m not here to scare anyone,\u201d he said, his voice clear. \u201cI want to protect this place, not haunt it.\u201d\n\nSurprised silence followed. Finally, Mr. Grayson stepped forward, curiosity flickering in his eyes. \u201cOkay, show us. If what you say is true, I\u2019ll do everything I can to keep this park open.\u201d\n\nElla felt a rush of hope. \u201cLet\u2019s show them how special this park is!\u201d she exclaimed, and the group sprang into action.\n\nWith Tony guiding them, they set up a mini skate session right there, showcasing tricks and flips, laughter echoing through the park. As the city workers watched, their skepticism began to fade. Ella landed an impressive kickflip, Mia performed an elegant grind, and Max, despite his earlier hesitation, executed a smooth ollie.\n\n\u201cI\u2019ll be\u2026\u201d one of the workers muttered, shaking his head in disbelief. Slowly, smiles began to spread among the onlookers, and Mr. Grayson\u2019s frown softened.\n\nBy the time the sun began to set, the park felt alive again, echoing with joy instead of fear. \u201cYou know,\u201d Mr. Grayson said, a smile breaking through his gruff exterior, \u201cmaybe we all need a second chance. Let\u2019s see what we can do to keep this place open.\u201d\n\nElla exchanged triumphant glances with her friends. They had faced their fears, discovered the truth, and, together, they had fought for something they loved.\n\nAs twilight painted the sky in shades of orange and purple, Ella smiled at Tony. \u201cThank you for believing in us.\u201d\n\n\u201cI believed in you all along,\u201d Tony replied, his spirit glowing brighter than before. \u201cNow, let\u2019s keep this place alive.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ella and her friends want to prove to Mr. Grayson?","options":["That the park is haunted","That the ghost is friendly","That they can skate better","That the park should be demolished"],"correct_answer":"That the ghost is friendly"},{"question":"What does Tony reveal to the group?","options":["He wants to scare everyone","He wants to keep the park safe","He is a skateboard champion","He lives in the abandoned building"],"correct_answer":"He wants to keep the park safe"},{"question":"What is the main action the group takes to convince the city workers?","options":["They call the police","They skate and show their skills","They leave the park","They hide from the workers"],"correct_answer":"They skate and show their skills"},{"question":"How does Mr. Grayson's attitude change by the end of the chapter?","options":["He becomes angrier","He remains indifferent","He starts smiling","He leaves the park"],"correct_answer":"He starts smiling"},{"question":"What is the significance of the sunset at the end of the chapter?","options":["It signals the end of the day","It symbolizes hope and new beginnings","It means the park is closing","It indicates a storm is coming"],"correct_answer":"It symbolizes hope and new beginnings"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_274_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_274_ch5_img1.png","plot_274_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":745,"reading_level":"Builder"}
