   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_275_7_10","title":"The Clue in the Cookie Jar","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Lily stood in the bustling cafeteria of Maplewood School. The sweet smell of cookies filled the air. Today was the big bake sale! \n\n\u201cLook at all those treats!\u201d Sarah, her best friend, said with wide eyes. \u201cI can't wait to try your cookies, Lily!\u201d\n\nLily smiled. \u201cThanks, Sarah! I hope everyone loves them!\u201d She had baked chocolate chip cookies, her favorite.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe cafeteria was colorful and lively. Students chatted and laughed. Tablecloths were decorated with bright patterns. Cookies, brownies, and cupcakes were piled high. Mr. Thompson, the principal, was busy making sure everything was perfect.\n\n\u201cWelcome, everyone!\u201d Mr. Thompson called out. \u201cLet\u2019s make this bake sale the best one yet!\u201d\n\nLily noticed a plate of cookies missing from the table. \u201cOh no! My cookies!\u201d she gasped. She had brought a whole batch. \n\n\u201cWhere could they be?\u201d Sarah asked, looking worried. \n\nLily's detective instincts kicked in. \u201cWe need to find out who took them! Let\u2019s look for clues!\u201d \n\n\u201cBut what if someone we know took them?\u201d Sarah frowned. \n\n\u201cThen we\u2019ll figure it out together,\u201d Lily said. \n\nThey walked around the cafeteria, searching for leads. Suddenly, Lily spotted a crumby trail leading to the corner. \u201cLook, Sarah! Cookie crumbs!\u201d \n\nThe girls followed the trail. It led them to a group of students gathered around a table. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d Lily asked. \n\n\u201cOh, we\u2019re just sharing some cookies!\u201d one of the students said with a grin. \n\n\u201cBut those are mine!\u201d Lily said, her heart racing. \n\n\u201cUh-oh,\u201d Sarah whispered. \u201cWhat if it was them?\u201d \n\nLily took a deep breath. She had to solve this mystery. But what if her friend Sarah was involved? \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep looking,\u201d Lily said. \n\nAs they searched, Lily felt a mix of excitement and worry. She couldn\u2019t believe someone would steal her cookies! But she had to find out who it was before the bake sale ended. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s split up,\u201d Lily suggested. \u201cI\u2019ll check the kitchen, you stay here.\u201d \n\n\u201cOkay, but be careful!\u201d Sarah replied. \n\nLily nodded and darted into the kitchen, her heart pounding. What if she found something surprising?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is Lily's favorite type of cookie?","options":["Oatmeal","Chocolate chip","Peanut butter","Sugar"],"correct_answer":"Chocolate chip"},{"question":"Who is Lily's best friend?","options":["Mr. Thompson","Sarah","The baker","A student"],"correct_answer":"Sarah"},{"question":"What does Lily decide to do when her cookies go missing?","options":["Cry","Give up","Investigate","Eat more cookies"],"correct_answer":"Investigate"},{"question":"Where does the cookie crumb trail lead?","options":["To the kitchen","To a group of students","To the principal's office","To the playground"],"correct_answer":"To a group of students"},{"question":"What does Lily suggest to Sarah?","options":["To eat cookies","To split up","To leave the bake sale","To tell Mr. Thompson"],"correct_answer":"To split up"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_275_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_275_ch1_img1.png","plot_275_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":354,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
