   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_275_7_10","title":"The Clue in the Cookie Jar","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Lily and Sarah stood in the bustling cafeteria of Maplewood School. The smell of cookies floated in the air, making their stomachs rumble. \u201cCan you believe someone took all those cookies?\u201d Lily asked, her eyes wide with determination. Sarah nodded. \u201cWe have to find them!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s talk to Mr. Thompson,\u201d Lily suggested. \u201cHe might have seen something.\u201d They rushed over to the cheerful but forgetful principal, who was trying to stack plates on a table. \n\n\u201cMr. Thompson!\u201d Lily called. He turned, his glasses slipping down his nose. \u201cDid you see anyone near the cookies?\u201d\n\n\u201cHmm\u2026 cookies?\u201d he replied, scratching his head. \u201cOh! I remember! I thought I saw Ben sneaking around earlier. But then again, I also thought I lost my keys!\u201d He laughed, shaking his head.\n\n\u201cThanks, Mr. Thompson!\u201d Sarah said, giggling. \u201cThat helps a lot!\u201d They waved goodbye and hurried towards the back room. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check if Ben is still there!\u201d Lily said. They tiptoed down the hallway. The excitement buzzed between them. Just as they reached the door, they heard whispers.\n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Sarah whispered back, wide-eyed. \n\nLily nodded and pushed the door open. Inside, they found Ben and a few other classmates. They were leaning over a table piled high with cookies! \n\n\u201cHey! What are you doing?\u201d Lily exclaimed, hands on her hips. \n\nBen jumped, dropping a cookie. \u201cUh-oh! We were just\u2026 um\u2026 taste-testing!\u201d he stammered.\n\nLily crossed her arms. \u201cTaste-testing? Or stealing?\u201d \n\nSuddenly, Sarah pointed at a plate. \u201cWait! That cookie has a bite taken out of it! It\u2019s one of Mr. Thompson\u2019s special chocolate chip cookies!\u201d\n\nBen\u2019s face turned red. \u201cOkay, okay! We wanted to help with the bake sale! But we thought we\u2019d make sure they were good first!\u201d\n\nLily smiled, her curiosity fading. \u201cSo, you weren\u2019t stealing? You just wanted to help?\u201d\n\n\u201cYes! We promise!\u201d Ben said, looking guilty.\n\nLily felt her heart lighten. \u201cThen let\u2019s all work together! We can make sure the cookies are ready for the bake sale!\u201d \n\n\u201cYay!\u201d Sarah cheered, clapping her hands. \n\nAs they returned to the cafeteria, Lily realized that friendship was just as important as being a good detective. Together, they made cookies that everyone loved. \n\nLily had found the missing cookies and learned that sometimes, it\u2019s better to work as a team. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who did Lily and Sarah talk to for help?","options":["Mr. Thompson","Ben","Their teacher","The janitor"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Thompson"},{"question":"What did Lily find Ben and the others doing?","options":["Eating lunch","Playing a game","Taste-testing cookies","Sleeping"],"correct_answer":"Taste-testing cookies"},{"question":"What was the special cookie mentioned in the chapter?","options":["Chocolate chip","Oatmeal raisin","Peanut butter","Sugar cookie"],"correct_answer":"Chocolate chip"},{"question":"What did Lily learn about teamwork?","options":["It's not important","It's better to work alone","It's helpful for baking","It can be boring"],"correct_answer":"It's helpful for baking"},{"question":"What did Mr. Thompson forget?","options":["His lunch","His keys","The bake sale","His glasses"],"correct_answer":"His keys"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_275_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_275_ch5_img1.png","plot_275_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":393,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
