   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_275_11_14","title":"The Clue in the Cookie Jar","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The bustling cafeteria of Maplewood School was a whirlwind of color and excitement. Tables were draped in bright tablecloths, while the aroma of freshly baked cookies wafted through the air, mingling with the chatter of students eager to buy their favorite treats. Lily stood at one of the tables, her heart racing with anticipation. Today was the day of the annual bake sale, and she had spent hours perfecting her chocolate chip cookie recipe, one she had learned from her grandmother.\n\n\u201cLook at all those cookies!\u201d her best friend Sarah exclaimed, her eyes wide with delight. She brushed a strand of curly hair behind her ear, a gesture that Lily recognized as a signal of her excitement. \u201cI can\u2019t wait to eat one! Or five!\u201d\n\nLily laughed. \u201cYou might need to pace yourself, Sarah. We don\u2019t want to spoil your dinner!\u201d\n\nJust then, Mr. Thompson, the cheerful but forgetful principal, appeared at the end of the table, his eyes dancing with mischief. \u201cGood morning, my little bakers! Have you saved a cookie for me?\u201d\n\n\u201cOf course, Mr. Thompson!\u201d Lily replied, her face lighting up as she held out a plate. \u201cThese are the best cookies in town!\u201d\n\nAs Mr. Thompson took a cookie, a wave of laughter and chatter filled the cafeteria, creating a cozy atmosphere that wrapped around Lily like a warm blanket. However, beneath the laughter, a sense of unease began to creep in. With just minutes to go before the sale started, Lily noticed something odd. One of the plates of cookies, her special batch, was missing!\n\n\u201cSarah, did you see where my cookies went?\u201d Lily asked, her voice tinged with worry.\n\nSarah shook her head, her brows furrowing in concern. \u201cNo, but they were right here a second ago! Maybe someone took them to set up?\u201d\n\nBut Lily had a sinking feeling in her stomach. She glanced around the cafeteria, scanning the faces of her classmates. Could it be that someone had stolen her cookies? With a determined spark in her eyes, she decided she had to get to the bottom of it.\n\n\u201cOkay, I\u2019m going to find out who took them,\u201d Lily declared, her detective instincts kicking in. \u201cIt\u2019s a mystery, and I love mysteries!\u201d\n\n\u201cWait, you can\u2019t do this alone,\u201d Sarah said, her tone shifting from worry to excitement. \u201cI\u2019m coming with you!\u201d\n\nThe two friends hurried around the cafeteria, asking other students if they had seen anything suspicious. The playful banter of voices surrounded them like a buzzing beehive, but Lily was focused. She noticed that some students were acting strangely, glancing away when she approached. It was like a scene from a detective novel, and she couldn\u2019t help but feel the thrill of the chase.\n\nThen, as they rounded the corner, Lily spotted a flash of movement near the dessert table. \u201cDid you see that?\u201d she whispered, pointing. \u201cThere\u2019s someone hiding behind the cookies!\u201d\n\nThey crept closer, heartbeats quickening, only to find one of their classmates, Tim, tugging nervously at his shirt. \u201cUh, hey, guys,\u201d he stammered. \u201cI was just\u2014um\u2014looking for some cookies.\u201d\n\nLily narrowed her eyes. \u201cAre you sure about that? Because it looks like you\u2019re trying to hide something.\u201d\n\nJust as Tim opened his mouth to respond, Sarah giggled, breaking the tension. \u201cLily, maybe we should play it cool. We don\u2019t have to accuse anyone yet!\u201d\n\nBut before Lily could reply, she caught a glimpse of something shiny nestled in Tim's pocket. Her heart raced. Was that a clue?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nIn that moment, Lily realized this mystery was just getting started. She took a deep breath, ready to tackle whatever came next. Who would dare steal cookies from a bake sale? And more importantly, could it be someone she knew?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cAlright, Tim,\u201d she said, her voice steady. \u201cLet\u2019s figure this out together.\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event is taking place at Maplewood School?","options":["A science fair","A bake sale","A sports day","A holiday party"],"correct_answer":"A bake sale"},{"question":"Who is Lily's best friend?","options":["Tim","Mr. Thompson","Sarah","Jessie"],"correct_answer":"Sarah"},{"question":"What is missing from Lily's table?","options":["Brownies","Cupcakes","Cookies","Pies"],"correct_answer":"Cookies"},{"question":"What does Lily want to do when her cookies disappear?","options":["Bake more cookies","Find out who took them","Tell the principal","Go home"],"correct_answer":"Find out who took them"},{"question":"How does Sarah react to Lily's detective instincts?","options":["She is uninterested","She is scared","She wants to help","She wants to leave"],"correct_answer":"She wants to help"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_275_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_275_ch1_img1.png","plot_275_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":648,"reading_level":"Builder"}
