   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_275_11_14","title":"The Clue in the Cookie Jar","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Lily stood in the bustling cafeteria of Maplewood School, the sweet smell of cookies wafting through the air like a warm hug. The bake sale was in full swing, and tables overflowed with colorful treats. She watched as her classmates eagerly sampled the goodies, their faces lighting up with delight. Her heart swelled with pride\u2014after all, she had baked the best chocolate chip cookies, carefully following her grandmother's secret recipe.\n\n\"Look, there\u2019s Sarah!\" Lily exclaimed, spotting her best friend at the edge of the crowd. Sarah was sampling a cupcake, her eyes sparkling with mischief. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs Lily approached, she noticed an unusual commotion at the serving table. Mr. Thompson, the cheerful but forgetful principal, was scratching his head, looking bewildered. \"Where did all the cookies go?\" he muttered to himself, glancing at the empty plate that had once held Lily\u2019s prized creations.\n\nLily\u2019s stomach sank. \"Mr. Thompson, are you serious? My cookies are missing!\" \n\nHe turned to her, concern spreading across his face. \"I\u2019m afraid they are, Lily. They were right here just a moment ago! This bake sale was supposed to be the best one yet!\"\n\nLily\u2019s detective instincts kicked in. She needed to solve this mystery, and fast. \"Who was at the table when they disappeared?\" \n\nMr. Thompson thought for a moment. \"I saw Sarah, James, and Emma all around here. But they were helping me serve the other desserts. It all happened so quickly\u2014one moment they were here, and the next, poof!\"\n\nHer heart raced. Sarah was her best friend, but was she also a suspect? If Sarah had taken the cookies, it would break Lily\u2019s heart. \"I need to ask Sarah some questions,\" Lily decided aloud, determination shining in her eyes.\n\nJust then, a commotion erupted nearby. Lily turned to see James, a boy with a reputation for being a prankster, holding up a cookie jar triumphantly. \"Look what I found!\" he shouted, his voice booming over the chatter of the cafeteria. \"Looks like our little bake sale burglar has been caught red-handed!\"\n\nLily\u2019s stomach twisted. The jar was the one that had contained her cookies, but why was it with James? \"James, where did you get that?\" she demanded, marching over.\n\nHe grinned, but there was something about his smile that felt off. \"Oh, I just found it behind the snack table. Thought it was a leftover from the last bake sale.\" \n\nLily raised an eyebrow, unconvinced. \"Right... because cookie jars just appear out of nowhere.\"\n\n\"Maybe you should be looking at Sarah instead,\" he teased, tossing a cookie into his mouth. \n\n\u201cStop it, James! She\u2019s my friend!\u201d Lily defended, feeling defensive and angry. But doubts crept into her mind like shadows, whispering questions she didn\u2019t want to face.\n\nAs she glanced back at Sarah, who was now nervously chewing on her nails, a pang of betrayal tugged at Lily\u2019s heart. Could her best friend really be involved? The thrill of the detective work was quickly turning sour. \n\nLily took a deep breath, trying to calm the storm of emotions swirling within her. \"I\u2019ll figure this out,\" she murmured to herself, eyes narrowed in concentration. The clock was ticking, and she needed to find the truth before the bake sale ended.\n\nJust then, she spotted a small piece of paper poking out from under the table where Mr. Thompson had been. \"What\u2019s this?\" she wondered aloud, kneeling down to retrieve it.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs she unfolded the note, her heart raced. It was a partially written recipe, but not just any recipe\u2014it was for cookies. The last line read: \u201cAdd a dash of secret ingredient, and you\u2019ll be the cookie hero.\u201d Who had written this, and what did it mean?\n\nNow, more than ever, Lily had to uncover the truth behind the missing cookies, her heart torn between friendship and her desire for justice. The mystery was deepening, and with each clue, the stakes were getting higher.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Lily discover is missing from the bake sale?","options":["Cupcakes","Brownies","Cookies","Pies"],"correct_answer":"Cookies"},{"question":"Who does Lily suspect might have taken her cookies?","options":["James","Emma","Sarah","Mr. Thompson"],"correct_answer":"Sarah"},{"question":"What object does James find that causes a stir?","options":["A cookie jar","A cupcake","A recipe book","A pie"],"correct_answer":"A cookie jar"},{"question":"What does the note Lily finds contain?","options":["A recipe for brownies","A grocery list","A cookie recipe","A birthday invitation"],"correct_answer":"A cookie recipe"},{"question":"What emotion does Lily feel as she investigates her missing cookies?","options":["Excitement","Fear","Confusion","All of the above"],"correct_answer":"All of the above"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_275_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_275_ch2_img1.png","plot_275_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":670,"reading_level":"Builder"}
