   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_275_11_14","title":"The Clue in the Cookie Jar","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The cafeteria buzzed with excitement as students filled the long tables lined with colorful platters of cookies, cupcakes, and brownies. The smell of baked goods wafted through the air, making Lily's stomach rumble with delight. She stood beside Sarah, her best friend, who was wearing a bright yellow apron adorned with smiley faces. \"I can't believe someone would steal cookies from a bake sale! It\u2019s just so\u2026 wrong,\" Lily said, her brow furrowed in concentration.\n\n\"Maybe we should ask Mr. Thompson if he saw anything strange,\" Sarah suggested, her eyes wide with curiosity. Yet, Lily felt a knot in her stomach. What if Sarah knew more than she was letting on? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs Lily and Sarah approached the principal\u2019s table, they spotted Mr. Thompson fumbling with a stack of papers. His gray hair seemed to stand on end, and he wore a sheepish grin as he glanced up. \"Ah! My star bakers! What can I do for you?\" \n\n\"Mr. Thompson, have you noticed anything unusual with the cookies? Like, um, anyone acting suspicious?\" Lily asked, trying to keep her voice steady. \n\nHe scratched his head, his eyes wandering as if lost in thought. \"Well, I can\u2019t say I noticed anything, but I did see Jason heading towards the cookie table a few times. You know how he loves sweets!\" \n\n\"Jason, huh?\" Lily mumbled, jotting down another name on her notepad. The mystery was thickening like a gooey chocolate chip cookie dough. \n\n\u201cDo you think he took them?\u201d Sarah asked, worry creeping into her voice. Lily hesitated, weighing her next words carefully. She didn\u2019t want to accuse anyone without proof, yet she couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that Sarah had become too close to the case, too involved. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check the kitchen next! Maybe there are more clues,\u201d Lily suggested, her detective instincts kicking in. \n\nThey pushed through the swinging doors leading to the kitchen, where the heat from the ovens wrapped around them like a warm blanket. The sight was chaotic\u2014bakers were rushing around, frosting cupcakes and filling jars with sprinkles. But something caught Lily's eye\u2014on the counter lay a crumpled piece of paper. Cautiously, she picked it up and unfolded it. \n\n\"Look, Sarah! It's a recipe!\" \n\nAs she read the ingredient list, her heart raced. But there was something odd about it\u2014the measurements were scribbled out, replaced with names of cookie flavors instead: \"Chocolate Chip,\" \"Oatmeal Raisin,\" and then\u2026 \"Peanut Butter Surprise.\" \n\n\u201cLily, what does it mean?\u201d Sarah asked, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\n\u201cI think it\u2019s a clue,\u201d Lily replied, her mind whirling with possibilities. The recipe was obviously altered, someone was hiding something. Just then, the kitchen door swung open, and they were greeted by none other than Jason, his face smeared with frosting. \n\n\u201cUh, hey! What are you two doing in here?\u201d he stammered, his eyes darting nervously. \n\nLily felt her heart race. \"We were just\u2014\u201d \n\nBefore she could finish, Sarah blurted, \u201cDid you take the cookies?\u201d \n\nJason looked taken aback. \u201cWhat? No! I swear, I wouldn\u2019t do that!\u201d \n\nThe tension in the air was palpable. Lily\u2019s mind raced. Was Jason telling the truth? Just then, a loud crash echoed from the hallway, followed by the sound of laughter. The trio exchanged worried glances. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go check it out,\u201d Lily said, her voice firm. They rushed out into the hallway, where a group of students was gathered, laughing and pointing. \n\n\u201cWhat now?\u201d Sarah asked, her excitement bubbling to the surface. \n\nBut Lily only frowned, her detective instincts flaring. \u201cI have a bad feeling about this\u2026\u201d \n\nThe laughter echoed louder, and Lily's heart raced. Every second felt like a ticking clock. Something important was about to be revealed, and she had to know what it was before the bake sale ended.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they neared the crowd, Lily steeled herself for whatever awaited them. This was it\u2014the moment of truth, and she couldn\u2019t help but wonder if Sarah was hiding something after all.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Lily discover in the kitchen?","options":["A crumpled piece of paper","A jar of cookies","A hidden camera","A lost bake sale poster"],"correct_answer":"A crumpled piece of paper"},{"question":"Who does Mr. Thompson suggest might be involved in the disappearance of the cookies?","options":["Sarah","Lily","Jason","Himself"],"correct_answer":"Jason"},{"question":"What flavors are listed in the altered recipe Lily finds?","options":["Chocolate Chip, Oatmeal Raisin, Peanut Butter Surprise","Peanut Butter, Sugar, Snickerdoodle","Brownie, Coconut, Chocolate Chip","Vanilla, Lemon, Gingerbread"],"correct_answer":"Chocolate Chip, Oatmeal Raisin, Peanut Butter Surprise"},{"question":"Why does Lily start to suspect Sarah?","options":["Sarah loves sweets too","Sarah was seen near the bake sale","Lily feels uneasy about the investigation","Sarah doesn't want to help find the cookies"],"correct_answer":"Lily feels uneasy about the investigation"},{"question":"What event interrupts the conversation between Lily, Sarah, and Jason in the kitchen?","options":["A loud crash from the hallway","Mr. Thompson calling for help","Another student stealing cookies","The fire alarm ringing"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash from the hallway"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_275_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_275_ch3_img1.png","plot_275_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":673,"reading_level":"Builder"}
