   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_275_11_14","title":"The Clue in the Cookie Jar","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the bustling cafeteria of Maplewood School filled with laughter and the sweet aroma of baked goods, Lily paced back and forth, her mind racing faster than a rollercoaster. She couldn\u2019t believe the cookies were still missing, especially with the bake sale just hours away. The tables were adorned with colorful platters, each one more delectable than the last, but Lily\u2019s heart sank every time she glanced at the empty space where her cookies used to sit.\n\n\u201cLily, you alright?\u201d Sarah asked, her voice laced with concern. She always had a knack for reading Lily's emotions, like how one reads a favorite book, cover to cover. \n\n\u201cNot really,\u201d Lily admitted, crossing her arms. \u201cIf I don\u2019t find those cookies soon, the bake sale is going to be a disaster! And now... you\u2019re a suspect.\u201d Her throat tightened as she said the last part, the words spilling out like a soda can shaken too hard.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe cheerful cafeteria buzzed with students sampling treats, oblivious to the mystery unfolding. In the corner, Jason was chatting with his friends, a mischievous grin plastered across his face. He had always been Lily\u2019s biggest rival in baking competitions, and the idea of him stealing her cookies didn\u2019t seem far-fetched. \n\n\u201cDo you really think I\u2019d take your cookies?\u201d Sarah asked, a mix of hurt and confusion flashing across her face. \u201cYou know I\u2019d never do that!\u201d\n\nLily sighed, the weight of her suspicion heavy in the air. \u201cI know, but I just\u2026 I need to consider all possibilities. What if someone tricked you into helping?\u201d\n\nThe thought made Sarah frown, her lips pressing into a line. \u201cWell, what do we do now? We can\u2019t just sit here!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s look for more clues,\u201d Lily said, her detective instincts kicking in. \u201cMaybe we can retrace our steps from earlier.\u201d\n\nTogether, they made their way to the kitchen, the clatter of baking trays echoing as they searched for any signs of where the cookies might have gone. As they rifled through drawers and cabinets, Lily\u2019s heart raced with every creak of the floor, a constant reminder of the mystery hanging over them.\n\nSuddenly, Lily spotted a small piece of parchment sticking out from the recipe book. She rushed over, pulling it free. It was a new recipe\u2014one that sounded oddly familiar.\n\n\u201cWait a minute!\u201d Lily exclaimed, her eyes widening in realization. \u201cThis is Mr. Thompson\u2019s famous chocolate chip cookie recipe, but it has something written at the bottom. \u2018Add a pinch of salt and a dash of mischief.\u2019\u201d\n\n\u201cDo you think it\u2019s a clue?\u201d Sarah asked, her expression shifting from disbelief to excitement.\n\n\u201cIt has to be,\u201d Lily replied, her mind whirring like a blender. \u201cBut what does it mean? Who would add mischief to a cookie recipe?\u201d\n\nJust then, they heard a loud crash from the nearby supplies shelf. They both spun around to see Jason, surrounded by toppled flour bags, his triumphant expression quickly morphing into panic. \n\n\u201cUh, I can explain\u2014\u201d he stammered, but Lily cut him off.\n\n\u201cNot a chance, Jason! You\u2019ve been acting suspicious all day!\u201d \n\nWith the tension mounting, Lily took a step closer, her mind racing. Could Jason really be the cookie thief after all? The pieces were starting to fit together, and she was determined to uncover the truth before the sale began.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s get to the bottom of this,\u201d Lily declared, her voice steady. \u201cIt\u2019s time to find out who really stole my cookies!\u201d\n\nWith renewed determination, they prepared to confront Jason, hoping that the clues would lead them to the answers they desperately needed.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What clue do Lily and Sarah find in the recipe book?","options":["A cookie ingredient list","Mr. Thompson's chocolate chip cookie recipe","A list of suspects","A baking schedule"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Thompson's chocolate chip cookie recipe"},{"question":"How does Lily feel about Sarah being a suspect?","options":["She is sure Sarah did it","She is confused and upset","She does not care","She thinks it's funny"],"correct_answer":"She is confused and upset"},{"question":"What happens when they confront Jason?","options":["He confesses immediately","He runs away","He is found in a mess of flour bags","He helps them"],"correct_answer":"He is found in a mess of flour bags"},{"question":"What is the setting of this chapter?","options":["The playground","The library","The cafeteria","The gym"],"correct_answer":"The cafeteria"},{"question":"What do Lily and Sarah decide to do in this chapter?","options":["Give up on the cookies","Look for more clues","Bake more cookies","Ask the principal for help"],"correct_answer":"Look for more clues"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_275_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_275_ch4_img1.png","plot_275_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":615,"reading_level":"Builder"}
