   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_275_11_14","title":"The Clue in the Cookie Jar","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Lily stood in the bustling cafeteria of Maplewood School, her heart racing as she scanned the crowd. The aroma of sweet cinnamon and melting chocolate chips wafted through the air, but it was tainted by a cloud of suspicion. She could see the table where the cookies had been displayed, now conspicuously empty except for a few crumbs and a lone cookie jar\u2014one that had been turned upside down. \n\n\u201cDo you think he took them?\u201d Sarah whispered, her eyes wide as she pointed towards Jason, who was in deep conversation with a group of classmates, laughing as if he hadn\u2019t a care in the world. Lily frowned, trying to decipher his expression. Was it guilt, or just the excitement of the bake sale? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Lily replied, her mind racing. \u201cBut if he did, we need to find proof.\u201d The two friends exchanged nervous glances before Lily hurriedly scribbled her thoughts in her ever-present notebook.\n\nAs lunch progressed, the cafeteria was filled with chatter and laughter. Yet, for Lily, the noise was just a dull hum overshadowed by her racing thoughts. She felt a pang in her stomach\u2014not just from hunger but from the gnawing fear of what would happen if Sarah was wrong about Jason. \u201cMaybe we should talk to him?\u201d Sarah suggested tentatively. \u201cIf he\u2019s innocent, we\u2019ll clear his name.\u201d\n\nLily took a deep breath. \u201cOkay, but let\u2019s be careful. If he is behind this, we don\u2019t want to give him an excuse to hide the evidence.\u201d They approached Jason with cautious steps, determined yet nervous.\n\n\u201cHey, Jason!\u201d Lily called out, forcing a smile. \u201cGot a minute?\u201d He turned, his eyes twinkling with mischief.\n\n\u201cSure! What\u2019s up?\u201d he replied, leaning back in his chair, seemingly relaxed. \n\nLily exchanged glances with Sarah before plunging into her questions. \u201cDid you see anyone hanging around the cookie table when the cookies went missing?\u201d\n\nJason shrugged, his expression unreadable. \u201cI was too busy trying to win the pie-eating contest to notice anything. But I did see Mr. Thompson near the table earlier. He seemed really\u2026 distracted.\u201d\n\nLily\u2019s heart skipped a beat. \u201cMr. Thompson? Distracted?\u201d she echoed. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\n\n\u201cOh, you know. He was talking to Mrs. Greene about a new kind of cookie recipe.\u201d Jason gestured vaguely, \u201cI think he forgot he was supposed to be supervising. He was all over the place!\u201d \n\n\u201cThanks, Jason. We\u2019ll keep that in mind,\u201d Lily said, her mind already spinning with new possibilities. After a hasty goodbye, she pulled Sarah aside. \u201cWhat do you think? Could Mr. Thompson be involved somehow?\u201d\n\nBefore Sarah could answer, they heard a loud shout from across the cafeteria. \u201cHey! Whose cookies are these?\u201d A student was holding up a plate of cookies, clearly labeled as the ones from Lily\u2019s bake sale. The crowd turned to look, and Lily\u2019s heart sank. \n\n\u201cThose were supposed to be for the sale! They\u2019re missing!\u201d shouted another student. \n\nJust then, Lily noticed something strange\u2014a piece of parchment peeking out from Jason\u2019s backpack. Her detective instincts kicked in. \u201cWait here,\u201d she whispered, darting towards him, her heart pounding. \n\nAs she reached Jason's backpack, Lily took a deep breath and peeked inside. The parchment slid out, revealing a half-finished recipe with a note scribbled in the margin: \u201cIf you want cookies, you know what to do.\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat is this?\u201d she muttered, her pulse racing. \n\nSuddenly, the cafeteria went quiet. All eyes were on her, and she could feel the weight of their curiosity. \n\n\u201cGotcha.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nLily turned, and there stood Sarah, a look of shock on her face. \u201cYou didn\u2019t think I stole the cookies, did you? Because I\u2026 I couldn\u2019t bear to think of you accusing me!\u201d \n\nLily\u2019s heart dropped. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean\u2026\u201d But before she could finish, Mr. Thompson appeared, his brow furrowing as he caught sight of the parchment. \n\n\u201cLily! What\u2019s going on here?\u201d he asked, his cheerful demeanor fading. \n\nLily took a deep breath, her voice steady now. \u201cMr. Thompson, I think there\u2019s more to this cookie theft than we know. And I think it starts with this note.\u201d \n\nAs the tension hung in the air, Lily realized that uncovering the truth might just mend the rift between her and Sarah.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who does Lily approach to ask about the missing cookies?","options":["Mr. Thompson","Sarah","Jason","Mrs. Greene"],"correct_answer":"Jason"},{"question":"What detail does Jason reveal about Mr. Thompson?","options":["He was eating cookies.","He seemed distracted.","He stole the cookies.","He was baking cookies."],"correct_answer":"He seemed distracted."},{"question":"What does Lily discover in Jason's backpack?","options":["A cookie jar","A recipe with a note","A cookie plate","A baking book"],"correct_answer":"A recipe with a note"},{"question":"How does the chapter end?","options":["Lily finds the cookies.","Students are surprised by a note.","Lily argues with Sarah.","Mr. Thompson leaves."],"correct_answer":"Students are surprised by a note."},{"question":"What is Lily's main concern regarding Sarah in this chapter?","options":["She was baking cookies.","She might be the thief.","She doesn't like cookies.","She wants to leave."],"correct_answer":"She might be the thief."}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_275_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_275_ch5_img1.png","plot_275_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":726,"reading_level":"Builder"}
