   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_275_15_18","title":"The Clue in the Cookie Jar","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Crime Solving","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the bustling cafeteria of Maplewood School filled with laughter and the sweet aroma of baked goods, Lily stood behind the bake sale table, her heart racing. The vibrant colors of frosting and sprinkles sparkled under the fluorescent lights, yet her mind was preoccupied with thoughts of the cookie thief. Where could they be hiding? She glanced at Sarah, who was meticulously arranging the last batch of cookies, her signature chocolate chip recipe that always drew a crowd. The sight of her best friend made Lily's chest tighten; she couldn't shake off the feeling that Sarah was somehow involved.\n\n\"Are you okay, Lily?\" Sarah asked, her brow furrowing as she noticed Lily's distracted gaze.\n\n\"Yeah, just...thinking,\" Lily replied, forcing a smile. \"You know, about the cookies.\"\n\nSarah nodded, but her expression shifted. \"I can't believe someone would steal from us\u2014especially from you. You worked so hard on those recipes.\"\n\nAs Lily contemplated her next move, the sounds of chatter around her faded into the background. She had to find a way to confront Sarah about the strange clue she had found\u2014the half-baked recipe written in a hasty scrawl, suggesting a secret ingredient only a few knew about. Was it possible that Sarah had been hiding something?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe cafeteria buzzed with excitement, but for Lily, its vibrancy felt muted. She needed clarity. Pulling Sarah aside, she whispered, \"Can we talk? It's important.\"\n\n\"Sure, what's up?\" Sarah asked, her eyes wide with curiosity.\n\n\"I found this,\" Lily said, revealing the crumpled piece of paper. \"Do you recognize this recipe?\" She held it out, her voice steady but her hands trembling.\n\nSarah studied it, her face pale. \"I... I might have seen it before. But I didn\u2019t think much of it.\" A flicker of guilt crossed her features. \"Lily, I would never\u2014\"\n\n\"I know, but you have to understand,\" Lily interrupted, her voice rising slightly. \"You're my best friend, and I don\u2019t want to believe you could be involved in this. But the clues keep pointing towards you.\"\n\nSarah's eyes widened, and a mix of anger and hurt clouded her expression. \"How could you even think that? You know me better than anyone!\"\n\nThe tension was palpable, and for a moment, Lily regretted bringing it up. But she reminded herself that truth was the path to resolution, no matter how painful.\n\n\"I'm just trying to figure this out,\" Lily said softly. \"We can solve this together.\"\n\nA flicker of hope sparked in Sarah's eyes. \"Okay, let\u2019s find out who really did this.\" \n\nThe two friends began to piece together their memories of the bake sale. As they exchanged thoughts, a sudden shout from the table interrupted them.\n\n\u201cHey! What happened to the cookies on this plate?\u201d Jenna\u2019s voice rang out, drawing everyone\u2019s attention. She stood with her hands on her hips, an incredulous look on her face. \u201cThey were right here!\u201d\n\nLily's heart raced as she exchanged a glance with Sarah, realizing the mystery wasn't over yet. The clues were multiplying, and the bake sale was far from finished.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nDetermined to find the truth, Lily approached Jenna. \"You saw the cookies last, right? What were they like?\"\n\nJenna crossed her arms. \"They were chocolate chip, with extra pecans. The best batch. I had my eye on them all day!\"\n\n\"Could you think of anyone who might want to take them?\" Sarah asked, her tone gentle but focused.\n\nJenna's expression softened as she considered. \"Well, I did see Mr. Thompson wandering around earlier, looking a bit lost. He has a notorious sweet tooth, you know.\"\n\nLily felt a rush of realization. If the principal had been in the vicinity, perhaps he held a key to the mystery. \"Let\u2019s talk to him,\" she suggested, her adrenaline surging. \n\nAs the three girls walked towards the principals\u2019 office, the weight of the unknown hung in the air. Would they uncover the truth, or would the cookie thief remain a phantom in their midst? Lily felt a surge of determination; she was not just a baker but a detective\u2014and she would see this case through to the end.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What clue does Lily confront Sarah about?","options":["A missing cookie recipe","A crumpled piece of paper","A comment from Jenna","A message from Mr. Thompson"],"correct_answer":"A crumpled piece of paper"},{"question":"Who does Jenna suspect might have taken the cookies?","options":["Sarah","Lily","Mr. Thompson","Another student"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Thompson"},{"question":"What internal conflict does Lily face in this chapter?","options":["Loyalty to her friend vs. the need to solve the mystery","Her fear of confrontation","Desire to win the bake sale","Her rivalry with Jenna"],"correct_answer":"Loyalty to her friend vs. the need to solve the mystery"},{"question":"What emotion does Lily feel towards Sarah when she confronts her?","options":["Anger","Disappointment","Fear","Concern"],"correct_answer":"Concern"},{"question":"What motivates Lily to continue her investigation?","options":["Her love for baking","Her friendship with Sarah","Her determination to uncover the truth","Her desire to impress Mr. Thompson"],"correct_answer":"Her determination to uncover the truth"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_275_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_275_ch4_img1.png","plot_275_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":694,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
