   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_266_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Missing Music Box","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the final act of the talent show approached, the backstage area buzzed with excitement and a hint of tension. Mia and Theo stood by the heavy curtain, peering into the dimly lit space where the mysterious backstage room loomed. The air was thick with the scent of popcorn and nervous energy. \n\n\u201cOkay, this is it. We need to figure out how to get in there,\u201d Mia said, her mind racing with ideas. She twirled a lock of hair around her finger, a habit she had when deep in thought.\n\nTheo adjusted his glasses, a glimmer of determination in his eyes. \u201cIf we can just find the key, or\u2026 maybe there\u2019s a way to unlock it without drawing attention. We don\u2019t have much time!\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from within the backstage room. Mia and Theo exchanged wide-eyed glances. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Mia whispered, gripping Theo's arm. \n\n\u201cYeah! We have to check it out!\u201d Theo replied, adrenaline pumping through him. \n\nThey tiptoed toward the backstage door, which was slightly ajar. The sound of murmuring voices grew louder, and they caught snippets of conversations. \n\n\u201c...if she finds out we were behind it...\u201d \n\n\u201c...the show will be ruined!\u201d \n\nMia's heart raced. Were these voices connected to the missing music box? She motioned for Theo to follow her as they crept closer, peering through the small crack in the door. \n\nInside, Lila, the show\u2019s biggest star, stood with a group of students, her face twisted in distress. \u201cI can\u2019t believe the music box is gone! It was my grandmother\u2019s!\u201d \n\nA tall girl with a dramatic flair replied, \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t have trusted anyone with it, Lila. Now it\u2019s too late!\u201d \n\nMia felt a mix of empathy and anger. She couldn\u2019t let Lila down. They had to solve this mystery, and quickly! \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s sneak in,\u201d Mia whispered to Theo, who nodded in agreement. \n\nJust then, the door creaked loudly as it opened wider. They froze. Ms. Pomeroy popped her head out, her curly hair bouncing with energy. \u201cAh! There you two are! I need your help with the final act!\u201d \n\n\u201cMs. Pomeroy, we can\u2019t right now!\u201d Theo said, glancing anxiously at the group. \n\n\u201cBut I need... wait a minute,\u201d she squinted suspiciously. \u201cWhat are you two doing here?\u201d \n\nMia swallowed hard. \u201cWe\u2019re just\u2026 um, checking on the props!\u201d \n\nMs. Pomeroy raised an eyebrow, clearly not buying their excuse. \u201cYou look like you\u2019re up to something. If I find out you\u2019re hiding something from me\u2026\u201d \n\n\u201cMs. Pomeroy, please! It\u2019s important!\u201d Mia pleaded, her eyes darting back to the group inside. \n\nSuddenly, another loud crash resonated from within the backstage room, causing everyone to jump. \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Lila exclaimed. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go see!\u201d one of the other students shouted, darting toward the source of the noise. \n\n\u201cWait!\u201d Mia and Theo exchanged desperate glances. They had to act quickly. \n\n\u201cMs. Pomeroy, we really have to help. Can you distract them?\u201d Mia asked, her voice rising with urgency. \n\nMs. Pomeroy took a deep breath and nodded. \u201cAlright, I\u2019ll handle this. You two better not get caught!\u201d \n\nWith that, she rushed toward the group, waving her arms and shouting about the importance of stage presence. \n\n\u201cNow\u2019s our chance!\u201d Theo whispered, and they slipped into the backstage room just before the door shut behind Ms. Pomeroy. \n\nInside, the room was dimly lit, filled with disorganized props and costumes. Mia felt a thrill of anticipation mixed with fear. They had to find the music box before anyone noticed they were missing. \n\nSuddenly, Theo pointed to a shadowy corner. \u201cLook!\u201d \n\nMia squinted, heart racing as she edged closer to the darkness. Something glimmered faintly against the wall. \u201cCould it be\u2026?\u201d \n\nJust then, the unmistakable sound of footsteps approached, sending a chill down their spines. They had to hide! \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they ducked behind a tower of costumes, Mia\u2019s heart raced. She hoped they weren\u2019t too late to uncover the truth.\n\n\u201cStay quiet,\u201d Theo whispered, his eyes wide as they waited to see who would enter.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nSuddenly, the door swung open, and in walked a familiar face\u2014Lila, looking frantic and determined. \u201cWhere is it? It has to be here somewhere!\u201d \n\nThe tension in the air thickened, and Mia and Theo exchanged a frustrated glance. They could feel the weight of the mystery closing in around them. Would they find the music box before it was too late?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Mia and Theo overhear that raises their suspicions?","options":["A crash from the backstage room","A song being performed","A teacher calling for them","Students laughing in the hallway"],"correct_answer":"A crash from the backstage room"},{"question":"Who do Mia and Theo ask for help to distract the other students?","options":["Lila","A janitor","Ms. Pomeroy","The principal"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Pomeroy"},{"question":"What is the main setting of this chapter?","options":["A classroom","The school's cafeteria","The backstage area of the auditorium","A park"],"correct_answer":"The backstage area of the auditorium"},{"question":"What emotion does Lila express when she enters the backstage room?","options":["Joy","Frustration","Indifference","Excitement"],"correct_answer":"Frustration"},{"question":"What do Mia and Theo find in the backstage room?","options":["Lila's music box","A secret passage","An old costume","An empty stage"],"correct_answer":"An old costume"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_266_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_266_ch3_img1.png","plot_266_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":749,"reading_level":"Builder"}
