   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_7_10","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The library was dark and cozy, filled with the smell of old books. Oliver, Zoe, and Leo huddled together near a tall shelf. The wind howled outside, and rain pounded on the windows. \n\n\u201cAre we really trapped here?\u201d Oliver asked, his voice shaking. \n\n\u201cWe have to be brave,\u201d Zoe said, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cThis is an adventure!\u201d\n\nJust then, the magical book glowed bright blue. \u201cSolve my riddle to escape!\u201d it chirped. The friends leaned in closer. \n\n\u201cHere\u2019s the riddle,\u201d said the book. \u201cI am not alive, but I can grow. I don\u2019t have lungs, but I need air. What am I?\u201d \n\n\u201cHmm,\u201d Leo scratched his head. \u201cThis is tough!\u201d \n\n\u201cWait! I know!\u201d Zoe exclaimed. \u201cIt\u2019s a fire! Fire needs air to burn, but it\u2019s not alive!\u201d \n\nThe book flickered, and a tiny flame creature popped out. It danced around them, waving its fiery arms. \n\n\u201cGood job! But there\u2019s more to do!\u201d it laughed. \u201cTo pass, you must face the Mischievous Mice!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed through the library. A flock of tiny mice, wearing capes and holding cheese wands, appeared. \n\n\u201cWho dares disturb our reading time?\u201d squeaked the smallest mouse, puffing out its chest. \n\n\u201cWe just want to escape!\u201d Leo shouted, trying not to laugh. \n\n\u201cNot so fast!\u201d the biggest mouse said. \u201cIf you want to pass, you must play our game!\u201d \n\nZoe stepped forward, fists on her hips. \u201cWhat\u2019s the game?\u201d \n\n\u201cCatch us if you can!\u201d squeaked the mice, darting through the shelves. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d shouted Oliver. The friends chased after the mice, laughter filling the library. \n\nThey zigzagged around towering shelves, ducking and dodging. Oliver felt lighter, his shyness melting away. They worked together, cornering the mice behind a stack of books. \n\n\u201cOkay, we give up!\u201d squeaked the smallest mouse. \u201cYou\u2019re fast! You can go!\u201d \n\nThe mice scattered, leaving behind a sparkling trail of cheese. \n\n\u201cYuck!\u201d Leo said, wrinkling his nose. \u201cWhat now?\u201d \n\nThe magical book glowed again. \u201cNow you must find the next riddle!\u201d \n\nExcitement bubbled inside Oliver. \u201cLet\u2019s do this!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What riddle did the magical book give the friends?","options":["What has wings?","What is a fire?","What runs fast?","What is a mouse?"],"correct_answer":"What is a fire?"},{"question":"Who did the friends have to chase in this chapter?","options":["Cats","Dogs","Mice","Bears"],"correct_answer":"Mice"},{"question":"What did Zoe say the answer to the riddle was?","options":["A tree","A fire","A cheese","A book"],"correct_answer":"A fire"},{"question":"How did Oliver feel during the chase?","options":["Scared","Brave","Tired","Sleepy"],"correct_answer":"Brave"},{"question":"What did the mice leave behind after they ran away?","options":["A book","A trail of cheese","A riddle","A toy"],"correct_answer":"A trail of cheese"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch2_img1.png","plot_267_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":351,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
