   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_7_10","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The library felt different now. The rain pounded harder, shaking the tall shelves. Oliver, Zoe, and Leo huddled together, their hearts racing. \u201cWhat do we do next?\u201d asked Oliver, his voice trembling.\n\n\u201cWe have to find another riddle in the book!\u201d Zoe exclaimed, her eyes shining with excitement. \u201cMaybe it will help us escape.\u201d \n\nLeo nodded but added, \u201cAnd no more mice, please!\u201d \n\nThey opened the magical book again. Suddenly, the pages flipped wildly. Then a bright light filled the room! \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nOut from the light stepped a giant figure. It was a friendly giant holding a feather quill. \u201cWelcome, brave kids! I am Grom, the Riddle Giant!\u201d he boomed. \u201cTo leave this library, you must solve my riddle!\u201d\n\n\u201cOkay, we\u2019re ready!\u201d Zoe shouted.\n\nGrom smiled. \u201cListen carefully. I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with wind. What am I?\u201d\n\nOliver scratched his head. \u201cThat sounds tricky!\u201d\n\nLeo jumped up. \u201cI know! It\u2019s an echo!\u201d \n\n\u201cGreat job, Leo!\u201d Zoe cheered. \n\nBut Grom\u2019s smile faded. \u201cYou may have solved my riddle, but a challenge awaits! You must face my Echo Guardians!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, shadows began to swirl around them. The shadows took shape, becoming small, swirling echoes. They giggled and danced, teasing the kids. \n\n\u201cRun!\u201d shouted Oliver. \n\nThey dashed between towering shelves, dodging the playful echoes. \u201cThis way!\u201d Zoe called, leading them towards a hidden door. \n\nAs they ran, Leo tripped and fell. \u201cNo! Come back!\u201d he yelled, reaching for his friends. \n\nZoe turned. \u201cWe can\u2019t leave him!\u201d \n\nOliver felt a surge of bravery. \u201cI\u2019ll help him!\u201d He raced back to grab Leo\u2019s hand.\n\nJust then, the echoes surrounded them, laughing and swirling. \u201cYou can\u2019t leave the library!\u201d one echo shrieked. \n\nThe clock struck ten, its sound echoing through the library. \u201cWe have to escape!\u201d Zoe cried, panic rising in her voice.\n\n\u201cFollow me!\u201d Oliver shouted, his heart pounding. \n\nTogether, they sprinted toward the hidden door, but the echoes closed in fast. Would they reach freedom before it was too late?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Grom ask the kids to solve?","options":["A riddle","A riddle about food","A math problem","A puzzle"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What do the Echo Guardians look like?","options":["Small, swirling echoes","Big, scary monsters","Friendly animals","Tall, shadowy figures"],"correct_answer":"Small, swirling echoes"},{"question":"What does Oliver feel when he decides to help Leo?","options":["Bravery","Fear","Sadness","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Bravery"},{"question":"What happens when the clock strikes ten?","options":["It starts to rain","They find another book","They must escape","They hear a loud noise"],"correct_answer":"They must escape"},{"question":"What does Zoe want to do when Leo falls?","options":["Leave him","Help him","Run away","Play with him"],"correct_answer":"Help him"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch3_img1.png","plot_267_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":347,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
