   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_11_14","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The storm raged outside the ancient library, its towering shelves filled with dusty tomes and secrets waiting to be uncovered. Lightning lit up the sky, illuminating the rain-soaked windows, and each rumble of thunder sent shivers down Oliver's spine. He clutched his favorite book, \u201cThe Adventures of Sir Cedric,\u201d tight against his chest, wishing he could escape into the pages instead of waiting for the storm to pass.\n\n\u201cCome on, Ollie! This is the best time to be in the library!\u201d Zoe exclaimed, her voice bubbling with excitement. She was practically bouncing on her feet, her wild curls bouncing along with her. Zoe had always been the brave one, dragging Oliver along on adventures that usually involved testing the limits of their small town's boundaries.\n\n\u201cYeah, if we survive the storm,\u201d Oliver replied, glancing nervously at the towering shelves around them. He was the kind of kid who liked to blend into the background, not the type to go looking for trouble. \n\n\u201cStop worrying! What\u2019s the worst that could happen?\u201d Leo chimed in, his mischievous grin revealing a hint of trouble. He perched on a nearby table, tossing a paper airplane that sailed through the air like a bird in flight. As the plane landed with a soft thud, a sudden crash echoed through the library, startling all three of them.\n\nThe heavy wooden doors slammed shut with a deafening thud, and the lights flickered ominously. \u201cDid you guys see that?\u201d Zoe gasped, her bravado faltering.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re stuck!\u201d Oliver said, panic rising in his throat. The library was known for its magical atmosphere, but this felt different. The air grew thick with tension, and shadows seemed to dance along the shelves, whispering secrets. \n\n\u201cOkay, okay! We just need to find a way out,\u201d Leo said, a hint of uncertainty creeping into his voice. \u201cLet\u2019s check the back room. Maybe we can find a window or something.\u201d\n\nAs they made their way through the library, each corner revealed more enchantment. A tapestry depicting a dragon and knight shimmered under the dim light, and as Oliver reached out, he could almost hear the faint roar of the beast. Finally, they reached a small room at the back, filled with shelves overflowing with books that looked as though they had been untouched for centuries.\n\n\u201cLook at this!\u201d Zoe shouted, pointing to a book perched on a pedestal in the center of the room. Its cover was adorned with golden lettering that seemed to pulse with light. \u201cIt looks magical!\u201d\n\nOliver felt a pull toward the book, an inexplicable urge to open it. As he approached, the book suddenly sprang open, and a gust of wind swept through the room. The pages fluttered wildly, and from them, a swirling mist began to emerge. \n\n\u201cHurry! Step back!\u201d Leo yelled, his usual bravado replaced with fear. \n\nBut it was too late. The mist enveloped them, and they were no longer in the library. They found themselves in a vibrant forest filled with towering trees and singing birds. \n\n\u201cWait, where are we?\u201d Zoe asked, her eyes wide with wonder. \n\n\u201cBack to the library!\u201d Oliver shouted, but as he turned around, the library was gone, replaced by the enchanted world of stories. \n\nThen, echoing through the trees, a soft voice whispered, \u201cTo escape, you must solve the riddles of the book. Only then will you find your way home\u2026\u201d \n\nOliver's heart raced as he exchanged glances with Zoe and Leo. \u201cWe\u2019re not just trapped in the library. We\u2019ve entered a story,\u201d he breathed, realizing they had to work together to navigate this magical adventure\u2014or risk being stuck forever. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event causes Oliver, Zoe, and Leo to feel trapped in the library?","options":["A power outage","A heavy storm","A magic spell","A book falling off a shelf"],"correct_answer":"A heavy storm"},{"question":"What does Zoe encourage Oliver to do in the library?","options":["Read quietly","Join her on an adventure","Help her with a project","Leave the library"],"correct_answer":"Join her on an adventure"},{"question":"What magical item do the kids discover in the library?","options":["A glowing sword","A treasure map","A magical book","A talking statue"],"correct_answer":"A magical book"},{"question":"How do the characters feel when they are transported into the enchanted world?","options":["Excited and curious","Frightened and confused","Bored and tired","Angry and upset"],"correct_answer":"Excited and curious"},{"question":"What do the characters need to do in order to escape the enchanted world?","options":["Find a hidden treasure","Solve the riddles of the book","Make a new friend","Read more books"],"correct_answer":"Solve the riddles of the book"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch1_img1.png","plot_267_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":610,"reading_level":"Builder"}
