   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_11_14","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The storm outside raged on, its howling winds and relentless rain creating a cacophony that seemed all too eager to invade the ancient library. As Oliver, Zoe, and Leo huddled around the magical book, its pages shimmered with an ethereal glow, illuminating their faces with a soft light. Oliver's heart raced\u2014he had never felt so alive, and yet, so frightened. \u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d he whispered, glancing nervously at the towering shelves that seemed to loom over them like silent giants.  \n\nZoe, her eyes alight with excitement, leaned closer to the book. \u201cWe read! That\u2019s how we\u2019ll figure out how to escape.\u201d Her hands trembled slightly as she turned the pages, revealing vibrant illustrations of characters from tales they knew well: a grinning Cheshire Cat, a fierce dragon, and a brave young girl with a bow and arrow. The book was alive with magic, but it felt ominous too.  \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]  \n\n\u201cWait,\u201d Leo said, a mischievous glint appearing in his eyes. \u201cWhat if we just prank one of these characters? I could distract them while you guys look for clues!\u201d He chuckled at the thought, but the tension in the air was palpable.  \n\n\u201cLeo, this isn\u2019t a game,\u201d Oliver replied, his voice steadying as he spoke up for the first time, a spark of courage igniting within him. \u201cWe need to work together if we want to get out of here.\u201d  \n\nZoe nodded, acknowledging Oliver\u2019s newfound boldness. \u201cLet\u2019s see what the book says about the first challenge.\u201d She turned a page, and a riddle floated off the parchment, swirling around them like a whispering wind:  \n\n*\u201cTo find the key, you must be brave,  \nIn a place where stories crave,  \nSeek the tale of shadows deep,  \nAnd in the dark, your secret keep.\u201d*  \n\nThe words echoed in the vast library, sending shivers down their spines. \u201cShadows deep?\u201d Leo mused, scratching his head. \u201cWhat does that even mean?\u201d  \n\n\u201cI think it could refer to the basement,\u201d Zoe suggested, her adventurous spirit pushing her forward. \u201cI\u2019ve heard stories about it being a dark, scary place full of forgotten books.\u201d  \n\nOliver swallowed hard. \u201cBut what if there\u2019s something dangerous down there?\u201d  \n\n\u201cOr something that can help us!\u201d Zoe countered, her enthusiasm infectious. \u201cWe have to take the risk, guys.\u201d  \n\nStill, doubt lingered in Oliver\u2019s mind. Just then, the lights flickered ominously, and a thunderclap rattled the windowpanes. From the shadows of a nearby bookshelf, a soft giggle echoed, followed by a figure stepping into the dim light\u2014a girl with wild, curling hair and a playful grin, dressed in what looked like a patchwork fairy costume.  \n\n\u201cWelcome to my story!\u201d she chirped, her eyes twinkling with mischief. \u201cI\u2019m Pippa, the keeper of the shadows!\u201d  \n\n\u201cWho are you?\u201d Oliver exclaimed, stepping back, his heart pounding.  \n\n\u201cI\u2019m here to help you, or maybe to keep you. Depends on what you choose!\u201d Pippa sang, twirling around them as if she were dancing to a melody only she could hear. \u201cSolve my riddle, and I\u2019ll guide you. Fail, and the library will become your forever home!\u201d  \n\nZoe stepped forward, her determination shining brighter than the storm outside. \u201cWe accept your challenge, Pippa. Tell us your riddle!\u201d  \n\nWith a mischievous smile, Pippa clapped her hands, and the air thickened with anticipation. The stakes had been raised, and Oliver felt a mix of fear and excitement. Time was running short, and they had to uncover the truth hidden within the library's enchanted walls before the clock struck midnight.  \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]  \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s get started,\u201d Oliver said, feeling the weight of their predicament settle on his shoulders. \u201cWe\u2019ll solve this together.\u201d  \n\nAs he exchanged glances with Zoe and Leo, something shifted in their bond; they were no longer just friends trapped in a library\u2014they were partners on an adventure to reclaim their freedom.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the riddle the characters must solve?","options":["To find the key, you must be brave...","In the dark, your secret keep...","Seek the tale of shadows deep...","All of the above."],"correct_answer":"All of the above."},{"question":"What challenge does Pippa present to the group?","options":["A game of hide and seek","A riddle challenge","A race against time","A scavenger hunt"],"correct_answer":"A riddle challenge"},{"question":"What does Zoe suggest they search for?","options":["The basement","The attic","The main hall","The reading nook"],"correct_answer":"The basement"},{"question":"How does Oliver feel about their situation in the library?","options":["Excited","Fearful","Indifferent","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Fearful"},{"question":"What does the storm outside symbolize for the characters?","options":["Chaos and danger","Adventure and fun","Calm and peace","Friendship and teamwork"],"correct_answer":"Chaos and danger"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch2_img1.png","plot_267_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":647,"reading_level":"Builder"}
