   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_11_14","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As thunder boomed outside like a giant drum, Oliver, Zoe, and Leo huddled together in the grand reading room, the swirling storm casting eerie shadows on the towering shelves. \u201cWhat if we never get out of here?\u201d Oliver whispered, his voice shaking slightly. Zoe placed a reassuring hand on his shoulder. \u201cWe will, Oliver. We just need to solve this next riddle. We\u2019re a team, remember?\u201d \n\nThe enchanted book lay open on a table, its pages fluttering as if alive. A line of sparkling text caught Leo's eye: \u201cTo find the truth, seek the hidden, but beware the trickster\u2019s game.\u201d \u201cWhat does that even mean?\u201d he exclaimed, his usual playful demeanor fading. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe room suddenly felt colder, as if the very air was thick with magic and mystery. \u201cMaybe we should split up?\u201d suggested Leo, though a hint of doubt laced his tone. \u201cNo way!\u201d Zoe said firmly. \u201cWe\u2019re stronger together. Plus, we\u2019re dealing with\u2026 tricksters.\u201d \n\nJust then, the shadows shifted, and from behind the stacks, a character stumbled forward\u2014a peculiar jester with a vibrant outfit and a sly grin. \u201cWell, well! Who dares to challenge me?\u201d he taunted, his voice smooth like honey. \u201cI am the Master of Mischief, and I love a good puzzle!\u201d\n\nOliver\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat do we have to do?\u201d \n\nThe jester twirled, spreading his arms wide. \u201cAnswer my riddle, and I shall let you pass. Fail, and you\u2019ll be trapped in my tale forever!\u201d The ground beneath them trembled, and Oliver felt the weight of the library pressing down on him. \u201cWhat\u2019s the riddle?\u201d he managed to ask.\n\n\u201cListen closely,\u201d the jester said, his eyes glinting. \u201cI speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with the wind. What am I?\u201d \n\nZoe furrowed her brow, her mind racing. \u201cThis sounds familiar\u2026 it\u2019s... it\u2019s an echo!\u201d she shouted, her voice echoing off the ancient walls. The jester\u2019s smile faltered, then he clapped his hands, and the shadows danced wildly around them.\n\n\u201cCorrect! But beware, my friends, for the next challenge lies ahead!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the room spun like a merry-go-round, and the trio found themselves standing at the edge of a vast chasm. A narrow bridge, made of glowing books, spanned the gap. \u201cWe have to cross that?\u201d Leo said, his bravado waning. \n\n\u201cYes, but look!\u201d Zoe pointed at the other side. \u201cThere\u2019s a door! If we can reach it, we might find a way out.\u201d \n\nJust then, the jester\u2019s laughter echoed, wrapping around them like a vine. \u201cNot so fast! The bridge will crumble if you don\u2019t walk in pairs! Only those who trust each other will succeed!\u201d \n\nOliver and Zoe exchanged determined glances, while Leo hesitated. \u201cWhat if I fall?\u201d \n\n\u201cThen we\u2019ll catch you!\u201d Oliver insisted, courage swelling inside him. With a deep breath, they stepped onto the bridge, the books humming beneath their feet. Each step felt wobbly, and with every movement, Oliver felt the weight of their friendship pulling them back. \n\n\u201cStay together!\u201d Zoe urged, her heart racing. Just as they reached the center, a loud crack sounded beneath them, and the bridge shuddered violently. \n\n\u201cLeo!\u201d Oliver shouted, reaching out as Leo stumbled. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith a desperate leap, Oliver grabbed Leo\u2019s arm just in time. \u201cI got you!\u201d he exclaimed, but the bridge trembled ominously. \n\n\u201cHold on tight!\u201d Zoe yelled, her eyes wide with fear. \n\nAs they hung on, the clock began to toll ominously in the distance\u2014each chime echoing the urgency of their plight. They had to escape, and fast. But would the next challenge be even more dangerous than the last?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What challenge do the kids face in this chapter?","options":["Crossing a narrow bridge","Solving a math problem","Finding a hidden door","Learning a new spell"],"correct_answer":"Crossing a narrow bridge"},{"question":"Who is the character that tests the kids with a riddle?","options":["Pippa","The Master of Mischief","Oliver","Leo"],"correct_answer":"The Master of Mischief"},{"question":"What is the answer to the riddle posed by the jester?","options":["A shadow","An echo","A ghost","A whisper"],"correct_answer":"An echo"},{"question":"What happens to the bridge when the kids reach the center?","options":["It crumbles","It glows brighter","It expands","It opens a secret passage"],"correct_answer":"It crumbles"},{"question":"What is Oliver's reaction when Leo stumbles on the bridge?","options":["He runs away","He grabs Leo's arm","He laughs","He gives up"],"correct_answer":"He grabs Leo's arm"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch3_img1.png","plot_267_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":619,"reading_level":"Builder"}
