   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_11_14","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the echoes of thunder rolled through the library, Oliver, Zoe, and Leo huddled together near the towering shelves lined with ancient tomes. The air was thick with the scent of old paper and the crackling energy of magic. \u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d Leo asked, glancing nervously at the gleaming cover of the enchanted book that had brought them this crazy adventure.\n\n\u201cWe need to figure out the next riddle,\u201d Zoe said, her voice steady despite the chaos outside. \u201cRemember what Pippa said? Every story has a lesson, and we have to find ours.\u201d She picked up the book, flipping through the pages, each filled with swirling illustrations and shimmering words.\n\nSuddenly, the lights flickered, and a page turned by itself. The words glowed brightly, transforming into an ornate riddle:\n\n*To escape the grasp of tales untold,  \nFind the key where courage is bold.  \nSeek the knight who slayed the dragon,  \nBut first prove your worth; let bravery be your beacon.*\n\nOliver\u2019s heart raced. \u201cA knight? A dragon? We must be in a fairy tale!\u201d He took a deep breath, feeling the weight of the situation. \u201cWe can do this together. We just have to be brave.\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find this knight!\u201d Zoe exclaimed, her adventurous spirit igniting. Leo nodded, his usual mischief replaced by determination. \u201cRight, but no more pranks, okay? We need to stick together.\u201d \n\nAs they ventured deeper into the library, the sound of the storm faded, and the atmosphere shifted to a magical stillness. They passed shelves filled with books whispering secrets, their spines shimmering in hues of green and gold. In the center of a dimly lit aisle stood a life-sized statue of a knight in shining armor, brandishing a sword. The knight\u2019s eyes sparkled with a knowing glimmer.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cIs this him?\u201d Zoe pointed, her eyes wide. \u201cBut how do we prove our worth?\u201d\n\nJust then, the knight\u2019s voice boomed, startling them. \u201cBravery is not the absence of fear, but the strength to face it. Answer me this: What is more powerful than the mightiest sword?\u201d \n\nThe trio exchanged glances, their minds racing. \u201cFriendship!\u201d Oliver blurted out, his voice ringing with newfound strength.\n\n\u201cFriendship?\u201d the knight echoed, raising an eyebrow. \u201cElaborate, young one.\u201d\n\nLeo stepped forward. \u201cWhen we work together, we can face anything! That\u2019s what we\u2019ve been doing since we got trapped here.\u201d \n\nThe knight nodded, a smile forming beneath his helmet. \u201cIndeed. A bond forged in trust and loyalty is the truest strength.\u201d With a flourish, he lifted his sword, revealing a glowing key beneath it.\n\n\u201cTake this, and may it guide you to the next step of your journey!\u201d he declared. \n\nThe key was warm in Oliver\u2019s hand, filled with a comforting energy. \u201cWe did it! We\u2019re getting closer!\u201d Zoe cheered, her eyes sparkling with hope. \n\nHowever, just as hope settled in their hearts, the library trembled, and shadows danced across the pages. A gust of wind swept through, and out from behind the shelves emerged a mischievous figure, laughing as he twirled a feathered quill. \u201cOh, you think it\u2019ll be that easy?\u201d he taunted, his grin wide. \u201cWhy would I let you escape?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe\u2019ve faced tougher challenges!\u201d Oliver shouted, clutching the key tightly. \u201cWe\u2019re not giving up!\u201d \n\nThe figure\u2019s laughter echoed around them. \u201cLet\u2019s see if that courage lasts!\u201d \n\nWith a mix of excitement and trepidation, the trio prepared for whatever lay ahead, knowing they could rely on each other.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Zoe rallied, determination shining in her eyes. They stepped forward, ready to confront the next twist in their enchanted adventure, their hearts beating in sync.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What riddle do Oliver, Zoe, and Leo need to solve?","options":["To find a dragon's treasure","To escape the grasp of untold tales","To discover the library's secret","To summon a magical creature"],"correct_answer":"To escape the grasp of untold tales"},{"question":"What does the knight say is more powerful than a sword?","options":["Friendship","Magic","Knowledge","Bravery"],"correct_answer":"Friendship"},{"question":"What does Oliver feel in his hand when he receives the key?","options":["Coldness","Warmth","Fear","Sadness"],"correct_answer":"Warmth"},{"question":"What does Zoe suggest they need to do after solving the knight's riddle?","options":["Find more riddles","Go to the next challenge","Make more friends","Leave the library"],"correct_answer":"Go to the next challenge"},{"question":"Who threatens the group at the end of this chapter?","options":["The Knight","Pippa","The Master of Mischief","A mischievous figure"],"correct_answer":"A mischievous figure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch4_img1.png","plot_267_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":614,"reading_level":"Builder"}
