   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_11_14","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the storm raged outside, Oliver, Zoe, and Leo huddled in the ancient library, their hearts racing with both fear and excitement. The flickering candlelight cast dancing shadows on the towering shelves filled with books, each one whispering tales of adventure. They had narrowly escaped the clutches of the Master of Mischief, but now they faced yet another riddle from a new character.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s not just stories anymore; it\u2019s our lives at stake,\u201d Zoe said, gripping the magical book tightly. \u201cWe need to solve this riddle together.\u201d\n\nOliver nodded, his mind racing. \u201cWhat if\u2026 what if we read it aloud? Maybe it will give us clues.\u201d \n\nAs he opened the book, the pages turned by themselves, stopping at a bright illustration of a wise old owl with spectacles perched on its beak. Below it, the riddle read: \u201cI can fly without wings, I can cry without eyes. Whenever I go, darkness flies. What am I?\u201d\n\n\u201cCan we think of anything?\u201d Leo scratched his head, a frown on his face. \u201cI mean, it\u2019s not like we\u2019re dealing with normal riddles here.\u201d\n\nZoe\u2019s eyes lit up. \u201cA cloud! It can float and it makes rain! But darkness flies\u2026 that\u2019s the sun!\u201d\n\nOliver\u2019s face broke into a smile. \u201cYou\u2019re right! It\u2019s the sun!\u201d \n\nBefore they could celebrate, the library shook as a swoosh filled the air. A burst of light erupted from the book, and before them stood the owl, its feathers shimmering like gold.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe owl adjusted its glasses, looking over the three kids with a mix of curiosity and amusement. \u201cAh, the brave adventurers! You have answered correctly. But beware, for once you leave this riddle, the Master\u2019s mischief will not be far behind!\u201d\n\n\u201cWait!\u201d Leo shouted, stepping forward. \u201cWhat do we need to do to escape?\u201d\n\n\u201cTo leave the library, you must face the shadows of your fears,\u201d the owl hooted cryptically, its eyes sparkling with wisdom. \u201cOnly then will you find the key.\u201d\n\nSilence fell over the trio, the weight of the owl\u2019s words sinking in. Oliver exchanged glances with Zoe and Leo, each of them feeling a wave of determination wash over them.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s confront our fears together,\u201d Zoe said, her voice steady. \u201cWe can do it!\u201d\n\nLeo nodded. \u201cYeah! If we stick together, nothing can stop us!\u201d\n\nWith newfound courage, they turned back towards the book, but the library suddenly darkened. Shadows began to twist and writhe around them like vines. The Master of Mischief\u2019s laughter echoed, teasing them.\n\n\u201cWelcome back! Are you ready for a little game?\u201d \n\n\u201cWhatever it is, we\u2019re ready!\u201d Oliver declared, heart pounding but resolute.\n\nThe shadows advanced, each one taking the shape of a character from a story. Zoe stepped forward, her hands clenched. \u201cWe\u2019ll face you! We won\u2019t let you keep us here!\u201d\n\nWith a flash, they were transported into a vivid scene filled with swirling colors and challenges that would test their resolve. Each character they encountered\u2014brave knights, cunning foxes, and fierce dragons\u2014threw riddles and challenges their way. \n\nAs they worked through the trials, Oliver felt a spark of bravery he never knew he had. Zoe\u2019s adventurous spirit shone brighter with each challenge, and Leo realized his pranks could be used to outsmart the tricky characters.\n\nFinally, the last challenge approached. The Master of Mischief himself emerged from the shadows, a sly grin on his face. \u201cWill you finally admit defeat?\u201d\n\n\u201cNo!\u201d the trio shouted in unison, standing shoulder to shoulder.\n\nIn that moment, Oliver felt a surge of confidence. \u201cWe are stronger together! Let\u2019s show him what we\u2019ve learned!\u201d\n\nWith a final burst of collective strength, they confronted the Master, solving his final riddle and breaking the curse. As the clock struck midnight, the library doors swung open, and the storm outside began to calm.\n\nBreathless and exhilarated, the kids stepped outside, their hearts lighter than ever. They had not only escaped but had also discovered what true friendship and courage meant.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What riddle does the owl give to Oliver, Zoe, and Leo?","options":["I can fly without wings, I can cry without eyes.","I can dance without feet, I can sing without a voice.","I can grow without roots, I can shine without light.","I can run without legs, I can hide without a home."],"correct_answer":"I can fly without wings, I can cry without eyes."},{"question":"What must the kids face to escape the library?","options":["Their fears","Their parents","The storm outside","Their favorite books"],"correct_answer":"Their fears"},{"question":"How do Oliver, Zoe, and Leo feel at the beginning of this chapter?","options":["Excited and brave","Scared and determined","Bored and tired","Happy and careless"],"correct_answer":"Scared and determined"},{"question":"What does Leo realize about his pranks during their challenges?","options":["They can be silly","They can be used to outsmart characters","They aren't helpful","They make situations worse"],"correct_answer":"They can be used to outsmart characters"},{"question":"What happens when the clock strikes midnight?","options":["The library disappears","The Master of Mischief wins","The doors open and the storm calms","They find another riddle"],"correct_answer":"The doors open and the storm calms"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch5_img1.png","plot_267_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":676,"reading_level":"Builder"}
