   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_15_18","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The wind howled like a restless spirit as it whipped through the trees lining the streets of Eldergrove. Dark clouds loomed overhead, casting an ominous shadow over the town and its most cherished building\u2014the Eldergrove Library. With its towering shelves and ancient tomes, the library had always held an air of mystery, but today, it radiated an unsettling energy. Oliver, a quiet bookworm with tousled brown hair and thick glasses, stood outside the massive oak doors, hesitating.\n\n\"Come on, Ollie! Don\u2019t tell me you\u2019re scared of a little rain!\" Zoe called out, her voice bright and teasing. She was the embodiment of adventure, with wild curls and an eager grin that could light up even the gloomiest of days. \n\n\"I\u2019m not scared,\" Oliver replied, though he felt his heart racing. \"It\u2019s just\u2026 what if the storm makes it worse? The lightning could\u2014\"\n\n\"Please,\" Leo chimed in, rolling his eyes, \"It\u2019s just a storm. Besides, I\u2019m pretty sure we won't get electrocuted just because we\u2019re inside a library.\"\n\nLeo was the class clown, always armed with a joke or a prank to lighten the mood. His mischievous grin gave Oliver a strange sense of comfort, but today, an unease settled in the pit of his stomach. The trio often sought refuge in the library, but as they pushed through the heavy doors, an inexplicable chill enveloped them.\n\nThe interior was just as they remembered: towering shelves that stretched toward the vaulted ceiling, dimly lit corners, and the familiar scent of old paper mixed with polished wood. A flickering chandelier hung above them, casting dancing shadows across the marble floor. But something was different today. As the first crack of thunder rumbled outside, the heavy oak doors slammed shut behind them with a deafening bang.\n\n\"Okay, that's not normal,\" Zoe said, her voice tinged with excitement and fear. \n\nBefore Oliver could respond, the lights flickered, plunging them into momentary darkness. When they returned, the library felt more alive than ever. The shelves seemed to whisper secrets, and the air hummed with anticipation. \n\n\"Maybe we should just wait it out,\" Oliver suggested, trying to keep his voice steady. \n\n\"Where\u2019s the fun in that?\" Leo shot back, a glint of mischief in his eyes. \"Let\u2019s explore! There might be something amazing hidden here.\"\n\nWith Zoe leading the way, they moved deeper into the labyrinth of books. Each room was more enchanting than the last\u2014one filled with maps that shifted and changed as they approached, another where the characters from the stories seemed to peek from the pages, watching them curiously.\n\nSuddenly, an ancient book fell from a nearby shelf, landing with a soft thud at Oliver\u2019s feet. It was bound in worn leather, adorned with intricate gold lettering that glimmered even in the dim light. \"The Book of Enchantments,\" Zoe read aloud, her eyes sparkling with intrigue.\n\n\u201cLet me see that,\" Leo said, reaching for it. As he opened the book, the pages fluttered wildly as though a gust of wind had caught them. The words shimmered, then rippled like water. Suddenly, a bright light burst forth, and for a moment, the library faded away, swallowed by a swirl of colors.\n\nThey stood frozen as a tall, cloaked figure emerged from the glow, his eyes glinting mischievously. \u201cWelcome, guests of the enchanted library,\u201d he intoned, his voice echoing around them. \u201cYou have activated the book\u2019s magic. Solve its riddles, conquer its challenges, and you may escape before the clock strikes midnight. Fail, and you shall remain part of the stories forever.\u201d\n\nOliver\u2019s heart sank. This was no ordinary adventure. They were trapped in a world where tales came alive, where their wit and bravery would be tested against whimsical characters who would do anything to keep them there. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s not panic,\u201d Zoe said, though her voice trembled slightly. \u201cWe can figure this out together.\u201d\n\n\u201cTogether,\u201d Leo echoed, tossing Oliver a grin that didn\u2019t quite reach his eyes. \n\nWith the clock ticking ominously in the background, the trio exchanged determined glances. This was going to be the greatest adventure of their lives\u2014or their last. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they prepared to face the unknown, the library seemed to pulse with energy, and a sense of camaraderie began to weave between them, binding them together against the challenges ahead. \n\nWith a shudder, the clock struck six, and the air thickened with tension. The enchantment had begun, and the first riddle awaited them.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Zoe urged, her adventurous spirit igniting a spark of courage in Oliver\u2019s heart as they stepped deeper into the mystery of the enchanted library.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event causes Oliver, Zoe, and Leo to become trapped in the library?","options":["A sudden storm","The library doors slamming shut","A magical spell","A prank gone wrong"],"correct_answer":"The library doors slamming shut"},{"question":"What is the title of the magical book they discover?","options":["The Book of Enchantments","The Chronicles of Eldergrove","Tales of the Unknown","Riddles of the Past"],"correct_answer":"The Book of Enchantments"},{"question":"What must the trio do to escape the library?","options":["Fight the characters","Solve riddles and challenges","Find the exit","Make a deal with the librarian"],"correct_answer":"Solve riddles and challenges"},{"question":"Which character is described as the adventurous one?","options":["Oliver","Zoe","Leo","The cloaked figure"],"correct_answer":"Zoe"},{"question":"What is the main atmosphere of the library described as?","options":["Welcoming and bright","Ominous and mysterious","Chaotic and noisy","Boring and dull"],"correct_answer":"Ominous and mysterious"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch1_img1.png","plot_267_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":782,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
