   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_15_18","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Chapter 3: The Riddle of Shadows\n\nThe flickering lanterns cast dancing shadows across the library\u2019s carved wooden walls, the storm outside howling like a pack of wolves. Oliver stood frozen, his heart drumming against his ribs. Beside him, Zoe was scanning the room with an intensity that suggested she was already considering their next move. Leo, however, was pacing, a grin plastered on his face despite the palpable tension in the air.\n\n\u201cOkay, okay,\u201d Leo said, hands raised as if to calm an imaginary crowd. \u201cWe just need to figure out what this book wants from us. More riddles, right? How hard could it be?\u201d\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s not just about riddles,\u201d Oliver interjected, his voice barely above a whisper. \u201cWhat if each riddle comes with consequences? We need to be careful.\u201d \n\nZoe nodded solemnly, her eyes lingering on the magical book that lay open on a nearby table, its pages fluttering as if beckoning them closer. \u201cThe first riddle was misleading. We need to think deeper this time.\u201d\n\nAs if in response, the book shimmered, the words glowing faintly. Oliver moved forward, drawn in by the pulsing light. \u201cWhat does it say?\u201d\n\n\u201cListen closely,\u201d Zoe replied, leaning in. \u201cIt\u2019s not just words; it\u2019s a puzzle.\u201d \n\nThe riddle materialized before them, weaving itself from the pages in ethereal script:\n\n**\u201cIn shadows, I dwell, but bring light when I speak,  \nSolve my riddle, or face the fate you seek.  \nWhat am I?\u201d**\n\n\u201cWhat could that possibly mean?\u201d Leo ran a hand through his hair, frustration boiling beneath his usual bravado. \u201cA shadow? A whisper?\u201d \n\n\u201cOr maybe\u2026 a secret?\u201d Oliver suggested, though his voice trembled. Secrets had a way of turning the mundane into something monstrous. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe library\u2019s atmosphere was charged with an electric tension, the lanterns casting warm glows on the trio\u2019s faces while the shadows seemed to stretch and twist around them. Zoe\u2019s brow furrowed, illuminating her determination, while Leo\u2019s expression shifted from playful to serious as he contemplated the riddle\u2019s implications. \n\n\u201cC\u2019mon, guys!\u201d Leo finally exclaimed, breaking the heavy silence. \u201cThink! What do we know about secrets?\u201d\n\n\u201cThey can trap you,\u201d Zoe said, her voice low. \u201cJust like we\u2019re trapped here.\u201d \n\nOliver swallowed hard, the weight of her words anchoring him in a place of fear. \u201cAnd maybe this shadow wants to keep us here forever.\u201d\n\nA low rumble echoed through the library as thunder cracked like a whip, punctuating their dread. Suddenly, the ground trembled beneath their feet. The shadows swelled, swirling around them with a life of their own, as if the library itself were alive and reacting to their fears.\n\nWithout warning, a figure emerged from the darkness\u2014a tall, ominous shadow with no discernible features. \u201cYou seek the answer?\u201d it boomed, the voice echoing off the walls like a warning. \u201cBut every answer comes with a price.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat do you want?\u201d Zoe shouted defiantly, her courage surging. \n\n\u201cYour fears,\u201d it replied. \u201cFace them, and you may yet escape.\u201d\n\nOliver\u2019s heart raced as his worst fear spiraled through his mind: being forever alone, lost in stories with no one to share them. \u201cWe can\u2019t give you our fears!\u201d he yelled, desperation clawing at his throat.\n\nThe shadow laughed, a chilling sound that chilled the air around them. \u201cThen you shall remain here\u2014lost in your own tales.\u201d\n\n\u201cWait! The riddle!\u201d Zoe\u2019s voice broke through the chaos; she was suddenly focused. \u201cWhat if the answer is to face our fears? What if we\u2014\u201d\n\nBut before she could finish, the shadow lunged toward Oliver, its tendrils of darkness reaching for him like grasping hands. \n\n\u201cOliver!\u201d Zoe screamed, lunging forward. \n\nTime seemed to stretch as Oliver felt the cold tendrils wrap around his ankle, pulling him toward the darkness. Panic surged through him, but in that moment of despair, he remembered the courage he had drawn from the stories he loved. \u201cI\u2019m not afraid!\u201d he shouted, summoning every ounce of bravery he had. \n\nAs the shadow recoiled, he grasped at the air, determined not to let it claim him. \u201cWe\u2019re in this together!\u201d he called to Zoe and Leo. \n\nThe words strengthened their resolve. Leo rushed forward, grabbing Oliver\u2019s arm. \u201cDon\u2019t let go!\u201d he shouted, his earlier bravado replaced by a fierce determination. \n\nBut the shadow was relentless, and the library began to tremble, the lights flickering dangerously. \u201cChoose your fears, or be consumed!\u201d it roared.\n\nThe decision loomed before them, heavy as the storm outside. Oliver\u2019s mind raced, battling his fear and the shadow that threatened to swallow them whole. \n\n\u201cTogether,\u201d Zoe breathed, stepping closer to Oliver and Leo. \u201cWe face what we fear.\u201d\n\nAs the clock began to strike, echoing ominously through the library, they exchanged glances filled with unspoken understanding. They had to make a choice... but what would it cost them?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe shadows thickened, and the riddle loomed larger than life, the library\u2019s fate hanging in the balance as they steeled themselves for the confrontation ahead.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the riddle presented to the characters?","options":["In shadows, I dwell, but bring light when I speak.","What you seek is hidden beneath the floor.","The answer lies in the pages of the book.","I am the key to your darkest fears."],"correct_answer":"In shadows, I dwell, but bring light when I speak."},{"question":"What does the shadow demand from the group?","options":["To leave the library","Their fears","The magical book","Their friendship"],"correct_answer":"Their fears"},{"question":"What does Oliver fear the most?","options":["Being trapped in stories","Being alone","Failing his friends","The dark"],"correct_answer":"Being alone"},{"question":"How does Zoe suggest they confront the shadow?","options":["By running away","By facing their fears","By solving the riddle","By using magic"],"correct_answer":"By facing their fears"},{"question":"What happens as the clock begins to strike?","options":["The library lights up","The shadow grows stronger","They find the exit","They receive a warning"],"correct_answer":"The shadow grows stronger"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch3_img1.png","plot_267_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":842,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
