   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_267_15_18","title":"The Enchanted Library Lockdown","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The rain continued to hammer against the stone walls of the Eldergrove Library, a rhythmic symphony that barely masked the anxious whispers of Oliver, Zoe, and Leo. Cloaked in shadows and the scent of ancient parchment, they gathered around the magical book that had drawn their fates together. Each page they turned felt like a step deeper into a labyrinth filled with dangers and discoveries.\n\n\"Okay, I think we should focus,\" Oliver said, his voice barely rising above the storm's howl. He pushed his glasses up his nose, a habit he had developed whenever he was nervous. \u201cThe next riddle says: \u2018To find the door that leads to light, you must first confront the night.\u2019 What do you think it means?\u201d\n\nZoe, her fiery spirit igniting the dim room, leaned forward, her eyes sparkling with determination. \"It could mean we have to face something dark\u2014a character we haven't met yet. Maybe one of those shadows? But what does \u2018the door that leads to light\u2019 mean?\"\n\nLeo, lounging against a shelf lined with dusty tomes, rolled his eyes. \"Or what if it\u2019s just a metaphor for us being scared of the dark? Like, \u2018overcome your fears\u2019 kind of thing?\"\n\nOliver frowned, feeling the weight of the riddle sink into his thoughts. \"I don't think it\u2019s that simple. What if it\u2019s actually suggesting we need to enter a dark place to find the light? There might be a hidden room or something.\"\n\nWith that, the trio set off, navigating the labyrinthine aisles of towering bookshelves. The air was thick with the dust of countless unread stories, and the dim glow of their lantern flickered, casting elongated shadows that danced along the shelves. Suddenly, a soft giggle echoed through the library. They halted, exchanging wary glances.\n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Zoe asked, her bravado fading. \n\nOliver nodded, heart pounding. \u201cYeah, but I don\u2019t see anyone.\u201d\n\nBefore they could ponder further, a figure emerged from behind a shelf, a girl their age dressed in a flowing gown adorned with pages of different stories. She looked ethereal, her hair shimmering like silver threads. \u201cWelcome to my realm,\u201d she said with a mischievous grin. \u201cI am Lorelei, the Keeper of Tales. You\u2019ve come seeking the light, haven\u2019t you?\u201d\n\nThe trio exchanged glances, uncertain but intrigued. \u201cWe\u2019re trying to escape,\u201d Zoe explained. \u201cThe riddle mentioned confronting the night, and we think it leads to\u2026 you?\u201d\n\nLorelei chuckled, a sound sweet like ringing bells. \u201cIndeed, I embody the night. To find the light, you must play a game\u2014a trial of wits. If you succeed, I will show you the path. But beware, should you fail\u2026\u201d Her voice trailed off ominously.\n\nOliver cleared his throat, stepping forward. \u201cWhat kind of trial?\u201d\n\n\u201cAh, a simple test. Answer my riddle, and the door will reveal itself. Fail, and you shall remain here as a tale I tell. Are you ready?\u201d Her eyes sparkled with a mix of challenge and mischief.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s hear it,\u201d Leo said, his usual bravado returning.\n\nLorelei leaned closer, her voice a whisper. \u201cI speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with the wind. What am I?\u201d\n\nThe room fell silent, the only sound the distant rumble of thunder. The answer danced just out of reach in Oliver's mind. He could feel the pressure of the moment, the weight of expectation from his friends.\n\n\u201cAn echo!\u201d Zoe exclaimed suddenly, her eyes wide with realization. \n\n\"Correct!\" Lorelei clapped, and the atmosphere shifted. The air shimmered, revealing a door hidden behind the shelves, glowing softly. \u201cYou\u2019ve proven your worth. Proceed, brave souls.\u201d\n\nAs they stepped toward the illuminated door, an ominous shadow slithered between them. It was the same shadow that had taunted them before, a swirling mass of darkness. \u201cNot so fast,\u201d it hissed, its voice like rusted metal. \u201cYou think you can escape that easily?\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWith their hearts racing, the trio faced the shadow together. \u201cWe\u2019re not afraid of you,\u201d Oliver declared, finding strength in the unity of their voices. \u201cWe\u2019ve faced our fears, and we won\u2019t let you trap us.\u201d\n\nThe shadow recoiled, its form flickering. Zoe raised her lantern, illuminating the darkness. \u201cYou want to keep us here, but we\u2019ve found our courage!\u201d\n\nAs their words washed over the shadow, it began to dissolve, the darkness breaking apart like fragile glass. The room brightened, revealing the glowing door behind them once more.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cRun!\u201d Zoe shouted, her spirit emboldened, as they dashed toward the door, hearts pounding in unison. With one last glance at the dissipating shadow, they burst through the entrance, the storm outside now a distant murmur.\n\nThey emerged into a sunlit glade, the library behind them fading away. Breathless, Oliver turned to his friends. \u201cWe did it. We really did it. We faced our fears and escaped.\u201d\n\nZoe smiled, her face radiant with triumph. \u201cAnd we did it together. That\u2019s what matters most.\u201d\n\nAs the sun dipped low, casting golden hues across the sky, they shared a moment of exhilaration and relief, knowing they had grown in ways they had never imagined.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who is Lorelei in the story?","options":["A villain trying to trap the kids","The Keeper of Tales","A character from a book","An illusion of the library"],"correct_answer":"The Keeper of Tales"},{"question":"What does the riddle given by Lorelei ask?","options":["What is the meaning of life?","What speaks without a mouth?","What is the secret of the library?","What is your greatest fear?"],"correct_answer":"What speaks without a mouth?"},{"question":"How do Oliver, Zoe, and Leo manage to face the shadow?","options":["By escaping through a door","By confronting their fears together","By using magic spells","By running away"],"correct_answer":"By confronting their fears together"},{"question":"What does Zoe do to fight the shadow?","options":["She runs away.","She holds a lantern.","She uses a magic spell.","She distracts it."],"correct_answer":"She holds a lantern."},{"question":"What lesson do the characters learn in this chapter?","options":["That running away is the best option","That fear should be avoided","That teamwork and facing fears leads to strength","That magic can solve everything"],"correct_answer":"That teamwork and facing fears leads to strength"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_267_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_267_ch5_img1.png","plot_267_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":867,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
