   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_268_7_10","title":"Secrets of the Clock Tower","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Sam, Jenna, and Max stood at the base of the clock tower. The tower was tall and dark, with a wooden door that looked ancient. \u201cIt must be at least a hundred years old!\u201d Jenna exclaimed, her eyes wide with wonder. \n\n\u201cWe have to find a way inside,\u201d Sam said, clenching his fists. \u201cThe festival is almost here!\u201d\n\nMax pulled out a small gadget. \u201cI can try to hack the lock, but we need to be quick. The caretaker doesn\u2019t like strangers.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, they heard a creaking sound. The caretaker, Mr. Gloom, peeked out from behind a bush. His gray hair was wild, and his glasses hung low on his nose. \u201cWhat are you kids doing here?\u201d he barked.\n\n\u201cWe were just admiring the clock!\u201d Jenna said, her voice shaking a little. \n\n\u201cAdmiring, huh? You better hurry along now,\u201d Mr. Gloom warned. \u201cSecrets should stay hidden!\u201d\n\nThe friends exchanged worried glances. They had to act fast. \u201cLet\u2019s go around the back,\u201d Sam whispered. They darted behind the tower, where the stone was cool beneath their hands.\n\nAs they reached the back, they found a small window. It was dusty and cracked. \u201cIf we can just get that open\u2026\u201d Max said, pulling out his gadget again. \u201cI can boost the signal.\u201d\n\nJust then, they heard footsteps. \u201cQuick!\u201d Sam said. \u201cWe need to hide!\u201d\n\nThey squeezed behind a pile of old crates. The footsteps grew louder. Sam held his breath. Max's eyes darted nervously. \n\n\u201cDo you think he saw us?\u201d Jenna whispered.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Sam replied, trying to stay calm. Just as they thought it was safe, a shadow loomed over the crates.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe kids peeked out to see Mr. Gloom, frowning at the window. \u201cI know you\u2019re out there!\u201d he shouted. \u201cGo home before I call your parents!\u201d\n\nThe friends froze. Their hearts raced. \u201cIf we don\u2019t act now, we won\u2019t make it to the festival!\u201d Sam declared. \n\nWith a determined nod, Max pressed a button on his gadget. Suddenly, there was a beep, and the window creaked open. \u201cGot it!\u201d he cheered softly. \n\nSam smiled and said, \u201cLet\u2019s climb in before he catches us!\u201d They scrambled through the window, ready to uncover the secrets of the clock tower. \n\nBut what they found inside was even more surprising than they expected\u2026\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Sam, Jenna, and Max want to do at the clock tower?","options":["Climb to the top","Take photos","Find a way inside","Play hide and seek"],"correct_answer":"Find a way inside"},{"question":"What does Mr. Gloom tell the kids?","options":["To leave","To stay and help","To play a game","To climb the tower"],"correct_answer":"To leave"},{"question":"How did Max plan to open the window?","options":["With his hands","By climbing up","By using a gadget","With a key"],"correct_answer":"By using a gadget"},{"question":"Why did the friends hide behind the crates?","options":["To play","To eat lunch","To avoid Mr. Gloom","To find treasure"],"correct_answer":"To avoid Mr. Gloom"},{"question":"What did the friends find when they entered the clock tower?","options":["Nothing important","Surprising secrets","A treasure chest","Their parents"],"correct_answer":"Surprising secrets"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_268_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_268_ch2_img1.png","plot_268_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":392,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
