   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_268_15_18","title":"Secrets of the Clock Tower","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The air in the clock tower was thick with the scent of dust and aged wood, the golden light of late afternoon filtering through the small, jagged windows. Sam stood at the foot of the spiral staircase, his heart pounding with the weight of their mission. \u201cThis is it,\u201d he said, glancing back at Jenna and Max. \u201cIf we can get to that room, we might just save the festival.\u201d \n\nJenna brushed a stray lock of hair behind her ear, her eyes wide with excitement and anxiety. \u201cBut what if Hargrove catches us? He\u2019s already warned us twice.\u201d \n\nMax, his fingers tapping nervously against his smartphone, shrugged. \u201cWe can\u2019t let fear win. Besides, I\u2019m working on a way to bypass any alarms he might have set up. We have to try.\u201d \n\nWith a determined nod, Sam stepped onto the first step, the creaking wood echoing around them like a whispered warning. Each step felt heavier than the last, as though the tower itself was testing their resolve. \n\nAt the top of the staircase, they reached a massive wooden door, reinforced with rusty iron bands. Sam\u2019s breath caught in his throat. \u201cThis is it. The locked room.\u201d \n\nJenna traced her fingers over the intricate carvings on the door, her mind racing with possibilities. \u201cIf we can just figure out how to open it\u2026\u201d \n\nBefore she could finish, Max\u2019s phone buzzed. \u201cHold on, I think I can get us in.\u201d His fingers flew over the screen, but the tension was palpable, thickening the air like smoke. \n\nSuddenly, the door swung open with a loud creak. The room beyond was dimly lit, a long table cluttered with blueprints and old mechanical pieces. Shadows danced across the walls, and the eerie tick-tock of the clock echoed from somewhere deep within the tower. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]  \nThe scene depicts the massive wooden door to the locked room, flanked by shadows. The intricate carvings on the door hint at the clock tower\u2019s age and secrets. Sam, Jenna, and Max stand at the threshold, their expressions a mix of awe and trepidation.\n\nAs they entered, the door slammed shut behind them with a thunderous bang, plunging them into darkness. Max fumbled for the flashlight app on his phone, illuminating the dusty surfaces and age-old machinery. Jenna\u2019s eyes lit up as she recognized one of the blueprints. \u201cThis is it! This shows how the clock works!\u201d \n\nBut Sam felt a chill crawl down his spine. \u201cLook at this place. It feels\u2026 alive.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the sound of footsteps echoed outside the door they had just entered. Panic surged through Sam. \u201cSomeone\u2019s coming! What do we do?\u201d \n\nMax\u2019s face paled. \u201cWe can\u2019t get caught. Not now!\u201d \n\nAs the footsteps grew louder, Jenna\u2019s gaze darted around the room, landing on an open window, the darkening sky beckoning them. \u201cWe might be able to escape out there!\u201d \n\nBut Sam hesitated. \u201cWe need to find what we came for first. We can\u2019t leave empty-handed.\u201d \n\nJust then, a shadow fell across the doorway, illuminated by the flickering light of a lantern. It was Mr. Hargrove, his face a mask of anger and determination. \u201cWhat are you doing in here?\u201d he thundered. \n\nMax instinctively stepped in front of Jenna and Sam, his voice trembling. \u201cWe\u2019re just trying to understand the clock better!\u201d \n\nHargrove\u2019s eyes narrowed, filled with suspicion. \u201cUnderstand? Or meddle in matters that do not concern you?\u201d \n\nBefore Sam could respond, Hargrove took a step forward, his lantern casting an ominous glow over the ancient machinery. \u201cYou have no idea what you\u2019re dealing with.\u201d \n\nJust as Hargrove reached for them, Sam\u2019s heart raced. He felt a surge of defiance. \u201cNo! We must know the truth! We can\u2019t let the clock stay silent when the festival depends on it!\u201d \n\nHargrove paused, his expression flickering between anger and something softer, almost regretful. \u201cThe truth? It carries a heavy burden.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the lantern flickered and went out, plunging them into darkness. Sam felt his resolve harden. They had to find a way to restart the clock and confront whatever secrets lay hidden in the tower. Time was running out, and the festival\u2014and perhaps their town's future\u2014depended on them. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d he shouted, and they bolted deeper into the room, the shadows closing in behind them.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]  \nThe image captures the intense moment as Mr. Hargrove confronts the trio in the dimly lit room filled with ancient machinery. Hargrove stands illuminated by a flickering lantern, his expression a mix of anger and regret, while Sam, Jenna, and Max look determined and fearful, highlighting the tension and stakes of the encounter.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What key action do the friends take in this chapter?","options":["They confront Mr. Hargrove.","They leave the clock tower.","They start the clock.","They find a treasure."],"correct_answer":"They confront Mr. Hargrove."},{"question":"What is Max trying to do with his phone?","options":["Call for help.","Bypass alarms.","Take a picture.","Track Hargrove."],"correct_answer":"Bypass alarms."},{"question":"How does Mr. Hargrove react when he finds the friends in the locked room?","options":["He helps them.","He is angry.","He is pleased.","He is confused."],"correct_answer":"He is angry."},{"question":"What does Sam feel as they enter the locked room?","options":["Excitement.","Fear.","Nervousness.","Defiance."],"correct_answer":"Defiance."},{"question":"What does Jenna recognize in the room?","options":["A hidden treasure.","The blueprints for the clock.","A secret passage.","An old diary."],"correct_answer":"The blueprints for the clock."}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_268_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_268_ch3_img1.png","plot_268_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":782,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
