   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_268_15_18","title":"Secrets of the Clock Tower","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As dawn broke over Eldridge, the first rays of sunlight filtered through the dusty windows of the clock tower\u2019s attic, illuminating the vast array of gears and blueprints scattered across the room. Sam stood at the center, his heart racing as he scanned the intricate mechanisms. \u201cThis is incredible,\u201d he breathed, running a finger along a rusted gear. \u201cIt\u2019s like something out of a steampunk novel.\u201d\n\nJenna, her eyes alight with curiosity, pulled a few sheets closer. \u201cLook at this!\u201d she exclaimed, revealing a faded blueprint of the clock tower. \u201cIt shows a hidden compartment right next to the main clockwork. If we can find it, maybe it will help us restart the clock.\u201d\n\nMax leaned back against the wall, arms crossed, his brow furrowed. \u201cBut how do we get Mr. Hargrove to let us access it? He\u2019s already made it clear he wants us out of here.\u201d\n\nThe thought of the old caretaker sent a shiver down Sam's spine. Mr. Hargrove had guarded the tower and its secrets like a dragon hoarding treasure. \u201cI think he\u2019s hiding something. Maybe the history of this place is more complicated than we realize. We need to dig deeper,\u201d Sam replied, a determined glint in his eyes.\n\nJenna nodded thoughtfully, her enthusiasm palpable. \u201cIf we can find out why the clock stopped, it might give us leverage to confront him. And we need to hurry; the festival is just days away.\u201d\n\nAs they strategized, the sunlight created shadows that danced across the walls, casting an air of mystery around them. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s head to the library,\u201d Max suggested, a plan already forming in his mind. \u201cThere should be archives or records about the clock tower\u2019s history. Maybe it will explain why Hargrove is so protective.\u201d\n\nThe trio made their way down the narrow staircase, their minds buzzing with possibilities. Jenna led the way, her heart racing with both excitement and anxiety. What if they uncovered something that could change everything?\n\nAt the town library, the familiar smell of old books enveloped them as they entered. Jenna darted to the history section, her fingers brushing against the spines of books. \u201cHere! This one should have information on the town\u2019s founding,\u201d she said, pulling out a volume thick with dust.\n\nThey settled at a table, flipping through pages filled with faded photographs and stories of Eldridge\u2019s past. Hours slipped away unnoticed until Max suddenly stopped, his finger resting on an image of the clock tower from the late 1800s. \u201cWait, look at this!\u201d\n\nJenna leaned in, her eyes widening. \u201cThis picture shows a gathering at the base of the clock tower. That can\u2019t be Hargrove, can it?\u201d She pointed to a young man who bore a striking resemblance to the caretaker, his expression both proud and solemn.\n\n\u201cCould it be his ancestor?\u201d Sam mused, intrigued. \u201cWhat if the clock\u2019s malfunction has to do with some family secret?\u201d\n\nJust then, the library door creaked open, and in walked Mr. Hargrove, his gaze landing on the three of them. \u201cWhat are you children doing here?\u201d he barked, stepping closer.\n\nSam\u2019s heart pounded. \u201cWe were just\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cWe were researching,\u201d Jenna interjected, her voice steady despite the fear rising in her chest. \u201cAbout the clock tower. We think it might be connected to your family.\u201d\n\nHargrove's demeanor shifted, the stern mask cracking just slightly. \u201cMy family\u2019s history is not for you to explore,\u201d he warned, but there was a flicker of uncertainty in his eyes.\n\nMax took a deep breath, clearly weighing his words. \u201cBut if we don\u2019t find out why the clock stopped, the festival will be ruined. Don\u2019t you care about the town?\u201d\n\nFor a moment, silence hung in the air like a thick fog. Hargrove's shoulders slumped as he looked at the three friends, and Sam sensed a glimmer of hope. \u201cFine,\u201d he said, his voice softer. \u201cMeet me here tomorrow. I\u2019ll show you something\u2014but only if you promise to keep it a secret.\u201d\n\nAs Hargrove turned to leave, Sam, Jenna, and Max exchanged hopeful glances, the weight of their predicament lightening just a little. They had made a breakthrough, and the stakes were rising higher than ever. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] \n\n\u201cDid that just happen?\u201d Jenna whispered, her eyes sparkling with excitement.\n\n\u201cTomorrow, we\u2019ll uncover the real secret of the clock tower,\u201d Sam replied, feeling a wave of determination wash over him. They were getting closer, and with each step, the mysteries began to unravel.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam, Jenna, and Max discover in the clock tower's locked room?","options":["A hidden treasure","Ancient gears and blueprints","A ghost","A diary"],"correct_answer":"Ancient gears and blueprints"},{"question":"What is the main conflict in Chapter 4?","options":["Finding a way to restart the clock","Confronting Mr. Hargrove","Preparing for the festival","Researching town history"],"correct_answer":"Finding a way to restart the clock"},{"question":"What motivates Mr. Hargrove to cooperate with the friends?","options":["His love for history","A personal connection to the clock tower","Fear of losing his job","The town's pressure"],"correct_answer":"A personal connection to the clock tower"},{"question":"What do Sam and his friends plan to do next?","options":["Leave town","Continue their research","Confront Mr. Hargrove again","Attend the festival"],"correct_answer":"Continue their research"},{"question":"What is the significance of the images they find in the library?","options":["They reveal the clock's location","They show a family connection to Hargrove","They are unrelated","They depict the festival"],"correct_answer":"They show a family connection to Hargrove"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_268_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_268_ch4_img1.png","plot_268_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":756,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
