   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_269_7_10","title":"The Case of the Cranky Cat","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the lights dimmed at the Paws and Claws Pet Shop, Lucy and Benny stood near the mysterious locked room. It was filled with colorful toys and happy animals. But today, it was missing one very cranky cat\u2014Mr. Whiskers!\n\n\u201cWhere could he be?\u201d Lucy wondered aloud. \u201cHe was just here a moment ago!\u201d\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, Lucy,\u201d replied Benny, scratching his head. \u201cBut we have to find him before the event ends!\u201d\n\nLucy nodded. \u201cLet\u2019s check the locked room!\u201d She tugged at the shiny bell they had found earlier. \u201cMaybe this will help us get in.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud meow from behind the door. \u201cMr. Whiskers?\u201d Lucy shouted. \u201cAre you in there?\u201d\n\nThe meowing sounded louder, but the door stayed shut. \u201cIt\u2019s locked tight!\u201d Benny exclaimed. \u201cWhat do we do?\u201d\n\nLucy thought hard. \u201cWe need to find a clue! Maybe someone saw something.\u201d\n\nJust then, a little girl named Mia approached them. \u201cI saw Mr. Whiskers before he vanished! He was chasing a toy mouse!\u201d \n\n\u201cA toy mouse?\u201d Lucy\u2019s eyes sparkled with excitement. \u201cWhere did you see it?\u201d\n\n\u201cOver there!\u201d Mia pointed to a colorful pile of toys. \u201cBut be careful! There\u2019s a lot of noise!\u201d\n\nLucy and Benny rushed to the pile. \u201cWe have to dig through these toys!\u201d said Lucy. They began to search, tossing stuffed animals aside.\n\nBenny picked up a bright yellow toy mouse. \u201cLook! Is this the one?\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe!\u201d Lucy exclaimed, holding it up. Just then, a loud CRASH echoed through the shop. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nThey turned to see a shelf of dog treats topple over! Treats scattered everywhere! \u201cOh no! We have to clean this up!\u201d cried Benny.\n\nSuddenly, a big, fluffy dog trotted over, wagging its tail. \u201cWoof! Woof!\u201d It barked. Lucy laughed. \u201cI think he wants to help!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find Mr. Whiskers first,\u201d said Benny, trying to focus. They quickly grabbed the toy mouse and headed back to the locked door. \n\n\u201cMr. Whiskers, we\u2019re coming!\u201d Lucy shouted, waving the toy. But to their surprise, the door creaked open just a little. \u201cIt\u2019s not locked!\u201d Lucy said wide-eyed. \n\nThe door swung open, revealing a dark room. They took a deep breath. \u201cReady?\u201d Benny whispered. \n\n\u201cReady!\u201d Lucy replied, stepping inside. The room was full of shadows, but they could hear a soft purring coming from the corner. \n\n\u201cMr. Whiskers?\u201d Lucy called softly. \n\nAs they moved closer, the shadows shifted. Suddenly, a fluffy tail flicked out from behind a box. \n\n\u201cIs that him?\u201d Benny gasped. \n\n\u201cYes! But why is he hiding?\u201d Lucy wondered, inching forward. \n\nThey had to find out, and time was running out!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia say she saw Mr. Whiskers chasing?","options":["A toy mouse","A dog","A cat","A bird"],"correct_answer":"A toy mouse"},{"question":"What happened when Lucy and Benny searched through the toys?","options":["They found Mr. Whiskers","A shelf of treats fell","They found a dog","They got locked in"],"correct_answer":"A shelf of treats fell"},{"question":"What did Lucy use to try to unlock the door?","options":["A key","A shiny bell","A toy","A rope"],"correct_answer":"A shiny bell"},{"question":"How did Benny react when they found the door was not locked?","options":["He was scared","He was excited","He was sad","He was confused"],"correct_answer":"He was excited"},{"question":"What did Lucy and Benny hear when they entered the dark room?","options":["Laughter","Meowing","Barking","Screaming"],"correct_answer":"Meowing"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_269_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_269_ch2_img1.png","plot_269_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":441,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
