   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_269_7_10","title":"The Case of the Cranky Cat","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Lucy and Benny stood inside the locked room, their hearts racing. The tall figure they had encountered was just Mrs. Paws, the pet shop owner. Her glasses sparkled as she bent down to look at them. \u201cYou two scared me! I thought I was alone!\u201d\n\n\u201cSorry, Mrs. Paws,\u201d Lucy said, taking a deep breath. \u201cWe heard Mr. Whiskers purring in here. We need to find him!\u201d \n\n\u201cOh dear!\u201d Mrs. Paws exclaimed. \u201cThat cranky cat has gone missing again! I saw him just before the lights dimmed.\u201d\n\n\u201cBut where could he be?\u201d Benny asked, scratching his head. The room was filled with colorful toys and bags of cat food. It was cozy, but it held secrets.\n\nLucy walked over to the tangled pile of yarn they had found earlier. \u201cMaybe this yarn is a clue,\u201d she said, pulling at the strings. \u201cWhat if Mr. Whiskers got stuck?\u201d\n\n\u201cOr playing!\u201d Benny added with a grin. He loved imagining Mr. Whiskers being silly. As they moved closer to the yarn, Lucy spotted something shiny underneath it. \n\n\u201cLook, Benny! A collar!\u201d She picked it up carefully. \u201cIt has a name tag.\u201d \n\nBenny leaned in closer. \u201cWhat does it say?\u201d\n\n\u201cMr. Paws!\u201d Lucy said, reading the tag. \u201cBut that\u2019s not Mr. Whiskers\u2019s collar! What does this mean?\u201d \n\n\u201cI think we should ask Mrs. Paws!\u201d Benny suggested excitedly.\n\n\u201cGood idea!\u201d Lucy nodded. \u201cMrs. Paws!\u201d \n\n\u201cYes, dears?\u201d Mrs. Paws turned around, her face curious.\n\n\u201cDo you know this collar? It\u2019s not Mr. Whiskers\u2019s,\u201d Lucy said, holding it up high. \n\nMrs. Paws\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cOh my! That belongs to Mr. Paws! He\u2019s been missing for days!\u201d \n\n\u201cSo Mr. Paws is here too?\u201d Benny asked, his eyes bright with hope. \n\nMrs. Paws scratched her chin. \u201cYes, but I thought he was somewhere else. I just can\u2019t find him!\u201d\n\nLucy felt a spark of excitement. \u201cLet\u2019s look for him together!\u201d \n\nThey searched every corner of the room. Just then, Lucy noticed a slight movement behind a shelf. \u201cBenny! Over there!\u201d \n\nThey rushed to the shelf and peeked behind it. Suddenly, a fluffy tail flicked out! \n\n\u201cThat\u2019s Mr. Whiskers!\u201d Lucy said, her voice full of joy. \n\nBut the cranky cat wasn\u2019t ready to be found. He hissed and darted through the room, knocking over a box of treats!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cOops! Sorry, Mr. Whiskers!\u201d Benny laughed, trying to catch the runaway cat.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s work together,\u201d Lucy said, smiling. \u201cWe can make him feel safe!\u201d \n\nWith gentle voices and tasty treats, they spread the snacks around. Slowly, Mr. Whiskers sniffed the air. \n\n\u201cCome on, Mr. Whiskers! You can do it!\u201d Lucy cheered. \n\nBenny clapped his hands in delight. \u201cHe\u2019s coming closer!\u201d \n\nWill they be able to catch the cranky cat before time runs out?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who did Lucy and Benny find in the locked room?","options":["Mr. Whiskers","Mr. Paws","Mrs. Paws","A dog"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Whiskers"},{"question":"What did Lucy find under the tangled yarn?","options":["A toy","A collar","A treat","A dog bone"],"correct_answer":"A collar"},{"question":"What did Mr. Whiskers do when he was found?","options":["He came out calmly","He hissed and ran","He purred loudly","He fell asleep"],"correct_answer":"He hissed and ran"},{"question":"Who is Mrs. Paws?","options":["The pet shop owner","A cat","Benny\u2019s mom","A customer"],"correct_answer":"The pet shop owner"},{"question":"What did Lucy and Benny use to coax Mr. Whiskers out?","options":["Voices and treats","A toy","A leash","A cage"],"correct_answer":"Voices and treats"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_269_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_269_ch4_img1.png","plot_269_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":466,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
