   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_269_11_14","title":"The Case of the Cranky Cat","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Lucy and Benny stood inside the dimly lit locked room, the air thick with tension. Dust motes floated lazily in the slivers of light that broke through the cracks in the walls. \u201cWe can\u2019t just sit here,\u201d Lucy exclaimed, her dark curls bouncing with urgency. \u201cWe need to find Mr. Whiskers before the guests start panicking even more.\u201d\n\nBenny nodded, his brow furrowed as he scanned the room. \u201cBut where do we even begin?\u201d He kicked at a crumpled toy mouse on the floor, the plastic squeaking in protest. It was a strange noise in the otherwise silent room. \n\nJust then, a low growl echoed from a corner. Lucy\u2019s heart raced. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d she whispered. Benny nodded, wide-eyed. They crept toward the sound, inching closer to a pile of colorful blankets. \u201cMr. Whiskers?\u201d Lucy called softly, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\nSuddenly, a small, frightened tomcat darted out from the blankets, wide-eyed and fluffy. \u201cNot Mr. Whiskers,\u201d Lucy sighed in disappointment. But the tomcat looked at them with an expression that seemed to say, \u201cHelp me!\u201d \n\n\u201cHey there, little fella,\u201d Benny knelt down, extending his hand cautiously. \u201cWhat\u2019s got you all worked up?\u201d The cat hissed, but Benny\u2019s gentle demeanor calmed it slightly. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see if he leads us somewhere,\u201d Lucy suggested, and as if on cue, the tomcat turned and dashed toward a stack of boxes. They hurried after him, excitement bubbling in Lucy\u2019s chest. \n\nThey followed the green-eyed cat through a narrow opening between the boxes until they found themselves in a hidden nook. \u201cWhoa, look at this!\u201d Benny exclaimed, pointing to a faded poster on the wall. It was a picture of Mr. Whiskers with a big trophy and a list of past charity winners. \n\n\u201cDo you see that?\u201d Lucy tapped on the trophy's name: \u201cBest Feline Friend.\u201d She squinted. \u201cWhat if the trophy is a clue? Maybe it means something about where Mr. Whiskers likes to hide or play?\u201d \n\nBenny\u2019s eyes sparkled with enthusiasm. \u201cThat makes sense! But what could it mean?\u201d \n\nBefore Lucy could answer, the tomcat pawed at a loose floorboard, drawing their attention. \u201cWhat do you think is under there?\u201d she asked, her curiosity piqued. \n\nBenny bent down to lift the board just as a loud scraping sound resonated from outside the room. Both of them froze. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Lucy whispered, her heart pounding in her chest.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we have to check it out,\u201d Benny replied, glancing back at the hidden nook. \u201cShould we take the tomcat with us?\u201d\n\nLucy nodded. \u201cLet\u2019s go, little guy! We might need your help.\u201d \n\nAs they ventured out, the tomcat trotted along behind them, his little tail twitching like a flag. Just outside the door, they spotted a small group of worried guests peering inside, their faces a mix of confusion and concern. \n\n\u201cThere you are!\u201d one of the guests exclaimed. \u201cWhat were you two doing in there?\u201d \n\nLucy took a deep breath. \u201cTrying to find Mr. Whiskers. But we think we\u2019re onto something!\u201d Her eyes sparkled with determination. \u201cWe just need to follow a few more clues.\u201d\n\nBenny gave her a thumbs-up, and the small crowd seemed to lean in closer, curiosity igniting their interest. The room was alive with the hum of possibility. \n\nThough the mystery was far from solved, Lucy felt a flicker of hope. They were getting closer, and together with Benny, they would unravel the truth about the cranky cat.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Lucy and Benny initially find when they enter the locked room?","options":["A trophy","A frightened tomcat","Mr. Whiskers","A treasure map"],"correct_answer":"A frightened tomcat"},{"question":"What does Lucy suggest about the trophy they find?","options":["It has no significance","It might lead them to Mr. Whiskers","It's a prize for Benny","It's broken"],"correct_answer":"It might lead them to Mr. Whiskers"},{"question":"How does Benny react to the frightened tomcat?","options":["He runs away","He is indifferent","He comforts it","He scolds it"],"correct_answer":"He comforts it"},{"question":"What do Lucy and Benny plan to do next?","options":["Leave the pet shop","Gather more clues","Take a break","Ignore the guests"],"correct_answer":"Gather more clues"},{"question":"What feeling do Lucy and Benny share as they uncover clues?","options":["Fear","Frustration","Hope","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Hope"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_269_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_269_ch4_img1.png","plot_269_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":589,"reading_level":"Builder"}
