   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_270_11_14","title":"The Adventure of the Secret Room","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting elongated shadows across the sprawling grounds of Windmere Mansion, Emma and Jake huddled around the campfire, their faces illuminated by flickering flames. The air was thick with the smell of roasted marshmallows, and the crackle of the fire was the only sound interrupting the eerie silence of the old estate.\n\n\"Can you believe we're actually camping in a mansion?\" Jake said, his blue eyes sparkling with excitement. He was only twelve, but his imagination was as wild as the forest surrounding them. \"What if we find a ghost? Or treasure?\"\n\nEmma rolled her eyes, though a smile tugged at her lips. \"You always think there\u2019s treasure. It's probably just an old house filled with dust. Besides, do you really think ghosts are real?\"\n\n\"Absolutely!\" Jake exclaimed, leaning closer, his voice dropping to a conspiratorial whisper. \"What if the previous owner left clues to find something amazing? Like a secret room!\"\n\nA soft giggle escaped Emma's lips. \"You and your wild ideas. But\u2014\" She paused, her expression turning serious as she gazed into the darkened windows of the mansion. \"I did hear something earlier, like a whispering sound coming from inside.\"\n\nHer words hung in the air, and the camp leader, Mr. Gibbons, who had been listening nearby, stepped forward. \"The Windmere Mansion has a reputation for being a little\u2026 peculiar,\" he said, his eyes twinkling with mischief. \"They say it has hidden rooms and forgotten treasures. But beware \u2014 some say the former owner set traps to keep people out. Or worse.\"\n\nJake's eyes widened. \"See, Emma? We have to explore! We can't just sit here!\"\n\nBefore Emma could respond, Mr. Gibbons clapped his hands. \"Alright, adventurers! Let's gather around for tonight's story. But afterwards, who's up for a scavenger hunt? Maybe we\u2019ll find something extraordinary!\"\n\nAs Mr. Gibbons began spinning tales of ghostly figures and hidden passages, Emma felt a mix of excitement and apprehension. She loved her imaginative brother, but she often found herself in the role of the responsible older sister, and his wild schemes made her uneasy.\n\nThe night deepened, and when the tales of the mansion faded into whispers, Emma turned to Jake. \"Let\u2019s check out that old library after everyone goes to bed. It might have something useful.\"\n\nJake's face lit up. \"Really? You mean it?\"\n\n\"Sure. Just promise me we stick together. No running off, okay?\"\n\n\"Deal!\" Jake said, bouncing on his toes. But as the fire dwindled to embers, and the campers drifted to sleep, Emma felt a shiver run down her spine. What if they did find something? What if it was dangerous?\n\nHours later, when the moon cast a silvery glow over the mansion, Emma gently shook Jake awake. \"Time to go,\" she whispered, her heart racing with both fear and excitement.\n\nThey crept through the halls, the mansion\u2019s silence wrapping around them like a thick blanket. Each creak of the old floorboards sent a jolt through Emma, making her wonder if they were truly alone. Just as they reached the library door, a faint whisper echoed from the walls. Emma halted, her breath hitching in her throat.\n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d she whispered.\n\nJake nodded, his eyes wide with wonder. \"It\u2019s right here! The secret could be behind this door!\"\n\nAs he reached for the handle, a chill swept through the room, and the door creaked open slightly, revealing a dark space beyond. Emma exchanged a nervous glance with Jake. \u201cWhat if there are traps?\u201d\n\nHe grinned, his adventurous spirit shining through. \u201cThen we\u2019ll be careful!\u201d\n\nWith that, they pushed the door wider, revealing a glimpse of dusty shelves and cobwebs, and the musty scent of forgotten stories wafted through. But just as they stepped inside, a hidden mechanism clicked behind the wall, and Emma felt her heart race. \n\n\"Let's find out what secrets this room holds,\" she said, stepping cautiously into the unknown.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What are Emma and Jake doing at Windmere Mansion?","options":["Visiting friends","Camping","Exploring a cave","Attending a festival"],"correct_answer":"Camping"},{"question":"What does Jake believe they might find in the mansion?","options":["A ghost","A treasure","A monster","A time machine"],"correct_answer":"A treasure"},{"question":"Who is their camp leader?","options":["Mr. Gibbons","Mr. Smith","Ms. Jones","Mr. Brown"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Gibbons"},{"question":"What makes Emma feel uneasy about exploring the mansion?","options":["The dark rooms","The story of traps","Jake's excitement","The cold weather"],"correct_answer":"The story of traps"},{"question":"What do Emma and Jake hear that intrigues them?","options":["The sound of footsteps","Whispers","A door creaking","Laughter"],"correct_answer":"Whispers"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_270_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_270_ch1_img1.png","plot_270_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":662,"reading_level":"Builder"}
