   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_270_11_14","title":"The Adventure of the Secret Room","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Locked Room","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the sun began to disappear behind the trees, casting long shadows across the mansion grounds, Emma and Jake huddled near the old wooden chest they had discovered in the cellar. They had spent the last hour poring over the photographs and the dusty journal, deciphering the faded handwriting that held secrets of their family's past. \n\n\u201cLook at this one,\u201d Emma said, pointing to a photograph of a young girl standing next to a large oak tree. Her face was familiar, and Emma felt a spark of recognition. \u201cIsn't that Grandma when she was a child?\u201d \n\nJake peered closer, squinting his eyes. \u201cIt looks like her! But why is she standing near that creepy old tree?\u201d He shivered, remembering the stories Mr. Gibbons had told them about the haunted oak that stood in the yard. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s a clue,\u201d Emma suggested, her fingers tracing the edge of the photo. \u201cWe need to find out more about this tree.\u201d \n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed through the cellar, sending a wave of adrenaline through both siblings. They exchanged nervous glances, their hearts racing. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Jake whispered, glancing toward the dark doorway that led back into the mansion. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s a ghost?\u201d \n\n\u201cStop it!\u201d Emma said, rolling her eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s probably just something falling upstairs. Let\u2019s check it out.\u201d \n\nWith tentative steps, they made their way toward the staircase. The air felt thick with tension, and every creak of the old wood sounded ominous. As they reached the bottom of the stairs, another sound filled the air, a soft, whispering echo\u2014like a voice calling from the walls. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Jake gasped, his eyes wide. \n\n\u201cYes! It\u2019s coming from the library,\u201d Emma replied, her curiosity igniting despite her fear. \u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d \n\nThey raced back through the darkened cellar and into the library, where a faint glow illuminated the room. There, in front of the hidden door, stood Mr. Gibbons. His eyes sparkled with mischief, and he held a lantern that flickered like a candle in the breeze.\n\n\u201cI thought you two could use some help,\u201d he said, a grin spreading across his face. \u201cWhat have you discovered?\u201d \n\n\u201cWe found pictures and a journal! But there are whispers in the walls and a locked door,\u201d Emma exclaimed, trying to catch her breath. \n\nMr. Gibbons nodded, intrigued. \u201cAh, the mysteries of Windmere Mansion never cease. You must learn how to listen,\u201d he said, leaning closer. \u201cSometimes, the past speaks louder than words.\u201d\n\nWith renewed determination, Emma and Jake shared their discoveries with Mr. Gibbons, piecing together the clues about their family\u2019s history. The journal spoke of adventures and hidden treasures, but it also warned of traps set by the mansion\u2019s previous owner to protect the secrets within.\n\n\u201cTraps?\u201d Jake exclaimed, his eyes growing wider. \n\n\u201cYes,\u201d Mr. Gibbons replied, \u201cbut if you work together, you might just unlock the secrets of the room.\u201d \n\nFeeling the weight of their task, Emma and Jake exchanged glances. They had fought and bickered, but now they understood that they needed each other to solve this mystery. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s do it,\u201d Emma said, determination shining in her eyes. \u201cTogether.\u201d \n\nWith that, they turned back to the hidden door, ready to face whatever lay beyond, united in their purpose.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they placed their hands on the door, the whispers grew louder, swirling around them like a soft breeze. The air crackled with anticipation. \u201cAre you ready?\u201d Emma asked, her heart pounding. \n\n\u201cAlways!\u201d Jake grinned, excitement bubbling in his voice. \n\nWith a deep breath, they pushed the door open, and the mysteries of the room awaited them.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Emma and Jake find in the old chest?","options":["Toys","Photographs and a journal","A treasure map","An old game"],"correct_answer":"Photographs and a journal"},{"question":"What do the siblings hear coming from the walls?","options":["A song","Whispers","Laughter","Creaking sounds"],"correct_answer":"Whispers"},{"question":"Who helps Emma and Jake understand the mysteries of the mansion?","options":["Their parents","Mr. Gibbons","A ghost","Their friends"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Gibbons"},{"question":"What lesson do Emma and Jake learn in this chapter?","options":["To compete against each other","The importance of teamwork","How to avoid traps","To explore alone"],"correct_answer":"The importance of teamwork"},{"question":"What do Emma and Jake decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Open the hidden door","Leave the mansion","Go home","Play a game"],"correct_answer":"Open the hidden door"}]},"images":null,"word_count":613,"reading_level":"Builder"}
