   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_261_11_14","title":"The Vanishing Act","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun hung low in the sky, casting a warm golden glow over the bustling town of Maplewood. Today was the annual Magic Festival, and the streets were alive with laughter, music, and the scents of candy apples and popcorn. Mia\u2019s heart raced with excitement as she and her best friend, Zoe, wove through the colorful tents adorned with shimmering streamers and twinkling lights.\n\n\u201cLook at that!\u201d Zoe exclaimed, pointing to a magician performing card tricks near a giant spinning wheel. \u201cCan you believe how amazing this all is?\u201d\n\nMia nodded, her eyes sparkling. \u201cI can\u2019t wait to see the grand illusionist later. They say he can make things disappear!\u201d\n\nZoe grinned, her adventurous spirit shining through. \u201cMaybe we can find some magic of our own today!\u201d\n\nJust then, Mia spotted her neighbor, Mr. Finch, adjusting his top hat as he emerged from his quirky antique shop. With his wild white hair and mismatched clothes, he looked like he had stepped right out of a storybook. \u201cMia! Zoe! Come here, I have something special to show you!\u201d\n\nThe girls rushed over, curiosity bubbling within them. Mr. Finch beckoned them to follow him into his shop, where the air was thick with the scent of old books and mystery. He led them to a dusty old trunk in the corner. \u201cThis belonged to my mentor, a master magician. There are secrets inside\u2014secrets I never fully understood.\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s eyes widened as Mr. Finch opened the trunk, revealing a collection of odd trinkets: a silver wand, a deck of worn cards, and a shimmering scarf that glimmered in the dim light. \u201cEach item holds a story,\u201d he said, his voice low and serious. \u201cAnd perhaps\u2026 a clue.\u201d\n\nBefore Mia could ask what he meant, Zoe\u2019s eyes darted to the window. \u201cHey, where did that girl go?\u201d she asked, squinting outside. Mia turned to look, but the street was now a blur of laughter and colorful costumes.\n\n\u201cWhich girl?\u201d Mr. Finch asked, his brow furrowing.\n\n\u201cThe one in the blue dress,\u201d Zoe replied, her tone suddenly urgent. \u201cShe was right outside just a moment ago.\u201d\n\nMia felt a chill creep up her spine. \u201cMaybe we should check it out,\u201d she suggested, glancing back at Mr. Finch.\n\n\u201cJust be careful, girls. Magic can be unpredictable,\u201d he warned, a hint of worry in his voice.\n\nAs they stepped back outside, Mia noticed something unusual\u2014a glimmering trail of sparkles leading down the street. \u201cLook!\u201d she exclaimed. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s a sign!\u201d\n\nWith excitement coursing through her veins, they followed the shimmering path, weaving through festival-goers. But as they rounded the corner, Mia\u2019s heart sank. Zoe was gone.\n\n\u201cZoe?\u201d Mia called, panic rising in her chest. She felt as though the world around her had frozen. The laughter and music faded, leaving only the sound of her own heartbeat.\n\nJust then, a gust of wind blew, and Mia spotted something glinting on the ground\u2014a playing card with a familiar symbol on it. She picked it up, her hands trembling. It was the Ace of Spades, and scrawled across it in her best friend\u2019s handwriting were the words: \u201cFind me where magic whispers.\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s determination flared. She had to solve the riddle, but time was slipping away. \u201cI won\u2019t leave you behind, Zoe,\u201d she whispered, gripping the card tightly. \n\n\u201cMr. Finch!\u201d she called, turning back towards the shop, her mind racing. \u201cI need your help!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMia and Zoe in the vibrant atmosphere of the festival, surrounded by colorful tents and performers, with laughter and light filling the scene.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia's expression of panic as she realizes Zoe has vanished, the glimmering card in her hand, with the bustling festival now a blur in the background.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event is taking place in Maplewood?","options":["A music festival","A food fair","A magic festival","A sports competition"],"correct_answer":"A magic festival"},{"question":"Who is Mia's best friend?","options":["Mr. Finch","The magician","Zoe","The girl in the blue dress"],"correct_answer":"Zoe"},{"question":"What does Zoe see that makes her alert?","options":["A strange animal","A girl in a blue dress","A magician","A candy stall"],"correct_answer":"A girl in a blue dress"},{"question":"What clue does Mia find after Zoe disappears?","options":["A note","A scarf","A playing card","A wand"],"correct_answer":"A playing card"},{"question":"What does Mr. Finch warn Mia and Zoe about?","options":["To avoid the food stalls","That magic can be unpredictable","To leave the festival early","Not to speak to strangers"],"correct_answer":"That magic can be unpredictable"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_261_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_261_ch1_img1.png","plot_261_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":630,"reading_level":"Builder"}
