   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_262_7_10","title":"The Secret of Pine Hollow","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Oliver stood at the edge of Pine Hollow woods. The trees were tall and ancient. Sunlight filtered through the leaves, making the ground shimmer. Clara, his adventurous sister, had run off to explore the woods. \u201cBe back for lunch!\u201d their mom had called after her.\n\n\u201cWhere do you think she went?\u201d Oliver asked, glancing at his friends, Lily and Jake.\n\n\u201cI bet she found a secret cave!\u201d Jake said, eyes wide with excitement. \n\n\u201cOr a treasure!\u201d Lily added, jumping up and down. \n\nOliver felt a little nervous. Clara was always daring. But today, she hadn\u2019t come back. \n\n\u201cWe should look for her!\u201d Oliver said, clenching his fists. \u201cShe\u2019s probably fine, but what if she needs help?\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Jake shouted, swinging his backpack over his shoulder. \n\nThe three friends stepped into the woods. It felt cooler under the trees. The path was narrow and twisted. Oliver felt a shiver run down his spine. \n\nSuddenly, they heard a rustling noise. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Lily whispered, her eyes wide.\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s a bear!\u201d Jake said, pretending to be scared. \n\nOliver rolled his eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s probably just a squirrel. Or maybe even Clara!\u201d \n\nThey continued walking, listening closely. The woods were full of sounds\u2014birds chirping, leaves rustling, and something that sounded like laughter. \n\n\u201cDo you think we\u2019re getting close?\u201d Lily asked, looking around. \n\n\u201cI hope so!\u201d Oliver replied. \n\nJust then, they spotted something shiny on the ground. Oliver ran to it. \n\n\u201cIt looks like Clara\u2019s bracelet!\u201d he shouted, picking it up. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cWhat if this is a clue?\u201d Jake said, his eyes shining with interest. \n\n\u201cMaybe she went this way!\u201d Lily exclaimed, pointing down a narrow path covered in flowers. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s follow it!\u201d Oliver said, feeling braver. \n\nThey raced down the path, excitement bubbling in their chests. But the deeper they went, the more strange things appeared. \n\n\u201cDid you see that?\u201d Jake asked, stopping suddenly. \n\n\u201cWhat?\u201d Oliver replied, looking back. \n\n\u201cI thought I saw something move behind that tree!\u201d \n\nThe three friends looked at each other, unsure. They could hear whispers in the wind. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep going,\u201d Oliver urged. \u201cWe can\u2019t give up on Clara!\u201d \n\nThey stepped carefully, deeper into the heart of Pine Hollow. Each step held a new mystery.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith every twist and turn, Oliver felt a mix of fear and excitement. What secrets did Pine Hollow hold? \n\n\u201cClara, where are you?\u201d he called out softly, hoping she would hear him.\n\nThe thrill of the adventure pulsed through him. They had to find Clara before it was too late.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Clara do before she went missing?","options":["She went to school","She went to explore the woods","She played video games","She took a nap"],"correct_answer":"She went to explore the woods"},{"question":"What did Oliver find on the ground?","options":["A toy","A shiny rock","Clara's bracelet","A map"],"correct_answer":"Clara's bracelet"},{"question":"How did Oliver feel when they entered the woods?","options":["Excited and brave","Scared and nervous","Sleepy and bored","Happy and relaxed"],"correct_answer":"Scared and nervous"},{"question":"What did Jake pretend to be scared of?","options":["A mountain","A bear","A ghost","A wolf"],"correct_answer":"A bear"},{"question":"What were the friends hoping to find in the woods?","options":["A treasure","A secret cave","Clara","A picnic spot"],"correct_answer":"Clara"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_262_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_262_ch1_img1.png","plot_262_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":432,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
