   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_262_7_10","title":"The Secret of Pine Hollow","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The sun dipped low in the sky, casting long shadows through the trees. Oliver, Lily, and Jake stood at the edge of a winding path in Pine Hollow. The air was thick with mystery. \n\n\"This is it. We have to go deeper,\" Oliver said, his voice shaky but determined. Lily nodded, her eyes shining with excitement.\n\n\"Do you think we\u2019ll find Clara?\" Jake asked, biting his lip.\n\n\"We will,\" Oliver replied firmly. \"Pip knows this place.\"\n\nJust then, Pip fluttered down from a tree branch, his tiny wings sparkling. \"Follow me! I found something!\" he chirped, zipping ahead.\n\nAs they hurried after Pip, the trees grew thicker. Leaves rustled, and the soft ground squished beneath their feet. The path twisted and turned, leading them to a clearing filled with glowing mushrooms. The sight was magical!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nIn the middle of the clearing, they spotted a shimmering light dancing around a large, ancient tree. \"Is that...?\" Lily gasped.\n\n\"It looks like the light we saw earlier!\" Jake exclaimed.\n\n\"But what does it mean?\" Oliver wondered aloud.\n\nPip flew closer, his eyes wide. \"This light is special! It\u2019s a beacon! It leads to secrets!\"\n\nJust then, a loud rustling came from the bushes. The friends jumped back, hearts racing. Out popped a creature with big, googly eyes and a fluffy tail.\n\n\"Who are you?\" it squeaked. \"Are you here for the treasure?\"\n\n\"Treasure?\" Oliver whispered, excitement bubbling in his chest. \"Is it Clara's?\"\n\n\"Maybe,\" the creature replied with a grin. \"But you must solve the riddle first!\"\n\nThe creature began to sing:\n\n\u201cIn the light of the moon, so silver and bright,  \nFind the path to the right, before it\u2019s out of sight.  \nWhat once was lost, will soon be found,  \nBut only the brave can turn around.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat does that mean?\u201d Jake shouted, trying to drown out his fear.\n\nPip floated close to Oliver. \u201cIt means we have to be brave and find the right path. But are you ready?\u201d\n\nOliver felt a rush of courage. \u201cLet\u2019s go! We can\u2019t leave Clara behind!\u201d\n\nWith a deep breath, Oliver stepped forward, ready to face whatever lay ahead. But suddenly, the ground beneath them trembled. A loud crack echoed through the air. \n\n\u201cUh-oh!\u201d Lily cried. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?!\u201d\n\nThe clearing started to shake, and the light flickered wildly. In that moment, Oliver knew they had to make a decision. Choose the right path or face the danger ahead!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWhich way do we go?\u201d Oliver asked, his heart pounding.\n\n\u201cRight!\u201d Jake shouted, pointing to a narrow path filled with twinkling lights. \n\n\u201cLeft!\u201d Lily insisted, her eyes wide with fear. \n\nOliver looked back and forth. \u201cWe need to decide now!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Pip lead the friends to in the clearing?","options":["A treasure","A cave","A riddle","A monster"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What do the friends discover in the clearing?","options":["Glowing mushrooms","A giant tree","A hidden path","All of the above"],"correct_answer":"All of the above"},{"question":"What happens when Oliver and his friends try to decide on a path?","options":["The ground shakes","They find Clara","They meet a monster","They get lost"],"correct_answer":"The ground shakes"},{"question":"What is the creature's special feature?","options":["It can fly","It has sharp teeth","It is very large","It is invisible"],"correct_answer":"It can fly"},{"question":"What is the friends' main goal in this chapter?","options":["To find treasure","To find Clara","To solve a riddle","To explore the woods"],"correct_answer":"To find Clara"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_262_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_262_ch3_img1.png","plot_262_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":453,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
