   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_262_11_14","title":"The Secret of Pine Hollow","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Oliver stood at the edge of Pine Hollow woods, his heart racing like a train barreling down the tracks. The trees towered high above him, their gnarled branches twisting like fingers reaching for the sky. Sunlight filtered through the leaves, casting playful shadows on the ground, yet an unsettling chill swept through the air. Today was supposed to be a day of adventure, but instead, it felt like he was staring into the mouth of a great, hungry beast.\n\n\u201cAre you sure we should go in there?\u201d Oliver asked, glancing at his best friends, Lily and Jake, who stood beside him. Lily, with her wild curls bouncing in the breeze, wore a brave smile, while Jake fidgeted nervously, his gaze darting around as if expecting something to leap out at him.\n\n\u201cClara\u2019s been gone for too long,\u201d Lily replied, her voice steady. \u201cWe have to at least try to find her.\u201d\n\nOliver nodded, recalling the last time he had seen his older sister. Clara had been bursting with excitement, her eyes alight with dreams of discovering hidden treasures in the woods. \u201cJust a quick look,\u201d she had said, tossing her hair back. \u201cI\u2019ll be back before lunch.\u201d That was hours ago. Now, with the sunlight fading, an uneasy feeling settled in Oliver\u2019s stomach.\n\n\u201cOkay,\u201d he said, steeling himself. \u201cLet\u2019s go.\u201d They stepped forward, the crunch of leaves beneath their feet echoing in the eerie silence. \n\nAs they walked deeper into the woods, the trees seemed to close in around them, their trunks like ancient sentinels keeping secrets. A rustling sound came from the bushes nearby, and Jake jumped, letting out a small yelp. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d \n\n\u201cJust a squirrel,\u201d Oliver said, trying to sound braver than he felt. But a part of him wondered if they were truly alone in this enchanted place.\n\nSuddenly, a glint of something caught Oliver\u2019s eye. He knelt down, brushing aside the fallen leaves to reveal a small silver locket. It was tarnished and dull, but as he opened it, a tiny picture of Clara smiled back at him. \u201cLook! I found Clara\u2019s locket!\u201d he shouted, excitement bubbling in his chest. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nLily leaned closer, her eyes wide. \u201cThat means she was here! We\u2019re getting closer!\u201d\n\n\u201cOr she dropped it when she was running away from something,\u201d Jake murmured, his face paling.\n\n\u201cStop it, Jake!\u201d Oliver snapped, feeling a rush of frustration. \u201cWe need to think positively! Clara would never abandon her stuff.\u201d\n\nJust then, a rustling came again, louder this time. The three friends froze, exchanging worried glances. The underbrush parted, and out stepped a peculiar creature. It was small, no taller than Oliver\u2019s knee, with shimmering wings that reflected the light like a thousand tiny stars. Its eyes, large and curious, locked onto theirs. \n\n\u201cWho dares to enter the Hollow?\u201d it chirped in a sing-song voice, tilting its head as if sizing them up. Oliver\u2019s heart pounded in his chest. \n\n\u201cI\u2019m Oliver, and this is Lily and Jake. We\u2019re looking for my sister, Clara. She went missing!\u201d he exclaimed.\n\nThe creature blinked, its expression shifting from curiosity to concern. \u201cMany have lost their way in these woods. Are you brave enough to face the truth that lies ahead?\u201d\n\nOliver swallowed hard. \u201cWe have to be. We can\u2019t leave without her.\u201d\n\n\u201cThen follow me\u2014if you dare,\u201d the creature said, hovering just above the ground and beckoning with a tiny hand.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith a deep breath, Oliver nodded to his friends. They had come too far to turn back now. He followed the shimmering creature deeper into Pine Hollow, where secrets whispered in the wind and the adventure of a lifetime awaited.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Oliver find in the woods?","options":["A feather","A locket","A map","A stone"],"correct_answer":"A locket"},{"question":"Who are Oliver's friends?","options":["Clara and Jake","Lily and Jake","Mia and Sam","Nina and Jake"],"correct_answer":"Lily and Jake"},{"question":"What does the creature ask Oliver and his friends?","options":["Who are you?","Do you want to leave?","Are you brave enough?","Have you seen Clara?"],"correct_answer":"Are you brave enough?"},{"question":"What feeling does Oliver experience at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["Happiness","Fear","Excitement","Boredom"],"correct_answer":"Fear"},{"question":"What promise does Clara make before she goes missing?","options":["She will return before lunch","She will explore the entire woods","She will find treasure","She will take her friends"],"correct_answer":"She will return before lunch"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_262_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_262_ch1_img1.png","plot_262_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":622,"reading_level":"Builder"}
