   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_7_10","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Ella sat in her favorite spot in the schoolyard. It was a sunny afternoon. The trees swayed gently in the breeze. She watched as her friends gathered around her. \n\n\u201cDid you hear?\u201d Maya exclaimed, her eyes sparkling. \u201cMr. Lopez is starting a treasure hunt!\u201d\n\nSam rolled his eyes. \u201cTreasure? Like pirate treasure? Really?\u201d\n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Ella replied, bouncing on her toes. \u201cHe said it\u2019s hidden around the school and town. We need to work together!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, the school bell rang. It was time for history class. The three friends hurried inside. The classroom was bright, with maps and pictures on the walls. Mr. Lopez stood at the front, grinning.\n\n\u201cWelcome, class! Today, I have something special for you,\u201d he said. \u201cWe\u2019re going on a treasure hunt!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe classroom buzzed with excitement. Ella\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat\u2019s the treasure?\u201d she whispered to Maya.\n\nMr. Lopez cleared his throat. \u201cThe treasure is part of our history. It connects to our town\u2019s past. But there\u2019s a twist. You must find me first! I\u2019ll leave clues!\u201d\n\n\u201cClues? This is going to be awesome!\u201d Sam said, finally smiling.\n\nMr. Lopez handed out the first clue. \u201cThis clue will lead you to the old bridge. Be there by sunset!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat if we can\u2019t find you?\u201d Maya asked, looking worried.\n\n\u201cTrust yourselves. Work as a team!\u201d he replied, winking. \n\nAs the class ended, they rushed out. \u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Ella shouted, grabbing the clue. \n\nThey ran towards the old bridge. It was a big, wooden bridge with a lovely view. But when they got there, something was wrong. Mr. Lopez was nowhere to be seen.\n\n\u201cWhere is he?\u201d Sam asked, looking around anxiously. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Ella said, her heart sinking. \u201cWe have to find him before someone else claims the treasure!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s look for more clues!\u201d Maya suggested, pulling out her tablet. \n\n\u201cI\u2019ll check the trees!\u201d Sam said, running off.\n\nElla stood still, thinking. \u201cMaybe we need to follow the first clue better. What if there\u2019s another hint nearby?\u201d\n\nSuddenly, Maya shouted. \u201cLook here! I found something!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nElla and Sam rushed over. Maya pointed to a piece of paper stuck to a tree. It had a riddle on it. \n\n\u201cThis must be our next clue!\u201d Maya declared. \n\nThey all leaned in to read it together. The riddle was tricky. It spoke of a place where \u201cold stones remember tales of yore.\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat could that mean?\u201d Sam wondered aloud. \n\n\u201cI think we should go to the old library!\u201d Ella suggested. \u201cIt has lots of old stones and stories!\u201d\n\n\u201cThen what are we waiting for? Let\u2019s go!\u201d Maya exclaimed.\n\nWith a new sense of purpose, the trio raced toward the library. They were determined to solve the mystery and find their teacher!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who announces the treasure hunt?","options":["Ella","Mr. Lopez","Maya","Sam"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Lopez"},{"question":"What is the first clue about?","options":["A hidden cave","The old bridge","The school library","A pirate ship"],"correct_answer":"The old bridge"},{"question":"What does Maya find stuck to the tree?","options":["A treasure map","A riddle","A note from Mr. Lopez","A key"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"Where do they decide to go next?","options":["The old bridge","The park","The school cafeteria","The old library"],"correct_answer":"The old library"},{"question":"What are the friends trying to find?","options":["A lost dog","Mr. Lopez","A hidden treasure","Both Mr. Lopez and treasure"],"correct_answer":"Both Mr. Lopez and treasure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch1_img1.png","plot_263_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":469,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
