   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_7_10","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The sun shone brightly on Willow Creek Middle School. Ella, Sam, and Maya stood by the big oak tree. They had their treasure map unfurled in front of them.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d said Ella, pointing. \u201cThis X marks where we need to go!\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, but where\u2019s Mr. Lopez?\u201d Sam asked, frowning. \u201cWe can\u2019t just leave him behind.\u201d\n\nMaya adjusted her glasses. \u201cLet\u2019s follow the clues and find him. The first clue says to look near the old clock tower.\u201d \n\nThey raced through the schoolyard, excited and nervous. As they reached the clock tower, they saw the tall structure looming. It was old and covered in vines. The air felt thick with mystery. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cWhat if the treasure is hidden inside?\u201d Maya suggested, peering up at the clock face.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t think we can climb that,\u201d Sam said, shaking his head. \u201cWhat if we get stuck?\u201d\n\nElla grinned. \u201cNo one gets left behind. We\u2019ll work as a team!\u201d\n\nThe three friends decided to search around the base of the tower. Suddenly, they heard a loud CLANK! \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Sam jumped back.\n\nMaya pulled out her tablet. \u201cI\u2019ll check the security cameras!\u201d She swiped the screen. \u201cIt looks like someone is at the tower!\u201d\n\nElla squinted. \u201cIs that... Mr. Lopez?\u201d \n\nBefore they could think, a shadow moved behind the tower. It was tall and had a wide-brimmed hat. \n\n\u201cHey! Who are you?\u201d Sam shouted, his heart racing.\n\nThe figure turned. \u201cI am the Keeper of Secrets,\u201d it said in a deep voice. \u201cIf you want the treasure, you must answer my riddle!\u201d\n\nElla stepped forward. \u201cWhat\u2019s the riddle?\u201d\n\n\u201cHere it is: I can be cracked, made, told, and played. What am I?\u201d\n\nThe friends looked at each other, puzzled. They had never heard a riddle like this. Just then, Maya gasped. \u201cI know! It\u2019s a joke!\u201d\n\nThe Keeper of Secrets nodded. \u201cYou are wise. Find the next clue under the big clock, but beware! Time is running out!\u201d\n\nWith a rush of excitement, they scrambled to the base of the old clock. Ella reached her hand underneath and felt something cool and hard. \n\n\u201cGot it!\u201d she shouted, pulling out an old, dusty key.\n\n\u201cWow! What does this open?\u201d Sam wondered, his eyes sparkling.\n\n\u201cMaybe it opens a chest with the treasure inside!\u201d Maya suggested, bouncing on her heels.\n\nBut as they celebrated, the shadowy figure stepped closer. \u201cRemember, children, not all treasures are gold. Some secrets are better left hidden. Choose wisely!\u201d\n\nThe friends exchanged worried glances. What did that mean for Mr. Lopez?\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s hurry! We don\u2019t have much time!\u201d Ella urged. \n\nAs they turned to leave, they heard a loud tick, tick, tick. The clock was counting down\u2026 \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cUh-oh! We need to move fast!\u201d Sam said, sprinting ahead.\n\nBut suddenly, the ground shook under them. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?\u201d Maya screamed.\n\nThe friends grabbed each other\u2019s hands tight. They were about to discover something big, but would it save Mr. Lopez or lead them into danger?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ella, Sam, and Maya find at the clock tower?","options":["A treasure chest","A dusty key","A map","A riddle"],"correct_answer":"A dusty key"},{"question":"What does the Keeper of Secrets ask the kids?","options":["To find Mr. Lopez","To solve a riddle","To leave the tower","To share their treasure"],"correct_answer":"To solve a riddle"},{"question":"What is the answer to the riddle?","options":["A key","A joke","A treasure","A clock"],"correct_answer":"A joke"},{"question":"What does Sam feel when he hears the loud clank?","options":["Excited","Nervous","Happy","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What happens as they try to leave the clock tower?","options":["It starts to rain","The ground shakes","They find more clues","They meet Mr. Lopez"],"correct_answer":"The ground shakes"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch3_img1.png","plot_263_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":508,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
