   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_7_10","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Ella, Sam, and Maya gathered at the old school library. The sun shone through the tall windows, lighting up the dusty shelves. The smell of old books filled the air. \n\n\u201cOkay, everyone,\u201d Ella said, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cWe have the key! Let\u2019s see where the next clue leads us!\u201d \n\nSam crossed his arms. \u201cBut what if it doesn\u2019t lead anywhere? We might just be wasting our time.\u201d\n\nMaya shook her head. \u201cNo way! Mr. Lopez wouldn\u2019t give us a clue if it wasn\u2019t important. We just have to believe in ourselves.\u201d\n\nElla nodded. \u201cLet\u2019s look at the treasure map again!\u201d She spread it out on a big wooden table. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe map showed a big \"X\" near the old oak tree in the park. \u201cThat\u2019s where we need to go next!\u201d Ella pointed excitedly. \n\nThey hurried outside, their hearts racing. The park was only a few blocks away, but it felt like a mini-adventure. They dodged puddles and skipped past flowers.\n\nWhen they arrived, the oak tree towered over them. Its thick trunk had deep scars, like it had seen many years. \u201cDo you think the clue is hidden in the tree?\u201d Maya asked.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check!\u201d Ella suggested. They searched around the roots, digging through leaves and dirt. Suddenly, Sam shouted, \u201cWait! I found something!\u201d\n\nHe pulled out a small, dusty box. \u201cWhat\u2019s in here?\u201d he wondered aloud. The box had a rusty lock, but no key.\n\n\u201cI\u2019ll see if I can hack it open!\u201d Maya said, pulling out her tablet. Her fingers danced across the screen as she tapped and swiped. Suddenly, the lock clicked open!\n\nThe box creaked as they lifted the lid. Inside, they found an old piece of paper. Ella unfolded it carefully. \u201cIt\u2019s a letter!\u201d \n\nHer hands shook with excitement. \u201cIt\u2019s from Mr. Lopez! He wrote about a treasure that belonged to a famous explorer!\u201d \n\nJust then, they heard a noise behind them. They turned to see a shadowy figure watching them from the bushes. \u201cWho\u2019s there?\u201d Sam called out, trying to sound brave.\n\nThe figure stepped closer, revealing himself to be Mr. Lopez! \u201cYou found my letter!\u201d he smiled. \u201cI was testing your skills.\u201d\n\nElla, Sam, and Maya jumped with joy. \u201cYou\u2019re okay!\u201d they cried.\n\nMr. Lopez nodded. \u201cYes! I left clues to teach you about history and teamwork. Now, let\u2019s find that treasure together!\u201d\n\nThe friends cheered, feeling hopeful as they prepared for the next step in their adventure. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they gathered around Mr. Lopez, they felt like a real team, ready to solve the mystery together. \u201cWhere do we go next?\u201d they asked in unison, eager for more.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ella, Sam, and Maya find at the oak tree?","options":["A treasure map","A dusty box","A key","A letter"],"correct_answer":"A dusty box"},{"question":"What does Maya use to help open the box?","options":["A key","A tablet","A hammer","A wrench"],"correct_answer":"A tablet"},{"question":"Who appears at the end of the chapter?","options":["A shadowy figure","Mr. Lopez","A park ranger","A dog"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Lopez"},{"question":"What is the main emotion of Ella, Sam, and Maya when they see Mr. Lopez?","options":["Anger","Sadness","Joy","Fear"],"correct_answer":"Joy"},{"question":"What is the theme of this chapter?","options":["Friendship","Greed","Fear","Failure"],"correct_answer":"Friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch4_img1.png","plot_263_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":455,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
