   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_7_10","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Ella, Sam, and Maya stood at the old oak tree in the schoolyard. The sun shone brightly, casting long shadows. They had found a new clue! \n\n\u201cOkay, let\u2019s see what this clue says,\u201d Ella said, holding the letter. Her heart raced with excitement. \n\nMaya adjusted her glasses and leaned in. \u201cIt says, \u2018The treasure lies where the past whispers.\u2019 What do you think that means?\u201d\n\nSam shrugged. \u201cWhispers? Sounds spooky. Maybe it\u2019s in the library?\u201d\n\nElla\u2019s eyes lit up. \u201cThe library has a lot of old books. That could be it!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Maya exclaimed. They hurried towards the entrance of the school, their footsteps quick and eager. \n\nAs they entered the library, the air felt cool and calm. Rows of books towered above them. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\n\u201cLook for anything that whispers history,\u201d Ella said, scanning the shelves. She pulled out a dusty book. \u201cThis one might have clues!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, Maya pointed excitedly. \u201cGuys! Look at that old globe! It must be from the 1800s!\u201d \n\nThey rushed over. The globe was covered in dust. Sam wiped it off, revealing bright colors. \u201cWow! It looks so cool!\u201d\n\n\u201cWait! There\u2019s a note taped under it!\u201d Maya said, her fingers trembling. \n\nElla carefully peeled the note off. It read, \u201cThe next clue is where you can find a friend who loves to read.\u201d \n\n\u201cA friend who loves to read?\u201d Sam asked, scratching his head. \u201cThat could be anyone!\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s Miss Thompson, the librarian!\u201d Maya said, her eyes sparkling.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s ask her!\u201d Ella said, her excitement bubbling. They dashed to the librarian\u2019s desk. \n\nMiss Thompson smiled. \u201cWhat can I help you with?\u201d \n\n\u201cWe think there\u2019s a clue about the treasure! It mentions a friend who loves to read!\u201d Maya explained. \n\nMiss Thompson\u2019s eyes twinkled. \u201cOh, I think I know just the place! Follow me!\u201d \n\nThey followed her to a cozy corner filled with soft cushions and colorful books. \u201cHere it is,\u201d Miss Thompson said, pointing. \u201cThis is where I keep the historical books. You\u2019ll find many stories about adventures!\u201d\n\n\u201cI see a book on pirates!\u201d Sam yelled. \n\n\u201cPirates could lead us to treasure!\u201d Ella said, her heart racing again. \n\nAs they searched through the books, they found another note tucked inside a page. \u201cThe treasure lies beneath the oldest tree in town,\u201d it read.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Ella shouted. They hurried out of the library, their minds racing with thoughts of what they might find. \n\n\u201cMr. Lopez is waiting for us!\u201d Maya said, determined. \u201cWe can\u2019t let him down!\u201d\n\nWith renewed energy, they raced towards the town park, ready for their next adventure. But little did they know, danger lurked nearby, watching their every move.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cKeep your eyes open!\u201d Sam whispered. \u201cWe\u2019re getting closer!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did the clue in the library mention?","options":["A treasure map","A friend who loves to read","A hidden room","A sports game"],"correct_answer":"A friend who loves to read"},{"question":"Where did Ella, Sam, and Maya think to look for the next clue?","options":["The schoolyard","The library","The clock tower","The cafeteria"],"correct_answer":"The library"},{"question":"Who helped them find the next clue?","options":["Mr. Lopez","Miss Thompson","The Keeper of Secrets","Their principal"],"correct_answer":"Miss Thompson"},{"question":"What did they find under the globe?","options":["A map","A treasure chest","A note","A key"],"correct_answer":"A note"},{"question":"What was the next location they were heading to?","options":["The town park","The library","The old oak tree","The playground"],"correct_answer":"The town park"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch5_img1.png","plot_263_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":466,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
