   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_11_14","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: The First Clue\n\nElla paced back and forth in the empty classroom, her heart pounding like a drum. \u201cWhere could he have gone?\u201d she murmured, glancing at the door as if expecting Mr. Lopez to walk right back in, laughing off their worries. Sam leaned against a desk, arms crossed, his skeptical expression matching his crossed arms.\n\n\u201cMaybe he just went to grab something,\u201d he said, trying to sound nonchalant. But Ella could see the concern lurking below his bravado. Maya was already at the whiteboard, scribbling down everything they knew about the treasure hunt. \n\n\u201cRemember what Mr. Lopez said before he rushed out?\u201d Maya asked, her eyes lighting up with excitement. \u201cHe mentioned something about a hidden key!\u201d\n\n\u201cThat\u2019s right!\u201d Ella replied, feeling a spark of hope. \u201cHe said the first clue was hidden somewhere significant to our town\u2019s history.\u201d She paused, her mind racing. \u201cWhat if it relates to him?\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from the hallway, causing them to jump. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Sam asked, eyes wide.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find out!\u201d Ella exclaimed, her determination firing up. The three friends scrambled for the door, but just as they reached the hallway, they were met with a breathtaking sight. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nIn the bright light filtering through the windows, they saw a group of older students gathered around a display case filled with artifacts. One of them, a tall boy with a baseball cap, was holding what appeared to be an old map. Ella\u2019s heart raced; it could be one of the treasure clues!\n\n\u201cHey, what do you have there?\u201d Ella called out, forcing a brave smile as they approached the older kids.\n\n\u201cNone of your business, twerps!\u201d the boy sneered, stuffing the map into his backpack. Before they could react, the group dispersed, laughter fading down the hallway.\n\n\u201cThat\u2019s not fair!\u201d Maya said, her fists clenched. \u201cWe need to get that map!\u201d\n\nElla nodded, feeling a surge of resolve. \u201cLet\u2019s split up. Maya, you stay here and gather any info on the map from the school\u2019s history database. Sam and I will check around the school for any clues that might lead us back to Mr. Lopez.\u201d\n\nAs they moved into action, a sense of urgency propelled them forward. The sun dipped lower in the sky, casting long shadows down the hall. Ella felt the weight of responsibility settling on her shoulders. They needed to find Mr. Lopez, and fast.\n\nThe first stop was the library, a hushed sanctuary filled with ancient books and whispers of the past. With stacks of history tomes surrounding them, Ella felt a connection to their teacher. \u201cMaybe we\u2019ll find something about him here,\u201d she suggested, flipping through a dusty book on local legends.\n\nSuddenly, a loud thud resonated from the back of the library. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Sam whispered, eyes wide.\n\n\u201cYeah,\u201d Ella said, her stomach twisting in knots. They both crept towards the noise, hearts racing. As they turned the corner, they saw Maya, her face pale, standing next to an overturned table.\n\n\u201cI found something!\u201d she exclaimed, pointing to a small, ornate box lying on the floor. \u201cBut I think it was moved!\u201d\n\nElla\u2019s breath caught as they approached the box. Its intricate carvings looked ancient, and there was a faint glimmer of something inside. \u201cCould this be part of the treasure?\u201d she wondered aloud.\n\nBefore they could reach for it, the library doors slammed shut, echoing ominously. The three friends exchanged worried glances. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d Sam demanded, panic creeping into his voice. The tension hung thick in the air as they realized they were now trapped in the library.\n\nMaya rushed to the door, pulling at the handle. \u201cIt\u2019s locked!\u201d she shouted, fear flooding her features. \n\n\u201cThen we need to find a way out,\u201d Ella said, determination bubbling inside her. They had to stay focused\u2014not just on the treasure, but on finding Mr. Lopez before it was too late.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they turned back to the mysterious box, their minds raced with questions. What secrets lay within? And what would they discover about their teacher\u2019s past? The adventure was just beginning.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Ella and her friends first hear that caused concern?","options":["A bell ringing","A loud crash","A door slamming","A teacher shouting"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash"},{"question":"What did the older boy have that caught Ella's attention?","options":["A treasure map","A history book","A golden key","A piece of jewelry"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"What did Maya find at the library?","options":["A locked door","An ornate box","A treasure chest","A hidden key"],"correct_answer":"An ornate box"},{"question":"How did Ella feel when they were trapped in the library?","options":["Relieved","Confused","Determined","Excited"],"correct_answer":"Determined"},{"question":"What theme is highlighted as the friends face challenges together?","options":["Friendship","Competition","Isolation","Fear"],"correct_answer":"Friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch2_img1.png","plot_263_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":701,"reading_level":"Builder"}
