   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_11_14","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Ella, Sam, and Maya stood in the dimly lit library, the musty smell of old books surrounding them. Heavy shadows danced on the walls as they stared at the ornate box that had just been unlocked. Inside lay Mr. Lopez's journal, the pages worn and filled with his neat handwriting. \"This is it,\" Ella whispered, her heart racing. \"This could lead us to him!\"  \n\nAs they gathered around, Maya flipped open the journal. \"Look at this!\" she exclaimed, pointing to a passage about a hidden cave near the old mill on the outskirts of town. \"Mr. Lopez wrote about a treasure map that belonged to his grandfather. I think the treasure he mentioned is connected to that cave!\"  \n\nSam furrowed his brow, still skeptical. \"But how do we know this isn\u2019t just some wild goose chase? It could be a dead end.\"  \n\n\u201cMaybe, but what if it isn\u2019t?\u201d Ella countered, determination shining in her eyes. \u201cWe can\u2019t give up on Mr. Lopez. He believed in us.\u201d  \n\nThey began to map out a plan, scribbling down the clues and discussing what they would need to venture to the mill. A sense of hope blossomed within them, but before they could finish, a sudden noise echoed through the library\u2014like a faint whisper of someone calling for help.  \n\nThe three friends exchanged wide-eyed glances. \"Did you hear that?\" Maya asked, her voice trembling.  \n\n\u201cYeah,\u201d Sam replied, his bravado faltering. \u201cIt sounded like it came from the back room.\u201d  \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out,\u201d Ella urged, her heart pounding. They crept towards the source of the sound, the hairs on the back of their necks standing on end.  \n\nAs they turned the corner, they found themselves standing before a heavy wooden door that had always been locked. To their surprise, it was now slightly ajar. \u201cIs it just me, or does that look like it was opened recently?\u201d Maya pointed out.  \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go,\u201d Ella said, her voice steady but with an underlying urgency. They pushed the door open together, revealing a dark room filled with dust and cobwebs. In the center stood an old wooden table with a faded map laid out on it.  \n\n\u201cCould this be the treasure map?\u201d Sam wondered aloud, stepping closer. Just as he reached for it, they heard the distant sound of footsteps echoing outside the library. Panic surged through them. \u201cWhat if someone else is after the treasure?\u201d  \n\nElla grabbed Sam\u2019s arm, her eyes wide. \u201cWe need to hurry. If they find it first\u2026\u201d  \n\nMaya quickly snapped a picture of the map with her phone. \u201cWe can\u2019t let anyone take it! Let\u2019s go!\u201d The trio darted back to the main part of the library, clutching the journal tightly.  \n\nElla felt a flicker of hope. \u201cWe\u2019re one step closer. We can\u2019t let fear stop us now.\u201d As they moved swiftly, the shadows in the library seemed to close in around them, adding to their urgency.  \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]  \n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from the back room, and they all froze. \"What was that?\" Maya gasped, her hand tightening around her phone.  \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we need to find Mr. Lopez before it\u2019s too late,\u201d Ella said, determination hardening in her voice. They hurried towards the exit, adrenaline pumping through their veins.  \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]  \n\nAs they burst into the sunlight outside, they felt a renewed sense of purpose. They had to follow the clues in Mr. Lopez's journal and get to the old mill before anyone else did. Little did they know, the greatest surprises awaited them there, including revelations about their teacher's mysterious past.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ella and her friends discover in Mr. Lopez's journal?","options":["A treasure map","A letter","A diary","A photograph"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"What do the characters hear that causes them to feel alarmed?","options":["A loud crash","A voice","Footsteps","A door slamming"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash"},{"question":"Where do Ella, Sam, and Maya plan to go next?","options":["The school","The library","The old mill","Mr. Lopez's house"],"correct_answer":"The old mill"},{"question":"How does Ella feel about their chances of finding Mr. Lopez?","options":["Hopeful","Pessimistic","Indifferent","Scared"],"correct_answer":"Hopeful"},{"question":"What emotion does Sam display throughout the chapter?","options":["Skepticism","Joy","Fear","Excitement"],"correct_answer":"Skepticism"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch4_img1.png","plot_263_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":609,"reading_level":"Builder"}
