   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_15_18","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Ella stood at the entrance of the school\u2019s library, the smell of old books mingling with the faint scent of polished wood. Sunlight streamed through the tall windows, casting golden patterns on the floor, but today, the warmth felt distant, almost mocking. Sam paced back and forth, the soles of his sneakers squeaking against the tiles, while Maya adjusted her glasses and tapped furiously on her tablet. They had just learned that Mr. Lopez had gone missing, leaving not just a void in their hearts but a mystery that demanded to be solved.\n\n\u201cWe can\u2019t just sit here!\u201d Ella exclaimed, clenching her fists. \u201cHe wouldn\u2019t disappear without a reason. The treasure hunt was his idea, and now he\u2019s gone. It has to be connected.\u201d \n\n\u201cBut a missing teacher? What kind of clues are we even looking for?\u201d Sam retorted, his skepticism evident in the way he crossed his arms. \u201cIt\u2019s not like we\u2019re detectives. We\u2019re just seventh graders.\u201d\n\nMaya, her brow furrowed in thought, chimed in. \u201cActually, we might have a better chance than you think. Mr. Lopez is passionate about local history. There are historical landmarks all over town that he\u2019s always talked about. Maybe the treasure hunt clues are hidden at those sites.\u201d\n\nSam stopped pacing, tilting his head as he considered Maya\u2019s suggestion. \u201cOkay, but if we do this, we need a plan. We can\u2019t just charge into the unknown blindly.\u201d \n\nElla nodded, feeling a surge of purpose. \u201cLet\u2019s start at the old clock tower. It\u2019s one of the oldest buildings in town and has been a part of several of Mr. Lopez\u2019s lessons. Maybe there\u2019s something there.\u201d \n\nTogether, they slipped out of the library, their hearts racing with anticipation. The late afternoon sun cast long shadows as they made their way down the tree-lined street, the air thick with the scent of blooming flowers and the sound of distant laughter. However, as they approached the clock tower, an unsettling feeling settled over Ella. What if they were too late? What if someone else was already searching for Mr. Lopez\u2019s secret treasure?\n\nUpon reaching the clock tower, they found its worn stone walls and ivy-clad entrance imposing yet inviting. As they stepped inside, the musty air filled their lungs, and the muted light created an atmosphere that felt both sacred and secretive. \u201cLook at this!\u201d Maya exclaimed, pointing to a series of old photographs lining the walls, each depicting previous townsfolk and their contributions to the town\u2019s history.\n\n\u201cWait,\u201d Sam said, his voice dropping to a whisper. \u201cWhat if we look closely? There could be something hidden in one of these.\u201d \n\nAs they examined the photographs, Ella spotted one that piqued her interest. It was a picture of a group of students with Mr. Lopez, standing proudly in front of the clock tower during a past field trip. \u201cLook at the girl in the front! She\u2019s holding a map,\u201d Ella said, her pulse quickening. \u201cIt looks like a treasure map!\u201d\n\nMaya leaned closer to the photograph, her eyes widening as she noticed something else. \u201cThat\u2019s the same map Mr. Lopez used for our field trip last year. Maybe there\u2019s something about it that leads to the treasure!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, the sound of footsteps echoed through the tower, drawing their attention. They turned to see a tall figure looming in the shadows. A chill surged through Ella as the figure stepped into the fading light. \n\n\u201cWho are you kids? This is private property,\u201d the stranger barked, his expression stern, casting an unsettling aura over the trio.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re just looking for Mr. Lopez,\u201d Ella stammered, her confidence wavering. \u201cHe went missing, and we think he might be connected to the treasure hunt.\u201d \n\nThe stranger\u2019s eyes narrowed. \u201cThat treasure belongs to the town. You kids should be careful. There are people out there who would do anything to get their hands on it\u2014and on Lopez. Now, leave before it\u2019s too late!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs the stranger\u2019s shadow loomed ominously, Ella, Sam, and Maya exchanged anxious glances, their earlier resolve now shaken. \u201cWe need to find the clues before someone else does,\u201d Sam whispered, his bravado fading as they felt the weight of the unknown pressing on their shoulders.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s not give up,\u201d Maya urged, her fingers tightening around her tablet. \u201cWe can figure this out together.\u201d\n\nThey agreed silently and turned back to the photographs, determined to uncover the truth, knowing that every moment counted.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nTaking a deep breath, Ella said, \u201cWe need to figure out what that girl in the photo knew. We can\u2019t let fear stop us from finding Mr. Lopez. He\u2019s counting on us.\u201d\n\nAs the tension escalated, they found themselves caught in a web of history and danger, inching closer to uncovering a mystery that could change everything.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the main location where Ella, Sam, and Maya search for clues?","options":["The school library","The old clock tower","The park","Their homes"],"correct_answer":"The old clock tower"},{"question":"What did Maya suggest as a potential source of clues?","options":["The school cafeteria","Local historical landmarks","The gym","Online forums"],"correct_answer":"Local historical landmarks"},{"question":"How does Sam initially feel about the investigation?","options":["Excited","Skeptical","Indifferent","Fearful"],"correct_answer":"Skeptical"},{"question":"What warning does the stranger give the kids?","options":["To leave the clock tower","To stop searching for the treasure","To be careful of dangerous people","To go home"],"correct_answer":"To be careful of dangerous people"},{"question":"What is Ella's emotional state when they encounter the stranger?","options":["Confident","Fearful","Excited","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Fearful"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch2_img1.png","plot_263_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":820,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
