   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_15_18","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The sun dipped lower in the sky, casting long shadows across Hillcrest Middle School\u2019s courtyard. As Ella, Sam, and Maya gathered near the old oak tree, the weight of their mission pressed heavily upon them. Ella\u2019s fingers fidgeted with the photograph they had found\u2014the image of Mr. Lopez standing beside a historical landmark, a warm smile on his face, but the secrets behind that smile had begun to unravel.\n\n\u201cGuys, what if we\u2019re in over our heads?\u201d Sam broke the silence, his voice taut with skepticism. \u201cI mean, we\u2019re just seventh graders. What do we really know about treasure hunting? Or about Mr. Lopez?\u201d\n\nElla looked up, determination igniting in her hazel eyes. \u201cWe know he\u2019s missing, and we\u2019re the only ones who seem to care enough to look for him. Plus, every mystery has a solution, right?\u201d Her confidence was contagious, yet Sam\u2019s furrowed brow betrayed his doubts.\n\nMaya, tapping on her tablet, interrupted. \u201cHold on. There\u2019s something else.\u201d She turned the screen towards them, revealing a map of their town with several locations marked in red. \u201cThese spots\u2014look closely. They all link to the clues from the photo. We need to check them out, one by one.\u201d\n\nBefore Sam could voice more concerns, Ella grabbed Maya's arm. \u201cLet\u2019s go to the library first. It\u2019s got to have something about this place, right?\u201d\n\nAs they strode towards the library, the tension between them crackled like static electricity. Ella felt the weight of leadership resting squarely on her shoulders, a burden she never asked for. Yet, she couldn\u2019t shake the nagging feeling that something larger than them was at play.\n\nInside the library, stacks of books loomed like ancient sentinels. The smell of aged parchment filled the air, mixing with the palpable anxiety swirling among the trio. \u201cMaya, you start searching online for anything about Mr. Lopez\u2019s past. Sam and I will dig through these books,\u201d Ella instructed, a plan forming in her mind.\n\n\u201cFine. But if we don\u2019t find anything soon, I\u2019m out,\u201d Sam replied, crossing his arms. The tension festered; he was torn between loyalty to his friends and his inherent skepticism about the hunt.\n\nHours passed, and the library remained eerily quiet, save for the rustling of pages and the occasional hum of Maya\u2019s tablet. Just as Ella began losing hope, Sam called from the back of the library, his voice echoing with a mix of excitement and fear. \u201cElla! You need to see this!\u201d\n\nElla exchanged a glance with Maya before racing towards Sam. When she arrived, he stood beside a dusty book titled \u201cLegends of Hillcrest.\u201d As he flipped through the pages, Ella\u2019s heart thudded in her chest. There, illustrated in vibrant colors, was the very landmark from the photograph of Mr. Lopez\u2014a hidden statue dedicated to an unknown hero. \n\n\u201cThat\u2019s it!\u201d Maya exclaimed, leaning closer. \u201cIf the treasure is linked to this statue, then we have to figure out what makes it so significant. But why would Mr. Lopez care?\u201d\n\nBefore they could contemplate further, the library doors swung open violently, startling them. A tall figure entered, cloaked in shadows. The same stranger they encountered at the clock tower. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be here,\u201d he warned, his voice low and gravelly. \u201cYou are digging into things that should remain buried.\u201d\n\nElla\u2019s heart raced as anger surged within her. \u201cAnd you are? Why do you care?\u201d\n\nThe stranger\u2019s eyes glinted, a mixture of menace and regret. \u201cBecause the treasure you seek isn\u2019t just gold or jewels. It\u2019s something far more dangerous.\u201d\n\nJust then, the lights flickered, plunging the library into darkness. Panic gripped Ella as she fumbled for her phone, the screen casting a weak glow. In that fleeting moment, the stranger vanished into the shadows, leaving the three friends trembling.\n\n\u201cDid you see that?\u201d Sam\u2019s voice trembled. \u201cWhat if he knows something?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe have to go after him!\u201d Ella insisted, adrenaline coursing through her veins. But as they made their way to the exit, a decision loomed ahead\u2014follow the stranger into the unknown or stay and search for Mr. Lopez\u2019s truth in the darkness of the library.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What discovery do the friends make in the library?","options":["A hidden treasure map","A book about legends","A letter from Mr. Lopez","A photograph of the stranger"],"correct_answer":"A book about legends"},{"question":"How does Sam feel about the treasure hunt?","options":["Excited and enthusiastic","Skeptical and reluctant","Indifferent","Supportive and hopeful"],"correct_answer":"Skeptical and reluctant"},{"question":"What warning does the stranger give the trio?","options":["To stop searching for treasure","To leave the library","To trust Mr. Lopez","To solve the mystery quickly"],"correct_answer":"To stop searching for treasure"},{"question":"What is the tone of the scene when the lights flicker?","options":["Joyful and celebratory","Tense and suspenseful","Calm and peaceful","Confusing and chaotic"],"correct_answer":"Tense and suspenseful"},{"question":"What decision do the friends face at the end of the chapter?","options":["To leave the library for help","To continue their search outdoors","To follow the stranger or stay in the library","To give up the treasure hunt"],"correct_answer":"To follow the stranger or stay in the library"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch3_img1.png","plot_263_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":714,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
