   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_263_15_18","title":"The Case of the Lost Treasure","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the sun rose, casting golden rays over the schoolyard, Ella, Sam, and Maya gathered at their usual meeting spot by the old oak tree. The events of the previous day replayed in Ella\u2019s mind like a film on rewind: the shadowy figure, the warning, Mr. Lopez\u2019s passionate speech about history, and the tantalizing clues they had uncovered. Today, however, felt different; it bore the weight of determination. \n\n\u201cDid you guys think about what that figure said?\u201d Sam broke the silence, his brow furrowed. \u201cWhat if we\u2019re getting in over our heads?\u201d\n\nElla shook her head. \u201cWe can\u2019t think like that. Mr. Lopez is counting on us. We need to focus on the next clue. The statue is our best lead.\u201d\n\nMaya, her fingers tapping rhythmically against her tablet, chimed in. \u201cAccording to the library\u2019s archives, the statue isn\u2019t just any piece of art. It\u2019s part of the founding story of our town, tied to the treasure Mr. Lopez mentioned. We have to go back.\u201d\n\nThey trekked through the school halls, the atmosphere thick with anticipation. The worn wooden floors creaked underfoot, echoing their resolve. As they reached the library, the scent of aged paper and polished wood enveloped them. The room was dimly lit, shadows dancing around the corners like secrets.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s split up. I\u2019ll check the history section for anything on the statue,\u201d Maya suggested, her eyes gleaming with excitement. Sam nodded, moving toward the far end of the library where the art books were kept, while Ella approached the statue, its marble surface gleaming under the soft light, as if inviting her to touch its cold exterior. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nElla ran her fingers along the statue\u2019s intricate carvings, deciphering the symbols etched into the stone. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s a code?\u201d she pondered aloud, her voice barely above a whisper. \u201cOr a map?\u201d \n\nAt that moment, Maya returned, holding a tattered book that seemed to be centuries old. \u201cLook at this! It has a drawing of the statue and mentions the treasure! It says it\u2019s hidden where \u2018the sun meets the shadow at the hour of the crow.\u2019 What do you think that means?\u201d \n\nJust as they began to discuss the meaning, a loud crash echoed through the library, freezing them in place. The shadowy figure from the previous day emerged from behind a bookshelf, eyes glinting with menace. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t be here,\u201d the figure warned, an edge of desperation in their voice. \n\n\u201cWhy are you after the treasure? What do you know about Mr. Lopez?\u201d Ella demanded, stepping forward, her heart racing. \n\nThe figure hesitated, and for an instant, vulnerability flickered in their eyes. \u201cI know more than you think, but you need to walk away. It\u2019s not what you believe.\u201d \n\nBefore they could respond, the figure darted toward the exit, leaving the trio in stunned silence. \n\n\u201cDid we just let them get away?\u201d Sam exclaimed, frustration bubbling beneath the surface. \n\n\u201cNo,\u201d Maya replied, determination hardening her voice. \u201cWe need to follow them. They might lead us to Mr. Lopez.\u201d \n\nWith renewed urgency, they sprinted out of the library, the whispers of the shadows trailing behind them, echoing the uncertainty of their mission. \n\nAs they raced through the school grounds, a sense of hope washed over Ella. Perhaps, just perhaps, they were closer to unraveling the mystery than they had thought. \n\nThe path ahead was shrouded in uncertainty, yet their resolve crystallized: they would find Mr. Lopez. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe trio paused at the edge of the woods, the sun dipping behind the treetops, casting long shadows that mirrored their fears. \u201cAre we ready for this?\u201d Sam asked, eyes darting to the dense thicket before them. \n\nElla nodded, her heart pounding with a mix of excitement and trepidation. \u201cTogether,\u201d she affirmed, taking a step forward, her friends following closely behind. \n\nIn the distance, a crow cawed, its voice echoing like a warning. \n\nThey ventured into the unknown, ready to confront whatever awaited them, driven by the belief that every clue brought them closer not only to a treasure but to a truth that could change everything.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What clue do Ella and her friends find in the library related to the treasure?","options":["A map to the treasure","A drawing of the statue","A letter from Mr. Lopez","A photograph of the figure"],"correct_answer":"A drawing of the statue"},{"question":"What warning does the shadowy figure give to Ella and her friends?","options":["To leave town","Not to trust Mr. Lopez","Not to pursue the treasure","To stop asking questions"],"correct_answer":"Not to pursue the treasure"},{"question":"What is the significance of the phrase 'the sun meets the shadow at the hour of the crow'?","options":["It describes the location of the treasure","It is a warning about danger","It indicates when to start the treasure hunt","It relates to Mr. Lopez's past"],"correct_answer":"It describes the location of the treasure"},{"question":"How does Ella feel when they decide to follow the shadowy figure?","options":["Fearful and anxious","Hopeful and determined","Indifferent and bored","Excited and reckless"],"correct_answer":"Hopeful and determined"},{"question":"What does the crow's caw signify at the end of the chapter?","options":["A sign of danger","A call to adventure","An indication of success","A warning to turn back"],"correct_answer":"A sign of danger"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_263_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_263_ch4_img1.png","plot_263_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":692,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
