   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_264_7_10","title":"The Whispers in the Wind","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"It was a warm summer afternoon when Leo, thirteen years old, arrived at the campsite with his family. The tall trees swayed gently in the breeze, and a bright sun peeked through the leaves. Leo loved camping, but this trip felt different. \n\n\u201cLook, Leo! I can see the lake!\u201d shouted Tess, his eight-year-old sister, as she raced ahead.\n\n\u201cWait up, Tess!\u201d Leo called, following her. Her curly hair bounced as she ran. They reached the shimmering lake, where Grandma Rose sat on a rock, her eyes sparkling like the water.\n\n\u201cGrandma! What are you doing?\u201d Leo asked.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m listening to the whispers in the wind,\u201d she replied with a smile. \u201cThey have stories to tell.\u201d\n\nLeo smiled back, but he didn\u2019t understand. What could the wind possibly say? As they set up the tent, Grandma continued to gaze into the trees, lost in thought. \n\nLater that evening, they gathered around the campfire. The crackling flames danced as Leo roasted marshmallows. Suddenly, Grandma Rose stood up. \n\n\u201cI\u2019ll be right back,\u201d she said. \n\n\u201cWhere are you going?\u201d Leo asked, concerned. \n\n\u201cJust\u2026 listen to the wind,\u201d she murmured, walking toward the trees.\n\nLeo and Tess watched her go. \n\n\u201cDo you think she heard something?\u201d Tess asked, her eyes wide.\n\n\u201cMaybe. But she\u2019s always been a little strange about the forest,\u201d Leo replied.\n\nAs night fell, the forest seemed to change. The wind grew louder. It whistled and sighed through the trees. Suddenly, the whispers felt different. \n\n\u201cTess, did you hear that?\u201d Leo whispered.\n\n\u201cHear what?\u201d Tess asked.\n\n\u201cThe wind! It\u2019s like it\u2019s calling us!\u201d Leo\u2019s heart raced. \n\nSuddenly, the whispers became clearer. \u201cFind her\u2026 find her\u2026\u201d they seemed to say.\n\n\u201cFind who?\u201d Tess asked, gripping Leo\u2019s arm.\n\n\u201cGrandma!\u201d Leo exclaimed. \u201cWe need to go after her!\u201d\n\nBefore he could think twice, Leo grabbed Tess\u2019s hand. \u201cCome on!\u201d \n\nThey dashed into the dark woods, the whispers guiding them deeper. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nThe trees loomed overhead, casting shadows in the moonlight. Twigs snapped underfoot as they hurried. \n\n\u201cLeo, wait! What if we get lost?\u201d Tess said, a tremble in her voice.\n\n\u201cJust follow the whispers,\u201d he urged. \n\nThen, they reached a small clearing. The wind was loud here, swirling around them. \n\n\u201cGrandma?\u201d Leo called out, but only the wind answered.\n\nSuddenly, Tess gasped. \u201cLook!\u201d she shouted, pointing to a shimmering light in the distance. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Leo urged, feeling a mix of fear and excitement. \n\nAs they approached the light, the whispers grew louder, echoing through the trees. \u201cFind her\u2026 find her\u2026\u201d \n\nWhat secrets did the wind hold? Leo felt a thrill of adventure rush through him. They had to solve this mystery. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] \n\n\u201cDo you think Grandma is near?\u201d Tess asked nervously, her wide eyes searching the shadows.\n\n\u201cI believe she is,\u201d Leo replied, determination rising in his chest. \u201cLet\u2019s keep moving!\u201d\n\nAnd with that, the two siblings stepped into the unknown, ready to uncover the secrets hidden in the forest.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Grandma Rose say she is listening to?","options":["The trees","The whispers in the wind","The lake","The stars"],"correct_answer":"The whispers in the wind"},{"question":"What does Leo feel when he hears the whispers?","options":["Fear","Excitement","Sleepy","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"},{"question":"Who follows Leo into the forest?","options":["His mom","His dad","His sister Tess","His friend"],"correct_answer":"His sister Tess"},{"question":"What does the wind say as Leo and Tess move deeper into the forest?","options":["Stay here","Find her","Go back","Stop now"],"correct_answer":"Find her"},{"question":"What do Leo and Tess see in the distance?","options":["A bear","A shimmering light","A campfire","A river"],"correct_answer":"A shimmering light"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_264_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_264_ch1_img1.png","plot_264_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":499,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
