   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_264_11_14","title":"The Whispers in the Wind","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun dipped low in the sky, casting long shadows among the towering trees of Cedarwood Forest. Leo adjusted the straps of his backpack, excitement bubbling in his chest. This was no ordinary camping trip; it was a chance to escape city life and dive into an adventure. He glanced over at his little sister, Tess, who was busy trying to catch a butterfly flitting by. She was only eight, but her adventurous spirit often matched his own. \n\n\u201cTess, you\u2019re going to scare it away!\u201d he called, half-exasperated, half-amused.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m not! I\u2019m just being quiet!\u201d she insisted with a grin, her eyes sparkling with mischief. Leo chuckled as he walked ahead, the path winding deeper into the forest, where the trees whispered secrets only the brave dared to uncover. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they set up camp in a small clearing, the air buzzed with the sounds of nature. Leo could hear birds chirping and leaves rustling. It was picturesque, the kind of place where stories began. Grandma Rose had always told them tales of the forest\u2014of magic and mystery hidden among the trees. But Leo\u2019s heart tightened as he thought of her absent presence. She should have been here, directing their camping trip with her usual flair. \n\n\u201cDo you think Grandma will come out hiking with us tomorrow?\u201d Tess asked, her voice breaking through Leo\u2019s thoughts. \n\n\u201cI hope so,\u201d he replied, forcing a smile. \u201cBut she\u2019s probably just tired. You know, age and stuff.\u201d \n\nTess scrunched her nose, clearly not satisfied with that answer. \u201cBut she\u2019s not old! She\u2019s fun!\u201d \n\n\u201cYeah, she is.\u201d Leo felt a pang of worry. Grandma Rose had promised to come. But with each passing hour, he felt the weight of something unsettling. \n\nAs dusk settled in, a soft wind began to weave through the trees, tenderly brushing against Leo\u2019s cheek. It felt\u2026 different. Not just a breeze, but something more alive. He paused, feeling compelled to listen. \n\n\u201cTess, do you hear that?\u201d he asked, squinting into the dimming light. \n\n\u201cHear what?\u201d She looked up at him, her brow furrowed in confusion.\n\n\u201cThe wind. It\u2019s\u2026 whispering.\u201d \n\n\u201cWhispering?\u201d She giggled, but there was a hint of curiosity in her voice. \n\n\u201cYeah, like it\u2019s trying to tell us something.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the wind picked up, swirling around them, and Leo felt a strange pull in his chest. It was as if the forest itself was beckoning him forward. \n\n\u201cTess, stay close, okay?\u201d Leo said, his heart pounding. \u201cI think we should follow it.\u201d\n\n\u201cFollow the wind? You\u2019re crazy!\u201d she exclaimed, but there was a spark of excitement in her eyes. \n\n\u201cJust trust me,\u201d Leo said, taking a tentative step toward the trees. The whispers grew more distinct, swirling around him like an invisible thread guiding his way. Whatever the wind was hiding, Leo felt deep down that it was connected to Grandma Rose\u2019s disappearance. \n\nHe turned back to Tess, who was biting her lip, excitement mixed with apprehension. \u201cAre you ready for an adventure?\u201d \n\n\u201cMore than ready!\u201d she squealed, her fear evaporating as her adventurous spirit took hold. \n\nWith hearts pounding and the wind at their backs, they ventured into the unknown, following the whispers that promised answers and perhaps something even more magical.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they stepped deeper into the forest, the trees loomed large, their branches thick and twisted. Leo glanced back at Tess, who was peering wide-eyed at everything around her. The night was falling fast, but the whispers of the wind seemed to guide their path, weaving through the shadows, leading them toward a mystery that was begging to be unraveled.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Leo hear that he believes is guiding him?","options":["A bird singing","The wind whispering","Grandma calling him","A rustling in the bushes"],"correct_answer":"The wind whispering"},{"question":"What is Tess's initial reaction to the idea of following the wind?","options":["She thinks it's a great idea","She is scared","She is skeptical","She wants to go home"],"correct_answer":"She is skeptical"},{"question":"Where are Leo and Tess camping?","options":["In their backyard","At Cedarwood Forest","In a national park","By a lake"],"correct_answer":"At Cedarwood Forest"},{"question":"How does Leo feel about his grandmother's absence during the trip?","options":["He doesn't care","He feels excited","He feels worried","He feels angry"],"correct_answer":"He feels worried"},{"question":"What does the forest seem to promise as Leo and Tess venture deeper?","options":["A safe journey","An unexpected adventure","A picnic","A scary encounter"],"correct_answer":"An unexpected adventure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_264_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_264_ch1_img1.png","plot_264_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":611,"reading_level":"Builder"}
