   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_7_10","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Ava was excited for the day ahead. It was a sunny Monday morning at Maplewood Middle School. The school was big and bright, filled with laughter and chatter. Kids rushed through the halls, their backpacks bouncing. Ava loved the buzz of her school, but today felt different.\n\n\u201cHave you seen Ben?\u201d Ava asked her friend, Mia. Ben was her classmate and a good friend. He always made everyone laugh with his jokes. But today, he was missing.\n\n\u201cNo, I haven\u2019t seen him since Friday,\u201d Mia replied, worry creeping into her voice. Ava frowned. Something didn\u2019t feel right. \n\nJust then, Lily, Ben\u2019s sister, rushed into the school. She had eyes like bright blue marbles, full of determination. \u201cHave you guys seen Ben?\u201d she asked, almost shouting. \n\nAva shook her head. \u201cNo, we were just talking about him. I hope he\u2019s okay.\u201d \n\nLily looked even more worried. \u201cI have to find him! He wouldn\u2019t just disappear.\u201d \n\nAva felt a spark of courage. \u201cLet\u2019s look for clues! Maybe he left something behind.\u201d \n\nAs they walked towards the lockers, Ava noticed a small, old journal lying on the floor. It was covered in dust and looked very mysterious. She picked it up. \u201cWhat\u2019s this?\u201d she asked. \n\nLily leaned closer. \u201cIt looks like a diary. It could be important!\u201d \n\n\u201cYes! It might have clues about where Ben is!\u201d Ava exclaimed. \n\nThey opened the journal and looked inside. The pages were filled with strange drawings and scribbles. Some pages were torn, and words were hard to read. Ava felt her heart race. \n\n\u201cThis is it!\u201d she said with excitement. \u201cWe have to figure this out!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud crash behind them. It was just a bunch of kids playing, but it made them jump. \u201cLet\u2019s find a quiet place to read this,\u201d Lily suggested. \n\nThey hurried to the empty art room, where the walls were colorful with paintings. They spread the journal out on a table and began to read. \n\nAva pointed at a drawing of a tree. \u201cWhat if this is a clue? Do you think it means something?\u201d \n\nLily nodded, biting her lip. \u201cI hope so. We need to hurry. Ben could be in trouble!\u201d \n\nThey spent the next few minutes studying the journal carefully. Ava felt a mix of excitement and fear. The mystery was just beginning. Would they find Ben before it was too late?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who is missing at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["Ava","Mia","Ben","Lily"],"correct_answer":"Ben"},{"question":"What do Ava and Lily find on the floor?","options":["A backpack","A notebook","A journal","A book"],"correct_answer":"A journal"},{"question":"What do they decide to do with the journal?","options":["Throw it away","Read it for clues","Hide it","Give it to a teacher"],"correct_answer":"Read it for clues"},{"question":"How does Ava feel when she finds the journal?","options":["Scared","Excited","Bored","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"Where do they go to read the journal?","options":["The library","The playground","The art room","The cafeteria"],"correct_answer":"The art room"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_265_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_265_ch1_img1.png","plot_265_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":405,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
