   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_7_10","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Ava and Lily hurried through the school halls. The chatter of students filled the air. But today, it felt different. Today, they were on a mission.\n\n\u201cDid you read any of the journal?\u201d Ava asked, clutching it tightly. She was nervous but excited.\n\n\u201cI peeked at a few pages,\u201d Lily replied. \u201cThere are strange drawings and notes. I think they\u2019re clues!\u201d\n\nThey reached their favorite spot, the old art room. It was a little messy but cozy. Paintings were scattered everywhere. This room was their secret hideout. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAva looked around. \u201cWe should figure out what these clues mean. Ben needs us!\u201d\n\nLily nodded, determination shining in her eyes. \u201cLet\u2019s start with the first page.\u201d She opened the journal and pointed to a drawing of a tree.\n\n\u201cThis looks like the big oak tree in the courtyard,\u201d Ava said. \u201cRemember where we used to play?\u201d\n\n\u201cYes! It\u2019s a perfect spot to hide something,\u201d Lily exclaimed. \u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d\n\nThe girls raced to the courtyard. The sun was shining, and the tree stood tall and proud. They searched around the trunk but found nothing.\n\n\u201cWait,\u201d Ava said, squinting at something shiny. \u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d\n\nLily leaned closer. \u201cIt looks like a piece of paper!\u201d\n\nAva quickly grabbed it. The paper had strange symbols and a drawing of a compass. \u201cWhat does it mean?\u201d\n\n\u201cI think it\u2019s telling us to go north!\u201d Lily said, looking excited. \u201cBut which way is north?\u201d\n\nAva looked around. The school was big, and the courtyard was buzzing with kids. She felt a flutter of fear. \u201cWhat if we can\u2019t find Ben in time?\u201d\n\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry,\u201d Lily said, squeezing Ava\u2019s hand. \u201cWe\u2019ll figure it out together!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a loud bell rang, signaling the end of lunch. Students began to scatter in all directions. Ava felt the urgency rise in her chest. They had to hurry!\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check the library,\u201d Ava suggested. \u201cIt might help us decode the symbols!\u201d\n\nAs they ran back inside, they heard a familiar voice. It was Mr. Thompson, the grumpy math teacher. \u201cYou two! Where are you rushing off to?\u201d\n\nLily gulped. \u201cUm, we\u2019re just going to the library!\u201d \n\nMr. Thompson raised an eyebrow. \u201cMake sure you stay out of trouble!\u201d\n\n\u201cOf course!\u201d Ava said, forcing a smile. Once he turned away, the girls hurried down the hall.\n\n\u201cWhat if Mr. Thompson knows something?\u201d Lily wondered.\n\n\u201cWe can\u2019t think like that,\u201d Ava replied. \u201cLet\u2019s focus on the clues!\u201d\n\nThey burst into the library, their hearts racing with excitement. The mystery was thick in the air. The journal was their only hope to find Ben.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find a quiet corner to work,\u201d Ava suggested, scanning the rows of books.\n\nAs they settled at a table, they opened the journal again. The next clue awaited them, and they had to solve it fast!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Ava and Lily find at the oak tree?","options":["A treasure chest","A piece of paper","A book","A toy"],"correct_answer":"A piece of paper"},{"question":"What does Lily think the drawing of the tree represents?","options":["A clue","A game","A secret","A warning"],"correct_answer":"A clue"},{"question":"Where do Ava and Lily decide to go to decode the clues?","options":["The playground","The library","The gym","The art room"],"correct_answer":"The library"},{"question":"How do Ava and Lily feel about their mission?","options":["Nervous","Excited","Bored","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What does Mr. Thompson warn Ava and Lily about?","options":["To be quiet","To stay out of trouble","To leave school","To go home"],"correct_answer":"To stay out of trouble"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_265_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_265_ch2_img1.png","plot_265_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":482,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
