   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_7_10","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ava and Lily rushed into the library, the smell of old books filling the air. Shelves towered high, and the soft light made everything look magical. Ava clutched the mysterious journal tight. \n\n\u201cWhere should we start?\u201d Lily asked, her eyes wide with determination.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check the first clue again,\u201d Ava suggested. They sat at a big, round table, covered in books and papers. \n\nAva flipped open the journal. \u201cIt says here, \u2018Where knowledge lies, a path is clear. Search beneath the starlit sphere.\u2019 What does that mean?\u201d\n\nLily frowned. \u201cA starlit sphere? Is it talking about a globe?\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe,\u201d Ava said, glancing around the library. \u201cLook! There\u2019s a big globe by the window!\u201d \n\nThey both jumped up and hurried over to the globe. It was shiny and spun easily. Ava gave it a good twist. \u201cIf we look under it, maybe we\u2019ll find something!\u201d\n\nThey knelt down and peered under the globe. But all they found was a dust bunny. \u201cEw! Gross!\u201d Lily giggled. \n\nSuddenly, Ava noticed something shiny on the floor. \u201cWait! What\u2019s that?\u201d \n\nLily squinted. \u201cIt looks like a key!\u201d \n\nAva picked it up, amazed. \u201cCould this be the key to finding Ben?\u201d \n\nJust then, the library door creaked open. Ava\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s a teacher?\u201d \n\nLily whispered, \u201cQuick! Hide!\u201d \n\nThey ducked behind a shelf, holding their breath. A tall figure entered. It was Mr. Thompson, the science teacher. He walked past them, looking grumpy. \n\n\u201cPhew! That was close!\u201d Ava whispered once Mr. Thompson was out of sight. \n\nThey stood up and exchanged nervous smiles. \u201cLet\u2019s keep searching,\u201d Lily said, her voice steady. \u201cMaybe the next clue is nearby.\u201d\n\nWith the key in her pocket and excitement in her heart, Ava felt ready for anything. \n\nSuddenly, Ava remembered something. \u201cThe oak tree! We need to go back there!\u201d \n\n\u201cRight!\u201d Lily agreed. \u201cWe can\u2019t give up now!\u201d\n\nAs they hurried out of the library, Ava felt the weight of the key. What secrets would it unlock? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe library scene filled with books, shelves, and Ava and Lily standing by the big globe. Ava holds the journal while Lily points excitedly at the globe. The atmosphere is lively and colorful, with sunlight streaming through the windows.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAva and Lily crouched behind a bookshelf, looking worried yet curious. The library is quiet and mysterious, with shadows cast by the tall shelves. Mr. Thompson, the science teacher, can be seen in the background, adding to the suspense.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ava and Lily find under the globe?","options":["A book","A key","A map","A toy"],"correct_answer":"A key"},{"question":"Who almost catches Ava and Lily in the library?","options":["The principal","Mr. Thompson","Ben","A librarian"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Thompson"},{"question":"What is the first clue in the journal about?","options":["A secret door","A starlit sphere","A hidden book","A treasure chest"],"correct_answer":"A starlit sphere"},{"question":"What do Ava and Lily plan to do next?","options":["Go home","Search for more keys","Head back to the oak tree","Tell a teacher"],"correct_answer":"Head back to the oak tree"},{"question":"How do Ava and Lily feel when they find the key?","options":["Scared","Tired","Excited","Confused"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":null,"word_count":423,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
