   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_7_10","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Ava and Lily stood in the school basement. It was dark, and the air felt cool. They clutched the shiny key and the silver bracelet. \n\n\u201cWhat if this bracelet belongs to Ben?\u201d Lily asked, her eyes wide with worry.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check the journal again!\u201d Ava replied. She opened the mysterious journal. The pages were filled with Ben's neat handwriting. A new clue caught her eye. \n\n\u201cIt says here, \u2018Under the oak, where secrets sleep, the answer lies, and promises keep.\u2019\u201d Ava read aloud.\n\nLily frowned. \u201cThe oak tree! We need to go there now!\u201d\n\nThey rushed out of the basement. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nOutside, the sun shone bright. The schoolyard was buzzing with kids playing. Ava and Lily hurried to the large oak tree. Its branches stretched high. They could see the leaves rustling like whispers.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Ava pointed. \u201cThere\u2019s something under the tree!\u201d\n\nThey knelt down. There, half-buried in the dirt, was a small box. It looked old and dusty. \n\n\u201cOpen it, Ava!\u201d Lily urged.\n\nWith trembling hands, Ava opened the box. Inside, they found a crumpled note. It read, \u201cHelp me! I\u2019m trapped!\u201d\n\n\u201cOh no!\u201d Lily gasped. \u201cBen must be in trouble!\u201d\n\n\u201cBut where is he?\u201d Ava wondered aloud. \n\nJust then, they heard a familiar voice. \u201cHey! What are you doing?\u201d It was their friend Mia, standing by the swing set.\n\n\u201cMia! We\u2019re looking for Ben!\u201d Lily cried. \n\nMia rushed over. \u201cI saw him near the old storage shed. He didn\u2019t look happy!\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Ava said, determination in her voice.\n\nThey raced across the playground, hearts pounding. The storage shed was old and covered with vines. It looked spooky but also a little exciting.\n\n\u201cDo you think Ben is in there?\u201d Lily whispered.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we have to check,\u201d Ava replied.\n\nThey opened the door slowly. Inside, it was dark. But then\u2014 \n\n\u201cBen!\u201d Ava shouted. And there he was, sitting on the floor, looking scared but safe.\n\n\u201cAva! Lily! I\u2019m so glad to see you!\u201d Ben said, jumping up.\n\n\u201cWhat happened?\u201d Lily asked, running to him.\n\n\u201cI was hiding from a prankster. I didn\u2019t mean to worry you,\u201d Ben explained, relief washing over his face.\n\nAva smiled. \u201cYou scared us! But we found the clues and the box because of you.\u201d\n\nThey all laughed, feeling the weight lift off their shoulders. Friends were meant to stick together, through thick and thin.\n\nAs they walked back to the school, Ava felt happy. They had solved the mystery. And they learned that friendship was the strongest clue of all. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cNext time, let\u2019s just hang out instead of getting into trouble!\u201d Ben chuckled.\n\n\u201cDeal!\u201d Lily said, grinning. \n\nTogether, they walked toward the sun, ready for their next adventure.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Ava and Lily find under the oak tree?","options":["A box","A ball","A book","A toy"],"correct_answer":"A box"},{"question":"Why was Ben hiding?","options":["He was playing a game","He was lost","He was scared of a prankster","He was studying"],"correct_answer":"He was scared of a prankster"},{"question":"What did Ava and Lily discover in the box?","options":["A letter","A toy","A picture","A map"],"correct_answer":"A letter"},{"question":"Who saw Ben near the old storage shed?","options":["Mia","Lily","Ava","The teacher"],"correct_answer":"Mia"},{"question":"What is the main lesson of this chapter?","options":["Don't hide","Friendship is important","Always play games","Stay in school"],"correct_answer":"Friendship is important"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_265_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_265_ch5_img1.png","plot_265_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":461,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
