   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_11_14","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Ava Parker stood at the edge of the bustling schoolyard, watching the sea of students hustle between classes. The sun hung high, casting warm, golden rays that danced on the pavement, but Ava felt a chill creeping up her spine. Something was off today, and she couldn\u2019t shake the uneasy feeling lodged in her stomach like a stone.\n\n\u201cHave you seen Ben?\u201d Lily, Ben\u2019s sister, rushed up to Ava, her brown hair bouncing wildly as she spoke. Her usually cheerful face was clouded with worry, and her bright eyes darted around, searching the crowd as if Ben might materialize right in front of her.\n\nAva shook her head. \u201cNo, I thought he was with you.\u201d\n\nLily\u2019s lips pressed into a thin line. \u201cHe didn\u2019t come home last night. Mom\u2019s freaking out.\u201d\n\nAva felt a knot tighten in her chest. Ben was one of the good ones\u2014helpful, funny, and always ready to lend a hand. The idea that he was missing was like a dark cloud rolling in, casting shadows over their ordinary middle school life. \u201cMaybe he just stayed at a friend\u2019s house.\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe,\u201d Lily said, her voice tinged with disbelief. \u201cBut... I called everyone. No one has seen him since school yesterday.\u201d\n\nJust then, a shrill bell rang, signaling the end of lunch. Students started to disperse, the laughter and chatter swirling around Ava and Lily like wind pushing leaves. But instead of heading to class, Ava felt a pull\u2014something deeper than curiosity, like a magnet drawing her closer to the truth.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check his locker,\u201d Ava suggested, glancing at the looming brick school building. The thought of prying into Ben\u2019s things felt wrong, yet a flicker of determination sparked in her heart.\n\n\u201cOkay,\u201d Lily replied, her voice steeling with resolve. \u201cHe wouldn\u2019t just disappear. There has to be a reason.\u201d\n\nThey made their way through the crowded hallways, the scent of old books and chalk dust filling the air. As they approached Ben's locker, Ava noticed the usual jumbled mess of sticky notes and doodles had disappeared. Instead, it stood almost eerily pristine\u2014its metal surface reflecting the fluorescent lights above.\n\nAva knelt down, feeling a rush of adrenaline. \u201cHelp me open it?\u201d \n\nLily nodded, her hands trembling slightly as she turned the dial. \u201cWhat if we find something\u2026 weird?\u201d\n\n\u201cOr something that helps us find him,\u201d Ava whispered, her heart racing with a mix of fear and excitement. With a final click, the locker swung open, revealing a jumble of books and\u2026 a journal. It was battered and worn, its leather cover crinkled like an old map. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Lily exclaimed, lifting it out. As she opened it, the pages fluttered like wings, revealing hurried scribbles and odd drawings. Ava leaned over, her mind racing with possibilities. Could this journal hold the clues they needed?\n\nSuddenly, a noise echoed down the hallway\u2014a shout, mixed with laughter, that turned their attention. Ava looked up, her heart pounding. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d \n\nLily nodded, her expression shifting from determination to alarm. \u201cThat sounded like it came from\u2026 the basement!\u201d\n\nAva glanced at the journal in Lily\u2019s hands, feeling the weight of the mystery pressing down on her. They had to find out what Ben knew. \u201cWe should check it out,\u201d she said, her voice steady despite the tremor in her hands.\n\nAs they exchanged glances, a shared understanding passed between them. They were in this together, and they wouldn\u2019t stop until they found Ben, no matter what secrets lay ahead.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAva and Lily stand near Ben's empty locker, a sense of urgency surrounding them, with students bustling past. The locker door is open, revealing the journal inside, while Ava kneels in front of it, and Lily stands close, her eyes wide with concern.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAva and Lily are peering at the journal, surrounded by the school\u2019s dimly lit hall with shadows stretching out behind them. A sense of discovery and tension hangs in the air as they prepare to dive into the mystery contained within its pages.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is Ava's initial feeling when she arrives at school?","options":["Excitement","Fear","Curiosity","Joy"],"correct_answer":"Fear"},{"question":"Why is Lily worried when she meets Ava?","options":["She lost her lunch","Ben went missing","She forgot her homework","She failed a test"],"correct_answer":"Ben went missing"},{"question":"What do Ava and Lily find in Ben\u2019s locker?","options":["A letter","A book","A journal","A photo"],"correct_answer":"A journal"},{"question":"What does Ava suggest they do to find Ben?","options":["Go to class","Check the journal","Visit the library","Ask teachers"],"correct_answer":"Check the journal"},{"question":"What does the sound they hear in the hallway signify?","options":["Students playing","Someone in trouble","The end of class","An announcement"],"correct_answer":"Someone in trouble"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_265_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_265_ch1_img1.png","plot_265_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":685,"reading_level":"Builder"}
