   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_11_14","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Ava Parker took a deep breath as she entered Lincoln Middle School. The bustling hallways rang with laughter and chatter, but there was an underlying tension in the air. Her heart raced as she thought about Ben. Where could he possibly be? She glanced at the familiar faces of her classmates, their carefree smiles contrasting sharply with her worry. \n\nJust then, she spotted Lily leaning against a locker, her arms crossed tightly. The determination in her eyes set Ava\u2019s mind at ease, if only a little. \u201cDid you find anything in the journal?\u201d Lily asked, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\nAva nodded, clutching the leather-bound book to her chest. \u201cThere are some strange notes, but I think we might be onto something.\u201d \n\nThey stepped into a quieter corner of the hall, where the sunlight filtered through the windows, casting patterns on the floor. Ava opened the journal, and they leaned in closer. \u201cLook at this,\u201d she pointed to a scribbled line. \u201cIt says, \u2018Under the bleachers, where secrets breathe.\u2019 What do you think that means?\u201d\n\nLily frowned, her brow furrowing in concentration. \u201cThe gym? We should check there. It\u2019s the only place with bleachers.\u201d \n\nAs they hurried down the hall, they encountered a group of students, laughing and whispering amongst themselves. Ava felt a wave of unease wash over her. Those kids had always been a little\u2026 mean. They were the kind to tease others without a second thought. \u201cDo you think they know anything about Ben?\u201d Ava asked, glancing at Lily. \n\n\u201cMaybe,\u201d Lily replied, but her voice lacked conviction. \n\nJust then, a loud shout erupted from the group. \u201cLook, it\u2019s the Missing Kid\u2019s best friend!\u201d one of the boys jeered, pointing at Ava. \u201cWhat\u2019s it like, knowing you\u2019ll never see him again?\u201d \n\nAva's face flushed with embarrassment, anger bubbling in her chest. Before she could respond, Lily stepped forward. \u201cStop it! You don\u2019t know anything!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, Lily\u2019s fierce defense only seemed to fuel their taunts. Ava grabbed Lily\u2019s arm. \u201cLet\u2019s just go. We have more important things to do.\u201d \n\nThey turned to walk away, but not before Ava caught a glimpse of something shiny on the floor, near the lockers. \u201cWait!\u201d she exclaimed, kneeling down. It was a small, silver key. \n\n\u201cWhat do you think it opens?\u201d Lily asked, her curiosity piqued. \n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s connected to the journal!\u201d Ava replied, her excitement returning. \n\nWith renewed determination, they made their way to the gym. When they arrived, the space felt larger than life, echoing their footsteps as they approached the bleachers. They exchanged nervous glances, but they knew they couldn\u2019t turn back now. \n\nAs they crawled under the bleachers, musty air filled their lungs. \u201cIt\u2019s dark in here,\u201d Lily whispered, shivering slightly. \n\nAva flicked on her phone\u2019s flashlight, illuminating dusty corners and forgotten objects. There, in the shadows, a box lay hidden. Ava's heart leaped. \u201cThis must be it! It could hold more clues!\u201d \n\nJust as Ava reached for it, a loud noise echoed from above. Footsteps. \u201cSomeone\u2019s coming!\u201d Lily squeaked, her eyes wide with fear.\n\n\u201cQuick, hide!\u201d Ava urged, diving behind the bleachers. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe girls huddled together, hearts pounding in sync as the footsteps grew louder. They could hear laughter\u2014mocking, familiar laughter. Ava\u2019s stomach dropped. It was the group of students from earlier. Had they followed them?\n\nSuddenly, the laughter stopped, and one of the boys called out, \u201cHey! What\u2019re you doing under there? Come out!\u201d\n\nAva exchanged a terrified glance with Lily. There was no way they could let them discover their secret. \n\n\u201cStay quiet,\u201d Ava whispered, her voice trembling. \n\nThe tension hung thick in the air. Would they be discovered? The fate of their mission rested on the next few moments, and Ava could feel the weight of her courage slipping away.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ava and Lily find under the bleachers?","options":["A journal","A silver key","A hidden box","A school trophy"],"correct_answer":"A hidden box"},{"question":"What does the group of students taunt Ava about?","options":["Her grades","Ben's disappearance","Her outfit","Her friendship with Lily"],"correct_answer":"Ben's disappearance"},{"question":"Where do Ava and Lily believe the first clue leads them?","options":["The library","The gym","The cafeteria","The playground"],"correct_answer":"The gym"},{"question":"How does Ava feel when the group of students confronts them?","options":["Happy","Angry","Indifferent","Excited"],"correct_answer":"Angry"},{"question":"What is the main conflict in this chapter?","options":["Finding Ben","Decoding the journal","Avoiding bullies","Exploring the gym"],"correct_answer":"Avoiding bullies"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_265_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_265_ch2_img1.png","plot_265_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":648,"reading_level":"Builder"}
