   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_11_14","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ava and Lily stood in the shadowy corner of the school library, the musty smell of old books wrapping around them like a blanket. Sunlight streamed through dusty windows, illuminating the countless volumes lining the shelves, but their focus was on a single, mysterious journal resting on the table before them. \n\n\u201cWhat if this is just a wild goose chase?\u201d Lily whispered, her fingers nervously tapping the edge of the journal. \u201cWhat if we don\u2019t find Ben after all?\u201d\n\nAva glanced at Lily, her heart racing with a mix of fear and determination. \u201cWe have to try. The last clue led us here for a reason. Remember what it said\u2014\u2018In shadows where the stories lie, the truth awaits beneath the sky?\u2019 It must mean something!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAva\u2019s mind raced as she flipped through the journal\u2019s weathered pages filled with Ben\u2019s neat handwriting. \u201cIt feels like he\u2019s talking to us,\u201d she said, pointing to a line that read, \"Seek the hidden room where secrets bloom.\u201d \n\n\u201cHidden room?\u201d Lily frowned. \u201cWe don\u2019t even have a map of this place, and this school is full of rumors. What if it\u2019s all just stories?\u201d\n\n\u201cOr what if it\u2019s leading us to Ben?\u201d Ava replied, her voice firm. \u201cWe can\u2019t give up; we\u2019re so close.\u201d\n\nLily took a deep breath, her shoulders squared as she leaned over the journal. \u201cOkay, what\u2019s our next move?\u201d\n\nAs if in response, a sudden noise echoed through the library\u2014footsteps, and then laughter. Ava\u2019s stomach twisted. \u201cWe need to hide!\u201d\n\nThey ducked behind a high shelf just as a group of popular kids strolled in, their voices ringing out like alarm bells. \u201cI can\u2019t believe they\u2019re still looking for Ben,\u201d one boy scoffed. \u201cHe probably just didn\u2019t want to face the science test.\u201d\n\nAva clenched her fists, anger bubbling inside her. \u201cHow can they be so cruel?\u201d \n\n\u201cShh!\u201d Lily hissed. \u201cListen!\u201d\n\nThe laughter faded, replaced by the sound of books slamming shut. \u201cLet\u2019s check the gym; maybe they found him there,\u201d another girl suggested. \n\n\u201cThat\u2019s our cue!\u201d Ava whispered urgently. \u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d\n\nThey crept out from their hiding spot, glancing around to ensure the coast was clear. As they raced toward the gym, the journal clutched tightly in Ava\u2019s hands, her heart pounded with both excitement and fear. What if they found Ben? What if they didn\u2019t? \n\nAt the gym, a heavy metal door marked \u201cSTAFF ONLY\u201d caught Ava\u2019s eye. \u201cWhat about that door?\u201d she said, pointing. \u201cIt could be the hidden room!\u201d\n\nLily peered at it, biting her lip. \u201cBut what if it\u2019s locked?\u201d\n\nAva stepped closer, her mind racing. \u201cWe\u2019ll never know unless we try. Come on!\u201d\n\nWith a deep breath, Ava pushed open the door. It creaked ominously, revealing a dark, cluttered storage room filled with old sports equipment and a hint of something musty. The air felt electric as they stepped inside. \n\nSuddenly, they heard a soft thud from the far corner. Lily gasped. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d\n\nAva turned, her heart pounding. \u201cI don\u2019t know, but we have to find out!\u201d\n\nAs they approached the source of the sound, a shadow flickered in the corner of their eyes. \u201cBen?\u201d Ava called out, her voice trembling with hope.\n\nThe darkness shifted, and they caught a glimpse of something\u2014a glint of metal? Ava\u2019s breath hitched as she realized it was a small, locked box. \u201cThis must be it,\u201d she said, her eyes wide with realization. \u201cWhatever it is, it could lead us to Ben!\u201d\n\nBut before they could reach it, the door slammed shut behind them, plunging them into darkness. \n\n\u201cUh-oh,\u201d Lily whispered, panic rising in her voice. \u201cWe\u2019re trapped!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAva felt a chill run down her spine as she turned toward the door, pounding on it. \u201cLet us out!\u201d she shouted, but her voice echoed back at them, swallowed by silence. They were alone, and time was running out.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ava and Lily discover in the library?","options":["A hidden map","Ben's journal","A treasure chest","A lost dog"],"correct_answer":"Ben's journal"},{"question":"What do Ava and Lily hear that makes them hide?","options":["A teacher's voice","Footsteps and laughter","A loud crash","A school bell ringing"],"correct_answer":"Footsteps and laughter"},{"question":"What do they find in the storage room?","options":["A hidden diary","A locked box","A broken window","A secret passage"],"correct_answer":"A locked box"},{"question":"How do Ava and Lily feel when they realize they are trapped?","options":["Excited","Bored","Happy","Panicked"],"correct_answer":"Panicked"},{"question":"What emotion does Ava show when she finds the journal's clues?","options":["Disinterest","Fear","Determination","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Determination"}]},"images":null,"word_count":674,"reading_level":"Builder"}
