   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_11_14","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Ava and Lily stood outside the library, their hearts pounding with anticipation. The large oak doors loomed in front of them, ancient and mysterious, just like the secrets they hoped to uncover. Sunlight filtered through the tall windows, casting playful patterns on the floor. They shared a determined glance, ready to face whatever lay inside.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see what else the journal has to reveal,\u201d Ava said, clutching the leather-bound book in her hands. The smell of old paper filled the air, a comforting yet eerie scent that sent shivers down her spine. As they stepped inside, the quiet rustle of pages and the faint scent of dust seemed to whisper secrets of their own.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe library was more than just shelves filled with books; it was a labyrinth of knowledge, with hidden corners and cozy nooks. Ava remembered the first clue in the journal: \u201cWhere stories sleep, the truth will leap.\u201d They exchanged puzzled looks, trying to decipher its meaning.\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s a hint about a specific book?\u201d Lily suggested, her brow furrowed. \u201cWhat if we check the old folktales section? That\u2019s where we found the first clue.\u201d\n\nAs they maneuvered through the aisles, they could feel the weight of the mystery pressing down on them. Suddenly, their attention was drawn to Jake and his gang, who were huddled by the entrance, exchanging mocking glances. Jake sauntered over, a smug expression plastered on his face.\n\n\u201cWell, look who it is! The detective duo,\u201d he sneered. \u201cStill trying to find your precious Ben? Good luck with that!\u201d\n\nAva felt a surge of defiance. \u201cYou don\u2019t know anything, Jake! Ben\u2019s missing, and we\u2019re going to find him.\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, right,\u201d Jake scoffed, before turning to his friends. \u201cLet\u2019s see how brave you are when you\u2019re trapped in the library\u2019s secret room!\u201d\n\nBefore Ava could respond, Jake and his friends darted down a hidden staircase at the back of the library, laughter echoing through the aisles. Ava and Lily exchanged glances, their curiosity ignited.\n\n\u201cSecret room?\u201d Ava whispered, her heart racing. \u201cWe have to check it out!\u201d\n\nThey hurried after Jake, descending the creaking staircase, hoping to find answers\u2014and Ben. At the bottom, they found a heavy door, locked tight. Ava pulled out the journal, flipping through its pages until she found what looked like a keyhole sketch.\n\n\u201cMaybe this is the key!\u201d Ava exclaimed, pointing to a drawing that resembled the door they stood before.\n\nLily knelt down, inspecting the lock. \u201cIf we can just find a way to open it\u2026\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a loud creak echoed through the dark room, and the door swung open, revealing a dimly lit chamber filled with dusty artifacts and old school projects. They stepped inside, the air thick with mystery.\n\nAs they explored, a glimmer caught Ava\u2019s eye. She rushed over to a small chest tucked beneath a table, the lock rusty but intact. With a determined breath, she pulled it open, revealing a collection of photos and notes that hinted at Ben\u2019s whereabouts.\n\nBut just as they began to piece things together, the door slammed shut behind them. They were trapped!\n\n\u201cGreat, now what?\u201d Lily exclaimed, panic rising in her voice.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Ava pointed to a nearby window. \u201cMaybe we can open it from the inside.\u201d\n\nAs they rushed to the window, a loud noise echoed from the other side of the door. The girls exchanged a worried glance, their hearts racing. They had to find a way out\u2014and fast.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith a surge of determination, they focused on the lock, knowing that the key to their freedom, and possibly to finding Ben, lay within this tangled web of secrets.\n\n\u201cWhatever happens, we\u2019re in this together,\u201d Ava said, her voice steadying as she glanced at Lily. They had come too far to give up now.\n\nThe sound of voices grew louder outside, but Ava and Lily were ready. They would face whatever challenges came their way, fueled by hope, courage, and the unbreakable bond of friendship.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What clue do Ava and Lily find in the journal about a specific location?","options":["The gym","The cafeteria","The old folktales section","The science lab"],"correct_answer":"The old folktales section"},{"question":"What does Jake say to mock Ava and Lily?","options":["They will never find Ben","They should give up","They are great detectives","They are wasting their time"],"correct_answer":"They will never find Ben"},{"question":"What happens when Ava and Lily enter the secret room?","options":["They find Ben","The door locks behind them","They discover treasure","They see their classmates"],"correct_answer":"The door locks behind them"},{"question":"What do Ava and Lily hope to find in the secret room?","options":["A way out","Clues about Ben","A treasure map","A book"],"correct_answer":"Clues about Ben"},{"question":"What is the main theme of Ava and Lily's journey in this chapter?","options":["Friendship","Winning a competition","Making new friends","Solving a puzzle"],"correct_answer":"Friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_265_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_265_ch5_img1.png","plot_265_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":677,"reading_level":"Builder"}
