   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_15_18","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Ava sat on the bleachers, her gaze drifting over the chaotic scene of Maplewood Middle School's gym. The air was thick with laughter and the sound of squeaking sneakers, yet beneath the surface energy, something felt amiss. It was Tuesday, and as far as Ava was concerned, Tuesdays were the worst. The weight of the week bore down on her, an uncomfortable reminder of the unending pressure to make the right choices while navigating the tumultuous waters of adolescence.\n\nSuddenly, her thoughts were interrupted by the unmistakable sound of a commotion near the entrance. A group of students was gathered, their whispers rising like a crescendo of anxious voices. Curiosity piqued, Ava slid off the bleachers and made her way over, her heart beating a little faster with each step. As she approached, she spotted Lily, Ben's sister, her face flushed with panic.\n\n\u201cWhere\u2019s Ben?\u201d Ava pressed, her instincts kicking in. She had known Ben since kindergarten\u2014always the one to crack a joke or lighten the mood. His absence was a gaping hole in their circle. \n\nLily, her dark hair framing her face in disarray, looked up at Ava with wide, terrified eyes. \u201cHe didn\u2019t come home last night. I thought he was just hanging out with friends, but\u2014\u201d her voice trembled. \u201cI can\u2019t reach him. He\u2019s missing.\u201d\n\nAva felt a chill creep up her spine. Ben was the type of guy who would never vanish without telling anyone, even if it was just a text. \u201cHave you told the teachers?\u201d she asked, already knowing the answer. \n\n\u201cThey said to give it some time. But\u2026 what if something\u2019s wrong?\u201d Lily\u2019s voice cracked, and the vulnerability behind her tough exterior shook Ava. She placed a reassuring hand on her shoulder, feeling a deep-seated urge to help her friend. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s look for him,\u201d Ava suggested, her mind racing. \u201cMaybe he left a clue or something.\u201d \n\nAs they began to search the school, Ava remembered the old library at the end of the hall\u2014its dusty shelves and forgotten corners. It was a treasure trove of secrets. Perhaps a hidden clue awaited them in its depths. The school felt different now, not just a maze of lockers and classrooms, but a labyrinth where the truth could be concealed.\n\nEntering the library, the musty scent of paper and ink enveloped them. Sunlight filtered through the tall, narrow windows, casting long shadows that danced on the floor. Ava's eyes roamed over the shelves, dense with books that seemed to whisper their own stories. She felt a strange pull towards the far corner, where an old table sat, littered with forgotten volumes.\n\n\u201cOver here,\u201d she called to Lily, who had been examining a stack of books nearby. Ava reached for a tattered journal that seemed to stand out among the others. The leather cover was worn, and the edges were frayed, as if it had been thumbed through many times before.\n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d Lily asked, her curiosity piqued.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but it looks like it\u2019s seen some action,\u201d Ava replied, brushing off the dust. She opened it cautiously, the pages crackling under her fingertips. The writing was messy, a hurried scrawl that hinted at urgency. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Ava pointed to a passage. The words seemed to jump off the page. \u201c'The hidden clue lies where whispers meet, beneath the gaze of the painted elite.' What do you think that means?\u201d\n\nLily frowned, her brow furrowing in thought. \u201cWhispers meet... painted elite? Maybe it\u2019s talking about the art room? There are all those portraits of the old principals and their fancy frames.\u201d\n\nAva felt a surge of excitement mixed with anxiety. \u201cLet\u2019s go\u2014fast!\u201d \n\nBefore they could leave, the door creaked open, and a tall figure stepped inside. It was Mr. Jacobs, their history teacher, his expression darkening as he spotted them. \u201cWhat are you two doing in here?\u201d\n\nAva exchanged a glance with Lily, her heart racing as she realized they might be in trouble. But the urgency of their mission outweighed the fear of being caught. \u201cWe were just looking for some research materials,\u201d Ava lied, her voice steady despite her nerves.\n\nMr. Jacobs raised an eyebrow, skepticism written all over his face. \u201cMake sure you keep it down. The library is for studying, not for running wild.\u201d\n\nAva nodded, swallowing her apprehension. As Mr. Jacobs left, she felt a mix of relief and dread. The journal was their only hope now, and the clock was ticking. They had to find Ben before it was too late.\n\nWith determination set in her eyes, Ava turned to Lily. \u201cLet\u2019s get to the art room. We need to know what this clue means.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the main reason Ava feels concerned at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["She has a test to study for.","Her friend Ben is missing.","She is not feeling well.","She has a fight with her parents."],"correct_answer":"Her friend Ben is missing."},{"question":"What does Lily reveal about her brother Ben?","options":["He has a secret plan.","He didn't come home last night.","He is at a friend's house.","He is skipping school."],"correct_answer":"He didn't come home last night."},{"question":"What clue do Ava and Lily find in the library?","options":["A map of the school.","An old journal.","A letter from Ben.","A diary of the principal."],"correct_answer":"An old journal."},{"question":"What does the clue in the journal suggest?","options":["To look in the cafeteria.","To find a hidden room in the library.","To visit the art room.","To ask the teachers for help."],"correct_answer":"To visit the art room."},{"question":"How does Mr. Jacobs react when he sees Ava and Lily in the library?","options":["He encourages them to keep looking.","He scolds them for making noise.","He offers them help.","He ignores them."],"correct_answer":"He scolds them for making noise."}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_265_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_265_ch1_img1.png","plot_265_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":795,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
