   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_265_15_18","title":"The Hidden Clue","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Missing Person","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting long shadows across the school\u2019s brick facade, Ava and Lily stood before the art room door, their hearts pounding in unison. The atmosphere felt thick, charged with anticipation and an undercurrent of fear. Ava turned to Lily, her mind racing. \u201cWhat if we\u2019re wrong? What if this is just a wild goose chase?\u201d \n\nLily\u2019s determined gaze met hers, eyes shining with fierce resolve. \u201cWe can\u2019t think like that, Ava. This journal has to lead us to Ben. It\u2019s our last chance.\u201d With a deep breath, she pushed the door open, their footsteps echoing in the dimly lit room filled with easels and half-finished canvases. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe air was tinged with the smell of paint and varnish, a nostalgic reminder of creativity that now felt hauntingly out of place. Ava scanned the room, her eyes landing on a large, colorful mural painted on the far wall. It depicted a vibrant sunset, but upon closer inspection, the colors seemed to swirl into a chaotic blend, much like the turmoil brewing within her. \n\n\u201cLook at this,\u201d she said, her voice barely above a whisper as she pointed to a corner of the mural. Beneath the vibrant strokes, a series of small symbols caught her attention\u2014arrows intertwined with spirals. \u201cDo you think these could be more clues?\u201d\n\nLily leaned closer, her brow furrowing in concentration. \u201cMaybe they mean something\u2026 or lead somewhere. We should take a picture.\u201d As Ava snapped a photo, the soft click echoed like a gunshot, amplifying their anxiety.\n\nWith newfound determination, the girls began rummaging through Ben\u2019s old art supplies, hoping to find more hidden messages. \u201cWhat about this?\u201d Lily exclaimed, pulling out a sketchbook crammed between old canvases. The cover was tattered, and it felt wrongfully intimate, as if they were stealing secrets from Ben\u2019s mind.\n\nAs they flipped through the pages, intricate sketches came to life\u2014depictions of places around the school, but something was off. Each drawing was accompanied by cryptic phrases that hinted at deeper meanings. \u201cThis one looks like the library,\u201d Ava pointed out, \u201cbut why would he draw it like this?\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the shrill ring of Lily\u2019s phone startled them both. It was a text from her mother: *\u201cLily, you need to come home now. It\u2019s urgent.\u201d*\n\n\u201cDo you have to go?\u201d Ava asked, a knot tightening in her stomach. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Lily said, biting her lip, torn between her family\u2019s call and her commitment to find Ben. \u201cI can\u2019t leave this. What if it\u2019s the last clue?\u201d \n\nAva, sensing Lily\u2019s internal struggle, reached out, placing a reassuring hand on her shoulder. \u201cWe\u2019ll figure this out. Let\u2019s decipher as much as we can now, then we can regroup.\u201d \n\nBut just then, the door creaked open, and in walked Marcus and his group of followers\u2014Ben\u2019s biggest tormentors at school. Their smirks sent a chill down Ava\u2019s spine. \n\n\u201cWhat are you two losers doing in here?\u201d Marcus sneered, stepping closer, the air thickening with tension. \u201cLooking for your little friend? He\u2019s probably better off without you.\u201d\n\n\u201cLeave us alone, Marcus,\u201d Lily fired back, her voice steady despite the uncertainty swirling in her heart. \n\nMarcus shifted his gaze to the sketchbook in Ava\u2019s hands, his expression shifting from mockery to curiosity. \u201cWhat\u2019s that? Some kind of secret diary?\u201d \n\nAva felt a surge of protectiveness. \u201cIt\u2019s not yours. Just\u2014stay away!\u201d \n\n\u201cOr what?\u201d Marcus taunted, reaching for the sketchbook. In that split second, Ava\u2019s instincts kicked in. She darted back, clutching the book to her chest. \n\nLily stepped forward, her voice fierce. \u201cYou don\u2019t want to mess with us, Marcus. This is about Ben.\u201d\n\nThe tension hung heavy in the air, a palpable standoff that seemed to stretch into eternity. Just then, the lights flickered, plunging the room into half-darkness, and the moment stretched, filled with uncertainty. \n\n\u201cRun!\u201d Ava shouted as the lights flickered again, and they bolted past Marcus and his friends, adrenaline propelling them forward. \n\nAs they escaped into the hallway, the realization hit them: they were not just racing against time; they were racing against something much darker. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cDid they see anything important?\u201d Lily panted as they reached safety, leaning against the wall to catch her breath. \n\n\u201cNo, but they\u2019re going to be on high alert now. We need to find Ben, and fast.\u201d \n\nAva\u2019s heart raced with the weight of impending danger and the sense of urgency. \u201cWe have to decode the rest of the sketchbook tonight. I feel like we\u2019re on the brink of something huge.\u201d \n\nBut as they prepared to regroup, the flicker of the lights returned to her mind, a dark omen hinting that their troubles had only just begun.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ava first suggest they do in the art room?","options":["Take pictures of all the art","Leave the room immediately","Search for hidden messages","Draw their own mural"],"correct_answer":"Search for hidden messages"},{"question":"What urgent message does Lily receive while in the art room?","options":["Ben has been found","There\u2019s been an emergency at home","They need to leave the school","Marcus is coming"],"correct_answer":"There\u2019s been an emergency at home"},{"question":"Who interrupts Ava and Lily's investigation in the art room?","options":["Ben's friends","Their teachers","Marcus and his followers","The principal"],"correct_answer":"Marcus and his followers"},{"question":"What do Ava and Lily decide to do when confronted by Marcus?","options":["Apologize and leave","Stand their ground","Call for help","Ignore him"],"correct_answer":"Stand their ground"},{"question":"What realization do Ava and Lily come to at the end of this chapter?","options":["They should give up on finding Ben","They are racing against dark forces","They need to tell the teachers","They can only trust each other"],"correct_answer":"They are racing against dark forces"}]},"images":null,"word_count":810,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
