   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_256_7_10","title":"The Case of the Missing Homework","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Ava stood in front of Sunnyvale Middle School. The sun shone brightly, and the air buzzed with excitement. Today was the big day\u2014the science fair! Ava couldn\u2019t wait to show her project. She had worked so hard on it.\n\n\u201cHey, Ava!\u201d Leo called, running up to her. His glasses were slipping down his nose, and he had a big grin on his face. \u201cAre you ready for the fair?\u201d\n\n\u201cReady as I\u2019ll ever be!\u201d Ava replied. She reached into her backpack to take out her project. But when she looked inside, her heart sank. The backpack was empty!\n\n\u201cWhat?! Where\u2019s my homework?\u201d Ava gasped, her eyes wide.\n\nLeo adjusted his glasses. \u201cDid you check the bottom?\u201d\n\n\u201cYes! It\u2019s not there!\u201d Ava said, panic rising in her voice. \u201cThe science fair starts in one hour!\u201d\n\nLeo scratched his head. \u201cDon\u2019t worry! We can solve this mystery together. Where do you think it could be?\u201d\n\nAva thought hard. \u201cI last had it in Ms. Thompson's class! We need to go back!\u201d\n\nThey rushed down the hallway, dodging students and posters. The walls were decorated with colorful drawings and science fair banners. It felt like a maze. Together, they pushed through the crowd.\n\nSuddenly, they heard a giggle. Ava turned and spotted Lucy, a mischievous classmate, hiding behind a locker. \u201cLooking for something, Ava?\u201d she asked, winking.\n\n\u201cUh, no!\u201d Ava replied, trying to sound confident. But Leo stepped closer.\n\n\u201cWait! Did you see my homework?\u201d he demanded.\n\nLucy shrugged, but her smile was too wide. \u201cMaybe I did! But it\u2019s a secret!\u201d\n\nAva frowned. \u201cLucy, we need it for the fair. Can you help us?\u201d\n\nLucy thought for a moment. \u201cI might know something. Meet me at the art room in ten minutes!\u201d Then, she dashed away.\n\n\u201cDo you think she has a clue?\u201d Ava asked, anxiety bubbling in her stomach.\n\n\u201cShe might! Let\u2019s hurry!\u201d Leo shouted, and they raced toward the art room, hearts pounding.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they reached the art room door, Ava felt a mix of hope and worry. What would they find?\n\n\u201cReady?\u201d Leo whispered, taking a deep breath.\n\n\u201cReady,\u201d Ava answered, her determination lighting up her eyes.\n\nThey opened the door slowly. The room was filled with bright paint and colorful crafts. \u201cLucy?\u201d Ava called. \u201cAre you here?\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nLeo looked around, his eyes darting from one colorful project to another. \u201cI hope she\u2019s not playing a trick on us!\u201d he said, biting his lip.\n\nAva nodded. \u201cWe have to find my homework before it\u2019s too late!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ava find missing in her backpack?","options":["Her lunch","A pencil","Her homework","A book"],"correct_answer":"Her homework"},{"question":"Who is Ava's best friend?","options":["Lucy","Ms. Thompson","Leo","Mr. Smith"],"correct_answer":"Leo"},{"question":"What does Lucy say she might know?","options":["Where the homework is","A secret code","A riddle","A new game"],"correct_answer":"Where the homework is"},{"question":"What is the main setting of the story?","options":["The park","Sunnyvale Middle School","A library","A coffee shop"],"correct_answer":"Sunnyvale Middle School"},{"question":"What do Ava and Leo need to do before the fair starts?","options":["Finish their lunch","Find Ava's homework","Play a game","Help their teacher"],"correct_answer":"Find Ava's homework"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_256_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_256_ch1_img1.png","plot_256_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":431,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
