   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_256_7_10","title":"The Case of the Missing Homework","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Ava and Leo entered Sunnyvale Middle School, buzzing with excitement. Posters for the science fair covered the walls. \u201cLook at all these projects!\u201d Ava pointed at a colorful volcano model. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cYeah, but none will be as cool as your robot fish!\u201d Leo grinned, his eyes shining. Ava felt a little better. She loved her robot fish! It swam and danced, and she worked on it for weeks. \n\nAs they walked to their classroom, Ava's heart raced. \u201cWhat if my homework is lost for good?\u201d she worried. Leo scratched his head. \u201cMaybe we should check the lost and found first!\u201d \n\nThey hurried to the lost and found. It was a big box filled with old lunch boxes and mismatched socks. \u201cEww!\u201d Leo exclaimed, lifting a pair of purple socks. \u201cNot this!\u201d \n\nAva laughed. \u201cI don\u2019t think my homework will be in there!\u201d They dug through the box, but all they found were forgotten items. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s think!\u201d Leo said, tapping his chin. \u201cWhere did you last have your homework?\u201d \n\n\u201cI had it in my backpack before lunch,\u201d Ava replied, her eyes widening. \u201cBut I also showed it to Ms. Thompson after school!\u201d \n\n\u201cThen that\u2019s our next stop!\u201d Leo declared. They raced to the science room, dodging students. \n\nWhen they burst through the door, Ms. Thompson was busy setting up her own project. \u201cMs. Thompson!\u201d Ava called out. \u201cDid you see my homework?\u201d \n\nThe teacher turned, her glasses slipping down her nose. \u201cHmm, I might have seen it,\u201d she mused. \u201cBut it was with the green slime project.\u201d \n\n\u201cGreen slime?\u201d Leo repeated, bouncing on his feet. \u201cThat\u2019s a bit messy!\u201d \n\n\u201cExactly. It was very bouncy!\u201d Ms. Thompson chuckled. \n\nAva groaned. \u201cOh no! If it's mixed with the slime, it could be ruined!\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go find it!\u201d Leo urged, grabbing Ava's hand. \n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud SPLAT! They turned to see a giant blob of green slime flying through the air. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s all over the place!\u201d Ava shouted. \u201cWe need to be careful!\u201d \n\nAs they ducked, they noticed a sparkly object glinting in the slime. \u201cCould it be your homework?\u201d Leo asked, eyes wide with hope. \n\n\u201cMaybe!\u201d Ava said, her heart racing again. \u201cBut how will we get it?\u201d \n\nWith time running short, they knew they had to think fast.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Where do Ava and Leo first look for the homework?","options":["The library","The lost and found","Ms. Thompson's desk","The cafeteria"],"correct_answer":"The lost and found"},{"question":"What color is the slime mentioned in this chapter?","options":["Blue","Green","Pink","Yellow"],"correct_answer":"Green"},{"question":"What does Ava feel about her homework being lost?","options":["Excited","Nervous","Happy","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What does Leo find in the lost and found?","options":["A pair of shoes","Purple socks","A lunch box","A book"],"correct_answer":"Purple socks"},{"question":"How do Ava and Leo react to the green slime?","options":["They ignore it","They laugh","They are scared","They duck for cover"],"correct_answer":"They duck for cover"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_256_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_256_ch2_img1.png","plot_256_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":387,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
