   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_256_7_10","title":"The Case of the Missing Homework","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ava and Leo stood in the hallway of Sunnyvale Middle School. The walls were buzzing with excitement. Students chatted about their science projects. Ava's heart raced. The science fair was just hours away! \n\n\u201cI can\u2019t believe my homework is still missing!\u201d Ava exclaimed, tapping her foot. \n\n\u201cWe have to solve this mystery!\u201d Leo replied, his eyes shining like stars. \u201cMaybe we can find a clue in the art room.\u201d \n\nAva nodded fiercely. \u201cGood idea! Ms. Thompson might have seen something!\u201d\n\nThey hurried down the hallway, passing colorful posters of volcanoes and planets. As they approached the art room, Ava spotted something shiny on the floor. \n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d she asked, pointing. \n\nLeo bent down and picked it up. \u201cIt\u2019s a key! But where does it lead?\u201d \n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud crash from the art room. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Leo whispered, his voice trembling. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out!\u201d Ava said bravely. \n\nThey creaked open the door. The art room was a mess! Paint splatters covered the floor and tables. And there in the center of the chaos stood Ms. Thompson, looking frazzled. \n\n\u201cOh no! I accidentally knocked over the paint!\u201d she said, her hands covered in blue and green. \n\n\u201cMs. Thompson! Have you seen my homework?\u201d Ava asked urgently. \n\n\u201cI haven\u2019t seen it, but I found something,\u201d Ms. Thompson said, holding up a crumpled paper with scribbles. \u201cIt looks like a riddle!\u201d\n\nAva leaned closer. \u201cWhat does it say?\u201d\n\nMs. Thompson read aloud, \u201cTo find what you seek, look where the secrets peek. Behind the curtain, dark and deep, treasures are waiting, if you dare to leap.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat does that mean?\u201d Leo asked, scratching his head. \n\nAva\u2019s eyes sparkled with excitement. \u201cIt must mean the old stage in the auditorium! Let\u2019s go!\u201d\n\nAs they raced down the corridor, Ava clutched the key tightly. What if it opened something important? \n\nThen, they heard a loud bang. The doors to the auditorium slammed shut! \n\n\u201cUh-oh,\u201d Leo said, eyes wide. \u201cWhat if we\u2019re trapped?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe can\u2019t give up now!\u201d Ava urged, determined. \n\nJust then, a shadow moved near the stage curtain. Ava felt a shiver down her spine. \u201cSomeone\u2019s in there!\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s the homework thief!\u201d Leo said, his voice barely above a whisper.\n\nAva took a deep breath. \u201cWe have to see who it is!\u201d \n\nWith the key in one hand and courage in the other, they stepped toward the curtain. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Where do Ava and Leo decide to go after finding the riddle?","options":["The library","The cafeteria","The auditorium","The playground"],"correct_answer":"The auditorium"},{"question":"What does Ms. Thompson knock over?","options":["Books","Paint","Scissors","Glue"],"correct_answer":"Paint"},{"question":"What does the riddle mention about treasures?","options":["They are hidden in the library","They are waiting behind the curtain","They are in the lost and found","They are on the playground"],"correct_answer":"They are waiting behind the curtain"},{"question":"What does Ava find in the art room?","options":["A clue","Her homework","A book","A pencil"],"correct_answer":"A clue"},{"question":"How does Leo feel when they hear a loud bang?","options":["Excited","Bored","Scared","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Scared"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_256_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_256_ch3_img1.png","plot_256_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":413,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
