   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_256_15_18","title":"The Case of the Missing Homework","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Ava stood at her locker, the hum of Sunnyvale Middle School buzzing around her like a swarm of excited bees. It was the day of the science fair, and the air was thick with anticipation. Students darted past, clutching poster boards and intricate models. Her heart raced, not from the thrill of the event but from the weight of her own project\u2014her prized holographic solar system, carefully crafted and endlessly revised.\n\n\u201cHey, Ava! You ready to blow everyone\u2019s minds?\u201d Leo\u2019s voice cut through the chatter, his messy hair bouncing as he approached.\n\nAva smiled, grateful for her best friend\u2019s unwavering support. \u201cIf I can find my homework, maybe.\u201d She opened her backpack to retrieve the project notes, but her heart sank. The interior was empty; the pages that had occupied her hours of hard work had vanished into thin air.\n\n\u201cUh-oh, did the homework goblins get you?\u201d Leo joked, trying to lighten the mood, but Ava\u2019s face fell. \n\n\u201cNot funny, Leo. I had everything in here! My notes, my drawings\u2026\u201d She rummaged through the bag again, panic rising as she pulled out crumpled papers and a half-eaten granola bar. \u201cIt\u2019s all gone!\u201d\n\n\u201cOkay, okay. Let\u2019s retrace your steps. When did you last have it?\u201d Leo offered, his eyes darting around as if the answer lay hidden in the hallways.\n\n\u201cI had it after class yesterday. I remember talking to Ms. Thompson about my project.\u201d She felt a pang of worry; Ms. Thompson was eccentric, to say the least, often distracted by her own whirlwind of ideas. \u201cWe were in the science lab. Maybe I left it there?\u201d\n\n\u201cThen that\u2019s our first clue!\u201d Leo declared, his excitement palpable. \u201cWe\u2019ll have to move fast. The fair starts in less than an hour.\u201d\n\nWith a shared determination, they hurried down the bustling corridor, feet pounding against the polished floor. The cacophony of voices faded as they entered the quiet sanctuary of the science lab. The smell of chemicals mingled with the faint scent of burnt toast from the cafeteria wafted through the air.\n\n\u201cWhere would you have left it?\u201d Leo scanned the room, his eyes gleaming with curiosity. \n\n\u201cRight here at this table,\u201d Ava said, pointing to the workstation cluttered with beakers and notebooks. \u201cI was showing Ms. Thompson my model.\u201d \n\nThey searched under piles of papers and over brimming bins of supplies, but Ava\u2019s notes were nowhere to be found. Frustration bubbled within her, each second ticking away like a countdown to disaster.\n\nSuddenly, Leo\u2019s attention was drawn to an unusual corner of the lab. \u201cWait a second\u2026\u201d He pulled open a cabinet, revealing a kaleidoscope of forgotten projects and dusty equipment. However, it was something else that caught his eye\u2014a glimmering edge of paper tucked into a corner.\n\n\u201cIs that\u2026?\u201d Ava rushed over, her heart pounding in her chest. She reached for the paper, but as she did, a shadow loomed ominously behind them.\n\n\u201cMs. Thompson!\u201d They both exclaimed as their science teacher entered, her wild hair bouncing with each step. \u201cWe were just\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cI hope you\u2019re not rummaging through my treasures!\u201d she interrupted, peering intently at Ava\u2019s hands. \n\n\u201cUh, no! I just\u2014my homework\u2014\u201d Ava stammered, heat rising to her cheeks. \n\nMs. Thompson waved a hand, her expression shifting from curiosity to concern. \u201cHomework? In my lab? It might just be...\u201d \n\nJust then, the bell rang, echoing ominously through the hallways. \n\n\u201cQuick! We need to find it before class starts!\u201d Ava said, urgency clawing at her throat. \n\n\u201cRight! We\u2019ll split up. I\u2019ll check the art room; I think I saw some of my papers there too,\u201d Leo said, darting toward the door.\n\n\u201cAva?\u201d Ms. Thompson\u2019s voice held a hint of seriousness. \u201cDon\u2019t you want to know what I think about your project?\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2026 um, yes!\u201d\n\n\u201cGood. So focus! You\u2019ll need that project to shine at the fair. Let\u2019s use our heads,\u201d she said, a glimmer of mischief in her eyes. \u201cRemember, mysteries require more than just searching\u2014they require thinking.\u201d \n\nAva nodded, determination surging within her. She was going to recover her project, no matter what. \n\nAs she stepped back outside, a thought struck her: with Leo\u2019s help, they would uncover the truth behind the missing homework. The science fair loomed like a shadow over them, and the clock was ticking.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nShe glanced at the brightly decorated science fair posters lining the walls, each showcasing the hard work of her classmates. The vibrant colors seemed to mock her predicament, but she couldn\u2019t let the anxiety consume her. She took a deep breath, willing herself to remain calm.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nJust then, Leo rejoined her, panting slightly from his run. \u201cI can\u2019t find anything! But I have this strange feeling\u2014like we\u2019re being watched.\u201d His voice dropped to a whisper, the intensity of his eyes drawing her in. \u201cWhat if someone took it on purpose?\u201d\n\nAva\u2019s heart raced. \u201cYou think?\u201d\n\n\u201cOnly one way to find out.\u201d \n\nWith newfound resolve, they plunged into the mystery together, ready to untangle the threads before it unraveled completely.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What project did Ava create for the science fair?","options":["A model of the solar system","A chemistry experiment","A robot","A poster on climate change"],"correct_answer":"A model of the solar system"},{"question":"Who is Ava's best friend?","options":["Ms. Thompson","Leo","Sarah","Jake"],"correct_answer":"Leo"},{"question":"What is the main conflict Ava faces in this chapter?","options":["She has to finish a project","Her homework is missing","She has a fight with Leo","She is late for school"],"correct_answer":"Her homework is missing"},{"question":"What does Ms. Thompson encourage Ava to focus on?","options":["Finding her project","Working with other students","Learning more about science","Using her imagination"],"correct_answer":"Finding her project"},{"question":"What feeling does Leo express when he reappears to Ava?","options":["Excitement","Worry","Anger","Boredom"],"correct_answer":"Worry"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_256_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_256_ch1_img1.png","plot_256_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":860,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
