   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_256_15_18","title":"The Case of the Missing Homework","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ava's heart raced as she and Leo stepped into the dimly lit corridor of Sunnyvale Middle School, the fluorescent lights flickering overhead like a warning. The science fair was just hours away, and the weight of her missing project loomed over her like a storm cloud. \u201cWe need to retrace my steps,\u201d Ava said, her voice catching slightly as the gravity of the situation pressed down upon her. Leo adjusted his glasses, his usual clumsiness replaced by an unusual sense of determination. \n\n\u201cRight! So, where do we start?\u201d he asked, glancing nervously around the hallway. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go to the library first,\u201d Ava suggested, recalling that she\u2019d done some last-minute research there the previous week. \n\nAs they navigated their way through the bustling hallways, filled with students excitedly discussing their science projects, Ava felt a pang of jealousy. Everyone was getting ready to showcase their hard work, while her own project lay hidden somewhere within the school\u2019s labyrinthine confines. \n\nUpon entering the library, the musty scent of old books enveloped them. Ava spotted her science teacher, Ms. Thompson, organizing a shelf. \u201cMs. Thompson!\u201d she called out, her voice rising in urgency. \u201cHave you seen my homework? It\u2019s missing, and I really need it back before the fair!\u201d\n\nMs. Thompson looked up, her eyes vibrant with curiosity. \u201cMissing homework? That\u2019s quite the conundrum! You know what they say, Ava\u2014mysteries are often in plain sight.\u201d \n\nAva's brow furrowed. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d \n\n\u201cConsider where you\u2019ve been, who you\u2019ve interacted with, and what might\u2019ve been overlooked,\u201d she advised cryptically before returning to her task, leaving Ava and Leo in a swirl of confusion. \n\n\u201cGreat, more riddles,\u201d Leo muttered under his breath. \u201cLet\u2019s check the storage closet next. Maybe you dropped it there when you were getting your supplies.\u201d \n\nThey hurried through the library and down a narrow staircase leading to the school's storage area. As they approached the door, Ava noticed something peculiar\u2014a set of muddy footprints trailing toward the closet. \u201cLeo, look!\u201d she pointed excitedly. \n\n\u201cFootprints! Whoever took your homework probably went this way,\u201d Leo exclaimed, enthusiasm bubbling up in his normally anxious demeanor. \n\nWith a deep breath, Ava pushed the door open, revealing a cluttered space filled with forgotten science projects and old furniture. The air was thick with dust, and the shadows danced along the walls, creating a sense of foreboding. They stepped inside cautiously, the floor creaking beneath their feet. \n\nSuddenly, the door swung shut behind them with a loud bang, sending a jolt of adrenaline through Ava's veins. \u201cLeo, did you\u2014?\u201d \n\n\u201cI didn\u2019t touch it!\u201d he gasped, looking over his shoulder nervously. \n\n\u201cOkay, we need to stay calm. Let\u2019s search for clues\u2014maybe your project is hidden in here.\u201d \n\nAs they rummaged through boxes and old posters, a sudden noise erupted from behind them. Ava whirled around, her heart pounding as she caught a glimpse of an object slipping out of view. \u201cDid you see that?\u201d she whispered, panic rising. \n\n\u201cYeah, I did! It looked like someone was just here,\u201d Leo replied, his voice shaky. \n\nJust then, the lights flickered ominously, plunging them into near darkness. Ava's breath hitched; the atmosphere crackled with tension. \u201cThis isn\u2019t good, Leo. What if someone is trying to keep me from finding my project?\u201d \n\n\u201cOr worse, what if they\u2019re trying to sabotage the science fair?\u201d Leo added, his eyes wide with a mixture of fear and excitement. \n\nDetermined, Ava pressed onward, forging through the maze of forgotten artifacts. They stumbled upon a dusty box, the lid slightly ajar. \u201cMaybe this holds a clue,\u201d she said, reaching for it. \n\nBefore she could open it, the door slammed open, revealing a shadowy figure silhouetted against the hallway light. \u201cWhat are you two doing in here?\u201d The voice was deep and intimidating. \n\nAva\u2019s heart dropped as she recognized the figure. It was Jason, the school\u2019s notorious prankster, known for his elaborate schemes and penchant for trouble. \n\n\u201cWe\u2019re just looking for something,\u201d Ava said, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\n\u201cYeah, right. You\u2019re not supposed to be in here! Better get out before I make you regret it,\u201d Jason threatened, stepping closer. \n\nAva exchanged a panicked glance with Leo. They were trapped, their search for the project hanging by a thread. \u201cLeo, what do we do?\u201d \n\nThe tension in the room escalated, and Ava felt an overwhelming mix of fear and determination. They had to act fast. \n\nAt that moment, the lights flickered again, casting an eerie glow over Jason\u2019s face. With adrenaline surging, Ava knew they had to make a decision\u2014fight back or flee. \n\n\u201cLeo, we need to think of something\u2014now!\u201d \n\nAnd just as she spoke, Leo's eyes lit up with an idea. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What location do Ava and Leo search in Chapter 3?","options":["The library","The principal's office","The storage closet","The science lab"],"correct_answer":"The storage closet"},{"question":"Who do Ava and Leo encounter in the storage closet?","options":["Ms. Thompson","Jason","Their classmates","The janitor"],"correct_answer":"Jason"},{"question":"What advice does Ms. Thompson give Ava?","options":["To give up and try again next year","To consider overlooked details","To stop searching","To ask someone else for help"],"correct_answer":"To consider overlooked details"},{"question":"What do Ava and Leo find in the storage closet?","options":["Old textbooks","Mud on the floor","A hidden passage","A science fair trophy"],"correct_answer":"Mud on the floor"},{"question":"What decision do Ava and Leo face at the end of the chapter?","options":["To continue searching or to flee","To call for help","To give up","To sneak out quietly"],"correct_answer":"To continue searching or to flee"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_256_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_256_ch3_img1.png","plot_256_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":801,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
