   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_256_15_18","title":"The Case of the Missing Homework","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Ava stood frozen in the shadowy corner of the storage closet, her heart racing as she processed the muddy footprints that led deeper into the labyrinthine hallways of Sunnyvale Middle School. \"Leo, look!\" she whispered, pointing urgently at the trail of prints. \"These could be our key to finding my homework!\"\n\n\"Or a trap,\" Leo replied, his voice a mix of excitement and trepidation. \"Jason could have set this up to throw us off the scent.\" He glanced over his shoulder, half-expecting to see the notorious prankster lurking behind them. The dim light flickered overhead, casting eerie shadows that danced along the walls, amplifying the tension of their clandestine adventure.\n\n\u201cWe have to follow them,\u201d Ava insisted, her determination hardening into resolve. The science fair was only hours away, and the thought of letting her classmates down gnawed at her. She had put her heart into the project, and the idea of presenting an empty board was unbearable.\n\nAs they ventured out of the closet, the bustling energy of the school poured over them like a tidal wave. Students were busy prepping their projects, their laughter and chatter a stark contrast to the urgency that weighed on Ava\u2019s shoulders. The hallways felt more alive than ever, and yet, she felt isolated in her quest.\n\nThey reached the first intersection of the hall, where the footprints veered left towards the art room. \u201cWhy would Jason go there?\u201d Leo pondered aloud, scratching his head as if trying to untangle the mystery. \u201cUnless he\u2019s trying to add a splash of color to his next prank.\u201d\n\n\u201cOr he thinks it\u2019s the perfect hiding place,\u201d Ava countered. \u201cLet\u2019s check it out.\u201d The art room door creaked open, revealing a chaotic haven of paint-splattered tables and half-finished sculptures. The air was thick with creativity and chaos, but Ava's focus was singular. \n\nAs they crept inside, they were greeted by a sight that made Ava\u2019s heart drop. A familiar figure hunched over a table, surrounded by an assortment of art supplies\u2014Jason, the prankster. His back was turned, but even from behind, Ava could see the mischief in his posture. \n\n\u201cGreat, we found him,\u201d Leo whispered, but his voice faltered as anxiety crept in. \u201cNow what?\u201d\n\n\u201cLet me talk to him,\u201d Ava proposed, her confidence flickering. She took a deep breath and stepped forward, determined to face her fears. \u201cHey, Jason!\u201d she called out, trying to sound brave despite the knot in her stomach.\n\nHe turned, surprise flashing across his face. \u201cAva? What are you doing here? Planning a last-minute masterpiece?\u201d He smirked, a glimmer of amusement in his eyes. \n\nAva crossed her arms, summoning her strength. \u201cActually, I\u2019m looking for my missing homework. I think you might know something about it.\u201d\n\nJason raised an eyebrow, feigning innocence. \u201cMe? Why would I take your homework? I\u2019m just trying to create art, unlike some people who are glued to their science fair boards.\u201d\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t have time for your games,\u201d she replied, frustration bubbling to the surface. \u201cThis is serious! If you know where it is, just tell me!\u201d\n\n\u201cOr what?\u201d he challenged, leaning back against the table, arms crossed. \u201cYou\u2019ll report me for a harmless prank? You know I\u2019d never ruin your project. It\u2019s too easy.\u201d\n\nAva felt her composure wavering. \u201cThis isn\u2019t about pranks, Jason. I care about my work. It matters to me.\u201d\n\nFor a moment, the air turned electric, and there was a flicker of understanding in Jason\u2019s eyes. Perhaps he recognized the weight of her passion. \u201cAlright, maybe I did see something suspicious in the hallway earlier,\u201d he admitted, his tone shifting from playful to serious. \u201cBut you\u2019ve got to promise me something in return.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat?\u201d Ava asked, wary of his sudden change in demeanor.\n\n\u201cI want to check out your project at the fair. If I help you find it, you have to let me see what you\u2019ve been working on.\u201d\n\nAva hesitated, torn between her desire to reclaim her homework and the nagging doubt about trusting Jason. But she could sense Leo\u2019s eager anticipation beside her. \u201cDeal,\u201d she finally said, her voice steadying as hope surged within her. \n\nWith that, Jason leaned closer, conspiratorially. \u201cFollow me. I think I saw someone near the gym who was acting weird. Let\u2019s see if they\u2019ve got your precious homework.\u201d \n\nAs they moved toward the gym, a swirl of adrenaline charged the atmosphere. Ava could feel the clock ticking, driving them forward. She and Leo exchanged glances of unspoken determination, ready to dive deeper into the mystery.\n\nAs they pushed open the gym door, a wave of noise and chaos enveloped them. The bright lights reflected off the polished floor, illuminating a scene full of bustling students and their projects. But amidst the frenzy, Ava's heart raced with the realization that time was slipping away.\n\nThen, just as they entered, Leo suddenly stopped. \u201cWait, look over there!\u201d He pointed toward a group of students laughing near the bleachers, and Ava's breath hitched as she recognized the silhouette of her homework project.\n\n\u201cLeo, that\u2019s it!\u201d she exclaimed, hope igniting as they rushed forward, [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] capturing the moment of discovery, the thrill of the chase. \n\nAva's heart pounded in her chest, ready for the confrontation ahead. \"Let's get it back.\"","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ava and Leo find in the storage closet?","options":["A clue to find the homework","Jason hiding","A note from Ms. Thompson","A lost science project"],"correct_answer":"A clue to find the homework"},{"question":"What does Jason ask for in exchange for helping Ava?","options":["A ride home","Information about the science fair","To see her project","Extra credit"],"correct_answer":"To see her project"},{"question":"How does Ava feel about her homework project?","options":["Indifferent","Excited","Angry","Passionate"],"correct_answer":"Passionate"},{"question":"What atmosphere is present in the gym when Ava and Leo enter?","options":["Quiet and tense","Chaotic and vibrant","Dark and gloomy","Peaceful and calm"],"correct_answer":"Chaotic and vibrant"},{"question":"What motivates Ava to confront Jason?","options":["Curiosity","Desperation","Fear","Frustration"],"correct_answer":"Frustration"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_256_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_256_ch4_img1.png","plot_256_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":893,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
