   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_257_7_10","title":"The Secret of the Haunted Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Emily and Max stood in the old town library, peering around. The shelves towered high, filled with dusty books waiting to be read. Max sniffed the air, wagging his tail. \u201cWhat do you think, boy?\u201d Emily asked. \u201cShould we start our treasure hunt?\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud THUD echoed through the library. A book fell from the shelf nearby, landing with a soft poof of dust. Emily jumped. \u201cWhoa! That was creepy!\u201d She glanced at Max, who barked softly, ready to investigate. \n\nAs they approached the fallen book, Emily noticed it was a thick, leather-bound volume. Its title was barely visible. \u201cLook, Max! It\u2019s \u2018The Secrets of Our Town.\u2019 I wonder if it has any clues?\u201d Carefully, she picked it up and opened it. Pages were filled with stories, but one page seemed different. It had a strange drawing on it.\n\n\u201cHey, look at this!\u201d Emily exclaimed, pointing to the drawing. It was a map! It showed paths leading to different spots in the library. \u201cThis must be part of the treasure map Mr. Jenkins gave us!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the lights flickered again. The room felt colder, and a whisper echoed, \u201cFind the key!\u201d Emily shivered, her heart racing. \u201cDid you hear that, Max? We need to find a key!\u201d \n\nMax wagged his tail, sniffing excitedly. They followed the map, which led them to a dusty corner of the library. There, a large, ornate chest sat hidden behind a stack of old encyclopedias. \u201cThis must be it!\u201d Emily said, her eyes wide with excitement. They approached the chest cautiously. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s open it together!\u201d Emily said, pulling on the rusty latch. Suddenly, the chest creaked open, revealing a collection of strange items: old keys, a compass, and a beautiful, shining locket. \u201cWow! These could be important!\u201d \n\nJust then, they heard footsteps approaching. Emily\u2019s stomach dropped. \u201cOh no! We have to hide!\u201d she whispered. They quickly ducked behind the chest. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nEmily held her breath, peeking out. Mr. Jenkins, the librarian, appeared, looking around suspiciously. \u201cI know someone is here,\u201d he muttered. Emily squeezed Max\u2019s paw. \u201cWhat if he finds us?\u201d \n\nThe footsteps faded, and Emily sighed in relief. But she knew they had to move quickly. \u201cWe can\u2019t let anyone stop us! We have to figure out what these things mean!\u201d \n\nMax barked softly as if he understood. They had their work cut out for them. Finding the key was only the beginning!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep searching, Max! We\u2019re getting closer to the treasure!\u201d Emily said, her voice filled with determination. They gathered the items from the chest, putting them safely in Emily\u2019s backpack. With the map in hand, they ventured deeper into the library, ready for whatever adventure awaited them next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What fell off the shelf at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["A pencil","A book","A toy","A newspaper"],"correct_answer":"A book"},{"question":"What did Emily find inside the chest?","options":["A treasure map","A shiny locket","A magic wand","A photo album"],"correct_answer":"A shiny locket"},{"question":"Who is the librarian?","options":["Mr. Jenkins","Mr. Smith","Ms. Johnson","Ms. Brown"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"question":"What did the whisper say?","options":["Find the key!","Close the book!","Leave the library!","Help me!"],"correct_answer":"Find the key!"},{"question":"What are Emily and Max looking for?","options":["A lost dog","A treasure","A book","A friend"],"correct_answer":"A treasure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_257_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_257_ch2_img1.png","plot_257_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":460,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
