   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_257_7_10","title":"The Secret of the Haunted Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Emily blinked as the lights flickered back on. She and Max were still trapped in Mr. Jenkins's office. The old clock on the wall ticked loudly. \"What do we do now?\" Emily whispered, her heart racing.\n\nMax sniffed around the room, his tail wagging. He seemed to sense something. \"You\u2019re right, buddy! We need to find that treasure map!\" she said, feeling hopeful again.\n\nSuddenly, Max nudged a dusty book with his nose. It was a big, old book with golden letters on the spine. Emily rushed over and opened it. Inside, she found a parchment that looked just like their treasure map! \"Look, Max! It\u2019s our map!\" she exclaimed. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\"Now we can follow it!\" Emily said, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \"I wonder what secrets it holds. Maybe it will lead us to the treasure!\" She traced her finger over the lines and marks on the map, trying to remember the clues they had collected.\n\nJust then, Emily heard a soft laugh from behind them. \"Ah, I see you found my little secret!\" Mr. Jenkins stood at the door, a twinkle in his eye. Emily jumped but quickly regained her courage. \"We\u2019re not afraid, Mr. Jenkins! We want to help uncover the library's mysteries!\"\n\nMr. Jenkins smiled. \"Then let\u2019s work together! The next spot on the map is in the children\u2019s section. There's a hidden bookshelf that holds the next clue!\"\n\nWith Mr. Jenkins leading the way, Emily felt a rush of hope. \"Let\u2019s go, Max!\" she said, feeling braver than ever. They dashed through the library, the flickering lights now just a part of the adventure. \n\nAs they reached the children\u2019s section, Emily noticed a strange glimmer. \"Look over there!\" she pointed. A bookshelf was moving slightly, as if it had a secret. \"That must be it!\" she shouted.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\"Let\u2019s see what\u2019s inside!\" Mr. Jenkins said, pushing the shelf aside. As it creaked open, a cloud of dust flew into the air. Emily and Max coughed, but they didn't back away. They were too excited! Inside the hidden space, they saw a box filled with colorful stones. Each stone had a letter carved into it.\n\n\"What do you think they mean?\" Emily asked, her curiosity buzzing. \n\nMr. Jenkins scratched his head. \"I believe they spell out the next location! We\u2019re getting closer to the treasure, Emily!\"\n\nEmily beamed with excitement. \"We\u2019re really doing it! I can\u2019t wait to see what\u2019s next!\"","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Emily and Max find in Mr. Jenkins's office?","options":["A treasure chest","A treasure map","A scary book","A ghost"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"What does Mr. Jenkins agree to do?","options":["Leave the library","Help Emily and Max","Close the library","Hide the treasure"],"correct_answer":"Help Emily and Max"},{"question":"Where do they go after the office?","options":["Outside","The children's section","The basement","The attic"],"correct_answer":"The children's section"},{"question":"What do they find behind the hidden bookshelf?","options":["A treasure chest","A box of colorful stones","A ghost","A secret door"],"correct_answer":"A box of colorful stones"},{"question":"What does Emily feel as they uncover the mysteries?","options":["Scared","Bored","Excited","Tired"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_257_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_257_ch4_img1.png","plot_257_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":420,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
