   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_257_7_10","title":"The Secret of the Haunted Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Emily took a deep breath as she and Max stood in Mr. Jenkins' office. The treasure map was back in her hands! \u201cWe need to find out what these strange stones mean, Max!\u201d she said, her eyes sparkling with excitement.\n\nMax wagged his tail, eager to help. They spread the map out on the dusty table. It showed a picture of a big bookshelf, hidden behind a curtain. \u201cLook, Max! This must be our next clue!\u201d Emily pointed at the map.\n\nSuddenly, a loud creak echoed through the library. Emily jumped, and Max barked. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, boy. We\u2019ll face whatever it is together!\u201d They clasped hands once more, ready for the adventure ahead.\n\nThey raced back into the library, the floorboards creaking under their feet. The flickering lights seemed to dance around them as they approached the big bookshelf. Emily felt a little scared, but she was more curious than afraid. \u201cLet\u2019s see if the map is right!\u201d she whispered.\n\nAs they reached the bookshelf, Emily noticed a loose book on the shelf. It was a colorful book titled \u201cThe Hidden Treasures of the Library.\u201d With a gentle pull, the book slid out. To their surprise, the bookshelf began to move! Dust swirled around them as a secret room opened behind it.\n\n\u201cWow!\u201d Emily gasped. \u201cLook at all these colorful stones!\u201d They sparkled like gems in the dim light. Each stone had a letter carved into it. Emily and Max stepped inside, their hearts racing with wonder. \n\n\u201cWhat do these letters mean?\u201d Emily wondered aloud. Max sniffed the stones, his tail wagging. \u201cI think they\u2019re clues!\u201d she declared excitedly. \u201cLet\u2019s sort them!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nEmily and Max began to gather the stones, making words as they went. \u201cE, L, I, M, Y! That spells my name!\u201d she shouted happily. Max barked, as if he understood. \n\nJust then, Mr. Jenkins appeared in the doorway, looking surprised. \u201cWhat are you two doing in here?\u201d he asked, his eyes wide with curiosity.\n\n\u201cWe found letters, Mr. Jenkins! And we think they lead to the treasure!\u201d Emily exclaimed. Mr. Jenkins smiled and walked into the secret room. \u201cYou\u2019ve discovered something truly special,\u201d he said. He knelt down, examining the stones. \u201cThese stones hold the key to a wonderful story.\u201d\n\nEmily\u2019s heart swelled with joy. Together, they would unravel the mystery of the haunted library and find the treasure! \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep going!\u201d Emily cheered. Max barked in agreement, ready for the next clue.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWe have a treasure to find!\u201d she shouted, feeling brave and excited.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Emily and Max find behind the bookshelf?","options":["A treasure chest","A secret room","A scary monster","A new book"],"correct_answer":"A secret room"},{"question":"What did the colorful stones have on them?","options":["Numbers","Pictures","Letters","Words"],"correct_answer":"Letters"},{"question":"How did Emily feel when they found the stones?","options":["Scared","Bored","Excited","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"Who appeared in the doorway of the secret room?","options":["A librarian","A ghost","A dog","A cat"],"correct_answer":"A librarian"},{"question":"What did Emily shout at the end of the chapter?","options":["I want to go home!","Let\u2019s keep going!","This is scary!","Where\u2019s the treasure?"],"correct_answer":"Let\u2019s keep going!"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_257_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_257_ch5_img1.png","plot_257_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":430,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
