   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_257_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Haunted Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Emily stood in the shadowy corner of the library, clutching the mysterious map she had just discovered. The flickering lights cast eerie shadows against the tall bookshelves, and the air was thick with the smell of old paper. She could feel Max\u2019s excitement radiating next to her, his tail wagging furiously as he sniffed the air, searching for clues. \u201cThis place is definitely hiding something,\u201d Emily said, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s start with this map,\u201d she continued, spreading it out on the nearest dusty table. There were strange markings and an \u2018X\u2019 that seemed to lead deeper into the library. \u201cWhat do you think, Max? Should we follow the treasure trail?\u201d Max barked in agreement, and his eyes sparkled with determination.\n\nAs they traced the lines on the map, Emily\u2019s heart raced with excitement and a hint of fear. She couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that they weren\u2019t alone. \u201cIt\u2019s just a library,\u201d she told herself, attempting to suppress her growing anxiety. But when a loud thump echoed from the back of the library, her heart skipped a beat. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d she asked Max, who responded with a hesitant whine. \n\nTogether, they crept towards the source of the noise, the floor creaking beneath their feet. The deeper they went, the darker it became, and soon the faint light from the main room was just a glimmer behind them. The air felt cooler, almost as if the shadows were alive and breathing.\n\nSuddenly, Emily spotted Mr. Jenkins, the mysterious librarian, standing in front of a towering shelf filled with ancient encyclopedias. He looked up, his glasses slipping down his nose. \u201cAh, Emily! Max!\u201d he greeted with an unexpected smile. \u201cWhat brings you two here at this hour?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe heard a noise,\u201d Emily replied, her voice wavering slightly. \u201cAnd we found this map. Do you know anything about it?\u201d\n\nMr. Jenkins examined the map with a furrowed brow. \u201cThis library holds many secrets, my dear. But be careful. Not everything hidden is meant to be found.\u201d His warning sent a shiver down Emily\u2019s spine.\n\nBefore she could respond, a loud crash resounded from the far end of the library, followed by a faint whisper that seemed to float through the air. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Emily gasped, gripping the edge of the table. \u201cIt sounded like\u2026 someone else is here.\u201d\n\nMax\u2019s ears perked up, and he padded towards the sound, his instincts kicking in. \u201cWait, Max!\u201d Emily called out, but he was already off, darting into the shadows. \u201cI have to go after him!\u201d \n\nRushing after her loyal companion, Emily felt the tension building in her chest. The whispers grew louder, echoing off the walls as they ventured deeper into the library\u2019s hidden corners. She could sense a presence, something\u2014or someone\u2014watching them. \u201cThis isn\u2019t just a mystery,\u201d she whispered to herself, her courage wavering. \u201cIt\u2019s a challenge.\u201d\n\nAs she turned a corner, she stumbled upon a dusty old door, slightly ajar. The whispers seemed to emanate from within. Emily hesitated, her heart pounding in her ears. Should she push the door open? Taking a deep breath, she reached for the handle, just as Max nudged her leg, urging her on.\n\n\u201cOkay, here goes nothing,\u201d she mumbled, and with a firm tug, she swung the door open wide.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBefore her lay a hidden room filled with cobwebs and forgotten treasures\u2014old books, trinkets, and\u2026 a shimmering object on a pedestal at the far end. What was it? Could this be part of the mystery? Emily felt a thrill of anticipation mixed with trepidation. She had no idea what awaited her, but one thing was clear: they were now deeper into the secret of the haunted library than she had ever expected.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Emily find in the library?","options":["A treasure chest","A mysterious map","A ghost","A secret door"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious map"},{"question":"What does Mr. Jenkins warn Emily about?","options":["Not to touch the books","Not everything hidden is meant to be found","To leave the library","To take Max outside"],"correct_answer":"Not everything hidden is meant to be found"},{"question":"How does Max react to the noises in the library?","options":["He runs away","He barks in excitement","He hides behind Emily","He falls asleep"],"correct_answer":"He barks in excitement"},{"question":"What emotion does Emily feel as she approaches the hidden room?","options":["Excitement","Boredom","Fear","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"},{"question":"What is the atmosphere like in the library?","options":["Bright and cheerful","Dark and eerie","Noisy and crowded","Warm and cozy"],"correct_answer":"Dark and eerie"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_257_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_257_ch2_img1.png","plot_257_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":639,"reading_level":"Builder"}
