   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_257_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Haunted Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the clock struck midnight, the old town library stood shrouded in an eerie glow, the flickering lights casting dancing shadows across dusty bookshelves. Emily clutched her golden key tightly, feeling the weight of her discovery and the challenge that lay ahead. She had come too far to turn back now; the secrets of the library were waiting to be uncovered. \n\n\u201cAre you ready, Max?\u201d Emily whispered, glancing down at her loyal dog, who was wagging his tail with excitement. The scent of old pages and musty air filled the room as they stepped deeper into the heart of the library. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe large wooden doors creaked as they entered the Forbidden Section, marked by a sign that read, \u201cAuthorized Personnel Only.\u201d Emily\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWe need to find the next clue,\u201d she said, her voice barely above a whisper. Shadows flickered on the walls, almost as if the library itself was alive, urging them forward.\n\nAs they moved past rows of ancient tomes, Emily recalled Mr. Jenkins\u2019s words about the treasure connected to the library\u2019s history. \u201cThe answer lies within the books,\u201d he had said. But which book? Her eyes skimmed the spines, searching for something that seemed out of place.\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed through the room. A book flew off the shelf and landed at her feet. Emily jumped back, her heart pounding in her chest. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d she gasped, glancing at Max, who was barking at the fallen book. \n\n\u201cOkay, you brave pup, let\u2019s see what you\u2019ve found,\u201d she said, kneeling to pick up the book. It was an old, leather-bound volume, its spine cracked and worn. As she opened it, a piece of parchment slipped out and fluttered to the floor. \n\n\u201cLook, Max!\u201d Emily exclaimed, bending down to retrieve the parchment. It was a map, and as she spread it out on the dusty carpet, her eyes widened. \u201cThis looks just like the layout of the library!\u201d\n\nMax sniffed the map, his tail wagging faster. \u201cDo you think this could lead us to the treasure?\u201d Emily\u2019s mind raced with possibilities. \u201cWe need to figure out what these symbols mean.\u201d\n\nTracing her finger over the parchment, she spotted the first clue\u2014an illustration of the library\u2019s grand staircase. \u201cIt says we need to go to the highest point in the library. That must be the observatory!\u201d she said, bubbling with excitement.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s hurry before anything else happens,\u201d Emily urged, urgency filling her voice. They raced up the winding staircase, the wooden steps creaking under their weight. As they reached the top, the door to the observatory loomed before them, slightly ajar as if inviting them in.\n\nWith a deep breath, Emily pushed the door open. The room was filled with dust motes dancing in the moonlight, revealing a small telescope in the corner and a large stained-glass window depicting a majestic owl. The atmosphere was thick with a sense of history and mystery.\n\n\u201cWow, it\u2019s beautiful,\u201d Emily breathed, taking in the intricate designs. But she couldn't linger long; she had a mystery to solve. \n\nJust then, a gust of wind swept through the room, slamming the door shut behind them. Emily\u2019s heart skipped a beat. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d she whispered, feeling a chill run down her spine. \n\n\u201cMax, stay close,\u201d she instructed, trying to steady her breath. In that moment of fear, she felt a flicker of determination ignite within her. They had come this far and weren\u2019t turning back now. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find the treasure,\u201d she declared, her voice steady. \u201cWe\u2019re nearly there!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they began to search the observatory, Emily felt a sense of hope wash over her. They were piecing together the library\u2019s puzzle, and the mystery was beginning to unravel. But what would they find next? \n\nWith Max at her side, she was ready to face whatever lay ahead in the haunted library.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Emily find that leads her to the next clue?","options":["A dusty old book","A golden key","A mysterious letter","A locked chest"],"correct_answer":"A dusty old book"},{"question":"Where do Emily and Max decide to go after finding the map?","options":["The basement","The observatory","The attic","The reading room"],"correct_answer":"The observatory"},{"question":"What happens when they enter the observatory?","options":["The lights go out","The door slams shut","A book falls from the shelf","A ghost appears"],"correct_answer":"The door slams shut"},{"question":"What emotion does Emily feel as she uncovers the library's secrets?","options":["Fear","Excitement","Boredom","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"},{"question":"What animal is depicted in the stained-glass window in the observatory?","options":["A cat","A dog","An owl","A lion"],"correct_answer":"An owl"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_257_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_257_ch4_img1.png","plot_257_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":659,"reading_level":"Builder"}
