   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_257_15_18","title":"The Secret of the Haunted Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The old town library stood at the end of Willow Street like a forgotten relic, its stone fa\u00e7ade weathered and weary as if it had carried centuries of whispered secrets. Inside, the air was thick with the scent of aged paper and dust, a musty aroma that reminded Emily of her grandmother's attic. As she stepped onto the creaky wooden floors, she felt a shiver run down her spine, a blend of excitement and apprehension swirling within her. \n\n\u201cMax, do you feel that?\u201d she whispered, glancing down at her loyal golden retriever who was wagging his tail with unbridled enthusiasm. He seemed oblivious to the eerie stillness that enveloped the library, his nose twitching as he sniffed the air, searching for invisible clues. \n\n\u201cI swear, if one more book falls off a shelf, I\u2019m going to lose it,\u201d she muttered, remembering the latest incident that had sent the library patrons scattering like startled birds. Flickering lights, ominous shadows, and a string of unexplained noises had turned the once-bustling haven of stories into a ghost town. \n\nAs Emily meandered through the towering shelves, her fingers brushed against the spines of forgotten volumes, each one a portal to another world. But it was the thrill of the unknown that drew her in, deeper into the cavernous library. She had always been fascinated by mysteries\u2014ever since she devoured her first Nancy Drew book at age ten, she dreamed of becoming a detective. Perhaps this was her chance to prove herself, to unravel the threads of this peculiar enigma.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see what Mr. Jenkins knows,\u201d Emily decided, heading toward the back of the library where the librarian\u2019s office lay hidden behind a wall of encyclopedias. Mr. Jenkins was an enigma himself\u2014an elderly man with round spectacles that magnified his eyes to an almost comical size, he spoke in riddles and seemed to be as much a part of the library as the books themselves.\n\nWhen she reached the office, she knocked lightly, unsure if he was even there. To her surprise, the door creaked open slowly, revealing the faint glow of a desk lamp illuminating a sea of papers and old maps. Mr. Jenkins looked up, his white eyebrows knitting together in curiosity.\n\n\u201cAh, Emily! What brings you here?\u201d he asked, his voice gravelly but warm.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m investigating the strange happenings,\u201d she answered, her heart racing. \u201cWhat do you know about it?\u201d\n\nHe leaned back in his chair, a thoughtful look crossing his face. \u201cLegends say that this library is built on the site of an old estate, once owned by a notorious treasure hunter. They say he hid a map somewhere within these walls, a map that leads to unimaginable riches. But beware, for many who sought it out\u2026 disappeared.\u201d\n\nEmily felt a thrill of excitement, her mind racing with visions of treasure hunts and daring escapades. \u201cDo you think that\u2019s what\u2019s causing the disturbances? The search for the treasure?\u201d\n\nMr. Jenkins nodded solemnly. \u201cIt\u2019s certainly a possibility. The quest for treasure can stir up restless spirits, or perhaps something more\u2026 tangible.\u201d\n\nAs the words hung in the air, the lights flickered again, momentarily plunging the room into darkness. Emily clenched her fists, trying to suppress the swell of fear that bubbled within her. \u201cI need to find that map,\u201d she declared, determination igniting her spirit.\n\nWith a faint smile, Mr. Jenkins slid a dusty book across the table. \u201cThis might help. It\u2019s the history of the library. You\u2019ll find it contains old legends and perhaps a clue or two.\u201d\n\nEmily took the book and opened it to find yellowed pages filled with illustrations and tales of the town\u2019s past. But it was the crumpled piece of parchment that fell from between the pages that caught her breath. Unfolding it carefully, she gasped. There, hand-drawn and faded, was a map of the library with a marked \u2018X\u2019 in the lower section, near the children\u2019s reading nook.\n\n\u201cMax, look!\u201d she exclaimed, her pulse racing. \u201cThis could be it!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed from somewhere deep in the library, causing her heart to pound fiercely. She exchanged a wary glance with Max, who stood alert, ears perked. \u201cIt\u2019s time to uncover the truth about this haunted place!\u201d Emily declared with renewed fervor, gripping the map tightly.\n\nTogether, they ventured deeper into the shadows of the library, where secrets lay waiting to be discovered.  \n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]  \nAs Emily stands inside the dimly lit library, surrounded by towering shelves and dusty books, her expression is a blend of wonder and apprehension. Max, her loyal dog, sits beside her, his nose twitching in anticipation. The atmosphere is thick with mystery, the flickering lights casting dancing shadows that hint at the secrets hidden within the library's walls.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]  \nAmidst a tense moment, the flickering lights reveal Emily's shocked expression as she clutches a crumpled treasure map, a sense of urgency in her eyes. The room is filled with an eerie tension, shadows looming around her while Max stands protectively at her side, alert to the unseen dangers lurking nearby.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is Emily's main goal in this chapter?","options":["To find the treasure map","To scare away patrons","To meet Mr. Jenkins","To close the library"],"correct_answer":"To find the treasure map"},{"question":"Who is Mr. Jenkins?","options":["The town mayor","A mysterious librarian","Emily's teacher","A treasure hunter"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious librarian"},{"question":"What strange occurrences have been happening in the library?","options":["Books falling off shelves and flickering lights","New books arriving","Visitors coming in droves","Renovations being made"],"correct_answer":"Books falling off shelves and flickering lights"},{"question":"What does Emily discover that excites her in the librarian's office?","options":["A new book","A treasure map","A ghost","A diary"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"What does Emily's determination reveal about her character?","options":["She is fearful and hesitant","She is adventurous and curious","She is uninterested in mysteries","She is shy and reserved"],"correct_answer":"She is adventurous and curious"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_257_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_257_ch1_img1.png","plot_257_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":857,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
