   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_257_15_18","title":"The Secret of the Haunted Library","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Emily stood in the middle of the library's grand reading room, her heart racing as the flickering lights cast eerie shadows across the timeworn wooden shelves. The scent of aged paper and dust filled the air, a reminder of the secrets that lay hidden in this sanctuary of stories. She glanced down at Max, who was tugging at his leash, eager to explore the nooks and crannies of this mysterious place. \n\n\u201cOkay, buddy,\u201d Emily whispered, trying to quell her own rising anxiety. \u201cLet\u2019s stick together. There has to be a logical explanation for all of this.\u201d \n\nThe library had always been a refuge for her, a place where she could lose herself in novels that transported her to far-off lands. But now, as she surveyed the dimly lit corners and towering stacks, an unsettling feeling gripped her. Was it just her imagination, or did the library seem to be holding its breath, waiting for something to happen?\n\nMax suddenly perked up, his ears standing alert. He began to sniff the air, then darted toward a collection of ancient tomes sitting on a rickety table. Emily followed closely, her curiosity piqued. When she reached him, he was pawing at an ornate, leather-bound volume, its spine cracked and faded. \n\n\u201cWhat's got you so excited?\u201d Emily knelt down beside him, brushing her fingers over the book\u2019s surface. It felt oddly warm, as though it had been recently touched. She opened it, revealing yellowed pages filled with handwritten notes. A chill ran down her spine; the handwriting was spidery and barely legible, yet it piqued her detective instincts. \n\n\u201cMax, look!\u201d she exclaimed, flipping through the pages. \u201cIt\u2019s a diary! We might find some clues about this place.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a loud thud echoed from the far end of the aisle, causing both Emily and Max to jump. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d she breathed, glancing around as a shiver rippled through her. \u201cLet\u2019s check it out.\u201d \n\nAs they crept down the aisle, the tension thickened. The dim light flickered again, and Emily\u2019s pulse quickened. They rounded the corner to find Mr. Jenkins, the librarian, standing by a toppled shelf, his expression one of utter dismay. \n\n\u201cMr. Jenkins!\u201d Emily called out, her voice trembling slightly. \u201cAre you okay?\u201d\n\nHe looked up, his brow furrowed. \u201cJust a little\u2026 accident,\u201d he muttered, brushing dust off his glasses. \u201cBut you shouldn\u2019t be here. It\u2019s not safe.\u201d \n\n\u201cNot safe?\u201d Emily challenged, her determination flaring. \u201cThere\u2019s something strange going on, and we\u2019re going to find out what it is. Have you heard the noises at night? The lights?\u201d \n\nMr. Jenkins hesitated, his eyes darting to the shadows. \u201cSometimes, old buildings have a way of revealing their secrets. But some secrets are better left undiscovered.\u201d \n\nEmily felt an unsettling weight in his words. What was he hiding? \n\n\u201cI found this diary,\u201d she said, holding it out for him to see. \u201cIt might have some clues about the library\u2019s history.\u201d \n\nMr. Jenkins\u2019 eyes widened briefly, then narrowed as he took a step closer. \u201cWhere did you find that?\u201d \n\n\u201cOver there,\u201d Emily gestured toward the table, feeling a mix of unease and excitement. \n\n\u201cI didn\u2019t think anyone would find it again\u2026\u201d he trailed off, lost in thought. \n\nBefore she could ask more, an ominous creaking filled the air as the lights flickered violently, plunging them into darkness. Emily\u2019s heart raced as she grabbed Max\u2019s collar, unsure of what was happening. \n\nA moment later, the lights returned, but something had changed; the air felt charged with an energy she couldn\u2019t quite grasp. She looked at Mr. Jenkins, who seemed more pale than before, his eyes darting nervously. \n\n\u201cPerhaps it\u2019s time you two left,\u201d he said, his voice barely a whisper. \n\n\u201cNo!\u201d Emily insisted, drawing herself up. \u201cWe\u2019re staying. I want to know the truth.\u201d \n\nWith that declaration, she felt a sudden rush of resolve. The library had mysteries to reveal, and she would be the one to uncover them. \n\nAs they took a step back toward the reading room, Emily noticed a flicker of movement from the corner of her eye\u2014a shadow darting from the stacks. \u201cDid you see that?\u201d she whispered, her pulse racing. \n\n\u201cWhat?\u201d Max barked softly, sensing her tension. \n\n\u201cIt\u2019s time to follow the clues,\u201d she murmured, her voice steady. But what awaited them in the shadows? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] captures Emily kneeling beside Max, examining the aged diary with a sense of wonder and determination. The warm glow of the library lights contrasts with the cool shadows, illuminating Emily\u2019s intense gaze as she shares the moment with her loyal dog. Dust motes dance in the air, hinting at the secrets waiting to be discovered.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] depicts the moment of darkness as the lights flicker violently. Emily stands protectively in front of Max, a look of fierce determination on her face, while Mr. Jenkins appears more distraught, standing amongst the shadows of the library. The atmosphere is charged with tension, emphasizing the unknown dangers that lurk within the haunted library.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What discovery does Emily make in the library?","options":["A treasure chest","A leather-bound diary","A haunted painting","An old map"],"correct_answer":"A leather-bound diary"},{"question":"How does Mr. Jenkins react to Emily\u2019s discovery?","options":["He ignores it","He seems alarmed","He is excited","He is confused"],"correct_answer":"He seems alarmed"},{"question":"What happens when the lights flicker violently?","options":["The library is destroyed","They find the treasure","The atmosphere becomes tense","Emily leaves"],"correct_answer":"The atmosphere becomes tense"},{"question":"What does Emily resolve to do despite Mr. Jenkins\u2019 warnings?","options":["Leave the library","Uncover the truth","Forget about the diary","Go home"],"correct_answer":"Uncover the truth"},{"question":"What does Max sense when the lights flicker?","options":["Happiness","Fear","Curiosity","Confusion"],"correct_answer":"Fear"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_257_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_257_ch2_img1.png","plot_257_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":849,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
