   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_258_11_14","title":"The Great Chocolate Caper","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Mia's heart raced as she scanned the crowd, the enticing aroma of chocolate wafting through the air. The festival was a swirl of colors\u2014bright balloons danced above booths decorated with ribbons, while the laughter of children mixed with the cheerful chatter of adults. But something felt wrong. The pedestal that had held the magnificent chocolate sculpture was bare, the crowd's buzz now replaced by whispers of disbelief.\n\n\u201cDid you see the look on Ms. Choco's face?\u201d Jake exclaimed, nudging his sister. \u201cShe looked like she\u2019d seen a ghost! We have to find out who did this!\u201d\n\nMia nodded, her mind already racing with possibilities. \u201cLet\u2019s start with Ms. Choco. She knows everyone in town and probably has a theory about who might be involved.\u201d Together, they squeezed through the throngs of festival-goers, their excitement mingling with a growing sense of urgency.\n\nAs they approached Ms. Choco\u2019s stall, a whimsical setup filled with intricately decorated chocolate cakes and confections, Mia caught a glimpse of the eccentric chocolatier. Ms. Choco\u2019s wild, curly hair bounced as she animatedly spoke to a group of children who eagerly clutched chocolate bars. There was a sparkle of mischief in her eyes, but beneath it, Mia could sense a tide of worry.\n\n\u201cMs. Choco!\u201d Mia called out, gripping Jake\u2019s arm tightly. \u201cWe need your help! The chocolate sculpture is gone!\u201d\n\nThe chocolatier turned, her expression shifting from joy to concern. \u201cOh dear! This is terrible news! I had spent months preparing for that sculpture!\u201d Her voice trembled slightly, revealing her deep connection to the festival. \u201cBut I have a suspicion...\u201d\n\nMia leaned closer, eager for the next piece of the puzzle. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\n\nMs. Choco lowered her voice, glancing around as if someone might be listening. \u201cThere\u2019s been talk of a rival chocolatier who wanted to sabotage the festival. His name is Mr. Bitterman, and he\u2019s been acting strange lately.\u201d \n\nJust then, the chatter of the crowd hit a crescendo as a loud crash echoed from a nearby stall. Chocolate bars and fudge splattered across the ground, and Mia felt her stomach knot. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d she gasped.\n\nBefore they could investigate, they heard a familiar voice, \u201cMia! Jake!\u201d It was their friend Max, his face pale with shock. \u201cYou won\u2019t believe it! I saw someone running away from the sculpture just before it went missing!\u201d \n\n\u201cWho was it?\u201d Jake asked, his eyes wide.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but I think they went toward the alley behind the festival!\u201d Max exclaimed, pointing with urgency.\n\nMia exchanged a quick glance with Jake. This was the lead they needed! But the thought of following a potential thief sent a shiver down her spine. \u201cWe can\u2019t just run after them. We need a plan,\u201d she said, the weight of responsibility settling on her shoulders.\n\n\u201cWe could split up. I can distract the crowd at Ms. Choco\u2019s stall while you guys sneak around back!\u201d Jake suggested, his adventurous spirit shining through.\n\nMia hesitated, her heart racing with apprehension. \u201cBut what if something happens to you?\u201d \n\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry! I can handle myself,\u201d Jake replied, determination flashing in his eyes. \n\nMia sighed, torn between fear and her brother's bravery. \u201cAlright, but we have to be careful and stick to the plan!\u201d\n\nAs they prepared to execute their scheme, Mia felt a mix of excitement and dread. Would they uncover the chocolate thief before the festival fell apart? \n\nWith their hearts pounding, Mia and Jake exchanged a determined nod, ready to dive deeper into the mystery.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs Mia and Jake stood in front of Ms. Choco\u2019s colorful stall, vibrant chocolates twinkled under the sun. Ms. Choco, with her wild hair and expressive eyes, animatedly discussed the festival with a group of eager children, embodying the joy of the Chocolate Festival.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nIn a tense moment, Max urgently shares his discovery about the mysterious figure running away from the sculpture. The trio stands on the edge of excitement and fear, the bustling festival behind them, unaware of the theft that could change everything.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ms. Choco reveal about a potential rivalry?","options":["She has no idea who stole it","Mr. Bitterman is acting strangely","She's planning to leave the festival","She suspects the kids did it"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Bitterman is acting strangely"},{"question":"Who does Max say he saw running away?","options":["Jake","Mia","A mysterious figure","Ms. Choco"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious figure"},{"question":"What plan do Mia and Jake come up with?","options":["To call the police","To split up and follow clues","To give up","To confront Ms. Choco"],"correct_answer":"To split up and follow clues"},{"question":"How does Mia feel about the plan at first?","options":["Excited","Confident","Nervous","Indifferent"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What is the main conflict introduced in this chapter?","options":["Mia and Jake argue","A chocolate spill at the festival","The theft of the chocolate sculpture","Ms. Choco's secret recipe"],"correct_answer":"The theft of the chocolate sculpture"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_258_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_258_ch2_img1.png","plot_258_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":686,"reading_level":"Builder"}
