   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_258_11_14","title":"The Great Chocolate Caper","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the sun dipped low in the sky, painting the bustling town square in hues of gold and pink, Mia and Jake felt a surge of determination. The Chocolate Festival sparkled with vibrant stalls, each offering delicious treats and sweet delights. But at the center of it all stood the empty pedestal that had once housed the grand prize chocolate sculpture, the crowd's gasps echoing in their ears. \n\n\u201cLooks like it\u2019s time for a chocolate mystery!\u201d Mia announced with a confident grin, her eyes twinkling like the twinkling fairy lights strung overhead. Jake nodded, clutching a map of the festival, filled with marked locations of chocolatiers they still needed to investigate.\n\n\u201cWhere to next?\u201d he asked eagerly, his adventurous spirit igniting.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s head to Ms. Choco\u2019s stall first,\u201d Mia suggested, recalling the eccentric chocolatier\u2019s odd behaviors and peculiar recipes. As they maneuvered through the throngs of festival-goers, the sweet scent of melting chocolate surrounded them, tempting their taste buds and distracting them from their mission.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWhen they reached Ms. Choco\u2019s stall, it was a kaleidoscope of colors and flavors. Chocolate sculptures of all shapes and sizes decorated the counter, like a gallery of sweet art. Ms. Choco was there, her wild hair sticking out in every direction, her apron stained with chocolate splatters. \n\n\u201cMia! Jake! Have you found the sculpture yet?\u201d she asked, her voice a melodious mix of excitement and worry.\n\n\u201cNot yet,\u201d Mia replied, \u201cbut we\u2019re on the case. Did you see anyone suspicious around your stall?\u201d\n\nMs. Choco\u2019s eyes narrowed, her expression turning serious. \u201cWell, I did notice Mr. Bitterman lurking near the sculpture earlier. He was muttering to himself about 'the best chocolate ever.' But I thought nothing of it\u2026 until now.\u201d\n\nJake\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cWe already talked to him! He gave us a clue about the thief being someone unexpected. Do you think he was trying to warn us?\u201d\n\n\u201cPerhaps,\u201d Ms. Choco said thoughtfully. \u201cOr maybe he knows more than he\u2019s letting on.\u201d \n\nJust then, a loud commotion erupted from the nearby candy stall. The siblings exchanged glances and raced toward the noise. As they rounded the corner, they spotted Mr. Bitterman arguing with a group of festival-goers.\n\n\u201c\u2014I\u2019m telling you, I had nothing to do with it!\u201d he shouted, his face flushed with frustration.\n\n\u201cThen why were you so close to the sculpture?\u201d a festival-goer challenged, crossing his arms.\n\nMia and Jake paused, trying to piece together the situation. Suddenly, Jake\u2019s eyes lit up. \u201cWhat if the thief is someone we haven\u2019t even considered yet?\u201d\n\n\u201cLike who?\u201d Mia asked.\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s someone trying to frame Mr. Bitterman!\u201d he suggested, his voice rising with excitement. \n\nMia thought for a moment. \u201cYou could be right. But who would go to such lengths?\u201d\n\nThey decided to confront Mr. Bitterman. As they approached, Mia felt a mix of nerves and determination. \u201cMr. Bitterman! Can we talk?\u201d she called out.\n\nAs he turned, a flash of guilt passed over his face, but he quickly masked it with annoyance. \u201cWhat now?\u201d\n\n\u201cDid you see anyone else near the sculpture?\u201d Mia pressed, her heart racing. \n\nHis expression softened slightly. \u201cThere was someone, yes. A figure in a cloak. Not just anyone, but\u2026 someone familiar.\u201d \n\n\u201cWho?\u201d Jake asked, his voice barely above a whisper.\n\nBefore Mr. Bitterman could answer, a sudden crash interrupted them. A small boy had knocked over a pile of chocolate bars. Everyone turned to look, and in that moment, Mia caught sight of a figure darting away from the market square, a dark cloak billowing behind them.\n\n\u201cFollow that figure!\u201d Mia shouted, adrenaline coursing through her veins as they sprinted after the mysterious figure, hearts pounding like the thumping drums of the festival.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they chased the cloaked figure through the crowds, the sweet scent of chocolate mingled with the tension in the air. They could feel their excitement rising, knowing they were close to uncovering the truth. \n\n\u201cJake, do you remember which direction the art supply store is?\u201d Mia yelled over her shoulder.\n\n\u201cYeah! It\u2019s right past the apple bobbing booth!\u201d he replied, determination glinting in his eyes.\n\nThe figure glanced back, and for a brief moment, Mia caught a glimpse of a familiar face. \u201cIs that\u2026?\u201d she started, her mind racing.\n\n\u201cKeep going!\u201d Jake urged, and together they pushed through the crowd, closing in on their elusive suspect.\n\nThe mystery was about to unfold, and as the festival buzzed around them, Mia and Jake knew they were on the brink of a delicious revelation.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who do Mia and Jake decide to talk to at the Chocolate Festival?","options":["Mr. Bitterman","Ms. Choco","The festival-goers","The cloaked figure"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Choco"},{"question":"What does Ms. Choco reveal about Mr. Bitterman?","options":["He stole the sculpture","He was seen near the sculpture","He is a friend","He was at home"],"correct_answer":"He was seen near the sculpture"},{"question":"What unexpected clue does Mr. Bitterman provide?","options":["A recipe","A figure in a cloak","A chocolate bar","A map"],"correct_answer":"A figure in a cloak"},{"question":"What does Mia suggest about the thief?","options":["It's someone familiar","It's Mr. Bitterman","It's Ms. Choco","It's a festival-goer"],"correct_answer":"It's someone familiar"},{"question":"What action do Mia and Jake take at the end of the chapter?","options":["They give up","They chase the cloaked figure","They eat chocolate","They go home"],"correct_answer":"They chase the cloaked figure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_258_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_258_ch5_img1.png","plot_258_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":767,"reading_level":"Builder"}
