   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_258_15_18","title":"The Great Chocolate Caper","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun was just starting to dip below the horizon, casting a warm amber glow over the bustling town square. Mia stood at the edge of the crowd, her heart racing with excitement. The annual Chocolate Festival was the highlight of the year for their small town of Sweetvale, where the air was thick with the mouthwatering scent of cocoa. The town square was adorned with colorful stalls, each brimming with delectable treats: chocolate-covered strawberries, truffles, and fudge that glistened in the soft light. Laughter and chatter filled the air, creating a symphony of joy as festival-goers indulged in their sweet fantasies.\n\nMia, a fifteen-year-old with a knack for solving puzzles, scanned the crowd for her younger brother, Jake. He was a curious eleven-year-old, always up for an adventure, especially when chocolate was involved. Just as she spotted his messy dark hair bobbing between a group of teenagers, the cheerful jingle of the festival\u2019s theme song was interrupted by an urgent shout.\n\n\u201cHelp! Someone has stolen the grand prize sculpture!\u201d A voice rang out, piercing through the festive atmosphere, and suddenly, the joyous laughter turned to gasps of disbelief.\n\nMia's heart sank into her stomach. The grand prize was a magnificent chocolate sculpture of a soaring eagle, crafted by Ms. Choco, the town's eccentric chocolatier known for her secret recipes and whimsical creations. It was the centerpiece of the festival, and without it, the event would lose its luster. She glanced at Jake, who looked up at her with wide, incredulous eyes.\n\n\u201cLooks like it\u2019s time for a chocolate mystery!\u201d Mia exclaimed, a grin spreading across her face despite the chaos around them.\n\nBefore they could make their way to the empty pedestal where the sculpture had stood, a crowd began to swarm around Ms. Choco\u2019s stall. The chocolatier, with her wild curls and flour-dusted apron, was pacing back and forth, her expression a mix of alarm and determination. The townsfolk murmured among themselves, casting curious glances toward the once-grand pedestal, now just a shadow of lost sweetness.\n\n\u201cWe have to talk to Ms. Choco,\u201d Mia declared, her eyes sparkling with resolve.\n\nAs they approached, Mia could see Ms. Choco\u2019s hands trembled slightly. \u201cThis is unprecedented! My masterpiece is gone!\u201d she cried, her voice cracking. \n\n\u201cMs. Choco,\u201d Mia said, stepping closer, \u201cdo you have any idea who might want to take it?\u201d\n\nThe chocolatier turned to Mia, her eyes wide and serious. \u201cThere are\u2026rumors about some rival chocolatiers,\u201d she whispered, glancing around as if to ensure no one was listening. \u201cEspecially with the prize being so prestigious. But I never thought\u2026\u201d Her voice trailed off. \n\nJake leaned in, his eyes gleaming with curiosity. \u201cDo you think someone from the festival could have done it?\u201d\n\n\u201cAnyone could be a suspect,\u201d Mia mused, pulling Jake closer. They exchanged conspiratorial glances, the thrill of the chase igniting a spark between them. \n\n\u201cBut we need to act fast!\u201d Mia insisted. \u201cThe festival starts in just a few hours.\u201d\n\n\u201cRight!\u201d Jake replied, his excitement matching hers. \u201cLet\u2019s follow the clues. If it\u2019s chocolate-related, we\u2019ll track it down!\u201d\n\nJust then, a shadow crossed in front of them, and they turned to see a tall figure in a dark coat passing by, his gaze fixed on them, a knowing smirk on his face. Mia felt a shiver run down her spine. Who was he? Was he connected to the theft? \n\n\u201cDid you see that guy?\u201d Jake asked, tugging at Mia\u2019s sleeve. \u201cHe looked suspicious.\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s follow him,\u201d Mia said, her detective instincts kicking into high gear. The thrill of an adventure loomed ahead, but they had to be cautious. This was more than just chocolate; it was about uncovering secrets, and they were ready to unravel the sweet mystery of the Great Chocolate Caper.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they set off through the lively festival, with sweet melodies and laughter surrounding them, Mia couldn't shake the feeling that they were stepping into a world of hidden dangers. The atmosphere was electric, but beneath the joyful facade lay the depth of intrigue they were about to explore.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe tension hung palpably in the air as they spotted the mysterious figure slipping into a darkened alley behind the stalls. Mia\u2019s heart raced; it was time for action.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event is taking place in Sweetvale?","options":["Chocolate Festival","Harvest Festival","Spring Festival","Winter Festival"],"correct_answer":"Chocolate Festival"},{"question":"Who is the eccentric chocolatier mentioned in the chapter?","options":["Ms. Choco","Ms. Cocoa","Mr. Fudge","Mr. Chocolate"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Choco"},{"question":"What do Mia and Jake decide to do after the sculpture goes missing?","options":["Go home","Eat more chocolate","Become detectives","Call the police"],"correct_answer":"Become detectives"},{"question":"What is the main conflict introduced in this chapter?","options":["A chocolate shortage in town","The theft of the grand prize sculpture","A chocolate-making competition","A feud between chocolatiers"],"correct_answer":"The theft of the grand prize sculpture"},{"question":"What clues do Mia and Jake suspect might lead to the thief?","options":["The weather","Rival chocolatiers","The festival's theme","The type of chocolate"],"correct_answer":"Rival chocolatiers"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_258_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_258_ch1_img1.png","plot_258_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":720,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
