   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_258_15_18","title":"The Great Chocolate Caper","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Mia and Jake stood at the edge of the bustling town square, where the air was thick with the sweet scent of chocolate. The festival was alive with laughter and the delightful chatter of festival-goers, but an undeniable cloud of tension loomed over the scene. The grand prize chocolate sculpture, a masterpiece crafted by the enigmatic Ms. Choco, was still absent from its pedestal, and the murmurs of disbelief echoed in their ears like an ominous drumbeat.\n\n\u201cDid you see how everyone reacted?\u201d Jake said, his eyes alight with excitement. \u201cIt was like a scene from a movie! I can\u2019t believe the chocolate sculpture is really gone.\u201d\n\nMia frowned, her mind racing with possibilities. \u201cThis isn\u2019t just some prank, Jake. Whoever took it must have a reason. We need to find out what happened.\u201d She scanned the crowd, noting the faces of their neighbors, each one shadowed by worry and suspicion.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe vibrant stalls around them, draped in colorful bunting, seemed less inviting now, transformed into a maze of potential suspects. As Mia and Jake began their investigation, they spotted Ms. Choco standing by her stall, her hands trembling as she dabbed at her eyes with a frilly handkerchief. \u201cMy sculpture\u2026 it\u2019s irreplaceable,\u201d she sobbed, her voice thick with despair. \u201cWhat will I do without it?\u201d\n\n\u201cMs. Choco!\u201d Mia called, darting toward the chocolatier, who had become a local legend for her delectable confections and bizarre yet brilliant recipes. \u201cCan you tell us when you last saw the sculpture?\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2026 I set it up yesterday,\u201d Ms. Choco replied, her gaze drifting to the empty pedestal. \u201cIt was perfect! My creation was meant to symbolize the heart of Sweetvale. But this morning, it was gone!\u201d\n\nJake nudged Mia. \u201cWe should check the stalls. Maybe someone saw something.\u201d\n\nThe siblings split up, each moving cautiously through the throng of festival-goers. Mia approached the stall of Mr. Ganache, a gruff chocolatier known for his bitter chocolate but sweeter personality. \u201cMr. Ganache, did you notice anything unusual this morning?\u201d she asked, her voice steady.\n\nHe scratched his beard, his dark eyes narrowing in thought. \u201cJust the usual, I suppose. People getting their sugar fix before the festival. But,\u201d he paused, glancing around, \u201cI did see someone lurking near the sculpture last night. A shadowy figure. Sorry, don\u2019t remember much else.\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s heart raced. A shadowy figure? It was a lead, albeit a vague one. She relayed the information to Jake, who had just returned, his arms laden with chocolate samples.\n\n\u201cDid you find anything?\u201d he asked eagerly, his mouth half-full.\n\n\u201cMr. Ganache saw someone near the sculpture last night,\u201d Mia replied. \u201cWe need to find out who it was.\u201d She rubbed her temples, frustration creeping in. \u201cBut how?\u201d\n\nAt that moment, a loud crash echoed from the direction of the festival stage, drawing the attention of the crowd. Mia and Jake exchanged worried glances before racing toward the commotion. As they reached the front, they saw a group of teenagers gathered around a toppled stack of chocolate boxes, the contents spilling like marbles across the cobblestones.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Jake shouted, pointing. \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 that\u2019s the box from Ms. Choco\u2019s stall!\u201d\n\n\u201cSomeone\u2019s getting away,\u201d Mia exclaimed, spotting a figure darting through the crowd, their arms full of chocolate bars.\n\nWithout thinking, they both took off after the mysterious figure, weaving through stalls and oblivious festival-goers. Mia\u2019s heart pounded in her chest. \u201cWe can\u2019t let them escape!\u201d\n\nJust as they were closing the distance, the figure turned down an alley that led to the back of the town square. The siblings followed, fueled by adrenaline and determination. But as they rounded the corner, the alley was empty, save for a few stray chocolate wrappers fluttering in the breeze.\n\nMia leaned against the wall, panting. \u201cWe lost them\u2026 but who was that?\u201d \n\n\u201cWe need to find out,\u201d Jake insisted, his eyes bright with excitement. \u201cLet\u2019s ask around. Someone must have seen something.\u201d\n\nAs the siblings began their search anew, a shadow loomed over them, and a chilling realization settled in Mia\u2019s stomach. \u201cJake,\u201d she whispered, \u201cwhat if this isn\u2019t just about the sculpture? What if it goes deeper than we think?\u201d\n\nWith a shared nod of determination, they plunged back into the crowd, the mystery of the Great Chocolate Caper thickening with every passing moment.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mr. Ganache report seeing near the sculpture?","options":["A mysterious shadowy figure","Another chocolate sculpture","A group of children","A falling chocolate box"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious shadowy figure"},{"question":"How do Mia and Jake react when they hear the loud crash?","options":["They run towards it","They ignore it","They feel scared","They start eating chocolate"],"correct_answer":"They run towards it"},{"question":"What leads Mia and Jake to chase after a figure?","options":["The smell of chocolate","A tip from Mr. Ganache","A loud noise","A chocolate wrapper"],"correct_answer":"A tip from Mr. Ganache"},{"question":"What realization hits Mia at the end of Chapter 2?","options":["The festival will be canceled","The theft may involve more than just the sculpture","Jake is too young to help","Ms. Choco is the thief"],"correct_answer":"The theft may involve more than just the sculpture"},{"question":"What are the siblings' feelings toward the mystery they are involved in?","options":["Indifference","Excitement and determination","Fear and anxiety","Boredom"],"correct_answer":"Excitement and determination"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_258_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_258_ch2_img1.png","plot_258_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":732,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
