   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_259_7_10","title":"The Mystery of the Stolen Star","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Leo and Lila stood in front of the old oak tree. The leaves rustled like whispers from the stars above. \u201cThis is where the riddle led us, Lila!\u201d Leo exclaimed. \n\nThey looked around. The park was quiet, with only the soft glow of fireflies lighting the way. \u201cWhat do you think the clue means?\u201d asked Lila, tapping her chin. \n\n\u201cMaybe we should search the area!\u201d Leo suggested. They began to look closely at the tree. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Lila pointed at a knot in the tree trunk. \u201cIt looks like a little door!\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s open it!\u201d Leo said, his eyes shining with excitement. They gently pulled at the knot, and to their surprise, the small door creaked open. Inside, they found a rolled-up piece of paper. \n\n\u201cThis must be the next clue!\u201d Lila said, carefully unrolling it. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe paper held a drawing of the town\u2019s planetarium. \u201cIt looks like we need to go back there!\u201d Leo said, feeling a rush of energy. \n\nAs they hurried to the planetarium, Lila said, \u201cWhat if someone has already taken the star map there?\u201d \n\n\u201cThen we need to be quick! We can\u2019t let the stargazing event be ruined!\u201d Leo replied, determination in his voice. \n\nAt the planetarium, they noticed Mr. Cosmos pacing outside. \u201cThere you are! I\u2019ve been looking for you!\u201d he called out. \n\n\u201cWe found a clue!\u201d Lila shouted. \u201cIt leads us here!\u201d \n\nMr. Cosmos\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cA clue? What does it say?\u201d \n\n\u201cIt shows the planetarium!\u201d Leo said, feeling a spark of hope. \n\nSuddenly, a shadow flickered behind the planetarium. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Lila whispered. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out!\u201d Leo said, heart racing. They tiptoed toward the shadow. \n\nBehind the building stood Miss Stella, holding the star map! \u201cI was just\u2026 uh\u2026 borrowing it for a moment!\u201d she said sheepishly. \n\n\u201cBut why?\u201d Lila asked, crossing her arms. \n\n\u201cI wanted to make a surprise for the stargazing event!\u201d Miss Stella explained, her cheeks turning pink. \u201cI was going to show everyone how to draw constellations.\u201d \n\nLeo and Lila exchanged glances. \u201cThat\u2019s a great idea, but you should have asked!\u201d Leo said. \n\nMiss Stella nodded. \u201cYou\u2019re right. I\u2019m sorry!\u201d \n\nLila smiled. \u201cLet\u2019s work together to make the event special!\u201d \n\nThe three of them hurried back to the park, carrying the star map. With teamwork, they set up telescopes and arranged the stars. \n\nAs the sky darkened, townsfolk gathered, excited to see the stars. Leo looked at Lila and smiled. \u201cWe solved the mystery, and now everyone can enjoy the stargazing!\u201d \n\nThe stars twinkled above them, and Leo whispered, \u201cThe stars have a story to tell, and we figured it out together!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Leo and Lila find inside the oak tree?","options":["A treasure chest","A rolled-up piece of paper","A telescope","A map of the park"],"correct_answer":"A rolled-up piece of paper"},{"question":"Who was holding the star map behind the planetarium?","options":["Mr. Cosmos","Lila","Leo","Miss Stella"],"correct_answer":"Miss Stella"},{"question":"What did Miss Stella want to do with the star map?","options":["Hide it","Make a surprise for the stargazing event","Give it away","Destroy it"],"correct_answer":"Make a surprise for the stargazing event"},{"question":"What lesson did Leo and Lila learn?","options":["To be quiet","To solve mysteries alone","The importance of teamwork and communication","To never trust anyone"],"correct_answer":"The importance of teamwork and communication"},{"question":"What did Leo whisper at the end of the chapter?","options":["The stars have a story to tell","Let's go home","I want ice cream","We did nothing"],"correct_answer":"The stars have a story to tell"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_259_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_259_ch5_img1.png","plot_259_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":450,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
