   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_259_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Stolen Star","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"With the starlit park glowing above them, Leo and Lila hurried through the rows of telescopes, their hearts racing with the thrill of adventure. The cheerful buzz of the crowd surrounded them, but all they could feel was the weight of the missing star map. \"We need to find out who took it!\" Lila declared, her fingers fidgeting with the edge of her jacket. \n\nThe twins decided their first stop would be Mr. Cosmos, the town's quirky astronomer. He was setting up his telescope under the grand oak tree, surrounded by colorful lights that twinkled like stars in the night sky. As they approached, they could see his wild hair standing on end and a pair of thick glasses perched precariously on his nose. \n\n\u201cMr. Cosmos!\u201d Leo called out, his voice almost lost in the crowd. The astronomer turned, a faint smile appearing on his face. \u201cAh, Leo! Lila! Have you come to gaze at the stars or do you seek something more?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe're investigating the stolen star map,\u201d Lila said, her eyes sparkling with determination. \u201cDid you see anything suspicious?\u201d\n\nMr. Cosmos rubbed his chin, a thoughtful expression crossing his face. \u201cWell, I did see Mrs. Pendergast lurking near the map display earlier. She loves to collect things, you know.\u201d \n\nJust as they were about to probe further, a loud commotion erupted nearby. A group of children had gathered around a telescope, arguing over who got to look through it first. Leo and Lila exchanged glances, then rushed over to see what was going on. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe scene was chaotic, with children shoving and yelling. \u201cIt\u2019s my turn! You had it last!\u201d one boy shouted, his face red with frustration. Lila jumped in, her quick wit taking over. \u201cHey! Why don\u2019t we all take turns? It\u2019s just like sharing the stars!\u201d \n\nWith a few persuasive words, she managed to quiet the crowd, and the children reluctantly agreed to share. Leo admired Lila\u2019s ability to diffuse a situation. It was a reminder of how well they worked together, balancing each other\u2019s strengths and weaknesses. \n\nOnce the telescope debacle was resolved, they returned to Mr. Cosmos, who was now frantically searching through a stack of star charts. \u201cI can\u2019t believe I lost it!\u201d he exclaimed, his voice cracking. \u201cThe original star map is more than just a decoration; it\u2019s the heart of our event!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Leo asked, concern bubbling in his stomach. \n\n\u201cIt tells the story of the constellations,\u201d Mr. Cosmos explained, his gaze darting around the park. \u201cBut if it\u2019s not found by midnight, the stargazing event may have to be canceled. We need to find it, and fast!\u201d \n\nLila\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cThis is worse than we thought. We might have to search every corner of the park. But where do we start?\u201d \n\nSuddenly, Leo spotted something glittering near the trees\u2014something unusual that could be a clue. \u201cLook! Over there!\u201d he pointed, excitement igniting in his voice. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they approached the shimmering object, a chilling feeling settled in their stomachs. Was this the clue they had been hoping for, or a trap laid out by the thief? They had to make a decision quickly. \n\n\u201cReady?\u201d Lila whispered, her heart pounding. \u201cLet\u2019s uncover the mystery of the stolen star map!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who do Leo and Lila first speak to about the stolen star map?","options":["Mrs. Pendergast","Mr. Cosmos","The Mayor","The Baker"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Cosmos"},{"question":"What does Mrs. Pendergast love to collect?","options":["Star maps","Telescopes","Things","Books"],"correct_answer":"Things"},{"question":"What does Lila suggest to calm the arguing children?","options":["To let one child look through first","To share the telescope","To wait until the stargazing event","To play a game"],"correct_answer":"To share the telescope"},{"question":"What is the significance of the original star map?","options":["It is decorative","It tells the story of the constellations","It belongs to Mr. Cosmos","It's only used for one event"],"correct_answer":"It tells the story of the constellations"},{"question":"What do Leo and Lila discover near the trees?","options":["A telescope","A clue","Another map","A book"],"correct_answer":"A clue"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_259_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_259_ch2_img1.png","plot_259_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":556,"reading_level":"Builder"}
