   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_259_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Stolen Star","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The sun dipped below the horizon, casting long shadows across the park that surrounded the Celestia Planetarium. Stars began to twinkle in the darkening sky, their light a beacon of hope for Leo and Lila. The twins stood at the entrance of the planetarium, the excitement of the stargazing event tinged with worry. \n\n\u201cThe stars have a story to tell, and we need to find out what it is!\u201d Leo exclaimed, his eyes gleaming with determination. Lila nodded, the thrill of the hunt coursing through her veins like a shooting star.\n\nThey decided to start their investigation with Mr. Cosmos. The local astronomer was known for his vast knowledge, but there was something mysterious about him. As they approached his weathered observatory, Lila whispered, \u201cDo you think he really knows more than he\u2019s letting on?\u201d\n\n\u201cI hope so,\u201d Leo replied, adjusting the strap of his telescope. \u201cHe\u2019s our best bet to find a lead.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe observatory was dimly lit, shadows dancing across the walls like the constellations above. Mr. Cosmos was hunched over a cluttered table, surrounded by charts and models of planets. He looked up, squinting through his glasses, and a warm smile broke across his face. \u201cAh, twins! What brings you here?\u201d\n\n\u201cMr. Cosmos,\u201d Lila started, her voice steady. \u201cThe star map has been stolen, and we need your help to find it.\u201d\n\nHis smile faded, replaced by a look of concern. \u201cI feared this day would come. The map is not just a treasure; it holds secrets of the universe. But I can\u2019t help if I don\u2019t know what you\u2019ve discovered.\u201d\n\nLeo quickly recounted their findings, including the shimmering clue they had spotted in the park\u2014the silver thread woven into the grass. \u201cIt feels like a breadcrumb,\u201d he said, \u201cbut it\u2019s leading us somewhere.\u201d\n\nMr. Cosmos leaned back in his chair, his expression serious. \u201cYou must tread carefully, children. The stars may guide you, but they can also mislead. There are those who would do anything to keep the secrets of the universe hidden.\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash interrupted their conversation. The door burst open, and a figure stumbled in\u2014Mia, the town\u2019s prankster. \u201cI saw someone sneaking around the observatory!\u201d she shouted, breathless. \u201cThey had something shiny!\u201d\n\nLila and Leo exchanged wide-eyed glances. \u201cDid you see who it was?\u201d Lila asked, her heart racing.\n\n\u201cNo,\u201d Mia replied, wiping sweat from her brow. \u201cBut they dropped this.\u201d She held out a glittering object, and as she dropped it onto the table, it rolled to a stop, revealing a small, intricately designed star-shaped pendant.\n\nLeo gasped. \u201cThat\u2019s the same design as the star map!\u201d \n\nA sudden chill filled the room, and Mr. Cosmos\u2019s expression darkened. \u201cThis is worse than I thought. The pendant belongs to someone who\u2019s been after the star map for years.\u201d \n\nThe twins felt a surge of determination mixed with fear. \u201cWho?\u201d Lila asked, her voice barely a whisper.\n\n\u201cSomeone in this room,\u201d Mr. Cosmos said ominously, his eyes scanning their faces. \u201cAnd I suspect it might be\u2026.\u201d\n\nBefore he could finish, the lights flickered, and the room was plunged into darkness. The twins could hear the rush of footsteps, then silence. Panic surged through Leo as he grabbed Lila\u2019s hand. \u201cWe need to figure this out now!\u201d\n\nWith their hearts pounding, they raced to the door, ready to confront whatever awaited them outside.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they stepped into the night, the stars shone down like watchful eyes, their stories waiting to be uncovered. \n\n\u201cWhere do we go from here?\u201d Lila asked, scanning the darkened park. \n\n\u201cThe stars might help us,\u201d Leo said, gazing up. \u201cLet\u2019s find that shining clue before it\u2019s lost forever!\u201d\n\nThe mystery of the star map loomed larger than ever, and their adventure was just beginning.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What object did Mia bring to Mr. Cosmos?","options":["A telescope","A star-shaped pendant","A star map","A book of constellations"],"correct_answer":"A star-shaped pendant"},{"question":"What did Mr. Cosmos warn Leo and Lila about?","options":["The stars can mislead you","They will find the star map quickly","They should leave the observatory","They need to gather more friends"],"correct_answer":"The stars can mislead you"},{"question":"What happened when the lights flickered?","options":["They found the star map","They heard footsteps and the room went dark","Mr. Cosmos left the room","Mia made a joke"],"correct_answer":"They heard footsteps and the room went dark"},{"question":"How did Leo feel about their investigation?","options":["Excited and determined","Bored and tired","Scared of the dark","Confused and lost"],"correct_answer":"Excited and determined"},{"question":"What did Leo suggest they do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Find more clues in the park","Go home and rest","Ask Mr. Cosmos for help","Leave Celestia"],"correct_answer":"Find more clues in the park"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_259_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_259_ch3_img1.png","plot_259_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":643,"reading_level":"Builder"}
