   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_259_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Stolen Star","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The stars twinkled brightly over Celestia as Leo and Lila stood outside the planetarium, gazing up at the night sky. The air was crisp, and a gentle breeze rustled the leaves above them. \u201cWe need to decode the mystery of the stolen star map,\u201d Leo said, determination lighting up his eyes. \u201cI think Mr. Cosmos might be hiding something more.\u201d\n\nThey decided to revisit Mr. Cosmos, the local astronomer whose vast knowledge of the cosmos was accompanied by an equally vast collection of secrets. The twins approached the door, their hearts racing. The sound of the door creaking open felt like the beginning of a new adventure. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nInside, the planetarium was dimly lit, casting a soft glow on the walls decorated with murals of planets and galaxies. Mr. Cosmos sat behind a desk cluttered with star charts and old telescope parts. His glasses were perched precariously on his nose as he peered through a pair of binoculars, seemingly lost in the universe. \n\n\u201cAh, Leo, Lila! How good to see you!\u201d he exclaimed, lowering the binoculars. \u201cWhat brings you back?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe need your help, Mr. Cosmos,\u201d Lila said, her voice steady despite the whirlwind of thoughts racing through her mind. \u201cWe found this pendant.\u201d She pulled it from her pocket, the silver glimmering under the soft light. \u201cDo you recognize it?\u201d\n\nMr. Cosmos examined the pendant closely, his brow furrowing. \u201cThis belonged to a friend of mine\u2026 someone who was very passionate about astronomy and the mysteries of the universe. But I thought it was lost long ago.\u201d His voice trailed off as a shadow crossed his face.\n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Leo asked, leaning forward, eager for answers.\n\n\u201cHe had a theory about the star map, a connection to a legend of lost stars that could grant the wish of anyone who found them,\u201d Mr. Cosmos explained, his eyes shimmering with nostalgia. \u201cBut it was just a myth\u2026 or was it?\u201d\n\n\u201cCould this be a clue?\u201d Lila wondered aloud, her mind racing with possibilities. If the pendant belonged to someone who believed in the legend, perhaps the star map was more important than they realized.\n\nAs they discussed the implications, Leo noticed a large telescope aimed at the sky through the planetarium\u2019s glass dome. \u201cWhat if we looked at the stars? Maybe they can guide us to the next clue.\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s do it!\u201d Lila exclaimed, her excitement infectious. They hurried over to the telescope, peering through the lens. The expanse of the universe unfolded before them in a breathtaking display of colors and twinkling lights.\n\nSuddenly, Leo gasped. \u201cLila, look! That constellation\u2026 it\u2019s different from the one on our star map!\u201d He pointed at a cluster of stars that seemed to form a different shape than he had seen before.\n\nThe realization hit them both at once. \u201cIt\u2019s a hidden message!\u201d Lila said, her voice bubbling with excitement. \u201cIf we can decipher it, we might find out who took the map!\u201d\n\nJust then, the lights flickered ominously, and the planetarium was plunged into darkness. Heart pounding, Lila fumbled for her phone, quickly turning on the flashlight feature. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?\u201d she whispered, fear creeping into her voice.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know! But we need to stay focused!\u201d Leo replied, pulling out a few pieces of paper from his backpack. \u201cLet\u2019s write down what we see, even in the dark!\u201d\n\nWith their phones casting a faint glow, they quickly sketched the new constellation, unaware that someone was watching them from the shadows, a figure cloaked in mystery.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they scribbled, Lila felt a surge of hope. They were getting closer\u2014closer to unraveling the mystery. \u201cWe can\u2019t give up now, Leo. The stars are telling us something, and we\u2019re almost there.\u201d\n\nLeo nodded, determination etched on his face. \u201cLet\u2019s keep going. The truth is out there, and we\u2019ll find it together!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Leo and Lila find at the planetarium?","options":["A telescope","A silver pendant","An old map","A space book"],"correct_answer":"A silver pendant"},{"question":"What was Mr. Cosmos's reaction to the pendant?","options":["He was indifferent","He recognized it","He didn\u2019t care","He was scared"],"correct_answer":"He recognized it"},{"question":"What did Leo see through the telescope that surprised him?","options":["A UFO","A new constellation","The moon","A shooting star"],"correct_answer":"A new constellation"},{"question":"What major event happened while they were in the planetarium?","options":["A meteor shower","The lights went out","A fire alarm","An earthquake"],"correct_answer":"The lights went out"},{"question":"What do Leo and Lila hope to achieve by studying the stars?","options":["Finding treasure","Solving the mystery","Watching a movie","Winning a prize"],"correct_answer":"Solving the mystery"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_259_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_259_ch4_img1.png","plot_259_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":653,"reading_level":"Builder"}
