   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_259_15_18","title":"The Mystery of the Stolen Star","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun dipped below the horizon, painting the sky in shades of violet and indigo as the town of Celestia prepared for its annual stargazing event. Lila stood under the grand archway of the planetarium, her fingers brushing against the wooden sign that read \u201cCelestial Wonders.\u201d Next to her, Leo adjusted his glasses, a spark of excitement lighting up his hazel eyes.\n\n\u201cDo you think Mr. Cosmos is going to show us the new telescope tonight?\u201d Lila asked, her voice tinged with anticipation. She had always admired the local astronomer, whose passion for the stars equaled her brother's own.\n\n\u201cOf course,\u201d Leo replied, his tone infused with earnestness. \u201cHe wouldn\u2019t miss this for the world. Plus, he was hinting about a secret feature he added. I can\u2019t wait to see it!\u201d \n\nAs they made their way inside, the dimly lit planetarium felt alive with the murmurs of eager townsfolk. The scent of popcorn wafted through the air, mixing with the faint aroma of old books and polished wood. Lila glanced around, her sharp eyes catching glimpses of familiar faces\u2014Mrs. Hawthorne, the librarian, who always had a new star fact to share, and Mr. Jensen, the town historian, wearing a sweater adorned with constellations.\n\nSuddenly, the sound of a commotion broke through the atmosphere of excitement. Leo\u2019s head snapped toward the source\u2014a small crowd had gathered around the main display case. Lila\u2019s heart raced as she followed her brother\u2019s gaze; their prized celestial star map was gone.\n\n\u201cNo!\u201d Leo exclaimed, rushing forward. \u201cIt can\u2019t be missing!\u201d\n\nLila pushed through the throng, her mind racing. The star map had been the centerpiece of the event, a beautifully illustrated guide to the constellations that had been handed down through generations. Without it, the stargazing would lose its magic. \n\n\u201cEveryone, please calm down!\u201d Mr. Cosmos\u2019s voice boomed, resonating with urgency. He stepped forward, his usual calm demeanor shaken. \u201cThe star map has indeed been stolen. We must act quickly to recover it before the evening begins.\u201d\n\nLila glanced at Leo, her brother\u2019s brow furrowed in concentration. This was not just a theft; it was a challenge. \u201cWe can\u2019t let this ruin the night,\u201d she said, determination settling in her voice. \u201cWe need to find out who did this.\u201d\n\nLeo nodded, his enthusiasm igniting a spark of inspiration. \u201cThe stars have a story to tell, and we need to find out what it is!\u201d His resolve echoed Lila\u2019s own. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s start by interviewing the townsfolk,\u201d Lila suggested. \u201cThey might have seen or heard something unusual.\u201d \n\nAs they began their search, Lila approached Mrs. Hawthorne first. \u201cDid you notice anything strange before the map went missing?\u201d\n\nThe librarian adjusted her glasses, her expression contemplative. \u201cActually, I did see Mr. Jensen leave early to take a phone call. He seemed rather flustered.\u201d \n\nLeo\u2019s eyes narrowed. \u201cThat\u2019s interesting. Let\u2019s investigate him next.\u201d \n\nThey found Mr. Jensen near the refreshment table, nervously tapping his foot. \u201cOh, Leo, Lila! You\u2019re just in time. Did you hear about the map?\u201d \n\n\u201cYeah,\u201d Lila interjected, trying to gauge his reaction. \u201cWhat were you doing before it went missing?\u201d \n\n\u201cI was merely answering a call! Nothing important, I assure you!\u201d His voice trembled slightly, and Lila exchanged a knowing glance with Leo. \n\nAs the investigation continued, they gathered clues and testimonies, piecing together a narrative that led them deeper into the heart of the mystery. With each conversation, the tension mounted, the stakes grew higher, and the impending stargazing event loomed ever closer.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nLila and Leo stood in the planetarium\u2019s main hall, the soft glow of the stars projected above them casting ethereal shadows across their faces. Leo\u2019s expression was one of fierce determination, while Lila\u2019s quick wit shone through as she contemplated their next move, her brow furrowed in thought.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check with Mr. Cosmos one more time,\u201d Leo said. \u201cHe might have some insight that we\u2019re missing.\u201d \n\nThey approached the astronomer, who was now pacing back and forth, a worried frown etched on his face. \u201cThe map is more than just a piece of paper,\u201d he said, his voice heavy with unspoken history. \u201cIt holds the knowledge of our past and the key to our future.\u201d\n\nTheir conversation was interrupted by a loud crash, reverberating through the planetarium. Leo and Lila exchanged panicked looks as they rushed toward the sound, hearts pounding with anticipation and fear. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe two twins entered the room to find a telescope toppled over, luminous lenses reflecting the ambient light like shards of shattered dreams. The atmosphere shifted, crackling with tension, as suspicion began to weave its way through the remaining townsfolk. \n\n\u201cWhoever did this is still here,\u201d Lila whispered fiercely to Leo, her eyes scanning the crowd, searching for clues.\n\nThe mystery deepened, and with it, their resolve grew stronger. They would uncover the truth, no matter how elusive it seemed, before the stars began their silent vigil above.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event is the town of Celestia preparing for?","options":["An art exhibit","A stargazing event","A science fair","A book festival"],"correct_answer":"A stargazing event"},{"question":"Who is the local astronomer mentioned in the chapter?","options":["Mr. Jensen","Mrs. Hawthorne","Mr. Cosmos","Leo"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Cosmos"},{"question":"What do Leo and Lila decide to do after discovering the map is missing?","options":["Ignore it","Call the police","Interview the townsfolk","Go home"],"correct_answer":"Interview the townsfolk"},{"question":"What does Lila notice about Mr. Jensen during their conversation?","options":["He is calm","He looks nervous","He is excited","He is angry"],"correct_answer":"He looks nervous"},{"question":"What happens when Leo and Lila approach Mr. Cosmos for information?","options":["He is happy","He is angry","He is worried","He is confused"],"correct_answer":"He is worried"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_259_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_259_ch1_img1.png","plot_259_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":838,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
