   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_259_15_18","title":"The Mystery of the Stolen Star","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The dark blanket of night enveloped Celestia, only punctuated by the silver glimmer of stars overhead. Leo stood beside his twin sister, Lila, at the edge of the town park, the familiar landscape transformed into a sea of shadows and shimmering lights. The park was adorned with glowing lanterns and telescopes set up by eager townsfolk, all waiting for the grand stargazing event. Yet, a heavy cloud of unease loomed over them, a shadow cast by the missing celestial star map.\n\nLila tapped her chin thoughtfully, her eyes scanning the bustling crowd. \u201cWe should start with the people who were closest to the map when it disappeared. Mr. Cosmos would be a good first target.\u201d Her quick wit often cut through Leo's more analytical approach, and together, they were a formidable team.\n\n\u201cRight, but we need to tread carefully. We don\u2019t know who might be involved,\u201d Leo replied, adjusting the strap of his backpack filled with a flashlight, a notebook, and a couple of snacks. He had meticulously prepared for this evening, knowing they might be out for hours.\n\nAs they made their way to the planetarium, the air crackled with a mixture of excitement and tension. Leo\u2019s thoughts drifted to the star map\u2014an intricate guide to the heavens that had taken years to create. To think that someone would steal it felt like a betrayal against the cosmos itself.\n\nUpon entering the planetarium, they were greeted by the sight of Mr. Cosmos, his tall figure silhouetted against the backdrop of a massive projection of constellations. His face, usually warm and inviting, was now etched with concern. \u201cAh, Leo, Lila,\u201d he said, his voice strained. \u201cI\u2019m afraid things have taken a turn for the worse.\u201d\n\nLila raised an eyebrow. \u201cWorse than the theft of the star map?\u201d\n\n\u201cYes,\u201d he sighed, running a hand through his graying hair. \u201cThe stargazing night is not just about the map; it\u2019s also about the stories behind each constellation. This year, we were meant to unveil a new story about the Celestial Twins. Without the map, the event will feel incomplete.\u201d \n\nLeo exchanged a glance with Lila; the stakes were higher than they thought. \u201cDo you have any leads, Mr. Cosmos?\u201d Lila asked, her determination igniting.\n\n\u201cJust whispers,\u201d he murmured. \u201cThere\u2019s been talk of someone selling rare astronomical items online, and I suspect they might have acquired the map. I saw someone in the crowd earlier, wearing a dark hoodie, looking out of place. They left just before the theft was discovered.\u201d\n\nLeo\u2019s heart raced; they had a direction now. \u201cDo you remember anything else about the person?\u201d he pressed.\n\n\u201cNot much, just a glimpse. They seemed nervous, almost as if they were waiting for something,\u201d Mr. Cosmos replied shakily, glancing towards the telescope setups outside. \u201cI wish I had more to go on.\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go check the crowd,\u201d Lila suggested, her voice firm. They stepped outside, the stars twinkling above as if they were watching the unfolding drama below. As they walked through the park, they began to question the townsfolk who had mingled near the planetarium, searching for anyone who fit Mr. Cosmos's description.\n\nThey approached the mayor, a jovial man with a booming laugh that now seemed forced. \u201cMayor Thompson, did you see anyone suspicious?\u201d Leo inquired, noting the way the mayor\u2019s eyes darted away, unwilling to meet their gaze.\n\n\u201cSuspicious? Nah, just a bunch of excited folks looking at stars. It\u2019s a big night after all!\u201d He laughed nervously, but Leo sensed the underlying tension. \n\nJust then, Lila caught sight of a shadowy figure slipping through the trees at the edge of the park. \u201cHey! Wait!\u201d she called, instinctively running after them. The figure paused, glancing back, eyes wide with fear. \n\nIn that heartbeat, everything shifted. The figure turned to flee. \u201cLeo!\u201d Lila yelled, her voice cutting through the night air. The chase was on. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey dashed through the park, heartbeats pounding in sync with their footsteps against the gravel path. Lila felt a mix of excitement and dread. Who was this person? Why were they running?\n\nAs they chased the figure into the darkness, the thrill of the pursuit mingled with the weight of uncertainty. Leo\u2019s mind raced with questions, but the most pressing was: what if they were too late? \n\nSuddenly, the figure stumbled and fell, revealing a small satchel that had tumbled from their grasp. The contents spilled out\u2014scrolls, papers, and a familiar glimmer of gold. Lila gasped as she recognized a segment of the star map. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cStop!\u201d Leo shouted, and the figure turned, revealing a face that struck both twins as oddly familiar. \u201cYou!\u201d Lila exclaimed, her heart sinking. \u201cWhy did you take the map?\u201d\n\nAs the figure scrambled to their feet, the tension in the air thickened, and Leo and Lila braced themselves for a confrontation that would unravel the threads of the mystery they had begun to weave.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the primary objective of Leo and Lila in this chapter?","options":["To find the star map","To host the stargazing event","To ask Mr. Cosmos for help","To gather trivia about stars"],"correct_answer":"To find the star map"},{"question":"Who does Lila suggest they interrogate first?","options":["The mayor","Mr. Cosmos","The figure in the park","The townsfolk"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Cosmos"},{"question":"How does Mr. Cosmos react to the theft of the star map?","options":["He is indifferent","He is excited","He is deeply concerned","He blames the twins"],"correct_answer":"He is deeply concerned"},{"question":"What clues do Leo and Lila find about the potential thief?","options":["A dark hoodie and nervous behavior","A shiny telescope","A map of the park","An old book on astronomy"],"correct_answer":"A dark hoodie and nervous behavior"},{"question":"What emotion do Leo and Lila feel as they chase the figure?","options":["Fear","Excitement","Indifference","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_259_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_259_ch2_img1.png","plot_259_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":829,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
