   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"mystery_260_7_10","title":"The Case of the Disappearing Dog Treats","genre":"Mystery","sub_genre":"Detective","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Mia and Buddy stood outside the dog shelter. The sun was shining on the bright blue building. Mia could hear the happy barks of dogs waiting to be adopted.\n\n\u201cBuddy, we need to solve this mystery before the fundraiser!\u201d she said, determined. They walked towards the park, where the squirrels had been spotted.\n\nSuddenly, Buddy paused. His nose twitched. \u201cWhat is it, Buddy?\u201d Mia asked. \n\nHe sniffed the ground and wagged his tail. \u201cI think he smells something!\u201d Mia followed Buddy as he led her to a big oak tree. There, they found a pile of dog treat wrappers! \n\n\u201cMmm, these smell like the ones from Mrs. Jenkins\u2019 bakery!\u201d Mia exclaimed. She picked one up and examined it closely. \u201cLooks like the squirrels have been munching away!\u201d\n\nJust then, Mr. Whiskers appeared, his green eyes glinting in the sunlight. \u201cDid you find anything interesting?\u201d he asked slyly.\n\nMia narrowed her eyes. \u201cWe found wrappers, Mr. Whiskers. Do you know anything about the missing treats?\u201d\n\nMr. Whiskers flicked his tail. \u201cMaybe I do, maybe I don\u2019t. But I saw the squirrels with something shiny this morning.\u201d \n\n\u201cShiny?\u201d Mia\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat was it?\u201d \n\n\u201cCome with me, and I\u2019ll show you,\u201d he said with a grin. \n\nMia and Buddy followed Mr. Whiskers as he led them to a nearby bush. They peeked inside and gasped. There were a bunch of dog treats stolen from many dogs in the neighborhood! \n\n\u201cWow! Look at all those treats!\u201d Mia shouted. \u201cWe need to get them back!\u201d \n\n\u201cBut how?\u201d Buddy woofed, looking worried. \n\nSuddenly, a loud rustling came from the bushes. \u201cUh-oh, looks like we are not alone!\u201d Mia whispered. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMia\u2019s heart raced. Was it the squirrels? Or something else? \n\nJust then, the bushes shook again, and out popped a squirrel holding a bright blue collar in its tiny paws! \u201cYou\u2019ll never catch me!\u201d it squeaked, darting away with the collar.\n\nMia sprang into action. \u201cWe can\u2019t let it get away, Buddy! Run!\u201d They raced after the squirrel, dodging branches and leaping over rocks. \n\nAs they chased it, Mia thought of the upcoming fundraiser. \u201cWe need to catch that squirrel before the dogs lose their treats for good!\u201d \n\nBut the squirrel was fast\u2014much faster than they expected. They were getting closer, but would they catch it in time? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s the plan, Mia?\u201d Buddy barked, panting hard.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know! We have to think quickly!\u201d she replied, feeling the pressure. \n\nJust then, they reached a fork in the path. \u201cWhich way should we go?\u201d Mia asked, glancing at Buddy. They had to make a decision fast. \n\n\u201cLeft or right?\u201d Mia wondered aloud.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia find by the oak tree?","options":["A pile of dog treats","A shiny collar","A squirrel","A map"],"correct_answer":"A pile of dog treats"},{"question":"Who told Mia about the shiny object?","options":["Buddy","Mrs. Jenkins","Mr. Whiskers","The squirrels"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Whiskers"},{"question":"What color was the collar that the squirrel was holding?","options":["Red","Blue","Green","Yellow"],"correct_answer":"Blue"},{"question":"What did Mia and Buddy need to do before the fundraiser?","options":["Catch the squirrel","Find new treats","Go to the shelter","Play with the dogs"],"correct_answer":"Catch the squirrel"},{"question":"What decision did Mia have to make at the fork in the path?","options":["Which way to go","What to eat","When to rest","How to play"],"correct_answer":"Which way to go"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_260_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_260_ch3_img1.png","plot_260_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":448,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
