   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_177_7_10","title":"The Whispering City","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Urban Fantasy","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Sam and Lila raced through the bustling streets of the Whispering City. The sun was shining, and the buildings all seemed to smile. \"I can\u2019t believe we have to save the skyscrapers!\" Sam said, his eyes wide with excitement. \n\n\"But how?\" Lila asked, turning to Gus, the wise old skyscraper. Gus's windows glimmered as he replied, \"We need to gather the citizens. They must understand the importance of our voices.\"\n\nJust then, a loud rumble shook the ground. Sam and Lila looked up. The developer\u2019s big, black truck rolled into view, and it looked as mean as a lion waiting to pounce. \u201cOh no!\u201d cried Lila. \u201cHe\u2019s here already!\u201d\n\n\u201cWe have to act fast!\u201d Sam shouted. \u201cLet\u2019s head to City Square. We can talk to the people there!\u201d\n\nThey dashed to the square, where colorful stalls lined the streets. The air smelled like popcorn and sweet candy. Sam felt hopeful. Perhaps the people would listen!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nAs they approached the crowd, they heard a loud voice. \u201cListen up, folks!\u201d It was Mr. Greed, the developer. \u201cI\u2019m here to make this city better! We will have new, shiny buildings, and you will all love them!\u201d\n\n\u201cShiny doesn\u2019t mean better!\u201d Lila yelled, stepping forward. \u201cThe buildings already here have stories to tell!\u201d\n\n\u201cStories?\u201d Mr. Greed scoffed. \u201cWho cares about stories? They are just old bricks!\u201d\n\nThe crowd murmured, confused. Sam took a deep breath. \u201cBut they have feelings! They are alive! We can\u2019t just let them be destroyed!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, Gus's voice boomed from above. \u201cCitizens of Whispering City! We are not just buildings! We hold the city\u2019s history and dreams! Help us fight for our lives!\u201d\n\nThe crowd gasped. Some people seemed to understand. \u201cWe can\u2019t let them go!\u201d one woman shouted. \n\nBut then, Sam saw Mr. Greed smile. \u201cYou think you can stop me? I have the power of money!\u201d he said with a sneer.\n\nThe tension grew thick in the air. Would the people side with the skyscrapers or the developer? Sam felt the weight of the moment. He had to decide. \n\n\u201cLila, we need a plan. Fast!\u201d he said, his heart racing. \n\n\u201cWhat if...?\u201d Lila began, her eyes sparkling with a new idea.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWould they figure out a way to save the skyscrapers before it was too late?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mr. Greed want to do?","options":["Build new buildings","Protect the skyscrapers","Help the citizens","Make the city worse"],"correct_answer":"Build new buildings"},{"question":"What is Gus's role in this chapter?","options":["He is a citizen","He is a skyscraper","He is a developer","He is a teacher"],"correct_answer":"He is a skyscraper"},{"question":"Where do Sam and Lila go to gather support?","options":["City Square","A mall","Their school","A park"],"correct_answer":"City Square"},{"question":"What do the citizens need to understand about the skyscrapers?","options":["They are old","They are just buildings","They have stories to tell","They are ugly"],"correct_answer":"They have stories to tell"},{"question":"What feeling does Sam have at the end of the chapter?","options":["Happiness","Worry","Joy","Sleepiness"],"correct_answer":"Worry"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_177_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_177_ch3_img1.png","plot_177_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":391,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
