   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_180_7_10","title":"The Timekeeper's Challenge","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Urban Fantasy","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ben and Maria stood in the middle of the marketplace. The air was filled with strange smells and colorful sights. People in funny clothes hurried past them. \"Where do we start?\" Ben asked, scratching his head. \n\n\"We need to find the Clock of Changes,\" Maria replied, her eyes sparkling with excitement.\n\nSuddenly, a tiny sprite flew by, giggling and swirling around them. It was bright blue with sparkly wings. \"Catch me if you can!\" it squeaked, zooming away. \n\n\"Hey! Wait!\" Ben shouted, but the sprite was too fast. \n\n\"We have to follow it!\" Maria said, running after the sprite. They dashed through the crowd, dodging stalls and baskets of fruit. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey raced until they found themselves near a tall tower. \"Look!\" Maria pointed. There it was, the Clock of Changes, gleaming in the sunlight. But before they could celebrate, the sprite zapped in front of them. \n\n\"To reach the clock, you must solve my riddle!\" it chimed, bouncing up and down. \n\n\u201cOh, I love riddles!\u201d Maria exclaimed. \n\nThe sprite giggled. \u201cI\u2019m in the sky, but I\u2019m not a plane. I make clouds, but I\u2019m not the rain. What am I?\u201d \n\nBen frowned. \u201cHmm\u2026 What do you think, Maria?\u201d \n\n\u201cI think it\u2019s a cloud! No, wait! It could be the sun!\u201d she said, pacing back and forth. \n\nJust then, the sprite clapped its tiny hands. \u201cTime is running out! You have only one guess!\u201d \n\nBen took a deep breath. \u201cI think\u2026 it\u2019s the sun!\u201d he shouted. \n\nThe sprite burst into laughter. \u201cWrong! But good try!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, chaos erupted. The other sprites appeared, spinning around the clock and flinging sparkles everywhere. The air shimmered, and the clock began to tick backward. \n\n\u201cWe have to stop them!\u201d Maria yelled, her voice barely heard over the noise. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s push the sprites away!\u201d Ben suggested, waving his arms. They both jumped and swatted at the sprites. \n\n\u201cGo away, you little rascals!\u201d Maria laughed, trying to catch one. \n\nBut just as they thought they were making progress, the clock chimed loudly. It echoed across the marketplace. The world around them began to swirl. Colors mixed, shapes blurred, and before they knew it, everything went dark.\n\n\u201cBen! Maria! Hold on!\u201d \n\nBut it was too late. The darkness swallowed them up.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What must Ben and Maria solve to reach the Clock of Changes?","options":["A riddle","A puzzle","A test","A question"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What color is the sprite that challenges them?","options":["Red","Green","Blue","Yellow"],"correct_answer":"Blue"},{"question":"What happens to the clock after the sprite's riddle?","options":["It ticks backward","It stops","It shines brighter","It disappears"],"correct_answer":"It ticks backward"},{"question":"How do Ben and Maria feel when they first see the marketplace?","options":["Excited","Angry","Bored","Scared"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What do Ben and Maria do to try to stop the sprites?","options":["Run away","Try to catch them","Speak to them","Ignore them"],"correct_answer":"Try to catch them"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_180_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_180_ch3_img1.png","plot_180_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":381,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
