   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_180_7_10","title":"The Timekeeper's Challenge","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Urban Fantasy","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Ben and Maria stood in the bustling historical marketplace. The air was filled with the scent of spices and the sound of laughter. Bright colors surrounded them, from the merchants' stalls to the clothes of the people. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\"Wow, look at all this!\" Ben said, pointing at a stall with shiny trinkets. \"Can you believe we\u2019re really here?\"\n\nMaria grinned. \"I can. But we have to find the Clock of Changes. Time is running out!\"\n\nThey dashed through the crowd, dodging sellers and excited children. Suddenly, a small figure zipped past them. It was a time sprite, giggling as it twisted a sign that read, \"Beware of the Riddle!\"\n\n\"Did you see that?\" Ben exclaimed, wide-eyed. \"We need to be careful.\"\n\nAs they approached the Clock of Changes, it loomed before them, tall and ornate. Its hands spun wildly as if caught in a storm. Maria pointed. \"There it is! We need to figure out the sprite's riddle to stop it!\"\n\nJust then, the mischievous sprite appeared again. \"To fix the time, you must be brave. Answer my riddle, or you'll misbehave!\"\n\nBen and Maria exchanged nervous glances. \"What\u2019s the riddle?\" Maria asked, her voice steady.\n\n\"Listen closely,\" the sprite said, \"I'm not a bird, but I can fly. I have no feet, yet I travel high. What am I?\"\n\nBen scratched his head. \u201cIt\u2019s not a bird, but it flies. What could it be?\u201d\n\nMaria thought hard. \u201cWhat about\u2026 a kite! A kite can fly!\u201d\n\nThe sprite clapped its tiny hands, giggling. \u201cYou got it! Now, you must hurry!\u201d \n\nWith a flick of its wrist, the sprite pointed to the clock. \u201cYou must turn the hands back to the hour of the great feast. Do it quickly, or the past will be lost!\u201d\n\nBen and Maria nodded. Together, they reached for the clock's hands. They turned it slowly, the tick-tock echoing in the air. Suddenly, the clock glowed with a warm light.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Ben shouted, as the clock\u2019s hands began to move backward. \u201cIt\u2019s working!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut just then, the time sprites swarmed around them, laughing and swirling like a colorful storm. \u201cYou can\u2019t catch us!\u201d they chanted. \n\nMaria clenched her fists. \u201cWe must stay focused! Keep turning!\u201d\n\nWith determination, they turned the clock faster. The light grew brighter, and the sprites began to fade. Together, they shouted, \u201cWe can do this!\u201d\n\nThe hands finally stopped moving. The clock chimed loudly, and the marketplace shimmered. Ben and Maria exchanged excited glances. \n\n\u201cDid we do it?\u201d Ben asked, breathless.\n\nTheir surroundings began to shift, colors swirling around them. \u201cI think we did!\u201d Maria cheered. \n\nBut then, another portal appeared, pulling them through with a flash. \u201cLet\u2019s hope the next place is easier!\u201d Ben shouted as they vanished.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ben and Maria need to find?","options":["The Clock of Changes","A treasure map","A magic potion","A time sprite"],"correct_answer":"The Clock of Changes"},{"question":"What is the riddle given by the sprite?","options":["I am a kite","I am a bird","I am a plane","I am a cloud"],"correct_answer":"I am a kite"},{"question":"What do Ben and Maria have to do to the clock?","options":["Turn the hands back","Break the clock","Paint the clock","Hide the clock"],"correct_answer":"Turn the hands back"},{"question":"What happens when they turn the clock?","options":["The sprites disappear","The clock breaks","They get stuck","They travel to the future"],"correct_answer":"The sprites disappear"},{"question":"What do Ben and Maria hope for after fixing the clock?","options":["To go home","To have a feast","To meet more sprites","For the next place to be easier"],"correct_answer":"For the next place to be easier"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_180_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_180_ch4_img1.png","plot_180_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":466,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
