   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_172_11_14","title":"The Prophecy of the Forgotten Crown","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Prophecies","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"In the dusty attic of their grandmother's old house, Leo and Maya rummaged through boxes filled with forgotten treasures. Sunlight streamed through a small window, illuminating motes of dust dancing in the air. Leo, an adventurous thirteen-year-old with wild, untamed hair and an ever-present smirk, was determined to unearth something extraordinary. Maya, two years younger yet sharper and more thoughtful, followed closely behind, her eyes wide with curiosity.\n\n\"Come on, Leo! There has to be something cool up here,\" Maya urged, brushing aside a cobweb with the back of her hand.\n\nLeo grinned, \"I bet we\u2019ll find a pirate\u2019s treasure or an ancient relic! Just think about it!\u201d\n\nAs they combed through the clutter, Maya's fingers brushed against a rolled parchment tucked away in an old leather satchel. \u201cWhat\u2019s this?\u201d she wondered aloud, pulling it out with a flourish. The scroll was adorned with intricate patterns resembling leaves and waves, and the edges were frayed with age.\n\n\u201cWow! What does it say?\u201d Leo leaned in, his excitement bubbling like a fizzing potion. He could practically hear the whispers of adventure calling out to him.\n\nMaya carefully unrolled the scroll, revealing faded text that seemed to shimmer under the morning light. \u201cIt\u2019s a prophecy about a forgotten crown that can unite the four magical kingdoms,\u201d she read, her voice a mix of awe and disbelief. \u201cEarth, Water, Fire, and Air\u2026 it says the crown was lost long ago, and only the chosen ones can find it.\u201d\n\nLeo\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cSo, we could be those chosen ones! This is epic!\u201d He could already imagine their names echoing through the ages. But Maya\u2019s brow furrowed. \u201cLeo, what if it\u2019s just a story? What if we\u2019re not meant for this?\u201d\n\n\u201cWhy not?\u201d Leo shot back, his impatience flaring. \u201cSomeone has to find it! And who better than us?\u201d\n\nBefore Maya could respond, a sudden rustling noise interrupted them. They turned to see a tiny figure darting across the attic\u2014a sprite, no taller than Leo\u2019s hand, with sparkling wings that glimmered like gemstones.\n\n\u201cHide it! Hide it!\u201d the sprite shrieked in a voice like tinkling bells. \u201cYou don\u2019t know who\u2019s after it!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nLeo and Maya exchanged bewildered glances. \u201cWho are you?\u201d Maya asked, her heart racing with a mixture of fear and fascination.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m Cora,\u201d the sprite introduced herself, her eyes darting nervously. \u201cAnd you\u2019ve just opened a door that should have remained closed. The crown is powerful, and there are others out there who want it for themselves.\u201d\n\nLeo\u2019s adventurous spirit surged. \u201cThen we have to find it first!\u201d he declared.\n\nCora hesitated, glancing back at the attic entrance as if sensing danger lurking beyond. \u201cIt\u2019s not just a matter of finding it. You\u2019ll face challenges\u2014riddles and guardians who protect the crown. And you must be sure of who you are.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Maya asked, feeling a knot of anxiety twist in her stomach.\n\n\u201cThe prophecy speaks of unity, but it also reveals truths about your family\u2019s past. You can\u2019t just rush into this without understanding what you\u2019re up against,\u201d Cora warned, her tiny face serious.\n\nAs the weight of the scroll\u2019s words settled upon them, Leo felt a flicker of doubt. Could they truly be the ones destined to save the kingdoms? But the thrill of adventure ignited his spirit once more. \u201cWe\u2019ll figure it out,\u201d he replied, determination in his voice. \u201cWe have to try.\u201d\n\nWith Cora guiding them, the siblings prepared to embark on a journey that could change everything. But as they left the attic behind, shadows gathered at the edges of their thoughts. What if they weren\u2019t enough?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe air crackled with anticipation as they stepped into the unknown, the fate of the four kingdoms resting in their hands.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Leo and Maya find in their attic?","options":["A treasure map","An ancient scroll","A magical book","A lost key"],"correct_answer":"An ancient scroll"},{"question":"What does the prophecy say?","options":["A crown can unite the kingdoms","A treasure will be found","A battle will begin","A spell will be cast"],"correct_answer":"A crown can unite the kingdoms"},{"question":"Who is Cora?","options":["A guardian","A sprite","A teacher","A warrior"],"correct_answer":"A sprite"},{"question":"What is Leo's personality like?","options":["Cautious and nervous","Adventurous and headstrong","Thoughtful and quiet","Lazy and indifferent"],"correct_answer":"Adventurous and headstrong"},{"question":"What emotion does Maya feel about the prophecy?","options":["Joy","Doubt","Anger","Fear"],"correct_answer":"Doubt"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_172_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_172_ch1_img1.png","plot_172_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":650,"reading_level":"Builder"}
