   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_172_11_14","title":"The Prophecy of the Forgotten Crown","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Prophecies","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the warm afternoon sun poured through the attic window, Leo and Maya carefully unfurled the ancient scroll that had sent their hearts racing. The faded ink danced across the parchment, revealing the prophecy of the forgotten crown. They stood, surrounded by old boxes and cobwebs, the air rich with the scent of timeworn memories.\n\n\u201cLook at this!\u201d Leo exclaimed, his finger tracing over the intricate drawings of the four kingdoms. \u201cEarth, Water, Fire, and Air\u2026 Do you think we really have to visit all of them?\u201d\n\nMaya squinted at the scroll, her brow furrowing. \u201cIt makes sense. The crown is supposed to unite them. But how do we even start? And what if we can\u2019t?\u201d\n\nCora, the mischievous sprite, buzzed around their heads like a tiny whirlwind. \u201cYou just have to believe in yourselves! The first kingdom is the Kingdom of Earth, ruled by the wise Elder Moss. He knows where the crown is hidden! But beware\u2014there are those who want it too.\u201d\n\nLeo\u2019s heart thudded loudly in his chest. \u201cWho are they? And how do we find Elder Moss?\u201d\n\n\u201cThe treasure hunters,\u201d Cora chimed, her eyes twinkling with mischief. \u201cThey\u2019re after the crown as well. If they find it first, they\u2019ll use its power to seize all four kingdoms!\u201d\n\nMaya felt a chill run down her spine. \u201cWe have to move quickly, then. But\u2026 what if we\u2019re not ready? What if we fail?\u201d\n\n\u201cFailure?\u201d Leo scoffed, but he couldn\u2019t completely mask the tremor in his voice. \u201cWe\u2019re destined for this, Maya! We can\u2019t chicken out now.\u201d\n\nMaya twirled a lock of her hair nervously. \u201cOkay, let\u2019s just plan. If we\u2019re going to find the crown, we need supplies and a map.\u201d\n\nJust as Leo opened his mouth to reply, a loud crash echoed from downstairs. They exchanged alarmed glances, and Cora darted to the attic\u2019s edge, peeking through a crack in the floor.\n\n\u201cNo time to waste!\u201d Cora squeaked. \u201cGrab what you need, and let\u2019s go! It might be them!\u201d\n\nThe siblings hurriedly stuffed enchanted trinkets and the scroll into a small bag. Maya grabbed a shimmering compass from their father\u2019s old collection, hoping it would lead them to safety. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWith a quick glance back, Leo and Maya bolted down the attic stairs, their hearts pounding like thunder. They reached the living room just as the door swung open, revealing two tall figures cloaked in dark robes, their faces shadowed.\n\n\u201cLooking for something?\u201d one of them sneered, revealing sharp teeth and a menacing grin. \u201cThat crown belongs to us now!\u201d\n\nTension crackled in the air as Leo stepped protectively in front of Maya. \u201cWe won\u2019t let you take it!\u201d\n\nThe figures lunged forward, and the siblings barely dodged. Cora flickered around them, darting like a lightning bug. \u201cThis way! Jump through the back door!\u201d \n\nMaya grabbed Leo\u2019s arm, and together they dashed through the kitchen, narrowly escaping the clutches of the treasure hunters. As they burst outside, the cool evening air filled their lungs with a mix of exhilaration and dread. \n\n\u201cWhich way to the Kingdom of Earth?\u201d Leo gasped, adrenaline coursing through him.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know! The compass!\u201d Maya rummaged through her bag, her hands shaking as she pulled out the shimmering compass. It spun wildly before suddenly pointing east. \n\n\u201cThen east it is!\u201d Leo shouted, his heart racing not only from fear but also from the thrill of the adventure ahead. They sprinted into the dimming light, the weight of their quest heavy on their shoulders, even as hope flickered in their hearts.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe night surrounded them like a blanket, and the sound of distant rustling leaves echoed behind them, a reminder that they weren\u2019t alone on this journey. The stakes were higher than ever, and with each step, Leo and Maya began to understand: this wasn\u2019t just about finding a crown; it was about finding themselves.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Leo and Maya find in the attic?","options":["A treasure map","An ancient scroll","A magical book","A hidden door"],"correct_answer":"An ancient scroll"},{"question":"Who warns Leo and Maya about the treasure hunters?","options":["An old wizard","Their parents","Cora the sprite","A talking animal"],"correct_answer":"Cora the sprite"},{"question":"What item does Maya grab to help them on their journey?","options":["A shield","A sword","A compass","A potion"],"correct_answer":"A compass"},{"question":"What do the cloaked figures reveal about the crown?","options":["It is cursed","It belongs to them","It has magical powers","It is lost forever"],"correct_answer":"It belongs to them"},{"question":"What direction does the compass point when they escape?","options":["North","East","West","South"],"correct_answer":"East"}]},"images":null,"word_count":664,"reading_level":"Builder"}
