   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_173_7_10","title":"The Dragon's Last Wish","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Prophecies","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: The Shimmering Grove\n\nAsh stood at the edge of Dragonheart Valley. The valley was beautiful, with its tall, green trees and sparkling streams. But Ash felt scared. \"What if I can't save the dragons?\" he whispered.\n\nEmber, the wise dragon, landed beside him. Her scales glimmered like stars. \"You have the heart of a hero, Ash. We must believe in ourselves,\" she said gently. Ash looked into her warm eyes. He felt a little braver.\n\nZara walked up, her sword gleaming in the sunlight. \"We need to find the Dragonstone before the sorceress does. She wants the dragons\u2019 magic for herself!\" Her voice was strong and confident. Ash nodded, determination growing inside him.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey made their way into the Shimmering Grove. The trees were tall, and the leaves sparkled like diamonds. \"This place feels magical!\" Ash exclaimed, his worries fading with each step. Zara smiled. \"We\u2019ll find the Dragonstone here.\"\n\nSuddenly, a loud roar echoed through the grove. Ash jumped. \"What was that?\" he gasped. Ember's eyes narrowed. \"Stay close. It could be the sorceress. We must guard the Dragonstone.\"\n\nAs they walked deeper into the grove, shadows danced around them. Ash spotted a glowing light ahead. \"Look!\" he pointed. They hurried toward it, excitement bubbling inside.\n\nBut just as they reached the light, a dark figure appeared. It was the sorceress! Her eyes sparked with greed. \"You think you can stop me?\" she sneered. Ash's heart raced. \"We won\u2019t give up!\" he said, trying to sound brave.\n\nThe sorceress raised her hand, and a powerful wind swirled around them. \"You are too late! The Dragonstone will be mine!\" she laughed wickedly. Ash felt a chill run down his spine. How would they defeat her?\n\n\"Together, we can do this!\" Zara shouted. \"We just need to believe!\" Ash took a deep breath. He could feel the warmth of Ember beside him. They had to find a way to save the dragons. \n\nSuddenly, a crackling sound filled the air. Ash felt a spark of magic rising within him. \"I can feel the energy!\" he shouted. But the sorceress was stronger than she seemed. What would happen next?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe battle was just beginning, and Ash knew he had to act fast.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What place do Ash and his friends enter in this chapter?","options":["The Dark Cave","The Shimmering Grove","The Dragon's Nest","The Crystal Lake"],"correct_answer":"The Shimmering Grove"},{"question":"Who threatens Ash and his friends in this chapter?","options":["A giant","A dragon","The sorceress","A wizard"],"correct_answer":"The sorceress"},{"question":"What does Ash feel when he stands at the edge of the valley?","options":["Excited","Scared","Happy","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Scared"},{"question":"What does Zara believe they need to do?","options":["Run away","Find the Dragonstone","Fight each other","Hide forever"],"correct_answer":"Find the Dragonstone"},{"question":"What magical feeling does Ash experience in the grove?","options":["Coldness","Happiness","Energy","Sleepiness"],"correct_answer":"Energy"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_173_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_173_ch2_img1.png","plot_173_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":376,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
