   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_173_7_10","title":"The Dragon's Last Wish","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Prophecies","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Ash stood tall, the shimmering Dragonstone glowing in his hand. Ember\u2019s faded light flickered with hope. \u201cYou did it, Ash!\u201d she roared, her voice echoing through the Shimmering Grove. \u201cYou\u2019ve found the Dragonstone!\u201d\n\nZara jumped with excitement. \u201cNow we can save the dragons! Let\u2019s go!\u201d She grabbed Ash\u2019s arm, pulling him toward the exit. But just as they reached the edge of the grove, a dark shadow loomed overhead. \n\n\u201cNot so fast!\u201d The sorceress appeared, her dark cloak billowing like storm clouds. \u201cYou think you can use that stone against me?\u201d Her eyes sparkled with wicked glee. \n\nAsh felt a shiver of fear. \u201cI-I can\u2019t let you take the magic!\u201d he stammered. Ember nudged him gently. \u201cRemember the prophecy, Ash. You are the last hope. Believe in yourself!\u201d\n\nTaking a deep breath, Ash held the Dragonstone high. \u201cNo! I won\u2019t let you harm the dragons!\u201d A bright light burst from the stone, filling the grove with warmth. The sorceress gasped, stumbling back. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe light danced around them, igniting the colors of the grove. \u201cWhat is this magic?\u201d the sorceress cried, shielding her eyes from the glow.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s the magic of hope!\u201d Zara shouted, stepping forward. \u201cAnd it\u2019s stronger than your darkness!\u201d \n\nWith a loud roar, Ember joined the light, her spirit rising as the colors swirled around them. Ash felt a rush of confidence. \u201cTogether, we can defeat you!\u201d \n\nThe sorceress shrieked in anger. \u201cYou fools! You can\u2019t stop me!\u201d She raised her hands to unleash her dark magic, but Ash focused on the light from the Dragonstone. \n\n\u201cNow!\u201d he shouted, and he and Ember unleashed a powerful beam of light. It struck the sorceress, her magic shattering like glass. She screamed as the light surrounded her, pulling her into a whirlpool of colors.\n\nAs the light faded, the grove returned to its peaceful state. The sorceress was gone. Ash looked at Ember and Zara, their eyes shining bright. \u201cWe did it!\u201d\n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Zara cheered, her smile wide. \u201cYou found your courage, Ash!\u201d\n\nEmber\u2019s light flickered, now shining stronger than before. \u201cYou are a true hero, Ash. The dragons will be safe.\u201d \n\nAs the sun set over Dragonheart Valley, Ash felt warmth in his heart. He had faced his fears, and with his friends, he had saved the day. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go home,\u201d Ash said, his voice steady. \u201cThe dragons need us.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith laughter and joy, the three friends walked back, ready to share their victory and restore the magic of the dragons forever.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ash find in the Shimmering Grove?","options":["A sword","The Dragonstone","A treasure chest","A dragon"],"correct_answer":"The Dragonstone"},{"question":"Who helps Ash defeat the sorceress?","options":["A knight","His friends Ember and Zara","A wizard","A dragon"],"correct_answer":"His friends Ember and Zara"},{"question":"What does the sorceress want?","options":["To free the dragons","To harness dragons' magic","To find the Dragonstone","To become a hero"],"correct_answer":"To harness dragons' magic"},{"question":"What helps Ash find his courage?","options":["The Dragonstone","His fear","Ember\u2019s nudging","Zara\u2019s shield"],"correct_answer":"The Dragonstone"},{"question":"What happens to the sorceress at the end?","options":["She escapes","She is defeated","She becomes a dragon","She helps Ash"],"correct_answer":"She is defeated"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_173_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_173_ch5_img1.png","plot_173_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":428,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
