   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_173_11_14","title":"The Dragon's Last Wish","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Prophecies","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The sun peeked over the jagged peaks of Dragonheart Valley, casting a warm golden light that danced through the trees. Ash stood at the edge of a cliff, feeling the cool breeze brush against his skin. This place, which had once been filled with dragon flames and laughter, now felt like a quiet graveyard, shrouded in a heavy mist. He squeezed the Dragonstone in his pocket, its weight a constant reminder of the responsibility weighing on his shoulders.\n\n\u201cAre you ready, Ash?\u201d Zara asked, her fiery red hair blowing in the wind. She stood strong beside him, her hand resting on the hilt of her sword, ready for whatever lay ahead. \u201cWe can\u2019t let Morgath find the Dragonstone first.\u201d\n\nAsh nodded, though doubt crept into his heart. \u201cI\u2019m not sure I can do this, Zara. What if I fail?\u201d\n\nEmber, the wise dragon, landed gracefully behind them, her scales shimmering like molten gold. \u201cYou have more courage than you know, young Ash. Remember, every great adventure begins with a single step.\u201d Her voice was soothing, yet there was an urgency in her words.\n\nThey began their descent into the valley, the path becoming narrower, flanked by towering trees that whispered secrets of a long-lost era. As they walked, Ash gathered his thoughts, trying to silence the doubts that echoed in his mind like distant thunder.\n\nSuddenly, a flicker of movement caught his eye. A shadow darted through the trees, too quick to identify. Ash\u2019s heart raced. \u201cDid you see that?\u201d he whispered, glancing back at Zara and Ember.\n\nZara\u2019s eyes narrowed, her warrior instincts kicking in. \u201cStay alert. It could be Morgath\u2019s spies.\u201d Just as she spoke, a figure emerged from the underbrush\u2014a small, scruffy creature with bright eyes and a mischievous grin.\n\n\u201cNot spies, friends!\u201d it squeaked, bouncing on its feet. \u201cI\u2019m Nibbles, the best guide in all of Dragonheart Valley! You need me to find the Dragonstone!\u201d\n\nAsh blinked in surprise. \u201cWhat do you know about the Dragonstone?\u201d\n\nNibbles bounced closer, his enthusiasm contagious. \u201cI know all the secret paths! The way is dangerous, but with me, you\u2019ll make it!\u201d His whiskers twitched with excitement. \n\nZara exchanged a skeptical glance with Ash. \u201cCan we trust him?\u201d\n\nEmber chimed in, \u201cSometimes, the most unexpected allies can lead us to our destinies.\u201d\n\nWith a reluctant grin, Ash nodded. \u201cAlright, Nibbles. Lead the way.\u201d\n\nAs they moved deeper into the valley, the air became thicker, charged with magic. Ash could feel the pull of the Dragonstone, like a heartbeat echoing through the valley. But with each step, the sense of danger loomed larger. \n\nSuddenly, the ground shook beneath them. Trees creaked like old bones, and a fierce wind roared through the valley. \u201cWhat is happening?\u201d Ash yelled, struggling to maintain his balance.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re not alone!\u201d Zara shouted over the howling wind. \u201cIt\u2019s Morgath!\u201d\n\nJust then, a dark silhouette emerged from the shadows, cloaked in swirling mist. Morgath\u2019s eyes glowed with a malicious light as she laughed, a sound that chilled Ash\u2019s bones. \u201cYou\u2019ll never reach the Dragonstone!\u201d she sneered, her voice dripping with malice. \n\nFear surged through Ash, but he felt Zara\u2019s hand tighten around his wrist. \u201cWe can\u2019t give up!\u201d she urged, her determination igniting his own courage. \n\nJust then, Nibbles pointed ahead. \u201cThere! The cave of echoes! We can lose her there!\u201d \n\nWith renewed hope, they dashed toward the cave, the darkness swallowing them as Morgath\u2019s furious cries faded behind them. In that moment of refuge, Ash knew they still had a chance. He could feel it\u2014the Dragonstone was close.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they entered the cave, the walls sparkled with crystals that glimmered like stars. The sound of dripping water echoed around them, creating a mesmerizing symphony. Ash felt a sense of wonder wash over him, even amidst the danger. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep moving!\u201d Zara urged, her voice steady despite the uncertainty. Ash\u2019s heart raced with a mixture of fear and determination. They had to find the Dragonstone and confront Morgath once and for all.\n\nWith Ember guiding them and the flicker of hope brighter than before, Ash took a deep breath and stepped into the unknown, ready to embrace his destiny.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who do Ash and Zara meet in the valley?","options":["Morgath","Nibbles","Ember","A dragon"],"correct_answer":"Nibbles"},{"question":"What happens when they enter the cave?","options":["They find the Dragonstone immediately","Morgath follows them","They meet more dragons","They get lost"],"correct_answer":"Morgath follows them"},{"question":"What does Ember encourage Ash to remember?","options":["His fears","His courage","His friends","His past"],"correct_answer":"His courage"},{"question":"How does Zara react to Ash\u2019s doubts?","options":["She agrees with him","She ignores him","She encourages him","She criticizes him"],"correct_answer":"She encourages him"},{"question":"What is the cave filled with?","options":["Dragons","Gold","Crystals","Monsters"],"correct_answer":"Crystals"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_173_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_173_ch4_img1.png","plot_173_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":714,"reading_level":"Builder"}
