   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_175_7_10","title":"The Starflower Prophecy","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Prophecies","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The sun peeked through the tall trees of the Wishing Woods, creating a patchwork of light and shadows. Nia, Grumble, and Luna walked carefully, the forest alive with the sounds of chirping birds and rustling leaves. \n\n\u201cDo you think we\u2019ll find the Dream Crystal today?\u201d Nia asked, her heart racing with hope. \n\nGrumble scratched his beard and frowned. \u201cFinding it is one thing, but getting past the Trickster Gnome is another. He can be tricky!\u201d \n\n\u201cTrickster Gnome? More like a silly gnome!\u201d Luna giggled, fluttering around Nia\u2019s head. \u201cLet\u2019s show him our bravery!\u201d\n\nNia smiled, feeling a little lighter. \u201cRight! We can do this together!\u201d\n\nAs they walked deeper into the woods, they spotted flowers glowing softly. Nia knelt down to touch one. \u201cLook at these! They\u2019re so beautiful!\u201d\n\nLuna twirled in the air, her wings sparkling. \u201cThey are! But we need to focus on the crystal!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud cackle. \u201cWho dares enter my woods?\u201d A small figure with a pointed hat appeared. It was the Trickster Gnome! \n\nNia felt her stomach drop. \u201cUh-oh! What do we do now?\u201d \n\nGrumble stepped forward, his eyes serious. \u201cWe must solve his riddle. It\u2019s the only way!\u201d \n\nLuna whispered, \u201cJust remember, Nia. You are brave and kind. You can do this!\u201d\n\nNia took a deep breath. \u201cOkay, Gnome! What\u2019s your riddle?\u201d \n\nThe gnome crossed his arms. \u201cI have keys but open no locks. I have space but no room. I have you but no me. What am I?\u201d\n\nNia thought hard. The words swirled in her mind. \u201cKeys but no locks\u2026 Space but no room\u2026 You! You are a keyboard!\u201d she exclaimed. \n\nThe Trickster Gnome jumped back, surprised. \u201cYou solved it! My, my, you\u2019re clever!\u201d \n\nNia felt a warm glow in her heart. \u201cReally? Does that mean we can pass?\u201d \n\nThe gnome hesitated but smiled. \u201cYou earned it, brave child! Go ahead!\u201d \n\nNia, Grumble, and Luna cheered. They had made progress! \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe gnome waved them through a magical doorway that glimmered with light. Beyond it, they could see a meadow filled with sparkling Starflowers. \n\n\u201cLook at that!\u201d shouted Luna, clapping her tiny hands. \n\nNia\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cIt\u2019s beautiful! We\u2019re so close!\u201d \n\nAs they entered the meadow, a strange sound filled the air. It was a soft, melodic humming. \n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d Grumble asked, raising an eyebrow. \n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s the Dream Crystal!\u201d Nia suggested, her heart leaping. They hurried toward the sound, filled with excitement and wonder. \n\nBut just then, Luna stopped. \u201cWait! What if there\u2019s another riddle? What if it\u2019s a trap?\u201d \n\nNia felt doubt creep in, but she remembered Grumble and Luna\u2019s encouragement. \u201cTogether, we can face anything!\u201d \n\nWith a deep breath, they stepped forward, ready for whatever came next. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What creature do Nia and her friends meet in the woods?","options":["A dragon","A unicorn","A Trickster Gnome","A giant"],"correct_answer":"A Trickster Gnome"},{"question":"What does Nia need to solve to get past the gnome?","options":["A puzzle","A riddle","A quiz","A test"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What does Nia find after solving the riddle?","options":["A treasure","A hidden cave","A magical meadow","A scary monster"],"correct_answer":"A magical meadow"},{"question":"How does Nia feel about her bravery?","options":["Doubtful","Excited","Scared","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"Who helps encourage Nia throughout the chapter?","options":["Grumble and Luna","Boggle","The gnome","The flowers"],"correct_answer":"Grumble and Luna"}]},"images":null,"word_count":469,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
