   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_166_7_10","title":"The Stolen Banner","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Warring Kingdoms","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Elara stood at the edge of the castle courtyard. The sun gleamed on the stone walls, and the flags waved gently in the breeze. She felt a mix of excitement and fear. Today was the day to confront the Duke of Alderwood.\n\n\"Are you ready, Flick?\" she asked her fox, who sat at her feet, tail flicking back and forth.\n\n\"Ready as ever!\" Flick replied, his eyes sparkling with mischief. Kian leaned against the castle wall, arms crossed. His mischievous grin made Elara smile.\n\n\"Let's get that banner back!\" he said confidently.\n\nElara nodded. Together, they walked through the courtyard. As they entered the grand hall, the Duke\u2019s guards stood tall, their armor shining. Elara had to think fast. She needed to distract them.\n\n\"Look over there!\" Elara shouted, pointing toward a window. The guards turned, and in that moment, Elara, Kian, and Flick dashed past them. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey found themselves in a room filled with colorful tapestries and strange artifacts. Elara\u2019s heart raced. This was where the stolen banner might be hidden!\n\n\"Which way do we go?\" Kian asked, looking around.\n\nFlick sniffed the air. \"I smell something\u2014it's close!\" he said, leading the way. They followed Flick down a dark hallway. Suddenly, they stopped. There, hanging on the wall, was the royal banner, glowing like a star.\n\n\"It's beautiful!\" Elara exclaimed. But just then, they heard footsteps behind them.\n\n\"Oh no! We need to hurry!\" Kian shouted. They grabbed the banner, and Elara felt its warmth in her hands. She had to protect it!\n\nRunning back, they faced a group of guards. \"Stop right there!\" one yelled.\n\nElara took a deep breath. \"We need to show this to the people! The banner belongs to everyone!\" she cried.\n\nKian nodded. \"And it will bring peace!\" he added. The guards hesitated, unsure what to do.\n\nElara stepped forward, holding the banner high. \"This banner is a symbol of our unity! We can end this war together!\" \n\nJust then, the Duke himself appeared. He looked at the banner, then at Elara. \"You are brave, girl. Perhaps it is time to listen.\"\n\nThe guards lowered their weapons. Elara felt a wave of hope wash over her. Maybe they could save Liora after all.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\"Let's go to the town square!\" Elara shouted, her spirit soaring. Kian, Flick, and the guards followed her. Together, they would unite the kingdom with the stolen banner.\n\nThe sun shone brightly as they rushed outside, ready to bring peace back to Liora.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Elara and her friends find in the dark hallway?","options":["A treasure chest","The royal banner","A magic potion","A sleeping dragon"],"correct_answer":"The royal banner"},{"question":"Who helps Elara distract the guards?","options":["Kian","Flick","The Duke","The guards"],"correct_answer":"Flick"},{"question":"What does Elara want to show the people?","options":["The guards","The Duke's crown","The stolen banner","Her magic skills"],"correct_answer":"The stolen banner"},{"question":"How does the Duke react to Elara's bravery?","options":["He gets angry","He laughs","He listens","He runs away"],"correct_answer":"He listens"},{"question":"What is the main message Elara wants to share?","options":["The banner is pretty","Books are important","Unity brings peace","Flick is her favorite"],"correct_answer":"Unity brings peace"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_166_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_166_ch5_img1.png","plot_166_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":419,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
