   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_166_11_14","title":"The Stolen Banner","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Warring Kingdoms","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun hung low in the sky, casting a golden hue over the vibrant kingdom of Liora. Rolling hills and lush forests painted a picturesque landscape, while the sound of a bubbling brook danced through the air. Nestled between two towering mountains, the kingdom was divided by an ancient rivalry\u2014each side ruled by a castle belonging to the House of Verenth and the House of Draven. The two factions had lived in tension for generations, yet many believed peace could still be woven among the threads of their history.\n\nElara, a banner weaver's apprentice, sat cross-legged on the workshop floor, her nimble fingers stitching vibrant fabrics together. The wooden beams of the workshop creaked gently, the air filled with the sweet scent of dyes and the soft hum of her mentor, Master Orin, as he worked nearby. Elara was a girl of eleven, with wild chestnut curls that danced around her face as she worked. Her sparkly green eyes reflected her determination. She took great pride in her craft, believing that every thread she wove could hold the stories of her kingdom.\n\n\u201cRemember, Elara, each banner tells a tale,\u201d Master Orin reminded her with a warm smile. \u201cIt carries the hopes and dreams of our people.\u201d \n\nElara nodded, her heart swelling with pride. She had always felt a connection to the banners they created\u2014objects that represented more than just fabric; they were symbols of unity. \n\nJust then, the workshop door swung open with a crash, startling both Elara and Master Orin. A breathless boy named Arlo burst inside, his face flushed with excitement. \n\n\u201cHave you heard? The royal banner has been stolen!\u201d he exclaimed.\n\nElara blinked in disbelief. The royal banner, a magnificent piece adorned with the colors of Liora, was the heart of their kingdom. It was said to possess magic that protected them from harm. Without it, the peace between Verenth and Draven could unravel. \n\n\u201cWhat do you mean stolen?\u201d Elara asked, her heart racing. \n\n\u201cWord from the castle guards says a mysterious thief slipped into the castle during the festival last night. No one saw their face, but they left chaos behind!\u201d Arlo's eyes sparkled with the thrill of adventure.\n\nA grim expression crossed Master Orin\u2019s face. \u201cIf the royal banner is lost, it could ignite war between the factions. Elara, you must be cautious.\u201d\n\nElara's resolve hardened. She had to act. \u201cI will retrieve it,\u201d she declared, her voice steady. \u201cI know the stories of the banners\u2014perhaps they will guide me in finding the thief.\u201d \n\nFlick, her clever fox companion, curled around her legs, sensing her determination. With a flick of his bushy tail, he seemed to say, \u201cI\u2019m with you.\u201d\n\nAs the sun dipped below the horizon, casting long shadows across the workshop, Elara gathered her supplies. She felt the weight of her decision settle upon her. She would venture into the unknown, through treacherous territories, risking everything to recover the banner and save Liora. \n\nElara took a deep breath, glancing at the door that led outside to the vast kingdom. Her adventure was about to begin. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\nThe scene shows Elara working diligently on a vibrant banner in the workshop, surrounded by colorful fabrics and tools. Master Orin watches her with pride, while sunbeams filter through the workshop window, illuminating the lively colors of the threads.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\nThe moment captures Elara, determined and resolute, standing at the open workshop door with Flick the fox at her side. The twilight sky is painted with hues of orange and purple, hinting at the adventure that awaits her beyond the threshold.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What significant event happens in this chapter?","options":["Elara learns to weave banners","The royal banner is stolen","Elara goes on a quest","Master Orin retires"],"correct_answer":"The royal banner is stolen"},{"question":"Who is Elara's loyal companion?","options":["A dog named Dash","A fox named Flick","A bird named Sky","A cat named Whiskers"],"correct_answer":"A fox named Flick"},{"question":"What does Elara aim to retrieve?","options":["A treasure","A map","The royal banner","A magical sword"],"correct_answer":"The royal banner"},{"question":"What does Master Orin emphasize about the banners?","options":["They are made of silk","They carry stories of the people","They are just decorations","They are easy to make"],"correct_answer":"They carry stories of the people"},{"question":"How does the chapter end?","options":["Elara gives up on her quest","Elara prepares to leave for her adventure","Elara celebrates the festival","Elara receives a reward"],"correct_answer":"Elara prepares to leave for her adventure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_166_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_166_ch1_img1.png","plot_166_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":601,"reading_level":"Builder"}
