   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_166_11_14","title":"The Stolen Banner","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Warring Kingdoms","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Elara stood at the edge of the ancient stone bridge, her heart racing in her chest. The sun dipped low behind the mountains, casting long shadows across the valley of Liora. Flick, her clever fox companion, twitched his ears, sensing her unease. \u201cWe have to be careful, Elara,\u201d he said, his voice a soft whisper against the breeze. \u201cThe rival prince's castle is just ahead, and we can\u2019t trust anyone.\u201d\n\nKian stood beside her, the rogue prince with tousled dark hair and piercing green eyes. \u201cWe\u2019ll get the banner back,\u201d he reassured her, but even he could not mask the tension in his voice. The castle loomed ahead, its dark spires piercing the sky like pointed fingers. Elara took a deep breath, steeling herself for what lay beyond those walls. \n\nAs they crossed the bridge, Flick darted ahead, his small form a flash of orange against the gray stone. Elara felt a flutter of hope in her chest. If they could just reach the castle\u2019s great hall without being seen, they might find the banner before it was too late. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe great hall was a cacophony of colors, banners of all shapes and sizes draped across the walls, each representing a different faction. Elara\u2019s eyes scanned the room, searching for the royal banner, her heart sinking as she realized it was not among them. \u201cIt has to be here somewhere,\u201d she murmured, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\nSuddenly, a figure stepped forward\u2014Roderick, the cunning advisor who had been a thorn in their sides since the beginning of their journey. \u201cLooking for something, Elara?\u201d he sneered, his icy blue gaze locking onto hers. \n\nElara's heart raced. \u201cWe know you have the banner, Roderick! We will get it back!\u201d She felt Kian move closer, his presence a comfort as they faced their adversary. \n\n\u201cOh, but it\u2019s not that simple, is it?\u201d Roderick's smile was a thin line. \u201cThis banner represents more than just a piece of cloth. It is the heart of the kingdom! And you, young banner weaver, are far too naive to understand its true power.\u201d \n\nElara clenched her fists, frustration bubbling inside her. \u201cIt\u2019s not just a banner! It\u2019s a symbol of unity!\u201d \n\n\u201cAnd unity is a fragile thing,\u201d Roderick replied, leaning in, his voice low and conspiratorial. \u201cPerhaps you should reconsider your quest, Elara. Not everyone wishes for peace.\u201d \n\nThe tension in the room thickened like fog, and Elara exchanged a determined glance with Kian. They had come too far to back down now. Just then, Flick let out a sharp yelp, darting toward a tapestry hanging in the corner. \n\nElara followed him, her heart pounding. Behind the tapestry, there it was\u2014the royal banner, beautifully embroidered with golden threads, shimmering even in the dim light. \u201cThere!\u201d she shouted, lunging forward. \n\nBut Roderick was quicker. He moved to block her path, a wicked grin spreading across his face. \u201cI think not, dear apprentice.\u201d\n\nWith the flick of her wrist, Elara summoned her courage. \u201cWe\u2019ve come to reclaim what\u2019s rightfully ours!\u201d \n\nThe air crackled as she stepped closer, her determination igniting a fire within her. Kian moved alongside her, ready for whatever came next. Together, they formed a barrier against Roderick, their hearts united in purpose. \n\nAs the room filled with shouts and chaos, Elara lunged for the banner. She grasped it tightly, feeling its weight and significance in her hands. The banner was more than a symbol; it was a promise to her kingdom. \n\nThe energy shifted. With Flick by her side and Kian\u2019s fierce loyalty, Elara felt a surge of strength. They were not just fighting for a banner; they were fighting for the future of Liora. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nElara\u2019s heart raced as Roderick lunged forward, but this time, she was ready. With a swift movement, she dodged his grasp and dashed for the door, Kian and Flick right behind her. \u201cWe have to get out of here!\u201d Kian shouted, urgency lacing his voice.\n\nClutching the banner tightly, Elara felt a sense of purpose swell inside her. Despite the chaos, she knew they had ignited a spark of hope within the kingdom. Together, they would restore the bonds that had been torn apart. \n\nAs they burst through the castle doors and into the cool night air, Elara turned to Flick and Kian, her eyes bright with determination. \u201cWe did it! Now, let\u2019s bring this back to the people of Liora!\u201d\n\nThe stars twinkled above them like a million tiny eyes watching their journey unfold, and Elara smiled, ready to embrace whatever challenges lay ahead.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Elara retrieve from behind the tapestry?","options":["A sword","The royal banner","A map","A treasure chest"],"correct_answer":"The royal banner"},{"question":"What does Roderick imply about unity?","options":["It is easy to achieve","It is fragile","It is not important","It is unnecessary"],"correct_answer":"It is fragile"},{"question":"Who is Elara's companion that helps her during the quest?","options":["A wolf","A mouse","A clever fox named Flick","A dragon"],"correct_answer":"A clever fox named Flick"},{"question":"What do Elara and Kian plan to do with the banner once they retrieve it?","options":["Hide it","Sell it","Bring it back to the people of Liora","Keep it for themselves"],"correct_answer":"Bring it back to the people of Liora"},{"question":"What is the main emotion Elara feels when confronting Roderick?","options":["Fear","Joy","Determination","Sadness"],"correct_answer":"Determination"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_166_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_166_ch5_img1.png","plot_166_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":773,"reading_level":"Builder"}
