   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_167_15_18","title":"The Dragon's Peace","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Warring Kingdoms","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Zazra perched atop a craggy cliff, her scales glinting like polished emeralds in the pale morning sun. Below, the vast expanse of Eldoria unfurled, its serene valleys a stark contrast to the fiery terrain of Dracos. She felt a surge of hope, mingled with the ever-watchful weight of responsibility. Beside her, Arlen adjusted the grip on his sword, casting a sidelong glance at her. \n\n\u201cAre you ready?\u201d he asked, his voice steady yet tinged with concern.\n\n\u201cReady as I\u2019ll ever be,\u201d Zazra replied, her tone firm. \u201cIf we are to convince them, we must start with the Council of Elders.\u201d\n\nAs they descended the rocky path, Mira fluttered her fingers, conjuring tiny motes of light that danced around them like fireflies. \u201cI sense a change in the air,\u201d she chimed, a mischievous smile lighting her face. \u201cHope, or perhaps just the lingering scent of impending doom?\u201d\n\nArlen chuckled, though his gaze remained serious. \u201cWe can\u2019t afford to underestimate their fear, Mira. The dark dragon is a manifestation of their nightmares, and we must confront that fear with truth.\u201d\n\nUpon reaching the grand hall of Eldoria, Zazra felt her heart quicken. The architecture was breathtaking, with colored glass windows depicting ancient tales of unity and conflict. Yet today, the air felt thick with skepticism. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe council chamber was filled with the murmurs of the Eldorian elders, their faces lined with the wrinkles of many years, wisdom shadowed by distrust. Zazra inhaled deeply, drawing strength from her companions.\n\n\u201cI declare!\u201d she began, her voice resonating with an uncharacteristic confidence, \u201cWe have unearthed a prophecy\u2014a means to unite our lands against the true threat lurking beyond our borders!\u201d\n\nThe elders shifted, their expressions a mixture of intrigue and disdain. \u201cAnd why should we believe a dragon, of all beings?\u201d one elder challenged, his voice a dry rasp. \u201cYour kind has brought nothing but flames and destruction to our doorsteps.\u201d\n\nZazra felt the sting of his words but pressed on. \u201cNot all dragons seek war. I am different. I want peace for both our kingdoms!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat proof do you have?\u201d another elder interjected, skepticism etched across his brow. \n\nBefore she could respond, a loud crash echoed outside, and the earth trembled beneath them. A shadow flitted across the stained-glass windows, causing the light to fracture into a thousand colors. Panic surged through the chamber, and Arlen instinctively moved to shield Zazra, his body tense with readiness. \n\n\u201cIt\u2019s him!\u201d Arlen shouted. \u201cThe dark dragon is here!\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a deafening roar filled the hall, reverberating through the stone walls and shaking the windows. Zazra\u2019s heart raced\u2014this was the moment they\u2019d feared, the moment that could either bind the kingdoms or break them entirely. \n\n\u201cListen!\u201d Zazra cried, her voice cutting through the chaos. \u201cIf we don\u2019t stand together, we will fall apart! The dark dragon seeks to divide us!\u201d\n\nThe elders exchanged glances, uncertainty flickering in their eyes. In that instant of doubt, Zazra took a step forward, her wings unfurling slightly, an instinctive display of her power. \u201cI am asking you to trust me, to trust the prophecy. We can end this conflict, but only if we unite!\u201d\n\nJust then, the doors burst open, revealing a massive figure, dark as night with eyes like molten gold. The dark dragon loomed in the doorway, a harbinger of destruction. Zazra\u2019s breath caught as she met his gaze, the weight of her mission pressing down on her like a heavy mantle.\n\n\u201cFoolish creatures, clinging to dreams while darkness envelops your hearts,\u201d the dark dragon hissed, his voice chilling as it slithered through the chamber. \u201cYou will pay for your defiance.\u201d\n\nIn that moment of confrontation, a spark ignited within Zazra. This was not merely a battle of physical might, but a battle for the very souls of their kingdoms. She could see the flicker of determination amidst the elders\u2019 fear, and she knew what she had to do. \n\n\u201cTogether,\u201d she proclaimed, her voice rising with fervor. \u201cWe can defeat him!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe chamber fell silent, the elders\u2019 eyes sharpening with newfound resolve as they exchanged glances. Zazra could feel the shift, the burgeoning possibility of unity that was once only a dream. \n\nWith her heart pounding, Zazra turned to Mira and Arlen. \u201cIt begins now. We fight for our future, together.\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Zazra reveal to the Eldorian council?","options":["A new weapon","An ancient prophecy","A plan to attack Dracos","A message from the dark dragon"],"correct_answer":"An ancient prophecy"},{"question":"How do the Eldorian elders initially react to Zazra's claims?","options":["With immediate trust","With skepticism and disdain","With excitement","With indifference"],"correct_answer":"With skepticism and disdain"},{"question":"What event interrupts the meeting in the grand hall?","options":["A loud crash","An earthquake","The arrival of a messenger","A magical explosion"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash"},{"question":"What does Zazra feel when the dark dragon appears?","options":["Fear and doubt","Hope and determination","Anger and frustration","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Hope and determination"},{"question":"What is Zazra's ultimate goal in this chapter?","options":["To defeat the dark dragon alone","To convince the council to fight with her","To escape to Dracos","To gather more allies"],"correct_answer":"To convince the council to fight with her"}]},