   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_170_7_10","title":"The Last Heir of Ivalis","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Warring Kingdoms","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Aiden stared out of his window. The kingdom of Ivalis was a mess. Once, it had been a bright and beautiful place, but now, it was filled with shadows and whispers of war. Tall castles stood crumbling, and smoke rose from the fields. He sighed deeply.\n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, Aiden?\u201d asked his best friend, Finn. Finn was always full of energy. He had messy, brown hair and a cheerful smile. \n\n\u201cIt\u2019s just... everything feels wrong,\u201d Aiden replied. \u201cWhy can\u2019t everyone just get along?\u201d\n\nFinn shrugged. \u201cI don\u2019t know. But we can play knights! You can be the brave prince!\u201d\n\nAiden chuckled, but deep down, he felt uneasy. He never wanted to be a knight or a king. He just wanted to be Aiden.\n\nSuddenly, a loud knock at the door broke their laughter. A cloaked figure entered. It was Thalia, the mysterious woman who always seemed to appear out of nowhere.\n\n\u201cAiden, we need to talk,\u201d she said, her voice serious. Her silver hair danced in the light. \u201cThere\u2019s news from the forest.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat news?\u201d Aiden asked, feeling a chill run down his spine.\n\n\u201cWar is coming,\u201d Thalia said. \u201cThe factions are gathering. They think you are the key to peace.\u201d\n\nAiden\u2019s heart raced. \u201cMe? I\u2019m just a boy!\u201d \n\nThalia stepped closer. \u201cYou are the last heir of Ivalis. You have to help us.\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat if I can\u2019t?\u201d Aiden whispered.\n\n\u201cYou must try,\u201d Thalia replied, her eyes shining with hope. \u201cYou are stronger than you think.\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud explosion echoed outside. Aiden\u2019s heart pounded like a drum. He ran to the window and gasped. Smoke filled the air, and he could see figures in the distance.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d he shouted. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nFinn peered over his shoulder. \u201cIs that a battle?\u201d\n\n\u201cYes,\u201d Thalia said. \u201cWe must move. Now!\u201d \n\nAiden took a deep breath. His hands trembled. \u201cOkay, let\u2019s go!\u201d \n\nThalia led them down the winding stairs. They hurried through dark hallways, avoiding the castle\u2019s guards. Aiden felt a fire ignite inside him. He could help fix this. \n\nOutside, the forest loomed ahead. Aiden felt a mix of excitement and fear. \u201cWhat do we do next?\u201d\n\nThalia smiled gently. \u201cWe find the rebels. They will help you reclaim your birthright.\u201d\n\n\u201cReclaim my what?\u201d Aiden asked, confused.\n\n\u201cYour throne,\u201d Thalia said. \u201cIt\u2019s time to embrace who you are.\u201d\n\nAiden looked around. The trees whispered secrets, and he felt the weight of his destiny. \u201cI\u2019m ready,\u201d he said, his voice firm.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut inside, he still wondered if he truly could be a leader.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Aiden see when he looks out the window?","options":["A beautiful kingdom","A crumbling kingdom","A sunny day","A rainbow"],"correct_answer":"A crumbling kingdom"},{"question":"Who is Thalia?","options":["Aiden's friend","A rebel leader","A mysterious mentor","A castle guard"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious mentor"},{"question":"What does Thalia say Aiden must help with?","options":["Finding treasure","Reclaiming his birthright","Playing knights","Running away"],"correct_answer":"Reclaiming his birthright"},{"question":"What happens when Thalia arrives?","options":["She tells a joke","She brings good news","She talks about war","She leaves the castle"],"correct_answer":"She talks about war"},{"question":"How does Aiden feel about being a leader?","options":["Excited","Nervous","Indifferent","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_170_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_170_ch1_img1.png","plot_170_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":435,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
