   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_164_7_10","title":"Beneath the Starlit Scales","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Dragons & Creatures","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: A Fire-breathing Problem\n\nJamie and Ember stood in the backyard, looking at the sky. \u201cWe need to hurry. The full moon rises soon!\u201d Jamie said, his voice shaky. He could hear the townsfolk gathering, their worried whispers floating through the air.\n\n\u201cWhat if they come for me?\u201d Ember asked, her bright eyes wide. She flicked her tail nervously. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean to frighten anyone.\u201d \n\n\u201cYou didn\u2019t frighten me,\u201d Jamie replied softly. \u201cI think you\u2019re amazing!\u201d\n\nEmber smiled, her scales glinting in the sunlight like stars. They both looked towards the edge of the enchanted forest. Thick trees loomed over them, casting dark shadows. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d said Jamie, trying to sound brave. He took a big breath and stepped forward. As they entered the forest, the world around them changed. Sunlight danced through the leaves, and colorful flowers peeked from the ground. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, a loud shout broke the peaceful sounds of the forest. \u201cThere it is! The dragon!\u201d A group of townsfolk appeared, holding torches and pitchforks. Jamie's heart raced like a rabbit. \n\n\u201cQuick, Ember!\u201d he whispered. \u201cWe have to hide!\u201d They ducked behind a bush, but Ember\u2019s tail was too big. It stuck out like a glowing beacon.\n\n\u201cWhat if they see me?\u201d Ember whispered, her voice trembling.\n\n\u201cThey won\u2019t if you stay very still,\u201d Jamie said, holding his breath. The townsfolk walked closer, their eyes scanning the trees. \n\n\u201cLook! It went this way!\u201d Mrs. Hargrove, the town elder, shouted. \u201cWe must protect our town! That dragon is dangerous!\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2019m not dangerous!\u201d Ember cried softly. \u201cI just want to go home!\u201d \n\nJamie felt a wave of fear wash over him. \u201cWhat if they hurt you?\u201d he asked, glancing at Ember. She looked so sad, her shimmering scales dimming in the shadow.\n\n\u201cWe have to keep moving,\u201d Jamie said, taking a deep breath. \u201cThere\u2019s a secret path near the river. It might take us to the mountain where you live!\u201d\n\nEmber nodded, hope flickering in her eyes. \u201cLead the way, Jamie!\u201d\n\nThey dashed through the trees, but the path was tangled and tricky. Jamie stumbled over roots and branches, and Ember had to weave around the trees carefully. \n\n\u201cCareful!\u201d Ember called, but in her gentle tone. \n\n\u201cI\u2019m trying!\u201d Jamie said, struggling to keep up. Just then, he tripped and fell. He looked up, and Ember was right beside him. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go, buddy!\u201d She nudged him with her snout. \u201cWe can do this together!\u201d\n\nWith a burst of courage, Jamie got up. \u201cTogether!\u201d he shouted, feeling braver. \n\nBut in that moment, a loud noise crashed through the trees. It sounded like thunder. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Jamie gasped. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know!\u201d Ember replied, looking frightened. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s hurry!\u201d Jamie urged, knowing time was running out.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey dashed towards the river, their hearts pounding. But as they rounded the last tree, a huge fallen log blocked their way! \n\n\u201cNow what?\u201d Jamie said, panting and looking at the log. \u201cWe can\u2019t go over it!\u201d\n\nEmber looked worried. \u201cHow will we get to the mountain?\u201d\n\nJamie took a deep breath. \u201cI have an idea! You\u2019re a dragon. Can you help me fly over?\u201d\n\nEmber blinked, her eyes brightening. \u201cI can try! Get on my back!\u201d\n\nWith a flutter of excitement, Jamie climbed onto Ember\u2019s back. \u201cHold on tight!\u201d she said, and with a powerful leap, they soared into the air. The ground dropped away, and Jamie felt a rush of wind whip through his hair.\n\n\u201cWow!\u201d he yelled, feeling a spark of bravery. \u201cThis is amazing!\u201d\n\nBut just as they flew over the log, Jamie spotted the townsfolk racing towards the river. \u201cThey\u2019re coming!\u201d he shouted, gripping Ember tightly. \n\n\u201cWe need to go faster!\u201d Ember spread her wings wide, and they shot through the sky, racing against the setting sun.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Jamie and Ember try to avoid in the forest?","options":["Townsfolk","Flowers","Animals","Rocks"],"correct_answer":"Townsfolk"},{"question":"What does Ember ask Jamie when they first enter the forest?","options":["What is magic?","What if they see me?","Where is the cave?","Can we go home?"],"correct_answer":"What if they see me?"},{"question":"What does Jamie suggest to help them get over the log?","options":["Climb over it","Build a bridge","Fly on Ember's back","Go around it"],"correct_answer":"Fly on Ember's back"},{"question":"How does Jamie feel when he first rides on Ember's back?","options":["Scared","Excited","Sleepy","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"Who shouts, 'There it is! The dragon!'?","options":["Jamie","Ember","Mrs. Hargrove","A child"],"correct_answer":"Mrs. Hargrove"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_164_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_164_ch2_img1.png","plot_164_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":644,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
