   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_164_7_10","title":"Beneath the Starlit Scales","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Dragons & Creatures","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the sun dipped low, Jamie stood before the crowd. He felt small. The townsfolk whispered and pointed at Ember, who curled up behind him. Her shimmering scales sparkled in the fading light.\n\n\"Please, listen to me!\" Jamie shouted, his voice shaky. \"Ember is not a monster! She\u2019s my friend!\" \n\nMrs. Hargrove stepped forward. Her face was lined with worry. \"We don\u2019t trust dragons, Jamie. They breathe fire and cause trouble.\"\n\n\u201cBut Ember is gentle!\u201d Jamie insisted, stepping closer to Ember. \u201cShe just wants to go home. We need to help her before the full moon rises!\u201d \n\nThe crowd murmured, uncertain. Jamie could see doubt on their faces. He took a deep breath and remembered Ember's kind eyes. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s work together!\u201d Jamie said. \u201cIf we all help, we can guide Ember to the mountain. If we don\u2019t, she could get lost forever!\u201d \n\nThe townsfolk exchanged glances. Finally, a boy named Tommy spoke up. \u201cI think we should give it a try!\u201d \n\n\u201cMe too!\u201d said another voice, a girl named Lily. \u201cI\u2019ve always wanted to see a dragon up close!\u201d\n\nSlowly, more townsfolk nodded. Jamie's heart raced with hope. Maybe they could do this together! \n\n\u201cAlright,\u201d Mrs. Hargrove said hesitantly. \u201cWe\u2019ll help you, Jamie. But if anything goes wrong, we will protect the town.\u201d\n\n\u201cThank you!\u201d Jamie beamed. \u201cWe can do this!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey gathered supplies: ropes, lanterns, and some snacks. Ember watched with wide eyes. \u201cWhat can I do to help?\u201d she asked, her voice soft. \n\n\u201cYou can fly low to guide us!\u201d Jamie replied. \u201cJust make sure to stay close to the trees!\u201d\n\nAs they ventured into the enchanted forest, Jamie felt excited. With Ember flying beside them, the townsfolk felt braver. They walked together, their shadows dancing in the lantern light. \n\nSuddenly, a rustle came from the bushes. Everyone froze. Ember landed softly beside Jamie. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d she whispered.\n\n\u201cJust a deer,\u201d Tommy said, peeking behind a tree. \u201cSee?\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a spark of light zoomed past! It was a firefly, glowing bright. \u201cLook!\u201d Jamie pointed. \u201cThe fireflies are helping us!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith renewed energy, they continued deeper into the forest. The trees glowed with tiny lights, twinkling like stars. Jamie felt a warm glow in his heart. Maybe they could really make it!\n\nBut then, they heard a loud rustle. The townsfolk stopped in their tracks. Jamie\u2019s heart sank. What now? \n\n\u201cWe need to keep moving!\u201d Jamie said, feeling brave. \u201cEmber, can you help us?\u201d\n\n\u201cOf course!\u201d Ember took a step forward, her wings stretching wide. \u201cLet me show you the way!\u201d\n\nTogether, they faced the unknown, determined to reach the Starlit Cave before it was too late. Jamie glanced up at the sky. The full moon loomed closer, bright and round. They were running out of time!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Jamie ask the townsfolk to help him do?","options":["Catch a deer","Return Ember home","Build a cave","Make a fire"],"correct_answer":"Return Ember home"},{"question":"Who steps forward to support Jamie?","options":["Mrs. Hargrove","Tommy","A deer","Lily"],"correct_answer":"Tommy"},{"question":"What do the townsfolk gather for the journey?","options":["Paints and brushes","Ropes, lanterns, and snacks","Books and toys","Baskets and blankets"],"correct_answer":"Ropes, lanterns, and snacks"},{"question":"What do Jamie and the townsfolk see that gives them hope?","options":["A dragon's fire","A firefly glowing","A rainbow","A scary shadow"],"correct_answer":"A firefly glowing"},{"question":"What does Ember do to help the townsfolk?","options":["She roars loudly","She flies low to guide them","She hides behind a tree","She collects food"],"correct_answer":"She flies low to guide them"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_164_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_164_ch4_img1.png","plot_164_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":470,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
