   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_164_11_14","title":"Beneath the Starlit Scales","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Dragons & Creatures","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As Jamie stepped cautiously into the town square, the sun dipped lower in the sky, casting long shadows from the buildings that loomed like giants over him. The chatter of townsfolk mingled with the rustling leaves, but there was an underlying tension in the air that made Jamie\u2019s heart race. He had to find Mrs. Hargrove and convince her to help Ember, but the sight of the gathering crowd made him want to turn back. \n\n\u201cJamie!\u201d a voice called. It was his best friend, Liam, rushing towards him. \u201cI heard you found a dragon! Is it true?\u201d His eyes sparkled with excitement, but Jamie\u2019s stomach churned. \n\n\u201cYeah, but... it's complicated,\u201d Jamie replied, glancing over his shoulder at the gathering crowd. \u201cThey think she\u2019s dangerous.\u201d\n\nLiam frowned, the excitement draining from his face. \u201cBut she\u2019s not! You know her. You can talk to her. What if we show them?\u201d\n\nBefore Jamie could respond, a loud shout pierced the air. \u201cThere\u2019s the boy! The one who brought the beast to our town!\u201d The voice belonged to Mr. Thompson, a burly man with a face as red as his flannel shirt. The crowd turned, eyes wide with fear and suspicion. \n\n\u201cI didn\u2019t bring her. She just landed in my backyard!\u201d Jamie yelled, trying to defend Ember. \u201cShe needs help to get back home!\u201d\n\nMrs. Hargrove stepped forward, her expression stern and skeptical. \u201cDragons are creatures of destruction, Jamie. You think it\u2019s safe to have one in our midst? What if she breathes fire?\u201d\n\nJamie felt a surge of frustration. \u201cShe\u2019s gentle! She saved me when I fell into the creek. If you\u2019d just give her a chance\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cEnough!\u201d Mrs. Hargrove\u2019s voice cut through the murmurs. \u201cWe cannot risk the safety of our town for a whim. I suggest you leave that dragon where she belongs\u2014far away from us!\u201d\n\nPanic washed over Jamie. What if they decided to chase Ember away? She was only trying to find her way home, just like he was trying to find his voice. \u201cI won\u2019t let you hurt her!\u201d he shouted, surprising even himself with his own courage. \n\nThe crowd gasped. Jamie stood firm, his heart pounding louder than ever. The sky was darkening, and the full moon was almost upon them. With every second that passed, he could feel the weight of Ember\u2019s fate pressing down on him.\n\n\u201cJamie, listen,\u201d Liam said quietly, placing a hand on his shoulder. \u201cYou can\u2019t do this alone. We need a plan.\u201d\n\nJust then, a low rumble echoed through the square, and a gust of wind swept through, sending hats flying and rattling the wooden stalls. Gasps filled the air as Ember\u2019s silhouette appeared in the distance, her scales shimmering like the night sky. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d someone shouted, pointing. \n\nSuddenly, fear transformed into chaos as the townsfolk stumbled back, some shouting for help, others rushing to grab weapons. Jamie\u2019s heart raced as he realized this was the moment he had to confront his greatest fear. \n\n\u201cEmber! Come here!\u201d he called, desperation tinging his voice. He knew that if he didn\u2019t act now, he might lose both Ember and the chance to stand up for what was right. \n\nAs Ember soared closer, her eyes met Jamie\u2019s, sparkling with confusion and worry. He felt a surge of determination. \u201cI have to protect her,\u201d he whispered to himself, stepping forward. \n\nBut before he could take a step, Mrs. Hargrove raised her hand, and the crowd went silent. \u201cYou\u2019ve made your choice, Jamie. We cannot allow her to stay!\u201d \n\nThe moment hung heavily over them, and Jamie\u2019s mind raced. What would he do? He could either run to Ember, risking the wrath of the townsfolk, or stand his ground and fight for her right to belong. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nIn that moment of tension, Jamie\u2019s courage surged within him. He clenched his fists, ready to face the storm that lay ahead. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nHe took a deep breath, feeling the weight of the dragon\u2019s life resting on his shoulders. Just then, a loud screech echoed through the air, making everyone jump. Ember\u2019s cry mingled with Jamie\u2019s resolve, and the decision he had to make loomed closer than ever\u2014would he stand up for his friend, or turn back into the shadows of his fears?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Jamie discover about the townsfolk's feelings towards Ember?","options":["They are excited to meet her.","They believe she is a threat.","They want to keep her as a pet.","They are indifferent."],"correct_answer":"They believe she is a threat."},{"question":"Who is the town elder that challenges Jamie?","options":["Mr. Thompson","Liam","Mrs. Hargrove","Jamie\u2019s mom"],"correct_answer":"Mrs. Hargrove"},{"question":"What does Jamie realize he has to do as Ember appears?","options":["Run away from the crowd","Stand up for Ember","Hide behind Liam","Call for help"],"correct_answer":"Stand up for Ember"},{"question":"What significant event occurs as Jamie faces the townsfolk?","options":["Ember lands peacefully in the square.","The sun sets completely.","A gust of wind disrupts the crowd.","The townsfolk cheer for Jamie."],"correct_answer":"A gust of wind disrupts the crowd."},{"question":"What is Jamie's internal struggle throughout this chapter?","options":["Deciding what to have for dinner","Choosing between staying silent or speaking up","Finding a way to escape","Understanding dragon lore"],"correct_answer":"Choosing between staying silent or speaking up"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_164_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_164_ch3_img1.png","plot_164_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":731,"reading_level":"Builder"}
