   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_157_7_10","title":"The Curious Case of Class 7-B","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Magic School","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Chapter 5: The Thief Revealed\n\nDax, Sofia, and Jaden stood in the swirling halls of the Magic School for Unconventional Wizards. The walls shimmered with colors that danced around them. They had just discovered the enchanted spellbook. Now it was time to confront the mysterious figure.\n\n\u201cDo you think it was them?\u201d whisper Dax, glancing nervously at Sofia and Jaden.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m sure of it!\u201d said Sofia, her eyes sparkling with determination. \u201cWe need to find out who it really is!\u201d\n\nJaden fiddled with his gadget, a small, glowing orb. \u201cThis is a Spell Tracker. It can show us who used the magic last!\u201d He pressed a button, and the orb blinked like a star.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe orb floated into the air, leaving a trail of glittering light. It led them down a twisting corridor filled with strange, singing portraits. Each painting seemed to giggle and gossip about the trio.\n\nSuddenly, the orb stopped in front of a door marked, \u201cClassroom of Forgotten Spells.\u201d They exchanged worried looks. \u201cWhat if the thief is in there?\u201d asked Dax, his heart racing.\n\n\u201cOnly one way to find out,\u201d said Jaden, pushing the door open. The hinges creaked ominously.\n\nInside, the room was dimly lit. Dust hung in the air like sparkles. Shelves were piled high with old spellbooks. In the center of the room stood a shadowy figure, hunched over an open book.\n\n\u201cStop right there!\u201d shouted Sofia, stepping forward.\n\nThe figure turned. It was Avery, the class prankster! \u201cYou caught me,\u201d Avery said, grinning sheepishly. \u201cI just wanted to impress everyone at the showcase.\u201d\n\n\u201cBut stealing spells isn\u2019t right!\u201d Dax said, his voice steady.\n\nAvery nodded. \u201cI know. I thought if I borrowed them, everyone would think I\u2019m cool. I didn\u2019t mean to ruin things.\u201d\n\nSofia smiled gently. \u201cWe can help you learn real magic instead. Teamwork makes us all stronger!\u201d\n\n\u201cReally?\u201d Avery\u2019s eyes brightened.\n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Jaden said. \u201cLet\u2019s all practice with honesty together.\u201d\n\nThe room filled with laughter as the four joined forces. They gathered the stolen spells and returned them to the spell lab. With teamwork, they made their showcase ideas even more magical.\n\nAnd just like that, Class 7-B learned an important lesson: honesty is the best magic of all!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s make this showcase unforgettable!\u201d Dax said, beaming with confidence. \n\nThe friends left the classroom, excited for the adventures ahead!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who do Dax, Sofia, and Jaden find in the Classroom of Forgotten Spells?","options":["Avery","Jaden","A Fuzzy Wumpus","A teacher"],"correct_answer":"Avery"},{"question":"What device does Jaden use to track the spells?","options":["Spell Finder","Magic Mirror","Spell Tracker","Wand of Wonders"],"correct_answer":"Spell Tracker"},{"question":"What lesson do the friends learn in this chapter?","options":["Teamwork isn\u2019t important","Honesty is the best magic","Spells are not fun","Pranks are okay"],"correct_answer":"Honesty is the best magic"},{"question":"What does Avery hope to achieve by stealing spells?","options":["To ruin Class 7-B","To impress everyone at the showcase","To scare the teachers","To keep the spells for himself"],"correct_answer":"To impress everyone at the showcase"},{"question":"How does the chapter end?","options":["With a fight","With laughter and friendship","With Avery running away","With no resolution"],"correct_answer":"With laughter and friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_157_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_157_ch5_img1.png","plot_157_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":400,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
