   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_157_11_14","title":"The Curious Case of Class 7-B","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Magic School","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the first rays of the sun spilled through the swirling clouds over the Magic School for Unconventional Wizards, Class 7-B gathered in their vibrant, shifting classroom. The walls shimmered with colors that changed with the mood of the students. Dax fidgeted in his seat, his eyes darting between his classmates, each of whom seemed to pulse with their own unique magic.\n\n\u201cOkay, everyone! I know the showcase is important, but we have a more pressing issue,\u201d Sofia announced, her voice steady and commanding. She stood at the front, confidence radiating from her like a warm fire. The class fell silent, anticipation crackling in the air. \u201cWe need to figure out who\u2019s been stealing our spells!\u201d\n\nDax felt a shiver run down his spine. The thought of a thief lurking among them was unsettling. \u201cBut\u2026 what if it\u2019s one of us?\u201d he whispered, his voice barely audible.\n\nSofia placed a reassuring hand on his shoulder. \u201cWe\u2019ll get to the bottom of this. Together.\u201d As she spoke, Jaden was busy tinkering with one of his latest inventions\u2014a Spell-Revealer\u2014a contraption that looked like a cross between a crystal ball and an old telephone. It whirred and buzzed, the lights flickering as he adjusted the dials.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s set a trap,\u201d Jaden suggested, his eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cIf we can lure the thief, we can catch them in the act!\u201d\n\n\u201cGreat idea!\u201d Sofia replied, clapping her hands. \u201cDax, you\u2019re good at blending in. Can you keep watch while we set it up?\u201d\n\nDax nodded, anxiety knotting in his stomach. The thought of being the lookout sent his heart racing. He felt like he was about to stand on a stage with all eyes on him, but he had to push through his fears. \u201cSure, I can do that.\u201d\n\nThey decided to set the trap in the Spell Lab, a room filled with bubbling cauldrons and fluttering spell scrolls. As they prepared, a tension hung in the air, thick like fog. Dax felt the weight of their expectations pressing down on him. He couldn\u2019t let them down.\n\nOnce everything was in place, Dax slipped into the shadows, trying to appear inconspicuous. He watched as Sofia and Jaden made a big show of leaving the room, pretending to forget their prized Spell-Binder, a shimmering book that could amplify spells. Dax\u2019s heart raced louder than ever, each beat echoing in his ears.\n\nSuddenly, he noticed a flicker of movement\u2014a shadow darting behind a stack of spell books. Dax held his breath, straining to see. A figure emerged, but it wasn\u2019t Zara or any of his classmates; it was a cloaked figure, their face obscured by a hood.\n\n\u201cGotcha!\u201d Dax shouted, stepping out of his hiding spot. The figure turned, eyes wide with surprise, and then dashed towards the exit. Dax bolted after them, adrenaline surging through his veins.\n\n\u201cStop! Thief!\u201d he yelled, but the figure was fast, weaving through the labyrinth of spell-laden tables. Dax could see Sofia and Jaden\u2019s shocked expressions as they rushed back into the room.\n\n\u201cDax!\u201d Sofia cried. \u201cWait!\u201d\n\nBut Dax was already committed. He chased the thief, who was now just a blur in front of him. As they rounded a corner, Dax caught a glimpse of the figure turning into a dark hallway\u2014the Forgotten Wing of the school, where whispers of lost spells and vanished students lingered like ghosts. \n\nDax hesitated, fear gripping him like a vice. The corridor loomed ahead, dark and eerie. Should he follow the thief into the unknown, or retreat and regroup with his friends? Before he could decide, a loud crash echoed behind him. He turned to see Sofia and Jaden skidding to a halt.\n\n\u201cDax, don\u2019t go alone!\u201d Jaden shouted, his gadget sparking dangerously in his hands. \n\nDax had a choice to make\u2014the dark hallway or safety with his friends. His heart raced like a wild stallion, and he knew this decision could change everything.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Dax feel as he prepares to be the lookout?","options":["Excitement","Anxiety","Indifference","Boredom"],"correct_answer":"Anxiety"},{"question":"What is Jaden inventing in this chapter?","options":["A Spell-Revealer","A flying broomstick","A potion","A magical creature"],"correct_answer":"A Spell-Revealer"},{"question":"What does Dax see that causes him to chase after the thief?","options":["A shadow","A spell book","A bright light","His friends"],"correct_answer":"A shadow"},{"question":"Where does the cloaked figure disappear into?","options":["The library","The courtyard","The dark hallway","The garden"],"correct_answer":"The dark hallway"},{"question":"What choice does Dax face at the end of the chapter?","options":["To chase the thief alone or return to his friends","To leave the school","To ignore the thief","To ask for help"],"correct_answer":"To chase the thief alone or return to his friends"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_157_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_157_ch3_img1.png","plot_157_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":670,"reading_level":"Builder"}
