   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_157_11_14","title":"The Curious Case of Class 7-B","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Magic School","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The walls of the Magic School for Unconventional Wizards twisted and shimmered as Dax, Sofia, and Jaden gathered in the vibrant common room of Class 7-B. Colorful banners danced in the fresh breeze from open windows, each one depicting a different spell or magical creature. Dax's heart raced, his fingers tapping nervously against the table. \"We need a plan,\" he murmured, looking up at his friends.\n\nSofia nodded, her eyes sparkling with determination. \"We can't let the showcase be ruined. We have to find out who\u2019s behind this.\" She glanced at Jaden, who was busy tinkering with a small gadget that whirred and clicked. \"What about your invention? Can it help us track down the missing spells?\"\n\nJaden paused, his glasses slipping down his nose. \"I\u2019ve been working on a Spell Sniffer 3000! It detects magical residue, but it\u2019s still not fully operational,\" he said, a hint of frustration creeping into his voice. \n\nDax leaned forward, curiosity piqued. \"What if we test it in the library? That\u2019s where the last spells disappeared.\"\n\nAs they made their way through the winding corridors, Dax felt the weight of uncertainty. The school felt different today, shadows lurking in corners and whispers echoing from the walls. He glanced sideways at Sofia, who marched confidently ahead, her long hair streaming behind her like a banner of bravery. \"What if it\u2019s someone in our class?\" Dax finally revealed his worry.\n\nSofia stopped abruptly, turning to face him. \"We can\u2019t jump to conclusions. We need to gather evidence first.\" Just then, a flicker of motion at the far end of the corridor caught their attention. A hooded figure slipped behind a door marked \u201cRestricted Section.\u201d \n\n\u201cDid you see that?\u201d Jaden exclaimed, excitement bursting in his voice. \u201cWe should follow them!\u201d\n\nWith their hearts pounding, the trio approached the door. Sofia pushed it open cautiously, revealing a dimly lit room filled with ancient scrolls and spell tomes. Dust motes danced in the narrow beams of light. Dax stepped inside first, the floor creaking under his weight. \n\nSuddenly, the Spell Sniffer 3000 beeped insistently, its whirring noise echoing ominously. Dax\u2019s breath hitched. \"What's that?\" he whispered. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe gadget glowed a vivid blue, indicating a high concentration of magical energy. Jaden grinned, adjusting his glasses. \"It\u2019s working! There\u2019s definitely something here!\" \n\nRacing to the nearest scroll, Dax picked it up, his fingers trembling as he read the faded ink. \u201cThis... this is a spell mix-up! If someone used the wrong combination, it could cause chaos at the showcase!\u201d Hope sparked in his chest. \n\nJust then, they heard footsteps approaching. Jaden quickly stashed the scroll in his backpack, his eyes wide with fear. \"We need to hide!\" \n\nThey ducked behind a towering stack of books just as the hooded figure re-entered the room. Dax held his breath, every second stretching into eternity. The figure was inspecting items on a nearby table, muttering incantations under their breath.\n\n\u201cWho are they?\u201d Sofia whispered, her voice barely audible. \n\nAs they waited in tense silence, a sliver of light caught Dax\u2019s eye. He recognized the figure\u2019s outline\u2014it was Zara, the girl from their class. \n\nDax\u2019s heart sank. Could she be the thief? \n\nThe air grew thick with expectation, and Dax felt a surge of courage. They had to confront her. \u201cOn three,\u201d he whispered, \u201cone, two\u2014\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBefore he could finish, Sofia burst from their hiding spot, pointing an accusatory finger. \u201cZara, what are you doing here?\u201d\n\nZara spun around, her expression shifting from surprise to defiance. \u201cI could ask you the same!\u201d \n\nDax felt the tension crackling between them like a spell on the brink of being unleashed. Could they really get to the bottom of this mystery?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What device is Jaden working on to help find the missing spells?","options":["Spell Sniffer 2000","Spell Sniffer 3000","Magic Tracker","Spell Locator 400"],"correct_answer":"Spell Sniffer 3000"},{"question":"Who do Dax, Sofia, and Jaden find in the restricted section?","options":["Zara","Mr. Twinkletoes","The Principal","A Ghost"],"correct_answer":"Zara"},{"question":"What happens when the Spell Sniffer 3000 is activated?","options":["It explodes","It glows blue","It goes silent","It plays music"],"correct_answer":"It glows blue"},{"question":"What is the main conflict driving Chapter 4?","options":["Finding a lost book","Confronting the hooded figure","Proving Zara is innocent","Discovering the missing spells' location"],"correct_answer":"Discovering the missing spells' location"},{"question":"What do Dax and his friends feel when they first see the hooded figure?","options":["Excitement","Fear","Joy","Confusion"],"correct_answer":"Fear"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_157_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_157_ch4_img1.png","plot_157_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":628,"reading_level":"Builder"}
