   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_157_11_14","title":"The Curious Case of Class 7-B","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Magic School","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The sun dipped low in the sky, casting a golden glow over the Magic School for Unconventional Wizards. Class 7-B was gathered in their usual meeting spot\u2014a cozy corner of the bubblegum-pink courtyard, where enchanted trees whispered secrets and colorful flowers hummed with magic. Dax fidgeted with the edges of his notebook, glancing nervously at Sofia, who was deep in thought.\n\n\u201cWe need to figure out what to do about Zara,\u201d Sofia finally said, her brow furrowed. \u201cIf she isn\u2019t the thief, we\u2019ve wasted time. If she is...\u201d\n\nJaden, tinkering with a gadget that sparkled with tiny circuits, chimed in. \u201cBut what if it\u2019s not her? We could be chasing shadows! She was reading about spell-crafting, not stealing spells.\u201d\n\nDax took a deep breath, summoning his courage. \u201cWhat if we confront her? We can ask her directly. It\u2019s better than hiding in the dark.\u201d\n\nSofia nodded thoughtfully, her expression softening. \u201cAlright. Let\u2019s give her a chance to explain. But we need to be careful\u2014trust can be shattered quickly.\u201d\n\nThey decided to meet Zara at the library, a labyrinth of books and magic that twisted like a vine. As they approached, the air crackled with anticipation. Dax felt a flutter in his stomach, a mix of hope and fear. Were they making the right choice?\n\nAs they stepped inside, the scent of parchment and ink wrapped around them like a warm blanket. The library was dimly lit, with the occasional glow of a floating candle illuminating the shelves. Dax spotted Zara hunched over a table, her fingers dancing over a scroll filled with shimmering glyphs.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nZara looked up, her eyes wide with surprise. \u201cWhat are you doing here?\u201d she asked, a hint of defensiveness in her voice.\n\n\u201cWe wanted to talk,\u201d Sofia said, her confidence shining through. \u201cAbout the missing spells. We think you know something.\u201d\n\nZara\u2019s expression shifted from surprise to something more guarded. \u201cI don\u2019t know what you\u2019re talking about. I\u2019m just trying to learn!\u201d\n\nDax stepped forward, his heart racing. \u201cBut we saw you in the restricted section. You were looking for spells.\u201d\n\n\u201cThose spells were to help us showcase!\u201d Zara exclaimed, frustration bubbling to the surface. \u201cYou think I took them? I\u2019m just as invested in this year-end showcase!\u201d\n\nJaden glanced around the library, the tension thick in the air. \u201cIf you didn\u2019t take them, then who did? We need to figure this out together.\u201d\n\nZara hesitated, her eyes narrowing as she weighed her options. Finally, she sighed. \u201cFine! I\u2019ve seen someone lurking around the spell storage after hours. I thought it was just a rumor, but now I think someone is really trying to sabotage us.\u201d\n\nA spark of realization ignited in Dax\u2019s mind. \u201cWho?\u201d\n\n\u201cLucas from class 7-A,\u201d Zara whispered, glancing over her shoulder as if the shadows had ears. \u201cHe always seemed too interested in our spells.\u201d\n\nSofia\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cWe need to find him!\u201d\n\nThe group rushed through the library and out into the swirling corridors of the school. Dax felt a thrill of determination surging through him. They weren\u2019t just classmates anymore; they were a team united by a shared goal.\n\nAs they rounded a corner, they spotted Lucas, a sly grin on his face, clutching a bundle of shimmering spells. \u201cWell, well, well,\u201d he taunted, \u201cLooks like you\u2019re too late!\u201d\n\nWith a burst of energy, Jaden activated his gadget, sending a surge of dazzling light toward Lucas, illuminating the hallway as if it were daytime. \u201cStop right there!\u201d\n\nLucas stumbled back, his eyes wide with shock. \u201cWhat? You think you can stop me?\u201d\n\nDax felt a rush of bravery. \u201cTogether, we can!\u201d he shouted, and as if the universe conspired to support them, the magic of friendship surged around them.\n\nThe confrontation unfolded, revealing the true strength that lay within their unity. They had learned that honesty and teamwork could vanquish even the trickiest of adversaries, and with one final powerful spell, they cornered Lucas, ensuring their showcase would shine brighter than ever.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs the dust settled, they stood together, triumphant. \u201cLooks like we will have our showcase after all,\u201d Sofia said with a grin.\n\nAnd as Dax looked around at his friends, he realized that the magic of their friendship was more powerful than any spell he could ever learn.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Dax, Sofia, and Jaden confront Zara about?","options":["The missing spells","Her grades","Her friendship","Her gadgets"],"correct_answer":"The missing spells"},{"question":"Who does Zara reveal as the real thief?","options":["Lucas","Dax","Jaden","Sofia"],"correct_answer":"Lucas"},{"question":"What does Jaden use to confront Lucas?","options":["A spell book","His gadget","A wand","A potion"],"correct_answer":"His gadget"},{"question":"What is the main theme of this chapter?","options":["Friendship and teamwork","Learning magic","Competition","Adventure"],"correct_answer":"Friendship and teamwork"},{"question":"How does Dax feel about his friends by the end of the chapter?","options":["Isolated","Powerful","Brave","Nervous"],"correct_answer":"Brave"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_157_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_157_ch5_img1.png","plot_157_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":732,"reading_level":"Builder"}
