   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_157_15_18","title":"The Curious Case of Class 7-B","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Magic School","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"In the heart of the Magic School for Unconventional Wizards, where laughter and chaos intertwined like colorful spells in the air, Class 7-B bustled with a peculiar energy. The corridors twisted and turned, sometimes leading to classrooms that shimmered with enchantment, while others bumbled into spell labs where bubbling potions emitted scents ranging from sweet caramel to the tang of sour lemon. It was a place where the extraordinary was routine, and the ordinary was enchanted.\n\nDax sat in his usual spot at the back of the classroom, a world of books and sketches surrounding him like a protective barrier. His hands fidgeted with the edges of his notebook, where he had been attempting to draft a new spell, one that could conjure a gentle breeze on a summer's day. But even as he wrote, he felt an unsettling weight in his chest, a nagging sensation that something was amiss. \n\nAcross the room, Sofia stood at the front, her presence commanding yet warm, as she organized a group project on the Art of Illusion. \u201cListen up, Class 7-B!\u201d she called, her voice ringing like a clear bell amidst the chatter. \u201cWe need to present our best spells for the year-end showcase, and I want everyone to bring their A-game. No more of this nonsense about disappearing spells!\u201d\n\nThe mention of disappearing spells sent a ripple of murmurs through the classroom. Dax could see Jaden, the quirky inventor with wild hair and an even wilder imagination, fiddling with a gadget that looked as if it had been cobbled together from spare parts and a dash of mischief. \u201cI swear, if I lose another invention to that invisible thief, I\u2019ll\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cShh! It\u2019s not just your inventions, Jaden,\u201d Sofia interrupted, her brow furrowing in concern. \u201cWe\u2019ve all been affected. Spells have been disappearing right before our eyes. We need to figure this out before the showcase. What\u2019s the point of magic if we can\u2019t trust each other?\u201d\n\nDax\u2019s heart raced. There was a darker undertone to Sofia\u2019s words, a hint of betrayal that hung in the air like a storm cloud. The thought that one of their own might be stealing spells sent a shiver down his spine. In a school where friendship was as vital as magic itself, the mere idea felt like a curse.\n\n\u201cWhat if it\u2019s a fellow student?\u201d he blurted out, his voice trembling slightly. \u201cWhat if someone in Class 7-B is\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cEnough!\u201d Sofia interjected, her fierce gaze sweeping across the room. \u201cWe need to stay focused. We\u2019re all in this together, and we can\u2019t let fear tear us apart. Let\u2019s meet after class and brainstorm ideas.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nDax glanced around the classroom, noting the anxious expressions etched on his classmates' faces. He felt a wave of uncertainty wash over him, mingling with determination. This wasn\u2019t just about spells; it was about trust, about the bonds they had forged over the years. He couldn\u2019t let anyone down, especially not when the showcase\u2014their moment to shine\u2014was so close.\n\nAs the bell rang, signaling the end of class, Dax gathered his belongings, his mind whirling with possibilities. Could a friend truly betray them? It was a question he had never wanted to consider, but with each passing moment, it felt more real, more urgent. \n\nOutside, the bright colors of the school faded into the backdrop of a gathering twilight, shadows stretching like ominous fingers. Dax joined Sofia and Jaden near the bubbling fountain that marked the entrance to the courtyard. \n\n\u201cWe need a plan,\u201d Sofia said, her expression resolute. \u201cWe\u2019ll search the library for clues. Spells don\u2019t just vanish without a trace.\u201d\n\n\u201cRight!\u201d Dax agreed, his voice infused with newfound courage. \u201cWe can also set up a surveillance charm. If someone tries to take a spell, we\u2019ll see it happen.\u201d\n\nJaden perked up, his eyes gleaming with excitement. \u201cAnd I can build a prototype that can track the last known spell location! This is going to be epic!\u201d\n\nBut just as their spirits began to lift, an eerie silence enveloped them. A chill coursed through the air, and Dax felt the hairs on the back of his neck stand on end. Had they just imagined the threat, or was it growing closer?\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go,\u201d Sofia urged, her voice barely above a whisper. They turned toward the library, unaware that eyes were watching them from the shadows, keeping secrets of their own.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they approached the grand library doors, the wood creaked ominously, and Dax\u2019s heart raced. He took a deep breath, ready to face whatever mystery lay ahead. But could he trust those beside him, or would betrayal unfold like a dark spell before their very eyes?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the primary conflict faced by Class 7-B?","options":["They need to prepare for the showcase","Their spells are disappearing","They are competing with another class","They have to build new gadgets"],"correct_answer":"Their spells are disappearing"},{"question":"Who is the confident leader of Class 7-B?","options":["Dax","Jaden","Sofia","The Principal"],"correct_answer":"Sofia"},{"question":"What does Dax fidget with during class?","options":["A wand","His notebook","A spell book","Jaden's gadget"],"correct_answer":"His notebook"},{"question":"What does Jaden suggest to help track the thief?","options":["A spell trap","A prototype device","A charm","A potion"],"correct_answer":"A prototype device"},{"question":"What feeling does Dax experience when he considers the possibility of betrayal?","options":["Fear","Happiness","Excitement","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Fear"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_157_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_157_ch1_img1.png","plot_157_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":799,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
