   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_157_15_18","title":"The Curious Case of Class 7-B","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Magic School","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The hallway of the Magic School for Unconventional Wizards hummed with an electric energy that mirrored the turbulence brewing in Class 7-B. Dax, his heart pounding, lingered by the entrance of the spell lab, now a chaotic maelstrom of bubbling potions and swirling magical orbs. A sense of foreboding cloaked the room, almost tangible, as whispers of the thief encircled them like a storm cloud.\n\nSofia brushed her fingers over a shelf laden with tomes of spells, her confidence now tinged with anxiety. \u201cWe need to figure out who\u2019s behind this before the showcase. The competition we face isn\u2019t just against other classes, but against our own fears.\u201d Her voice was steady, yet Dax caught the flicker of doubt in her eyes. \n\n\u201cMaybe we should set a trap,\u201d Jaden suggested, a glint of mischief dancing in his eyes. He was already rummaging through his gadget-laden backpack, pulling out a small device that looked like a cross between a compass and a miniature whirlwind. \u201cThis will help us detect any unauthorized spellcasting!\u201d \n\nDax\u2019s brow furrowed as he watched Jaden configure the device. \u201cBut what if it backfires? What if we accidentally catch the wrong person?\u201d \n\nSofia, sensing the rising tension, stepped closer to Dax, her voice softer. \u201cDax, we have to trust each other. The only way we can solve this is by working as a team.\u201d \n\nJaden finished fiddling and snapped the device shut, its surface gleaming with a faint blue light. \u201cLet\u2019s split up and see what we can find. The sooner we get to the bottom of this, the better.\u201d \n\nAs they dispersed, a heavy silence cloaked the lab. Dax ventured to the far corner, his heart thudding in his chest. Each shadow seemed to whisper secrets, and he wrestled with a rising feeling of betrayal. Could one of his friends truly be a thief? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe air shifted, the light dimmed, and Dax felt the weight of uncertainty pressing down on him as he peered into a bubbling cauldron. Wisps of lavender smoke swirled upward, and for a brief moment, he lost himself in the fragrance, recalling the warmth of camaraderie they once shared. \n\nSuddenly, a crash shattered the silence. Dax darted back to the center of the room, where he found Sofia standing over a shattered glass orb, its shards glimmering ominously on the floor. \u201cI thought I saw something, a flicker of magic,\u201d she explained, her voice barely above a whisper. \u201cBut it was gone before I could catch it.\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe it was a sign,\u201d Jaden piped up, scanning the room with renewed determination. \u201cOr a warning.\u201d \n\nBut as they spoke, an unsettling sensation settled over them. Their trust, once solid, felt fragile, like a web in a gusty wind. The shadows seemed to whisper accusations and doubts. \n\nThen, an unexpected presence filled the doorway. A figure stood cloaked in shadows, their features obscured. \u201cYou think you can catch me?\u201d the figure taunted, their voice dripping with malice. \n\nDax\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWho are you?\u201d \n\nThe figure stepped forward, revealing a familiar face twisted in a grin that chilled Dax to the bone. \u201cYou\u2019ve been looking for me, haven\u2019t you?\u201d \n\nIn that moment, time froze. The revelation struck like lightning\u2014betrayal carved deep into the very fabric of their friendship. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nDax\u2019s mind raced as emotions clashed within him. \u201cWhy?\u201d he managed to choke out, feeling as if the ground was slipping from beneath him. \n\n\u201cI needed the spells,\u201d the figure\u2014one he had trusted\u2014began, but the words tangled in a web of anger and confusion. \u201cYou wouldn\u2019t understand. I was only trying to prove myself.\u201d \n\nSofia stepped forward, her voice trembling slightly, yet holding a fierce edge. \u201cWhat do you mean? This will ruin everything!\u201d \n\n\u201cExactly,\u201d the figure smirked, stepping back into the shadows. \u201cBut for me, it\u2019s just the beginning.\u201d \n\nWith that, the figure vanished, leaving behind only echoes of betrayal and a storm of questions. Dax, Sofia, and Jaden stood frozen, grappling with the enormity of the moment. They needed to confront this betrayal, yet the path ahead twisted darkly, promising only uncertainty.\n\nWith resolve tightening his chest, Dax whispered to his friends, \u201cWe have to choose. We can either let this tear us apart, or we can fight back together.\u201d \n\nAs the last words hung in the air, a decision loomed larger than the mystery itself\u2014trust or vengeance, unity or division. And the haunting question remained: who among them could be truly trusted?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the main conflict Dax, Sofia, and Jaden face in this chapter?","options":["Finding the thief","Trust issues within the group","Preparing for the showcase","Deciding on a class project"],"correct_answer":"Trust issues within the group"},{"question":"What device does Jaden create to help find the thief?","options":["A magical compass","A spell-capturing jar","A gadget to detect spellcasting","A potion of invisibility"],"correct_answer":"A gadget to detect spellcasting"},{"question":"How does Dax feel about the possibility of betrayal?","options":["Excited","Indifferent","Angry","Conflicted"],"correct_answer":"Conflicted"},{"question":"What significant action occurs at the climax of this chapter?","options":["A spell is cast","A figure reveals themselves as the thief","The showcase is canceled","A friendship is mended"],"correct_answer":"A figure reveals themselves as the thief"},{"question":"What choice do the friends face at the end of the chapter?","options":["To confront the thief alone","To abandon their search","To unite against the betrayal","To report to the school authorities"],"correct_answer":"To unite against the betrayal"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_157_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_157_ch3_img1.png","plot_157_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":755,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
