   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_158_11_14","title":"The Elemental Trials","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Magic School","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The wind howled fiercely around Elemental Academy, whistling through the narrow crevices of the towering peaks that surrounded it. Kaia stood at the edge of the wooden balcony, overlooking the enchanted valley below, where the vibrant colors of the changing seasons danced like a lively painting. The view was breathtaking, but something felt off. Dark clouds churned ominously above, casting an eerie shadow over the school.\n\n\u201cKaia!\u201d A voice broke her reverie. It was Leo, his fiery red hair practically glowing against the gray sky. He charged toward her, his expression a mix of excitement and irritation. \u201cHave you seen the storm? It\u2019s like the elements are angry or something!\u201d\n\nKaia turned to face him, trying to keep her heart steady. \u201cIt\u2019s more than just a storm, Leo. I can feel it in the water. Something is coming, and it\u2019s not good.\u201d\n\nLeo scoffed, crossing his arms. \u201cThat\u2019s just the wind talking. You water mages are always so\u2026\u201d he paused, searching for the right word, \u201cmoody.\u201d\n\nKaia rolled her eyes. \u201cAnd you fire mages are always so hot-headed! Can\u2019t you just listen for a moment?\u201d\n\nJust then, a crack of lightning illuminated the sky, and a tremor shook the ground beneath them. The wind picked up, swirling around like a wild creature. Kaia\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWe have to warn the others!\u201d\n\nAs she turned to run inside, she spotted Zara, the wise earth mage, stepping out of the main building. With her long, flowing hair and earthy attire, Zara seemed rooted in the ground itself. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d she asked, her voice calm but piercing.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re in danger!\u201d Kaia exclaimed, glancing back at Leo, who was clearly trying to hide his concern behind bravado.\n\nZara narrowed her green eyes, assessing the storm forming above. \u201cThe elements are out of balance. We need to unite our houses or we\u2019ll never survive whatever is coming.\u201d\n\nKaia nodded, feeling a spark of hope. \u201cBut how do we work together with the rivalry between our houses?\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s focus on what\u2019s important,\u201d Zara said firmly. \u201cIf we don\u2019t join forces, we\u2019ll all be lost.\u201d\n\nJust then, a deafening roar echoed through the valley, sending a chill down their spines. The ground beneath them rumbled again, and Kaia felt the water around her surge with a strange energy. She glanced at Leo, who was staring wide-eyed at the dark clouds.\n\n\u201cOkay, I\u2019m in,\u201d he said reluctantly. \u201cBut we have to show those earth mages and water mages what fire can do!\u201d\n\nKaia took a deep breath, feeling the weight of their decision. \u201cThen let\u2019s start by gathering everyone. We can\u2019t wait any longer.\u201d\n\nAs they pushed forward, Kaia felt the wind whip fiercely around them, almost as if it were trying to warn them. Would they be able to unite their houses before the storm descended upon Elemental Academy? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nSuddenly, as they rounded a corner, the ground shuddered, and a fissure opened near the academy\u2019s heart. Kaia's breath caught in her throat. \u201cWhat if the storm is more than just a storm?\u201d \n\nZara knelt, touching the ground, her eyes wide with fear. \u201cThis isn\u2019t just weather. This is a call for the Elemental Trials.\u201d \n\nKaia felt a sense of dread. \u201cTrials? What trials? And how do we stop this?\u201d\n\nLeo clenched his fists, determination shining in his eyes. \u201cWe\u2019ll figure it out together. No more rivalry. We\u2019re stronger as one.\u201d\n\nThe weight of their shared challenge hung heavy in the air as they forged ahead, the storm building behind them. The fate of their school rested on their shoulders, and time was running out.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Kaia shouted, racing toward the heart of the academy, feeling the elements swirl with an energy that threatened to consume them all.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What magical affinities are represented at Elemental Academy?","options":["Earth, Air, Fire, Water","Earth, Ice, Fire, Lightning","Wind, Water, Fire, Light","Earth, Fire, Shadow, Light"],"correct_answer":"Earth, Air, Fire, Water"},{"question":"What does Kaia feel is wrong with the storm?","options":["It\u2019s just a normal storm","It feels like a warning","It's beautiful","It\u2019s too loud"],"correct_answer":"It feels like a warning"},{"question":"Who is the wise earth mage introduced in this chapter?","options":["Kaia","Leo","Zara","Mira"],"correct_answer":"Zara"},{"question":"What do the characters decide they need to do in response to the storm?","options":["Fight each other","Ignore the storm","Unite their houses","Hide in their rooms"],"correct_answer":"Unite their houses"},{"question":"What happens when Kaia and her friends approach the academy's heart?","options":["They find treasure","A fissure opens in the ground","They meet a dragon","The storm disappears"],"correct_answer":"A fissure opens in the ground"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_158_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_158_ch1_img1.png","plot_158_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":647,"reading_level":"Builder"}
