   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"fantasy_160_7_10","title":"The Potion Master's Apprentice","genre":"Fantasy","sub_genre":"Magic School","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Lila stood in the Potion Master\u2019s workshop, her heart racing. The purple mist still swirled around the room, dancing like sparks of mischief. She glanced at Master Eldrin, who wore a frown like a storm cloud. \n\n\u201cLila, if you want to be my apprentice, you must fix this potion,\u201d he said, crossing his arms. \u201cCan you do it?\u201d\n\nLila took a deep breath. \u201cYes, Master Eldrin. I can try.\u201d\n\n\u201cTry?\u201d he scoffed. \u201cYou need to be sure! Go, gather the ingredients.\u201d \n\nNodding, Lila and Sam dashed to the shelves. Jars filled with colorful potions sparkled like jewels. Lila scanned the labels. \u201cWe need blue moonflower petals, right?\u201d she asked.\n\n\u201cYes! And maybe dragon scale powder!\u201d Sam added, excitement bubbling in his voice. \n\nAs they collected the ingredients, Lila felt a spark of hope. \u201cWhat if we add crystal dust? It could help clear the mist!\u201d \n\n\u201cGreat idea!\u201d Sam cheered. \u201cLet\u2019s hurry!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nLila pointed at a tall jar filled with shimmering dust. \u201cThat one! Look how it sparkles!\u201d\n\nThey carefully measured each ingredient. Lila\u2019s hands shook, but she focused. \u201cOkay, time to mix!\u201d she said, pouring the petals first. The colors swirled together, creating a bright blue potion.\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed in the workshop. A shelf of jars tipped over, spilling colorful liquids everywhere! Lila gasped. \u201cWhat happened?\u201d\n\n\u201cI think it was the cat!\u201d Sam exclaimed, pointing at a fluffy creature that had leaped onto the table. \n\n\u201cFiddlesticks!\u201d Master Eldrin grumbled, rushing over. \u201cGet that cat out! We don\u2019t have time for distractions!\u201d\n\nLila felt despair wash over her. They were running out of time! But then, she remembered the potion. \u201cSam, we need to finish this!\u201d \n\nThey worked quickly, stirring and mixing. The potion bubbled furiously, giving off a bright glow. \u201cDo you think it will work?\u201d Sam asked nervously.\n\n\u201cIt has to!\u201d Lila said, her eyes shining with determination. \u201cHere goes nothing!\u201d\n\nLila carefully poured the potion into the mist. The room filled with a bright light, and the purple mist began to fade. Moments later, the workshop was clear. \n\nMaster Eldrin stared in disbelief. \u201cYou did it, Lila!\u201d His frown turned into a surprised smile. \u201cWell done!\u201d\n\nLila beamed. \u201cWe did it together, Sam!\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah! Teamwork!\u201d Sam shouted, jumping with joy. \n\nBut just then, a tiny puff of purple smoke appeared again. \u201cOh no! What now?\u201d Lila whispered, her excitement quickly fading.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey both stared at the smoke, waiting for a new surprise. Lila felt a thrill of adventure. \u201cLet\u2019s find out!\u201d she said, ready for whatever came next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Lila and Sam need to gather to fix the potion?","options":["Blue moonflower petals","Chocolate chips","Banana peels","Rainbow sprinkles"],"correct_answer":"Blue moonflower petals"},{"question":"What caused the crash in the workshop?","options":["A bird","A dog","A cat","A flying potion"],"correct_answer":"A cat"},{"question":"How did Master Eldrin react when Lila fixed the potion?","options":["He was angry","He was surprised","He laughed","He left the room"],"correct_answer":"He was surprised"},{"question":"What did Lila feel when she was mixing the potion?","options":["Fear","Joy","Determination","Sadness"],"correct_answer":"Determination"},{"question":"What hint of trouble appeared at the end of the chapter?","options":["A loud noise","Purple smoke","A new potion","A missing ingredient"],"correct_answer":"Purple smoke"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_160_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_160_ch4_img1.png","plot_160_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":433,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
