   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_326_7_10","title":"Whispers of the Green","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Mia and Sam raced through the vibrant grove, heartbeats quickening. The sun peeked through leaves that shimmered like emeralds. \u201cWe need to find the lost seeds!\u201d Mia exclaimed, determination in her voice. \n\n\u201cRight!\u201d Sam replied, adjusting his glasses. \u201cLet\u2019s check under the big willow tree!\u201d They dashed over, the ground soft beneath their feet.\n\nAs they reached the willow, a gentle breeze whispered through the branches. \u201cHello, young friends!\u201d called out a voice. It was Grassy, the wise plant. \u201cI see you are in a hurry!\u201d\n\n\u201cWe are, Grassy!\u201d Mia said, panting slightly. \u201cWe need seeds to save the grove!\u201d\n\nGrassy nodded wisely. \u201cI can help. Search the roots; you may find what you seek.\u201d \n\nJust then, they heard loud voices. \u201cThis way! They can\u2019t have gone far!\u201d It was the scavengers!\n\nMia felt a rush of fear. \u201cThey\u2019re coming! We have to hurry!\u201d \n\nWith Sam\u2019s clever gadgets, they quickly devised an escape plan. \u201cHow about we use the leaf glider?\u201d Sam suggested, pulling out a small device with colorful leaves attached.\n\n\u201cGreat idea!\u201d Mia grinned. They quickly set it up. \n\n\u201cNow, remember,\u201d Grassy said. \u201cIf you fly high, the scavengers won\u2019t see you!\u201d\n\nWith a whoosh, Mia and Sam soared into the air on their leaf glider. The grove below sparkled like a treasure. \u201cLook!\u201d Mia shouted, pointing. \u201cThere\u2019s a patch of glowing seeds!\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s land there!\u201d Sam cried out.\n\nAs they swooped down, the glowing seeds twinkled like stars. \u201cWe found them!\u201d they cheered together. \n\nSuddenly, a huge shadow loomed over them. A scavenger had spotted them! \u201cGet those kids!\u201d he yelled, reaching out. \n\nMia and Sam grabbed the seeds and dashed behind the glowing flowers. \u201cWe can do this!\u201d Mia said, her heart racing.\n\nThey hid while the scavenger searched, but then, Grassy spoke softly. \u201cUse the magic of the grove!\u201d \n\nMia closed her eyes. \u201cWhat do we do?\u201d \n\n\u201cTrust the plants!\u201d Grassy said. \u201cOn my count!\u201d \n\nTogether they whispered to the flowers, who began to bloom brightly. The colors exploded around them, and the scavenger stumbled back, blinded by the light. \n\n\u201cRun!\u201d shouted Sam. They dashed past the confused scavenger and zoomed back to safety.\n\nBreathless but excited, Mia and Sam held the glowing seeds tightly. \u201cWe did it!\u201d Mia laughed, feeling as if they were flying.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s plant them!\u201d Sam suggested. \u201cWe can restore the grove together!\u201d\n\n\u201cYes! The grove will be saved!\u201d Mia shouted, her heart full of hope.\n\nWith their newfound seeds, they felt a sense of triumph. Together, they learned that courage and teamwork could conquer any challenge.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Mia and Sam need to save the grove?","options":["Water","Magic rocks","Lost seeds","Food"],"correct_answer":"Lost seeds"},{"question":"Who helps Mia and Sam in the grove?","options":["A squirrel","A bird","Grassy, the wise plant","A tree fairy"],"correct_answer":"Grassy, the wise plant"},{"question":"What do they use to escape from the scavenger?","options":["A boat","A bike","A leaf glider","A car"],"correct_answer":"A leaf glider"},{"question":"What happens when they whisper to the flowers?","options":["They grow bigger","They bloom brightly","They wilt","They turn brown"],"correct_answer":"They bloom brightly"},{"question":"How do Mia and Sam feel after finding the seeds?","options":["Scared","Excited","Bored","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_326_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_326_ch5_img1.png","plot_326_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":438,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
