   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_327_7_10","title":"The Last Library","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Leo and Clara stood before the hidden library, their hearts racing. Dust danced in the air, swirling in the sunlight that peeked through broken windows. \"This place is amazing!\" Clara exclaimed, her eyes wide with wonder. \n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed outside. The siblings froze. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Leo whispered, his voice shaky. They hurried to the window and peeked out. A group of book hunters stormed into the abandoned street! \n\n\"We need to hide!\" yelled Clara, pulling Leo deeper into the library. They ducked behind a tall shelf filled with colorful books. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nThe hunters\u2019 voices grew louder. \u201cWe know there are books here! Find them!\u201d One hunter shouted, waving a flashlight. Leo\u2019s heart pounded. \"We have to protect these stories, Clara,\" he said urgently.\n\nClara nodded, her face serious. \"But how? We can\u2019t fight them!\u201d \n\nJust then, the quirky librarian appeared from the shadows, wearing a long, patchy coat. \"You two must listen carefully,\" she said, her eyes sparkling. \"These books hold magic. We must use it wisely.\"\n\n\u201cMagic?\u201d Leo asked, his curiosity piqued. \n\n\u201cWith the right words, you can summon stories to help you!\u201d she replied. \u201cBut the hunters want to control what you can and cannot read. You must be brave! We need to move!\u201d \n\nLeo took a deep breath. \u201cOkay! What do we do?\u201d \n\n\u201cFollow me. We\u2019ll gather the stories and move to safety!\u201d The librarian rushed to a hidden door behind the shelf. Clara grabbed Leo's hand, and they all squeezed through just as the hunters burst into the library.\n\n\u201cWhere did they go?!\u201d one hunter growled. They listened as footsteps echoed around the room. \n\nLeo felt a surge of fear. \u201cWhat if they find us?\u201d \n\nClara squeezed his hand tighter. \u201cThey won\u2019t! We\u2019ll outsmart them!\u201d \n\nAs they entered the secret passage, the librarian turned to them. \u201cThis is the key to the last library. Use the stories wisely!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the ground shook. A loud rumble filled the air. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?!\u201d Clara shouted. The walls began to tremble. \n\n\u201cQuickly! We need to hurry!\u201d The librarian shouted, leading them deeper into the darkness. \n\n\u201cWhere does this lead?\u201d Leo asked, panic rising in his chest. \n\n\u201cTo a place where the stories can be safe,\u201d she replied. But before she could explain, the ceiling above them cracked and a loud crash echoed.\n\n\u201cNo! We can\u2019t get trapped!\u201d Leo screamed. \n\nThey had to make a choice: stay and risk being caught or move forward into the unknown. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Clara shouted, pushing Leo ahead. They dashed forward as dust fell around them, the sound of the hunters growing fainter behind them. \n\nThe adrenaline surged. Leo could feel the weight of the stories in his heart. Would they find safety in this hidden world? The adventure was just beginning. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Leo and Clara find in the hidden library?","options":["Books","Toys","Food","Clothes"],"correct_answer":"Books"},{"question":"Who helps Leo and Clara escape from the hunters?","options":["Their parents","A librarian","A teacher","A friend"],"correct_answer":"A librarian"},{"question":"What do the hunters want?","options":["To help Leo and Clara","To find the books","To play games","To take a nap"],"correct_answer":"To find the books"},{"question":"What does the librarian say about stories?","options":["They are boring","They hold magic","They don't matter","They are expensive"],"correct_answer":"They hold magic"},{"question":"What happens at the end of the chapter?","options":["They find more books","The ceiling crashes","They go home","They meet new friends"],"correct_answer":"The ceiling crashes"}]},"images":null,"word_count":471,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
