   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_327_11_14","title":"The Last Library","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The sun hung low in the sky, casting long shadows over the crumbling buildings of the abandoned city. Dust swirled in the stagnant air, creating a hazy veil over what remained of a once-vibrant world. Leo, a fourteen-year-old with tousled hair and bright blue eyes, stepped cautiously through the remnants of a shattered street. He had heard tales of forgotten places, but nothing could have prepared him for the eerie stillness that surrounded him.\n\n\u201cLeo, wait up!\u201d Clara called, her voice echoing down the empty alleyway. She was his younger sister, wild and full of energy, her pigtails bouncing as she hurried to catch up. \u201cAre we really going to explore this whole city?\u201d\n\n\u201cJust a little further,\u201d Leo replied, his heart racing with both excitement and apprehension. \u201cI want to see if we can find any more books.\u201d The last library, they\u2019d learned, was hidden away, perhaps somewhere in this forsaken landscape. Leo could feel the weight of knowledge pressing on him like a forgotten promise.\n\nAs they rounded a corner, they stumbled upon a vast building with a towering entrance, its doors cracked open as if inviting them in. The faded sign above read \u201cLibrary.\u201d Leo\u2019s breath caught in his throat. This had to be it\u2014the last library! [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nClara\u2019s eyes sparkled with mischief. \u201cLet\u2019s go inside!\u201d she urged, pushing the door wide open. The hinges creaked ominously, and the pair stepped into a world frozen in time. Dust motes danced in the dim light, and the scent of old paper filled their noses. Shelves lined the walls, heavy with forgotten texts, their spines cracked and faded, but still full of stories waiting to be told.\n\n\u201cWhat if we could bring these back to everyone?\u201d Clara mused, her voice a whisper as they approached a central reading room. \u201cImagine if people remembered how to dream again.\u201d \n\n\u201cOr how to hope,\u201d Leo added, his heart swelling with the possibilities. As they explored, they discovered worn journals, tattered novels, and even some ancient tomes that seemed to hum with energy. Each book they touched felt like a spark of magic in their fingertips.\n\nSuddenly, a noise shattered the silence\u2014a loud crash from the entrance. Leo's stomach dropped. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d he asked, his voice barely above a whisper.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we should hide,\u201d Clara suggested, her eyes wide with fear. They darted behind a nearby shelf just as two figures entered the library. The strangers were rugged and rough-looking, with determined expressions. They were book hunters, scavengers who believed knowledge should be hoarded, not shared.\n\n\u201cWe can\u2019t let anyone else find these books,\u201d one of them growled, eyeing the shelves hungrily. \u201cLet\u2019s gather what we can and get out of here.\u201d\n\nLeo\u2019s heart raced as they watched. The urgency of their situation hit him hard. They couldn\u2019t let these book hunters take the treasures of the past. He exchanged a glance with Clara, and in that moment, they both knew\u2014they had to protect the last library, no matter the cost.\n\n\u201cThe stories can\u2019t die,\u201d Leo whispered, his resolve hardening. \u201cWe have to save them.\u201d [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs he formulated a plan, fear was replaced with determination. Together, he and Clara would gather the scattered tomes, protect their newfound treasure, and maybe\u2014just maybe\u2014bring stories back to their fractured world.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Leo and Clara discover inside the library?","options":["A secret treasure","A hidden computer","Forgotten books","A magical portal"],"correct_answer":"Forgotten books"},{"question":"What is the main conflict introduced in this chapter?","options":["Leo and Clara are lost in the city","Book hunters want to take the books","The library is collapsing","They can't find the library"],"correct_answer":"Book hunters want to take the books"},{"question":"How does Clara feel about bringing back stories to their world?","options":["She is indifferent","She is excited","She is scared","She wants to leave"],"correct_answer":"She is excited"},{"question":"What is the setting of the story?","options":["A colorful village","An abandoned city","A mystical forest","A futuristic school"],"correct_answer":"An abandoned city"},{"question":"What motivates Leo to protect the library?","options":["His love for adventure","His fear of the book hunters","His desire for knowledge","His wish to impress Clara"],"correct_answer":"His desire for knowledge"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_327_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_327_ch1_img1.png","plot_327_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":566,"reading_level":"Builder"}
