   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_327_11_14","title":"The Last Library","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the sun hung low in the sky, casting long shadows over the abandoned city, Leo stood at the entrance of the hidden library, his heart racing. Clara tugged at his sleeve, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cCan you believe this? It\u2019s like finding a treasure chest!\u201d \n\nLeo nodded, his mind racing ahead to the stories they might uncover. Dust motes danced in the golden light filtering through the cracked windows, illuminating rows of books lined against the walls. Each one seemed to whisper secrets of a world long forgotten.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s start with this one!\u201d Clara exclaimed, pulling a book off the nearest shelf. The cover was tattered, but the title, *Adventures in Other Worlds*, glimmered as if it were brand new. \u201cWhat do you think it\u2019s about?\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s about space travel or underwater kingdoms,\u201d Leo suggested, his imagination igniting. But as he opened the book, a sudden noise shattered their moment of wonder\u2014a loud crash echoed from the back of the library.\n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Clara\u2019s face paled. \n\n\u201cStay here,\u201d Leo whispered, his heart pounding like a drum. He crept towards the sound, the air thick with tension. Clara clutched the book tightly, her knuckles turning white.\n\nAs Leo rounded the corner, he spotted two figures rummaging through the shelves. Their faces were obscured by shadow, but he could see the glint of metal\u2014knives. He froze, realizing these must be the book hunters he had overheard in the market. \n\n\u201cWe need to move, Clara!\u201d Leo hissed, retreating back. \u201cThey\u2019re here!\u201d\n\nClara\u2019s eyes widened in fear. \u201cWhat do we do? They can\u2019t take the books!\u201d\n\n\u201cWe have to distract them,\u201d Leo said, thinking quickly. They couldn\u2019t let the hunters know about the hidden library\u2019s treasures. \u201cDo you still have that noise maker we found last week?\u201d\n\nClara nodded, her adventurous spirit igniting once more. \u201cYes! It\u2019s in my backpack!\u201d \n\n\u201cPerfect! We\u2019ll create a diversion, then sneak out the back.\u201d \n\nAs Clara rummaged through her bag, the sound of footsteps grew closer. Leo\u2019s heart raced. He could feel the hunters\u2019 presence like a weight pressing down on him. \u201cHurry!\u201d he urged, glancing back to see the dark figures moving closer. \n\nClara finally pulled out the small device. \u201cGot it! On three, we throw it to the left and run right!\u201d \n\n\u201cOkay. One, two\u2014\u201d\n\nSuddenly, the door creaked open behind them, and the hunters stepped into view. \u201cHey! You two! What are you doing here?\u201d one of them shouted, eyes narrowing.\n\nLeo\u2019s breath caught in his throat. They had been caught! \u201cNow, Clara!\u201d he yelled.\n\nShe hurled the noise maker. It clattered loudly to the floor, and a burst of sound erupted, echoing through the library. The hunters turned, momentarily distracted. \n\n\u201cGo!\u201d Leo shouted, grabbing Clara\u2019s hand. Together, they sprinted towards the back exit, adrenaline coursing through their veins. \n\nOutside, the cool air rushed over them as they stumbled into the shadows of the crumbling city. They could hear the hunters yelling behind them, but they didn\u2019t stop running until they reached a narrow alleyway, breathless and wide-eyed.\n\n\u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d Clara asked, panting heavily. \n\n\u201cWe need to find a safe place to hide and protect the library,\u201d Leo replied, determination resounding in his voice. \u201cThis is just the beginning. We can\u2019t let anyone take our stories.\u201d\n\nThe sun dipped further below the horizon, leaving the city cloaked in twilight. The shadows danced around them, as if whispering secrets of their own. They would have to be brave, clever, and above all, united if they wanted to keep the magic of stories alive.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Leo and Clara discover inside the hidden library?","options":["A treasure map","A spaceship","Books filled with stories","A secret passage"],"correct_answer":"Books filled with stories"},{"question":"What do the book hunters want to do?","options":["Share the books with everyone","Control the knowledge","Burn the books","Help Leo and Clara"],"correct_answer":"Control the knowledge"},{"question":"What do Leo and Clara use to distract the hunters?","options":["A loud noise maker","A book","Fireworks","Their voices"],"correct_answer":"A loud noise maker"},{"question":"How do Leo and Clara feel about their mission?","options":["Excited","Indifferent","Scared","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What do Leo and Clara plan to do next after escaping?","options":["Find more books","Go home","Protect the library","Talk to the hunters"],"correct_answer":"Protect the library"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_327_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_327_ch2_img1.png","plot_327_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":615,"reading_level":"Builder"}
