   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_327_11_14","title":"The Last Library","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting long shadows across the crumbling buildings of the abandoned city, Leo and Clara stood at the entrance of the last library. The air was thick with dust, and the silence was deep, broken only by the distant echoes of their footsteps. Leo felt a shiver run down his spine. \u201cDo you think they\u2019re still out there?\u201d he whispered, glancing nervously over his shoulder.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Clara replied, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cBut we have to find the rest of the books before those hunters do!\u201d \n\nSteeling himself, Leo nodded. They stepped inside, where the warm glow of the library\u2019s enchanted lights beckoned them further. Rows upon rows of books lined the walls, their spines whispering secrets of adventures waiting to be discovered. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed from the far corner of the library. Leo\u2019s heart raced as he turned to Clara. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d \n\n\u201cYeah,\u201d she said, her voice tinged with both fear and thrill. \u201cLet\u2019s check it out!\u201d\n\nThey crept toward the noise, the scent of old paper filling their lungs. As they rounded a shelf, they spotted a figure rummaging through a pile of books. A tall, shadowy person with tattered clothing was stuffing volumes into a worn backpack. \n\n\u201cStop!\u201d Clara shouted, her voice ringing like a bell. The figure whirled around, eyes wide with surprise. \n\n\u201cGet back!\u201d the stranger yelled, brandishing a rusty metal pipe. \n\nLeo\u2019s mind raced. \u201cWait! We\u2019re not here to fight! We\u2019re looking for\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cFor what? More stories to hoard?\u201d the stranger interrupted, taking a menacing step forward. \u201cYou don\u2019t understand. Knowledge is power, and it belongs to those who can control it!\u201d\n\nClara stepped in front of Leo, her small frame filled with determination. \u201cNo! Knowledge should be shared! We\u2019re trying to rescue these books from people like you!\u201d\n\nThe stranger hesitated, confusion flickering in their eyes. \u201cRescue? Why would you want to save them?\u201d\n\n\u201cBecause stories can change the world!\u201d Leo exclaimed, his voice growing stronger. \u201cIf we don\u2019t bring back the magic of books, what will happen to us?\u201d\n\nThe stranger's grip on the pipe loosened slightly. \u201cYou really believe that?\u201d \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Clara affirmed, her eyes bright with hope. \u201cWe have to fight for these stories. They might be the key to healing our broken world!\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from behind them, and Leo's heart sank as he turned to see a group of book hunters bursting through the library door. Their leader, a tall figure with a scar across his cheek, pointed directly at Leo and Clara. \u201cThere they are! Grab the books!\u201d\n\n\u201cRun!\u201d Leo shouted, grabbing Clara\u2019s hand as they dashed deeper into the library, books flying in their wake. They could hear the hunters\u2019 footsteps pounding behind them, a thundering heartbeat that matched their own.\n\n\u201cWhere do we go?\u201d Clara gasped, glancing around at the labyrinth of shelves. \n\n\u201cUp!\u201d Leo shouted, spotting a narrow staircase leading to the second floor. They sprinted up, the sound of the hunters growing closer. \n\nWhen they reached the top, Leo grabbed Clara's arm. \u201cWe have to find a way to hide!\u201d \n\nThey ducked behind a stack of books just as the hunters reached the stairs. Leo\u2019s heart pounded as he peered through the gaps, watching the hunters search frantically. \n\n\u201cWhere are they?\u201d the leader growled, his voice low and menacing. \n\nLeo held his breath, knowing every second counted. He exchanged a worried glance with Clara, who whispered, \u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d\n\nJust then, Leo\u2019s eyes landed on a small, hidden door at the end of the hallway. It was slightly ajar, a sliver of light spilling out. \u201cThere!\u201d he whispered urgently. \u201cWe can escape through there!\u201d\n\nAs they prepared to move, the hunters turned to head back downstairs. \u201cLet\u2019s check the second level!\u201d the leader shouted, and all at once, Leo and Clara knew they had to act fast. \n\n\u201cOn three,\u201d Leo whispered. \u201cOne\u2026 two\u2026 three!\u201d They bolted toward the door, adrenaline surging through them.\n\nAs they reached for the handle, the door suddenly swung open, revealing a dark, winding staircase leading down into the shadows. Leo and Clara exchanged a quick look filled with uncertainty. Should they trust the unknown?\n\n\u201cGo!\u201d Clara urged, and they plunged into the darkness together, the echoes of their pursuers fading behind them.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Leo and Clara find at the entrance of the library?","options":["A dark staircase","A hidden treasure","The last library filled with books","A group of book hunters"],"correct_answer":"The last library filled with books"},{"question":"What does the shadowy figure believe about knowledge?","options":["It should be shared","It belongs to everyone","It should be controlled","It's useless"],"correct_answer":"It should be controlled"},{"question":"What is Clara's response when the figure questions their intentions?","options":["She runs away","She argues back","She stays silent","She tells a story"],"correct_answer":"She argues back"},{"question":"What urgent decision do Leo and Clara have to make at the end of the chapter?","options":["To stay and fight the hunters","To run back into the library","To escape down a mysterious staircase","To give up their mission"],"correct_answer":"To escape down a mysterious staircase"},{"question":"What emotion drives Leo as he faces the hunters?","options":["Excitement","Fear","Confusion","Joy"],"correct_answer":"Fear"}]},"images":null,"word_count":740,"reading_level":"Builder"}
