   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_327_11_14","title":"The Last Library","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As Leo and Clara stumbled through the dusty corridors of the library, the air was thick with the smell of old paper and forgotten stories. Sunlight filtered through broken windows, casting eerie shadows that danced across the crumbling walls. \u201cThis place is amazing!\u201d Clara exclaimed, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cImagine all the worlds waiting for us!\u201d \n\n\u201cYeah, but we need to hurry,\u201d Leo reminded her, his heart racing as he thought of the book hunters lurking outside. \u201cWe can\u2019t let them find us here.\u201d\n\nJust then, they heard a low rumble\u2014a sound that sent a shiver down Leo\u2019s spine. It was the unmistakable growl of distant engines. \u201cThey\u2019re getting closer!\u201d Clara whispered, her voice trembling. Leo nodded, determination hardening his features. They needed to find more books before the hunters discovered their hideout.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s split up,\u201d Leo suggested, his mind racing with possibilities. \u201cI\u2019ll check the reading room, and you can explore the basement. Maybe we\u2019ll find something valuable.\u201d Clara hesitated, her adventurous spirit clashing with her concern for Leo\u2019s safety.\n\n\u201cBe careful, okay? I don\u2019t want you getting caught,\u201d she replied, biting her lip as she held his gaze. \n\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry. I\u2019ll be back before you know it,\u201d he said, trying to sound braver than he felt. With a reluctant nod, they went their separate ways.\n\nLeo crept into the reading room, a vast space lined with shelves that seemed to lean against gravity, burdened by the weight of the past. There were chairs that looked like they had stories of their own, and Leo couldn\u2019t help but imagine the people who once sat there, lost in adventures far beyond this desolate city. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, Leo\u2019s foot caught on something beneath a pile of dusty old newspapers. With a swift movement, he uncovered a small, leather-bound book. Its cover was worn, but the title was still legible: \u201cThe Lost Tales of Eldoria.\u201d His heart raced with excitement. This could be the key to rekindling the magic of storytelling!\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from the basement, and Leo\u2019s heart sank. Clara! He raced toward the sound, the book clutched tightly in his hand. \n\nRushing down the stairs, Leo found Clara standing over a large, toppled bookshelf. \u201cI was trying to reach that book,\u201d she explained breathlessly, pointing to a colorful volume wedged between the floor and the wall, but it had fallen with the shelf, sending a cascade of dust into the air. \n\n\u201cDid you hear that?\u201d Leo demanded, suddenly aware of the distant roar of the hunters\u2019 engines, now even closer. \u201cWe need to move\u2014fast!\u201d\n\nAs they gathered the scattered books, a shadow loomed in the doorway. Leo\u2019s breath hitched in his throat. It was one of the book hunters, a tall figure framed by the flickering light behind them. \u201cWell, well,\u201d he sneered, \u201clooks like I\u2019ve found some little thieves.\u201d\n\nClara stepped forward, her eyes aflame with courage. \u201cWe\u2019re not stealing! We\u2019re saving these stories!\u201d \n\nThe hunter chuckled darkly, but Leo could see a flicker of uncertainty in his eyes. \u201cSaving? Or hoarding?\u201d he replied. \u201cThis knowledge is too powerful for the likes of you.\u201d \n\nLeo\u2019s heart pounded, but he also felt a rush of hope. They were on the precipice of something great, and they wouldn\u2019t back down now. \u201cYou don\u2019t understand what these stories can do,\u201d Leo said, his voice steady. \u201cThey can inspire people. They can change lives!\u201d\n\nJust then, the sound of a door creaking open echoed through the basement, and Leo\u2019s mind raced. The librarian! If they could get to her, maybe she could help. \n\n\u201cWe need to get out of here!\u201d Leo shouted, grabbing Clara\u2019s hand. They dashed past the hunter, who momentarily hesitated, caught off guard by their sudden burst of bravery. \n\nAs they burst through the door, Leo felt a surge of determination. This was just the beginning. They were not just protecting books; they were protecting hope itself.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the title of the book Leo discovers?","options":["The Last Library","The Lost Tales of Eldoria","The Hunter's Secret","Stories of the Past"],"correct_answer":"The Lost Tales of Eldoria"},{"question":"What does Clara dream of achieving through stories?","options":["Becoming a librarian","Saving the world","Finding treasure","Traveling the universe"],"correct_answer":"Saving the world"},{"question":"Who threatens Leo and Clara in the basement?","options":["The librarian","A book hunter","Their parents","A librarian's ghost"],"correct_answer":"A book hunter"},{"question":"Why do Leo and Clara split up?","options":["To explore different sections","To escape the library","Because they were arguing","To find treasure"],"correct_answer":"To explore different sections"},{"question":"What motivates Leo to confront the hunter?","options":["Fear of getting caught","Desire to save stories","Wanting to impress Clara","Hoping for treasure"],"correct_answer":"Desire to save stories"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_327_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_327_ch4_img1.png","plot_327_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":677,"reading_level":"Builder"}
