   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_328_7_10","title":"Skyward: The Floating Village","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ava stood on the edge of the floating village, looking at the dark clouds gathering in the distance. The wind whistled through the wooden structures. \u201cWhat if the storm is worse than we thought?\u201d she asked Finn, her voice trembling.\n\nFinn shrugged, but his eyes sparkled with determination. \u201cWe have to find out! Let\u2019s go!\u201d \n\nMia and Oliver joined them, their faces set with resolve. \u201cTogether, we can face anything!\u201d Mia declared. The group moved toward the Sky Tower, the tallest point in the village. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe Sky Tower was a great, swirling spiral of wood and metal. At the top, they could see far and wide. Ava could hardly contain her excitement. \u201cMaybe we\u2019ll spot the storm\u2019s source from up there!\u201d \n\nThey climbed the winding stairs, their hearts racing. When they reached the top, the view was breathtaking. Below, the ocean of clouds rolled like a giant blanket. But on the horizon, a massive storm cloud loomed. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Oliver shouted, pointing. \u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d \n\nA flash of light flickered at the edge of the storm. \u201cI think it\u2019s\u2026 a ship!\u201d Mia exclaimed. \n\nAva squinted, her mind racing. \u201cDo you think it\u2019s the rival sky-dwellers?\u201d \n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed through the air. The tower trembled beneath their feet. \u201cWe need to get down!\u201d Finn shouted. \n\nThe friends hurried down the stairs. As they reached the ground, the storm began to swirl around them. \u201cWe have to warn the village!\u201d Ava cried. \n\nBut before they could move, a shadow swooped down. A rival sky-dweller appeared, his eyes gleaming with mischief. \u201cYou think you can stop the storm? You\u2019re wasting your time!\u201d \n\nAva\u2019s heart raced. This was it\u2014the moment of truth. Should they fight back or try to reason with him? \n\n\u201cWait! We just want to save our home!\u201d Ava shouted, standing tall. \n\nThe rival smirked, but his eyes flickered with doubt. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWhat if we worked together? We can fix this!\u201d Ava pleaded. \n\nSuddenly, another crash echoed, and the rival\u2019s ship began to falter. \u201cFine!\u201d he growled. \u201cBut if you fail, it\u2019s your fault!\u201d\n\nAva and her friends shared worried glances. They had no choice. They had to save their village\u2014together.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ava and her friends see from the Sky Tower?","options":["A beautiful rainbow","A rival sky-dweller's ship","A bird flying","A giant cloud"],"correct_answer":"A rival sky-dweller's ship"},{"question":"What major decision do Ava and her friends face?","options":["To leave the village","To fight or cooperate with the rival","To climb higher","To build a new ship"],"correct_answer":"To fight or cooperate with the rival"},{"question":"How does Ava feel about the storm?","options":["Excited","Worried","Angry","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Worried"},{"question":"What does Finn suggest at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["To hide","To explore the storm","To run away","To climb the Sky Tower"],"correct_answer":"To climb the Sky Tower"},{"question":"What happens just before Ava speaks to the rival?","options":["A loud crash shakes the ground","It starts to rain","A bird lands on her shoulder","They see a treasure map"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash shakes the ground"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_328_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_328_ch3_img1.png","plot_328_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":375,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
