   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_329_11_14","title":"Echoes of the Past","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"In the year 2157, the air felt thick with the weight of forgotten stories. Jax stood on the edge of the crumbling city ruins, his heart racing as he gazed into the skeletal remains of what were once vibrant buildings. The sky above was a swirling canvas of gray and orange, a daily reminder of the great catastrophe that had altered the course of their world. \n\n\"Do you think it\u2019s safe to go down there?\" Lila asked, fidgeting with the hem of her jacket. Her dark curls bounced as she peered over Jax's shoulder, her hazel eyes wide with curiosity and concern.\n\nJax shrugged, a mischievous grin spreading across his face. \u201cWhere\u2019s your sense of adventure? Besides, what\u2019s the worst that could happen?\u201d He stepped closer to the edge, squinting at the shadows that flickered beneath the rubble. \u201cWe might find something amazing!\u201d\n\nJust then, the wind howled, sending a chill through the air. Lila wrapped her arms around herself, glancing back at the distant figures of the elders, who stood atop the hill, their gazes fixed on the two teenagers. \"I don\u2019t think they would like us wandering down there,\" she said softly, worry knitting her brows.\n\nJax rolled his eyes, unfazed. \"They\u2019re just scared of what we might find. But that\u2019s the point, Lila! If we uncover the truth about what happened, maybe we can help everyone move on.\" He took a deep breath and turned to her, his expression serious. \u201cWhat if our ancestors left us something important, something that could change everything?\u201d\n\nAs they descended into the ruins, a sense of excitement bubbled within Jax, mingling with the familiar fear of the unknown. Cracked walls loomed beside them, their surfaces covered in layers of graffiti\u2014remnants of a past that felt both distant and haunting. \n\nSuddenly, a glimmer caught Jax\u2019s eye. He skidded to a stop, pointing at a patch of ground that seemed different from the rest. \u201cLook!\u201d He knelt, brushing away dirt and debris, revealing an intricate device, half-buried but still pulsing faintly with light. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cIt looks like\u2026 a machine?\u201d Lila\u2019s voice trembled as she knelt beside him, her eyes wide with awe. \u201cBut what does it do?\u201d\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but we have to find out.\u201d Jax\u2019s fingers danced along the edges of the mysterious device, a spark of thrill igniting in his chest. As he pressed a button, the machine hummed to life, and images began to swirl around them\u2014flashes of faces, places, and emotions that felt both familiar and alien. \n\n\u201cJax! What did you do?\u201d Lila gasped, her voice barely a whisper. The images grew clearer, and Jax could see the echoes of his ancestors\u2014smiling, laughing, and then, suddenly, chaos. The screen flickered menacingly, revealing the catastrophe that had ripped their world apart.\n\nJax felt a knot tighten in his stomach. \u201cWe have to stop it!\u201d He realized this was more than just curiosity; it was a race against time. The elders feared the truth, but Jax understood. To heal the scars of the past, they needed to confront it.\n\nBefore he could react, the machine whirred louder, and the images began to pulse violently, sending Jax tumbling backward. \"No! Lila, help!\" he shouted, reaching for her hand as the ground rumbled beneath them.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe echoes of the past turned into a storm of confusion, and Jax's mind raced. This was not just about uncovering memories; it was about facing the fear that had kept their community in shackles for so long. He took a deep breath, determination flooding his veins. He had to find a way to restore hope, even if it meant standing against the elders who wanted to protect their fragile peace.\n\nAs the images faded into darkness, Jax knew that this was just the beginning. The echoes of the past were calling to him, urging him to step forward into the unknown.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What year does the story take place?","options":["2047","2157","2200","2100"],"correct_answer":"2157"},{"question":"What do Jax and Lila discover in the ruins?","options":["A treasure chest","A hidden machine","An ancient book","A portal to another world"],"correct_answer":"A hidden machine"},{"question":"What emotion does Jax feel when he discovers the machine?","options":["Fear","Excitement","Indifference","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"},{"question":"What is the main conflict Jax faces?","options":["Finding treasure","Confronting the elders","Fighting aliens","Solving a mystery"],"correct_answer":"Confronting the elders"},{"question":"Why does Lila hesitate to explore the ruins?","options":["She is tired","She is afraid of the elders","She wants to go home","She doesn't like adventure"],"correct_answer":"She is afraid of the elders"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_329_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_329_ch1_img1.png","plot_329_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":660,"reading_level":"Builder"}
