   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_330_7_10","title":"The Bright Side of Ashes","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Post-Apocalyptic","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The ash-covered land stretched endlessly before Zuri, Milo, and Ashy. Gray dust floated on the wind, swirling around their feet. Zuri took a deep breath. \u201cThis place needs our help!\u201d she exclaimed.\n\nMilo looked around, his brow furrowed. \u201cBut what if those mysterious figures return? They seemed scary.\u201d\n\n\u201cThey want to take my powers,\u201d Zuri said, determination in her voice. \u201cBut I have to learn to use them. We can\u2019t let fear stop us!\u201d\n\nJust then, Ashy bounced up and down excitedly. \u201cLet\u2019s find a spot that needs life!\u201d he cheered, his ash body glowing slightly. \n\nZuri smiled. \u201cOkay! Right over there!\u201d She pointed to a barren patch near a broken wall. The ground looked hopelessly gray. Zuri closed her eyes and imagined flowers blooming, grass growing. She reached out her hands.\n\nSuddenly, Ashy jumped in, \u201cI can help!\u201d He spun around, puffing ash into the air. The ground shook. Zuri opened her eyes. Small green sprouts peeked through the ash! \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cWow! Look at that!\u201d Milo said, his mouth open wide. But their joy was short-lived. The air grew cold as the mysterious figures appeared again, their silhouettes sharp against the ash.\n\n\u201cZuri!\u201d one of them shouted. \u201cStop what you\u2019re doing! We need your powers!\u201d \n\nZuri felt her heart race. \u201cNo! I won\u2019t let you take them!\u201d \n\nThe leader stepped forward, eyes dark as coal. \u201cYou don't understand. You are special, and we can make your power even stronger.\u201d\n\nMilo stepped in front of Zuri. \u201cShe doesn\u2019t want your help! We\u2019re bringing life back ourselves!\u201d \n\n\u201cLife? In this wasteland?\u201d the figure laughed, but it wasn't a friendly laugh. Zuri could feel the tension in the air. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s show them what we can do!\u201d Zuri shouted, her hands glowing bright.\n\n\u201cOn three!\u201d Ashy said, bouncing as he prepared to help. \n\n\u201cOne, two, three!\u201d Zuri exclaimed, and they all focused on the ground. The sprouts grew taller, flowers blooming everywhere. \n\nBut the figures were not impressed. \u201cYou think this is enough? We can take it away!\u201d \n\nZuri felt fear creeping in, but she pushed it aside. \u201cNo! We won\u2019t let you!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the ground rumbled again, but this time, it was different. A crack appeared, and the ground opened wide. Zuri gasped. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?\u201d\n\nMilo grabbed her arm. \u201cZuri, we have to decide! Do we fight, or do we run?\u201d\n\nZuri looked at the bright flowers around her, then back at Milo. \u201cI won\u2019t run! I can\u2019t let them take my powers!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cThen let\u2019s fight together!\u201d Milo said. Zuri nodded, her heart pounding, ready for whatever came next. \n\nThe mysterious figures moved closer, and Zuri clenched her fists. \n\n\u201cWhat will happen now?\u201d she wondered, a mix of fear and courage swelling inside her.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Zuri want to do with her powers?","options":["Take them away","Bring life to the land","Hide from everyone","Make her friends sad"],"correct_answer":"Bring life to the land"},{"question":"Who helps Zuri with her powers?","options":["Milo","Ashy","The figures","No one"],"correct_answer":"Ashy"},{"question":"What happens when the figures approach?","options":["They run away","They want to help Zuri","They threaten Zuri","They join Zuri"],"correct_answer":"They threaten Zuri"},{"question":"What do Zuri and her friends see as they work?","options":["A rainbow","Flowers blooming","A storm coming","A giant monster"],"correct_answer":"Flowers blooming"},{"question":"What major decision do Zuri and Milo face?","options":["To run away or fight","To go home","To eat lunch","To play games"],"correct_answer":"To run away or fight"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_330_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_330_ch3_img1.png","plot_330_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":467,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
