   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_322_11_14","title":"The Time-Traveler's Headset","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Virtual Reality","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Sofia and Max stood at the edge of a vibrant marketplace in ancient Alexandria, the air thick with the scent of exotic spices and the sound of merchants shouting their wares. Max adjusted his glasses, his eyes wide with wonder. \"I can't believe we're really here. Look at those papyrus scrolls!\" He pointed excitedly at a stall overflowing with rolled manuscripts.\n\nBefore Sofia could respond, a familiar voice called out from behind them. \"You two look lost.\" They turned to see the mischievous boy from their last adventure, his dark hair tousled and a cocky grin plastered across his face. He was holding the glimmering time gem, the very object they needed to retrieve.\n\n\"We're not lost!\" Sofia shot back, but her heart raced. This was the boy who could change history with a single misstep. \"Give us the gem, please.\" She stepped forward, her hands clenched into fists.\n\nHe laughed, a bright sound that echoed in the bustling market. \"And why would I do that? It\u2019s way too fun to tease you!\" He turned on his heel, darting through the crowd, and Sofia instinctively followed, Max right behind her.\n\nThe chase led them through a narrow alleyway filled with colorful tapestries and strange smells. Suddenly, the boy stopped, spinning around to face them. \"Catch me if you can!\" With that, he vanished behind a towering stack of crates.\n\nSofia's heart pounded in her ears. \"We have to get that gem!\" she whispered urgently to Max. They exchanged a determined glance and then sprinted after him. As they rounded the corner, they found themselves in a secluded courtyard, sunlight streaming down, illuminating a fountain adorned with intricate carvings.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\"Where did he go?\" Max panted, scanning the area. Just then, they noticed the boy, perched atop a pedestal, holding the gem high above his head. \u201cYou\u2019ll never catch me!\u201d he taunted, his eyes sparkling with mischief.\n\n\u201cStop!\u201d Sofia shouted, but the boy only laughed and leaped down, darting toward the entrance of a nearby temple. Panic surged through Sofia\u2014if he got inside, they might lose him forever. She glanced at Max, who nodded, and without thinking, they bolted after him.\n\nInside the temple, the air was cool and heavy with the scent of incense. Sunlight streamed through the high windows, illuminating the golden inscriptions on the walls. The boy was nowhere to be seen, but they could hear his laughter echoing off the stone.\n\n\"He's playing with us,\" Max muttered, frustration creeping into his voice.\n\nSofia clenched her fists, her determination solidifying. \"We can't let him take the gem. It could change everything!\" They pressed deeper into the temple, shadows dancing around them as the laughter faded into silence. Suddenly, they stumbled upon an enormous room filled with ancient artifacts, and in the center stood a colossal statue of a pharaoh.\n\nThen, without warning, the ground trembled. The statue began to shift, its stone face twisting into a snarl. \"You dare disturb my rest?\" it boomed, sending chills down their spines. \n\nMax grabbed Sofia\u2019s arm, panic in his eyes. \u201cWhat do we do? We can\u2019t fight a statue!\u201d\n\nSofia's mind raced. \"We need to find the boy! He has the gem, and he\u2019s the only one who knows how to stop this!\" They turned to leave, but the temple door slammed shut, trapping them inside.\n\n\u201cNow what?\u201d Max cried, as the statue ominously advanced.\n\nSofia took a deep breath, her heart pounding like a drum. \u201cWe have to work together. If we can reach the boy, maybe he can help us.\u201d Just as she spoke, a shadow flitted by in the corner of her eye\u2014the boy was back, a sly smile on his face.\n\n\u201cLooking for me?\u201d he taunted, holding the gem above his head again. \u201cYou\u2019ll have to catch me first!\u201d\n\nWith no choice left, Sofia yelled, \u201cWe\u2019ll do whatever it takes to stop this! Hand it over!\u201d\n\nThe boy paused, his expression shifting. \u201cYou think you can change history? What if I told you there\u2019s a price to pay?\u201d His eyes danced with mischief, revealing a deeper truth.\n\nJust then, the statue lunged, and Sofia and Max knew they had to make a split-second decision: chase after the boy or confront the growing threat before them. Time was slipping away. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cNow or never!\u201d Sofia shouted, determination shining in her eyes as she sprinted toward the boy, aware that history\u2014and perhaps their very lives\u2014hung in the balance.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does the boy do with the time gem?","options":["He gives it to Sofia","He teases them with it","He loses it","He uses it to fly"],"correct_answer":"He teases them with it"},{"question":"What is inside the temple that poses a threat to Sofia and Max?","options":["A giant snake","A colossal statue","A secret door","Ancient scrolls"],"correct_answer":"A colossal statue"},{"question":"How do Sofia and Max feel as they chase the boy?","options":["Excited and happy","Determined and scared","Bored and tired","Angry and frustrated"],"correct_answer":"Determined and scared"},{"question":"What choice do Sofia and Max face at the end of the chapter?","options":["To chase the boy or confront the statue","To leave the temple","To fight the boy","To hide"],"correct_answer":"To chase the boy or confront the statue"},{"question":"What theme is highlighted through Sofia and Max's adventure?","options":["Friendship and teamwork","Betrayal and loss","Fear and sorrow","Happiness and joy"],"correct_answer":"Friendship and teamwork"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_322_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_322_ch3_img1.png","plot_322_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":753,"reading_level":"Builder"}
