   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_316_7_10","title":"The Time-Traveling Treasure Map","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Mia was a curious girl. She loved exploring. One sunny afternoon, she climbed into her attic. Dust floated in the air, shimmering like tiny stars. As she searched through old boxes, her eyes landed on a worn-out chest. \"What\u2019s inside?\" she wondered, her heart racing.\n\nMia opened the chest. Inside, she found clothes, old toys, and a strange, crinkled map. It was yellowed with age. \"Hey, this looks like a treasure map!\" she exclaimed. She traced her finger along the lines. \u201cX marks the spot!\u201d \n\nJust then, a gust of wind blew through the attic. The map began to glow! Mia gasped. \u201cWhat is happening?\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a swirling vortex appeared. It pulled at her clothes and made her spin. \u201cNo!\u201d she shouted, but it was too late. With a whoosh, the attic vanished.\n\nMia landed on a sandy beach. The sun was bright, and palm trees swayed. She looked around, confused. \u201cWhere am I?\u201d she asked. Then, she heard laughter.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nA group of kids ran past her. They wore pirate hats and eye patches! One girl stopped and smiled. \u201cHi! I\u2019m Lily. Are you lost?\u201d \n\n\u201cI think I\u2019m in the past!\u201d Mia replied. \u201cI found a treasure map, and then\u2014\u201d \n\n\u201cPirates! We need to find them before Captain Blackbeard does!\u201d Lily exclaimed, her eyes wide with excitement. \n\n\u201cCaptain Blackbeard? Is he scary?\u201d Mia asked, her heart racing again. \n\n\u201cOnly if you get in his way,\u201d Lily replied with a giggle. \n\nJust then, a loud voice boomed, \u201cAhoy there! Who dares to steal my treasure?\u201d A tall man with a long beard appeared. He wore a black hat and had a gleaming sword. \n\nMia\u2019s heart thudded. \u201cOh no! That must be him!\u201d \n\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry! We can outsmart him!\u201d Lily assured her. \u201cFollow me!\u201d \n\nAs they sprinted away, Mia felt a mix of fear and excitement. She had jumped into a real-life adventure. Would they find the treasure before the pirate captain? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia knew one thing for sure: she had to trust her new friend if they wanted to succeed.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mia find in the attic?","options":["A treasure map","A toy","A book","A clock"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"Who does Mia meet on the beach?","options":["Captain Blackbeard","Lily","A dog","A bird"],"correct_answer":"Lily"},{"question":"What happens when Mia opens the map?","options":["It glows","It tears","It disappears","It gets wet"],"correct_answer":"It glows"},{"question":"What is Captain Blackbeard known for?","options":["Being friendly","Chasing treasure","Cooking","Sailing fast"],"correct_answer":"Chasing treasure"},{"question":"What do Mia and Lily need to do?","options":["Find the treasure","Build a ship","Go home","Make friends"],"correct_answer":"Find the treasure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_316_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_316_ch1_img1.png","plot_316_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":347,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
