   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_316_11_14","title":"The Time-Traveling Treasure Map","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the sun dipped below the horizon, painting the sky in hues of orange and purple, Mia stood at the helm of the *Sea Serpent*, the pirate ship that had quickly become her new home. The salty spray of the sea kissed her cheeks, and she felt a thrill of excitement. They were just moments away from reaching Skull Island, the fabled resting place of the treasure.\n\n\"Are you ready for this, Mia?\" Lily shouted over the wind, her eyes sparkling with determination. Mia nodded, her heart pounding. She could hardly believe that just a few days ago, she had been in her attic, lost in dreams. Now she was on an adventure that many only read about in storybooks!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe crew scurried about, preparing for the landing. Captain Blackbeard stood tall at the bow, his voice booming like thunder as he barked orders. \"Steady as she goes! We\u2019ll not let Captain Flint beat us to the prize!\" He turned to Mia, a smirk playing on his lips. \"You\u2019re a brave lass. Your heart\u2019s in the right place, I can see.\"\n\nAs they approached the island, dark clouds loomed overhead. Mia felt a shiver crawl down her spine. She had heard tales of cursed treasure, and she worried what awaited them on Skull Island. But she pushed her fears aside. \"We can do this together,\" she said to Lily, who squeezed her hand encouragingly.\n\nThe ship anchored next to a jagged shoreline, and the crew leapt onto the sandy beach. The air was thick with mystery, and a sense of adventure hung heavily around them. They followed the map, which Mia clutched tightly against her heart. Every step felt monumental, as if they were crossing into a new world.\n\nSuddenly, a rustle in the bushes sent a wave of tension through the group. \"Stay sharp!\" Blackbeard cautioned. Mia\u2019s heart raced as she scanned the thick foliage. Just then, a figure emerged\u2014Captain Flint himself, flanked by his ruthless crew.\n\n\"Well, well, what do we have here?\" Flint sneered, his eyes narrow and calculating. \"The little treasure hunters think they can outsmart me? You\u2019ll find nothing but your doom here!\"\n\nMia stepped forward, her voice steady despite her fear. \"We\u2019re not afraid of you! We\u2019ll find the treasure first!\" She could feel the weight of her words, like a challenge thrown into a stormy sea. \n\nFlint laughed, a harsh sound that echoed through the trees. \"You think you can outwit me? Let\u2019s see how brave you are when the stakes are high!\" With a swift motion, he grabbed the map from Mia\u2019s hands, tearing it in half. Panic washed over her, and she watched as her chance at treasure seemed to slip away.\n\nBut Lily sprang into action. \"Mia, follow my lead!\" she shouted, and together they charged at Flint with fierce determination. In the chaos, Mia realized something important\u2014this was more than just about treasure. It was about standing up for what she believed in, about fighting for her friends and what they had built together.\n\nAs they wrestled with Flint and his crew, Mia\u2019s heart swelled with a newfound sense of bravery. With a final push, they managed to retrieve the map, its tattered edges flapping like frightened birds. Flint staggered back, defeated, and the rival crew retreated into the shadows of the jungle.\n\nBreathless and exhilarated, Mia and Lily exchanged triumphant grins. \"We did it!\" Mia exclaimed, her heart bursting with joy. Not only had they outsmarted Flint, but they had also proven that together, they were unstoppable. \n\nAs they gathered around the map, now partially torn but still legible, Mia knew they had to hurry. Time was running out, but she felt a sense of clarity wash over her. No matter what challenges lay ahead, she had found true friends in this strange and wonderful world.\n\nWith the map in hand, they set off toward the treasure, ready to face whatever adventures awaited them.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mia discover on Skull Island?","options":["A hidden cave","A pirate ship","A treasure","A rival crew"],"correct_answer":"A treasure"},{"question":"Who does Mia confront on Skull Island?","options":["Captain Blackbeard","Captain Flint","Lily","A ghost"],"correct_answer":"Captain Flint"},{"question":"What happens to the map during the confrontation?","options":["It is stolen","It is lost","It is torn","It is burned"],"correct_answer":"It is torn"},{"question":"What lesson does Mia learn in this chapter?","options":["To be alone","The importance of friendship","To avoid pirates","To treasure gold"],"correct_answer":"The importance of friendship"},{"question":"How does Mia feel after retrieving the map?","options":["Disappointed","Exhilarated","Afraid","Confused"],"correct_answer":"Exhilarated"}]},"images":null,"word_count":670,"reading_level":"Builder"}
