   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_316_15_18","title":"The Time-Traveling Treasure Map","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Mia had always been a dreamer. At twelve, she often found herself lost in stories of great adventures\u2014treasure-hunting, pirate escapades, and ancient mysteries. Yet, on the day she stumbled upon the old, dust-covered trunk in her attic, she had no idea her life was about to become one of those stories.\n\nAs the sun filtered through the attic\u2019s cobwebbed windows, dust motes danced in the golden light. Mia pried open the trunk with a creak that echoed through the silence, revealing an assortment of forgotten belongings. A faded brown map caught her eye, its edges frayed and the intricate lines barely visible. She gently pulled it from the trunk and unfolded it, revealing a sprawling depiction of the Caribbean\u2014tiny islands, swirling currents, and an \u2018X\u2019 marked boldly in red. \n\nHer heart raced. \u201cCould this be real?\u201d she whispered to herself, tracing the lines with her finger. Just then, the atmosphere shifted, a gust of wind swirling around her as if the very air was alive with possibility.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMia could almost hear the waves crashing against a distant shore. She was gripped by an overwhelming urge to explore, to discover what lay beyond the confines of her attic. Little did she know, the map was not merely a relic of the past; it pulsated with energy, a dormant portal awaiting a spark.\n\nIn the ensuing moments, Mia felt a strange tingling sensation in her fingertips. The room blurred, colors merging into a whirlpool of vivid hues, until she could no longer hold her ground. The attic vanished, replaced by a cacophony of sound\u2014the beat of drums, the cries of seagulls, and the unmistakable roar of the ocean. She found herself standing on a weather-beaten dock, surrounded by pirate ships swaying gently in the turquoise water.\n\n\"I knew it,\" she gasped, her voice barely above a whisper. The air smelled of salt and adventure, igniting her spirit. She had arrived in the late 17th century, a time when pirates ruled the seas.\n\nMia\u2019s wide-eyed wonder was interrupted by a figure emerging from the shadows\u2014a tall, rugged man with a long beard and a mischievous glint in his eye. \u201cAhoy, lass! Ye look lost!\u201d His voice boomed, yet it held a strange warmth.\n\n\u201cI\u2026I\u2019m Mia,\u201d she stuttered, still in shock. \u201cI think I found a treasure map.\u201d\n\n\u201cTreasure, ye say?\u201d The man\u2019s eyes sparkled with intrigue. \u201cI be Captain Blackbeard, and if it\u2019s treasure ye seek, ye might want to watch yer back. Many a scallywag would kill for a glimpse of gold. So, what\u2019s the plan?\u201d\n\nMia blinked, trying to gather her thoughts. \u201cI\u2026I don\u2019t really have a plan. I just\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cJust what, lass?\u201d Blackbeard leaned in, clearly amused by her naivety. \u201cTreasure don\u2019t just fall into yer lap. Ye\u2019ll need a crew, a ship, and maybe a bit of luck.\u201d\n\nBefore she could respond, a sharp shout pierced the air. \u201cCaptain! We\u2019ve spotted a rival ship on the horizon!\u201d A young girl, no older than Mia, ran up to them, her face flushed with urgency. \u201cIt\u2019s Captain Morgan! They\u2019re after our bounty!\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s heart raced again\u2014this was not just a fantastical adventure; it was dangerous. But as she looked at the girl beside her, determination sparkled in her dark eyes. \u201cLily, we need to act fast!\u201d \n\n\u201cI\u2019m in,\u201d Mia said, her pulse quickening. \u201cLet\u2019s find that treasure before they do!\u201d\n\nWith a nod from Blackbeard, the crew sprang into action. Mia felt a sense of belonging, even amidst the chaos. She was no longer a mere spectator in her own life\u2014she was part of a story much larger than herself.\n\nAs the ship sailed forth, the horizon stretched endlessly before them, shimmering with promise. \u201cWhat awaits at the \u2018X\u2019?\u201d she pondered, not just about the treasure, but about the friendships and challenges that lay ahead. \n\nLittle did she know, the true treasure might not be gold at all, but the bonds she formed along the way.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nJust as their ship cut through the waves, a cannonball whizzed past, splashing water on the deck. \u201cBrace yourselves!\u201d Blackbeard roared, his eyes fierce with command. Mia stood frozen, torn between fear and exhilaration. This was her moment. \n\nWith her heart pounding in rhythm to the chaos around her, she gripped the map tightly, determined to find her way through this tempest of adventure.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mia find in her attic?","options":["A treasure chest","An ancient treasure map","A pirate flag","A compass"],"correct_answer":"An ancient treasure map"},{"question":"Who does Mia first meet when she arrives in the Caribbean?","options":["Lily","Captain Morgan","Blackbeard","A rival pirate"],"correct_answer":"Blackbeard"},{"question":"What is Mia's initial feeling upon discovering the treasure map?","options":["Fear","Excitement","Indifference","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"},{"question":"What urgent news does Lily bring to Blackbeard?","options":["A storm is coming","Rival pirates are nearby","The treasure is lost","They are out of supplies"],"correct_answer":"Rival pirates are nearby"},{"question":"What does Mia hope to find at the 'X' on the map?","options":["Only treasure","Friendship","Adventure and treasure","A way home"],"correct_answer":"Adventure and treasure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_316_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_316_ch1_img1.png","plot_316_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":746,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
