   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_317_7_10","title":"The Clockwork Chronicles","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The sun shone brightly over the bustling city of 3023. Oliver and his friends stood in front of the shimmering time machine. \"We need to fix this before the Time Enforcement Officer finds us!\" Oliver said, his eyes wide with worry. \n\nAva tapped her chin. \"We have the key! What\u2019s next?\" Theo, juggling a small robot, cheered, \"Let\u2019s go, team! We can do this!\" \n\nThey hurried to the time machine. The engine sputtered and whirred. \"I think we need to connect these wires!\" Oliver exclaimed, pointing at the colorful cables. \n\nAva nodded. \"I\u2019ll help! You hold that one over there.\" They worked quickly, but the sound of footsteps echoed behind them. The Time Enforcement Officer was getting closer!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, the door swung open, revealing a tall, serious man in a shiny uniform. \"You kids are coming with me!\" he barked. \n\n\"Not if we can help it!\" Theo shouted, pulling a gadget from his pocket. It was a small flying drone. \"Go, little buddy!\" He launched the drone, and it zoomed toward the officer, distracting him just long enough.\n\n\"Now!\" Oliver yelled. Ava and Theo scrambled into the time machine. They all held their breath as Oliver flipped the last switch. \n\nThe machine hummed to life! Lights flashed, and the time vortex opened. \"Hold on tight!\" shouted Oliver. But the officer was too quick. He lunged for them as the machine began to shake.\n\n\u201cQuick! Press the green button!\u201d Ava yelled, pointing to a flashing light. Oliver pressed it just in time. The machine whirred louder and began to lift off the ground. \n\nWith a bright flash, they were gone! The officer was left behind, looking shocked. \n\nThey landed safely back in their own time, just outside their school. \"We did it!\" cheered Theo, doing a silly dance. \n\nOliver smiled, feeling proud of his friends. \"We worked together!\" he said. \"Even when it was scary.\" \n\nAva grinned. \"And we learned a lot about friendship and teamwork!\" \n\nThe trio looked at each other, realizing they\u2019d grown closer through their adventure. \n\n\"Next time, let\u2019s just go to the zoo,\" suggested Theo, chuckling. \n\nOliver laughed. \"Agreed!\" They all headed back to class, excited to share their story. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Oliver and his friends need to fix?","options":["A flying car","A time machine","A robot","A spaceship"],"correct_answer":"A time machine"},{"question":"Who was chasing Oliver and his friends?","options":["A robot","Their teacher","The Time Enforcement Officer","A flying car"],"correct_answer":"The Time Enforcement Officer"},{"question":"What did Theo use to distract the Time Enforcement Officer?","options":["A balloon","A toy","A drone","A robot"],"correct_answer":"A drone"},{"question":"What did the friends learn from their adventure?","options":["How to fly","The importance of teamwork","How to build a robot","How to play games"],"correct_answer":"The importance of teamwork"},{"question":"Where did the group want to go next?","options":["Back to the future","The zoo","The mall","A park"],"correct_answer":"The zoo"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_317_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_317_ch5_img1.png","plot_317_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":371,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
