   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_318_7_10","title":"The Secret of the Starlight Tree","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: Shadows in the Forest\n\nLeo and Lily stood in front of the Starlight Tree. Its silver leaves twinkled like stars in the night sky. \u201cWow! Look at how magical it is!\u201d whispered Leo, eyes wide with wonder. \n\nLily nodded, her heart racing. \u201cWhat do you think it will show us next?\u201d \n\n\u201cMaybe more about Grandma Rose!\u201d Leo exclaimed, pulling Lily closer to the tree. \n\nAs they placed their hands on the rough bark, a soft glow surrounded them. The air sparkled and hummed with energy. Suddenly, a shadow flickered behind them. \n\n\u201cDid you see that?\u201d Lily asked, her voice trembling. \n\n\u201cI did! It was right there!\u201d Leo replied, pointing into the shadows. \n\nWith a gulp, they turned back to the tree. \u201cLet\u2019s go to Grandma Rose!\u201d Leo said, trying to sound brave. \n\nIn a flash, the world around them blurred. They felt a whoosh, and then\u2014BAM! They landed on soft grass, surrounded by bright flowers. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey looked around. \u201cWhere are we?\u201d Lily wondered. \n\n\u201cLook! There\u2019s Grandma!\u201d Leo shouted, spotting a woman with silver hair. She was sitting under a tree, telling stories to children. \n\n\u201cCome on!\u201d Lily said, and they ran toward her. \n\n\u201cGrandma Rose!\u201d they called. But as they reached her, the shadow appeared again. It twisted and turned, making funny faces. \n\n\u201cBoo!\u201d it suddenly yelled, and everyone laughed. \n\n\u201cWho are you?\u201d Grandma Rose asked, her eyes sparkling with mischief. \n\n\u201cI\u2019m Leo, and this is Lily!\u201d Leo replied, still giggling. \n\n\u201cAre you here to learn our family\u2019s secrets?\u201d Grandma asked. \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d they shouted in unison. \n\nBut just as Grandma Rose began to speak, the shadow grew darker. \u201cNot all secrets are safe,\u201d it whispered. \n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Lily asked, feeling a chill run down her spine. \n\nThe shadow swirled, and Leo stepped back. \u201cMaybe we should go back!\u201d he said, looking worried. \n\n\u201cWait!\u201d Grandma Rose said. \u201cYou must hear this. There\u2019s a secret about your family\u2014one that can change everything.\u201d \n\nThe air crackled with tension. Leo and Lily exchanged nervous glances. They wanted to hear more, but what if the secret was too scary?\n\nJust then, the shadow lunged forward, blocking their path. \u201cYou can\u2019t just leave!\u201d it shouted. \n\n\u201cWhat do we do?\u201d Lily asked, her heart racing. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find out what happens!\u201d Leo said, determination in his voice. \n\nAnd with that, they took a step closer to the shadow. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cTell us more!\u201d they shouted together, ready to face whatever came next. \n\nThe shadow paused, then laughed. \u201cVery well, brave twins. Let\u2019s see if you can handle the truth!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who do Leo and Lily want to learn more about?","options":["Their friends","Grandma Rose","The shadow","The Starlight Tree"],"correct_answer":"Grandma Rose"},{"question":"What does the shadow say when it appears?","options":["I love stories!","Boo!","Who are you?","Let\u2019s go!"],"correct_answer":"Boo!"},{"question":"What do Leo and Lily feel when the shadow appears?","options":["Excited","Angry","Worried","Tired"],"correct_answer":"Worried"},{"question":"What do Leo and Lily decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Run away","Face the shadow","Climb the tree","Call for help"],"correct_answer":"Face the shadow"},{"question":"What did Grandma Rose start to tell them?","options":["A funny story","A family secret","A riddle","A song"],"correct_answer":"A family secret"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_318_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_318_ch2_img1.png","plot_318_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":436,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
