   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_318_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Starlight Tree","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As Leo and Lily stepped back into the mystical forest, the Starlight Tree loomed majestically above them, its silvery leaves shimmering like the night sky. The air buzzed with the energy of their last adventure, but a weight settled in Leo\u2019s chest. \u201cDo you think we should go back?\u201d he asked, glancing at Lily, whose brow was furrowed in thought.\n\n\u201cWe have to,\u201d Lily replied, her voice steady but her eyes flickering with uncertainty. \u201cGrandma Rose said we need to learn more about the secret. Maybe it\u2019s connected to that village we saw.\u201d\n\nWith a deep breath, they approached the tree, its bark glistening like stars against the twilight. As they touched the cool surface, the familiar warmth enveloped them, and in an instant, they were whisked away once more. \n\nThey landed in a bustling marketplace, vibrant with colors and sounds. The scent of spices filled the air, and vendors shouted cheerfully, but underneath the joyful chaos, an unsettling tension rippled through the crowd. A large banner hung above the marketplace, reading \u201cThe Festival of Truth.\u201d \n\n\u201cLook over there!\u201d Leo pointed. A pavilion stood at the center where a group of villagers gathered, their faces serious and worried. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d\n\nLily squinted, her heart racing. \u201cWe need to find out. Let\u2019s go.\u201d As they weaved through the crowd, they overheard snippets of conversations filled with whispers and fear. \n\n\u201cHe\u2019ll never forgive us,\u201d one villager muttered. \n\n\u201cDarkness surrounds the truth,\u201d another warned, shaking their head.\n\nWhen they reached the pavilion, a tall man with a stern expression stood before the crowd, holding an ancient book. \u201cWe must confront our past, or it will consume us!\u201d he declared. The crowd gasped, and Leo felt a shiver pass through him. Could this be about their family\u2019s secret? \n\nSuddenly, a voice called out from the back\u2014an old woman with silver hair and fierce, knowing eyes. It was Grandma Rose! \u201cDo not fear the truth!\u201d she shouted, stepping forward. \u201cWe have faced worse than this.\u201d\n\nLeo's heart raced. \u201cWe need to talk to her!\u201d he urged Lily, but as they pushed through the crowd, the atmosphere shifted. The villagers turned their backs, murmuring about the family that had brought the darkness upon them. \n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed through the market. A figure dressed in dark robes burst into the pavilion, brandishing a staff that crackled with energy. \u201cYou cannot hide from the truth!\u201d the figure bellowed, eyes glowing with anger. The crowd gasped, some people backing away in fear.\n\n\u201cWe have to help Grandma Rose!\u201d Leo shouted, adrenaline surging through him. But as he stepped forward, a memory flashed in his mind\u2014his grandmother telling stories of a betrayal that had torn their family apart. \n\n\u201cLeo, we can\u2019t!\u201d Lily grabbed his arm, terror in her eyes. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s too dangerous?\u201d\n\nBefore Leo could respond, the robed figure pointed their staff at Grandma Rose, and a bolt of energy shot forth. Time seemed to slow as Leo\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWe have to do something!\u201d \n\nJust as they were about to act, Grandma Rose raised her hand, and a shield of light enveloped her. \u201cThis isn\u2019t what it looks like!\u201d she called out, her voice steady, but Leo could see the fear in her eyes. \n\n\u201cDo you trust me?\u201d she asked, looking at Leo and Lily, her gaze piercing and full of wisdom. \n\nThe twins exchanged a glance, knowing this moment could change everything. \u201cYes!\u201d they chorused, but uncertainty gnawed at them. What if trusting her meant facing their family\u2019s darkest secret head-on? \n\nThe robed figure lowered their staff, eyes narrowing. \u201cYou think you can stop what\u2019s coming? The truth will unravel everything!\u201d\n\nAs the crowd watched in silence, the tension in the air thickened like fog. The choice was theirs: confront the truth, or run away from it forever.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nIn that pivotal moment, Leo felt a surge of determination. \u201cWe can\u2019t run from our past!\u201d he shouted, stepping onto the pavilion, ready to face whatever came next.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut just as he spoke, a crack of lightning struck nearby, making everyone jump. The pavilion trembled, and Leo felt the ground beneath him shift. Were they truly ready for the journey ahead? \n\n\u201cWhat will you choose?\u201d Grandma Rose asked, her voice echoing like a distant storm.\n\nAnd with that, the chapter ended, leaving an air of suspense and uncertainty hanging in the space between brave hearts and dark secrets.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the main event happening in the marketplace?","options":["A festival","A wedding","A circus","A battle"],"correct_answer":"A festival"},{"question":"Who is the figure that interrupts the festival?","options":["Grandma Rose","A villager","A mysterious figure","Leo"],"correct_answer":"A mysterious figure"},{"question":"What does Grandma Rose use to protect herself?","options":["A shield of light","A sword","Words of wisdom","A spell"],"correct_answer":"A shield of light"},{"question":"What do Leo and Lily decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Run away","Confront the truth","Hide","Leave the village"],"correct_answer":"Confront the truth"},{"question":"What is the main feeling in the marketplace during the festival?","options":["Joyful","Tense","Calm","Excited"],"correct_answer":"Tense"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_318_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_318_ch3_img1.png","plot_318_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":753,"reading_level":"Builder"}
