   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_319_11_14","title":"Robo-Rewind: Adventures in Time","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Sam's head swirled with excitement as he approached the entrance of Maplewood Middle School. The morning sun streamed through the trees, casting playful shadows on the sidewalk. Last night, after discovering Sparky\u2019s unique ability to rewind time, Sam had hardly slept a wink. The thought of all the possibilities made his heart race faster than a race car. Would today be the day he saved his lunch from the cafeteria\u2019s mystery meat?\n\nSparky rolled alongside him, humming a tune that sounded suspiciously like a pop song from the '80s. \u201cI\u2019m ready to assist you, Sam! Will we be rewinding time today?\u201d Sparky\u2019s eyes flickered with encouragement, their soft glow matching Sam\u2019s eager expression.\n\n\u201cDefinitely. But, Sparky, let\u2019s keep it to small stuff today. We don\u2019t want to create a time tornado or anything!\u201d Sam chuckled, though a hint of worry crept into his voice. After all, the last time he rewound, he accidentally joined the wrong gym class and had to endure a dance-off against the seventh graders.\n\nAs they entered the bustling hallway, the usual school chaos was in full swing. Lockers slammed, friends laughed, and the smell of burnt toast wafted in from the cafeteria. Mia spotted Sam from across the hall and waved, her freckled face lighting up like a neon sign. \u201cHey, Sam! You won\u2019t believe what happened in history class!\u201d\n\n\u201cWait, let me guess! Tim forgot his lines again, and Mrs. O\u2019Malley lost it?\u201d Sam replied, smiling. He could always count on Mia for some entertaining gossip.\n\n\u201cClose! But this time, she accidentally spilled coffee all over her notes. It was a total disaster!\u201d Mia exclaimed, a dramatic flair in her voice. \u201cI think she needs Sparky in her classroom.\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe,\u201d Sam said thoughtfully. \u201cBut I\u2019m trying to focus on smaller changes. I don\u2019t want to risk anything too big just yet.\u201d He glanced at Sparky, who was now vibrating with anticipation.\n\nThe bell rang, and they hurried to their first class. The day unfolded with its usual mix of boredom and excitement. Sam felt a jolt of anxiety when he recalled the upcoming science fair. The class project was due next week, and he had a brilliant idea involving Sparky and a miniature garden powered by solar energy. However, his classmates\u2019 projects were impressive, and Sam was worried his idea wouldn\u2019t stand out.\n\nDuring lunch, Sam\u2019s worries deepened. Seated with Mia at their usual table, he watched as the \u201ccool kids\u201d unveiled their grand plans for the science fair. \u201cWhat if I mess it up?\u201d he muttered, barely touching his food.\n\n\u201cSam, you\u2019ve got this! Just remember, it\u2019s about having fun, not just winning,\u201d Mia reassured him, her voice softening as she nudged his arm.\n\nSuddenly, the cafeteria erupted into chaos. A tray full of spaghetti slipped from a student\u2019s hands, sending noodles flying like confetti. Laughter mixed with shouts as the cafeteria staff scrambled to clean up the mess. Sam\u2019s heart sank. This was the moment he could use Sparky\u2019s power\u2014if only he could rewind ten minutes and warn the student to hold on tight.\n\n\u201cShould we?\u201d Mia asked, her eyebrows raised.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s do it,\u201d Sam decided, scrambling to his feet. \u201cI could save a lunch disaster and practice a little time travel!\u201d\n\nHe quickly pressed the button on Sparky\u2019s chest. \u201cRewind!\u201d The world blurred in a whirl of colors, and the cafeteria noise faded into a soft whoosh. When everything came back into focus, it was as if time had reset. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nNow, Sam stood just a few minutes before the impending mess. He rushed towards the table where the student was balancing the tray. \u201cHey! You might want to hold on tight!\u201d he shouted, just as the tray began to wobble.\n\nAs the student blinked in surprise, Sam felt a rush of triumph\u2014but the moment was short-lived. The tray tipped, and spaghetti still flew, but now it splattered directly onto the principal, Mr. Thompson, who had just entered the cafeteria. The room fell silent, and all eyes turned to the scene unfolding before them.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cOh no! This wasn\u2019t supposed to happen!\u201d Sam exclaimed, panic rising in his throat. He glanced at Mia, whose jaw had dropped in disbelief. The principal\u2019s furious expression sent a shiver down Sam\u2019s spine. He realized that his small attempt to fix an ordinary mistake had turned into an extraordinary disaster.\n\nNow, with spaghetti-sauce-covered shoes and the whole school watching, Sam had to figure out how to manage this new challenge without causing further chaos. Could he rewind time again, or was this mess now part of his story?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Sam struggle with regarding the science fair?","options":["He has no idea what to do","He feels his project won\u2019t stand out","He forgot about it","He doesn't want to participate"],"correct_answer":"He feels his project won\u2019t stand out"},{"question":"What event does Sam try to prevent during lunch?","options":["A food fight","Spaghetti spilling","A fire drill","A science experiment gone wrong"],"correct_answer":"Spaghetti spilling"},{"question":"How does Sam feel about using Sparky's ability?","options":["Excited","Nervous","Indifferent","Confused"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What does Mia think about the science fair?","options":["It's stupid","It's all about winning","It's about having fun","It's too difficult"],"correct_answer":"It's about having fun"},{"question":"What unexpected result occurs after Sam rewinds time?","options":["He wins the science fair","The principal gets covered in spaghetti","They get extra lunch","He meets a new friend"],"correct_answer":"The principal gets covered in spaghetti"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_319_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_319_ch2_img1.png","plot_319_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":791,"reading_level":"Builder"}
