   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_319_11_14","title":"Robo-Rewind: Adventures in Time","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the sun rose over Willow Creek, Sam felt a mix of excitement and dread. The school science fair was just hours away, and he could still picture the disaster of spaghetti sauce splattering on Principal Thompson\u2019s suit the day before. Sam had thought he could fix everything with Sparky, but the robot\u2019s quirky personality and the chaos that followed left him feeling more confused than ever. \n\n\u201cOkay, Sparky,\u201d Sam said, peering into the garage where the robot stood, a jumble of wires and blinking lights. \u201cWe have to figure this out. No more mistakes today!\u201d \n\nSparky tilted his head, its eyes flashing a bright blue as if it were pondering the situation. \u201cRewind?\u201d it chirped, as if eager to help but unaware of the weight of the moment. Sam nodded. He needed to prevent another embarrassing incident, especially with Mia counting on him.\n\n\u201cMia will be at the fair,\u201d Sam said, a knot tightening in his stomach. \u201cIf I mess this up, I\u2019ll never hear the end of it.\u201d \n\nWith Sparky by his side, they headed to school, the robot\u2019s metallic footsteps echoing behind him. The school loomed ahead, its brick walls and large windows reflecting the morning light. Vibrant posters announcing the science fair decorated the entrance, but Sam felt a chill run down his spine as he recalled the mishap from the previous day.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nInside, the gym buzzed with energy. Students were setting up their projects, and the air was thick with the scent of glue and excitement. Mia waved from her table, her project\u2014a model of the solar system\u2014sparkling under the fluorescent lights. \u201cHey, Sam! Ready for this?\u201d \n\nHe forced a smile. \u201cTotally ready! Just... checking on Sparky.\u201d \n\nAs he glanced at the robot, a flash of inspiration struck him. \u201cWhat if I rewind just a bit? Maybe there\u2019s something I can fix before it happens.\u201d He felt the familiar thrill of possibility coursing through him. \n\n\u201cTen minutes! Ten minutes!\u201d Sparky beeped with enthusiasm, unaware of the stakes. \n\nJust then, he spotted Kyle, the school bully, lurking by the snack table. His presence made Sam\u2019s stomach churn. Kyle was known for causing trouble, and Sam knew he had to act fast. With a quick glance at Mia, who was busy arranging her planets, he whispered to Sparky, \u201cLet\u2019s do this.\u201d\n\nUsing the small button on Sparky's side, he pressed it firmly. A whirl of colors and sounds enveloped him, the gym fading away for a heartbeat. When everything snapped back into focus, he found himself back at the lunch table moments before the chaos began. \n\n\u201cPerfect!\u201d he thought, spotting Kyle reaching for the last cookie. With a swift motion, he snatched it first. \u201cSorry, Kyle! Better luck next time!\u201d \n\nBut as he turned around, the unexpected happened. A tray of science fair cupcakes, stacked high and precariously balanced, tipped over. The colorful frosting flew into the air like a rainbow explosion, landing squarely on Principal Thompson\u2019s head. The gym fell silent, eyes wide with shock.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nSam\u2019s heart raced. \u201cOh no! This is worse!\u201d he exclaimed, panic rising in his throat. Sparky\u2019s sensors went haywire, beeping wildly as it processed the new catastrophe. \n\nMia\u2019s eyes widened in disbelief. \u201cWhat did you do, Sam?\u201d she gasped, trying to stifle a laugh but failing miserably. \n\n\u201cI thought I could fix it!\u201d Sam yelled back, desperation creeping into his voice. \u201cNow we need to do something\u2026 but what?\u201d \n\nIn that moment, he realized that even with the power to rewind time, the consequences of his actions were far more complicated than he had imagined. Sam had to figure out how to make things right, and fast, before the whole science fair turned into a disaster. \n\n\u201cTime to think,\u201d he muttered, looking at Sparky, whose eyes glinted with mischief. \u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d\n\nAnd as the evening sun colored the sky, Sam knew he was at a critical juncture. He had to decide whether to rewind again or confront the fallout of his choices\u2014his heart racing with the weight of the moment.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event is Sam preparing for in this chapter?","options":["A birthday party","The science fair","A school play","A sports competition"],"correct_answer":"The science fair"},{"question":"What does Sam accidentally cause to happen at the science fair?","options":["He breaks a project","He covers Principal Thompson with cupcakes","He spills juice everywhere","He loses his project"],"correct_answer":"He covers Principal Thompson with cupcakes"},{"question":"How does Sam feel about using Sparky's power?","options":["Excited but nervous","Disappointed","Indifferent","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Excited but nervous"},{"question":"What does Mia's project represent?","options":["The ocean","The solar system","A city","The human body"],"correct_answer":"The solar system"},{"question":"What critical decision does Sam face at the end of the chapter?","options":["To go home","To rewind time again or confront the consequences","To call his mom","To ignore the mess"],"correct_answer":"To rewind time again or confront the consequences"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_319_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_319_ch3_img1.png","plot_319_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":690,"reading_level":"Builder"}
