   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_320_7_10","title":"A Journey Through Time: The Quest to Save Dinosaurs","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: Trouble in the Jungle\n\nThe air was warm and filled with chirping insects. Ella, Jake, and Dr. Finch stood in a lush green jungle. Towering trees reached high into the sky. Bright flowers in shades of orange and pink bloomed everywhere. \u201cWow! This place is amazing!\u201d Ella exclaimed, her eyes wide with wonder. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, they heard a soft whimpering sound. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Jake asked, looking around. They followed the sound, stepping carefully between the large ferns. As they walked, they spotted a tiny dinosaur hiding behind a bush. It was a baby Triceratops!\n\n\u201cIt looks scared,\u201d Dr. Finch said, crouching down. \u201cWe need to help it!\u201d Ella nodded. \u201cBut we have to be careful! The poacher might be nearby.\u201d \n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed through the jungle. Branches snapped and leaves rustled. \u201cOh no, the poacher!\u201d Jake whispered. \u201cWe have to hide!\u201d They ducked behind a large rock. \n\nPeeking out, they saw a man in a dark coat. He had a net and a big cage. \u201cI\u2019m going to catch that little dinosaur!\u201d he growled. The kids gasped. Ella clenched her fists. \u201cWe can\u2019t let that happen!\u201d \n\nDr. Finch looked around. \u201cWe need a plan. We can distract him and help the baby dinosaur escape.\u201d Jake nodded. \u201cI can create a noise to draw his attention.\u201d \n\n\u201cGreat idea!\u201d Ella said. \u201cAnd I\u2019ll try to calm the baby Triceratops.\u201d They all agreed and quickly got into position. \n\nJake took a deep breath and shouted, \u201cHey, you! Over here!\u201d The poacher turned around, startled. \u201cWhat? Who\u2019s there?\u201d He moved closer to Jake. \n\nMeanwhile, Ella softly spoke to the baby dinosaur. \u201cIt\u2019s okay, little one. We\u2019re here to help you.\u201d The baby Triceratops blinked at her with big, trusting eyes. \n\nJust then, Dr. Finch noticed the poacher was getting too close. \u201cHurry! We need to move!\u201d He waved his arms, trying to keep the poacher distracted. \n\nSuddenly, the baby dinosaur let out a loud honk! The poacher jumped back in surprise. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d he shouted. \n\n\u201cNow, Jake!\u201d Ella yelled. Jake threw a rock away from them. The sound echoed through the trees. The poacher ran towards the noise. \u201cI\u2019ll catch you, little dinosaur!\u201d \n\nThe kids took this chance to help the baby Triceratops. But as they turned to escape, they heard something even louder\u2014a rumble! \n\n\u201cOh no! Is that a volcano?\u201d Jake pointed to the smoky mountain in the distance. Dr. Finch squinted. \u201cWe need to get to safety, fast!\u201d \n\nThey quickly gathered the baby dinosaur and ran deeper into the jungle, their hearts pounding. The adventure was getting more dangerous!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cDo you think we can outrun the poacher?\u201d Ella panted. \n\n\u201cI hope so!\u201d Jake replied. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s stick together,\u201d Dr. Finch said. \u201cWe can do this!\u201d \n\nAs they dashed through the thick jungle, they could hear the poacher yelling behind them. They were in trouble! \n\nBut the baby Triceratops kept up with them, its tiny legs moving fast. They had to find a way to protect it and escape the poacher. What would they do next?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do the kids find hiding in the jungle?","options":["A baby elephant","A baby Triceratops","A baby lion","A baby turtle"],"correct_answer":"A baby Triceratops"},{"question":"What does the poacher want to do?","options":["Help the dinosaurs","Catch the dinosaurs","Build a house","Make friends"],"correct_answer":"Catch the dinosaurs"},{"question":"What does Jake throw to distract the poacher?","options":["A rock","A stick","A toy","A ball"],"correct_answer":"A rock"},{"question":"What natural disaster do the kids hear?","options":["A thunderstorm","A tidal wave","A volcano rumble","An earthquake"],"correct_answer":"A volcano rumble"},{"question":"What is Dr. Finch's role in the story?","options":["To be the poacher","To guide the kids","To find treasure","To sleep"],"correct_answer":"To guide the kids"}]},"images":null,"word_count":520,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
