   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_320_7_10","title":"A Journey Through Time: The Quest to Save Dinosaurs","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The air was thick with excitement. Ella, Jake, and Dr. Finch stood in the lush green valley filled with ferns and tall trees. They could hear the distant calls of dinosaurs echoing in the air.\n\n\u201cLook at Tilly! She\u2019s playing by that stream!\u201d Ella shouted, pointing to the little Triceratops splashing in the water. Tilly was having the best time, her tiny horns glinting in the sun. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nJust then, a shadow fell over them. The kids turned to see the poacher sneaking through the trees. His eyes were locked on Tilly.\n\n\u201cWe need to protect her!\u201d Jake said urgently. \u201cWhat if he tries to capture her?\u201d\n\nDr. Finch scratched his head. \u201cWe need a plan. He must not get Tilly!\u201d\n\nElla had an idea. \u201cWhat if we lead him away? We can use the volcano as a distraction!\u201d\n\n\u201cGreat thinking, Ella!\u201d Jake replied. \u201cLet\u2019s move quickly.\u201d\n\nThe kids raced towards the volcano, the ground shaking beneath their feet. Tilly followed them, her little legs moving fast. \n\n\u201cThis way, Tilly!\u201d Ella called. The baby dinosaur chirped happily, unaware of the danger.\n\nAs they reached the volcano, they saw the poacher sneaking closer. \u201cHurry!\u201d shouted Dr. Finch. \u201cWe have to distract him now!\u201d\n\nJake grabbed a handful of rocks. \u201cI\u2019ll make a loud noise!\u201d He threw the rocks down the slope. They clattered and rolled, echoing like thunder.\n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d the poacher exclaimed, looking around in confusion. \n\n\u201cNow\u2019s our chance!\u201d Ella shouted. Together, they waved their arms. \u201cOver here! This way!\u201d\n\nThe poacher turned, running toward the noise. Tilly began to follow, but Ella quickly scooped her up. \u201cNot yet, Tilly! Stay with us!\u201d\n\nJust then, they heard a loud roar. The ground shook again. The volcano was waking up! \n\n\u201cOh no, we need to go! Now!\u201d Dr. Finch yelled. The kids ran as fast as they could, Tilly nestled safely in Ella\u2019s arms.\n\nThe roaring grew louder. Suddenly, a huge cloud of smoke billowed out of the volcano. The poacher was far behind, trapped by the noise and confusion. \n\nThe kids dashed to safety, breathless but smiling. \u201cWe did it!\u201d Jake cheered. \u201cWe saved Tilly!\u201d\n\n\u201cYes, and we learned how to work together!\u201d Ella added proudly.\n\nAs they caught their breath, Dr. Finch said, \u201cIt\u2019s important to protect these creatures. They belong here.\u201d\n\nThe adventure wasn\u2019t over just yet. They still needed to find a way home. But for now, they were happy. They had saved Tilly, and they had each other.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go find that time capsule!\u201d Ella said, determination in her eyes.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Ella suggest to protect Tilly?","options":["Hide Tilly","Lead the poacher away","Run away","Climb a tree"],"correct_answer":"Lead the poacher away"},{"question":"What did Jake throw to make a loud noise?","options":["Sticks","Rocks","Mushrooms","Leaves"],"correct_answer":"Rocks"},{"question":"What did the kids learn from their adventure?","options":["How to run fast","How to catch dinosaurs","The importance of teamwork","How to climb trees"],"correct_answer":"The importance of teamwork"},{"question":"Why did the ground shake during their adventure?","options":["A big dinosaur was walking","The volcano was waking up","A storm was coming","They were jumping"],"correct_answer":"The volcano was waking up"},{"question":"What did Dr. Finch say about protecting dinosaurs?","options":["They belong in zoos","It\u2019s important to protect them","They are scary","They are not real"],"correct_answer":"It\u2019s important to protect them"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_320_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_320_ch5_img1.png","plot_320_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":436,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
