   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_320_11_14","title":"A Journey Through Time: The Quest to Save Dinosaurs","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the sun rose over the colossal ferns and towering cycads of the Late Cretaceous period, Ella and Jake stood, breathless and wide-eyed at the sight before them. The lush landscape stretched endlessly, dotted with volcanic mountains that loomed like ancient giants. \"This is incredible!\" Ella exclaimed, her excitement bubbling over. She felt as if she had stepped into one of her favorite dinosaur books, where every page came to life.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, a rustling noise interrupted their wonder. From behind a giant tree, the baby dinosaur peeked out, its big, curious eyes shimmering like pools of water. \"There it is!\" Jake whispered, looking at Ella with urgency. They rushed towards the little creature, who seemed to be caught between fear and curiosity. Just as they reached it, a shadow fell over them, darkening their joy. \n\nElla turned slowly to see a figure approaching\u2014a tall man with a rugged demeanor, wearing a wide-brimmed hat and a sinister grin. The poacher. \"Well, what do we have here?\" he said, his voice smooth like oil. \"Two little scientists playing with their toys.\" \n\nJake clenched his fists, and Ella\u2019s heart raced. \"We\u2019re not here to play!\" she snapped, stepping protectively in front of the baby dinosaur. \"We need to get it back to its mother!\" \n\nThe poacher chuckled, pulling out a net from behind his back. \"And I need a pet dinosaur for my collection. You\u2019re in my way.\" \n\nPanic surged through Ella. She glanced at Jake, who was scanning their surroundings. \"We have to distract him,\" he whispered urgently. Drawing on their quick thinking, Ella pointed towards the foot of the volcano. \"Look! Is that a T-Rex?\"\n\nThe poacher's eyes bulged with greed and curiosity as he swung around, momentarily abandoning his trap. \"A T-Rex? Here?\" \n\nThis was their chance. \"Run!\" Jake shouted, grabbing Ella's hand. They dashed away, the baby dinosaur scampering after them, its small feet thumping against the soft earth. But the poacher was not far behind, his angry shouts echoing through the valley.\n\nAs they reached a grove of trees, Ella led them into the thick underbrush, hoping to lose him. \"What do we do now?\" she panted, her heart racing like a drum.\n\n\"We need to find a place to hide,\" Jake replied, but just then, they heard a loud roar. The ground shook beneath their feet, and they froze in terror. \n\nOut from behind the trees charged a massive Tyrannosaurus rex, its eyes fierce and hungry. The poacher, now distracted by the greater threat, stumbled backward. \"Oh no!\" he yelled, turning to flee. \n\nStill panting, Ella and Jake watched as the enormous dinosaur lumbered past them, its nostrils flaring and teeth bared. They both knew they had to act fast. \"We can use this to our advantage!\" Jake exclaimed, his mind racing with ideas.\n\nBut as they turned to escape deeper into the forest, Ella realized something important. \"Wait! We can't just run. We need to protect the baby dinosaur, too! We can't let the poacher get to it!\" \n\nJake nodded, determination glinting in his eyes. \"Then we\u2019ll outsmart him together. But we need to think of a plan\u2014fast!\"\n\nWith the roar of the T-Rex still rumbling in the background, they huddled together, committed to their mission. The stakes had never been higher. Would they be able to save the baby dinosaur and find a way back home?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ella want to do with the baby dinosaur?","options":["Play with it","Take it home","Get it back to its mother","Capture it"],"correct_answer":"Get it back to its mother"},{"question":"Who is the main antagonist in this chapter?","options":["Dr. Finch","The baby dinosaur","The poacher","A T-Rex"],"correct_answer":"The poacher"},{"question":"What tactic do Ella and Jake use to distract the poacher?","options":["They run away","They pretend to be dinosaurs","They shout for help","They point to a T-Rex"],"correct_answer":"They point to a T-Rex"},{"question":"What emotions do Ella and Jake experience during the confrontation with the poacher?","options":["Excitement and joy","Fear and determination","Anger and frustration","Boredom and indifference"],"correct_answer":"Fear and determination"},{"question":"What do Ella and Jake realize they need to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Run away from the dinosaurs","Find a way back home","Come up with a plan to save the baby dinosaur","Make friends with the poacher"],"correct_answer":"Come up with a plan to save the baby dinosaur"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_320_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_320_ch3_img1.png","plot_320_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":569,"reading_level":"Builder"}
