   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_320_11_14","title":"A Journey Through Time: The Quest to Save Dinosaurs","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As Ella and Jake cautiously navigated the lush undergrowth of the Late Cretaceous landscape, the air buzzed with the sounds of prehistoric life. Towering trees with thick, scaly trunks loomed overhead, their leaves rustling like a thousand tiny whispers. The sun filtered through the canopy, casting dappled shadows on the ground, while the earthy scent of damp soil filled their nostrils. \n\n\"We need to find a safe place for the baby dinosaur,\" Ella said, her eyes scanning the horizon for any sign of danger. She felt a surge of determination coursing through her. They had yet to see the poacher again, but the looming threat was like a shadow hanging over their heads.\n\nJake nodded, his brow furrowed in concentration. \"Maybe we can find somewhere near that river. It's secluded and hidden by those bushes.\" He pointed to a glint of water peeking through a cluster of ferns.\n\nAs they made their way toward the river, the ground trembled beneath their feet. Suddenly, a massive T-Rex burst into view, its massive jaws snapping dangerously close to where they stood. The creature was as fearsome as Ella had always imagined, with dark green scales and piercing eyes that seemed to glow with primal intelligence. \n\nThe kids froze, adrenaline coursing through their veins. \"What do we do?\" Jake whispered, panic creeping into his voice.\n\n\"Stay quiet! Maybe it won't see us,\" Ella whispered back, her heart pounding like a drum. They crouched behind a large fern, hoping the T-Rex wouldn\u2019t catch their scent.\n\nThe dinosaur sniffed the air, its nostrils flaring, and then continued its lumbering walk, oblivious to the two young scientists. Ella let out a breath she didn\u2019t realize she was holding. \"That was too close,\" she said, shaking slightly.\n\nAs they approached the river, they spotted the baby dinosaur nestled among the rocks, its small body trembling. Ella knelt beside it, gently stroking its rough skin. \"It's okay, little one. We're here to help.\"\n\nJake looked around nervously. \"But we still have to deal with that poacher. He\u2019s not going to just give up.\"\n\nSuddenly, a rustling sound caught their attention. A figure emerged from the trees, silhouetted against the sunlight. It was the poacher, his eyes gleaming with greed as he spotted the baby dinosaur. \"Ah-ha! There you are! Hand it over!\" he shouted, his voice slicing through the air like a knife.\n\nElla felt a surge of courage rise within her. \"No! You can't take him!\" she yelled, standing protectively in front of the baby dinosaur.\n\nThe poacher's smile widened, revealing crooked teeth. \"You think you can stop me? You\u2019re just kids!\" \n\nJust then, the ground shook again, but this time it was different. A distant roar echoed through the valley, more powerful than before. The poacher's expression turned to fear as he glanced in the direction of the sound. \n\nBefore anyone could move, the T-Rex re-emerged, drawn by the commotion. It charged toward the poacher, who stumbled back in shock. Ella grabbed Jake's arm. \"We need to get out of here! Now!\" \n\nAs they dashed away from the scene, Ella\u2019s heart raced with a mixture of fear and exhilaration. They had come closer to danger than ever before, but they had also taken a stand. \n\n\"Do you think we can outrun it?\" Jake asked, glancing back at the chaos that was unfolding.\n\n\"I don\u2019t know, but we have to try!\" Ella replied, determination igniting her spirit. Together, they dashed deeper into the underbrush, thoughts racing as fast as their feet.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[As they navigate through the lush landscape, Ella and Jake are seen exploring the vibrant world of dinosaurs around them. Towering trees surround them, with colorful foliage and hints of mysterious prehistoric creatures peeking from behind the foliage. Ella, with a determined look on her face, is kneeling beside a small, frightened baby dinosaur.]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n[The moment is tense as the poacher stands menacingly in front of the baby dinosaur, his greedy eyes fixed on it. In the background, the T-Rex looms larger than life, roaring and charging towards the poacher, creating an atmosphere of suspense and action. Ella and Jake are in the foreground, their expressions filled with fear yet resolute as they prepare to defend the baby dinosaur.]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ella want to do for the baby dinosaur?","options":["Capture it","Help it","Hide from it","Ignore it"],"correct_answer":"Help it"},{"question":"What animal do Ella and Jake encounter that poses a threat?","options":["A Triceratops","A Velociraptor","A T-Rex","A Pterodactyl"],"correct_answer":"A T-Rex"},{"question":"How does the poacher react when he sees the baby dinosaur?","options":["He runs away","He tries to capture it","He ignores it","He helps it"],"correct_answer":"He tries to capture it"},{"question":"What sound signals the arrival of the T-Rex?","options":["A loud bang","A distant roar","A soft rustling","A whisper"],"correct_answer":"A distant roar"},{"question":"What do Ella and Jake decide to do when they see the poacher?","options":["Run away","Fight him","Help him","Scream for help"],"correct_answer":"Run away"}]},"images":null,"word_count":713,"reading_level":"Builder"}
