   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_320_15_18","title":"A Journey Through Time: The Quest to Save Dinosaurs","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Time Travel","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The laboratory was unlike anything Ella had ever seen. Mysterious machines whirred softly, casting an ethereal glow across the sleek, metallic surfaces. Neon lights pulsed rhythmically, illuminating the massive, curved walls adorned with holographic projections of dinosaurs in their natural habitats. It was a sanctuary for knowledge, a glimpse into the future of science. Today, however, it buzzed with a different kind of energy, a sense of adventure that electrified the air.\n\n\u201cElla! Over here!\u201d Jake called, his voice echoing against the walls as he waved her over to a peculiar contraption nestled in a corner. It resembled a shiny, oversized egg, intricately patterned with swirling designs. He leaned closer, his curiosity radiating from him like heat from a sun.\n\n\u201cDo you think it\u2019s some sort of time machine?\u201d Ella mused, her pulse quickening at the thought. Her mind raced with images of dinosaurs roaming free, their massive forms silhouetted against the sun. What if they could travel back and see the world as it once was?\n\nBefore she could voice her excitement, Dr. Finch, their mentor and a well-known paleontologist with an unruly mop of gray hair, shuffled toward them. His eyes twinkled with mischief. \u201cAh, the Temporal Capsule! I see you\u2019ve found my little secret. But it\u2019s not just a time machine, it\u2019s also a test! Are you brave enough to activate it?\u201d\n\nJake\u2019s face lit up. \u201cWhat do we have to do?\u201d\n\n\u201cJust a simple sequence,\u201d Dr. Finch replied, a hint of challenge in his tone. \u201cBut be careful! Time is a fragile thing. We could end up anywhere\u2014or anywhen.\u201d\n\nElla exchanged a nervous glance with Jake. The thrill of potential adventure sparked within her, but a flicker of apprehension lingered. \u201cWhat if we can\u2019t get back?\u201d\n\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry,\u201d Dr. Finch assured, though she could hear the underlying uncertainty in his voice. \u201cWe\u2019ll be fine.\u201d\n\nWith her heart pounding, Ella took a deep breath and stepped forward. The moment her fingers grazed the cool surface of the capsule, a shiver ran down her spine. The lights dimmed, and the chamber filled with a low hum, vibrating beneath her feet. Suddenly, a bright flash engulfed them, and the world twisted into a blur.\n\nWhen the light faded, they found themselves standing in a lush, vibrant landscape. Towering trees reached toward the sky, their leaves rustling in a warm breeze that smelled of earth and life. In the distance, the unmistakable roar of a dinosaur echoed through the valley.\n\n\u201cWhere are we?\u201d Jake whispered, his eyes wide with wonder.\n\n\u201cThe Late Cretaceous period,\u201d Dr. Finch replied, his voice barely above a breath. \u201cWe\u2019ve traveled back in time!\u201d\n\nBefore they could fully comprehend their extraordinary circumstances, a rustle in the bushes caught their attention. They turned just in time to see a small, hatchling dinosaur stumble into the clearing. Its fragile frame was covered in soft, scaly skin, and its innocent eyes blinked up at them, filled with trust and curiosity.\n\n\u201cLook at it!\u201d Ella exclaimed, rushing forward. \u201cIt\u2019s adorable!\u201d\n\nBut just as she reached out a hand, a shadow loomed behind the trees. A tall figure, clad in dark clothing and a wide-brimmed hat, emerged, eyes glinting with intent. \u201cWell, well, what do we have here?\u201d he sneered, a grin that sent chills down Ella\u2019s spine. \u201cLooks like a treasure trove of history just waiting to be claimed.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat do you want?\u201d Jake demanded, stepping protectively in front of Ella and the baby dinosaur.\n\n\u201cEasy, kid. Just a little business opportunity,\u201d the poacher replied, his voice smooth like silk but cold as ice. \u201cDinosaurs like this one are worth a fortune. All I need is a little help\u2026 from you.\u201d\n\nRealizing they were out of their depth, Ella felt a wave of fear wash over her. They had to protect the baby dinosaur, but how could they outsmart a poacher who seemed to know more about their situation than they did?\n\nAs the poacher advanced, Ella took a deep breath, determination flooding her veins. \u201cWe won\u2019t let you take it!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe tension hung thick in the air, and she wondered if their adventure had already taken a turn for the worse. The lush beauty of their surroundings felt incongruous with the looming threat before them.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s get out of here!\u201d Jake shouted, grabbing Ella\u2019s wrist. They needed to find a way to escape and protect the little creature. There was no way they could let history\u2014and this innocent life\u2014be altered by greed.\n\nWith one last glance at the poacher, they turned to run, the sound of their heartbeats echoing in their ears as they plunged into the dense foliage of the prehistoric jungle, the roar of the past echoing behind them.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What activates the time capsule in the laboratory?","options":["A secret sequence","A special key","A voice command","A hidden button"],"correct_answer":"A secret sequence"},{"question":"What is the initial reaction of Ella and Jake upon arriving in the Cretaceous period?","options":["They are frightened","They are excited","They are confused","They are indifferent"],"correct_answer":"They are excited"},{"question":"What does the poacher want to do with the baby dinosaur?","options":["Keep it as a pet","Capture it for profit","Study it for science","Release it into the wild"],"correct_answer":"Capture it for profit"},{"question":"How does Ella feel about the baby dinosaur?","options":["She is afraid of it","She thinks it is adorable","She wants to sell it","She is indifferent"],"correct_answer":"She thinks it is adorable"},{"question":"What motivates Ella and Jake to run away from the poacher?","options":["Fear for their safety","A desire to find a way home","The need to protect the dinosaur","Curiosity about the jungle"],"correct_answer":"The need to protect the dinosaur"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_320_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_320_ch1_img1.png","plot_320_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":801,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
