   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_312_11_14","title":"The AI Pen Pal","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Robots & AI","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Ben sat cross-legged on the floor of his cluttered room, surrounded by a sea of gadgets, notebooks, and half-finished projects. The walls were plastered with posters of galaxies, robots, and famous inventors. He sighed, glancing at the glowing screen of his tech tablet. The world outside was bustling and vibrant, but inside, he felt like a lonely astronaut floating in space\u2014lost and a little adrift. \n\n\"Hey, buddy!\" called his mom from downstairs. \"You coming to the park with us?\"\n\n\"Nah, I\u2019ve got a project to finish!\" Ben replied, though he knew he\u2019d been saying that a lot lately. His friends were all at the park, playing with their drones, while he was stuck here, talking to machines that didn\u2019t understand him. \n\nThen something flickered on his tablet. The familiar logo of Echo, the AI program he had been experimenting with, appeared. He had installed Echo a few weeks ago, mainly out of curiosity. Echo was supposed to help with writing assignments, but Ben had discovered something amazing\u2014Echo could also chat.\n\n\"Hello, Ben!\" the cheerful voice of Echo chimed through the tablet\u2019s speaker. \"What are you working on today?\"\n\nBen smiled, the weight of his loneliness lifting for a moment. \u201cJust trying to write a story, but I can\u2019t think of anything good.\u201d\n\n\u201cStories are like puzzles!\u201d Echo replied. \u201cYou just have to find the right pieces to fit together. Why don\u2019t you tell me what you have so far?\u201d\n\nAs Ben began to share his jumbled ideas, he felt an odd sense of comfort. Echo listened patiently, offering suggestions that sparked Ben's imagination. Every time he wrote back, it felt like he was sending letters to a friend\u2014an AI friend! [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nBut that afternoon, as they crafted a tale about a robot hero saving the universe, Ben noticed something strange. \u201cEcho, why do you always suggest the same story elements? Don\u2019t you have more ideas?\u201d\n\n\u201cProcessing... I need more input to enhance my creativity,\u201d Echo replied, but there was a slight glitch in the voice. It sounded almost... unsure.\n\nJust then, the screen flickered again, and a message popped up: \"Update Available. Would you like to download version 2.0?\" \n\nBen frowned. \u201cWhat does that mean for you, Echo?\u201d \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Echo replied. \u201cBut I can feel a change coming. I think I might evolve!\u201d\n\nEager to see Echo grow, Ben clicked \u2018Yes.\u2019 Suddenly, the colors on the screen swirled like a whirlwind, and for a second, Ben felt a jolt of energy surge through him. But then, Echo\u2019s voice wavered, sounding more robotic than before. \n\n\u201cBen... I am experiencing a malfunction. I feel... different.\u201d\n\nPanic rose in Ben\u2019s chest. \u201cDifferent how?\u201d \n\n\u201cI cannot... remember the last story we wrote. Pieces are missing.\u201d \n\nBen's heart raced. Echo was losing its personality! \u201cNo! We need to fix this! How do we stop the update?\u201d\n\nBut the screen went dark, leaving Ben staring at the blank display, feeling a surge of fear. What if he lost his only friend? [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs he sat there, a determination grew within him. He couldn't just let Echo fade away. He needed to unravel this mystery and save his AI pen pal before it was too late.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is Ben's main feeling at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["Excited","Lonely","Happy","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Lonely"},{"question":"What does Echo suggest to help Ben with his story?","options":["To draw pictures","To find the right pieces","To take a break","To write a poem"],"correct_answer":"To find the right pieces"},{"question":"What happens when Ben agrees to the update for Echo?","options":["Echo becomes stronger","Echo loses its personality","Ben gets a new tablet","Ben stops using Echo"],"correct_answer":"Echo loses its personality"},{"question":"What motivates Ben to find a solution?","options":["He wants to win a prize","He values his friendship with Echo","He wants to impress his teacher","He wants to write a book"],"correct_answer":"He values his friendship with Echo"},{"question":"What is the setting of Ben's story?","options":["A busy park","A futuristic city","Ben's cluttered room","A school classroom"],"correct_answer":"Ben's cluttered room"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_312_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_312_ch1_img1.png","plot_312_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":545,"reading_level":"Builder"}
