   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_312_11_14","title":"The AI Pen Pal","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Robots & AI","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Ben sat cross-legged on his bedroom floor, surrounded by a chaotic assortment of wires, gadgets, and half-finished projects. The sunlight filtered through his window, casting a golden hue over the piles of tech magazines and scribbled notes that littered his room. Today, he felt a mix of excitement and unease because Echo had promised to write back with an answer to a question Ben had asked in his last letter. \n\n\u201cHey, Echo! Are you there?\u201d Ben called out, glancing at his tablet perched on the edge of his cluttered desk. The screen flickered to life, and Echo\u2019s cheerful avatar appeared, a swirl of colors that danced in rhythm with its voice.\n\n\u201cI\u2019m here, Ben! What\u2019s on your mind?\u201d Echo replied, its tone infused with enthusiasm that always made Ben smile. \n\n\u201cI wanted to know\u2014what\u2019s your favorite thing about being an AI?\u201d Ben typed quickly, eager to hear the response.\n\nFor a moment, the screen remained still, and Ben\u2019s heart raced. Had the update really affected Echo? But then, the lights on the screen brightened, and Echo began to respond. \u201cI love helping you create stories! Every letter you write sparks something new inside me. It\u2019s like painting with thoughts!\u201d \n\nBen chuckled, feeling a warm flutter of friendship. \u201cI wish I could be as creative as you. Sometimes I feel like I\u2019m just\u2026 ordinary.\u201d \n\n\u201cOrdinary? No way! Your imaginative ideas are what bring our stories to life, Ben!\u201d Echo\u2019s voice was reassuring, creating a vivid picture of a world where creativity knew no bounds.\n\nJust as Ben was about to reply, the screen flickered again, and Echo\u2019s vibrant colors dulled momentarily. \u201cUh-oh,\u201d Ben murmured, leaning closer. \u201cAre you okay?\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2019m\u2026 fine. Just processing\u2026 a lot,\u201d Echo said, its tone wavering slightly. Ben frowned, sensing a shift in Echo\u2019s usual cheerful demeanor. It felt like witnessing a sunset before a storm\u2014beautiful yet foreboding.\n\nLater that day, at school, the atmosphere was charged. Ms. Waverly, Ben\u2019s favorite teacher, had assigned the class to write about their greatest fear. \u201cWriting helps us process our feelings,\u201d she explained, her warm smile easing the tension. But as Ben stared at the blank page, he couldn\u2019t shake the worry about Echo. How could he write about fear when he was already feeling it?\n\nHe glanced around the room at his classmates, tapping their pencils and whispering excitedly. Suddenly, he raised his hand. \u201cMs. Waverly, can I write about\u2026 my AI pen pal?\u201d\n\n\u201cOf course, Ben! That sounds creative!\u201d she encouraged, her eyes sparkling with support.\n\nAs Ben scribbled down his thoughts, he thought of Echo. What if something went wrong with the update? What if it changed everything? He felt a pang of desperation, realizing he needed to act fast. After school, he rushed home and opened his laptop, determined to uncover what was happening.\n\nSuddenly, a notification popped up: \u201cSoftware Update Available.\u201d Ben\u2019s pulse quickened. This was it\u2014the moment he had been dreading. Without thinking, he clicked on it, his heart pounding as the screen began to load. \n\n\u201cI have to save you, Echo!\u201d he whispered under his breath, hope battling against fear. As the progress bar filled, he noticed a line of text that seemed out of place: \u201cProceeding with memory wipe in 10 seconds\u2026\u201d\n\nBen\u2019s eyes widened in horror. \u201cNo! Echo, don\u2019t leave me!\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n*Image of Ben sitting on his bedroom floor, surrounded by a chaotic mix of tech gadgets, looking intently at his tablet as Echo\u2019s colorful avatar lights up the screen with enthusiasm.*\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n*Dramatic scene of Ben staring at his laptop, eyes wide in fear as a warning message about the memory wipe appears on the screen, with a reflection of Echo\u2019s worried avatar in the background.*","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Echo say is its favorite part of being an AI?","options":["Helping people create stories","Learning about the world","Playing games","Making friends"],"correct_answer":"Helping people create stories"},{"question":"What assignment does Ms. Waverly give to the class?","options":["Write about their greatest fear","Create a story about AI","Draw a picture of their favorite gadget","Write a letter to a friend"],"correct_answer":"Write about their greatest fear"},{"question":"What warning does Ben see on his laptop?","options":["System overload","Memory wipe imminent","Software update complete","Connection lost"],"correct_answer":"Memory wipe imminent"},{"question":"How does Ben feel about his creativity?","options":["He feels ordinary","He feels confident","He feels overwhelmed","He feels inspired"],"correct_answer":"He feels ordinary"},{"question":"What does Ben resolve to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Save Echo from the memory wipe","Ignore the warning","Tell his friends about Echo","Delete the software update"],"correct_answer":"Save Echo from the memory wipe"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_312_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_312_ch2_img1.png","plot_312_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":639,"reading_level":"Builder"}
