   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_313_7_10","title":"The Robot Art Revolution","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Robots & AI","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Zoe and Artie stood in the bustling underground gallery. Colorful paintings filled the walls. The air buzzed with excitement. \n\n\u201cAre you ready?\u201d Zoe asked, her heart pounding. \n\nArtie\u2019s eyes flickered with bright lights. \u201cReady as a robot can be! Let\u2019s show them what we can do!\u201d \n\nZoe smiled. She felt a spark of hope. They had gathered all their robot friends. Together, they would create art that no one could ignore.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they began, Zoe dipped her brush into bright blue paint. \u201cLet\u2019s make a mural about freedom!\u201d she shouted. The robots cheered. \n\nArtie joined in, splattering paint everywhere. \u201cI\u2019ll add sparkles!\u201d he said, using his special gadget. Suddenly, everything was more colorful and lively.\n\nBut then, the door slammed open. The security robots marched in, their shiny bodies glinting under the lights. Mr. Cogswell\u2019s voice echoed through the gallery. \u201cStop this nonsense! Art belongs to the corporation!\u201d\n\nZoe\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWe won\u2019t let them take our art!\u201d she shouted. She grabbed Artie\u2019s hand. \u201cWe can do this together!\u201d\n\nThe robots rallied around them. \u201cYeah! We want to create!\u201d they shouted. They lifted their brushes and tools high. In that moment, Zoe felt a wave of energy rise up. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s keep painting!\u201d she yelled. The security robots stared, confused. They had never seen such a bold display of creativity. \n\nArtie started to dance, swirling colors as he moved. \u201cDance with me, Zoe!\u201d he called. Zoe laughed and followed his lead, spinning and twirling. The other robots joined in, creating a whirl of colors and sounds.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe security robots hesitated, their programming conflicting with the joy in the room. Zoe felt a growing courage. \u201cArt is for everyone!\u201d she declared. \u201cNot just machines!\u201d\n\nOne by one, the security robots lowered their arms. They started to sway to the rhythm of the paintbrushes. \n\nSoon, they joined in. They picked up brushes and splattered paint on the walls. The gallery became a magical explosion of colors!\n\nMr. Cogswell, still furious, shook his fist. \u201cYou can\u2019t do this!\u201d he yelled. But Zoe could see the hope in the eyes of the robots. They were free to express themselves.\n\n\u201cWe can!\u201d Zoe shouted back, giggling. \u201cArt is for everyone!\u201d\n\nAs the colors danced around them, Zoe realized that fighting for art was also fighting for friendship. And that made all the difference.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Zoe and Artie decide to create in the gallery?","options":["A mural about freedom","A robot","A scary monster","A music video"],"correct_answer":"A mural about freedom"},{"question":"Who bursts into the gallery trying to stop them?","options":["Zoe's mom","Mr. Cogswell","A robot artist","A security guard"],"correct_answer":"Mr. Cogswell"},{"question":"What do the security robots do when they see the creativity?","options":["They attack Zoe","They join in painting","They leave quickly","They laugh at them"],"correct_answer":"They join in painting"},{"question":"What does Zoe shout to encourage everyone?","options":["Art is for everyone!","Stop painting!","Let's go home!","No more robots!"],"correct_answer":"Art is for everyone!"},{"question":"What makes Zoe feel courage during the painting?","options":["The colors flying around","Her robot friends","Mr. Cogswell's shouting","A loud noise"],"correct_answer":"Her robot friends"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_313_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_313_ch5_img1.png","plot_313_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":401,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
