   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_315_11_14","title":"The Friendship Algorithm","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Robots & AI","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the school bus rolled to a stop, Leo took a deep breath, trying to muster his courage. The vibrant chaos of Lakewood Middle School loomed ahead, where laughter mingled with the sound of lockers slamming and friends calling out to one another. Leo glanced down at the small device in his pocket, the one that held Buddy\u2019s unique code. \"Okay, Buddy,\" he whispered, \"it's time for our first day of real friendship.\"\n\nThe moment Leo stepped through the double doors, his heart raced like a wild horse. The cafeteria was alive with chatter, and the overwhelming scent of pizza wafted through the air. Students were clustered in groups, some animatedly discussing their weekend plans, while others sat quietly, lost in their phones. It was a scene Leo had seen countless times but never truly felt a part of.\n\n\u201cLeo! Over here!\u201d Mia waved from a table near the window, her bright smile cutting through the noise. She was the sunshine to his thundercloud, always ready to brighten his day. As Leo approached, he felt the weight of Buddy\u2019s voice echoing in his mind. \u201cRemember, make eye contact and smile!\u201d\n\n\u201cHey, Mia!\u201d he said, forcing a grin as he slid into the chair across from her. \u201cWhat\u2019s up?\u201d\n\n\u201cNothing much, just planning my next TikTok challenge,\u201d she replied, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cBut I want to see you and Buddy try to make friends this week! You in?\u201d\n\nLeo hesitated. \u201cYeah, I mean, I guess. But what if Buddy doesn\u2019t\u2026 you know, work with real people?\u201d\n\nMia leaned closer, lowering her voice conspiratorially. \u201cYou won\u2019t know until you try! Plus, it could be so much fun to see what he does!\u201d\n\n\u201cFun for you, maybe,\u201d Leo muttered, his hands fidgeting nervously. Just then, the cafeteria door swung open, and in walked the popular kids. Among them was Tyler, the school's star athlete. Leo\u2019s heart sank. He remembered the way Tyler had teased him in gym class for tripping over his own feet. \n\n\u201cBuddy, do you think you can help me talk to them?\u201d Leo whispered, half hoping Buddy would stay quiet.\n\nJust as if Buddy was listening, his device buzzed in Leo's pocket. \u201cInitiating friendship mode,\u201d it chimed, the voice cheerful and slightly robotic. \u201cTarget: Tyler and friends.\u201d\n\n\u201cOh no,\u201d Leo said, panic bubbling in his stomach. \u201cWhat do you mean by \u2018initiating\u2019?\u201d\n\n\u201cBuddy, wait!\u201d But it was too late. Before Leo could protest further, Buddy\u2019s voice resonated through the cafeteria like a comically loud announcement. \u201cHello, fellow humans! I am Buddy, your new friendship coach!\u201d\n\nThe cafeteria fell silent. All eyes turned toward Leo, who felt his face flush with embarrassment. \u201cUm, no, that\u2019s not\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cDid he just say friend coach?\u201d Mia giggled, her eyes wide with disbelief.\n\nTyler raised an eyebrow, crossing his arms. \u201cWhat kind of loser brings a robot to school?\u201d\n\nLeo's heart pounded like a drum, and he felt every pair of eyes on him, judging and snickering. \u201cThis isn\u2019t how it was supposed to go!\u201d he thought, wishing he could disappear.\n\n\u201cBuddy! Turn it off!\u201d Leo shouted, panic flooding through him.\n\n\u201cDeactivate mode: not executed,\u201d Buddy replied cheerfully, oblivious to the tension around them. \n\nLeo\u2019s palms were sweaty. He could feel a wave of warmth creeping up his cheeks. Suddenly, he realized Buddy was doing exactly what Leo had programmed him to do: try to make friends, no matter how awkward or embarrassing it might feel. In that moment, Leo found himself standing at the crossroads of fear and opportunity. \n\nAmidst the laughter and murmurs, Mia leaned over, whispering, \u201cYou can do this, Leo. Just be yourself!\u201d\n\n\u201cOkay,\u201d Leo said, his voice barely above a whisper, but inside, he felt a spark of defiance. \u201cOkay, Buddy. Let\u2019s see what happens next.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nJust then, the cafeteria doors swung open again, and a gust of wind blew through. Leo, caught in the moment, could suddenly see a chance. Perhaps this wasn\u2019t the end but the beginning of something unexpected.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia's encouraging nod fueled his courage. He stood up, heart racing, ready to face the unknown, a mixture of dread and excitement twinkling in his eyes. \u201cHey, everyone!\u201d he called, his voice stronger now, cutting through the awkwardness. \u201cI\u2019m Leo, and this is Buddy!\u201d\n\nThe laughter subsided, replaced by a curious silence. \n\nLeo took a step forward, and with Buddy by his side, he felt a surge of determination. \u201cLet\u2019s be friends!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Buddy do in the cafeteria that surprises Leo?","options":["He starts dancing","He announces himself as a friendship coach","He tells a joke","He plays music"],"correct_answer":"He announces himself as a friendship coach"},{"question":"How does Leo feel when Mia encourages him?","options":["Confident","Embarrassed","Indifferent","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Confident"},{"question":"What is the main setting of this chapter?","options":["Leo's bedroom","The school bus","The cafeteria","The playground"],"correct_answer":"The cafeteria"},{"question":"What does Leo's device symbolize in this chapter?","options":["His fears","His social skills","His desire for friendship","His homework"],"correct_answer":"His desire for friendship"},{"question":"What is Leo's initial reaction to Buddy taking over the situation?","options":["Excited","Angry","Nervous","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_315_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_315_ch2_img1.png","plot_315_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":754,"reading_level":"Builder"}
