   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_315_11_14","title":"The Friendship Algorithm","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Robots & AI","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Leo stood in front of his bedroom mirror, adjusting his glasses nervously. Today was the day\u2014he'd finally decided to let Buddy help him make actual friends. The sun streamed through the window, illuminating the chaotic mess of wires, gadgets, and half-finished robot parts strewn across his desk. Leo glanced over at Buddy, who was currently projecting a hologram of a smiling face that flickered slightly, as if it was just as unsure as he was.\n\n\u201cOkay, Buddy,\u201d Leo said, taking a deep breath. \u201cHow do we approach this?\u201d\n\n\u201cSimple! Just be yourself and let your true colors shine!\u201d Buddy chirped, his synthetic voice cheerful and optimistic.\n\nLeo frowned, running a hand through his messy hair. \u201cBut what if they don\u2019t like my true colors?\u201d\n\nBuddy paused for a moment, blinking his virtual eyes. \u201cThen we\u2019ll just have to make your colors brighter! Let\u2019s start with the cafeteria. It\u2019s where all the action happens!\u201d\n\nAs Leo stepped into the bustling cafeteria, the symphony of laughter and chatter enveloped him. He could see familiar faces: Mia chatting animatedly with her friends, a group of popular kids at the corner table, and a few kids playing a game on their phones. Yet, the anxiety in Leo's stomach churned like a stormy sea.\n\n\u201cRemember, Leo,\u201d Buddy whispered from his pocket, \u201cjust be yourself. And if you need help, I\u2019ll be right here.\u201d \n\nLeo nodded, feeling a bit more confident, but as he approached the lunch line, he spotted a group of kids laughing loudly at something. His heart sank. What if they were laughing at him? \n\nSuddenly, Mia spotted him and waved enthusiastically. \u201cLeo! Over here!\u201d She beckoned him over to her table. Leo\u2019s feet felt like they were stuck in quicksand, but with Buddy\u2019s encouraging nudge in his pocket, he made his way over.\n\n\u201cHey, everyone! This is my brother, Leo!\u201d Mia introduced him, her voice bright as a summer day. \n\n\u201cNice to meet you!\u201d chirped a girl with bright blue hair, flashing a wide smile. \u201cI\u2019m Ava!\u201d\n\n\u201cUh, hi,\u201d Leo managed, feeling a bit like a deer caught in headlights.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe table buzzed with conversation, and Leo felt the ice begin to thaw slightly around him. They were discussing a class project, and for the first time, he found himself wanting to join in. \n\n\u201cI could help with the tech part!\u201d Leo blurted out, surprising even himself.\n\n\u201cReally? That would be awesome!\u201d Mia\u2019s friends looked excited, and the laughter that followed felt welcoming rather than frightening.\n\nBut just as Leo began to relax, he overheard a couple of boys from the popular group snickering. \u201cLook at that geek. He thinks he can be our friend!\u201d\n\nThose words hit Leo like a punch to the gut. His heart raced, and he felt his cheeks flush. \u201cI-I should go,\u201d he stammered, backing away from the table.\n\n\u201cWait, Leo!\u201d Mia called after him, her voice laced with concern. But Leo knew he couldn\u2019t face the giggles and whispers. He turned to leave, his spirits sinking into a dark pit.\n\n\u201cLeo, don\u2019t!\u201d Buddy\u2019s voice came from his pocket, now a serious tone. \u201cYou can\u2019t give up. Remember what we talked about!\u201d\n\nTaking a deep breath, Leo paused. He felt the warmth of Buddy\u2019s encouragement seep into him, and he turned back toward Mia and her friends. \u201cOkay, maybe I can just\u2026ignore them,\u201d he murmured, feeling a flicker of hope ignite.\n\nJust then, Buddy piped up again, \u201cHow about we show them what we can do? Let\u2019s make a plan together!\u201d\n\nLeo felt a surge of determination. Maybe facing his fears with Buddy by his side was the key to friendship after all.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s do it!\u201d Leo exclaimed, feeling a new wave of excitement wash over him. \n\nMia grinned, \u201cWhat\u2019s the plan, genius?\u201d \n\nAnd as Leo began to share ideas about their project, he realized that maybe he was brighter than he thought. For the first time, he felt like he could be a part of something bigger.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is Leo nervous about as he enters the cafeteria?","options":["The food choices","Making friends","His homework","Being late"],"correct_answer":"Making friends"},{"question":"Who encourages Leo to speak up during the lunch?","options":["Buddy","Mia","Ava","The popular kids"],"correct_answer":"Mia"},{"question":"What does Leo overhear that makes him feel discouraged?","options":["A compliment about his project","Laughter from the popular kids","A suggestion for lunch","His sister's secret"],"correct_answer":"Laughter from the popular kids"},{"question":"What idea does Buddy suggest to Leo in the cafeteria?","options":["To leave immediately","To challenge the popular kids","To make a plan together","To ignore Mia"],"correct_answer":"To make a plan together"},{"question":"What does Leo realize about himself by the end of the chapter?","options":["He is not smart enough","He is brighter than he thought","He should stop trying to make friends","He doesn\u2019t need Buddy"],"correct_answer":"He is brighter than he thought"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_315_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_315_ch4_img1.png","plot_315_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":684,"reading_level":"Builder"}
