   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_307_11_14","title":"The Last Seed of Earth","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Space Travel","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The hum of The Voyager enveloped Leo and Ava as they stepped into the control room, the glow of the control panels casting a soft blue light on their faces. The ship was sleek and modern, outfitted with every tool necessary for their monumental journey. Leo's heart raced; this was not just a spaceship\u2014it was their lifeline. \n\n\u201cAva, can you believe it? We\u2019re really doing this!\u201d he exclaimed, a mix of excitement and trepidation bubbling inside him. \n\n\u201cYeah, but we have to keep the seed safe,\u201d Ava replied, her voice serious. She was already at a terminal, her fingers flying over the keys as she checked the ship\u2019s systems. A tangle of brown hair fell into her eyes, but she didn\u2019t bother to brush it away. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, a red warning light blinked on the console, like a frantic heartbeat. Leo\u2019s stomach dropped. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?\u201d \n\n\u201cLooks like a debris field ahead,\u201d Ava said, furrowing her brow. \u201cI need to adjust the navigational settings.\u201d \n\nAs she worked, Leo felt a strange prickling sensation at the back of his neck, as if they were being watched. \u201cDo you think the other ships are nearby?\u201d \n\n\u201cMaybe,\u201d Ava said, her hands steady despite the tension in her voice. But Leo could see the worry in her eyes. \n\nJust then, a loud bang echoed through the ship, followed by the sound of metal scraping against metal. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Leo shouted, his heart racing even faster. \n\nAva\u2019s fingers froze above the controls. \u201cI don\u2019t know, but we need to check it out!\u201d \n\nWithout another word, they dashed towards the source of the noise. They found the cargo bay door ajar, swinging on its hinges like a crooked mouth. Both siblings peered inside. The seed\u2019s containment pod was still there, but something felt off.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s too quiet,\u201d Ava whispered, her voice barely above a breath. \n\nAs they moved closer, a figure emerged from the shadows\u2014a tall, shadowy silhouette. Leo\u2019s heart pounded in his chest. \u201cWho are you?\u201d he demanded, stepping in front of Ava protectively. \n\nThe figure stepped into the light, revealing a boy about their age, but his eyes glinted with mischief. \u201cI\u2019m here for the seed,\u201d he said with a sly grin. Before Leo could react, the boy lunged toward the pod. \n\n\u201cStop!\u201d Leo shouted, but it was too late. The boy grabbed the containment pod and, with a swift motion, began to pull it towards the open bay door. \n\nAva reacted instinctively. \u201cLeo, help me!\u201d She raced forward, grabbing the other side of the pod. \u201cPull!\u201d \n\nWith a grunt, they tugged against the intruder, their muscles straining. Leo\u2019s face turned red with effort. \u201cWe can\u2019t let him take it!\u201d \n\nThe boy laughed, but there was a layer of desperation in his eyes. \u201cYou don\u2019t know what you\u2019re dealing with! That seed belongs to me!\u201d \n\nJust then, the ship lurched violently, throwing them all off balance. The boy stumbled backward, losing his grip on the pod. In that instant, Ava seized the opportunity and slammed the door shut, locking it. \n\n\u201cWhat just happened?\u201d Leo asked, breathless and wide-eyed. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Ava replied, her face pale. \u201cBut I think we\u2019ve made an enemy.\u201d \n\nLeo nodded, his pulse still racing. They were in deeper trouble than he had ever imagined, and now they had to figure out how to protect the seed from both their rivals and the dangers of space itself. \n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s our next move?\u201d he asked, determination rising within him. \n\nBefore Ava could answer, a flashing red light illuminated the control panel. \u201cLeo, we\u2019re not alone,\u201d she said, her voice trembling. \u201cThere\u2019s another ship on our tail.\u201d \n\nLeo swallowed hard, realizing their mission was about to become more complicated than he\u2019d ever anticipated. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s prepare for a chase,\u201d Leo said, his mind racing. \u201cWe have to protect the last seed of Earth, no matter what it takes.\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What warning appears on the control panel at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["A fire alert","A warning about a debris field","A life support alert","A navigation error"],"correct_answer":"A warning about a debris field"},{"question":"What does the intruder want to take from Leo and Ava?","options":["Their spaceship","The last seed of Earth","Ava's inventions","Leo's navigation skills"],"correct_answer":"The last seed of Earth"},{"question":"How do Leo and Ava react when they first encounter the intruder?","options":["They run away","They stand their ground","They try to negotiate","They call for help"],"correct_answer":"They stand their ground"},{"question":"What unexpected event occurs while they are struggling with the intruder?","options":["The ship powers down","The ship lurches violently","An alarm goes off","They get locked inside"],"correct_answer":"The ship lurches violently"},{"question":"What does Ava discover at the end of the chapter?","options":["They are out of fuel","There is another ship pursuing them","They lost the seed","The ship has a malfunction"],"correct_answer":"There is another ship pursuing them"}]},"images":null,"word_count":671,"reading_level":"Builder"}
