   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_308_11_14","title":"Galactic Pen Pals","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Space Travel","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Sam Thompson had always been a dreamer, but lately, his dreams felt like they were stuck in a thick fog. At eleven years old, he was the shy boy who sat at the back of the class, often buried in books filled with tales of distant galaxies and brave heroes. His small town, Maplewood, never seemed to match the thrill of the adventures he read about. The familiar trees lining Maplewood streets seemed too ordinary, their leaves whispering secrets he was too afraid to uncover. \n\nOne rainy afternoon, as droplets pattered against his window like a cosmic countdown, a strange envelope slipped under his door. It was bright purple with swirling patterns that looked almost alive. Curious, he picked it up, heart racing. \n\n\u201cWhat if it\u2019s a prank?\u201d he muttered to himself, glancing over his shoulder to make sure no one was watching. Ignoring his doubts, he tore it open, revealing a colorful letter written in an elegant script that wiggled and sparkled.\n\nDear Sam,  \nI am Qel from the planet Zynara! I have heard you love adventures, and I need your help. My home is in danger!  \nIn friendship,  \nQel\n\nSam's eyes widened, his imagination igniting like a rocket. An alien? This had to be a joke, but the excitement was too much to resist. He quickly found a piece of paper and wrote back, asking about the danger. \n\nAs days turned into weeks, Qel\u2019s letters filled Sam\u2019s bedroom with stories of vibrant landscapes, where trees grew with shimmering fruit and rivers sparkled like diamonds under twin suns. Each letter brought riddles that teased and puzzled him, igniting a spark of curiosity he thought had long faded. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nBut it was Qel's latest letter that brought a wave of uncertainty crashing over him. \u201cThe Light Crystal is missing,\u201d Qel wrote, \u201cand without it, Zynara will fade away! I believe you can help me find it.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, Sam felt the weight of the cosmos resting on his small shoulders. He was just a kid from Maplewood; how could he possibly help an alien save a planet? He remembered how he once let his fear prevent him from trying out for the school play. The thought of doing it again made his stomach churn.\n\nHis thoughts spiraled into a whirlpool of doubt. He could hear the taunts of Grix, the school bully, echoing in his mind, \u201cYou can\u2019t even stand up for yourself, Thompson!\u201d \n\nJust then, Sam\u2019s phone buzzed. It was a message from Grix: \u201cMeet me at the park. I\u2019ve got something to show you.\u201d \n\nHis heart raced. Every instinct told him to ignore Grix, yet curiosity tugged at him. What did Grix want? \n\nAs he stepped outside, the gray clouds hung low, mirroring the storm brewing in his chest. Could he face Grix? Could he even face himself? \n\nThen he remembered Qel\u2019s words about bravery. With a deep breath, he took a step forward, the decision made.\n\nBut as he approached the park, a shrill laugh pierced the air. Sam's heart sank. Grix and his crew were gathered by the swings, snickering and pointing at him. The fear that had held him captive for so long threatened to pull him under again.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLook who decided to join us!\u201d Grix sneered, crossing his arms. \u201cWhat\u2019s the matter, Sam? Did you come to get bullied again?\u201d\n\nSam felt the heat rise to his cheeks, ready to retreat back into his shell. But then he remembered Qel, the alien who believed in him. He had a choice: stay silent or say something. \n\nWith a voice steadier than he felt, he replied, \u201cNo, I\u2019m here to stand up for myself. And you can\u2019t scare me anymore.\u201d\n\nAs Grix's laughter faded, the weight of the moment hung in the air. This was only the beginning of something much bigger. Would he be brave enough to face the challenges ahead?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who does Sam receive a letter from?","options":["A friend","An alien","His teacher","A bully"],"correct_answer":"An alien"},{"question":"What is the main problem Qel is facing?","options":["He is lost","He needs to find a Light Crystal","He wants to come to Earth","He is being bullied"],"correct_answer":"He needs to find a Light Crystal"},{"question":"What does Sam struggle with in this chapter?","options":["His homework","His friendship with Qel","His fear and self-confidence","His dislike for Maplewood"],"correct_answer":"His fear and self-confidence"},{"question":"Where does Sam go to meet Grix?","options":["The library","The park","His house","The school"],"correct_answer":"The park"},{"question":"What decision does Sam make at the end of the chapter?","options":["To ignore Grix","To run away","To stand up for himself","To stop writing to Qel"],"correct_answer":"To stand up for himself"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_308_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_308_ch1_img1.png","plot_308_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":658,"reading_level":"Builder"}
