   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_309_11_14","title":"The Cosmic Racing League","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Space Travel","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the dust settled over Starscape Station, Alex stood at the edge of the observation deck, gazing out at the swirling cosmos. The vibrant colors of distant planets danced like a kaleidoscope against the backdrop of twinkling stars. A rush of excitement coursed through him, but beneath it lurked a knot of anxiety. Today, he would test his skills in the simulator, and the stakes felt higher than ever. \n\n\u201cAre you ready for this, Alex?\u201d Mira\u2019s voice broke through his thoughts. She approached, her holographic tablet flickering with designs for his racing gear. Her eyes sparkled with determination, but Alex could see the concern underneath. \u201cRemember, practice makes perfect. You need to focus.\u201d\n\n\u201cI know,\u201d he replied, forcing a smile. \u201cBut what if I\u2019m not good enough?\u201d His voice barely rose above a whisper, but Mira caught it.\n\nShe placed a reassuring hand on his shoulder. \u201cYou have a natural talent. Captain Jax wouldn\u2019t have taken you under his wing if he didn\u2019t see something special in you.\u201d With a nod, she gestured toward the simulator room. \u201cLet\u2019s show them what you\u2019ve got.\u201d\n\nEntering the simulator, Alex felt a mix of excitement and dread. The cockpit was sleek and filled with lights, resembling a real racing pod. He settled into the seat, adjusting the straps like a knight donning armor. As the simulator powered up, a familiar voice crackled over the intercom.\n\n\u201cWelcome to your first training session, Alex! Let\u2019s see if you can handle the Asteroid Alley course.\u201d The voice belonged to Captain Jax, his mentor and a former champion racer. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe screen lit up, displaying a dazzling holographic track weaving through a field of spinning asteroids. Alex\u2019s heart raced. He gripped the controls as the countdown began: three\u2026 two\u2026 one\u2026 \n\n\u201cGo!\u201d \n\nWith a jolt, Alex shot forward. The sensation of speed surged through him, and for a brief moment, he felt invincible. He maneuvered around asteroids, narrowly avoiding collision. The adrenaline coursed through his veins, and he could almost hear the cheers of an imaginary crowd. But then, disaster struck. \n\nA sudden flicker on the screen caught his eye\u2014a shimmering object darting across his path. It was Dante\u2019s racing pod, the same one he had seen at the station. \u201cWhat\u2019s he doing here?\u201d Alex wondered, his thoughts racing. Then he remembered Dante\u2019s warning about using underhanded tactics to win.\n\n\u201cStay focused!\u201d Captain Jax\u2019s voice echoed, but it was too late. Alex tried to dodge, but the simulator\u2019s controls felt like they had a mind of their own. He swerved left, then right, but it was no use. With a resounding crash, everything went black.\n\n\u201cAlex! Are you okay?\u201d Mira rushed into the simulator room, her expression frantic. The simulation powered down, and Alex blinked against the bright lights. \u201cWhat happened?\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2026 I think I saw something,\u201d he stammered, still disoriented. \u201cDante was there. I can\u2019t shake the feeling he\u2019s up to something.\u201d\n\nMira frowned, her brow furrowed in thought. \u201cWe need to figure this out. If Dante is cheating, he could ruin everything for you. We can\u2019t let him get away with this.\u201d\n\nAlex nodded, determination igniting within him. \u201cYou\u2019re right. I need to race against him, but first, we have to gather evidence.\u201d \n\nAs they left the simulator, Alex\u2019s heart raced with purpose. The path ahead was fraught with challenges, but he felt ready to face them. Little did he know, the real danger was just beginning, lurking in the shadows of the Cosmic Racing League.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Alex see during his training session that raises his concerns?","options":["A holographic planet","Dante's racing pod","Mira's designs","Captain Jax's trophy"],"correct_answer":"Dante's racing pod"},{"question":"What is the main setting of this chapter?","options":["Starscape Station","Asteroid Alley","The simulator room","Captain Jax's workshop"],"correct_answer":"The simulator room"},{"question":"Who encourages Alex before his training session?","options":["Captain Jax","Dante","Mira","His parents"],"correct_answer":"Mira"},{"question":"What happens to Alex during the simulator session?","options":["He wins the race","He crashes","He designs new gear","He meets other racers"],"correct_answer":"He crashes"},{"question":"What does Alex resolve to do after his crash?","options":["Leave the league","Train harder","Gather evidence against Dante","Speak to Captain Jax"],"correct_answer":"Gather evidence against Dante"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_309_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_309_ch2_img1.png","plot_309_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":602,"reading_level":"Builder"}
