   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_310_11_14","title":"The Stars That Bind Us","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Space Travel","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Kira stood at the edge of the cliff, her heart racing as she gazed up at the vast expanse of night sky. Stars twinkled like diamonds scattered on a deep blue velvet cloth, each one whispering secrets from beyond. She had always felt a pull towards the stars, stronger than any earthly tether. The village of Starview lay below, its modest homes wrapped in shadows, but up here, the air was electric with possibilities. \n\n\u201cHey, Kira! You coming or what?\u201d Leo\u2019s voice broke through her reverie. He was scrambling up the rocky path, his breath heavy with excitement and a dash of mischief. Leo had been Kira\u2019s best friend since kindergarten, always ready to dive into an adventure\u2014or a little trouble.\n\n\u201cYeah, just\u2026 taking it all in,\u201d Kira replied, glancing back at him. She could see the glint of the stars reflecting in his curious eyes. \n\nThey had planned this night for weeks, eager to witness the meteor shower that was expected to illuminate the sky. As they settled on the cliff\u2019s edge, the first streaks of light fell across the sky, trailing like ribbons of silver. Kira felt a strange stirring in her chest, a vibration that seemed to resonate with the cosmic display.\n\n\u201cLook! There\u2019s one!\u201d Leo shouted, pointing upward. Kira followed his gaze just in time to see a brilliant meteor blaze across the sky, leaving a shimmering tail behind. It felt magical, like the universe was granting them a wish. But then, as if the light from the meteor had ignited something deep within her, Kira felt an unexpected warmth wash over her.\n\nSuddenly, a voice echoed in her mind, soft and melodic. \u201cKira, the stars are calling you.\u201d She gasped, clutching her head as a rush of images flooded her thoughts\u2014dancing lights, swirling galaxies, and a figure cloaked in starlight.\n\n\u201cKira? Are you okay?\u201d Leo\u2019s voice pulled her from the vision, concern etched on his face. \n\n\u201cI-I think so,\u201d she replied, though her hands trembled slightly. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d\n\n\u201cHear what?\u201d he asked, furrowing his brow. \u201cYou look like you\u2019ve seen a ghost!\u201d\n\n\u201cNever mind,\u201d she whispered, deciding to keep her newfound experience a secret for now. The feeling was both exhilarating and terrifying. Could she really hear the stars? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs the meteors continued to shoot across the sky, Kira felt a growing urgency. She had to understand what was happening to her. The voice had been so clear, so inviting. But before she could speak, a final meteor blazed brighter than the rest, exploding into a dazzling shower of fragments that rained down around them.\n\n\u201cWhoa! Did you see that?\u201d Leo exclaimed, his eyes wide as he jumped to his feet. \u201cThis is the best night ever!\u201d\n\nKira nodded absently, her heart pounding. The beautiful chaos above had unveiled a new reality for her, one filled with wonder and uncertainty. It was exhilarating, but the weight of responsibility hung heavy on her shoulders. She could almost sense it\u2014the cosmic disaster the voice had hinted at.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go back to the village,\u201d she finally said, her voice steadying. \u201cWe need to figure this out.\u201d \n\nBut as they made their way down the path, a flicker of light from the corner of her eye caught Kira's attention. She turned, just in time to see a shimmering figure descending from the sky\u2014a spirit made of starlight, its eyes like twin suns. \n\n\u201cHelp us, Kira,\u201d it whispered, before vanishing into the night. \n\nKira\u2019s breath caught in her throat. Fear mingled with determination. She knew her journey was just beginning, and the fate of her planet rested on her young shoulders.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Kira feel when she looks at the stars?","options":["Fear","Excitement","Indifference","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Excitement"},{"question":"What does Leo do when he sees the meteor shower?","options":["He gets scared","He jumps for joy","He runs away","He falls asleep"],"correct_answer":"He jumps for joy"},{"question":"What strange experience does Kira have during the meteor shower?","options":["She hears a voice","She sees a ghost","She feels sick","She falls asleep"],"correct_answer":"She hears a voice"},{"question":"What does Kira decide to do after seeing the spirit?","options":["Run away","Ignore it","Try to understand her powers","Tell her parents"],"correct_answer":"Try to understand her powers"},{"question":"What is the main conflict introduced in this chapter?","options":["Kira wants to become famous","Kira has to learn to control her powers","Kira is afraid of the dark","Kira doesn't like Leo"],"correct_answer":"Kira has to learn to control her powers"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_310_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_310_ch1_img1.png","plot_310_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":619,"reading_level":"Builder"}
