   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"sci-fi_310_11_14","title":"The Stars That Bind Us","genre":"Sci-Fi","sub_genre":"Space Travel","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Kira stood at the edge of the village, peering out over the vast stretch of the night sky. The stars shimmered like diamonds scattered over a velvety black blanket. She could feel their presence, pulsing gently in time with her heartbeat. Leo, ever the curious companion, leaned in closer, trying to catch the faint whispers that only Kira seemed to hear.\n\n\"Do you think they know what\u2019s going to happen?\" Leo asked, his voice a mix of excitement and fear.\n\nKira\u2019s brow furrowed. \"I don\u2019t know, but Celestia said we need to hurry. The Cosmic Alignment is just days away. If I can't control my powers, our planet\u2014\"\n\nBefore she could finish, a bright flash erupted from the center of the sky. A bolt of light danced among the stars, causing Kira to stumble back as if the ground had shifted beneath her feet. The world around them dimmed momentarily, the air crackling with energy. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\"What was that?\" Leo gasped, his eyes wide, reflecting the luminous glow above.\n\n\"It\u2019s a sign! I can feel it!\" Kira exclaimed, her heart racing. She closed her eyes, reaching out with her mind, trying to connect with the light. Stars began to swirl around her, their voices rising in a harmonious chorus. Kira felt their warmth wrap around her like a comforting embrace, but along with that, she sensed an undercurrent of urgency.\n\n\"We have to find Celestia!\" Kira declared. They raced back to the library, the pages of old texts still fresh in their minds. As they burst through the doors, the scent of parchment and dust enveloped them. They needed answers, and fast.\n\nFlipping through an ancient tome, Kira spotted a passage about a 'Celestial Convergence,' a rare event where the energy of the stars could be harnessed. But there was a warning: if the energy was uncontrolled, it could cause chaos.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Leo pointed at a faint illustration of the stars aligning in a brilliant formation. \u201cThat\u2019s it! The Cosmic Alignment!\u201d\n\nJust then, the lights flickered, and a sudden gust of wind swept through the library, sending papers flying from the tables. Kira felt a jolt of panic surge through her. \u201cLeo, we don\u2019t have much time! I need to find Celestia, but what if she can\u2019t help us?\u201d \n\nHer voice trembled, and Leo placed a reassuring hand on her shoulder. \u201cWe\u2019ve gotten this far together. I believe in you, Kira. You can talk to the stars. Maybe they can guide you to her.\u201d\n\nAs Kira concentrated, she felt the stars respond, a gentle tug pulling her thoughts outward. \u201cCelestia, can you hear me?\u201d she called silently, channeling her energy. The response was immediate\u2014a swirl of starry light spiraled from her fingertips, illuminating the room. \n\nBut then, just as suddenly, the glow faded, and with it, the energy around her grew heavy, darkening the library\u2019s corners. Kira\u2019s heart pounded. What if she failed? What if the stars refused to guide her?\n\n\u201cKira, look!\u201d Leo shouted, his face pale with fear. A shadow loomed at the doorway, flickering in and out of existence, like a star dimming in the night. \n\n\u201cWho\u2019s there?\u201d Kira\u2019s voice was barely a whisper, the uncertainty gnawing at her stomach. \n\nBefore she could defend herself, the figure stepped into the light, revealing a familiar face\u2014but it was twisted by an expression of anger and despair. \u201cYou shouldn't have stirred the stars, Kira.\u201d\n\nKira gasped. \u201cStarla?\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWhy are you here?\u201d Leo demanded, stepping protectively in front of Kira. \n\n\u201cI came to warn you. The stars are not your friends. They have chosen you as their vessel, but at a terrible price.\u201d\n\nKira felt her breath hitch. Was this the truth? Could she trust her ability? The pressure built inside her, a storm of doubt swirling in her mind. She had to decide\u2014could she control her powers, or would she let them consume her? \n\nThe clock was ticking. The Cosmic Alignment was fast approaching, and Kira\u2019s choice could mean the difference between salvation and destruction.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What urgent task do Kira and Leo face in this chapter?","options":["Finding Celestia","Reading more books","Ignoring the stars","Building a spaceship"],"correct_answer":"Finding Celestia"},{"question":"What happens when Kira tries to call out to Celestia?","options":["Nothing happens","Stars swirl from her fingertips","A storm occurs","She hears a loud voice"],"correct_answer":"Stars swirl from her fingertips"},{"question":"Who appears at the doorway during the climax of the chapter?","options":["Celestia","Leo","Starla","A stranger"],"correct_answer":"Starla"},{"question":"What does Kira doubt about her abilities?","options":["If she can control them","If they are real","If they are helpful","If they are dangerous"],"correct_answer":"If she can control them"},{"question":"What is the looming event that Kira and Leo are trying to prevent?","options":["A meteor shower","Cosmic Alignment","A star festival","A library closing"],"correct_answer":"Cosmic Alignment"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_310_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_310_ch3_img1.png","plot_310_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":686,"reading_level":"Builder"}
