   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_305_7_10","title":"The Library Rivalry","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Lucy loved the library. It was her favorite place in the whole school. The tall bookshelves were filled with colorful books, and the cozy nook had soft pillows to sit on. Mrs. Finch, the librarian, was always there with a warm smile.\n\nOne sunny morning, Mrs. Finch called all the students together. \u201cListen up, everyone!\u201d she said. \u201cThis month, we will have a reading contest! Which class can read the most books?\u201d\n\nThe room buzzed with excitement. Lucy\u2019s eyes sparkled. She loved reading! But Ethan, the star of the soccer team, frowned. \u201cReading is boring!\u201d he said. \u201cI\u2019d rather play outside.\u201d\n\n\u201cNot if you want to win!\u201d shouted Lucy, her hands on her hips. \u201cMy class will read more books than yours!\u201d\n\nEthan smirked, \u201cBring it on, bookworm! My class can read faster than you think!\u201d\n\nAs the students chatted, Mrs. Finch raised her hands. \u201cLet\u2019s make this a friendly competition! You\u2019ll find new treasures in books!\u201d She winked, and the students giggled.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]  \n\nLucy was determined. She grabbed her favorite book, *The Secret Garden*, and raced to the reading nook. She wanted to be the first to win the contest. But Ethan wasn\u2019t far behind. He picked up a book about superheroes. \u201cThis is going to be easy!\u201d he laughed.\n\nDays went by, and both classes read like crazy. They counted their books and cheered each time they reached a new number. But one rainy afternoon, something changed. Lucy and Ethan were in the library at the same time. \n\nSuddenly, Ethan dropped his book. It thudded on the floor. \u201cOuch! I just wanted to read about the flying superhero!\u201d he grumbled. Lucy picked it up and smiled. \u201cWant to take turns reading?\u201d she asked.\n\nEthan hesitated. \u201cFine,\u201d he said. \u201cBut only if you promise not to make it boring.\u201d\n\nAs they read together, something magical happened. They discovered a hidden map tucked inside the pages of Ethan's book!\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWhat is this?\u201d Lucy gasped, her eyes wide. \u201cIt looks like a treasure map!\u201d\n\nEthan leaned closer. \u201cLook! It shows a spot in the library! We have to find it!\u201d\n\nTogether, they pressed forward, forgetting about the contest. Maybe reading could lead to an adventure after all!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What contest does Mrs. Finch announce?","options":["A reading contest","A sports contest","A writing contest","A spelling contest"],"correct_answer":"A reading contest"},{"question":"What is Lucy's favorite thing to do?","options":["Play soccer","Read books","Draw pictures","Eat snacks"],"correct_answer":"Read books"},{"question":"What does Ethan find boring?","options":["Reading","Playing soccer","Eating","Drawing"],"correct_answer":"Reading"},{"question":"What do Lucy and Ethan discover together?","options":["A new book","A treasure map","A soccer ball","A funny story"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"How do Lucy and Ethan feel about reading by the end of the chapter?","options":["Bored","Excited","Angry","Confused"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_305_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_305_ch1_img1.png","plot_305_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":374,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
