   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_305_7_10","title":"The Library Rivalry","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Lucy and Ethan entered the library, but today it felt different. Excitement buzzed in the air. Books lined the shelves like colorful soldiers ready for battle. Lucy spotted her favorite reading nook, a cozy corner filled with soft cushions. It was the perfect place to dive into a story.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cReady to win?\u201d Ethan smirked, adjusting his baseball cap. \u201cMy class is going to read the most books ever!\u201d\n\n\u201cNot if I can help it!\u201d Lucy replied with a determined smile. \u201cMrs. Finch believes in us!\u201d\n\nAs the contest began, the library filled with the sound of pages turning and whispers of excitement. Lucy grabbed a book about a brave knight. She flipped through the pages quickly. Each word made her heart race as she imagined adventure.\n\nMeanwhile, Ethan wandered over to his friends. \u201cLet\u2019s read a bunch of comic books. They\u2019re quick!\u201d he suggested. His friends cheered and grabbed their favorites. \n\nBut just then, a loud crash echoed through the library. Books tumbled off a shelf, landing in a colorful heap! Lucy gasped, \u201cWhat happened?\u201d\n\nEthan ran over. \u201cAre you okay?\u201d he asked, looking concerned. \n\n\u201cI\u2019m fine! But look!\u201d Lucy pointed. Beneath the fallen books, a rolled-up piece of parchment peeked out. \n\n\u201cIs that a map?\u201d Ethan exclaimed, his eyes wide. \n\nLucy carefully pulled it out. \u201cIt looks old! Maybe it leads to treasure!\u201d \n\n\u201cBut we have to read more books first,\u201d Ethan reminded her. \n\nLucy frowned. \u201cWhat if we read together? We can help each other and find the treasure!\u201d \n\nEthan thought for a moment. \u201cOkay! But only if we can switch reading materials!\u201d\n\nThey both grinned, realizing they might just become allies in this reading battle.\n\nTogether, they found a big table and spread the map out. As they studied it, Lucy noticed a strange symbol. \u201cWhat do you think it means?\u201d \n\n\u201cI bet it\u2019s a clue!\u201d Ethan\u2019s face lit up with excitement. \u201cLet\u2019s solve it!\u201d \n\nJust as they began to read more about the symbol, Mrs. Finch appeared with a smile. \u201cWhat\u2019s this? A treasure map?\u201d \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Lucy and Ethan said in unison.\n\n\u201cBe careful,\u201d Mrs. Finch warned. \u201cTreasure hunting can be tricky.\u201d \n\nThe tension in the air grew. Lucy and Ethan exchanged determined looks. They knew this was just the beginning of their adventure, but what lay ahead? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find the treasure, then!\u201d Ethan said, his voice full of excitement.\n\n\u201cRight, but first we need to read those books!\u201d Lucy replied, her heart racing.\n\nAs they raced back to the shelves, the competition was on. Would they find the treasure together, or would their classes remain rivals?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Lucy and Ethan discover in the library?","options":["A treasure map","A new librarian","A comic book","A game"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"What does Ethan want to read with his friends?","options":["Novel books","Comic books","Fantasy books","Mystery books"],"correct_answer":"Comic books"},{"question":"Who warns them about treasure hunting?","options":["Mrs. Finch","Mr. Brown","Ethan","Lucy"],"correct_answer":"Mrs. Finch"},{"question":"What do Lucy and Ethan decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Work together","Read alone","Quit the contest","Ignore the map"],"correct_answer":"Work together"},{"question":"What emotion does Lucy feel when reading her book?","options":["Bored","Excited","Angry","Scared"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_305_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_305_ch2_img1.png","plot_305_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":443,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
