   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_305_11_14","title":"The Library Rivalry","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Lucy Hart loved the library more than anything else in the world. It was her sanctuary, a cozy haven filled with towering shelves of books, where the scent of paper and ink mingled in the air like a warm hug. She would often lose track of time, diving into fantastical worlds and meeting characters who felt like friends. Today, however, the atmosphere buzzed with excitement and tension, something she hadn\u2019t felt in the library before.\n\nMrs. Finch, the beloved librarian, stood at the front of the library, her eyes sparkling behind her round glasses. \u201cAttention, everyone!\u201d she called, clapping her hands to gather the attention of the students who were scattered among the shelves. \u201cI have an announcement!\u201d\n\nAs Lucy settled into her favorite reading nook, she could see the eager faces of her classmates. Ethan Rossi, the star of the soccer team, lounged nearby, tossing a pencil between his fingers. He seemed uninterested, but Lucy knew that he would perk up for a contest.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re starting a month-long reading challenge!\u201d Mrs. Finch declared, her excitement palpable. \u201cThe class that reads the most books by the end of the month will win a special prize\u2014an exclusive pizza party here in the library!\u201d\n\nA cheer erupted in the room. Lucy\u2019s heart raced. She could already picture her classmates devouring pizza while discussing their favorite stories. But Ethan\u2019s friends were quick to rally around him, their competitive nature igniting. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s show them who\u2019s boss!\u201d one of his friends shouted, grinning widely. \u201cNo way a bunch of bookworms can beat us!\u201d\n\nLucy frowned, feeling a knot form in her stomach. She was determined to do her best, but she knew that Ethan\u2019s class had a reputation for being rowdy. They rarely stepped foot into the library, and when they did, it was mostly to find a place to chat rather than read.\n\nAs if sensing the tension, Mrs. Finch smiled and encouraged everyone to work together, emphasizing that reading was meant to be fun. \u201cRemember, it\u2019s not just about winning,\u201d she reminded them. \u201cIt\u2019s about exploring new stories and ideas!\u201d\n\nLucy glanced at Ethan. He was leaning back, arms crossed, and appeared unfazed by the announcement. \u201cYou think you can beat us, Hart?\u201d he called out, a teasing grin on his face. \n\n\u201cBring it on, Rossi!\u201d she replied, her voice firm. \n\nSuddenly, Lucy\u2019s eyes wandered to the far corner of the library. Amid the chaos, a glimmer caught her attention. She squinted and noticed a dusty old book lying half-open on a shelf that was often overlooked. It seemed to call out to her, its spine cracked and faded. A thrill coursed through her. What if that book held a secret?\n\nJust then, Ethan stood up, stretching as if preparing for a race. \u201cI\u2019m going to read more than you, bookworm,\u201d he said, shooting her a competitive look.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s see about that!\u201d Lucy shot back. She had a plan forming in her mind. \n\nWith a determined stride, she made her way to the mysterious book. As she reached for it, she heard a loud thud behind her. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nIt was Ethan, tripping over his own feet, sending a stack of books tumbling to the floor. Laughter erupted around them, but Lucy felt a pang of sympathy. Maybe they were not so different after all; both classes wanted to win, but what if they could learn something together instead?\n\nAs Lucy opened the old book, a faded map slipped out and fluttered to the ground, revealing strange symbols and markings that seemed to hint at something hidden within the library. She gasped, her heart racing with a mixture of excitement and curiosity. \n\n\u201cWhoa, what\u2019s that?\u201d Ethan asked, bending down to pick up the map. His expression shifted from competitive confidence to genuine intrigue.\n\n\u201cLooks like we might have a little adventure on our hands,\u201d Lucy said, her voice barely above a whisper, eyes gleaming. The library wasn\u2019t just a battleground for reading anymore; it might just be the beginning of something extraordinary.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What contest does Mrs. Finch announce?","options":["A spelling bee","A reading challenge","A science fair","A sports tournament"],"correct_answer":"A reading challenge"},{"question":"What prize is offered for the reading challenge?","options":["A trophy","A pizza party","Extra recess time","Gift cards"],"correct_answer":"A pizza party"},{"question":"How does Lucy feel about the library?","options":["She dislikes it","It is her sanctuary","She finds it boring","She thinks it's too chaotic"],"correct_answer":"It is her sanctuary"},{"question":"What does Lucy discover in the old book?","options":["A hidden treasure","A secret map","A letter from a friend","A list of rules"],"correct_answer":"A secret map"},{"question":"What is Ethan's initial attitude towards the reading contest?","options":["He is uninterested","He is very supportive","He is excited and competitive","He doesn\u2019t care at all"],"correct_answer":"He is excited and competitive"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_305_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_305_ch1_img1.png","plot_305_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":684,"reading_level":"Builder"}
