   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_305_11_14","title":"The Library Rivalry","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Lucy Hart sat cross-legged on the library floor, surrounded by a fortress of books. The scent of aged paper and polished wood filled the air as she thumbed through the pages of the mysterious book she had found. Its cover was tattered, with gold letters that shimmered in the dim light. It felt like a treasure chest of stories waiting to be unlocked. \n\nJust then, Ethan Rossi burst into the library, his laughter echoing off the shelves like a mischievous ghost. He was flanked by his friends, all of them with the cocky swagger of athletes who believed they had already won the reading contest. \u201cWhat are you doing over there, Lucy? Building a castle of dusty words?\u201d he jeered, tossing a casual glance at the books surrounding her. \n\n\u201cActually, Ethan, I\u2019m discovering a hidden map!\u201d Lucy shot back, holding up the book as if it were a magic wand. Her heart raced with excitement, but the doubt in Ethan\u2019s eyes made her feel small. \n\nEthan\u2019s friends chuckled, but he seemed intrigued, his competitive spirit flickering just beneath the surface. \u201cA map? What kind of map?\u201d he asked. \n\nShe flipped to the middle of the book, where a yellowed page revealed an intricate drawing of the library itself, complete with red X's marking certain locations. \u201cLook! It shows hidden spots in the library,\u201d she explained, her voice rising with enthusiasm. \u201cMaybe it leads to something special!\u201d\n\nBefore Lucy could continue, Mrs. Finch, the beloved librarian with her glasses perched on the edge of her nose, appeared like a guardian spirit. \u201cLucy, Ethan, how wonderful to see you both exploring the library!\u201d she beamed, her arms gesturing to the towering shelves filled with stories. \u201cBut remember, this competition is about more than just reading. It\u2019s about discovering the magic in every book.\u201d \n\nLucy nodded, inspired by Mrs. Finch\u2019s words. \u201cWhat if we all worked together? We could find out what this map is leading to!\u201d \n\nEthan hesitated, glancing at his friends who whispered among themselves, their expressions clouded with skepticism. \u201cWhat\u2019s in it for us? Your class is already losing, Lucy,\u201d he replied, trying to sound disinterested, but the spark of curiosity was evident in his eyes.\n\n\u201cMaybe a secret passage to the treasure would change that,\u201d Lucy proposed, her eyes gleaming with determination. Just as she said this, a loud crash echoed from the back of the library. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nStartled, they all turned to see a bookshelf wobbling precariously, books tumbling to the ground like a waterfall of stories. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d one of Ethan\u2019s friends yelped, taking a step back.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out,\u201d Ethan said, his bravado returning. \u201cCould be a clue!\u201d \n\nThe group moved cautiously toward the shelves, where they found a pile of dusty tomes and an old wooden chest, half-buried beneath the fallen books. Lucy\u2019s heart raced. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s part of the treasure?\u201d she whispered, a mix of dread and excitement swirling in her stomach.\n\nEthan knelt down, brushing dirt off the chest. \u201cHelp me open it,\u201d he urged, his voice barely above a whisper as they gathered around. \n\nWith a collective effort, they lifted the heavy lid, revealing a collection of old coins and a parchment that seemed to glow with an otherworldly light. The air around them thickened, and Lucy felt the weight of their rivalry shift in that moment\u2014a new alliance forming as they looked at each other, a mix of surprise and uncertainty in their eyes.\n\n\u201cLooks like we found more than just books,\u201d Ethan said, his tone serious yet laced with excitement. \u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d\n\nLucy\u2019s mind raced with possibilities. \u201cWe read the parchment! It might tell us what this treasure means for our contest!\u201d \n\nThe tension hung in the air, crackling with potential. Would they continue to see each other as rivals or as teammates in this unexpected adventure? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAnd as they leaned in closer to read the parchment, Lucy realized that each new challenge was forging something deeper than competition\u2014perhaps this treasure could mean a new beginning for them all.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Lucy discover in the library?","options":["A map","A treasure chest","A mysterious librarian","A sports trophy"],"correct_answer":"A map"},{"question":"What is Ethan's initial reaction to Lucy's discovery?","options":["He laughs and mocks her","He is excited and wants to help","He ignores her","He becomes angry"],"correct_answer":"He laughs and mocks her"},{"question":"What does Mrs. Finch encourage the students to focus on?","options":["Winning the contest","Reading both together and independently","Ignoring their differences","Finding hidden treasures"],"correct_answer":"Reading both together and independently"},{"question":"What do the students find after the loud crash?","options":["A hidden door","An old wooden chest","More books","A secret passage"],"correct_answer":"An old wooden chest"},{"question":"What new challenge do Lucy and Ethan face at the end of the chapter?","options":["Deciding how to split the treasure","Understanding the parchment","Winning the contest","Ignoring their rivalry"],"correct_answer":"Understanding the parchment"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_305_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_305_ch2_img1.png","plot_305_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":691,"reading_level":"Builder"}
