   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_305_11_14","title":"The Library Rivalry","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Lucy\u2019s heart raced as she climbed the familiar steps to the cozy yet chaotic school library. The air was thick with the smell of old books and dusty pages, but today, there was an undercurrent of excitement. Instead of her usual quiet corner, she spotted her classmates gathered around a table, poring over books and whispering animatedly. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLook at them,\u201d Lucy thought, a mix of pride and anxiety bubbling inside her. She felt a tug of camaraderie with her fellow bookworms, but the memory of Ethan\u2019s smug grin from the previous day stung. Would they really win the contest against his class?\n\nMrs. Finch, with her bright glasses perched on her nose, bounced around the library, checking in on everyone. \u201cRemember, team! The race to read the most books in a month is on! Let\u2019s show the other classes what we\u2019re made of!\u201d Her enthusiasm was infectious, yet Lucy couldn\u2019t shake the weight of competition hanging over them.\n\nAs the days passed, the rivalry intensified. Lucy\u2019s class turned the library into a war room, charts and stickers marking their reading progress. Meanwhile, Ethan's group had taken to calling themselves \u201cThe Book Bashers,\u201d and their boastful shouts echoed through the shelves. But with each page turned, Lucy felt herself pulling away from the thrill of competition and leaning toward the story behind the mysterious book she had discovered.\n\nOne afternoon, during a particularly intense reading session, Lucy sat down with the old map and her favorite mystery novel. As she traced the faded lines, a sudden thought struck her. \u201cWhat if the treasure is real?\u201d She glanced over at Ethan, who was animatedly arguing with one of his friends about the best way to read a football playbook. What did he think of adventures beyond the field?\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash shattered Lucy\u2019s concentration. The sound came from the back of the library, a place they had yet to explore together. She shot up, her heart pounding in her chest. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d she called out, the echoes of fear and curiosity mingling.\n\n\u201cYeah! Let\u2019s check it out!\u201d shouted Max, one of Lucy\u2019s classmates, his eyes sparkling with excitement. The small group hustled toward the noise, the competition forgotten for a moment.\n\nThey rounded the corner to find Ethan and his friends already there, staring in shock at a toppled bookshelf. Books were strewn across the floor like fallen leaves in autumn. But what caught Lucy\u2019s eye was the glint of something shiny peeking from underneath one of the larger books.\n\n\u201cIs that\u2026?\u201d Lucy knelt down, her heart racing. She carefully pulled the thick book aside to reveal a small, ornate chest, its surface covered in dust but shimmering with promise.\n\n\u201cWhoa,\u201d Ethan breathed, stepping closer. \u201cWhat did you find?\u201d\n\n\u201cI think it\u2019s a treasure,\u201d Lucy whispered, her fingers tracing the intricate designs on the chest. The tension in the air shifted. For a moment, all rivalry was forgotten as they all felt the pull of adventure.\n\nJust as they began to gather around the chest, a loud shout broke through. \u201cWhat are you kids doing near that mess?\u201d Mrs. Finch appeared, her eyes wide with concern. \u201cYou can\u2019t go through things without permission!\u201d\n\nThe realization struck them all at once\u2014this was a turning point. Were they willing to risk the contest for something as mysterious as treasure? Would they dare to join forces?\n\nLucy exchanged a look with Ethan, their rivalry hanging in the air like an unsaid agreement. This could be more than just a contest; this could be the adventure they never knew they needed. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s open it together,\u201d Ethan suggested, his voice low but firm. \n\nLucy nodded, feeling the weight of the moment. Together, they approached the chest, tension and anticipation thickening the air around them.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey paused, hands hovering above the latch, a silent promise exchanged in their eyes. As they prepared to uncover the mystery, a familiar voice jolted them from their thoughts\u2014\u201cWhat\u2019s going on here?\u201d It was the principal, Mr. Harris, and he didn\u2019t look pleased.\n\nLucy\u2019s mind raced. Would they be caught? Would their moment of discovery slip through their fingers like sand? \n\n\u201cUm, we were just\u2014\u201d Lucy stammered, her heart thumping louder than ever. \n\nThe decision hung in the air, and Lucy knew they had to make it fast. Would they reveal the chest to their principal and risk losing everything, or would they hide it and take a chance on a greater adventure?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Lucy discover in the library?","options":["A hidden map","A treasure chest","A new book","A secret room"],"correct_answer":"A treasure chest"},{"question":"How do Lucy and Ethan\u2019s friends react to the discovery?","options":["They ignore it","They argue","They are excited","They want to leave"],"correct_answer":"They are excited"},{"question":"What does Mrs. Finch encourage her students to do?","options":["Compete against each other","Read as much as possible","Ignore the contest","Leave the library"],"correct_answer":"Read as much as possible"},{"question":"What is the main conflict in this chapter?","options":["The students are bored","Rivalry between classes","A missing book","A book report"],"correct_answer":"Rivalry between classes"},{"question":"What unexpected event occurs at the end of the chapter?","options":["The lights go out","The principal arrives","A book falls","A fire alarm rings"],"correct_answer":"The principal arrives"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_305_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_305_ch3_img1.png","plot_305_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":765,"reading_level":"Builder"}
