   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_305_11_14","title":"The Library Rivalry","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the golden afternoon sun streamed through the tall windows of the school library, Lucy stood before the towering shelves, her heart still racing from the unexpected encounter with Principal Grayson. She had never imagined that their quest for the treasure could lead to such trouble. \u201cWe need to figure out a plan, Ethan,\u201d she said, glancing nervously at the door. \u201cWhat if he tells Mrs. Finch?\u201d\n\nEthan leaned against a nearby bookshelf, his expression a mixture of frustration and determination. \u201cIt\u2019s not like we were doing anything wrong\u2026 well, maybe a little. But we\u2019re just trying to read, right?\u201d \n\nLucy nodded, but doubt flickered in her mind like a candle struggling against the wind. The reading contest was still on, and if they didn\u2019t act quickly, their classes might lose interest entirely. \u201cMaybe we could combine our classes for a reading party? We could share what we\u2019ve found!\u201d\n\nEthan raised an eyebrow, clearly skeptical. \u201cWhat do you mean \u2018share\u2019? My class won\u2019t want to read boring stuff.\u201d \n\nJust then, Mrs. Finch appeared, her arms laden with a stack of books. \u201cAh! Perfect timing, you two! I just found some incredible stories about treasure hunts and friendship. Would you like to help me organize a mini book festival?\u201d Her eyes sparkled with enthusiasm, and Lucy felt a warm rush of hope. \n\n\u201cActually, Mrs. Finch,\u201d Lucy began, her voice steadying. \u201cEthan and I were thinking about merging our classes to celebrate reading together. We\u2019ve found something special, and we want to share it!\u201d\n\nMrs. Finch\u2019s smile widened. \u201cWhat an excellent idea! A treasure hunt where each class presents their favorite book? You can each pick a book that inspired you from the library and then share what you love about it. It\u2019ll be a great way to bond!\u201d\n\nEthan scratched his head, a thoughtful frown crossing his face. \u201cSo, we read together, and then we talk about it? Sounds kinda lame\u2026 but maybe we could make it fun?\u201d He grinned, an idea sparking in his mind. \u201cWe could turn it into a competition! Like a reading relay or trivia game!\u201d\n\nLucy\u2019s heart swelled with excitement. \u201cThat could work! And we could include the treasure hunt too! What if we set up clues that lead to different books? We can use the map we found!\u201d \n\n\u201cYes! That\u2019s perfect!\u201d Mrs. Finch clapped her hands together. \u201cYou two are going to create a wonderful atmosphere for the festival. And I think your classmates will love the challenge.\u201d\n\nThey discussed plans late into the afternoon, crafting ideas that filled the library with laughter and excitement. The atmosphere shifted from rivalry to collaboration, and soon, both classes began to warm to the idea. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs Lucy and Ethan gathered supplies, their hands brushed against each other, and she felt a spark of something new\u2014friendship, perhaps? The library no longer felt like a battleground but a treasure trove of stories waiting to be unveiled.\n\nIn the days that followed, whispers of the reading festival spread through the school like wildfire. Posters decorated the hallways, and both Lucy and Ethan felt the excitement building. They spent hours in the library, not just reading, but sharing snippets of their favorite stories with each other\u2019s classmates. \n\nOn the day of the festival, anticipation hung thick in the air. Students filled the library, excitement buzzing like a beehive. But just as they were about to start the treasure hunt, an unexpected shadow loomed\u2014a familiar figure walked through the door.\n\nEthan felt his heart drop. It was Principal Grayson, and he didn\u2019t look pleased. \u201cI need to speak to you two. Now.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe room fell silent, tension hanging like a thick fog. Lucy exchanged a worried glance with Ethan, both of them wondering if their newfound friendship\u2014and the entire festival\u2014was about to crumble.\n\n\u201cUh-oh,\u201d Lucy whispered, fear creeping into her voice. \n\nWhat would happen next? They had taken a step toward friendship, but the looming figure of authority could change everything.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What plan do Lucy and Ethan come up with for the reading contest?","options":["To compete harder against each other","To merge their classes for a reading festival","To give up on the contest","To read secretly"],"correct_answer":"To merge their classes for a reading festival"},{"question":"What does Mrs. Finch propose to make their reading festival special?","options":["A treasure hunt related to books","A sports event","A movie night","A science fair"],"correct_answer":"A treasure hunt related to books"},{"question":"How do the students react to the idea of the reading festival?","options":["They are indifferent","They are excited and enthusiastic","They want to cancel it","They are confused"],"correct_answer":"They are excited and enthusiastic"},{"question":"What unexpected event occurs during the festival preparations?","options":["A fire alarm goes off","Principal Grayson arrives to speak with them","Lucy gets lost in the library","Ethan's friends show up"],"correct_answer":"Principal Grayson arrives to speak with them"},{"question":"What feeling does Lucy experience as she works with Ethan?","options":["Frustration","Boredom","Hope and friendship","Fear"],"correct_answer":"Hope and friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_305_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_305_ch4_img1.png","plot_305_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":678,"reading_level":"Builder"}
