   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_305_11_14","title":"The Library Rivalry","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the sun poured through the tall windows of the school library, casting golden streaks on the wooden floor, Lucy and Ethan gathered around the reading nook under the giant oak tree. The scent of old books mingled with fresh paper, creating an atmosphere that sparked excitement and curiosity. Mrs. Finch\u2019s eyes sparkled with enthusiasm as she clapped her hands, drawing everyone\u2019s attention.\n\n\u201cAll right, readers!\u201d she chimed, her voice echoing through the cozy space. \u201cToday, we\u2019re officially kicking off our reading festival! Let's remember, it\u2019s not just about who reads the most books, but about discovering stories together!\u201d\n\nThe words hung in the air, a blend of promise and challenge. Lucy felt a surge of hope. She turned to Ethan, who was fidgeting with the sleeve of his jacket. \u201cAre you ready?\u201d she asked, her eyes bright with determination.\n\nEthan nodded, though he looked more nervous than excited. \u201cLet\u2019s just win this, okay? I mean, we have to show my class we can do it.\u201d\n\nLucy grinned. \u201cWe can do it together. Besides, what if we find more treasures in the books?\u201d She motioned to the towering shelves, the mysteries hidden among the pages.\n\nAs they divided their tasks, Lucy grabbed a stack of adventure novels while Ethan went for the sports biographies. They both felt a thrill of anticipation, each imagining the characters that would spring to life from the words.\n\nJust as they were about to begin, a sudden commotion erupted from the back of the library. A group of Ethan\u2019s friends burst into laughter, jostling each other and accidentally knocking into a shelf. Books tumbled down like a waterfall, creating a chaotic scene. \n\n\u201cEthan! Watch out!\u201d Lucy shouted, ducking to avoid the cascade. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nEthan hurried to help his friends, but as they picked up the fallen books, something glimmered at the back of the shelf. \u201cHey, what\u2019s this?\u201d he asked, reaching for a small, dusty box wedged between the shelves.\n\nLucy\u2019s heart raced as she approached. \u201cWhat did you find?\u201d she asked, her voice barely a whisper, as if they had uncovered a hidden treasure.\n\nEthan opened the box with shaking hands, revealing a collection of old, hand-written letters tied with a faded ribbon. \u201cThese look ancient!\u201d he exclaimed, his initial bravado replaced by genuine curiosity.\n\nLucy leaned closer, her eyes widening. \u201cDo you think they belong to someone important?\u201d she wondered aloud. The sight of the letters made her forget about the competition for a moment.\n\nThey carefully unwrapped the bundle, revealing stories of friendships and adventures from years gone by. As they read together, they felt a sense of connection not just to the letters, but to each other. \n\n\u201cThis is incredible,\u201d Ethan said, his tone softening. \u201cIt\u2019s like these letters were waiting for us to find them.\u201d\n\nLucy nodded, her heart swelling with understanding. \u201cIt\u2019s not just about reading more books, is it? It\u2019s about sharing the experience.\u201d \n\nAs they flipped through the pages, laughter and camaraderie started to bloom between them. Mrs. Finch approached, her eyes twinkling. \u201cWhat\u2019s this? A treasure found in our very own library?\u201d \n\nThey exchanged smiles, feeling the warmth of shared discovery. At that moment, the rivalry between their classes began to fade. They were no longer just competitors but friends united by the stories they uncovered.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s showcase these letters at the festival!\u201d Lucy suggested excitedly. \u201cEveryone deserves to hear these tales.\u201d\n\nEthan grinned, his competitive spirit morphing into a collaborative one. \u201cYeah! We can read them aloud together. It's going to be the best part of the festival!\u201d\n\nAs they prepared to share their newfound treasure, Lucy realized that the true victory didn\u2019t come from reading the most books, but from the friendships and stories they shared along the way.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What are Lucy and Ethan preparing for in this chapter?","options":["A sports competition","A reading festival","A science fair","A writing contest"],"correct_answer":"A reading festival"},{"question":"What do Lucy and Ethan discover in the library?","options":["A treasure map","A box of letters","A hidden room","An old book"],"correct_answer":"A box of letters"},{"question":"What does Lucy realize about the competition?","options":["It is not important","It is too hard","It is unfair","It is easy to win"],"correct_answer":"It is not important"},{"question":"How does Ethan's attitude change during this chapter?","options":["He becomes more competitive","He loses interest","He becomes collaborative","He gets angry"],"correct_answer":"He becomes collaborative"},{"question":"Who encourages the students at the library?","options":["Principal Grayson","Ethan\u2019s friends","Mrs. Finch","Lucy\u2019s parents"],"correct_answer":"Mrs. Finch"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_305_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_305_ch5_img1.png","plot_305_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":640,"reading_level":"Builder"}
