   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_305_15_18","title":"The Library Rivalry","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The library buzzed with a mixture of excitement and tension, as Lucy and Ethan\u2019s classes geared up for the second week of the reading contest. The once-cozy atmosphere was now electric, with students lingering in front of the shelves, whispering strategies and glancing at their rivals. Lucy, perched on a stool in the corner, clutched her well-worn copy of \u201cPride and Prejudice,\u201d deep in thought. She felt an unsettling mixture of determination and doubt. \n\nAcross the room, Ethan was rallying his friends, his voice booming louder than necessary. \u201cIf we read double what they do this week, we\u2019ll secure our win!\u201d he declared, flexing his muscles for emphasis, eliciting a chorus of cheers from his teammates. But within him, beneath the bravado, a worry festered. His friends didn\u2019t understand the allure of the written word, and he was painfully aware that his involvement in this contest was more about proving himself than actually enjoying the stories.\n\n\u201cMaybe we should work together,\u201d Lucy blurted out during lunch, surprising even herself. She had initially thought of Ethan as a distraction\u2014a jock who didn\u2019t understand her world\u2014but seeing him rally his friends stirred something within her. A sense of unity washed over her. \u201cWe could split our points if we join forces.\u201d\n\nEthan raised an eyebrow, skepticism etched on his face. \u201cAnd why would I team up with you? Your class is the competition.\u201d He glanced at his friends, who snickered at the idea of working with the \u201cbookworms.\u201d But Lucy stood her ground, her heart racing.\n\n\u201cBecause,\u201d she said, her voice steadier than she felt, \u201cthere\u2019s something we both want. The treasure in the hidden room.\u201d The words hung between them, filled with unspoken challenges. The prospect of finding that treasure was the one thing that made Ethan\u2019s competitive spirit flicker with intrigue.\n\n\u201cThat hidden room?\u201d Ethan crossed his arms, a smirk on his face. \u201cYou really think that\u2019s a good idea? What if we don\u2019t even know what\u2019s there?\u201d\n\n\u201cThen we\u2019ll find out together,\u201d Lucy replied, her mind racing with possibilities. \u201cWhat\u2019s the worst that can happen? We lose a few points?\u201d\n\nAs the week wore on, the rivalry intensified. Lucy found herself retreating into the library\u2019s depths, seeking refuge among the musty tomes, while Ethan\u2019s competitive streak grew fiercer. Whispers filled the halls about how he was pushing his classmates to read faster and more recklessly, even resorting to dubious tactics to undermine Lucy\u2019s class. The tension escalated as each class began to sabotage the other\u2019s efforts, trading pranks and insults.\n\nThen came the fateful Friday afternoon when Lucy and Ethan, each unaware of the other\u2019s plans, decided to explore the hidden room. As they cautiously opened the creaky door, an overwhelming scent of dust and old paper greeted them. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nThe room was adorned with forgotten treasures: stacks of vintage books, age-worn maps, and peculiar artifacts from a bygone era. Lucy\u2019s eyes sparkled with wonder, while Ethan\u2019s initial bravado faded into awe. \u201cThis\u2026 this is amazing,\u201d he murmured, stepping further inside, his competitive nature temporarily replaced by genuine curiosity.\n\nJust as they began to explore, a loud crash echoed from outside, pulling them back to reality. The door swung shut behind them, trapping them in darkness. Panic flared in Lucy\u2019s chest as she fumbled for the doorknob, but it wouldn\u2019t budge. \u201cEthan!\u201d she shouted, her voice laced with urgency. \u201cWhat are we going to do?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe have to find a way out,\u201d he replied, his tone shifting from skepticism to resolve. Together, they felt their way through the shadows, illuminating the room with the faint glow of their phones. In their frantic search, they discovered a dusty crate hidden in the corner, containing not only more books but a strange, ancient-looking chest. \n\n\u201cDo you really think that\u2019s it? The treasure?\u201d Ethan asked, his excitement battling with apprehension. They exchanged a glance, the weight of their rivalry sinking into the background for a moment. \n\nSuddenly, a loud noise echoed from outside the room\u2014a mix of laughter and shouts. \u201cThey\u2019re coming!\u201d Lucy gasped, urgency flooding her voice. \u201cWe have to open it before they find us!\u201d \n\nAs they pried open the heavy lid, the air crackled with anticipation. Inside lay not just books but something far more intriguing\u2014a collection of letters and journal entries revealing secrets of former students, hidden romances, and even betrayals that shaped their school\u2019s history. \n\n\u201cLucy, this could change everything,\u201d Ethan whispered, his eyes wide with realization. But just as they began to sift through the letters, the door burst open, flooding the room with light and a swarm of their classmates, who had been searching for them. \n\n\u201cLooks like the bookworms are up to something!\u201d a voice jeered. The moment hung in the air, tension boiling over into chaos. \n\n\u201cEthan, what are we going to do?\u201d Lucy\u2019s voice trembled as she clutched a letter in her hand, the weight of their discovery heavy upon them. \n\n\u201cStay quiet,\u201d he replied, the competitive edge returning. \u201cWe can use this to turn the contest around.\u201d The uncertainty loomed heavy, as he glanced at Lucy, both aware that their rivalry might just have taken a turn they never anticipated.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What discovery do Lucy and Ethan make in the hidden room?","options":["A collection of rare books","Old artifacts and letters","A treasure map","An ancient artifact"],"correct_answer":"Old artifacts and letters"},{"question":"What moment leads to the escalating tension between Lucy and Ethan's classes?","options":["The discovery of the hidden room","The race to read books","Pranks exchanged by classmates","A lunch conversation"],"correct_answer":"Pranks exchanged by classmates"},{"question":"How does Lucy initially perceive Ethan?","options":["As an ally","As a distraction","As a friend","As a mentor"],"correct_answer":"As a distraction"},{"question":"What does Ethan want to do with the letters they find?","options":["Turn them into a contest","Share them with their classmates","Use them to turn the contest around","Hide them from everyone"],"correct_answer":"Use them to turn the contest around"},{"question":"What is the immediate consequence of their discovery in the hidden room?","options":["They become friends","They get trapped inside","They win the contest","They find a treasure map"],"correct_answer":"They get trapped inside"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_305_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_305_ch3_img1.png","plot_305_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":888,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
