   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_301_7_10","title":"The Great Science Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"It was a bright Monday morning at Maplewood Middle School. Sam and Mia sat at their desks, buzzing with excitement. Today was the day of the big science fair announcement! \n\nMr. Thompson, their science teacher, walked into the classroom. He wore his usual lab coat and thick glasses. \"Good morning, everyone!\" he said. \"I have exciting news!\" \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe students leaned forward in their chairs. Sam's eyes sparkled with curiosity. Mia tapped her pencil on her desk, thinking. \n\n\"We will have a science fair,\" Mr. Thompson continued. \"The best project will win a trophy!\" \n\nSam jumped up. \"We have to win!\" he shouted. \"I have the best idea!\" \n\nMia smiled. \"What is it, Sam?\" \n\n\"I want to make a robot that can do our homework!\" he exclaimed. \n\nMia laughed. \"That sounds great, but we need a plan first!\" \n\nAs they discussed their project, other students whispered about their ideas. Jake from the next class boasted, \"Our project will be the best!\" \n\nMia frowned. \"We can't let them win!\" \n\nSam nodded. \"No way! We have to work harder!\" \n\nBut as the days passed, the competition grew fierce. Sam and Mia started to argue about everything. \"I want to build the robot!\" Sam yelled. \n\n\"No! We need to focus on the strategy!\" Mia replied, crossing her arms. \n\nThe tension in the classroom grew as both friends worked separately. \n\nOne day, Mia noticed something strange. Sam's robot parts were gone! \"Sam! Did you see my gears?\" she asked, panic rising in her voice. \n\n\"No!\" Sam said, looking worried. \n\nMia felt upset. \"Maybe someone took them!\" \n\nJust then, they spotted Jake smirking in the hallway. \n\n\"Look at them!\" he mocked. \"Your project is doomed!\" \n\nMia felt angry. \"He must have taken them!\" \n\nSam's face turned red. \"We need to find out!\" \n\nMia nodded. \"Yes! Together, we can do this!\" \n\nAs they ran down the hall, they realized they needed each other. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey made a pact to work together again. \"No more fighting,\" Sam said, smiling. \n\n\"Agreed!\" Mia replied. \n\nWith their friendship back on track, they were ready to face the science showdown. \n\nBut would it be enough to win?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mr. Thompson announce?","options":["A sports game","A science fair","A school trip","A holiday party"],"correct_answer":"A science fair"},{"question":"What does Sam want to build?","options":["A time machine","A robot for homework","A volcano","A spaceship"],"correct_answer":"A robot for homework"},{"question":"Who does Mia think might have taken her gears?","options":["Sam","Mr. Thompson","Jake","The principal"],"correct_answer":"Jake"},{"question":"What do Sam and Mia decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Fight more","Give up","Work together","Compete separately"],"correct_answer":"Work together"},{"question":"What is the main problem in this chapter?","options":["They can't find their project","They argue and fight","They don't have enough time","They don't have a teacher"],"correct_answer":"They argue and fight"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_301_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_301_ch1_img1.png","plot_301_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":358,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
