   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_301_7_10","title":"The Great Science Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: The Ticking Clock\n\nThe sun shone bright on Maplewood Middle School. Sam and Mia sat at their desks, surrounded by science posters and colorful charts. \u201cWe have to win this science fair!\u201d Sam said, his eyes sparkling with excitement. \n\nMia nodded, feeling determined. \u201cYes! Our project will be the best!\u201d \n\nJust then, Mr. Thompson walked in. He held a stack of papers. \u201cAlright, class, listen up! The science fair is in two weeks!\u201d He smiled. \u201cI expect your projects to be innovative and creative!\u201d\n\nThe room buzzed with chatter. Sam bounced in his seat. \u201cLet\u2019s start right now! We can build a volcano!\u201d \n\nMia frowned. \u201cA volcano? Everyone does that! How about an invisible ink experiment? That\u2019s clever!\u201d \n\nSam crossed his arms. \u201cBut I want to build something big!\u201d \n\n\u201cBig isn\u2019t always better, Sam.\u201d Mia sighed. \u201cWe need to work together.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a loud noise came from outside. They rushed to the window and saw their rivals, the kids from Mr. Lee\u2019s class, setting up a giant robot. \n\n\u201cOh no!\u201d Sam exclaimed. \u201cThey\u2019ll win if we don\u2019t hurry!\u201d \n\nMia\u2019s face turned serious. \u201cWe need a plan, fast!\u201d \n\nAs the bell rang, they gathered their supplies and rushed to the science lab. But when they got there, they discovered a big mess! \n\n\u201cWho did this?\u201d Mia shouted. Beakers were tipped over, and papers were scattered everywhere.\n\n\u201cI bet it was Mr. Lee\u2019s class!\u201d Sam said, fuming. \u201cThey\u2019re trying to sabotage us!\u201d \n\nMia felt worried. \u201cWe can\u2019t let this stop us. We need to fix this!\u201d \n\nJust then, Sam spotted an old box of supplies. \u201cLook!\u201d he shouted. \u201cWe can use these!\u201d \n\nMia smiled. \u201cGreat idea! Let\u2019s clean up and get to work!\u201d \n\nThey dived into the mess with enthusiasm. But as they worked, they kept bumping heads and arguing about ideas. \n\n\u201cYour idea is too silly!\u201d Sam complained. \n\n\u201cAnd yours is too boring!\u201d Mia shot back.\n\nFrustrated, they took a step back. \u201cLet\u2019s take a break,\u201d Mia said. \n\nThey sat down, breathing heavily. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean to fight,\u201d Sam admitted. \n\n\u201cMe neither,\u201d Mia said softly. \u201cWe need to remember we\u2019re friends.\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s start fresh,\u201d Sam suggested. \n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud crash outside. They jumped up to see what happened. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWhen they looked out the window, their hearts sank. The kids from Mr. Lee\u2019s class had accidentally knocked over their giant robot! Parts were everywhere. \n\nMia gasped. \u201cOh no! They need help!\u201d \n\n\u201cShould we help them?\u201d Sam asked cautiously. \n\nMia thought for a moment. \u201cYes! Let\u2019s show them we can work together.\u201d \n\nSam nodded. \u201cOkay! Let\u2019s go!\u201d \n\nAs they ran outside, they realized they had a new challenge ahead: teamwork, not just with each other, but with their rivals too.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the science fair project Sam wants to build?","options":["A giant robot","A volcano","Invisible ink","A time machine"],"correct_answer":"A volcano"},{"question":"How does Mia feel about the volcano idea?","options":["Excited","Angry","Frowned","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Frowned"},{"question":"What do Sam and Mia find when they get to the science lab?","options":["A clean lab","A big mess","Finished projects","A science fair judge"],"correct_answer":"A big mess"},{"question":"What do Sam and Mia decide to do when they see the kids from Mr. Lee\u2019s class need help?","options":["Ignore them","Help them","Compete harder","Go home"],"correct_answer":"Help them"},{"question":"What do Sam and Mia realize they need to do to succeed?","options":["Compete alone","Work together","Give up","Do nothing"],"correct_answer":"Work together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_301_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_301_ch2_img1.png","plot_301_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":472,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
