   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_301_7_10","title":"The Great Science Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Sam and Mia stood in the bustling hallway of Maplewood Middle School. The air buzzed with excitement. \u201cI can\u2019t believe the science fair is only a week away!\u201d Mia exclaimed, her eyes sparkling. \n\n\u201cI know! Our project has to be the best!\u201d Sam replied, clenching his fists with determination. \n\nAs they hurried to the science lab, they passed their rivals, the Thunderbolts. Their robotic arm project looked amazing. \u201cLook at that!\u201d Mia pointed. \u201cThey have wires and lights!\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, but we have the best idea! Our volcano will erupt with real lava!\u201d Sam boasted. Mia frowned. Their volcano project was good, but was it good enough? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey rushed into the lab. The room was filled with strange sounds and smells. Mr. Thompson, their science teacher, clapped his hands. \u201cAll right, class! Time for teamwork! Remember, sharing ideas is important!\u201d\n\n\u201cI know what we need!\u201d Sam shouted. \u201cLet\u2019s add glitter to the lava!\u201d\n\nMia raised an eyebrow. \u201cGlitter? Is that really a good idea?\u201d \n\n\u201cTrust me, it will look awesome!\u201d Sam insisted.\n\nAs the days went by, their excitement turned into tension. Mia started working late after school. She wanted to plan everything perfectly. But Sam was busy tinkering with the volcano. They barely talked.\n\nOne afternoon, Mia walked into the lab and gasped. Sam had replaced her carefully measured ingredients with extra baking soda! \u201cSam! What did you do?\u201d she yelled. \n\n\u201cI thought it would make it explode more!\u201d Sam replied defensively. \n\nMia crossed her arms. \u201cYou can\u2019t just change things without asking! This is my project too!\u201d \n\nJust then, the door swung open. It was Mr. Thompson. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on here?\u201d \n\n\u201cWe\u2019re not working together!\u201d Mia exclaimed. \u201cI\u2019m going to make my own project!\u201d \n\n\u201cYou can\u2019t just quit!\u201d Sam shouted. \n\nMr. Thompson sighed. \u201cTeamwork is key. You both need to talk it out.\u201d \n\nMia took a deep breath. \u201cFine. Let\u2019s make a decision together.\u201d\n\nThey both stared at the volcano. It felt like a giant mountain of trouble. Suddenly, the door creaked open again. It was one of the Thunderbolts, sneaking in! They had an idea that could ruin everything. \n\n\u201cWhat are you two up to?\u201d he asked with a smirk. \n\nMia and Sam exchanged worried glances. \u201cWe have to decide now!\u201d Sam whispered.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cShould we stick together or risk it all?\u201d Mia asked, her heart pounding. \n\nJust then, the Thunderbolt grinned wider. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s time for a sabotage.\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat do we do?\u201d Sam asked, panic in his voice.\n\n\u201cWe can\u2019t let them win!\u201d Mia replied, determination flashing in her eyes. \u201cLet\u2019s show them what we can do!\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What project are Sam and Mia working on?","options":["A robot","A volcano","A spaceship","A garden"],"correct_answer":"A volcano"},{"question":"What does Mr. Thompson want the class to focus on?","options":["Winning the competition","Teamwork","Individual projects","Making messes"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork"},{"question":"Why does Mia get upset with Sam?","options":["He wants to change the project","He is too quiet","He doesn\u2019t want to work at all","He forgot her birthday"],"correct_answer":"He wants to change the project"},{"question":"What do the Thunderbolts want to do?","options":["Help Sam and Mia","Sabotage their project","Join their team","Make a new project"],"correct_answer":"Sabotage their project"},{"question":"What do Sam and Mia decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Quit their project","Work together","Change their project completely","Give up"],"correct_answer":"Work together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_301_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_301_ch3_img1.png","plot_301_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":444,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
