   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_301_7_10","title":"The Great Science Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Chapter 4: Teamwork Makes the Dream Work\n\nSam and Mia stood in their classroom. The science fair was just a few days away. Their project, a rocket made from recycled materials, was almost ready. But something felt off. Tension hung in the air like a thick fog. \n\n\u201cDo you think we can win?\u201d Sam asked, his eyes shining with excitement. \n\n\u201cI hope so!\u201d Mia replied, tapping her pencil on the desk. \u201cBut we need to work together. No more arguing!\u201d \n\nJust then, Mr. Thompson walked in. He cleared his throat. \u201cClass, I want you all to remember that science is about teamwork. It\u2019s not just about winning.\u201d \n\nAs he spoke, Sam and Mia exchanged glances. They knew they had let competition get the better of them. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAfter school, they headed to the lab. Sam grabbed the cardboard and glue, while Mia pulled out their sketches. \u201cLet\u2019s make the rocket better!\u201d she said, her eyes sparkling with ideas.\n\nThey worked side by side, sharing ideas and laughter. Sam attached the fins, while Mia painted bright colors on the rocket. It began to look amazing! \n\nBut then, disaster struck. As Mia turned around, she noticed something strange. The rival class, led by Jake, was sneaking into their lab! \n\n\u201cHey! What are you doing?\u201d Mia shouted. \n\nJake grinned mischievously. \u201cJust checking out the competition!\u201d \n\nBefore they could react, Jake knocked over their rocket! Sam gasped. \u201cNo! Our project!\u201d \n\nMia felt a surge of anger. But instead of shouting, she took a deep breath. \u201cSam, we can fix it. We can make it even better.\u201d \n\nSam nodded, determination sparking in his eyes. \u201cYou\u2019re right! Let\u2019s work fast!\u201d \n\nThey quickly picked up the pieces. As they glued and painted, they felt a new spark of hope. Together, they were stronger. \n\n\u201cI can\u2019t believe they tried to sabotage us!\u201d Sam huffed. \n\n\u201cI know! But we won\u2019t let them win,\u201d Mia replied. \n\nJust then, the door swung open. Mr. Thompson entered. \u201cHow\u2019s it going, team?\u201d he asked, smiling. \n\n\u201cGreat!\u201d they cheered together. \n\nMia and Sam exchanged a look. Maybe they could really do this together after all. \n\nAs they put the finishing touches on their rocket, a sense of excitement filled the room. They had faced a challenge, but they were ready to rise above it. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s show everyone what we can do!\u201d Sam said. \n\n\u201cTogether!\u201d Mia added, grinning from ear to ear.\n\nThe countdown was on, and the science fair awaited them. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith renewed energy, they finished just in time, eager for their moment to shine.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam and Mia work on together?","options":["A book","A robot","A rocket","A game"],"correct_answer":"A rocket"},{"question":"Who tries to sabotage their project?","options":["Mr. Thompson","Mia","Jake","Sam"],"correct_answer":"Jake"},{"question":"What lesson do Sam and Mia learn?","options":["Winning is everything","Teamwork is important","Competition is bad","Science is easy"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork is important"},{"question":"How do Sam and Mia feel after fixing their rocket?","options":["Angry","Sad","Excited","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What does Mr. Thompson remind the class about?","options":["Teamwork","Winning","Science experiments","Homework"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_301_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_301_ch4_img1.png","plot_301_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":431,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
