   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_301_7_10","title":"The Great Science Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Sam and Mia stood in their classroom, looking at their rocket project. It was finally coming together! Mr. Thompson walked in with a big smile. \u201cAre you two ready for the science fair?\u201d\n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Sam shouted, pumping his fist in the air. Mia nodded, her eyes shining with excitement. \u201cWe just need to finalize the launch countdown.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they worked, the classroom buzzed with energy. But then, the door swung open. It was Jake from the rival class, grinning like a mischievous cat. \u201cYou think you can win? Our project will blow yours away!\u201d\n\nMia frowned. \u201cOur rocket is going to fly higher than yours!\u201d\n\nSam felt a spark of competition. \u201cLet\u2019s show them, Mia! We can make it the best!\u201d\n\nHowever, as they practiced, things began to change. Sam wanted to make the rocket faster. Mia wanted to make it safer. They argued more and more. \u201cWe should add more engines!\u201d Sam insisted. \u201cNo, we need to focus on stability!\u201d Mia replied sharply.\n\nOne afternoon, as they worked, Sam noticed something strange. Their rocket had been tampered with! \u201cSomeone messed with our project!\u201d he shouted. Mia gasped. \u201cDid Jake do this?\u201d\n\nThey decided to confront Jake. They marched to his classroom, determined to find out. But when they got there, Jake was shocked. \u201cI didn\u2019t do it! We\u2019re not the only class competing.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, they heard laughter. It was the class next door! They had been sneaking over to ruin projects. Sam and Mia exchanged glances. \u201cWe have to work together to stop them!\u201d Sam said.\n\n\u201cWe can build a better rocket, together,\u201d Mia added, a smile spreading across her face. They hurried back to their project, excited. They combined Sam\u2019s speed idea with Mia\u2019s safety plan.\n\nAs they worked side by side, the tension faded like a cloud. They laughed and shared ideas. \u201cWhat if we paint it bright orange?\u201d Mia suggested. \u201cAnd add sparkly stickers!\u201d Sam added, giggling.\n\nFinally, the rocket was ready. They stood back and admired their creation. It was colorful and powerful! \u201cWe did it!\u201d Mia cheered.\n\nThe day of the science fair arrived. The auditorium was filled with buzzing excitement. Sam and Mia took a deep breath and launched their rocket. It soared high into the air, leaving a sparkling trail behind.\n\nEveryone clapped and cheered! Mia and Sam exchanged proud smiles. They realized that working together made them stronger. \u201cWe make a great team!\u201d Sam exclaimed.\n\n\u201cBest friends forever?\u201d Mia asked, holding out her hand. Sam took it, grinning. \u201cForever!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Sam and Mia decide to do when they found out their rocket was tampered with?","options":["Confront Jake","Give up","Change their project","Ignore it"],"correct_answer":"Confront Jake"},{"question":"What colors did Sam and Mia decide for their rocket?","options":["Blue and green","Red and yellow","Bright orange with sparkly stickers","Black and white"],"correct_answer":"Bright orange with sparkly stickers"},{"question":"How did the students react when Sam and Mia launched their rocket?","options":["They were quiet","They clapped and cheered","They laughed","They ran away"],"correct_answer":"They clapped and cheered"},{"question":"What lesson did Sam and Mia learn in this chapter?","options":["Never give up","Teamwork is important","Competing is fun","Rockets should be fast"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork is important"},{"question":"What did Sam and Mia decide about their friendship at the end?","options":["They wanted to be rivals","They would stop working together","They would be best friends forever","They wanted to change classes"],"correct_answer":"They would be best friends forever"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_301_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_301_ch5_img1.png","plot_301_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":427,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
