   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_301_11_14","title":"The Great Science Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The bustling halls of Crestwood Middle School buzzed with excitement as students darted to and fro, their voices mingling like a chaotic orchestra. Posters for the annual Science Fair decorated the walls, each one more colorful than the last, promising experiments and discoveries that would leave everyone in awe. Sam, with his wild, curly hair that bounced as he walked, had a spring in his step. He was, after all, the self-proclaimed inventor of their class.\n\n\u201cDid you see the poster for the science fair?\u201d he exclaimed, practically bursting with energy. \u201cWe have to make the best project ever, Mia! Imagine if we win!\u201d\n\nMia, with her glasses sliding down her nose and a thoughtful expression, looked up from her notebook. \u201cI know, Sam! But let\u2019s think this through. We can\u2019t just wing it like last time.\u201d She flipped her hair back with determination. \u201cWe need a solid plan.\u201d\n\n\u201cSolid plan? Pfft! We need something spectacular! Something nobody has ever seen before!\u201d Sam waved his hands, envisioning towering robots and glowing potions. He was the mad scientist, and the thrill of invention coursed through him like electricity. \n\n\u201cSure, but we can\u2019t forget about the judges,\u201d Mia said, her voice steady as she flipped the page of her notebook. \u201cThey\u2019re looking for creativity and practicality, not just flash.\u201d\n\nUnder the bright fluorescent lights, they settled into their favorite corner of the library, surrounded by stacks of science books and posters flashing pictures of past winners. Sam sketched a design for a solar-powered car while Mia listed out materials they needed. The library felt alive, filled with the scent of old paper and possibilities.\n\nAs they worked, tension began to creep in. Sam wanted to go big and bold, while Mia sought precision and strategy. \u201cWhat about a volcano?\u201d Sam suggested, doodling lava flows that seemed to erupt off the page.\n\n\u201cClassic, but everyone does volcanoes. We need something new and exciting,\u201d Mia countered, her brow furrowing. \n\nJust then, Mr. Thompson, their science teacher, appeared at the table. \u201cWhat\u2019s all this commotion? Planning to take home the trophy, I see!\u201d He smiled, his glasses perched on the tip of his nose. \u201cRemember, teamwork is key. Don\u2019t lose sight of that.\u201d\n\nSam and Mia exchanged glances. \u201cRight, teamwork,\u201d they both mumbled, but the competitive spark in Sam\u2019s eyes was undeniable. They both wanted to win, and as the countdown to the science fair began, the stakes felt higher than ever.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe weeks flew by, filled with late-night brainstorming sessions and heated debates. One afternoon, Mia discovered a new scientific experiment online\u2014a way to create renewable energy using everyday materials. \u201cThis could be it, Sam! We could even show how it works!\u201d she said, her eyes lighting up with inspiration.\n\nBut when Sam heard \u201ceveryday materials,\u201d he frowned. \u201cThat sounds boring. We need something that will blow their minds!\u201d \n\nAs their disagreement escalated, the tension between them thickened. They started to work on separate ideas, unsure if their friendship could withstand the pressure. Could they really pull this off, or would the competition tear them apart?\n\nMia sighed, staring out of the library window at the cloudy sky. \u201cWe\u2019re meant to be a team, but we\u2019re just\u2026 not getting anywhere.\u201d \n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed through the library. Both turned to see a fellow classmate from the rival class, Derek, smirking as he knocked over a display of books. \u201cYou two think you can win?\u201d he taunted, eyes gleaming with mischief. \u201cYou might want to rethink your project. It\u2019s going to take more than a little brainstorming to beat us!\u201d\n\nAs Sam clenched his fists, the air crackled with unspoken challenges. Mia felt a knot tighten in her stomach. \u201cIt\u2019s just a friendly competition,\u201d she whispered, but even she wasn\u2019t sure of that anymore.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith the fair just days away, they had to decide: would they stick together and combine their ideas, or let their rivalry grow into something far more destructive? The clock was ticking, and the pressure mounted like the bubbles in a boiling pot. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s show them what we\u2019re made of,\u201d Sam finally said, determination in his voice. But would it be enough?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the main goal of Sam and Mia in this chapter?","options":["To complete their science project","To win the science fair","To help other students","To become best friends"],"correct_answer":"To win the science fair"},{"question":"What are Sam's main qualities as described in the chapter?","options":["He is calm and strategic","He is enthusiastic and inventive","He is shy and reserved","He is competitive and lazy"],"correct_answer":"He is enthusiastic and inventive"},{"question":"What does Mia emphasize is important for their project?","options":["Creativity","Flashiness","Strategy","Speed"],"correct_answer":"Strategy"},{"question":"Which classmate taunts Sam and Mia about their project?","options":["Mr. Thompson","Derek","Mia","Sam"],"correct_answer":"Derek"},{"question":"What is the main conflict introduced in this chapter?","options":["Sam and Mia\u2019s project is too simple","Derek sabotages their project","Sam and Mia have different ideas and are becoming competitive","Mr. Thompson is too strict"],"correct_answer":"Sam and Mia have different ideas and are becoming competitive"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_301_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_301_ch1_img1.png","plot_301_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":712,"reading_level":"Builder"}
