   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_301_11_14","title":"The Great Science Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the sun dipped below the horizon, painting the sky in shades of orange and purple, Sam and Mia hurried through the bustling hallways of Maplewood Middle School. The science fair was just days away, and the pressure was mounting. Their classmates buzzed with excitement, showcasing their projects as if they were prized possessions. Sam could hardly contain his enthusiasm, his eyes darting from one colorful display to another.\n\n\u201cLook at that! Jake and Lily\u2019s project on renewable energy is amazing!\u201d Sam exclaimed, pointing to a solar-powered model car that glimmered under the fluorescent lights. His mind raced with ideas about how they could outdo their rivals. \n\nMia narrowed her eyes, a frown creasing her forehead. \u201cIt\u2019s impressive, but we can\u2019t let them intimidate us. Remember our plan? We need to focus on our own project.\u201d\n\n\u201cI know, but what if we added something extra? Like an interactive element?\u201d Sam suggested, his imagination sparking like a live wire.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s not get distracted,\u201d Mia replied, squeezing her notebook tightly. \u201cWe need to finalize our hypothesis first. What if we\u2019re not even scientifically sound?\u201d\n\nBut just then, a commotion erupted from the other side of the hallway. Sam and Mia exchanged glances, curiosity piqued. They made their way over, only to find Jake and Lily surrounded by a crowd, boasting about their project and throwing in jabs about how Sam and Mia would never win.\n\n\u201cCan you believe it? They think they\u2019re so clever with their little gadgets,\u201d Sam muttered, fists clenched at his sides.\n\n\u201cWe can\u2019t let them get to us. Remember what Mr. Thompson said: \u2018Science is about collaboration and innovation,\u2019\u201d Mia reminded him, her voice steady but her eyes betraying her own frustration.\n\nAs the days passed, the tension in the air thickened like the fog rolling in after a storm. Sam and Mia spent hours in the science lab, but their once harmonious partnership began to fray. Competing ideas clashed like thunder and lightning. \n\n\u201cWhy don\u2019t we make the volcano erupt instead of just bubbling? It\u2019ll be more eye-catching!\u201d Sam suggested during one of their brainstorming sessions.\n\n\u201cBecause that\u2019s not what our experiment is about! We need to focus on the chemical reaction involved!\u201d Mia countered, exasperated.\n\nOn the day before the fair, an unexpected crisis struck. Sam arrived at the lab early, eager to see the final results of their hard work. But what he found made his heart sink. Their project was lying in shambles\u2014elements scattered across the table. The poster board was torn, and their carefully measured experiment components were missing!\n\n\u201cWhat happened?\u201d Sam gasped, panic flooding his voice. He glanced frantically around the room, but the shadows offered no answers.\n\n\u201cI didn\u2019t touch anything!\u201d Mia exclaimed as she rushed in, her eyes darting around in disbelief. \u201cThis looks like sabotage! We have to figure out who did this!\u201d\n\nSam swallowed hard, recalling the night before when he\u2019d seen Jake lurking near their lab. \u201cI think I might know who\u2019s behind this.\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s expression shifted from shock to determination. \u201cThen we need a plan. We can\u2019t let them win without a fight.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the realization hit them both like a jolt of electricity: they couldn\u2019t succeed alone. They needed to put aside their differences and work as a team, not just against their rivals, but for their friendship too.\n\nAs they gathered the scattered pieces, a sense of urgency filled the air. They had one last chance to prove themselves and restore their project. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s show them what we can do together,\u201d Mia said, her eyes bright with newfound resolve. \n\nJust as they began to piece everything back together, the door creaked open. A figure loomed in the doorway, silhouetted by the bright hall lights.\n\n\u201cGoing somewhere?\u201d Jake smirked, leaning casually against the frame, a glint of mischief in his eyes. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam and Mia find when they arrive at the lab?","options":["Their project is complete","Their project is missing","Their project is ruined","Their project is being stolen"],"correct_answer":"Their project is ruined"},{"question":"Who do Sam and Mia suspect might be behind the sabotage?","options":["Mr. Thompson","Lily","Jake","A classmate"],"correct_answer":"Jake"},{"question":"What do Mia and Sam realize they need to do to succeed?","options":["Work harder alone","Ignore their rivals","Compete against each other","Collaborate and work together"],"correct_answer":"Collaborate and work together"},{"question":"What is the main conflict in this chapter?","options":["Sam and Mia\u2019s friendship is tested","Jake and Lily win the fair","Sam and Mia lose their project","Sam and Mia sabotage Jake"],"correct_answer":"Sam and Mia\u2019s friendship is tested"},{"question":"What does Jake do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Helps Sam and Mia","Mocks them from the doorway","Gives them their project back","Leaves the lab"],"correct_answer":"Mocks them from the doorway"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_301_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_301_ch3_img1.png","plot_301_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":658,"reading_level":"Builder"}
