   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_302_7_10","title":"Art Class Antics","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"It was a bright Monday morning in Miss Patel's art class. Sunlight poured through the big windows, shining on the colorful paintings hanging on the walls. The air smelled like fresh paint and crayons. Lila, the leader of the Color Crushers, stood tall at the front of the room. She wore a bright red beret and a big smile.  \n\n\"Today is the day, everyone!\" Lila shouted, waving her paintbrush in the air. \"We will create the best mural ever!\"  \n\nThe Color Crushers cheered. They were ready to win the title of 'Art Champions'!  \n\nAcross the room, the Paint Defenders were busy whispering. Jake, their leader, had a sneaky plan. He adjusted his blue baseball cap and said, \"Let\u2019s show those Color Crushers what we can do!\"  \n\nSuddenly, Miss Patel clapped her hands. \"Alright, artists! You have one hour to create your masterpiece. Remember, teamwork is key!\"  \n\nAs the students got to work, Lila started to paint a huge sun. Bright yellows and oranges filled the canvas. \"This will be the brightest sun ever!\" she said.  \n\nMeanwhile, Jake's team was mixing dark colors. They wanted to paint a stormy sky. \"We must be the best,\" Jake whispered with a grin. \"But first, let\u2019s make sure the Color Crushers don't finish!\"  \n\nJust then, Lila spotted Jake sneaking behind her with a bucket of water. \"Hey!\" she shouted. \"What are you doing?\"  \n\nJake quickly held up his hands. \"Just testing my paintbrush! No sabotage here!\"  \n\nLila narrowed her eyes but kept painting. She had a secret plan, too. She knew the Paint Defenders would try to mess with their mural.  \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]  \n\nAs the minutes ticked by, both teams were working hard. Suddenly, splat! Jake accidentally knocked over a can of blue paint. It splashed right onto Lila's mural!  \n\n\"Oops!\" Jake gasped, eyes wide with shock.  \n\nLila\u2019s face turned bright red. \"What did you do?\" she cried.  \n\n\"Sorry! I didn\u2019t mean to!\" Jake stammered, looking worried.  \n\nThe tension in the room grew thick as the Color Crushers stared at the blue blob on their sun. Lila took a deep breath. \"We can fix this!\" she exclaimed. \"Let\u2019s turn it into a beautiful ocean!\"  \n\nLila's idea surprised everyone. Even Jake couldn\u2019t help but smile. Maybe this rivalry was not as important as being creative together.  \n\nBut just then, a loud crash came from the back of the room. Both teams turned in shock. What had happened now?  \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Who is the leader of the Color Crushers?","options":["Jake","Miss Patel","Lila","The Paint Defenders"],"correct_answer":"Lila"},{"question":"What did Jake accidentally spill on Lila's mural?","options":["Red paint","Blue paint","Green paint","Yellow paint"],"correct_answer":"Blue paint"},{"question":"What does Lila want to paint on her mural?","options":["A stormy sky","A bright sun","An ocean","A rainbow"],"correct_answer":"A bright sun"},{"question":"What does Miss Patel encourage her students to focus on?","options":["Cheating","Teamwork","Winning","Speed"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork"},{"question":"What happens after Jake spills the paint?","options":["The mural is ruined","They all start laughing","They work together to fix it","Miss Patel gets angry"],"correct_answer":"They work together to fix it"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_302_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_302_ch1_img1.png","plot_302_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":411,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
