   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_302_7_10","title":"Art Class Antics","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Chapter 3: The Big Mix-Up\n\nThe art room buzzed with excitement. Lila and Jake stood at opposite sides, eyes sharp and focused. The colorful walls were filled with vibrant paintings. Canvases leaned against each other like friends sharing secrets. Miss Patel smiled at her students, her curly hair bouncing as she walked around.\n\n\u201cToday, we start working on our mural!\u201d she announced. \u201cYou will be combined into one team!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat?!\u201d Lila shouted. \u201cI can\u2019t work with Jake!\u201d\n\nJake crossed his arms. \u201cAnd I can\u2019t work with Lila! She\u2019ll ruin everything!\u201d\n\nMiss Patel nodded, \u201cTrust me. You\u2019ll learn from each other. Now let\u2019s begin!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nLila glared at Jake while sorting through paints. \u201cYou\u2019re not going to mess this up, right?\u201d\n\nJake smirked. \u201cI could say the same to you. Don\u2019t spill paint everywhere!\u201d\n\nThey began their mural, each planning to outshine the other. Lila carefully painted bright flowers. Jake, next to her, painted a big shiny sun. But soon, a sneaky idea popped into Lila\u2019s mind. \n\n\"What if I mix Jake\u2019s colors when he\u2019s not looking?\" she thought. A little giggle escaped her lips.\n\nJake noticed her sneaky smile. \u201cWhat are you up to, Color Crusher?\u201d\n\n\u201cNothing!\u201d Lila replied, trying to hide her grin.\n\nSuddenly, there was a loud crash! Jake had accidentally knocked over a bucket of water. It splashed everywhere, mixing with their paints.\n\n\u201cNo!\u201d they both shouted as colors turned into a messy brown puddle.\n\nLila sighed, \u201cGreat. Now we have a muddy mess.\u201d\n\nJake frowned. \u201cThis is all your fault!\u201d\n\nLila pointed at him. \u201cYou knocked it over!\u201d\n\nJust then, Miss Patel clapped her hands. \u201cOkay, team! Let\u2019s clean this up together!\u201d\n\nAs they cleaned, they talked. Lila learned that Jake loved drawing superheroes. Jake found out that Lila loved painting sunsets. \n\n\u201cWhat if we combined our ideas?\u201d Lila suggested. \u201cA sunset with a superhero flying into it!\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah! That could work!\u201d Jake agreed, his eyes lighting up.\n\nThey smiled at each other for the first time. But just when they seemed to be getting along, a new problem appeared. \n\n\u201cLook!\u201d Lila gasped. \u201cWhere\u2019s the blue paint? It\u2019s gone!\u201d\n\nJake looked around, panic rising. \u201cDid someone take it?\u201d\n\nThey both turned to the other students, who were busy with their own projects. Was someone trying to sabotage their mural again?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWho would do that?\u201d Lila asked, her voice shaking.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Jake whispered, eyes darting around.\n\nWith a new mystery on their hands, they knew they had to work together. The rivalry was still there, but a spark of teamwork was beginning to grow.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s find that paint!\u201d Lila declared.\n\n\u201cTogether?\u201d Jake asked, raising an eyebrow.\n\n\u201cTogether!\u201d Lila nodded, feeling a little excited.\n\nWhat would they discover?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What new challenge do Lila and Jake face in this chapter?","options":["They have to paint a tree.","They lose their blue paint.","They work in different groups.","They run out of brushes."],"correct_answer":"They lose their blue paint."},{"question":"What does Lila suggest they paint together?","options":["A giant flower","A sunset with a superhero","A rainbow","A city skyline"],"correct_answer":"A sunset with a superhero"},{"question":"How does Jake feel when he accidentally knocks over the water bucket?","options":["Happy","Excited","Panicked","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Panicked"},{"question":"What do Lila and Jake find out about each other while cleaning?","options":["They both love superheroes.","They like the same colors.","They have different hobbies.","They are best friends."],"correct_answer":"They have different hobbies."},{"question":"What does Miss Patel tell the students to do when the mess happens?","options":["Clean up together","Leave the room","Start a new project","Take a break"],"correct_answer":"Clean up together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_302_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_302_ch3_img1.png","plot_302_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":469,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
