   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_302_7_10","title":"Art Class Antics","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The sun streamed through the big windows of Miss Patel's art classroom. Colorful paintings lined the walls, splashes of paint decorated the tables, and brushes lay ready for action. Today was an important day for the Color Crushers and the Paint Defenders.\n\n\u201cAlright, everyone! Today, we will create our mural together!\u201d Miss Patel clapped her hands. Lila and Jake exchanged worried glances. Could they really work together?\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s make this the best mural ever!\u201d Lila said, trying to sound excited. Jake nodded, but he seemed deep in thought.\n\n\u201cThis is a disaster! Where\u2019s the blue paint? We need it!\u201d Jake exclaimed. The Color Crushers looked at each other, puzzled.\n\n\u201cI thought we had plenty left!\u201d Lila said, looking at her team. They searched high and low. The big jars were empty. \n\nJust then, Mia, a quiet girl from the Color Crushers, stood up. \u201cI saw Max from the Paint Defenders with a blue paint jar earlier!\u201d she said. \n\n\u201cMax? He wouldn\u2019t take it!\u201d Jake replied, crossing his arms. \n\n\u201cBut what if we ask him nicely?\u201d Lila suggested. \u201cWe can\u2019t finish the mural without blue!\u201d\n\nJake sighed. \u201cFine. Let\u2019s go ask him.\u201d\n\nThe two teams met in the middle of the room. Lila cleared her throat. \u201cUh, Max? Do you have any blue paint? We\u2019re out,\u201d she said courageously.\n\nMax looked surprised. \u201cOh, I didn\u2019t take it! I thought you had enough!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, everyone began to laugh. The tension floated away like a cloud.\n\n\u201cI guess we should check together,\u201d Jake said, smiling. They all began to search as a team.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe teams worked side by side, and they found a hidden blue paint jar behind a big canvas. Cheers erupted! \n\n\u201cThis will be the best mural ever!\u201d Lila said.\n\nThey spread the blue paint across the mural, creating a bright sky. As they painted, they shared stories and ideas. The rivalry faded away as they laughed together.\n\n\u201cWe make a good team!\u201d Max declared, dipping his brush into more blue. \n\nAt the end of the class, the mural was almost finished. \u201cLook at what we\u2019ve done!\u201d Jake said, beaming. Lila smiled back.\n\n\u201cArt really does bring people together,\u201d Lila said softly. \n\nMiss Patel clapped her hands again. \u201cI\u2019m so proud of you all. You worked together beautifully!\u201d\n\nAs the bell rang, the teams felt lighter. They had learned that friendship can bloom from rivalry, just like colorful flowers in a garden.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cSee you all tomorrow for more art fun!\u201d Lila waved. Jake nodded, feeling excited for their next adventure.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Lila and Jake need to finish their mural?","options":["Red paint","Green paint","Yellow paint","Blue paint"],"correct_answer":"Blue paint"},{"question":"Who suggested asking Max for blue paint?","options":["Jake","Lila","Mia","Miss Patel"],"correct_answer":"Lila"},{"question":"What happens after the teams start working together?","options":["They laugh and share stories","They argue more","They stop painting","They leave the classroom"],"correct_answer":"They laugh and share stories"},{"question":"How does Miss Patel feel about the teams' work?","options":["She is angry","She is proud","She is confused","She is sad"],"correct_answer":"She is proud"},{"question":"What lesson do Lila and Jake learn?","options":["Art is boring","Rivalry is good","Friendship can grow from rivalry","Painting is hard"],"correct_answer":"Friendship can grow from rivalry"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_302_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_302_ch5_img1.png","plot_302_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":432,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
