   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_302_11_14","title":"Art Class Antics","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the bell rang, Lila felt a surge of excitement mixed with anxiety. Art class was her favorite place, a vibrant haven where colors danced and creativity flowed like water from a brush. Today, the air buzzed with anticipation and a hint of rivalry. The Color Crushers gathered around their easels, vibrant posters of their art theme pinned to the wall, while across the room, the Paint Defenders plotted their next move, whispering like shadows in the corners.\n\n\u201cAlright, team! We have just one week left until the big competition!\u201d Lila called out, her voice cutting through the murmur. \u201cLet\u2019s use today to finalize our ideas for the mural. Remember, it has to showcase unity and creativity!\u201d\n\nJake, the leader of the Paint Defenders, smirked from his side of the room as he leaned against the wall, arms crossed. \u201cUnity? Good luck with that, Lila! Can\u2019t wait to see your mural fall apart!\u201d His teammates burst into laughter, the sound sharp and mocking.\n\nLila clenched her fists, but instead of retaliating, she smiled. \u201cWe\u2019ll see about that, Jake. Just remember, in art, the best creations come from support, not sabotage!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe classroom was a canvas of chaos, with paint splatters on the floor and colorful canvases leaning against the walls, begging for attention. Lila\u2019s heart raced as she envisioned their mural\u2014a stunning landscape with vibrant flowers, symbolizing friendship. As she turned back to her team, her eyes sparkled with determination.\n\nHowever, as the days progressed, she noticed strange happenings in the classroom. Paint tubes were mysteriously mixed up, and more than once, a canvas went missing from their side. It was as if an invisible hand was toying with their creativity. \n\nOne afternoon, Lila found herself alone in the classroom, cleaning up the mess left behind by their last project. Suddenly, she noticed a crumpled note nestled under her easel. Curiously, she unfolded it. \u201cDon\u2019t trust anyone. The Paint Defenders are planning something big.\u201d Her heart raced. Who had written this? Was it a prank or a warning? \n\nJust then, the classroom door creaked open, and in walked Miss Patel, her eyes twinkling like the stars. \u201cLila, what have you discovered?\u201d she asked, glancing at the note in Lila\u2019s hand.\n\n\u201cMiss Patel, I found this note!\u201d Lila exclaimed, her voice trembling with a mix of fear and excitement. \u201cI think the Paint Defenders might be up to something.\u201d\n\nMiss Patel frowned, her brows knitting together. \u201cRivalries can bring out the worst in people, but they can also reveal their true colors. Are you prepared to face whatever challenge comes your way, Lila?\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from the Paint Defenders\u2019 side of the room. Lila and Miss Patel hurried to investigate. There, Jake stood, paint spilling from a toppled jar, his expression caught between surprise and guilt. \n\n\u201cOops! Clumsy me,\u201d he said, trying to brush off the incident, but Lila could see the flicker of challenge in his eyes. Tension hung in the air, thick and electric, as they stared at each other\u2014rivals once more, but perhaps, something more was brewing beneath the surface.\n\nLila took a deep breath, determination shining through her eyes. \u201cYou know, Jake, sabotage won\u2019t help either of us win. Let\u2019s see who can create something truly amazing instead.\u201d\n\nJake\u2019s smirk faltered for a moment, and Lila wondered if perhaps, just perhaps, the rivalry could spark something else entirely.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they returned to their easels, the room felt charged, filled with the promise of conflict and creativity. Lila knew that with every paint stroke, the real battle was just beginning, and the stakes had never been higher. \n\nWhat was Jake really planning? And could they somehow turn this rivalry into something that would bring them together instead?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What warning does Lila find in the classroom?","options":["The Paint Defenders plan to sabotage their mural","Miss Patel is hiding secrets","Their paint supplies are running low","Lila's team should give up"],"correct_answer":"The Paint Defenders plan to sabotage their mural"},{"question":"What theme does Lila want their mural to represent?","options":["Chaos","Unity","Competition","Rivalry"],"correct_answer":"Unity"},{"question":"How does Jake react when paint spills on the floor?","options":["He blames Lila","He laughs it off","He feels guilty","He ignores it"],"correct_answer":"He feels guilty"},{"question":"What does Lila hope to achieve by confronting Jake?","options":["To win at all costs","To form a friendship","To destroy the Paint Defenders","To give up art"],"correct_answer":"To form a friendship"},{"question":"What does Miss Patel encourage Lila to do?","options":["Ignore the rivalry","Embrace the challenge","Compete aggressively","Change teams"],"correct_answer":"Embrace the challenge"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_302_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_302_ch2_img1.png","plot_302_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":638,"reading_level":"Builder"}
