   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_302_11_14","title":"Art Class Antics","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the sun filtered through the colorful windows of Miss Patel's art classroom, the air buzzed with anticipation. Canvases were set up, splattered with brilliant hues, waiting to be transformed into a masterpiece. Lila stood at the front, her auburn hair bouncing with excitement as she rallied her team of Color Crushers. \"Alright, team! Today, we\u2019re going to show the Paint Defenders what real art looks like!\"\n\nHer enthusiasm was infectious, but tension simmered just beneath the surface. On the other side of the room, Jake, the strategic mastermind of the Paint Defenders, folded his arms and smirked. \u201cGood luck, Lila. You\u2019ll need it. We\u2019re not going to let you win that easily.\u201d \n\nThe rivalry was palpable, and Miss Patel sensed it too. She clapped her hands, drawing everyone\u2019s attention. \u201cRemember, art is about expression, not just competition. Let\u2019s see how you can channel your emotions into your work!\u201d \n\nJust as Lila was about to respond, a loud crash echoed through the room. Both groups turned as a paint bucket tumbled to the floor, its red contents spilling everywhere. The Color Crushers exchanged uneasy glances; it was too perfect to be an accident. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs the teams scrambled to clean up, Lila noticed something glinting in the paint. She carefully reached down and pulled out a crumpled piece of paper. Unfolding it revealed a series of strange symbols and a warning: \u201cBeware the colors of chaos.\u201d \n\n\u201cJake!\u201d Lila exclaimed, her heart racing. \u201cDid you send this?\u201d \n\nJake raised an eyebrow, the corners of his mouth twitching. \u201cMe? Why would I waste my time on notes when I have art to create?\u201d \n\nBut Lila wasn\u2019t convinced. \u201cYou think this is a joke? Someone is trying to mess with our mural!\u201d\n\nTension hung thick in the air as the teams worked on their projects. As they painted, the Color Crushers began to notice small sabotage attempts\u2014their brushes were missing, colors seemed to disappear. Lila felt her frustration boil as she faced her team. \u201cWe can\u2019t let them get away with this! We need a plan.\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud thud caught everyone off guard. Jake had knocked over one of their easels, and the Color Crushers gasped as the fragile canvas fell, splattering paint all around them. \u201cOops!\u201d Jake feigned innocence with a smirk.\n\n\u201cEnough!\u201d Lila shouted, her voice cracking with emotion. \u201cThis isn\u2019t just about winning anymore. It\u2019s about respect!\u201d\n\nThe room fell silent, and Miss Patel stepped in, her expression serious. \u201cArt is a reflection of who we are. If you go on like this, you\u2019ll ruin not just your artwork, but your friendships too.\u201d \n\nThe weight of her words hung heavy as Lila and Jake exchanged glances. Just then, the classroom door creaked open, revealing a figure cloaked in shadows. \u201cYou think it\u2019s just a game?\u201d the figure hissed, sending chills down their spines. \u201cYou have no idea what you\u2019re getting into.\u201d\n\nWith that, the figure slipped away, leaving the room in stunned silence as Lila and Jake stared at each other, fear creeping in. \n\nLila knew they had to confront whoever was behind this. \u201cThis competition just got serious,\u201d she muttered, determination igniting within her.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What strange occurrence happens in Miss Patel's art class?","options":["A paint bucket spills","A student leaves","The lights go out","A canvas is torn"],"correct_answer":"A paint bucket spills"},{"question":"What does Lila find that raises her suspicion about sabotage?","options":["A paintbrush","A warning note","A paint color","An art book"],"correct_answer":"A warning note"},{"question":"How does Miss Patel feel about the rivalry between the teams?","options":["Supportive","Indifferent","Concerned","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Concerned"},{"question":"What does Lila realize about the competition by the end of the chapter?","options":["It\u2019s just for fun","It\u2019s not about winning","It\u2019s too easy","It\u2019s boring"],"correct_answer":"It\u2019s not about winning"},{"question":"Who makes a mysterious appearance at the end of the chapter?","options":["A teacher","A parent","A shadowy figure","A former student"],"correct_answer":"A shadowy figure"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_302_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_302_ch3_img1.png","plot_302_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":541,"reading_level":"Builder"}
