   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_302_11_14","title":"Art Class Antics","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The vibrant art classroom buzzed with energy as the Color Crushers and Paint Defenders prepared for their next challenge. Lila stood at the front, her voice bubbling with excitement. \u201cToday, we\u2019re going to collaborate! Let\u2019s blend our styles and create something amazing!\u201d Her enthusiasm lit up the room, but Jake, arms crossed, raised an eyebrow.\n\n\u201cCollaborate? Isn\u2019t that just a sneaky way for the Color Crushers to steal our ideas?\u201d he shot back, a hint of mischief in his smile.\n\n\u201cMaybe if you weren\u2019t so busy being suspicious, you\u2019d see it\u2019s a chance to show we can be more than rivals,\u201d Lila replied, her competitive spirit flickering with a hint of hope.\n\nAs they began working, the air was thick with paint and possibility. Canvases stretched against easels, waiting to be filled with colors and creativity. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] The room was alive with splatters of blue, red, and yellow, as students moved about, exchanging brushes and laughter. \n\nBut just as they started mixing paints, a shadow flitted past the window, causing Lila to pause mid-stroke. \u201cDid you see that?\u201d she whispered, glancing at Jake. He frowned, his competitive facade cracking for a moment as curiosity sparked in his eyes.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s check it out,\u201d he suggested, and without waiting for an answer, he dashed outside, Lila hot on his heels.\n\nOutside, the hallway was deserted. Sunlight streamed through the tall windows, casting long shadows. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Lila asked, her heart racing. They tiptoed along the corridor, ears pricked for any sound. Suddenly, they spotted a figure at the end of the hall, dressed in a hooded sweatshirt, glancing back at them.\n\n\u201cHey!\u201d Jake called out, but the figure turned and sprinted away. \u201cWe have to follow!\u201d he urged, adrenaline surging through him.\n\nThey raced down the corridor, weaving around lockers and dodging students, their rivalry forgotten in the thrill of the chase. The shadowy figure led them into the art supply room, a place filled with rolling carts of paint and stacks of canvases. Just as they entered, the figure slipped behind a curtain. \n\n\u201cWho are you?\u201d Lila demanded, her voice filling the quiet room. But there was no answer, only the rustle of fabric. As they pulled the curtain aside, they found\u2026nothing. Just an empty corner, eerily quiet. \n\n\u201cThis is getting strange,\u201d Jake murmured, his brow furrowed. \u201cWe should focus on the project.\u201d\n\nLila nodded, though a shiver of unease ran down her spine. What was that figure up to? And were they really just going to ignore it? A new sense of determination blossomed within her. \u201cLet\u2019s channel this mystery into our art,\u201d she said, her voice firm. \u201cWe can spin this into something powerful\u2014something that represents our journey.\u201d\n\nJake looked thoughtful. \u201cYeah, like a mural that tells the story of our rivalry and how we\u2019ve grown.\u201d \n\nAs they returned to their canvases, the atmosphere shifted. Instead of sabotage, there was a sense of shared purpose. Brushes moved with newfound energy, and laughter echoed louder as colors fused together in harmony. For the first time, the divide between the teams felt less like a chasm and more like a bridge.\n\nWhen the bell rang, signaling the end of class, Lila felt a flutter of hope. Perhaps art could truly bring them together. She and Jake exchanged smiles, a mutual understanding blossoming. \u201cTomorrow, let\u2019s keep working on this,\u201d Jake suggested, and Lila nodded eagerly, feeling that maybe, just maybe, they were on the brink of something beautiful.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] \n\nAs they left the classroom, the mystery of the shadowy figure lingered in the air, but a new alliance had formed. The final showdown was still ahead, but now, the Color Crushers and Paint Defenders had a shared vision. \n\n\u201cArt can be the battlefield,\u201d Lila thought, \u201cbut it can also be the canvas for friendship.\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Lila and Jake decide to focus on during class?","options":["Sabotaging each other","Collaborating on a mural","Ignoring each other","Racing outside"],"correct_answer":"Collaborating on a mural"},{"question":"What mysterious event occurs in this chapter?","options":["Lila loses her paintbrush","A shadowy figure is spotted","Jake spills paint","Miss Patel gives a lecture"],"correct_answer":"A shadowy figure is spotted"},{"question":"How do Lila and Jake feel about their rivalry by the end of this chapter?","options":["More competitive","Less connected","More united","Completely indifferent"],"correct_answer":"More united"},{"question":"What does Lila suggest they do with their experience?","options":["Forget about it","Make it into art","Write a story","Draw individual pictures"],"correct_answer":"Make it into art"},{"question":"What does the classroom symbolize in the story?","options":["A battlefield","A tranquil garden","A library","A playground"],"correct_answer":"A battlefield"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_302_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_302_ch4_img1.png","plot_302_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":647,"reading_level":"Builder"}
