   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_7_10","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"It was a sunny morning at Maplewood Elementary. The school buzzed with excitement. It was almost time for the annual Mathletes Challenge! Students wore bright T-shirts with math symbols. In Room 12, two teams prepared for the big event.\n\nAlex, the captain of the Number Ninjas, adjusted his glasses. He wrote out a plan on the whiteboard. \u201cOkay, team! We need to practice our puzzles,\u201d he said, his voice full of energy. \u201cThe Equation Eagles are strong, but we can outsmart them!\u201d\n\nZoe, the leader of the Equation Eagles, was just down the hall. She had a fierce look on her face. \u201cWe can beat them if we work together!\u201d she declared to her team. They nodded, ready to tackle any challenge.\n\nAs Alex and Zoe practiced, Mr. Kim, their quirky math teacher, burst into the room. \u201cMathletes! Are you ready for a surprise?\u201d He grinned widely. His colorful bowtie bounced as he spoke. \u201cToday, I\u2019ll give you your first clue for the scavenger hunt!\u201d\n\nEveryone gasped. A scavenger hunt? That sounded fun! Mr. Kim held up a card with a riddle on it. \u201cTo start your hunt, solve this riddle: What has keys but can't open locks?\" \n\nThe room fell silent. Alex scratched his head. \u201cA piano!\u201d he shouted suddenly. Mr. Kim clapped his hands. \u201cCorrect! Your first clue is hidden near the music room!\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d Zoe shouted, excitement shining in her eyes. The two teams raced down the hall together, each wanting to find the clue first. But then, they bumped into each other! \n\n\u201cOh no!\u201d Alex said, laughing. \u201cLooks like we\u2019re in this together now!\u201d \n\n\u201cOkay, let\u2019s team up!\u201d Zoe agreed. \u201cBut only for this clue!\" \n\nAs the teams joined forces, they began to search. Where could the music room be? They scanned the corridor, looking for anything that might help. \n\nSuddenly, they spotted a shiny golden key on the music room door! \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAlex reached for it. \u201cThis must be a sign! We\u2019re on the right track!\u201d \n\nAs they moved closer, a loud sound echoed from behind them. It was a loud crash! \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Zoe shouted, her heart racing. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe teams turned to see a group of students spilling out of the art room. Paint and paper flew everywhere! \u201cOops! We were just trying to finish our project!\u201d one of them giggled. \n\nThe distraction was funny, but it reminded the teams they had a challenge to complete. \u201cLet\u2019s focus!\u201d Alex said, pointing to the music room again. \n\nThey needed to hurry if they wanted to be the first to solve the riddle and win the Mathletes Challenge!","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the name of Alex's team?","options":["Equation Eagles","Number Ninjas","Math Masters","Puzzle Pals"],"correct_answer":"Number Ninjas"},{"question":"What type of challenge are the students preparing for?","options":["Art contest","Mathletes Challenge","Science fair","Reading competition"],"correct_answer":"Mathletes Challenge"},{"question":"What does Mr. Kim give the students?","options":["A test","A riddle","A book","A game"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What do the Number Ninjas and Equation Eagles have to do together?","options":["Build a rocket","Solve a riddle","Paint a picture","Write a story"],"correct_answer":"Solve a riddle"},{"question":"What unexpected event happens while they are working on the clue?","options":["A bell rings","Paper spills out","A loud crash occurs","A fire alarm goes off"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash occurs"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch1_img1.png","plot_303_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":442,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
