   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_7_10","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Chapter 2: The Riddle Race\n\nThe sun peeked through the classroom windows. The Number Ninjas and Equation Eagles were buzzing with excitement. Alex stood at the front of the room, holding a shiny golden envelope. \n\n\u201cOkay, everyone! The first riddle is here!\u201d he shouted. Zoe rolled her eyes. \u201cLet\u2019s just hope it\u2019s not too hard.\u201d Mr. Kim clapped his hands. \n\n\u201cGather around! Let\u2019s read the riddle!\u201d He opened the envelope, and everyone leaned in. \n\n\u201cWhat has keys but can\u2019t open locks?\u201d read Mr. Kim. The classroom fell silent. \n\nZoe frowned. \u201cWhat could it be?\u201d \n\nAlex scratched his head. \u201cA piano?\u201d \n\nEveryone giggled, but Zoe shook her head. \u201cNo, think about it! It must be something else!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a hand shot up. It was Sammy, one of the Number Ninjas. \u201cI know! It\u2019s a keyboard!\u201d \n\n\u201cGreat job, Sammy!\u201d Alex cheered. \u201cLet\u2019s check the computer lab!\u201d \n\nThe two teams dashed down the hallway. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nIn the computer lab, they searched everywhere. Desks were pushed aside, and papers flew! \u201cLook!\u201d shouted Zoe. \u201cThere\u2019s a note on that computer!\u201d \n\nAlex rushed over and read aloud, \u201cTo find the next clue, you must solve this: What is half of 100?\u201d \n\nThe teams looked around at each other. \u201cFifty!\u201d yelled someone from the back. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go to the library!\u201d Zoe said, her eyes shining. \n\nBut just then, they heard a loud crash. A stack of books toppled over in the corner! Everyone gasped. Could it be the librarian? \n\n\u201cNo!\u201d shouted Alex. \u201cIt\u2019s just a pile of math books!\u201d \n\nZoe sighed with relief. \u201cPhew! But this is getting serious. We need to hurry!\u201d \n\nAs they raced to the library, they felt the pressure. Could they solve the next riddle before time ran out? \n\n\u201cWhat if we can\u2019t work together?\u201d Zoe whispered. \n\nAlex nodded. \u201cThen we\u2019ll lose for sure!\u201d \n\nFinally, they reached the library doors. The next challenge awaited them inside! \n\n\u201cReady?\u201d Alex asked, gathering everyone. \n\n\u201cReady!\u201d they all shouted. \n\nWith a deep breath, they entered the library, ready for whatever came next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the first riddle that Mr. Kim reads?","options":["What has keys but can\u2019t open locks?","What is half of 100?","What is a keyboard?","What does a piano do?"],"correct_answer":"What has keys but can\u2019t open locks?"},{"question":"Where do the teams decide to go after solving the first riddle?","options":["The music room","The playground","The library","The cafeteria"],"correct_answer":"The library"},{"question":"What does Sammy shout out as the answer to the riddle?","options":["A piano","A keyboard","A book","A computer"],"correct_answer":"A keyboard"},{"question":"What causes a moment of panic in the library?","options":["A librarian appears","Books fall over","Someone shouts","The lights go out"],"correct_answer":"Books fall over"},{"question":"What is the main theme of this chapter?","options":["Teamwork and problem-solving","Competition is bad","Math is boring","Library rules"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork and problem-solving"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch2_img1.png","plot_303_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":345,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
