   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_7_10","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Chapter 3: Puzzles and Panic\n\nThe sun shone brightly over Maplewood Elementary. Alex paced in front of the Number Ninjas. \"Okay, team! We need to solve Mr. Kim's next riddle fast!\" \n\nZoe stood across the playground with the Equation Eagles. She had her arms crossed. \"We won't let you win, Alex!\" \n\nMr. Kim clapped his hands. \"Listen up, Mathletes! Your next clue is hidden in the library! But beware! It\u2019s a tricky one!\" \n\nThe teams dashed toward the library. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nInside, rows of books towered like castles. Alex scanned the shelves. \u201cWhat could it be?\u201d \n\nZoe called out, \u201cLook for numbers or shapes!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed through the library. A shelf tipped over! Books flew everywhere! \n\n\u201cYikes! Watch out!\u201d shouted Alex. They all scrambled back. \n\n\u201cIs everyone okay?\u201d Zoe checked on her team. They nodded, wide-eyed and nervous. \n\nThen, a spark of excitement hit Alex. \u201cWait! The riddle!\u201d \n\nHe spotted a piece of paper sticking out from under a fallen book. \u201cLook! It says \u2018Find the square that\u2019s not a square!\u2019\u201d \n\nThe Number Ninjas and Equation Eagles froze. \u201cWhat does that mean?\u201d Zoe asked, scratching her head. \n\n\u201cI have an idea!\u201d Alex exclaimed. \u201cIt\u2019s not a number, but maybe a shape!\u201d \n\nJust then, the library door swung open. Mr. Kim peeked in, smiling. \u201cGreat teamwork, Mathletes! But the clock is ticking!\u201d \n\nZoe\u2019s eyes sparkled with determination. \u201cWe\u2019ll solve this together!\u201d \n\n\u201cTogether?\u201d Alex was taken aback. \n\n\u201cYes!\u201d Zoe nodded. \u201cBut we must hurry!\u201d \n\nThe two teams joined forces, searching for clues. They found a square table, a square picture frame, and even a square box. But nothing was right! \n\nPanic started to rise. What could it be? Suddenly, Alex shouted, \u201cWhat about a circle? A circle is a shape, but it\u2019s not a square!\u201d \n\n\u201cGood thinking!\u201d Zoe cheered. \n\nThey looked around and spotted a giant circle on the wall. \u201cThat\u2019s it!\u201d they cried. \n\nAs they raced to the wall, Alex felt a twist of fear. What if they weren\u2019t fast enough? \n\nThe clock was ticking down! What if they lost? \n\nWith one final push, they reached the giant circle. Together, they shouted, \u201cHere! The clue is here!\u201d \n\nBut just when they thought they had it, something unexpected happened. The wall began to shake! \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] \n\n\u201cUh-oh,\u201d Alex whispered. \u201cWhat now?\u201d \n\nThey stared at the wall, eyes wide, as it started to reveal a hidden door! \n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s behind there?\u201d Zoe asked, heart racing. \n\n\u201cOnly one way to find out!\u201d Alex replied, fingers shaking. \n\nShould they go through the door?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mr. Kim say was hidden in the library?","options":["A treasure","A riddle","A book","A map"],"correct_answer":"A riddle"},{"question":"What did Alex and Zoe find in the library?","options":["A circle","A triangle","A square","A rectangle"],"correct_answer":"A circle"},{"question":"What happened when the teams shouted about the clue?","options":["The library filled with books","The wall began to shake","The lights went out","A book flew away"],"correct_answer":"The wall began to shake"},{"question":"What did Alex feel when the clock was ticking down?","options":["Excited","Calm","Fearful","Bored"],"correct_answer":"Fearful"},{"question":"What decision did the teams have to make at the end of the chapter?","options":["To go home","To enter the hidden door","To leave the library","To split up"],"correct_answer":"To enter the hidden door"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch3_img1.png","plot_303_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":428,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
