   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_7_10","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the Number Ninjas and Equation Eagles stood in front of the mysterious door, Alex whispered, \u201cShould we go in?\u201d Zoe nodded, biting her lip. \u201cWe have to find the next clue!\u201d\n\nWith a deep breath, they pushed the door open. It creaked like a sleepy bear. Inside, the room was filled with colorful shapes hanging from the ceiling. Bright triangles, squares, and circles danced in the light. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLook at all these shapes!\u201d Alex exclaimed, his eyes sparkling. \u201cThey must be part of the riddle!\u201d\n\n\u201cI see a triangle with a number!\u201d Zoe pointed. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s a clue!\u201d \n\nThe triangle had a big, bold \u20183\u2019 on it. \u201cThree sides, three corners,\u201d Alex said. \u201cWe need to find three clues in this room!\u201d\n\nThe two teams began searching. The Number Ninjas checked under tables while the Equation Eagles looked on the walls. Suddenly, Zoe shouted, \u201cI found something!\u201d\n\nShe held up a paper with a riddle written on it. It read:\n\n\u201cI am a shape with four sides, \nBut I\u2019m not a person who hides. \nCount my corners, one, two, three, four, \nSolve this riddle, then I\u2019ll show you more!\u201d\n\nAlex waved his hand. \u201cA square! We need to find a square!\u201d \n\nThe teams rushed to the corner. There, they found a big square drawn on the floor. Inside it was a box! \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s open it!\u201d Zoe said, her hands trembling with excitement. \n\nWith a little teamwork, they pulled the box open. Inside, they found a shiny trophy and a new riddle! \u201cThis is it! This is what we need!\u201d Alex cheered.\n\nBut then, the teams looked at each other. Would they still be rivals? Or could they work together? \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s read the next riddle together,\u201d Zoe suggested. \n\nAlex smiled. \u201cTogether! The more brains, the better!\u201d\n\nThey gathered in a circle, ready to solve the next challenge, feeling hopeful about what was to come.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What shape do Alex and Zoe find in the room?","options":["Circle","Triangle","Square","Rectangle"],"correct_answer":"Square"},{"question":"What do the teams find inside the box?","options":["A map","A trophy","A book","A gold coin"],"correct_answer":"A trophy"},{"question":"What do the teams decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Leave the room","Read the next riddle together","Go back to the library","Compete against each other"],"correct_answer":"Read the next riddle together"},{"question":"Who leads the Number Ninjas?","options":["Zoe","Mr. Kim","Alex","The Principal"],"correct_answer":"Alex"},{"question":"What was the first number mentioned in the chapter?","options":["1","2","3","4"],"correct_answer":"3"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch4_img1.png","plot_303_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":321,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
