   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_7_10","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"Chapter 5: The Power of Teamwork\n\nInside the hidden room, the walls were covered in colorful shapes. Alex stared at a giant triangle. \u201cLook at that!\u201d he said, pointing. \u201cIt looks like it\u2019s waiting for us to solve its riddle!\u201d\n\nZoe nodded, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cLet\u2019s read the next clue. It must be here somewhere!\u201d They searched around the room, looking under shapes and behind boxes. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, they found a small envelope stuck to the wall. Zoe pulled it off. \u201cIt says, \u2018To unlock your next clue, work together with a shape that\u2019s true!\u2019\u201d\n\nAlex grinned. \u201cWe have to find another shape!\u201d He ran to the square. \u201cWhat do you think it means?\u201d\n\n\u201cI think we have to combine our teams\u2019 ideas,\u201d Zoe said. \u201cThe Number Ninjas and the Equation Eagles must work together!\u201d\n\nAs both teams gathered, Mr. Kim peeked through the doorway. \u201cI see you\u2019ve found the next challenge! Remember, teamwork is the key to success! Use math to solve this puzzle.\u201d\n\nThe teams looked at each other, unsure. \u201cCan we really work together?\u201d Alex asked.\n\nZoe smiled. \u201cYes, let\u2019s try! All good ideas are welcome.\u201d The teams shared their thoughts. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s use patterns!\u201d suggested Mia, a member of the Equation Eagles. \u201cPatterns help us understand shapes better!\u201d\n\n\u201cGood idea!\u201d shouted Jake from the Number Ninjas. \u201cWe can start with the triangle and square!\u201d\n\nTogether, they began to draw in the air with their fingers. They drew lines connecting the shapes. It was fun! The shapes seemed to dance with joy. Suddenly, the square glowed brightly.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe glow revealed a new door! \u201cLook!\u201d Zoe pointed. \u201cWe did it together!\u201d\n\n\u201cYes!\u201d cheered Alex. \u201cNow we have a new path! But we must all go through it as one team.\u201d\n\nWith smiles on their faces, both teams linked arms. They stepped through the door, ready for their next challenge. \n\n\u201cMath is more than just numbers,\u201d Zoe declared. \u201cIt\u2019s about teamwork and friendship!\u201d\n\nAs they walked through, they knew they were closer to the Mathletes Challenge.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the next clue about?","options":["Working alone","Working together with a shape","Finding a trophy","Counting numbers"],"correct_answer":"Working together with a shape"},{"question":"What shape did they first notice in the room?","options":["Circle","Square","Triangle","Rectangle"],"correct_answer":"Triangle"},{"question":"What does Mr. Kim remind them about?","options":["To have fun","To work as individuals","To remember teamwork","To solve math alone"],"correct_answer":"To remember teamwork"},{"question":"What do Mia and Jake suggest to help solve the puzzle?","options":["Using colors","Drawing in the air","Using patterns","Counting shapes"],"correct_answer":"Using patterns"},{"question":"What do Alex and Zoe realize about math?","options":["It's boring","It's just numbers","It\u2019s about teamwork and friendship","It's too hard"],"correct_answer":"It\u2019s about teamwork and friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch5_img1.png","plot_303_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":347,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
