   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_11_14","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the morning bell rang through the halls of Maplewood Middle School, the excitement for the Mathletes Challenge pulsed like a drumbeat. Alex Chen, captain of the Number Ninjas, stood in the common area, his heart racing with anticipation. He scanned the room, spotting his teammates: Maya, the quick-witted problem solver, and Jonah, the math whiz who could calculate faster than a calculator. Together, they were ready to tackle any challenge.\n\n\u201cOkay, Ninjas,\u201d Alex said, his voice steady, \u201cremember the scavenger hunt component is brand-new this year. We need to stay sharp and focused.\u201d He could see Maya fiddling with her pencil, and Jonah was bouncing on his heels, a mix of anxiety and excitement swirling around him.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nJust then, Zoe Martinez entered the common area, her presence commanding attention. The leader of the Equation Eagles had a reputation for being fierce and determined, and Alex knew this year would be no different. She marched over with her teammates, a frown creasing her brow. \u201cI hope you\u2019re all ready for the hunt. We\u2019re going to crush it!\u201d she declared, her confidence filling the air.\n\n\u201cBring it on, Zoe!\u201d Alex shot back, a competitive spark igniting between them. Friends? Rivals? It was hard to tell sometimes. The two teams stood opposite each other, the tension palpable. The next few weeks would push them to their limits.\n\nAs the day unfolded, Mr. Kim, their eccentric math teacher, burst into the room with a wild grin. \u201cListen up, Mathletes! It\u2019s time to kick off the scavenger hunt!\u201d He waved a colorful envelope like a magician revealing a trick. \u201cYou\u2019ll need to solve riddles that will lead you to clues hidden around the school. The first team to solve all the riddles and find the final clue wins!\u201d\n\nThe announcement sent a wave of energy through the room. Alex felt his heart leap. This was it\u2014a chance to prove the Number Ninjas were the best. \n\n\u201cYour first riddle is this,\u201d Mr. Kim continued, his voice dipping into an amused whisper. \u201cFind me where the science experiments bubble and fizz, but beware the creature who makes a buzz!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat does that even mean?\u201d Jonah mumbled, scratching his head. \n\n\u201cWhere could there be bubbling experiments?\u201d Maya pondered, her brow furrowing. \u201cThe science lab?\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, but the creature that buzzes\u2026?\u201d Alex\u2019s mind raced. Then it hit him. \u201cThe beehive! It\u2019s in the garden next to the lab. Let\u2019s go!\u201d\n\nThe trio sprinted down the hall, dodging other students along the way. As they arrived at the science lab, they pushed the door open, revealing bubbling beakers and scattered papers. \u201cQuick! Look for anything that isn\u2019t a regular experiment,\u201d Alex urged. \n\nSuddenly, they heard a loud crash. Maya gasped, her eyes widening. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d\n\nWith a heavy heart, Alex stepped cautiously toward the sound. It had come from the art room across the hall. He exchanged a worried glance with his teammates. \u201cLet\u2019s check it out. It might lead us to the next clue.\u201d\n\nAs they entered the art room, they were met with a disaster. Paint splatters covered the floor, and a sculpture had toppled over. But what really caught their attention was a crumpled piece of paper lying near it. Alex picked it up and read aloud, \u201cSolve this to find your next clue: I am more than a number, I can change the game. In me, you\u2019ll find angles, but no two are the same.\u201d\n\n\u201cTriangles!\u201d Jonah shouted, his face lighting up with excitement. \u201cIt must be the geometry classroom!\u201d\n\nAs they raced toward their next destination, Alex couldn\u2019t help but feel a shift in the air. Would they be able to work together as a team, or would their rivalry with the Equation Eagles turn this scavenger hunt into mayhem? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut before they could reach the geometry classroom, they heard footsteps behind them. The Equation Eagles were closing in, and Zoe\u2019s voice cut through the air like a sharpened pencil. \u201cYou\u2019re not getting ahead of us!\u201d\n\nThe competition was on, and the stakes had never been higher.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the first riddle given by Mr. Kim?","options":["Find me where the science experiments bubble and fizz, but beware the creature who makes a buzz!","I am more than a number, I can change the game. In me, you'll find angles, but no two are the same.","Solve this to find your next clue: I have four sides and equal angles.","I am the root of all equations."],"correct_answer":"Find me where the science experiments bubble and fizz, but beware the creature who makes a buzz!"},{"question":"What does Alex think the first clue relates to?","options":["The library","The science lab","The gym","The playground"],"correct_answer":"The science lab"},{"question":"What do the Number Ninjas find when they enter the art room?","options":["A hidden treasure","A crumpled piece of paper","A glowing orb","A painting competition"],"correct_answer":"A crumpled piece of paper"},{"question":"What shape does Jonah identify as part of the next clue?","options":["Circle","Square","Triangle","Rectangle"],"correct_answer":"Triangle"},{"question":"What happens as the Number Ninjas rush toward the geometry classroom?","options":["They find a secret passage.","The Equation Eagles catch up to them.","They celebrate their victory.","They lose their way."],"correct_answer":"The Equation Eagles catch up to them."}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch2_img1.png","plot_303_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":692,"reading_level":"Builder"}
