   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_11_14","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the sun rose over Maplewood Middle School, a sense of excitement hung in the air like the smell of freshly baked cookies. The hallways buzzed with whispers and laughter, students racing to their classes, each one eager for what the day would bring. Alex adjusted his glasses, peering over at Zoe, who stood with her team near the big bulletin board.\n\n\u201cToday\u2019s the day, Ninjas!\u201d Alex called out, rallying his teammates with a fist pump. \u201cLet\u2019s show those Eagles what we\u2019ve got!\u201d\n\nZoe caught his eye, a determined glimmer sparking in hers. \u201cYou\u2019re going down, Ninjas,\u201d she challenged, a confident smile playing on her lips. The rivalry was electric, but beneath the banter, a tension brewed\u2014one that neither team fully understood yet.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWith Mr. Kim\u2019s riddles echoing in their minds, the teams gathered in the math lab where the first clue awaited. \u201cAlright, everyone!\u201d Mr. Kim clapped his hands, the enthusiasm spilling from him like a fountain of energy. \u201cYour first riddle is hidden right here. Solve it to find your next location!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat if we can\u2019t?\u201d someone from the back whispered, a hint of worry in their voice.\n\n\u201cThen teamwork is your best ally!\u201d Mr. Kim said, eyes twinkling behind his glasses. \u201cRemember, math is not just about numbers; it\u2019s about relationships too!\u201d\n\nAs the teams huddled together, Alex and Zoe exchanged glances. Their rivalry was thick like fog, but somewhere in that mist, they both knew they needed to solve the riddle quickly. The riddle was tricky, weaving numbers and words into an intricate tapestry. \u201cI\u2019m sure it has something to do with the cafeteria\u2019s lunch menu,\u201d Zoe suggested, her brow furrowing in concentration.\n\n\u201cOr the library\u2019s section on geometry,\u201d Alex countered, scratching his head as he paced the room. The clock ticked audibly, each second feeling like an eternity. Suddenly, a loud crash echoed from the hallway, pulling everyone\u2019s attention. They rushed outside, hearts pounding.\n\nIn the center of the chaos lay a broken box, the contents scattered like confetti. Puzzled, they approached cautiously. Inside the box, they discovered a series of math cards, each one bearing a different riddle. But more importantly, one card hinted at a secret: \u201cSeek the place where the numbers dance.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat does that even mean?\u201d one of the Ninjas mumbled, frustrated.\n\nZoe\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cThe gym! It has the dance floor\u2014the place where we practice for our Mathletes Challenge! It has to be there!\u201d\n\nWith a shared urgency, both teams began sprinting toward the gym, adrenaline coursing through their veins. But as they rounded the corner, they skidded to a halt, surprise etched on their faces. Their rival teams were not only racing against each other but against time. \n\nJust as they reached the gym doors, the lights flickered ominously. Suddenly, the doors swung shut with a loud bang, sealing them inside. \u201cWhat just happened?\u201d Alex exclaimed, panic rising in his chest.\n\nZoe turned to Alex, determination reflected in her eyes. \u201cWe can\u2019t let this stop us. We have to work together!\u201d\n\n\u201cBut why would we trust each other?\u201d Alex shot back, frustration bubbling over. \u201cWe\u2019re rivals!\u201d\n\n\u201cBecause right now, we\u2019re trapped!\u201d Zoe shouted back, her voice rising above the panic. \u201cIf we don\u2019t solve this together, we\u2019ll miss out on the Mathletes Challenge completely!\u201d\n\nThe air thickened with tension as the realization dawned on them\u2014this wasn\u2019t just a competition anymore; it was a fight for survival in the world of math. Would they be able to set aside their rivalry and unite to escape?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they formed an impromptu team, Alex couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that the scavenger hunt had just become something much more complex. Secrets loomed in the shadows, and the clock was ticking down. Would teamwork be the key to unlocking both their freedom and their friendship?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Alex and Zoe need to do to escape the gym?","options":["Solve riddles together","Fight against each other","Leave through the doors","Wait for help"],"correct_answer":"Solve riddles together"},{"question":"What does Mr. Kim emphasize is important in math?","options":["Numbers only","Relationships","Winning","Practicing alone"],"correct_answer":"Relationships"},{"question":"What major event happens when the teams reach the gym?","options":["They find a hidden treasure","The lights flicker and doors close","They win the challenge","They start dancing"],"correct_answer":"The lights flicker and doors close"},{"question":"How does Alex initially feel about teaming up with Zoe?","options":["Excited","Frustrated","Indifferent","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Frustrated"},{"question":"What is the main conflict in this chapter?","options":["Finding the next location","Being trapped in the gym","Winning the Mathletes Challenge","Solving equations"],"correct_answer":"Being trapped in the gym"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch3_img1.png","plot_303_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":657,"reading_level":"Builder"}
