   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_11_14","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"As the sunlight streamed through the high gymnasium windows, illuminating the scattered remnants of the previous challenge, Alex took a deep breath. The Number Ninjas and the Equation Eagles were finally free\u2014at least, for the moment. They stood in a circle, eyes darting between each other like wary animals sizing up a strange newcomer. \n\n\u201cOkay, what\u2019s next?\u201d Zoe asked, her voice steady despite the tension in the room. She brushed a strand of hair behind her ear, her determination evident. \n\n\u201cI think we should collaborate,\u201d Alex suggested, surprising even himself. \u201cWe\u2019re better together, right?\u201d \n\nZoe raised an eyebrow. \u201cYou really think our teams can work like that? You\u2019re still wearing your \u2018Number Ninjas\u2019 cape, and I\u2019m not ready to swap my \u2018Equation Eagles\u2019 feathers for anything.\u201d\n\nAlex chuckled, the hint of a smile breaking through the tension. \u201cMaybe we just need a new name\u2014Team Mathastic?\u201d \n\nBefore Zoe could respond, Mr. Kim burst through the gym doors, his wild hair bouncing as he entered. \u201cFantastic! I didn\u2019t know you were starting a band! Do you need a manager?\u201d The quirky math teacher beamed at them, clearly misinterpreting the situation. \n\n\u201cNot quite, Mr. Kim,\u201d Zoe replied, shaking her head but smiling. \u201cWe\u2019re just trying to figure out our next move.\u201d \n\n\u201cAh, I see!\u201d Mr. Kim clapped his hands together enthusiastically. \u201cYour next challenge is hidden in plain sight! Solve this riddle: \u2018I am a three-digit number. My tens digit is five more than my ones digit. My hundreds digit is eight less than my tens digit. What number am I?\u2019\u201d \n\nBoth teams groaned in unison, but Alex could see Zoe\u2019s mind racing. \u201cWe could break it down,\u201d she proposed, her voice more confident now. \u201cLet\u2019s write it out.\u201d \n\nThe teams quickly grabbed the nearest piece of paper, and under Alex\u2019s leadership, they worked together to solve the riddle. As they scribbled equations and eliminated possibilities, the atmosphere began to shift from rivalry to cooperation. \n\nSuddenly, an explosion of laughter erupted from the corner of the gym. A couple of students from the bleachers had overheard their brainstorming. \u201cIf you can\u2019t even solve that, how are you going to win the Mathletes Challenge?\u201d one teased. \n\nThe comment stung, but for some reason, it lit a fire under Alex. \u201cWe can\u2019t let them win,\u201d he said, determination creeping back into his voice. \u201cLet\u2019s nail this riddle and show everyone what we can do together.\u201d \n\nWith renewed energy, they poured over the numbers until finally, Zoe exclaimed, \u201cWait! The answer has to be\u2026 194!\u201d \n\nThe room fell silent for a split second, and then Mr. Kim clapped his hands with delight. \u201cCorrect! Now, follow the clue to the Math Hall!\u201d \n\nAs they raced out of the gym, adrenaline surged through Alex\u2019s veins. Could this be the turning point in their journey? Maybe they really could work together. \n\nJust as they reached the hallway, Zoe turned to Alex, a newfound respect shining in her eyes. \u201cYou know, maybe you\u2019re not just a Number Ninja after all.\u201d \n\nAlex grinned, feeling a sense of hope bloom in his chest. \u201cAnd maybe you\u2019re more than just an Equation Eagle.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe scene captures the vibrant energy of the gym, with sunlight pouring through the windows, illuminating Alex and Zoe in the center, surrounded by team members displaying a mix of determination and apprehension.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nA dynamic visual of the group huddled together, scribbling equations on a piece of paper, with expressions of focus and excitement. Mr. Kim is seen in the background, clapping enthusiastically, while students in the bleachers giggle, creating a sense of tension and camaraderie.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What riddle does Mr. Kim give the teams?","options":["What is a three-digit number?","What is the capital of France?","What is 2+2?","How many sides does a square have?"],"correct_answer":"What is a three-digit number?"},{"question":"What is the answer to the riddle?","options":["192","194","198","200"],"correct_answer":"194"},{"question":"How do Alex and Zoe's feelings towards each other change in this chapter?","options":["They become more competitive.","They start to respect each other.","They ignore each other.","They become best friends immediately."],"correct_answer":"They start to respect each other."},{"question":"What motivates Alex to push for teamwork?","options":["A book he read.","A comment from other students.","His favorite subject is art.","He is afraid of losing."],"correct_answer":"A comment from other students."},{"question":"Where do the teams need to go after solving the riddle?","options":["The Math Hall","The Library","The Playground","The Cafeteria"],"correct_answer":"The Math Hall"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch4_img1.png","plot_303_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":616,"reading_level":"Builder"}
