   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_11_14","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the sun poured through the tall windows of Maplewood Middle School, Alex and Zoe sat at a table in the bustling cafeteria, a pile of math books and colorful sticky notes scattered between them. The air buzzed with chatter and laughter, but their focus was unwavering. They had no idea what awaited them in the next puzzle.\n\n\"Okay, we need to break this down,\" Alex said, adjusting his glasses as he studied the latest riddle Mr. Kim had left for them. \u201cIt says here, \u2018To find the key to the next door, solve for X before you score.\u2019 What do you think it means?\u201d\n\nZoe tapped her chin, deep in thought. \u201cMaybe X is a number we need to find in the school? But what door are they talking about?\u201d\n\nJust then, the cafeteria door swung open, and Mr. Kim, with his signature bow tie and wild hair, strolled in. His eyes sparkled with excitement. \u201cAh, my mathletes! Remember, teamwork is the essence of winning!\u201d He tossed a piece of chalk in the air, catching it with a flourish. \u201cTogether, you can solve any riddle!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWith renewed determination, Alex and Zoe grabbed their notebooks and made their way to the math lab, where the walls were plastered with colorful equations and math-themed decorations. They flipped through the pages of the riddle book, brainstorming possible solutions. The lab was often quiet, but now it felt electric with their focused energy.\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed from the hallway. They both jumped, glancing at each other with wide eyes. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Zoe whispered, her heart racing.\n\nAlex shrugged but couldn\u2019t shake the sense of unease creeping up his spine. \u201cLet\u2019s check it out.\u201d\n\nAs they stepped into the hallway, they found several students gathered around a toppled science project, a model of the solar system. Among the onlookers, a few members of the Equation Eagles were whispering and pointing, clearly involved in some kind of discussion.\n\n\u201cDid you hear? There\u2019s a riddle hidden somewhere near the science lab!\u201d one of them exclaimed dramatically.\n\nZoe exchanged a look with Alex. \u201cWe should go see if we can find it.\u201d\n\nThey hurried to the science lab, where the room buzzed with activity. It was filled with colorful charts, bubbling beakers, and even a small planetarium. In the corner, Zoe spotted a glimmering object half-hidden behind a stack of textbooks.\n\n\u201cLook!\u201d She dashed over, her heart racing with excitement. As she picked it up, she realized it was a small key\u2014shiny and ornate, with the letter \u2018X\u2019 engraved on it.\n\n\u201cThis must be what we need!\u201d she exclaimed, holding the key up triumphantly. But as they turned around, they found the Equation Eagles approaching, led by Zoe\u2019s rival, Lila.\n\n\u201cNice find, but we saw it first!\u201d Lila sneered, crossing her arms. \u201cYou\u2019re not getting ahead of us in the competition.\u201d\n\nAlex stepped forward, surprising himself with his confidence. \u201cWhat if we join forces? We could work together to solve the next riddle; it could help both our teams!\u201d\n\nZoe nodded, her determination shining through. \u201cLet\u2019s put our rivalry aside for now. We\u2019re all in this together, right?\u201d\n\nThe Equation Eagles exchanged glances, and to Alex\u2019s surprise, Lila raised an eyebrow, considering the offer. \u201cAlright, let\u2019s see what you\u2019ve got, Number Ninjas.\u201d\n\nAs they began to collaborate, the tension in the room shifted. Alex felt a sense of camaraderie blossom, like a flower breaking through the cracks of concrete. They started discussing strategies, and the energy became contagious. Together, they worked through clues, laughter bubbling up as they shared their knowledge.\n\nThe riddle, it turned out, was not just about math; it was about understanding each other, learning from one another. In that moment, Alex knew they were on the brink of something greater than just winning a competition\u2014they were building connections that would last beyond the Mathletes Challenge.\n\nAs they finalized their plans and everyone rushed to grab their materials, Alex felt a warmth spread through him. Maybe math wasn\u2019t just about equations; it could also unlock friendships.\n\nAs they stepped out of the science lab into the hallway, filled with laughter and chatter, Alex looked at Zoe and said, \u201cWe did it! And you know what? I think we\u2019re going to make the best Mathletes team ever\u2014even if we\u2019re rivals.\u201d \n\nWith a smile, Zoe replied, \u201cYeah. Together, we can solve anything.\u201d","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Alex and Zoe discover in the science lab?","options":["A math book","A shiny key","A math puzzle","A model of the solar system"],"correct_answer":"A shiny key"},{"question":"What does Mr. Kim emphasize about winning?","options":["Individual talent","Teamwork","Competition","Speed"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork"},{"question":"How do Alex and Zoe feel about working with the Equation Eagles?","options":["Excited","Angry","Indifferent","Frustrated"],"correct_answer":"Excited"},{"question":"What is the main theme highlighted in this chapter?","options":["Winning is everything","Math is the only important subject","Teamwork can lead to friendship","Rivalries should be avoided"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork can lead to friendship"},{"question":"What does Alex realize about math by the end of the chapter?","options":["It\u2019s all about winning","It can unlock friendships","It\u2019s too difficult","It\u2019s not important"],"correct_answer":"It can unlock friendships"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch5_img1.png","plot_303_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":747,"reading_level":"Builder"}
