   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_303_15_18","title":"Mathletes in Mayhem","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The first light of dawn crept through the windows of Crestwood High, illuminating the math department hallway, which was decorated with posters of famous mathematicians. Alex sat at the edge of his desk, tapping his pencil against a stack of textbooks, his mind racing. The scavenger hunt had only just begun, and already the stakes felt higher than ever. \n\n\u201cCome on, Alex, focus!\u201d his teammate, Mia, urged, her fingers tangled in a mass of curly hair as she reviewed the first clue again. \u201cThe sooner we crack this, the sooner we can beat Zoe and her team.\u201d\n\n\u201cRight, but this clue is a riddle!\u201d Alex exclaimed, his frustration bubbling. \u201cWhat does 'the sum of the angles greater than the smallest' even mean?\u201d \n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s math themed? Like, every triangle has angles that sum up to\u2026 oh!\u201d Mia\u2019s eyes sparkled with realization. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s in the geometry room? You know, the one with the triangles on the wall?\u201d \n\n\u201cGood thinking!\u201d Alex grinned, his confidence reigniting. Before they rushed out, he glanced at the row of lockers lining the hall, and his gaze caught on Zoe, the Equation Eagles\u2019 captain, who was huddled with her team. Her serious expression mirrored his own determination. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe Number Ninjas dashed through the buzzing hallways, their footsteps echoing against the linoleum as they approached the geometry room. The door was slightly ajar, and Alex pushed it open, revealing a world of colorful shapes and diagrams. Yet, as they stepped inside, an unsettling silence enveloped them.\n\n\u201cWhere are the clues?\u201d Mia whispered, her eyes darting around the room.\n\nJust then, a loud crash erupted from behind the blackboard, drawing their attention. Alex and Mia exchanged glances, adrenaline coursing through their veins. \u201cStay here,\u201d Alex instructed, inching toward the sound. \n\nAs he peered behind the board, he found a math-themed treasure chest, covered in chalk dust. \u201cMia, you have to see this!\u201d\n\nBefore they could open it, the door swung open. Zoe stood in the doorway, flanked by her teammates, a smug smile gracing her lips. \u201cWell, well, if it isn\u2019t the Number Ninjas. You found my hiding spot.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat? This was here first!\u201d Mia protested, stepping forward. \n\nZoe raised an eyebrow, her confidence unwavering. \u201cI\u2019m sure it was meant for the winners of the last challenge. Don\u2019t worry, it\u2019s not too late for you to join us. Maybe we could work together?\u201d\n\n\u201cAre you serious?\u201d Alex scoffed, crossing his arms. \u201cWe\u2019re not teaming up with you just because you can\u2019t solve your own riddles.\u201d\n\nZoe sighed dramatically, her eyes narrowing. \u201cMaybe you\u2019ll regret that when you can\u2019t solve this one. But suit yourselves.\u201d With a flick of her hair, she turned and beckoned her team to follow. \n\nAs they exited the room, Alex felt a pang of doubt. \u201cWhat if we need to work together? We can\u2019t let our pride stand in the way of winning.\u201d\n\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry, Alex. We\u2019ve got this,\u201d Mia assured him, yet her voice lacked the conviction he hoped for. The tension hung thick in the air, a palpable reminder of the rivalry that threatened to tear them apart.\n\nDetermined to prove themselves, the Number Ninjas opened the treasure chest, revealing a series of intricate puzzles that glimmered like jewels in the sunlight filtering through the windows. \u201cThese look tough,\u201d Alex murmured, anxiety prickling at the back of his mind.\n\n\u201cWe can do it, but let\u2019s split up,\u201d Mia suggested, her eyes alight with challenge. \u201cI\u2019ll take the tangents, you handle the sequences.\u201d\n\nJust as they began to work, a loud clatter echoed down the hallway. They exchanged startled looks, and before they could react, a paper airplane swooped into the room, gliding gracefully before landing at their feet. Alex picked it up, unfolding it to reveal a new challenge written in bold letters: \u201cTo find the key, you must first solve the mystery of the locker that holds history.\u201d \n\n\u201cThat\u2019s it! The history locker!\u201d Mia exclaimed, her face lighting up with recognition. \u201cIt\u2019s the one with the old trophies and yearbooks!\u201d\n\n\u201cBut it could be anywhere,\u201d Alex said, a new wave of panic washing over him. \u201cWhat if it\u2019s locked?\u201d\n\n\u201cThen we\u2019ll find a way in,\u201d Mia replied, her determination infectious. \n\nWith a shared nod, they bolted out of the geometry room, ready to tackle whatever lay ahead, unaware of the twists that awaited them in their quest for the Mathletes Challenge glory. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs they raced down the corridor, the tension mounted like the notes in a symphony, harmonizing rivalry with the possibility of collaboration\u2014a melody that echoed in the hallways of Crestwood High, setting the stage for a confrontation that would change everything.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the first clue that the Number Ninjas try to solve?","options":["A riddle about angles","A math equation","A geography question","A science puzzle"],"correct_answer":"A riddle about angles"},{"question":"What does Zoe suggest to Alex and Mia?","options":["To join forces","To quit the competition","To leave the room","To solve it alone"],"correct_answer":"To join forces"},{"question":"What do Alex and Mia find inside the treasure chest?","options":["Math puzzles","Old trophies","A map","A notebook"],"correct_answer":"Math puzzles"},{"question":"Which locker is referenced in the new challenge?","options":["The geometry locker","The history locker","The science locker","The art locker"],"correct_answer":"The history locker"},{"question":"What emotion propels Alex as he navigates the scavenger hunt?","options":["Indifference","Confidence","Panic","Fear"],"correct_answer":"Panic"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_303_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_303_ch2_img1.png","plot_303_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":798,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
