   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_304_7_10","title":"Debate Duel: Words at War","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The school auditorium buzzed with excitement. Students filled the seats, all waiting for the big debate. Posters hung on the walls, showing the names of the two finalists: Leo and Yasmin. \n\nLeo sat in the front row, bouncing in his seat. He liked to win. \"I\u2019m going to crush Yasmin today!\" he whispered to his friend Mia. She giggled and nodded. \n\nYasmin sat a few seats away, calm and collected. She adjusted her glasses and smiled. \u201cIt\u2019s not just about winning,\u201d she said softly. \u201cIt\u2019s about making good points.\u201d \n\nMrs. Harper, the debate coach, stood at the front of the stage. She smiled warmly at the crowd. \u201cWelcome to the Great Debate Duel!\u201d she announced. The cheers grew louder. \u201cToday, we will see who can argue the best!\u201d\n\nLeo\u2019s heart raced. He loved the challenge. He was a passionate speaker, and he thrived on competition. But Yasmin was not afraid. She was a logical thinker who valued fairness. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cToday\u2019s topic is about helping others!\u201d Mrs. Harper continued. \u201cLeo will argue for, and Yasmin will argue against.\u201d \n\nLeo jumped up, his voice booming. \u201cHelping others is great! We should all do it!\u201d The crowd clapped loudly. \n\nYasmin stood up next, raising her hands for silence. \u201cHelping others is important, but we must also think about ourselves. Balance is key!\u201d \n\nLeo frowned. \"Balance? But what if we wait too long to help?\u201d \n\nThe crowd gasped. It was a good point! \n\nYasmin felt a tingle of excitement. \u201cHelp is good, but too much at once can be overwhelming.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe debate heated up. The audience cheered for both of them. Leo and Yasmin were locked in a battle of words. But as they spoke, both began to feel something new: respect for each other's ideas.\n\nMrs. Harper smiled. \u201cRemember, it\u2019s not just about winning!\u201d \n\nBoth Leo and Yasmin took a deep breath. They knew this duel was about more than just victory. It was a chance to understand. \n\nAs the debate continued, could they find a way to work together?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the topic of the debate?","options":["Helping others","Playing sports","Reading books","Science experiments"],"correct_answer":"Helping others"},{"question":"Who is the debate coach?","options":["Mr. Smith","Mrs. Harper","Ms. Brown","Dr. Lee"],"correct_answer":"Mrs. Harper"},{"question":"What does Leo love to do?","options":["Win debates","Play video games","Paint pictures","Read stories"],"correct_answer":"Win debates"},{"question":"How does Yasmin feel about helping others?","options":["It's bad","It's good","It's overwhelming","It's boring"],"correct_answer":"It's overwhelming"},{"question":"What do both characters learn during the debate?","options":["To argue better","To ignore each other","To respect each other's ideas","To speak louder"],"correct_answer":"To respect each other's ideas"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_304_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_304_ch1_img1.png","plot_304_ch1_img2.png"]},"word_count":346,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
