   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_304_7_10","title":"Debate Duel: Words at War","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Classroom Rivalries","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The auditorium buzzed with excitement. Students filled the seats, waving colorful banners for their favorite debaters. Leo and Yasmin stood at the front, ready for their final debate.\n\n\"Remember,\" Mrs. Harper said. \"Listen to each other and respect different views.\" She smiled, her glasses glinting under the bright lights. \n\nLeo took a deep breath. \"Today, we will debate the topic of teamwork! I believe teamwork means you must always win together!\" \n\nYasmin crossed her arms. \"But what if you listen to each other first? That is real teamwork.\"\n\nThe audience cheered. Leo felt a little nervous. He glanced at Yasmin, who looked calm and focused. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s show everyone what we\u2019ve learned!\u201d Yasmin said, her voice ringing clear. Leo nodded. \n\nAs they started debating, Leo remembered their teamwork during the power outage. He thought about how they had worked together instead of just competing. \"Okay, Yasmin,\" Leo said. \"I understand your points. Teamwork is about more than just winning.\" \n\nYasmin smiled, surprised. \"And I see your point too! Winning can be fun, but listening is part of it!\" \n\nThe crowd went wild. Students clapped and shouted their support. It felt electric. \n\nLeo and Yasmin began to share their ideas, weaving them together like a beautiful tapestry. Leo spoke passionately. \u201cTeamwork helps us lift each other up.\u201d \n\nYasmin added, \u201cAnd it allows us to grow together, learning from mistakes!\u201d \n\nThen came a moment of silence. The audience was listening intently. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s remember,\u201d Yasmin said. \u201cIt\u2019s not just about who is right. It\u2019s about understanding each other!\u201d \n\nLeo nodded, feeling proud. \u201cYes! We can win together by respecting everyone\u2019s ideas!\u201d \n\nThe debate ended with a roar of applause. Mrs. Harper beamed at both of them. \u201cYou both have shown what true teamwork looks like. Well done!\u201d \n\nLeo and Yasmin exchanged smiles. They realized they were not just rivals anymore but teammates. \n\n\u201cNow, let\u2019s celebrate!\u201d Yasmin said, grinning widely.\n\n\u201cTogether!\u201d Leo cheered, already thinking about the fun they would have.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the main topic of Leo and Yasmin's debate?","options":["Friendship","Teamwork","Competition","Listening"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork"},{"question":"What does Leo realize during the debate?","options":["Winning is everything","Listening is important","Debating is boring","He doesn't like Yasmin"],"correct_answer":"Listening is important"},{"question":"How does the audience react to the debate?","options":["They are silent","They cheer loudly","They leave early","They argue with each other"],"correct_answer":"They cheer loudly"},{"question":"What lesson do Leo and Yasmin learn by the end of the chapter?","options":["Winning is the only goal","They should never speak again","Understanding each other is key","Debates are not fun"],"correct_answer":"Understanding each other is key"},{"question":"What do Leo and Yasmin plan to do after the debate?","options":["Argue more","Celebrate together","Stop being friends","Leave the school"],"correct_answer":"Celebrate together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_304_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_304_ch5_img1.png","plot_304_ch5_img2.png"]},"word_count":337,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
