   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_296_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Friendship Bracelet","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"Mia sat at her desk, staring at the ancient friendship bracelet resting on her palm. It shimmered with a strange light, as if it held a secret just waiting to be unlocked. She had spent a sleepless night thinking about what it could mean for her and Zoe\u2019s friendship. Would it strengthen their bond, or was it a curse? The attic had felt like a treasure trove of mysteries, but this bracelet was different. It felt alive, pulsating with energy, and Mia couldn\u2019t shake the unease creeping up her spine.\n\n\u201cHey, Mia! Ready for school?\u201d Zoe\u2019s voice broke through her thoughts. Mia looked up to see her best friend at the door, her hair tied in a messy bun and a paint-splattered backpack slung over one shoulder. Zoe\u2019s sunny disposition always brightened Mia\u2019s day, but today, with the bracelet\u2019s shadow looming over her mind, she felt a knot in her stomach. \n\n\u201cYeah, just... give me a minute,\u201d Mia said, slipping the bracelet into her pocket, hoping it would disappear from her thoughts, at least for a little while.\n\nThe school day began like any other, filled with laughter and the clatter of lockers. Yet, as the hours passed, Mia noticed odd things happening. During lunch, her soda suddenly fizzed over, spraying her shirt, which made Zoe laugh. \u201cYou and that soda have a real rivalry going on!\u201d she teased, but Mia felt her smile falter. It was as if the bracelet was causing chaos around her, testing her patience.\n\nBy the time they reached art class, Mia\u2019s heart raced. She could have sworn she heard whispers in the air, soft and playful, like a gentle breeze. Zoe was busy chatting with their classmates, sketching in her notebook, completely unaware. Mia looked down at her own piece of art, half-finished and uninspired, feeling a sudden wave of jealousy wash over her. \n\nAs she glanced towards Zoe, a flicker of movement caught her eye. The bracelet glimmered, and Mia heard a soft giggle. It was as if it was laughing at her, teasing her insecurities. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, Mia?\u201d Zoe asked, noticing her friend\u2019s distracted state.\n\n\u201cNothing, just... I don\u2019t know,\u201d Mia replied, frustration bubbling inside her. \u201cDo you ever think there\u2019s something between us? Like something that isn\u2019t right?\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Zoe\u2019s eyebrows knitted together, confusion etched on her face.\n\nBefore Mia could reply, something crashed in the art room, sending paintbrushes flying. The classroom erupted in chaos as students ducked for cover. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Mia shouted, her heart pounding. \n\nZoe looked back at her, eyes wide with fear. \u201cI think it\u2019s that bracelet!\u201d \n\nMia felt a chill run down her spine, realizing that the bracelet might be more than just a simple piece of jewelry\u2014it could be the source of the trouble. \u201cWe have to figure this out, Zoe. But how?\u201d\n\nJust then, a gust of wind swept through the room, swirling papers and paintbrushes around them. The whispers grew louder, mixing with the chaos. Mia and Zoe exchanged terrified glances. They needed to confront whatever they had awakened.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go back to the attic after school. We need answers,\u201d Mia suggested, determination building inside her.\n\n\u201cOkay, but we need to be careful,\u201d Zoe said, her voice steadier. \u201cI don\u2019t want this to ruin our friendship.\u201d \n\nAs the bell rang, signaling the end of class, Mia felt a weight on her heart. The secrets of the bracelet loomed over them like a dark cloud, but she couldn\u2019t let it tear her and Zoe apart. They stepped into the hallway, ready to face whatever the attic held for them next.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1: A bright and bustling middle school hallway filled with students laughing and chatting. In the foreground, Mia stands looking thoughtfully at the ancient friendship bracelet in her hand, her expression a mix of curiosity and concern. Zoe, with her paint-splattered backpack, is playfully gesturing towards Mia, trying to lighten the mood.]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2: The art classroom in disarray, with papers flying through the air and students ducking. In the center, Mia and Zoe stand back-to-back, their faces a mix of fear and determination as they prepare to confront the chaos around them, with the mysterious bracelet faintly glowing in Mia's pocket.]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mia find in the attic?","options":["A dusty old book","An ancient friendship bracelet","A mysterious mirror","A secret map"],"correct_answer":"An ancient friendship bracelet"},{"question":"How does Mia feel during art class?","options":["Excited","Jealous","Bored","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Jealous"},{"question":"What strange event occurs during art class?","options":["A fire alarm goes off","A gust of wind causes chaos","Someone wins an award","A student falls down"],"correct_answer":"A gust of wind causes chaos"},{"question":"What do Mia and Zoe decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Go home","Return to the attic","Tell their teacher","Ignore the bracelet"],"correct_answer":"Return to the attic"},{"question":"What emotion does Mia struggle with throughout this chapter?","options":["Happiness","Fear","Jealousy","Excitement"],"correct_answer":"Jealousy"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_296_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_296_ch2_img1.png","plot_296_ch2_img2.png"]},"word_count":726,"reading_level":"Builder"}
