   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_296_11_14","title":"The Secret of the Friendship Bracelet","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Mia and Zoe crept back up to the attic, the wooden stairs creaking beneath their weight like the groans of ancient secrets. Dust danced in the rays of sunlight filtering through the small window, illuminating forgotten treasures scattered around them. As Mia stepped into the attic, her heart raced. The thrill of discovery mingled with dread\u2014what would they find this time?\n\n\u201cMia, are you sure about this?\u201d Zoe asked, her voice trembling slightly. She was clutching her sketchbook tightly, the pages filled with drawings inspired by their previous adventure. \u201cWhat if something else happens?\u201d\n\n\u201cWe won\u2019t know unless we look,\u201d Mia replied, determination sparking in her brown eyes. She glanced at the small, velvet pouch that now felt like a weight in her pocket. The friendship bracelet had become a symbol of their bond, but it was also a gateway to chaos.\n\nThey approached the dusty, old trunk where they\u2019d found the bracelet. Mia\u2019s fingers brushed over the worn wood, feeling its history pulse beneath her fingertips. \u201cLet\u2019s see if we can find anything else that might explain this,\u201d she suggested. \n\nJust then, a gust of wind swooshed through the attic, causing the loose papers to swirl around them. \u201cDid you feel that?\u201d Zoe gasped, her eyes wide, reflecting both excitement and fear. \n\nMia nodded, her heart pounding. \u201cIt\u2019s just the wind. Let\u2019s keep looking!\u201d She opened the trunk, revealing an array of forgotten items: a cracked mirror, an old-fashioned diary, and a set of beautifully crafted quills. \n\n\u201cLook at this!\u201d Zoe exclaimed, picking up the diary. \u201cIt might have belonged to the original owner of the bracelet.\u201d \n\nAs Zoe flipped through the pages, a shadow flickered across the walls, causing them both to freeze. \u201cDid you see that?\u201d Mia whispered, her voice barely audible.\n\nBefore Zoe could answer, the attic door slammed shut with a thunderous bang, sending a shiver down Mia\u2019s spine. \u201cThis isn\u2019t funny!\u201d she shouted, panic rising. \n\nSuddenly, a soft, mischievous laugh echoed around them. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t have disturbed my treasures,\u201d a voice chimed, light and airy, like the tinkling of wind chimes. \n\nZoe\u2019s eyes darted around the attic. \u201cWho\u2019s there?\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2019m just a friendly ghost,\u201d the voice teased. \u201cBut your bracelet? It\u2019s not just a piece of jewelry. It\u2019s a key\u2014a key to understanding each other!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d Mia demanded, her heart racing. \u201cWhat\u2019s the secret?\u201d \n\nThe ghost floated into view, a shimmering figure with a playful grin. \u201cTo unlock its power, you must understand what truly binds your friendship. Jealousy can break even the strongest of bonds.\u201d \n\nZoe and Mia exchanged glances, the weight of the ghost's words pressing heavily on their shoulders. The air thickened with tension as the ghost continued, \u201cYou have until the next full moon. If you don\u2019t resolve your issues, the bracelet will choose one of you to keep forever, while the other will be left behind in the shadows.\u201d\n\nMia felt a knot tighten in her stomach. \u201cWe can\u2019t let that happen! We\u2019ll figure this out!\u201d \n\nBut deep down, doubt crept in, whispering fears that had been growing since they discovered the bracelet. Could their friendship withstand the truth? \n\nAs the ghost giggled and faded, the attic door creaked open, leaving Mia and Zoe alone, their thoughts swirling like the dust motes in the sunbeam. \n\n\u201cWe need to talk,\u201d Zoe said, her voice shaking.\n\nMia nodded, the realization hitting her like a storm. They had to confront their feelings, or risk losing each other forever.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What item do Mia and Zoe find in the attic?","options":["An ancient map","A friendship bracelet","A golden crown","A treasure chest"],"correct_answer":"A friendship bracelet"},{"question":"What happens when they return to the attic?","options":["The door locks them in","They find more treasures","They meet a ghost","They find a secret passage"],"correct_answer":"They meet a ghost"},{"question":"What warning does the ghost give them?","options":["They will lose their friendship","They cannot leave the attic","The bracelet will choose one of them","They will be trapped forever"],"correct_answer":"The bracelet will choose one of them"},{"question":"What emotions are Mia and Zoe struggling with?","options":["Fear and excitement","Jealousy and misunderstanding","Happiness and pride","Anger and resentment"],"correct_answer":"Jealousy and misunderstanding"},{"question":"What does Mia realize at the end of the chapter?","options":["They need more time","They must confront their feelings","They should give up","They don\u2019t need the bracelet"],"correct_answer":"They must confront their feelings"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_296_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_296_ch3_img1.png","plot_296_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":603,"reading_level":"Builder"}
