   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_296_15_18","title":"The Secret of the Friendship Bracelet","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The sun dipped low on the horizon, casting an amber glow over the old Maplewood Middle School. Mia stood at the foot of the attic stairs, her heart racing. She could still remember the feel of the ancient friendship bracelet nestled in her palm\u2014the cool metal, the intricate designs etched into it like whispers of a forgotten time. Zoe, with her vivid imagination, had suggested they use it to reinforce their bond. But now, as shadows danced across the walls, Mia couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that the bracelet was more trouble than it was worth.\n\n\u201cMia, are you coming?\u201d Zoe\u2019s voice floated down the attic stairs, pulling Mia from her thoughts. \u201cI think I need some fresh air.\u201d \n\nNodding, Mia followed Zoe outside, the cool evening breeze ruffling their hair. They found themselves on the school\u2019s back lawn, a sprawling space of green that usually buzzed with laughter. Today, however, an uneasy silence enveloped them. The bracelet had transformed their once-unbreakable friendship into a tangled knot of jealousy and misunderstanding.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t get it,\u201d Zoe said, her brows furrowed. \u201cWhy did you hide the bracelet from me?\u201d\n\n\u201cI was scared! It felt like it had a mind of its own. Things started happening that I couldn\u2019t explain\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cLike when you turned the art room\u2019s paint into glow-in-the-dark sludge? That was hilarious!\u201d Zoe interrupted, a hint of resentment in her tone. \u201cBut then you just... stopped trusting me.\u201d\n\nMia sighed, feeling the weight of her friend\u2019s disappointment settle heavily on her shoulders. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean to, Zoe. I thought if I kept it to myself, I could figure it out without dragging you into it. I didn\u2019t want to lose you.\u201d\n\nZoe\u2019s expression softened, but the shadows of their recent arguments still lingered in her eyes. \u201cYou\u2019re not going to lose me, Mia. But we need to face whatever this bracelet is together. It\u2019s what friends do.\u201d \n\nAs they spoke, a sudden gust of wind whipped through the trees, rustling the leaves like whispers of mischievous spirits. In that moment, Mia felt a spark of hope ignite within her. Maybe they could mend what had been frayed.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s\u2014let\u2019s try again,\u201d Mia suggested, her voice tentative yet determined. \u201cWe can research the bracelet together. There has to be a reason it\u2019s causing these strange events.\u201d \n\nZoe nodded, a hint of excitement flickering across her face. \u201cAnd I bet we can find out more if we dig into the school\u2019s history. You know what they say about old places\u2026 they\u2019re full of secrets.\u201d\n\nWith a newfound sense of collaboration, the two friends made their way back inside, the evening air buzzing with anticipation. They climbed into the attic once more, rummaging through dusty boxes and forgotten relics. As they worked side by side, laughter began to replace the tension. Mia felt a sense of camaraderie blossom anew, even amidst the uncertainty surrounding the bracelet.\n\nAmidst the trinkets, Zoe suddenly gasped, her voice barely a whisper. \u201cMia, look at this!\u201d She held up an old yearbook, its cover faded and worn. \u201cIt\u2019s from when the school was first built!\u201d \n\nMia leaned in, her curiosity piqued. \u201cMaybe there\u2019s something about the bracelet in here?\u201d \n\nJust as Zoe opened the book, the air around them shimmered, and a chill ran down Mia\u2019s spine. An ethereal glow emanated from the bracelet, which they had laid on the attic floor. It pulsed rhythmically, drawing their eyes like moths to a flame. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMia\u2019s heart raced as she glanced at Zoe, who met her gaze with wide eyes. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?\u201d Zoe stammered, her artistic mind struggling to grasp the gravity of the moment. \n\n\u201cI think it\u2019s waking up,\u201d Mia replied, a mix of awe and fear suffusing her voice. \u201cWe need to figure out what it wants!\u201d \n\nSuddenly, the attic door creaked open, and a shadowy figure materialized. \u201cYou\u2019ve awakened me,\u201d it whispered, a playful tone lacing its words like a soft breeze. The mischievous ghost of their school seemed to glow softly in the dim light, its laughter echoing around them.\n\n\u201cWhat do you want?\u201d Mia summoned her courage, stepping forward. \n\n\u201cI seek a friendship that\u2019s stronger than the temptation to betray,\u201d the ghost replied, its eyes twinkling with mischief. \u201cReveal your truths, and the bracelet will share its secrets.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nMia and Zoe exchanged uncertain glances, the weight of the ghost\u2019s revelation settling heavily upon them. They had to confront their feelings, navigate their jealousy, and reforge their bond\u2014before the bracelet\u2019s power tore them apart forever.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s do this together,\u201d Zoe whispered, her hand reaching out for Mia\u2019s, determination glimmering in her eyes. \n\nWith the ghost watching over them, they took a deep breath, ready to unveil their truths and embrace the challenge ahead.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What triggers the tension between Mia and Zoe in this chapter?","options":["Mia hiding the bracelet","Zoe's jealousy","The ghost's appearance","Their different interests"],"correct_answer":"Mia hiding the bracelet"},{"question":"What does the ghost require from Mia and Zoe?","options":["Their secrets","The bracelet","Help with homework","A friendship promise"],"correct_answer":"Their secrets"},{"question":"How do Mia and Zoe begin to mend their friendship?","options":["By arguing","By going to the school dance","By researching together","By ignoring their problems"],"correct_answer":"By researching together"},{"question":"What does the ghost symbolize in this chapter?","options":["Jealousy","Mischief","Challenges to friendship","School spirit"],"correct_answer":"Challenges to friendship"},{"question":"What emotional state do Mia and Zoe find themselves in by the end of the chapter?","options":["Despair","Fear","Determination","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Determination"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_296_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_296_ch4_img1.png","plot_296_ch4_img2.png"]},"word_count":821,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
