   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_297_7_10","title":"The Great Talent Show Tangle","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"It was a bright, sunny morning at Maplewood Middle School. The hallways buzzed with excitement. Posters for the upcoming talent show decorated the walls. Sam and Alex hurried to their classroom, grinning from ear to ear.\n\n\u201cDid you hear about the talent show?\u201d Sam asked, his blue eyes sparkling. \u201cI can\u2019t wait to sing on stage!\u201d\n\n\u201cMe too!\u201d said Alex, adjusting his glasses. \u201cI\u2019m going to perform my best magic tricks!\u201d\n\nThe friends walked into Ms. Johnson\u2019s classroom. She smiled as they entered. \u201cGood morning, class! Who is excited about the talent show?\u201d \n\nEveryone cheered. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMs. Johnson clapped her hands. \u201cRemember, it\u2019s not just about winning. It\u2019s about having fun and sharing your talent!\u201d\n\nSam and Alex exchanged glances. They both wanted to be the star. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s make a pact!\u201d Sam suggested. \u201cNo matter what happens, we stay friends.\u201d\n\nAlex nodded, but inside he felt a twinge of worry. What if he won instead of Sam? \n\nAs the days passed, the talent show rehearsals began. Sam practiced singing in the school auditorium. \u201cLa, la, la!\u201d he belted out, filling the room with warmth. Alex watched, feeling nervous.\n\nOne afternoon, Sam was backstage, humming to himself. Suddenly, he overheard Alex talking to another student. \u201cI\u2019m going to win for sure. Sam is just a singer, and nobody cares about that!\u201d\n\nSam\u2019s heart sank. He felt betrayed. Was Alex really saying that? \n\nA cloud of confusion hung over Sam as he thought, \u201cMaybe Alex isn\u2019t my friend after all.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe next day, Sam confronted Alex. \u201cI heard what you said! Are you trying to backstab me?\u201d\n\nAlex looked shocked. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean it that way! I just want to win!\u201d\n\nThe tension grew between them. They both wanted to shine, but at what cost?\n\nThe day of the talent show was near. Sam and Alex were caught in a tangle of competition and hurt feelings. They needed to figure out what mattered more: winning or their friendship.\n\n\u201cWhat will happen next?\u201d Sam wondered.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What are Sam and Alex excited about?","options":["The talent show","Summer vacation","A school trip","A new movie"],"correct_answer":"The talent show"},{"question":"What talent does Sam want to showcase?","options":["Magic tricks","Singing","Dancing","Drawing"],"correct_answer":"Singing"},{"question":"What does Alex perform?","options":["Singing","Magic tricks","Comedy","Juggling"],"correct_answer":"Magic tricks"},{"question":"What does Ms. Johnson remind the students about the talent show?","options":["It's only about winning","It's about fun and sharing talent","It's very easy","It's a secret"],"correct_answer":"It's about fun and sharing talent"},{"question":"What conflict arises between Sam and Alex?","options":["They both want to sing","They can't find costumes","They argue over who will win","They want to perform together"],"correct_answer":"They argue over who will win"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_297_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_297_ch1_img1.png","plot_297_ch1_img2.png","story_297_7-10_ch1_img2_1751271644.png"]},"word_count":345,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
