   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_297_7_10","title":"The Great Talent Show Tangle","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The next day at Maplewood Middle School, the air buzzed with excitement. Posters for the talent show decorated the walls. Sam and Alex walked side by side down the bustling hallway.\n\n\u201cCan you believe the talent show is this Friday?\u201d Sam said, his smile wide. \u201cI can\u2019t wait to sing my song!\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, I\u2019m gonna blow everyone\u2019s mind with my magic tricks!\u201d Alex replied, puffing out his chest. But deep down, both of them felt the weight of competition.\n\nJust then, Ms. Johnson, their teacher, appeared with a bright smile. \u201cBoys! I\u2019m so proud of your hard work! Remember, supporting each other is the most important part of this show.\u201d\n\nSam nodded, but he couldn\u2019t shake off the feeling that Alex wanted to outshine him. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAfter school, Sam practiced in the empty auditorium. He stood on the stage, his voice echoing. \u201cTwinkle, twinkle, little star, how I wonder what you are!\u201d He felt great until he spotted Alex peeking through the curtains.\n\n\u201cHey, that was pretty good!\u201d Alex said with a grin. But then he added, \u201cDon't get too comfortable. I\u2019ve got a new trick that will wow the crowd!\u201d\n\nSam frowned. \u201cYou think you\u2019re better than me?\u201d\n\n\u201cNo! I just want to win!\u201d Alex replied, fire in his eyes. \n\nThe air in the auditorium grew tense. Sam crossed his arms. \u201cWinning is all you care about?\u201d\n\nBefore Alex could answer, a loud crash broke the silence. A prop box fell from the stage. \u201cOh no!\u201d Sam shouted, rushing to help. Alex ran after him, but then tripped over a stray wire.\n\n\u201cWatch out!\u201d Sam called, but it was too late. Alex tumbled down, landing in a pile of props. \n\n\u201cAre you okay?\u201d Sam asked, rushing over. \n\n\u201cYeah, I\u2019m fine,\u201d Alex grumbled, feeling embarrassed. But Sam couldn't help but laugh. \u201cYou look like a magician who lost his magic!\u201d\n\nAlex chuckled despite himself. \u201cWell, maybe I should stick to singing!\u201d\n\nThe boys shared a laugh, but the tension was still there. They both knew the competition was heating up, and they were miles apart from being friends. \n\nAs they gathered the props, Sam thought about what Ms. Johnson said. Could they still support each other? The thought lingered.\n\nSuddenly, Sam had a new idea. \u201cHey, what if we teamed up for the show?\u201d he suggested, his eyes sparkling with hope.\n\nAlex paused. \u201cReally? You think we could?\u201d\n\n\u201cWhy not? Two acts are better than one!\u201d\n\nThe boys stared at each other, their friendship shining through the fog of competition. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut just as they were about to shake on it, the principal, Mr. Thompson, burst in. \u201cBoys, I need to speak with you about the talent show. There\u2019s been a change!\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat kind of change?\u201d Sam asked, both curious and worried.\n\n\u201cYou\u2019ll find out soon!\u201d Mr. Thompson said with a mysterious smile.\n\nThe boys exchanged glances, unsure of what would happen next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What event is Sam and Alex preparing for?","options":["A talent show","A science fair","A sports competition","A field trip"],"correct_answer":"A talent show"},{"question":"What does Ms. Johnson remind Sam and Alex about?","options":["To practice more","To support each other","To compete harder","To sing together"],"correct_answer":"To support each other"},{"question":"What happens when Alex trips?","options":["He wins the competition","He falls into props","He joins Sam's song","He leaves the auditorium"],"correct_answer":"He falls into props"},{"question":"What idea does Sam suggest at the end of the chapter?","options":["To compete against each other","To quit the show","To team up for the show","To sing a duet"],"correct_answer":"To team up for the show"},{"question":"What does Mr. Thompson tell Sam and Alex?","options":["He likes their act","There's been a change","They need to practice more","They can team up"],"correct_answer":"There's been a change"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_297_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_297_ch2_img1.png","plot_297_ch2_img2.png","story_297_7-10_ch2_img1_1751271583.png","story_297_7-10_ch2_img2_1751271606.png"]},"word_count":495,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
