   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_297_7_10","title":"The Great Talent Show Tangle","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Chapter 3: Tensions Rise\n\nThe hallway at Maplewood Middle School buzzed with excitement. Posters for the talent show covered the walls. Bright colors and big letters shouted, \u201cJoin the Fun!\u201d Sam and Alex walked together, but something felt different. A thick silence hung between them.\n\n\"I can't believe Ms. Johnson said the winner gets a trophy!\" Sam said, trying to break the ice. \"I want that trophy more than anything!\"\n\n\"Me too,\" Alex replied, crossing his arms. \"But I really think I should win. My magic act is going to blow everyone away!\"\n\nSam's face turned red. \"No way! My singing is way better. Everyone loves my voice!\" \n\nSuddenly, Ms. Johnson appeared, smiling brightly. \"Boys, remember, the talent show is about showcasing your skills, not just winning!\"\n\nSam and Alex nodded, but the tension still lingered. \n\nLater that day, while practicing, Sam accidentally bumped into Alex. \u201cWatch it!\u201d Alex snapped, glaring at him. \n\n\"Are you trying to sabotage me?\" Sam shot back, his hands on his hips.\n\n\u201cNo! I just want to show everyone my magic!\u201d Alex yelled. \n\nIt was time for their rehearsals, and the auditorium was alive with sounds. Sam stood at center stage, singing his favorite song. He closed his eyes and let his voice soar through the air. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMeanwhile, Alex practiced his magic tricks behind the curtain. He pulled out a rabbit from a hat and accidentally dropped it! The rabbit squeaked and hopped away, making everyone laugh.\n\n\u201cAlex, focus!\u201d shouted Sam from the stage, and Alex\u2019s face turned bright red. \n\nThen came a loud noise! A strange rumble filled the auditorium. The lights flickered, and the audience gasped. \u201cWhat\u2019s happening?\u201d a student cried.\n\nAlex rushed out, \u201cIt\u2019s my fault! I used too many colorful smoke bombs during my trick!\u201d \n\n\u201cForget the show! We need to fix this!\u201d Sam exclaimed, looking worried. \n\nAs they scrambled to help, Sam and Alex locked eyes. For a moment, they realized something important. Winning the show didn\u2019t matter if the lights went out forever!\n\n\"Let\u2019s work together,\" Sam said, \"for the show.\" \n\n\"Together?\" Alex asked, surprised. \n\n\u201cYes! We can be a team. We\u2019ll save the show!\u201d \n\nBut just then, the lights went out completely! Sam and Alex held hands, ready to face whatever came next. \n\nWhat would happen to their friendship? Would they find a way to save the talent show together? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sam and Alex want to win?","options":["A trophy","A rabbit","A hat","A song"],"correct_answer":"A trophy"},{"question":"What happens to Alex's magic trick during rehearsals?","options":["He makes a rabbit disappear","He drops the rabbit","He finds a new hat","He wins the show"],"correct_answer":"He drops the rabbit"},{"question":"What does Ms. Johnson remind Sam and Alex about the talent show?","options":["It's about having fun","It's only for winners","It's too hard","It's just a practice"],"correct_answer":"It's about having fun"},{"question":"What causes a panic in the auditorium?","options":["The lights go out","A student falls","Someone sings badly","A bird flies in"],"correct_answer":"The lights go out"},{"question":"What decision do Sam and Alex make at the end of the chapter?","options":["To work separately","To give up","To work together","To leave the show"],"correct_answer":"To work together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_297_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_297_ch3_img1.png","plot_297_ch3_img2.png","story_297_7-10_ch3_img1_1751271542.png","story_297_7-10_ch3_img2_1751271565.png"]},"word_count":401,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
