   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_297_7_10","title":"The Great Talent Show Tangle","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The sun shone brightly on Maplewood Middle School. Sam and Alex were in the bustling hallway, passing by colorful posters for the talent show. \n\n\u201cLook at all these amazing acts!\u201d Sam said, his eyes wide with excitement. \n\n\u201cI know! I bet everyone is going to bring their best,\u201d Alex replied, but he felt a twinge of worry. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs they walked, Ms. Johnson, their supportive teacher, spotted them. \u201cHey, boys! How\u2019s your talent show practice going?\u201d she asked with a smile.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s going great!\u201d Sam said, puffing out his chest. \u201cI\u2019m going to win with my singing!\u201d\n\nAlex frowned. \u201cI\u2019m going to wow everyone with my magic tricks. You\u2019ll see!\u201d\n\n\u201cOh, I hope you both do well,\u201d Ms. Johnson replied, noticing the tension between them. \u201cRemember, it\u2019s not just about winning! It\u2019s about having fun too.\u201d\n\nAfter school, Sam and Alex practiced. Sam sang high notes that made the birds outside chirp in rhythm. Meanwhile, Alex made a floating card trick look easy. But deep down, they both wanted to impress their friends more than anything.\n\nSuddenly, the lights in the auditorium flickered\u2014then went out! Sam and Alex exchanged worried glances. \n\n\u201cWhat happened?\u201d Alex whispered. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know!\u201d Sam replied, his heart racing.\n\nJust then, they heard a loud crash. It was the stage prop falling over! They dashed toward the sound. \n\n\u201cBe careful!\u201d Sam shouted. \n\n\u201cWatch out!\u201d Alex warned. \n\nThey reached the stage just in time to fix the prop together. The lights flickered back on, and the audience clapped. \n\n\u201cThat was amazing teamwork!\u201d Ms. Johnson cheered. \n\nSam looked at Alex and smiled. \u201cWe really did that together.\u201d\n\n\u201cYeah, we did!\u201d Alex beamed. \n\nIn that moment, they realized that working together felt better than winning alone. \n\n\u201cMaybe we could combine our acts?\u201d Sam suggested. \n\n\u201cReally? You\u2019d want to?\u201d Alex\u2019s eyes widened with hope.\n\n\u201cOf course! Let\u2019s make the best show ever!\u201d Sam replied.\n\nThey began to brainstorm ideas, their friendship feeling strong again. \n\nWith a new sense of excitement, they plotted a plan for the show. What would happen next? Would they be able to pull it all off in time?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What happens in the auditorium during practice?","options":["The lights go out","A bird flies in","The stage breaks","Sam sings a song"],"correct_answer":"The lights go out"},{"question":"What does Ms. Johnson remind Sam and Alex?","options":["It\u2019s important to win","It\u2019s about having fun","They should practice harder","They need new talent"],"correct_answer":"It\u2019s about having fun"},{"question":"What do Sam and Alex decide to do?","options":["Compete against each other","Combine their acts","Leave the show","Practice alone"],"correct_answer":"Combine their acts"},{"question":"How do Sam and Alex feel after working together?","options":["Angry","Tired","Happy","Sad"],"correct_answer":"Happy"},{"question":"What does Sam suggest at the end of the chapter?","options":["To quit the show","To perform alone","To make the best show ever","To practice more"],"correct_answer":"To make the best show ever"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_297_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_297_ch4_img1.png","plot_297_ch4_img2.png","story_297_7-10_ch4_img1_1751271501.png","story_297_7-10_ch4_img2_1751271518.png"]},"word_count":365,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
