   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_297_7_10","title":"The Great Talent Show Tangle","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The day of the talent show had finally arrived. Excitement buzzed in the air at Maplewood Middle School. Sam and Alex stood backstage, holding hands. They could hear the cheers of their classmates. \n\n\u201cAre you ready?\u201d Sam asked, his heart racing.\n\n\u201cReady as I\u2019ll ever be!\u201d Alex replied, adjusting his magician\u2019s hat. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nThe backstage was filled with colorful costumes and props. Sam\u2019s microphone sparkled, and Alex\u2019s magic wand shone brightly. They glanced at each other. Moments ago, they had been rivals. Now, they were partners, ready to shine together.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s show them what we\u2019ve got!\u201d Sam said.\n\n\u201cTogether!\u201d Alex added, grinning from ear to ear.\n\nAs they stepped onto the stage, the spotlight flooded the area. The audience cheered, and Sam began to sing. He filled the air with his beautiful voice. Alex waved his wand and made sparkles appear in the air. \n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed from backstage. \u201cOh no! The backdrop!\u201d Sam shouted.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s falling!\u201d Alex exclaimed. \n\nWithout thinking, they rushed to save the backdrop. Together, they held it up with all their might. The audience gasped, then started to cheer them on. \n\n\u201cThis is teamwork!\u201d Sam yelled.\n\n\u201cKeep holding it!\u201d Alex encouraged.\n\nWith a final effort, they secured the backdrop just in time. The audience erupted in applause. Sam and Alex looked at each other, wide-eyed and smiling.\n\n\u201cWe did it!\u201d they both said at once.\n\nThey returned to the center of the stage. Instead of competing, they performed a dazzling duet. Sam sang, and Alex did magic tricks in sync with the music. Laughter and joy filled the auditorium.\n\nWhen they finished, the audience roared with applause. Ms. Johnson stood up, clapping wildly. \n\n\u201cThat was amazing!\u201d she shouted, beaming at them. \n\nSam and Alex hugged, realizing that sharing the spotlight was better than winning alone. They had worked together, and that made them true stars.\n\n\u201cVictory is great,\u201d Sam said, \u201cbut friendship is the best reward.\u201d \n\nAlex nodded. \u201cWe can shine together anytime!\u201d\n\nAs they left the stage, they felt proud and happy. No matter what happened next, they would always be best friends.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Sam and Alex perform at the talent show?","options":["A play","A duet","A dance","A poem"],"correct_answer":"A duet"},{"question":"What happened to the backdrop during the performance?","options":["It fell down","It was too small","It was colorful","It was missing"],"correct_answer":"It fell down"},{"question":"How did the audience react to their performance?","options":["They were bored","They cheered","They were quiet","They left"],"correct_answer":"They cheered"},{"question":"What did Sam and Alex realize was more important than winning?","options":["Competition","Friendship","Fame","Money"],"correct_answer":"Friendship"},{"question":"Who stood up and clapped for Sam and Alex?","options":["Their classmates","Ms. Johnson","The principal","Their parents"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Johnson"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_297_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_297_ch5_img1.png","plot_297_ch5_img2.png","story_297_7-10_ch5_img1_1751271466.png","story_297_7-10_ch5_img2_1751271481.png"]},"word_count":358,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
