   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_7_10","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Chapter 4: A New Plan\n\nThe cafeteria buzzed with laughter and chatter. Sarah sat at the table with Lily and Raj. She looked at the colorful trays of food, thinking about how hungry everyone seemed. \u201cI have an idea!\u201d Sarah said, her eyes sparkling. \u201cLet\u2019s make snack packs for everyone!\u201d\n\nLily's face lit up. \u201cThat\u2019s a great idea! We can share our lunches!\u201d \n\nRaj nodded. \u201cI can help! My mom has some extra snacks we can use.\u201d \n\nSarah smiled big. \u201cOkay! Let\u2019s plan it.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nThey gathered in a circle, discussing their plan. \u201cWe\u2019ll make mini sandwiches, cut-up veggies, and some fruit!\u201d Sarah said, excited. \u201cAnd don\u2019t forget cookies!\u201d Raj added with a grin. \n\n\u201cBut what about sharing?\u201d Lily asked, biting her lip. \u201cWhat if they still take our lunch?\u201d \n\nSarah thought for a moment. \u201cLet\u2019s put a name tag on each snack pack. That way, everyone knows who it belongs to.\u201d \n\nLily\u2019s eyes brightened. \u201cYes! And we can make a sign that says \u2018Take a snack, share a smile!\u2019\u201d \n\nAs they worked together, Sarah felt a warm feeling in her heart. They were not just solving the lunch mystery; they were making a difference. \n\nLater, during recess, they spread out their colorful snack packs on a big picnic blanket. Everyone gathered around, eyes wide with excitement. \u201cWow, look at all this food!\u201d shouted Jake, a classmate from across the yard.\n\n\u201cWe made it to share!\u201d Raj said, waving his hands in the air. \n\nSuddenly, Sarah spotted a shy girl sitting on a bench, watching them. \u201cHey, do you want to join us?\u201d Sarah called out. The girl smiled shyly and nodded. \n\nAs she approached, Sarah felt proud. This was more than just about food; it was about friendship and kindness. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThey all enjoyed the snack packs together, laughing and sharing stories. Lily looked at Sarah and said, \u201cThank you for believing in me.\u201d Sarah beamed back, feeling closer to her friend than ever.\n\n\u201cI think we\u2019re really doing something special,\u201d Sarah said. But in her heart, she still felt that there was more to learn about Lily. \n\nAs the bell rang, signaling the end of recess, Sarah whispered to Lily, \u201cCan we talk more later?\u201d \n\nLily nodded eagerly. \u201cYes! I want to tell you everything.\u201d \n\nSarah smiled, feeling hopeful. They had taken the first step toward understanding each other better. She couldn\u2019t wait to see what else they would discover.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Sarah, Lily, and Raj plan to do?","options":["Make snack packs","Play a game","Go to class","Eat lunch"],"correct_answer":"Make snack packs"},{"question":"What is the name of the shy girl?","options":["Lily","Sarah","Jake","They didn't say"],"correct_answer":"They didn't say"},{"question":"What did they put on the snack packs?","options":["Stickers","Name tags","Ribbons","Prices"],"correct_answer":"Name tags"},{"question":"What message did they write on the sign?","options":["Take a snack, share a smile!","Lunch is free!","We love food!","Join us for lunch!"],"correct_answer":"Take a snack, share a smile!"},{"question":"How did Sarah feel about their plan?","options":["Sad","Nervous","Proud","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Proud"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch4_img1.png","plot_298_ch4_img2.png","story_298_7-10_ch4_img1_1751270863.png","story_298_7-10_ch4_img2_1751270880.png"]},"word_count":412,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
