   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Sarah Thompson had seen some strange things in her twelve years at Crestview Elementary, but the disappearing lunches were at the top of the list. Every day, she packed her favorite turkey sandwich, a crisp apple, and a little bag of cookies. But every day, when lunch rolled around, she found her lunchbox empty, as if it had been swept into the void. Each time, she felt a mix of confusion and frustration, while her best friend, Lily, seemed oblivious. \n\nThe cafeteria buzzed with laughter and chatter as students filled their trays. The sun streamed through the tall windows, casting a warm glow over the colorful plastic tables. Sarah glanced over at Lily, her eyes wide and innocent. Could her best friend really be behind it all? \n\n\u201cHey, Sarah!\u201d Lily called, her voice bright like a summer day. She had a habit of wearing her heart on her sleeve, and today was no different, with her freckles dancing across her cheeks as she smiled. \u201cDid you bring that new sandwich you told me about?\u201d\n\n\u201cNot this time,\u201d Sarah said, trying to sound casual. \u201cJust the usual.\u201d She watched as Lily's eyes flitted toward their classmates, laughing and sharing food. \n\nSarah\u2019s gut tightened. \u201cWhat if she\u2019s just pretending not to know? What if she\u2019s the one taking my lunch?\u201d That thought nagged at her like a pesky fly. \n\nAs they moved through the lunch line, Raj, their clever classmate, joined them. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on, Sarah? You look like you lost a bet.\u201d \n\n\u201cMore like I\u2019m losing my lunch,\u201d she grumbled, glancing around, searching for any sign of mischief. \u201cI\u2019m starting to think someone\u2019s stealing it every day.\u201d \n\nRaj raised an eyebrow. \u201cThat\u2019s weird. Are you sure it\u2019s not just an accident? Maybe your lunchbox is too confusing?\u201d\n\n\u201cNo. I\u2019m sure!\u201d Sarah exclaimed, her frustration bubbling over. \u201cIt\u2019s gone! Every. Single. Day.\u201d \n\nLily bit her lip, her expression shifting slightly. \u201cMaybe someone really needs it. You know, some kids don\u2019t get enough to eat at home.\u201d \n\nSarah felt a pang of empathy but shook her head. \u201cThat doesn\u2019t make it right! I can\u2019t just let this go on.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, she spotted a shadowy figure slipping away from the table next to theirs. Sarah's heart raced. \u201cWait, I think I saw something!\u201d She nudged Raj as they both turned to see the figure vanish around the corner. \n\n\u201cWhat was that?\u201d Raj asked, his eyes gleaming with curiosity. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but I\u2019m going to find out.\u201d Sarah took a deep breath, determination sparking inside her. \n\nLily frowned, hesitant. \u201cBut what if it\u2019s someone who needs help?\u201d \n\nFor a moment, Sarah hesitated, weighing her options. The cafeteria felt smaller suddenly, the laughter fading into a low hum. \u201cI\u2019ll help them, but I have to know who it is first.\u201d \n\nAs they made their way toward the exit, Sarah glanced back at Lily, who looked like she was lost in thought. Did she really want to confront her about this? The stakes felt high, and the mystery was thick in the air, like a storm brewing just beyond the horizon. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d she urged, pushing past the tables with Raj in tow. The mystery of the vanishing lunch was about to unfold, and Sarah was determined to uncover the truth\u2014even if it meant facing her own best friend. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What problem is Sarah facing at school?","options":["Her lunch is disappearing","She lost her backpack","She has too much homework","She's being bullied"],"correct_answer":"Her lunch is disappearing"},{"question":"Who does Sarah suspect is behind the missing lunches?","options":["Raj","Lily","The cafeteria staff","No one"],"correct_answer":"Lily"},{"question":"What does Lily suggest about the missing lunches?","options":["They're just lost","Someone might need them","It's a prank","Sarah is imagining it"],"correct_answer":"Someone might need them"},{"question":"What does Sarah decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Ignore the problem","Investigate further","Ask the teacher for help","Tell her parents"],"correct_answer":"Investigate further"},{"question":"Who joins Sarah and Lily in the cafeteria?","options":["Raj","Emily","Tom","Michael"],"correct_answer":"Raj"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch1_img1.png","plot_298_ch1_img2.png","story_298_11-14_ch1_img1_1751270799.png","story_298_11-14_ch1_img2_1751270816.png"]},"word_count":577,"reading_level":"Builder"}
