   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The cafeteria buzzed with chatter as Sarah and Lily made their way to their usual table, the smell of pizza wafting in the air like a tantalizing invitation. Sarah\u2019s heart raced, not from the delicious aroma but from the gnawing mystery of her disappearing lunches. She glanced sideways at Lily, who was blissfully chatting about the latest episode of their favorite show.\n\n\u201cI can\u2019t believe you missed it!\u201d Lily exclaimed, her eyes sparkling. \u201cYou have to see how they\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cLily,\u201d Sarah interrupted, her voice tight with unease. \u201cHave you seen anyone around my lunch lately?\u201d\n\nLily\u2019s eyes widened, and for a moment, she looked genuinely surprised. \u201cNo, why? Is it still missing?\u201d\n\nSarah hesitated. Maybe it was unfair to suspect her best friend without proof. But the gnawing sensation in her stomach felt like a rock. She needed to discover the truth, and Raj had promised to help her after school.\n\nAfter class, Sarah and Raj huddled by the lockers. \u201cYou know, it could be anyone,\u201d Raj said, adjusting his glasses. \u201cHave you thought about setting a trap?\u201d\n\n\u201cA trap?\u201d Sarah raised an eyebrow, her curiosity piqued.\n\n\u201cYeah! Like leaving your lunch out and hiding nearby to see who takes it.\u201d He grinned, the light from the overhead fluorescents glinting off his glasses. \u201cIt\u2019ll be like a detective story!\u201d\n\nSarah felt a flicker of hope. \u201cThat\u2019s actually a brilliant idea! But\u2026 what if it is Lily? I don\u2019t want to accuse her without knowing for sure.\u201d\n\nRaj\u2019s expression turned serious. \u201cThen it\u2019s time to dig deeper. If she\u2019s your best friend, finding out the truth is important, even if it hurts.\u201d\n\nAs they plotted their plan, Sarah felt a knot of anxiety in her stomach. But she couldn\u2019t ignore her suspicion. Maybe Lily was just hungry and didn\u2019t want to tell her. But why hide it? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe next day, with her lunch packed carefully in a bright pink lunchbox, Sarah felt a mix of excitement and dread. They had decided to leave the lunch on the table while pretending to chat nearby. The cafeteria buzzed with students, each absorbed in their own worlds, while Sarah and Raj watched from a corner.\n\nMoments passed like hours, and Sarah\u2019s heart raced louder than the clamor around her. Just as she was about to suggest they give up, she spotted a shadow near their table. A familiar figure bent over the lunchbox, peering inside. It was Lily.\n\n\u201cWait!\u201d Sarah gasped, her voice barely above a whisper. \n\nBut before Sarah could move, Lily straightened up, a look of shock etched on her face. \u201cSarah! I wasn\u2019t\u2026 I mean, I didn\u2019t mean to,\u201d she stammered, her cheeks flushed a rosy hue. \n\nSarah felt a whirlwind of emotions\u2014confusion, betrayal, and a flicker of sympathy. \u201cWhy are you taking my lunch, Lily?\u201d\n\nLily\u2019s eyes darted to the floor, her voice barely a whisper. \u201cI didn\u2019t know how to tell you\u2026\u201d \n\nThe moment hung in the air, thick with tension. Lily looked like a deer caught in headlights, and Sarah\u2019s heart sank. What had she uncovered? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe realization hit her. \u201cYou\u2019ve been hungry?\u201d Sarah\u2019s voice softened, her anger fading. \n\nLily nodded slowly, tears glimmering in her eyes. \u201cI didn\u2019t want to worry you. Things at home\u2026 they\u2019re just not good right now, and I thought\u2014\u201d\n\nSarah\u2019s heart twisted. She hadn\u2019t realized the pressure her best friend had been facing. \u201cYou could\u2019ve told me,\u201d she said gently, stepping closer. \u201cI\u2019m here for you, you know that, right?\u201d\n\nLily took a shaky breath, the tension between them starting to dissolve. \u201cI know, but I thought you wouldn\u2019t understand.\u201d\n\n\u201cBut I do,\u201d Sarah replied, determination replacing her earlier frustration. \u201cWe\u2019ll figure this out together.\u201d\n\nAs they stood there, a wave of understanding washed over them, and Sarah\u2019s resolve began to shift. The mystery was deeper than stolen lunches; it was about friendship and supporting one another through thick and thin.\n\nBut as they hugged, Sarah wondered\u2014what else lay hidden beneath the surface?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What plan do Sarah and Raj come up with to catch the lunch thief?","options":["Hide in the cafeteria","Set a trap with Sarah's lunch","Ask the teacher","Follow Lily home"],"correct_answer":"Set a trap with Sarah's lunch"},{"question":"What emotion does Sarah feel when she suspects Lily is behind the missing lunches?","options":["Excitement","Confusion","Joy","Anger"],"correct_answer":"Confusion"},{"question":"What does Lily reveal about her situation at home?","options":["She has too much food","Things are not good","Her parents are away","She is moving to a new school"],"correct_answer":"Things are not good"},{"question":"How does Sarah respond to Lily's confession?","options":["She gets angry","She ignores her","She offers to help","She tells her to find her own food"],"correct_answer":"She offers to help"},{"question":"What does Sarah wonder at the end of the chapter?","options":["If she should change schools","What else lies hidden beneath the surface","If she will be hungry too","If Raj can help them"],"correct_answer":"What else lies hidden beneath the surface"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch2_img1.png","plot_298_ch2_img2.png","story_298_11-14_ch2_img1_1751270758.png","story_298_11-14_ch2_img2_1751270783.png"]},"word_count":695,"reading_level":"Builder"}
