   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Chapter 3: Revelations in the Cafeteria\n\nThe cafeteria buzzed with the usual lunchtime chatter as Sarah entered, her heart racing like a wild horse. It was a place where laughter mingled with the smell of pizza and fries, but today, the air felt thick with tension. Sarah scanned the tables, her eyes landing on Lily, who sat with her usual crew, giggling and chatting. She wondered if Lily had taken her lunch again. \n\nAs she joined her friends, Raj was already in action. \u201cSo, what\u2019s the plan?\u201d he asked, his eyes sparkling with mischief. \u201cAre we going to set a trap?\u201d\n\nSarah hesitated, unsure. \u201cI don\u2019t know, Raj. What if I\u2019m wrong about her?\u201d \n\n\u201cLook, she took your lunch yesterday in front of you. We can\u2019t let her get away with it,\u201d Raj replied, urgency lacing his voice. \n\nSuddenly, Sarah's stomach growled loudly, reminding her of the half-eaten sandwich she had stashed in her backpack. \u201cOkay, let\u2019s just watch her for now,\u201d she decided. That\u2019s when she noticed Lily glance around before pulling something out from her backpack\u2014a bag of chips. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cIsn\u2019t she supposed to have a lunch?\u201d Raj whispered. \n\nA pit formed in Sarah\u2019s stomach. Lily didn\u2019t look happy. In fact, she seemed to be avoiding eye contact, her laughter fading into an uneasy silence. Sarah couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that there was something deeper going on. \n\nAfter lunch, Sarah and Raj lurked outside the cafeteria, waiting for Lily to leave. As the bell rang, they followed her down the sunlit hallway. \u201cWhy does she keep taking your lunch?\u201d Raj asked, scratching his head. \u201cMaybe she\u2019s just really hungry?\u201d\n\n\u201cOr maybe she doesn\u2019t have enough at home,\u201d Sarah murmured, recalling the shadows that had flickered in Lily's eyes when they had talked about family last week. \n\nThey ventured to the library, where whispers of secrets echoed off the tall shelves. \u201cI need to confront her,\u201d Sarah finally said, determination fueling her words. \u201cBut what if I hurt her feelings?\u201d\n\nRaj nodded. \u201cYou have to be careful. If she\u2019s struggling, maybe you can find a way to help without losing your friendship.\u201d\n\nJust as Sarah was about to speak, someone burst through the library doors. It was Lily, her face flushed and eyes wide with urgency. \u201cSarah! I need to talk to you\u2014\u201d \n\nBut before she could finish, a small crumpled note fell from her pocket and fluttered to the floor. Sarah's heart thudded as she picked it up, her eyes scanning the words: \u201cI\u2019m sorry. I\u2019ll make it up to you. Please don\u2019t tell.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s this?\u201d Sarah demanded, her voice trembling with confusion and a hint of betrayal. \n\nLily\u2019s expression shifted, panic rising in her eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s not what you think! I can explain!\u201d \n\nThe air in the library grew thick with tension as Sarah grappled with a whirlwind of emotions. Should she push for the truth, or give her friend a chance to explain?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBefore Sarah could decide, the bell rang again, signaling the end of lunch and the beginning of a new class. \u201cI\u2019ll meet you after school,\u201d Lily said hurriedly, her voice barely a whisper, before slipping away.\n\nStanding alone, Sarah felt the weight of the note in her hand. She had expected answers, but now she was left with more questions than ever. What did Lily mean by \u201cmake it up to you\u201d? \n\nAs she headed to her next class, Sarah knew one thing: she had to find out the truth, even if it meant risking everything she thought she knew about her best friend.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Sarah find in the library that raises her suspicions about Lily?","options":["A sandwich","A note","A backpack","A book"],"correct_answer":"A note"},{"question":"Why does Sarah hesitate to confront Lily about the lunches?","options":["She is afraid of getting in trouble","She is unsure if Lily is actually guilty","She doesn't want to embarrass Lily","All of the above"],"correct_answer":"All of the above"},{"question":"What does Raj suggest Sarah do about the situation?","options":["Set a trap for Lily","Ignore Lily","Tell the teacher","Confront Lily angrily"],"correct_answer":"Set a trap for Lily"},{"question":"What is Lily's reaction when she sees Sarah in the library?","options":["She runs away","She is angry","She looks panicked","She is happy"],"correct_answer":"She looks panicked"},{"question":"What does Sarah decide to do at the end of this chapter?","options":["Ignore Lily","Find out the truth","Go home","Tell Raj everything"],"correct_answer":"Find out the truth"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch3_img1.png","plot_298_ch3_img2.png","story_298_11-14_ch3_img1_1751270717.png","story_298_11-14_ch3_img2_1751270738.png"]},"word_count":614,"reading_level":"Builder"}
