   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_11_14","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the sun filtered through the windows of Crestview Elementary, the cafeteria buzzed with excitement. Sarah sat at her usual table, her heart pounding like a drum. She glanced at the sprawling spread of food\u2014pizza, sandwiches, and salads\u2014while her mind raced. Today was the day, she decided. Today, she would confront Lily.\n\n\"Are you ready?\" Raj whispered, leaning closer with a knowing smile. He had been a great partner in this investigation, unraveling clues like a detective in a mystery novel. \n\n\"I guess so,\" Sarah replied, biting her lip. The thought of confronting her best friend made her stomach twist. She stole a glance at Lily, who sat at the other end of the table, laughing with some classmates. Her light brown hair bounced as she spoke animatedly, her smile bright enough to light up the room.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nJust then, Lily caught Sarah\u2019s gaze and waved. Sarah felt a pang of guilt. Was it really fair to suspect her friend? But every day, her lunch vanished into thin air, and Sarah was determined to get to the bottom of it. \n\nAs they moved through the lunch line, Sarah's mind whirred. She picked up a slice of pizza and a carton of milk, her favorite lunch pair. But instead of sitting down, she turned to Raj. \"I think I should talk to her now. Before we make any more assumptions.\"\n\n\"Just remember, it might not be what you think,\" Raj warned gently. \"People can surprise you.\"\n\nWith a deep breath, Sarah approached Lily. The chatter around them faded as she stood before her friend. \"Hey, can we talk for a minute?\"\n\nLily's expression shifted from cheerful to concerned. \"Sure, what's up?\"\n\nSarah glanced around, feeling the eyes of her classmates on them. \"I\u2014I\u2019ve been wondering about my lunches... They keep disappearing, and I thought maybe you knew something.\"\n\nLily's eyes widened in shock, and she took a step back. \"You think I took your lunch?\"\n\n\"I didn\u2019t want to believe it,\" Sarah rushed to explain, \"but it seemed like the only answer. I\u2019m sorry, I just\u2014\"\n\n\"Sarah, I would never do that!\" Lily's voice trembled. \"I\u2019ve been dealing with a lot at home... My parents are fighting all the time, and sometimes I just... forget to bring my lunch. I\u2019m so embarrassed!\"\n\nIn that moment, Sarah felt her heart squeeze. The weight of Lily\u2019s words hung in the air, heavy with unspoken worries. She had been so focused on her own frustration that she hadn\u2019t considered what was happening in Lily\u2019s life. \"I had no idea,\" Sarah said softly, her voice barely above a whisper. \"I\u2019m really sorry.\"\n\nLily's shoulders relaxed. \"I thought you were mad at me for taking your lunch. I didn\u2019t want to tell you any of this.\"\n\nTears pricked at Sarah's eyes. \"I wasn\u2019t mad, I was just confused. I should have asked you sooner. Can we start over? I can share my lunch with you until things get better at home.\"\n\nA slow smile spread across Lily\u2019s face, lighting up her features like the morning sun breaking through clouds. \u201cReally? You\u2019d do that for me?\u201d\n\n\u201cOf course!\u201d Sarah grinned back. \u201cFriends share everything, right? Even lunches.\u201d\n\nJust then, Raj joined them, thumbs up. \u201cNow that\u2019s teamwork! We can figure this out together.\u201d\n\nThe three of them stood there, united by the realization that friendships sometimes required understanding and kindness over suspicion. As they walked back to the table, Sarah felt a wave of relief and warmth envelop her. \n\n\u201cHey, how about a pizza party next week? My treat!\u201d Sarah suggested, feeling lighter than air. \n\n\u201cOnly if it\u2019s pepperoni!\u201d Lily laughed, her earlier worries melting away into joy.\n\nTogether, they laughed and chatted, the shadows of misunderstandings fading like forgotten dreams. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs the cafeteria buzzed around them, Sarah knew that their friendship would grow stronger, ready to face whatever mysteries life would throw at them next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Sarah decide to do in this chapter?","options":["Ignore Lily","Confront Lily about her missing lunches","Tell a teacher","Ask for a different lunch"],"correct_answer":"Confront Lily about her missing lunches"},{"question":"What does Lily reveal about her home life?","options":["She moves to a new school","Her parents are fighting","She has a pet cat","She lost her lunch money"],"correct_answer":"Her parents are fighting"},{"question":"How does Sarah feel when she learns about Lily's situation?","options":["Angry","Indifferent","Guilty","Excited"],"correct_answer":"Guilty"},{"question":"What suggestion does Sarah make at the end of the chapter?","options":["To have a pizza party","To change schools","To ignore their problems","To go home early"],"correct_answer":"To have a pizza party"},{"question":"Who helps Sarah in her investigation?","options":["Lily","Raj","The teacher","Her parents"],"correct_answer":"Raj"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch5_img1.png","plot_298_ch5_img2.png","story_298_11-14_ch5_img1_1751270645.png","story_298_11-14_ch5_img2_1751270660.png"]},"word_count":671,"reading_level":"Builder"}
