   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_15_18","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The scent of freshly baked pizza wafted through the bustling cafeteria of Crestview Elementary, mingling with the chatter of students eagerly anticipating their lunch break. Sarah Carver sat at her usual table, a corner spot where the sunlight streamed in through the tall windows, casting warm pools of light on the worn wooden surface. She absently twirled a pencil between her fingers, her mind racing with thoughts that had little to do with the upcoming math test. \n\n\"Are you even listening, Sarah?\" Lily's voice broke through her reverie, pulling her back into the present. Her best friend, with her bright, curly hair bouncing with every animated word, leaned closer, her hazel eyes wide with excitement. \n\n\"Yeah, sorry. Just thinking about\u2026 you know, lunch,\" Sarah replied, forcing a smile as she pointed to her uneaten sandwich, its edges already growing stale. \n\nLily pouted, a playful frown accentuating her features. \"You always think about lunch. If you keep neglecting it, I might just have to finish it for you.\" \n\nSarah chuckled but quickly glanced at her lunch bag, a sinking feeling settling in her stomach. For the past week, her lunches had mysteriously disappeared. Each day, she would pack her favorites\u2014turkey wraps, pasta salad, even homemade brownies\u2014but by the time she reached the cafeteria, her bag felt lighter than it should. \n\n\u201cMaybe we should investigate?\u201d Raj, their clever classmate with an insatiable curiosity, chimed in from across the table, his dark eyes sparkling with mischief. \u201cA mystery at Crestview? I\u2019m in.\u201d \n\n\u201cInvestigation? What are we, detectives?\u201d Sarah raised an eyebrow, intrigued despite herself. \n\n\u201cWhy not? Someone is stealing your lunch, and that\u2019s serious business!\u201d Raj grinned, his enthusiasm infectious.\n\nAs they joked about forming a \u2018Lunch Detective Agency\u2019, Sarah\u2019s heart raced at the thought of confronting the issue. The idea of accusing Lily loomed over her, heavy and suffocating. What if it was her best friend? Although Lily had been acting strangely lately, Sarah couldn\u2019t shake the nagging feeling that there was more to this than just disappearing lunches. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSarah, lost in thought, stared at Lily as she animatedly recounted her latest crush. The sunlight illuminated her curly hair, casting a halo-like glow around her. In this moment, she looked serene, but Sarah knew the truth was more complicated. It was almost as if the brightness of the cafeteria contrasted with the shadows lurking in Lily's life, shadows Sarah was yet to uncover.\n\n\u201cHey, Sarah, you\u2019re zoning out again!\u201d Raj\u2019s voice pulled her back. \u201cWhat if we each take turns watching our lunches? You know, to catch the thief in action. I can set up a video camera.\u201d \n\nSarah chuckled at the absurdity. \u201cRight, because every school cafeteria has surveillance cameras just waiting for a lunch thief to show up.\u201d \n\n\u201cOkay, okay, so maybe not a camera, but you get my point! We need to be clever,\u201d Raj insisted, his brow furrowing in concentration. \n\n\u201cClever, huh? And what if it actually is Lily? What then?\u201d Sarah felt her heart sink at the thought. Despite their friendship, the possibility that Lily could be behind the theft made her stomach twist. She didn\u2019t want to confront her friend, especially if the truth turned out to be more complicated than she had imagined.\n\nThe bell rang sharply, signaling the end of lunch. As students began to rise and chatter filled the air, Sarah glanced at Lily, who was now focused on her phone. The anxiety tightened in Sarah\u2019s chest. Should she let it go? Support her friend? Or should she dig deeper into a mystery that might unravel everything?\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s meet after school and plan our stakeout,\u201d Raj said, breaking the silence. \u201cI\u2019ll bring the snacks.\u201d \n\n\u201cGreat, snacks will make everything better,\u201d Sarah replied, her smile faltering. The mystery of the vanishing lunches held a secret she needed to uncover, but it threatened to shatter the fragile facade of their friendship. \n\nAs they filed out of the cafeteria, Sarah\u2019s mind raced with possibilities. Maybe the missing lunches were more than just food; perhaps they were the key to understanding the struggles Lily faced. But would she have the courage to find out? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe late afternoon sun cast long shadows across the schoolyard as Sarah stood at the entrance, clutching her backpack tightly. The weight of the mystery hung in the air, thick and palpable, intertwining with her feelings of loyalty and doubt. She could feel her heart pounding, a rhythm of uncertainty as she braced herself for the journey ahead.\n\n\u201cAre you ready?\u201d Raj\u2019s voice drew her back to the present, but Sarah\u2019s gaze lingered on the horizon, not entirely sure of the path she was about to take.\n\n\u201cReady as I\u2019ll ever be,\u201d she replied, taking a deep breath. The adventure was just beginning, and with it, the potential to unearth truths that would challenge everything she thought she knew about friendship.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What seems to be the main problem Sarah is facing?","options":["Her lunch is missing","She failed a test","She has a crush on Raj","She is moving away"],"correct_answer":"Her lunch is missing"},{"question":"Who is Sarah's main ally in her investigation?","options":["Lily","Raj","Her teacher","Her mom"],"correct_answer":"Raj"},{"question":"What does Sarah feel conflicted about?","options":["Whether to confront Lily","Whether to eat her lunch","Whether to study for her test","Whether to go to the dance"],"correct_answer":"Whether to confront Lily"},{"question":"What is the setting of the story?","options":["A park","A mall","Crestview Elementary","A library"],"correct_answer":"Crestview Elementary"},{"question":"What does Sarah's lunch bag symbolize in the chapter?","options":["A mystery","Friendship","Happiness","Conflict"],"correct_answer":"A mystery"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch1_img1.png","plot_298_ch1_img2.png","story_298_15-18_ch1_img1_1751270601.png","story_298_15-18_ch1_img2_1751270624.png"]},"word_count":828,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
