   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_15_18","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The cafeteria was a cacophony of laughter and clattering trays, a vibrant microcosm of Crestview Elementary where students gathered not just to eat, but to forge social alliances. Sarah perched at her usual table, the spot where she and Lily had shared countless lunches. The sunlight streamed in through the windows, casting warm, golden hues across the lunchroom. Yet today, a chill laced through Sarah\u2019s heart as she absentmindedly shifted her gaze toward the empty seat across from her.\n\n\u201cHey, Sarah! You okay?\u201d Raj\u2019s voice cut through her reverie, his brow furrowed in concern. He was always the one to notice when something was amiss, his perceptiveness often surprising her.\n\n\u201cJust thinking,\u201d she mumbled, her appetite having vanished along with her lunches. She picked at her salad, the lettuce feeling more like cardboard than a meal. \u201cIt\u2019s just\u2026 Lily hasn\u2019t been around much lately.\u201d\n\nRaj leaned in, intrigued. \u201cYou think she\u2019s skipping lunch to hang out with someone else?\u201d His eyes glimmered with mischief that only deepened Sarah\u2019s unease.\n\n\u201cNo!\u201d she exclaimed, perhaps too loudly, earning a few glances from the nearby tables. \u201cIt\u2019s not like that. It\u2019s just\u2026\u201d Sarah paused, her mind racing. She needed to understand why her best friend would resort to sneaking food when they both knew Lily could just ask. \n\nJust then, she spotted a familiar face at the opposite end of the cafeteria. Lily stood with a group of older girls, their laughter ringing above the surrounding noise, yet the light in her eyes was dimmer than Sarah remembered. She felt a pang of guilt\u2014was she wrong to suspect her best friend? The thought lingered like a shadow, darkening the lunchroom\u2019s brightness.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go talk to her,\u201d Raj suggested, standing up with an air of determination that momentarily lifted Sarah\u2019s spirits.\n\nAs they approached, Sarah\u2019s heart raced. The closer they got, the more she noticed the way Lily\u2019s smile didn\u2019t reach her eyes. It was a mask, a fragile fa\u00e7ade hiding something deeper. \u201cHey, Lily!\u201d Sarah called, attempting to sound cheerful.\n\nLily turned, her expression shifting from surprise to a practiced neutrality. \u201cHey, guys!\u201d she replied, though Sarah could sense the effort behind her words. \n\nRaj chimed in, \u201cWe were just talking about you! Want to join us?\u201d \n\nLily hesitated, her gaze flickering toward her friends, who were glancing back, whispering among themselves. \u201cUm, maybe later,\u201d she said, the words feeling like a dismissal rather than an invitation. \n\nAs they walked back to their table, Sarah\u2019s mind spun with questions. Could Lily be hiding something? And if so, what? Her intuition screamed at her to dig deeper, but where to begin? \n\n\u201cWell, that was awkward,\u201d Raj said, breaking the silence as they settled back down. \u201cI mean, it\u2019s like she\u2019s avoiding you.\u201d\n\n\u201cOr maybe she\u2019s just overwhelmed,\u201d Sarah countered. \u201cYou know how things have been at home for her.\u201d\n\nRaj nodded, but his expression remained skeptical. \u201cYou mean her dad? I just hope she\u2019s not too hard on herself. It\u2019s like she\u2019s trying to pretend it\u2019s all okay when we know it isn\u2019t.\u201d\n\nAs they continued to talk, Sarah felt the weight of her suspicions pressing down on her like an anchor. Was it right to confront Lily when she might be struggling? But if she didn\u2019t confront her, would she ever discover the truth behind the vanishing lunches? \n\nJust as Sarah was about to voice her conflict, an unexpected commotion erupted from the front of the cafeteria. A girl stood on a table, her arms raised triumphantly, a half-eaten sandwich in hand. \u201cWho stole my lunch?!\u201d she shouted, and the room fell silent, all eyes glued to her dramatic display.\n\nLily\u2019s face turned crimson, her eyes darting away in a panic. It was a momentary flash of emotion, but in that instant, Sarah caught something deeper\u2014a flicker of fear. \n\n\u201cDid you see that?\u201d Raj whispered, eyes wide. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s not just about lunches. There\u2019s something more happening here.\u201d\n\nSarah nodded but felt a knot form in her stomach as she wrestled with her thoughts. All at once, the stakes had risen. If the lunches were linked to something more significant, she needed to uncover the truth\u2014not just for herself, but for Lily. The question now was, how far was she willing to go to support her friend?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs Sarah pondered her next move, the chaotic energy of the cafeteria enveloped her, a blend of anxiety and determination fueling her resolve. She would need to approach this delicately, balancing her loyalty to Lily with her need for answers.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe scene had shifted. A palpable tension hung in the air as the girl on the table continued her tirade, and Sarah caught a glimpse of Lily\u2019s face\u2014a mixture of fear, anger, and something else, something she couldn\u2019t quite decipher but knew she would have to confront.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s talk to her after school,\u201d Raj suggested, and Sarah could only nod, her heart pounding with the weight of the decisions ahead.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Sarah feel when she sees Lily with the older girls?","options":["Pride","Fear","Guilt","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Guilt"},{"question":"Who does Sarah enlist to help her understand the situation?","options":["Lily","Raj","The teacher","The principal"],"correct_answer":"Raj"},{"question":"What unexpected event happens during lunch?","options":["A food fight","A girl standing on a table","A fire drill","A surprise party"],"correct_answer":"A girl standing on a table"},{"question":"How does Sarah feel about confronting Lily?","options":["Confident","Nervous","Disinterested","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What does Raj suggest they do after school?","options":["Go home","Talk to Lily","Have a snack","Join a club"],"correct_answer":"Talk to Lily"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch2_img1.png","plot_298_ch2_img2.png","story_298_15-18_ch2_img1_1751270563.png","story_298_15-18_ch2_img2_1751270584.png"]},"word_count":863,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
