   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_15_18","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"The sun hung high over Crestview Elementary, casting a warm glow over the bustling cafeteria. Sarah sat at her usual table, her lunch tray untouched, her mind swirling with thoughts of Lily. It had been a week since the mysterious vanishings began, and the weight of uncertainty pressed heavily on her chest. She glanced around, searching for a glimpse of her best friend, hoping to catch a sign that would ease her turmoil.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nFrom across the room, Lily's laugh rang out, a bright sound that seemed to cut through the anxiety that enveloped Sarah. But today, the laughter was tinged with something else\u2014an edge of forced cheerfulness that sent a shiver down Sarah's spine. She couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that something was off.\n\n\u201cHey, are you going to eat that?\u201d Raj\u2019s voice broke through her reverie. He nudged her tray, raising an eyebrow with a mix of curiosity and concern. \n\n\u201cI\u2019m just not hungry,\u201d Sarah replied, her voice distant. She couldn\u2019t focus on her lunch when Lily\u2019s glances towards the back of the cafeteria sent her heart racing. \n\n\u201cMore like you\u2019re worried about Lily,\u201d Raj observed, his tone teasing but gentle. \u201cYou should just ask her what\u2019s going on.\u201d \n\n\u201cI can\u2019t just ask her if she\u2019s stealing my lunch. What if I\u2019m wrong?\u201d Sarah sighed, rubbing her temples as if to dispel the mounting anxiety.\n\n\u201cYou won\u2019t know unless you confront her,\u201d Raj pressed, his expression serious now. \u201cMaybe there\u2019s something deeper happening.\u201d\n\nJust then, a loud crash erupted from the opposite end of the cafeteria, drawing the attention of every student. Sarah\u2019s heart raced as she turned to see Lily standing frozen, her lunch tray splattered across the floor. The remnants of a half-eaten sandwich and spilled juice painted a stark picture against the polished tiles. Whispers rippled through the room, and Sarah felt her stomach drop. \n\nLily stood there, eyes wide, her cheeks flushed with embarrassment. As students erupted into laughter, Sarah\u2019s instinct kicked in. She jumped out of her seat, weaving through the throng of curious onlookers. \n\n\u201cLily, are you okay?\u201d she called, her voice slicing through the noise. \n\nIn the midst of the laughter, Lily\u2019s eyes flashed with anger, her usual sweetness replaced by a fierce glare. \u201cJust leave me alone, Sarah!\u201d she snapped, her voice trembling. The cafeteria went silent, the laughter replaced by a collective breath of shock. \n\nA moment passed, tension hanging thick in the air. Sarah's heart pounded. Should she push, or should she retreat? She could feel the weight of every gaze in the room, the judgment. But the look in Lily\u2019s eyes, a mix of pain and vulnerability, compelled her to step closer.\n\n\u201cLily, please. I\u2019m not trying to judge you. I just want to understand,\u201d Sarah urged, her heart racing with the urgency of her emotions.\n\n\u201cUnderstand what? That I can\u2019t keep my lunch because I don\u2019t know how to deal with my family?\u201d The words tumbled out of Lily\u2019s mouth like a dam breaking, raw and overflowing. \u201cYou think it\u2019s funny to accuse me, but you don\u2019t know anything about me!\u201d\n\nThe anger in Lily\u2019s voice pierced through Sarah, and she took a step back, the realization crashing down on her like a wave. It wasn\u2019t just about the lunches; it was about something much deeper. \n\n\u201cLily, I\u2019m so sorry. I didn\u2019t mean to upset you. I thought\u2026\u201d Her voice faltered, the weight of her assumptions pushing down on her.\n\nBut before she could finish, a familiar figure stepped into the fray\u2014Ms. Thompson, their history teacher. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on here?\u201d she demanded, her authoritative tone silencing the murmurs.\n\nSarah glanced at Lily, who had turned away, her face a mask of frustration and hurt. The moment hung precariously in the air, and Sarah knew she had to make a choice. Would she confront this truth head-on and support her friend through her struggles, or would she retreat into the safety of her assumptions?\n\nWith the question burning in her mind, Sarah took a deep breath, ready to bridge the chasm that had formed between them. But just as she opened her mouth to speak, a shadow fell over her, darkening the room around them.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe tension reached an electrifying peak, and Sarah braced herself for a revelation that could change everything.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What incident occurs in the cafeteria that escalates the conflict?","options":["Lily spills her lunch","Sarah confronts Raj","A food fight breaks out","Ms. Thompson arrives"],"correct_answer":"Lily spills her lunch"},{"question":"How does Sarah feel about Lily during this chapter?","options":["Confident and assured","Frustrated and angry","Concerned and conflicted","Indifferent"],"correct_answer":"Concerned and conflicted"},{"question":"What does Lily reveal about her home life?","options":["She enjoys cooking","She struggles with family issues","She loves her family","She has a pet cat"],"correct_answer":"She struggles with family issues"},{"question":"What choice does Sarah face at the end of the chapter?","options":["To ignore Lily","To confront her assumptions","To leave the cafeteria","To tell Ms. Thompson"],"correct_answer":"To confront her assumptions"},{"question":"Who intervenes during the confrontation between Sarah and Lily?","options":["Raj","Another student","Ms. Thompson","The principal"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Thompson"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch3_img1.png","plot_298_ch3_img2.png","story_298_15-18_ch3_img1_1751270525.png","story_298_15-18_ch3_img2_1751270546.png"]},"word_count":746,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
