   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_298_15_18","title":"The Mystery of the Vanishing Lunch","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The cafeteria buzzed with the familiar sounds of laughter and chatter, an orchestra of adolescent voices harmonizing with the clatter of lunch trays. Sarah sat at her usual table, a corner spot where the sunlight streamed through the large windows, casting warm, inviting rays over her half-eaten apple and the remains of her sandwich. She glanced around, searching for Lily, who was running late again. The unease in Sarah\u2019s stomach twisted tighter, a silent reminder of yesterday\u2019s confrontation. \n\nJust as she was about to reach for her phone to text Lily, Raj slid into the seat across from her, his eyebrows raised in curiosity. \u201cYou look like you\u2019ve seen a ghost,\u201d he teased, but his smile faltered as he noticed the worry etched on her face.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s Lily. I don\u2019t know how to fix this,\u201d she confessed, her voice barely a whisper. \u201cI thought I understood her, but now\u2026 it\u2019s like I don\u2019t know anything at all.\u201d\n\nRaj leaned back, his expression thoughtful. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s time to talk to her properly? Not just about the lunches, but everything. Sometimes, the things we think we know are just the surface of a much deeper issue.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe sunlight illuminated the space between them, a tangible warmth that felt almost like a protective barrier against the chaos of the cafeteria. Sarah could feel the weight of Raj\u2019s words sinking in. Maybe this was what she needed\u2014a real conversation with Lily, one that transcended their usual banter and delved into the heart of their friendship.\n\nLater that afternoon, Sarah found herself standing outside Lily\u2019s house, a place that had always been a second home to her. The familiar scent of freshly cut grass mixed with the faint aroma of cookies wafting from the kitchen, but today, the cheerful ambiance felt muted, shadowed by the uncertainty of what lay ahead. She knocked gently, her heart racing in her chest.\n\nWhen Lily opened the door, her eyes were wide with surprise. \u201cSarah? What are you doing here?\u201d\n\n\u201cI wanted to talk,\u201d Sarah said, taking a hesitant step inside. \u201cAbout everything\u2014about us.\u201d\n\nAs they settled on the worn couch, the silence thickened between them, filled with unspoken words and unresolved feelings. Sarah took a deep breath, her resolve hardening. \u201cI know you\u2019ve been going through a lot. I shouldn\u2019t have jumped to conclusions about your stealing my lunch.\u201d\n\nLily\u2019s face softened, a flicker of vulnerability breaking through her usual facade. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean for it to happen. I was just so hungry and\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cLily, it\u2019s okay. I just wish you\u2019d told me. I\u2019m your friend. I want to help you,\u201d Sarah replied, her voice steady yet gentle, the weight of their shared history hanging in the air.\n\nLily\u2019s gaze fell to her hands, twisting the fabric of her sweatshirt. \u201cI didn\u2019t want you to know. I didn\u2019t want to burden you.\u201d\n\n\u201cBut that\u2019s not how friendship works! We\u2019re supposed to lean on each other, not hide from one another,\u201d Sarah urged, frustration and concern mingling in her chest.\n\nJust then, the door swung open further, revealing Lily\u2019s younger brother, Max, his face smeared with chocolate. \u201cLily, can you help me with my homework?\u201d he asked, oblivious to the tension. \n\nLily sighed, glancing at Sarah, her expression shifting from unease to a kind of reluctant acceptance. \u201cGive me a minute, okay? I\u2019ll be right there.\u201d\n\nAs Lily turned back to Sarah, something shifted. The air around them seemed to crackle with the possibility of understanding, of rebuilding what had been frayed. \u201cI promise I\u2019ll be honest from now on,\u201d Lily said softly, her voice trembling with emotion. \u201cI just didn\u2019t know how to ask for help.\u201d\n\nSarah nodded, a smile breaking through her tension. \u201cThen let\u2019s figure this out together.\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe moment hung between them, electrifying and fragile, as they reached a silent agreement to mend the rift that had threatened to pull them apart. Outside, the world continued its fast pace, but within the cocoon of the living room, hope began to bloom.\n\n\u201cCan we start fresh?\u201d Sarah suggested, her heart lifting. \u201cMaybe we can even share lunches? You know, work as a team against the cafeteria\u2019s mystery.\u201d\n\nLily laughed, a sound that felt like sunlight breaking through clouds. \u201cI\u2019d like that. But just so you know, you\u2019re going to have to share your cookies with me.\u201d\n\nAs they chatted, the laughter flowed easier, the barriers that had once separated them beginning to crumble. The deeper issues remained unaddressed, but today marked a turning point\u2014an inkling of the friendship they could revive.\n\nAs Sarah left, she felt lighter, her heart buoyed by the prospect of resolution. The mystery of the vanishing lunches had led her here, but the real journey was just beginning.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Sarah confront Lily about in this chapter?","options":["Her grades","Missing lunches","Friendship issues","Family problems"],"correct_answer":"Missing lunches"},{"question":"What does Raj suggest Sarah should do?","options":["Ignore Lily","Talk to Lily about her issues","Share her lunch","Ask the teacher for help"],"correct_answer":"Talk to Lily about her issues"},{"question":"How does Lily feel about asking for help?","options":["Confident","Reluctant","Indifferent","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Reluctant"},{"question":"What is the emotional tone of the chapter?","options":["Joyful","Tense","Mysterious","Hopeful"],"correct_answer":"Hopeful"},{"question":"What agreement do Sarah and Lily reach at the end of the chapter?","options":["To stop being friends","To share lunches","To keep their problems secret","To confront their teachers"],"correct_answer":"To share lunches"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_298_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_298_ch4_img1.png","plot_298_ch4_img2.png","story_298_15-18_ch4_img1_1751270478.png","story_298_15-18_ch4_img2_1751270505.png"]},"word_count":823,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
