   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_299_7_10","title":"The BFF Band Break-Up","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Ellie and Maya walked into the music room. It was their favorite place. The walls were bright blue, and instruments hung everywhere. Guitars, drums, and even a shiny piano sparkled in the sunlight. Jake was already there, tapping on his drums. \n\n\u201cHey, you two! Ready to rock?\u201d he asked with a grin. \n\n\u201cTotally! Let\u2019s practice our song,\u201d Ellie replied, holding her guitar tightly. \n\nMaya hesitated. \u201cUm, I was thinking maybe we could try something slower?\u201d \n\nEllie frowned. \u201cBut our song is supposed to be upbeat! We need energy for the festival!\u201d\n\nMaya bit her lip. \u201cI just want it to sound nice.\u201d \n\nEllie sighed. \u201cWe can make it sound nice and fun! It\u2019s a festival, not a lullaby!\u201d \n\nThe tension in the room thickened. Jake noticed it. \u201cHow about we take turns picking the tempo?\u201d \n\nMaya nodded slowly, but Ellie crossed her arms. \u201cFine. But we should stick to the original idea.\u201d \n\nThey started to play, but it felt wrong. The music didn\u2019t flow. \n\n\u201cStop! Let\u2019s try again,\u201d Ellie shouted, frustration bubbling up. \n\nMaya frowned. \u201cI don\u2019t think we\u2019re getting anywhere.\u201d \n\nJust then, a strange sound echoed from the corner of the room. It was a loud crash! They all turned to see a pile of music sheets on the floor. \n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d Jake asked, his eyes wide. \n\nEllie rushed over. \u201cI think something fell!\u201d \n\nMaya followed, feeling her heart race. As they picked up the sheets, Ellie found something hidden beneath them. It was an old flyer for the last music festival, with a picture of her mom singing! \n\n\u201cEllie, look!\u201d Maya exclaimed. \n\nEllie\u2019s eyes sparkled. \u201cMy mom used to sing here? I had no idea!\u201d \n\n\u201cMaybe she has tips for us?\u201d Maya suggested. \n\nEllie thought for a moment. \u201cBut I don\u2019t want to ask her. It feels... different.\u201d \n\nSuddenly, their argument about the song seemed small. They both stared at the flyer, realizing their music meant more than just a festival. \n\n\u201cWe need to figure this out,\u201d Maya said quietly. \n\n\u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d Jake asked, his drumming hands still.\n\nEllie looked at Maya. \u201cMaybe we can blend both ideas? A fast part and a slow part?\u201d \n\nMaya smiled. \u201cI like that! But we have to practice together.\u201d \n\nAs they began to play again, the door creaked open. Mr. Thompson peeked in. \u201cWhat\u2019s the commotion?\u201d \n\nEllie\u2019s heart raced. \u201cUm, we were just\u2026 trying to figure things out.\u201d \n\n\u201cGood! Remember, teamwork makes the dream work!\u201d he said, closing the door.\n\nEllie and Maya exchanged worried glances. What if they couldn\u2019t fix things in time? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey took a deep breath and dove back into the music. But the shadow of doubt lingered. Could they really work together before the festival? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nEllie felt the stress build. \u201cMaya, if we can\u2019t agree, we might have to break up the band!\u201d \n\n\u201cWhat?\u201d Maya gasped. \n\nEllie\u2019s heart sank. \u201cI can\u2019t do this without you! But we need to make a choice, fast.\u201d \n\nThe clock ticked loudly. Their friendship and their band were in jeopardy.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What instrument does Ellie play?","options":["Guitar","Drums","Piano","Violin"],"correct_answer":"Guitar"},{"question":"What is the main conflict between Ellie and Maya?","options":["Their friendship","Their music style","Jake's drumming","The weather"],"correct_answer":"Their music style"},{"question":"What did Ellie find under the music sheets?","options":["A guitar pick","An old flyer","A drumstick","A songbook"],"correct_answer":"An old flyer"},{"question":"What advice did Mr. Thompson give?","options":["Practice more","Teamwork makes the dream work","Play louder","Take a break"],"correct_answer":"Teamwork makes the dream work"},{"question":"What is Ellie worried about by the end of the chapter?","options":["Breaking up the band","Losing her guitar","Not getting to the festival","Jake's drumming"],"correct_answer":"Breaking up the band"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_299_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_299_ch3_img1.png","plot_299_ch3_img2.png","story_299_7-10_ch3_img1_1751270338.png","story_299_7-10_ch3_img2_1751270354.png"]},"word_count":521,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
