   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_299_11_14","title":"The BFF Band Break-Up","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The music room was a world of its own, bursting with colorful instruments and the vibrant hum of creativity. Ellie stood in front of her guitar, her fingers lightly strumming the strings, sending ripples of sound dancing through the air. She felt a thrill run through her\u2014today was the day they\u2019d find out if their band had been selected for the school music festival. \n\n\u201cEllie, stop daydreaming!\u201d Maya\u2019s voice broke through her thoughts, a soft laugh lacing her words. Maya was perched on a stool, her long hair falling over one shoulder as she flipped through a notebook filled with lyrics. Her hazel eyes sparkled with anticipation, but Ellie could sense a hint of nervousness beneath her calm exterior.\n\n\u201cSorry! I just can\u2019t help it,\u201d Ellie replied, a grin spreading across her face. \u201cThis could be our big break!\u201d She glanced around the room: the drum set in the corner, the keyboards, and the colorful posters of past music festivals plastered on the walls. It looked like a dreamscape, and it was about to burst with their potential.\n\nJust then, Jake burst through the door, the drummer of their trio, with a grin that could light up the dimmest day. \u201cGuess what? The announcement\u2019s in ten minutes! Are you ready to rock?\u201d He held up his sticks like a triumphant warrior.\n\n\u201cAbsolutely!\u201d Ellie exclaimed, her excitement bubbling over. \u201cWhat do you think the judges will think of our song?\u201d\n\nMaya bit her lip, glancing at her notebook. \u201cI hope they like it. I worked hard on those lyrics.\u201d \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe three friends gathered together, their faces illuminated by the glow of the overhead lights. Jake tapped his drumsticks rhythmically, while Maya hummed a few notes, her voice soft yet melodic. Ellie felt a rush of heat; they had all put so much effort into this song, and now it was time to see if it was enough.\n\nAs the minutes ticked by, the atmosphere in the room shifted. Ellie could feel the tension mounting, like a drawn bowstring ready to snap. What if the judges didn\u2019t understand their music? What if their song didn\u2019t resonate with the crowd? She glanced at Maya, who was tapping her pencil nervously against the page, and her heart tugged with concern. \n\n\u201cHey, no matter what happens, we\u2019ll still be a band, right?\u201d Ellie said, attempting to reassure her friend. \n\n\u201cRight,\u201d Maya replied, but the uncertainty in her voice was unmistakable.\n\nJust then, the school principal appeared at the doorway, clearing her throat to capture their attention. \u201cAlright, everyone. The results are in!\u201d\n\nEllie\u2019s heart raced faster than ever. She could hardly breathe as the principal announced the names of the bands selected for the festival. One by one, they heard familiar group names echoed in the room, but Ellie could feel a knot tightening in her stomach. \n\n\u201cAnd the final band to perform is\u2026 The Harmony Crew!\u201d The principal\u2019s voice boomed, and for a moment, Ellie was paralyzed by disbelief. Then, it hit her like a burst of sunlight breaking through clouds\u2014They had made it! \n\n\u201cYES!\u201d Jake shouted, jumping up and down, his sticks clashing in celebration.\n\nBut then Ellie turned to Maya, expecting to see her face light up with joy. Instead, she found a frown etched on her features. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d Ellie asked, confusion swirling inside her.\n\n\u201cI\u2014I just don\u2019t think our song is good enough,\u201d Maya admitted, her voice barely above a whisper, yet the weight of her words filled the room. \u201cWhat if we fail?\u201d\n\nEllie's heart sank. Their excitement was starting to unravel, and with it, their friendship. \u201cMaya, we can work on it together. We have time, right?\u201d\n\nA long silence stretched between them, thick with uncertainty. \u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Maya said, and Ellie felt a chill creep into the air.\n\nAs they gathered their things, Ellie couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that this was only the beginning of their challenges. \n\nWould they be able to find their rhythm again before the big show?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the name of the band that was selected for the festival?","options":["The Harmony Crew","The Rhythm Band","Ellie and Friends","Maya's Dream"],"correct_answer":"The Harmony Crew"},{"question":"What instrument does Ellie play?","options":["Drums","Keyboard","Guitar","Violin"],"correct_answer":"Guitar"},{"question":"How does Maya feel about their song at first?","options":["Excited","Confident","Nervous","Angry"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What does Jake do when they hear the results?","options":["Sits quietly","Starts crying","Jumps up and down","Leaves the room"],"correct_answer":"Jumps up and down"},{"question":"What is the main conflict introduced in this chapter?","options":["Ellie and Jake fight","Maya is unhappy with the band","Creative differences threaten their friendship","They lose their instruments"],"correct_answer":"Creative differences threaten their friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_299_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_299_ch1_img1.png","plot_299_ch1_img2.png","story_299_11-14_ch1_img1_1751270229.png","story_299_11-14_ch1_img2_1751270250.png"]},"word_count":682,"reading_level":"Builder"}
