   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_299_11_14","title":"The BFF Band Break-Up","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the vibrant sounds of laughter and chatter echoed through the school hallways, Ellie and Maya found themselves in the music room, which was buzzing with anticipation for the upcoming festival. The room was alive with colorful posters of past performances, and the air smelled faintly of fresh paint and popcorn from the cafeteria. Ellie strummed her guitar, fingers dancing over the strings like a butterfly flitting from flower to flower. She had always loved the rush of creating music, and the thought of performing at the festival lit a fire in her heart.\n\nMaya stood in front of the microphone, her fingers nervously fiddling with her necklace. She had a beautiful voice, but speaking up was always a challenge. The excitement in the room felt electric, but Ellie sensed an undercurrent of tension swirling between them. \u201cLet\u2019s try that new song we wrote!\u201d Ellie suggested, her eyes sparkling with enthusiasm.\n\n\u201cUm, okay,\u201d Maya replied quietly, her voice barely above a whisper. She took a deep breath and nodded, trying to match Ellie\u2019s excitement. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThey started the song, the notes weaving together like threads in a tapestry. But halfway through, Ellie\u2019s guitar riff clashed with Maya\u2019s melody. \u201cWait, hold on,\u201d Ellie said, stopping mid-strum. \u201cI think we need to change the tempo here.\u201d\n\n\u201cChange the tempo?\u201d Maya blinked, her brow furrowing in confusion. \u201cBut I thought we decided to keep it slow. It gives the song emotion.\u201d\n\nEllie shrugged, frustration bubbling just beneath the surface. \u201cBut it feels too\u2026 sleepy. We need more energy! It\u2019s a festival, not a lullaby!\u201d\n\nMaya's cheeks tinged pink, and she crossed her arms. \u201cWell, not everyone can be as loud and energetic as you, Ellie. I want people to feel something when they hear my voice.\u201d\n\nEllie opened her mouth to argue, but the hurt in Maya\u2019s eyes made her hesitate. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean it like that,\u201d she said softly. \u201cI just want our song to be the best it can be.\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe you should just play solo then,\u201d Maya shot back, her heart pounding. \u201cYou obviously have a vision for how this should go!\u201d\n\nThe room fell silent, save for the distant sound of students laughing in the halls. Jake, their quirky drummer, who had been observing from the sidelines, decided to jump in. \u201cHey, why don\u2019t we take a break? We can grab some snacks and talk this out. Sometimes it\u2019s hard to see the music when you\u2019re too close to it.\u201d\n\nMaya nodded vigorously, grateful for the distraction. \u201cYeah, maybe we need to step back for a bit.\u201d\n\nAs they left the music room, Ellie couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that their friendship was hanging by a thread. What if they couldn\u2019t resolve this? What if the band broke up before they even got on stage? The thought was like a dark cloud threatening to overshadow their dreams.\n\nOnce outside, they wandered into the cafeteria, the aroma of pizza and fries enveloping them like a warm hug. But instead of enjoying their meal, Ellie picked at her food, her mind racing. \u201cJake, what do you think? Should we change the song to make it more upbeat?\u201d she asked, her voice strained.\n\nJake shrugged, his usual goofy demeanor replaced with a serious expression. \u201cHonestly, I think both of you have good points. But if you want to make it work, you\u2019ll need to find common ground. Music is like a dance; it takes two to tango.\u201d \n\nEllie and Maya exchanged glances, unsure of how to bridge their differences. Could they really save their band? Just then, Ellie noticed something out of the corner of her eye\u2014a poster on the wall announcing a local music competition that would take place right after the festival. A spark of inspiration flickered inside her, but was it the right time to bring it up?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cHey, look at this!\u201d Ellie exclaimed, pointing at the poster. \u201cMaybe we could enter this competition too! It could be our chance to showcase our style together.\u201d\n\nMaya hesitated, biting her lip. \u201cWhat if we aren\u2019t ready? What if we mess up?\u201d\n\nEllie felt a surge of determination. \u201cBut what if we succeed? This could be our moment!\u201d\n\nWith her heart pounding, Ellie realized they were at a crossroads. It was time for them to decide: would they fight through their differences and take a leap of faith together, or would they let fear pull them apart?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What causes tension between Ellie and Maya during their practice?","options":["Ellie wants to change the tempo","Maya doesn't want to sing","Jake brings snacks","They forget the lyrics"],"correct_answer":"Ellie wants to change the tempo"},{"question":"What suggestion does Jake make to help resolve the conflict?","options":["Take a break","Change the song","Stop practicing","Leave the band"],"correct_answer":"Take a break"},{"question":"What opportunity does Ellie notice at the end of the chapter?","options":["A music festival","A local music competition","A talent show","A school concert"],"correct_answer":"A local music competition"},{"question":"How does Ellie feel about the possibility of the band breaking up?","options":["Indifferent","Excited","Confident","Worried"],"correct_answer":"Worried"},{"question":"What metaphor does Jake use to describe working together in music?","options":["Music is a journey","Music is like a dance","Music is a puzzle","Music is a story"],"correct_answer":"Music is like a dance"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_299_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_299_ch2_img1.png","plot_299_ch2_img2.png","story_299_11-14_ch2_img1_1751270184.png","story_299_11-14_ch2_img2_1751270213.png"]},"word_count":753,"reading_level":"Builder"}
