   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_299_11_14","title":"The BFF Band Break-Up","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Chapter 3: Crescendo of Conflict\n\nThe music room buzzed with a mixture of excitement and anxiety. Sunlight streamed through the tall windows, casting a golden glow on the rows of instruments waiting to be played. Ellie sat on a worn-out stool, her guitar cradled in her arms like a precious treasure. She strummed a few chords, the harmonious sounds filling the air. Across from her, Maya stood clutching her microphone, her gaze locked on the ground. Jake, their quirky drummer, tapped a beat on his knees, trying to lighten the heavy atmosphere.\n\n\u201cCome on, Maya! Just let loose a little,\u201d Ellie urged, her voice cheerful but edged with frustration. They had practiced the same song for what felt like hours, but something felt off. \u201cYou\u2019ve got an amazing voice! I know you can do better than that.\u201d\n\nMaya\u2019s cheeks flushed pink as she bit her lip. \u201cIt\u2019s just... I\u2019m not sure if this is the right style for me,\u201d she admitted, her voice barely above a whisper. \u201cI mean, what if the judges don\u2019t like it?\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nEllie let out an exasperated sigh. She had always loved Maya\u2019s voice, but lately, it felt like every time they rehearsed, they were drifting further apart. \u201cBut we\u2019re supposed to be a team! If you don\u2019t believe in yourself, how can we expect anyone else to?\u201d \n\nMaya looked up, her brown eyes shimmering with unshed tears. \u201cIt\u2019s not that simple, Ellie. I just feel like I\u2019m not good enough. You\u2019re so talented, and Jake...\u201d She glanced nervously at Jake, who was lost in his own rhythm. \u201cWhat if I mess it up? We can\u2019t afford to fail now, not with the festival coming up!\u201d\n\nJake, sensing the tension, chimed in, \u201cHey, you know what they say, right? \u2018Practice makes perfect!\u2019 We can work it out together!\u201d \n\nBut Ellie\u2019s patience was wearing thin. \u201cTogether? It feels like I\u2019m the only one who cares about this band!\u201d \n\nThe words hung in the air, thick as fog. Maya\u2019s face hardened, and in an instant, the bond they had forged felt like it was teetering on the edge of collapse. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s not worth fighting for if you think that,\u201d Maya replied, her voice trembling.\n\n\u201cWait! What do you mean by that?\u201d Ellie shot back, her heart racing. \n\nMaya hesitated. \u201cI\u2026 I think maybe I need to find my own sound. I don\u2019t want to hold you back, Ellie. I just can\u2019t do this right now.\u201d\n\nEllie could feel the space between them widening, like a chasm that threatened to swallow her whole. \u201cYou can\u2019t just give up!\u201d she exclaimed, her voice rising. \u201cThis band is everything to me! It\u2019s not just about the music, it\u2019s about us!\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe it\u2019s time to choose, then,\u201d Maya whispered, her words cutting deeper than any guitar string. \u201cAre you ready to pick the band over our friendship?\u201d\n\nThe silence fell heavy, each heartbeat pounding like a drum. Ellie\u2019s mind raced, and she felt trapped between her passion for music and her fear of losing her best friend. \u201cMaya, please\u2026\u201d\n\nBefore she could finish her thought, Jake intervened, \u201cGuys, we\u2019re better together. Let\u2019s figure this out before it\u2019s too late.\u201d But Ellie barely heard him; the tension was suffocating, and she couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that everything was crumbling around her.\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from the storage room next door, breaking their moment of silence. \u201cWhat was that?\u201d Maya jumped, eyes wide with alarm.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d Ellie replied, adrenaline pumping through her veins. \u201cBut I think we should check it out. It might give us a distraction\u2026 or maybe an answer.\u201d\n\nAs they cautiously approached the door, Ellie felt a knot in her stomach. The festival was just days away, and their friendship was hanging by a thread. What if the answer they found changed everything?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut as they opened the door, the mystery revealed itself in a swirl of dust and scattered papers, and Ellie realized that this could either be the beginning of a new chapter or the end of everything they had built. They stood on the brink, and whatever lay ahead would determine the fate of their band\u2014and their friendship.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Ellie want Maya to do during rehearsal?","options":["Sing louder","Let loose a little","Play the guitar","Practice more"],"correct_answer":"Let loose a little"},{"question":"What is Maya's main concern about their performance?","options":["Not having enough time to practice","Her voice not being good enough","The band breaking up","Ellie being too bossy"],"correct_answer":"Her voice not being good enough"},{"question":"How does Ellie feel about the future of the band?","options":["Indifferent","Excited","Determined","Scared"],"correct_answer":"Determined"},{"question":"What interrupts the intense conversation between the girls?","options":["A phone call","A loud crash","A teacher entering","Jake playing a solo"],"correct_answer":"A loud crash"},{"question":"What is the main conflict in this chapter?","options":["Ellie and Maya disagree about a song","The band is chosen for the festival","Maya considers leaving the band","Jake wants to change the drumming style"],"correct_answer":"Maya considers leaving the band"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_299_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_299_ch3_img1.png","plot_299_ch3_img2.png","story_299_11-14_ch3_img1_1751270150.png","story_299_11-14_ch3_img2_1751270169.png"]},"word_count":728,"reading_level":"Builder"}
