   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_299_11_14","title":"The BFF Band Break-Up","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Chapter 4: Finding the Beat\n\nThe music room buzzed with the lively energy of students preparing for the school music festival. Posters of colorful guitars and microphones plastered the walls, and the air smelled faintly of polished wood and fresh paint. Ellie sat on a stool, her guitar cradled in her arms, strumming a few notes absentmindedly. Her heart raced, but it wasn\u2019t from excitement; instead, it felt heavy with worry about Maya. \n\n\u201cEllie, can you play that part again?\u201d Jake's voice broke through her thoughts. He was hunched over the drums, tapping out a rhythm that filled the room with a pulse. \n\n\u201cUh, sure,\u201d Ellie replied, trying to push aside her unease. She launched into the chorus of their original song, but the notes felt off, like a puzzle missing its final piece. \n\nJust as Jake began to nod along, the door swung open with a loud creak. Maya stepped in, her expression a mix of determination and uncertainty. \u201cHey, guys!\u201d she called out, but the excitement in her voice felt strained. \n\nEllie\u2019s heart sank. It was hard to ignore the tension that had been brewing since their last rehearsal. The air felt thick with unsaid words, like storm clouds hanging overhead. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nMaya walked over to her spot, glancing at her guitar, which lay untouched on its stand. She seemed lost in thought, her gaze distant. \u201cCan we talk about the song structure? I think we should change the bridge,\u201d she suggested, her voice barely above a whisper.\n\nEllie felt a flicker of frustration. \u201cWe\u2019ve already discussed this, Maya. The bridge is fine the way it is. It\u2019s what gives the song its energy!\u201d\n\n\u201cEnergy? Or chaos?\u201d Maya shot back, her cheeks reddening. \u201cI\u2019m just trying to make sure it\u2019s perfect for the festival!\u201d \n\n\u201cPerfect?\u201d Ellie\u2019s voice rose, echoing throughout the room. \u201cYou mean perfect in your way!\u201d \n\nJake, sensing the rising tension, set down his drumsticks. \u201cWhoa, hold on. This isn\u2019t helping. We need to find a way to make this work, not tear each other apart.\u201d \n\nEllie crossed her arms, bitterness bubbling within her. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s not worth it if it\u2019s just going to be a fight every step of the way!\u201d \n\nMaya\u2019s eyes dropped to the floor, hurt flashing across her face. \u201cI thought we were a team,\u201d she murmured, her voice cracking.\n\nThe passion behind Maya\u2019s words echoed in Ellie\u2019s heart, softening her anger. She took a deep breath, trying to steady her thoughts. \u201cWe are a team, but we need to listen to each other. Maybe we can compromise?\u201d\n\nMaya looked up, hope flickering in her eyes. \u201cYou mean\u2026 we could try both ideas in the bridge? See what feels right?\u201d \n\n\u201cYeah, let\u2019s give it a shot. I really want this to work too,\u201d Ellie said, a small smile breaking through. \n\nAs they began to brainstorm together, the tension that once filled the room started to dissipate, replaced by a sense of collaboration. They experimented with both melodies, their voices rising and falling in harmony. With every note, they found a rhythm that was uniquely theirs\u2014one that blended their differences into something beautiful.\n\nJust then, a loud crash echoed from the back of the room, startling them. They turned to see a stack of music stands topple over, revealing a dusty, old trunk they had never noticed before.\n\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that?\u201d Jake exclaimed, eyes wide with curiosity. \n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, but it looks interesting!\u201d Maya said, her earlier worries forgotten as excitement danced on her face. \n\nEllie felt a thrill of adventure bubbling up inside her. \u201cLet\u2019s check it out!\u201d \n\nAs they approached the trunk, the possibility of uncovering something special filled the air with anticipation. Perhaps it could help them not only find their music again but also mend their friendship.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe three friends gathered around the trunk, hearts pounding with a mixture of nerves and excitement. Whatever lay inside might just be the key to turning their band\u2014and their friendship\u2014back into something truly magical.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ellie and Maya initially disagree about?","options":["The festival location","The song structure","Jake's drumming","Their friendship"],"correct_answer":"The song structure"},{"question":"What emotion does Maya express when she feels hurt by Ellie?","options":["Anger","Frustration","Sadness","Happiness"],"correct_answer":"Sadness"},{"question":"What do the friends discover at the end of the chapter?","options":["A new song","An old trunk","A recording studio","A lost instrument"],"correct_answer":"An old trunk"},{"question":"What is Jake's role in the band?","options":["Guitarist","Vocalist","Drummer","Manager"],"correct_answer":"Drummer"},{"question":"What do Ellie and Maya ultimately agree to do about their song?","options":["Change the entire song","Try both of their ideas in the bridge","Stop practicing","Invite more band members"],"correct_answer":"Try both of their ideas in the bridge"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_299_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_299_ch4_img1.png","plot_299_ch4_img2.png","story_299_11-14_ch4_img1_1751270118.png","story_299_11-14_ch4_img2_1751270135.png"]},"word_count":684,"reading_level":"Builder"}
