   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_299_11_14","title":"The BFF Band Break-Up","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"The music room buzzed with anticipation. Ellie and Maya stood side by side, their fingers brushing against their instruments. The walls were adorned with posters of past music festivals, a reminder of the excitement and creativity that thrived within those four walls. Jake, their quirky drummer, was busy setting up his gear, a whirlwind of energy and enthusiasm. \n\n\u201cCan you believe we\u2019re actually performing at the festival?\u201d Ellie exclaimed, her eyes sparkling. She strummed a few notes on her guitar, letting the sound resonate through the room. \n\n\u201cI know! It\u2019s like a dream come true!\u201d Maya replied, her voice slightly shaky but filled with excitement. However, a flicker of doubt crossed her face. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nBut as they started rehearsing their song, the tension from their earlier conflicts resurfaced. Ellie\u2019s guitar riffs clashed with Maya\u2019s softer melodies, creating a cacophony instead of harmony. With each missed note, Ellie\u2019s frustration grew. \u201cMaya, can you try to sing a little louder? We need to make a real impact!\u201d \n\n\u201cI-I\u2019m trying, okay? It\u2019s just\u2026 I\u2019m not used to this kind of pressure,\u201d Maya stammered, her shyness creeping back. \n\n\u201cYou\u2019re too soft! We\u2019re supposed to be a band, not a lullaby,\u201d Ellie snapped, her voice sharper than she intended. \n\nMaya\u2019s expression crumpled, and Ellie instantly regretted her words. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean to hurt you,\u201d she said more softly, reaching out. \u201cBut we need to figure this out before the festival. It\u2019s our big chance!\u201d \n\nAs they took a break, Maya pulled out the old trunk they had discovered during their last rehearsal. \u201cMaybe we can use some of these old notes to inspire us?\u201d she suggested, her eyes lighting up with curiosity.\n\nEllie nodded, intrigued. They both knelt down and opened the trunk, revealing a treasure trove of forgotten song ideas, lyrics scribbled on napkins, and a dusty old notebook. As they flipped through the pages, memories of their musical journey washed over them, reminding them of why they started the band in the first place. \n\n\u201cThis one!\u201d Maya pointed to a faded piece of paper. \u201cRemember when we wrote this together in your garage?\u201d \n\nEllie smiled, the tension in the room easing. \u201cYeah! We can blend that with the new stuff we\u2019ve been working on. It\u2019ll be amazing!\u201d \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s try it!\u201d Maya exclaimed, her smile returning. \n\nThey spent the next hour experimenting with the old and new ideas, their voices blending together in perfect harmony. The music flowed like a river, strong and beautiful. \n\n\u201cSee? When we work together, it\u2019s magic,\u201d Ellie said, feeling a sense of unity wash over them. \n\nSuddenly, Jake burst in, holding a pair of drumsticks like a conductor\u2019s baton. \u201cWhat\u2019s this? A collaboration? I love it!\u201d \n\nAs they played together, laughter filled the room, and the worries of the festival began to drift away. They were no longer just Ellie and Maya; they were a team\u2014two friends who had found their rhythm once again.\n\nAs they finished their song, they looked at each other, a shared understanding sparking between them. \u201cNo more fighting, okay?\u201d Ellie said earnestly.\n\n\u201cAgreed,\u201d Maya replied, her voice filled with warmth. \u201cWe\u2019re better together.\u201d \n\nWith a renewed sense of purpose, they moved forward, ready to face the festival together, stronger than ever.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What major conflict do Ellie and Maya face in this chapter?","options":["Creative differences","Lack of instruments","Jake's absence","Their school's rules"],"correct_answer":"Creative differences"},{"question":"What do Ellie and Maya discover that helps them with their music?","options":["A new songbook","An old trunk","A famous music video","A music teacher's advice"],"correct_answer":"An old trunk"},{"question":"How does Ellie feel after snapping at Maya?","options":["Excited","Regretful","Indifferent","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Regretful"},{"question":"What emotion does Maya primarily show at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["Confidence","Doubt","Anger","Indifference"],"correct_answer":"Doubt"},{"question":"What lesson do Ellie and Maya learn by the end of the chapter?","options":["They should quit the band","They can work through their differences","They don't need Jake","They should perform solo"],"correct_answer":"They can work through their differences"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_299_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_299_ch5_img1.png","plot_299_ch5_img2.png","story_299_11-14_ch5_img1_1751270067.png","story_299_11-14_ch5_img2_1751270084.png"]},"word_count":559,"reading_level":"Builder"}
