   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_299_15_18","title":"The BFF Band Break-Up","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"The music room hummed with an undercurrent of tension, a stark contrast to the vibrant decorations for the upcoming festival. Ellie adjusted her guitar strap, her fingers trembling slightly as she strummed a few chords, the sound echoing in the otherwise quiet space. Maya sat cross-legged on the floor, her notebook sprawled open next to her, filled with hastily scribbled lyrics and doodles. Jake was absent\u2014a rare occurrence that left the air thick with unspoken words.\n\n\u201cEllie, can we just talk about what happened yesterday?\u201d Maya\u2019s voice was barely above a whisper, but the weight of her request hung heavily in the air. Ellie paused, her heart racing. It was clear they couldn\u2019t avoid the fallout any longer.\n\n\u201cDo we have to?\u201d Ellie snapped, her frustration bubbling over. \u201cYou suggested replacing me! How is that even a conversation we have?\u201d\n\nMaya flinched, her gaze dropping to the notebook. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean it like that. I just\u2014\u201d\n\n\u201cJust what? Think I\u2019m not good enough?\u201d Ellie felt the heat rise in her cheeks, betraying her true emotions. She clenched her fists around the guitar, the instrument suddenly feeling like a weight rather than a source of solace.\n\n\u201cNo! Ellie, it\u2019s not that! I\u2019m scared,\u201d Maya said, her voice rising as she finally looked up. \u201cWe have a chance to be something great, but what if we fail? What if I can\u2019t keep up with you?\u201d\n\nEllie took a deep breath, the tension slowly unraveling into something fragile. \u201cMaya, we need to get through this together. I\u2019ve always been scared too. Especially about losing this\u2014us.\u201d\n\nFor a moment, silence enveloped them, fragile yet profound. Ellie noticed the sunlight streaming in through the window, casting soft shadows across the room. It illuminated the dust motes swirling in the air, creating an almost magical atmosphere. She suddenly felt a flicker of hope. Could they mend the rift?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs the morning wore on, they worked through their frustrations in a series of jam sessions. The rhythm of their music shifted, mirroring the unspoken dialogue between them. Ellie found herself experimenting with new guitar riffs, while Maya\u2019s lyrics transformed from hesitant lines into powerful verses. They began to rediscover their shared vision\u2014one that fused Ellie\u2019s fiery guitar with Maya\u2019s soulful voice.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s try that chorus again,\u201d Ellie suggested, her excitement bubbling over. \u201cBut this time, try to let it soar. Feel it, Maya!\u201d\n\nMaya nodded, her eyes alight with determination. As they began to play, the room transformed. The walls, once lined with reminders of their discord, now resonated with the harmonies of their efforts, blending seamlessly.\n\n\u201cJake will be back tomorrow,\u201d Ellie said, breaking the rhythm as they took a breather. \u201cWe should show him what we\u2019ve worked on.\u201d\n\nMaya smiled, a bright spark igniting in her eyes. \u201cYeah, I want him to see this new direction. It feels\u2026right.\u201d\n\nBut just then, a sharp knock interrupted their moment of peace. Jake burst through the door, his usual energetic demeanor slightly dimmed. \u201cHey, guys! Sorry I\u2019m late. You won\u2019t believe what I\u2014\u201d He paused, sensing the shift in the atmosphere. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d\n\nEllie exchanged a glance with Maya, her heart racing as she prepared to explain their rocky past week. \u201cWe\u2019ve been\u2026working things out,\u201d she admitted, the weight of the moment settling around them like an embrace.\n\nMaya added, \u201cWe\u2019re trying to find a way back to what we started. Can we show you?\u201d The invitation hung heavy with possibility.\n\nAs they launched into their newly-crafted song, something shifted in the room. The music carried their doubts and fears, intertwining them into a tapestry of sound. Jake\u2019s drumming joined in, a steady heartbeat propelling them toward something greater.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nIn that instance, the noise faded into a melody of hope. Ellie felt the walls of their friendship begin to mend, brick by brick, note by note.\n\nThe song concluded, leaving a palpable silence that buzzed with anticipation. \u201cWow, guys, that was epic,\u201d Jake finally exclaimed, his enthusiasm rekindling. \u201cYou both have something amazing here. We just need to keep building on it.\u201d\n\nEllie and Maya shared a glance, their hearts buoyed by the promise of collaboration. It wasn\u2019t over yet, but today felt like the first step toward healing. The festival was just around the corner, and they had a chance to reclaim their sound and their friendship.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s get back to work,\u201d Ellie said, a smile breaking through the tension. \u201cWe have a show to prepare for.\u201d\n\nAs they dove back into the music, Ellie felt a surge of excitement. Maybe, just maybe, they could find their rhythm again before the big show.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Ellie and Maya primarily confront in this chapter?","options":["Their creative differences","Jake's absence","The upcoming festival","Their musical inspirations"],"correct_answer":"Their creative differences"},{"question":"What emotion does Maya express when she suggests replacing Ellie?","options":["Fear","Joy","Anger","Confusion"],"correct_answer":"Fear"},{"question":"What do Ellie and Maya begin to rediscover in this chapter?","options":["Their friendship","Their individual styles","Their instruments","Their band\u2019s name"],"correct_answer":"Their friendship"},{"question":"How does Jake react when he returns to the music room?","options":["He is indifferent","He is excited","He is sad","He interrupts them"],"correct_answer":"He is excited"},{"question":"What is the main theme of this chapter?","options":["Competition","Fear of failure","Collaboration","Friendship"],"correct_answer":"Collaboration"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_299_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_299_ch4_img1.png","plot_299_ch4_img2.png","story_299_15-18_ch4_img1_1751269915.png"]},"word_count":797,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
