   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_300_11_14","title":"The Social Media Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The bright halls of Riverdale High buzzed like a hive, students zipping past with their heads buried in glowing screens. Jamie\u2019s laughter echoed as she strolled with her best friend Kira, her caramel curls bouncing with every step. The walls, splashed with murals of bright colors and hashtags, felt alive, just like the digital world they were both a part of.\n\n\u201cDid you see the views on my latest video?\u201d Jamie beamed, pulling out her phone to check the numbers once more.\n\nKira forced a smile, her heart sinking like a stone. \u201cYeah, it\u2019s... really impressive,\u201d she replied, her voice trailing off. It was hard to be genuinely happy when Jamie\u2019s viral fame was like a spotlight, shining bright and warm, while Kira felt left in the shadows.\n\nAs they turned the corner, Jamie spotted their tech-savvy classmate Jordan, who was tapping away at his tablet, oblivious to the world around him. \u201cHey, Jordan!\u201d Jamie called, her enthusiasm infectious. \u201cDid you see my video?\u201d\n\nJordan looked up, his eyes widening. \u201cOf course! It\u2019s everywhere! Even Mr. Thompson mentioned it in class today. You\u2019re a star!\u201d\n\nKira couldn\u2019t help but roll her eyes slightly, her jealousy bubbling just beneath the surface. \u201cYeah, a star. How great for you, Jamie,\u201d she muttered under her breath.\n\nFeeling the tension, Jamie glanced at Kira, confusion flickering across her face. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong? You don\u2019t sound excited.\u201d\n\nKira shrugged, biting her lip. \u201cNothing. Just... you know, the usual.\u201d But it wasn\u2019t nothing. Every time her phone buzzed with likes and comments meant for Jamie, it felt like a dagger in her chest, each notification a reminder of her own quiet life, of standing in Jamie\u2019s shadow.\n\nAs they walked into the cafeteria, the buzz of chatter and clinking trays surrounded them like a wave. Kira watched as students surrounded Jamie, eager to hear about her latest video. She could see Jamie basking in the attention, a bright beam of sunlight while Kira felt like a forgotten cloud.\n\nSuddenly, someone called out, \u201cHey Jamie! Show us the dance from your video!\u201d The crowd erupted in cheers, and Jamie's eyes sparkled with joy. Kira felt her stomach twist. The laughter and excitement wrapped around Jamie like a cozy blanket, but Kira felt cold and alone.\n\n\u201cCome on, Kira! You should join in!\u201d Jamie invited, turning to her friend with a hopeful smile. But Kira shook her head, the knot in her stomach tightening. Jamie\u2019s shining moment felt like a spotlight that dimmed Kira\u2019s own.\n\n\u201cI\u2019ll just, um, get us some drinks,\u201d Kira said quickly, breaking away from the group. As she walked to the counter, she felt the heat of betrayal creeping into her heart. Why did Jamie have to steal the show? \n\nThe cafeteria felt deafeningly loud, and Kira found herself staring at the menu, not really seeing it. Just then, she caught a glimpse of Jamie through the crowd, laughing and smiling as the music played. It was a beautiful moment, but Kira\u2019s heart ached. A sudden thought hit her: Would she ever be more than just Jamie\u2019s best friend?\n\nJust then, a notification popped up on her phone. It was a comment on Jamie\u2019s video that made her freeze. \u201cKira is just Jamie\u2019s sidekick.\u201d The words felt heavy, like a backpack full of rocks. \n\nKira\u2019s heart raced, a mix of anger and sadness colliding inside her. She gripped her phone tighter, her knuckles turning white. This was more than just a video now; it felt like a battle for her identity, her place in the world.\n\nAnd in that moment, as she stared into the bright screen, Kira made a decision. She would not let this define her. She would show Jamie\u2014and everyone\u2014that she was more than just the girl in the background.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nKira\u2019s thoughts swirled, and she felt a surge of determination as she glanced at Jamie, who was surrounded by friends and laughter. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nAs Jamie danced, Kira\u2019s expression shifted, her determination evident, a fire igniting in her eyes. The cafeteria\u2019s laughter faded into the background, and Kira felt a storm brewing within her.\n\nHow would she confront Jamie about how she felt? The thought lingered in her mind, as uncertain as the future.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is the main conflict introduced in Chapter 1?","options":["Jamie becomes too popular","Kira feels overshadowed by Jamie","Jordan tries to steal Jamie's spotlight","They both forget about each other"],"correct_answer":"Kira feels overshadowed by Jamie"},{"question":"How does Kira feel about Jamie's success?","options":["Happy and supportive","Indifferent","Jealous and resentful","Proud"],"correct_answer":"Jealous and resentful"},{"question":"What does the cafeteria symbolize in the story?","options":["A place of friendship","A hub of social media drama","A quiet study area","A sports center"],"correct_answer":"A hub of social media drama"},{"question":"What does Kira decide to do at the end of the chapter?","options":["Forget about Jamie","Confront Jamie about her feelings","Join in the dance","Leave the school"],"correct_answer":"Confront Jamie about her feelings"},{"question":"Who is the tech-savvy classmate mentioned in Chapter 1?","options":["Jamie","Kira","Jordan","Mr. Thompson"],"correct_answer":"Jordan"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_300_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_300_ch1_img1.png","plot_300_ch1_img2.png","story_300_11-14_ch1_img1_1751269650.png","story_300_11-14_ch1_img2_1751269673.png"]},"word_count":727,"reading_level":"Builder"}
