   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_300_11_14","title":"The Social Media Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the sun peeked through the tall windows of Riverdale High, casting a warm glow on the buzzing hallways, Jamie felt a rush of excitement. Her phone buzzed with notification after notification, each one a reminder that her viral video was trending. Students milled around her, laughing and chatting, their faces lit up by the glow of their screens, but Jamie barely noticed anyone else. She was riding high on her newfound popularity, basking in the attention, as if she were the star of her own movie.\n\nKira, on the other hand, stood a few steps away, her heart sinking with each cheer that erupted from the crowd around Jamie. She watched as her best friend exchanged high-fives and selfies, the envy curling up in her stomach like a heavy stone. \u201cHey, Jamie!\u201d she called, forcing a smile. \u201cThat was a really great video.\u201d\n\n\u201cThanks, Kira!\u201d Jamie replied, her eyes sparkling. \u201cDid you see all the views? I\u2019m almost at a million!\u201d\n\nKira nodded, but her smile felt like a mask. How could she celebrate Jamie\u2019s success when it felt like her own shadow was growing longer? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nJust then, Jordan, the tech-savvy boy from their math class, approached them with a curious look. \u201cWow, Jamie! You\u2019re basically famous now. I mean, everyone is talking about you.\u201d He turned to Kira, his expression shifting slightly. \u201cAnd, uh, how do you feel about it?\u201d\n\nKira hesitated. \u201cIt\u2019s great for Jamie. Really.\u201d Her words felt hollow, even to her. To hide her discomfort, she picked at the fraying edge of her backpack strap, her mind racing.\n\n\u201cCome on, Kira! Let\u2019s celebrate after school!\u201d Jamie suggested, her voice bubbling with enthusiasm. \u201cWe could post about it together!\u201d\n\nKira\u2019s heart sank further. Together? It felt more like Jamie\u2019s moment, not theirs. \u201cYeah, sure,\u201d she replied, forcing the excitement into her tone. \u201cSounds fun.\u201d But she couldn\u2019t shake the feeling of being an extra in Jamie\u2019s story.\n\nLater that day, as they settled down in the library for their usual study session, Kira\u2019s fingers drummed nervously on the table. \u201cSo, what\u2019s the plan for this video thing?\u201d she asked, trying to sound casual.\n\n\u201cI was thinking maybe I could do a challenge video next,\u201d Jamie said, tapping her chin thoughtfully. \u201cYou know, like the one where you try to eat a lemon without making a face. People love that stuff!\u201d\n\nKira\u2019s heart raced. \u201cBut what about the things we used to do together? Like our skits?\u201d \n\nJamie looked taken aback. \u201cOh, Kira! I didn\u2019t mean to step on your toes. We can still do them, I promise!\u201d Yet, Kira could see the excitement in Jamie\u2019s eyes; it was a new world, one she was eager to conquer, with or without her.\n\nSuddenly, Jordan appeared at their table again, his face serious. \u201cHey, I\u2019ve been hearing rumors about a fake account that\u2019s been making fun of Jamie\u2019s video. They\u2019re calling it cringy and saying it\u2019s just for attention.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat? That\u2019s not fair!\u201d Kira exclaimed, feeling a mix of anger and concern for Jamie. Jamie\u2019s face fell, the spark in her eyes dulling. \u201cI didn\u2019t know about that. Do you know who it is?\u201d\n\nJordan shook his head. \u201cNo one knows yet, but it\u2019s causing a stir. You should be careful, Jamie.\u201d\n\nJamie\u2019s expression shifted to one of uncertainty. \u201cI didn\u2019t think this would happen. I just wanted to have fun.\u201d\n\nAs Kira watched her friend\u2019s excitement wane, something inside her twisted painfully. The friendship they had built was suddenly standing on a tightrope, swaying in the winds of jealousy and insecurity. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s watch the video together,\u201d Kira suggested, her voice barely above a whisper. Maybe if they faced it together, they could find a way back to the friendship they once had.\n\nAs Jamie nodded, a new challenge loomed on the horizon, and Kira felt the weight of their friendship resting in her hands.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"How does Kira feel about Jamie's newfound popularity?","options":["Excited","Jealous","Indifferent","Supportive"],"correct_answer":"Jealous"},{"question":"What idea does Jamie have for her next video?","options":["A cooking tutorial","A challenge video","A music cover","A vlog about her day"],"correct_answer":"A challenge video"},{"question":"What rumor does Jordan share with Jamie and Kira?","options":["That Jamie's video is fake","That Jamie's video is cringy","That Kira is jealous","That Jamie is unfriendly"],"correct_answer":"That Jamie's video is cringy"},{"question":"What does Kira suggest they do to address the situation?","options":["Ignore it","Make a response video","Watch the video together","Tell a teacher"],"correct_answer":"Watch the video together"},{"question":"What theme is developing in this chapter?","options":["Competition","Friendship","Adventure","Mystery"],"correct_answer":"Friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_300_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_300_ch2_img1.png","plot_300_ch2_img2.png","story_300_11-14_ch2_img1_1751269591.png","story_300_11-14_ch2_img2_1751269622.png"]},"word_count":676,"reading_level":"Builder"}
