   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_300_11_14","title":"The Social Media Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the bright morning sun streamed through the windows of Riverdale High, Jamie stood in front of her locker, mentally preparing for another day. The vibrant halls buzzed with chatter and the sounds of notifications pinging from phones. Jamie could feel a flutter of excitement in her stomach\u2014her viral video had gained even more attention, and students were now approaching her for selfies and shoutouts. But amidst the cheers, she spotted Kira, lingering near the corner, her expression shadowed by uncertainty.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n\u201cHey, Jamie!\u201d called out Jordan, waving enthusiastically. He was always the peacemaker, the one who seemed to effortlessly blend technology with empathy. \u201cDid you see how many followers you gained last night? It\u2019s insane!\u201d\n\nJamie smiled, though she felt a twinge of guilt. \u201cYeah, I guess it\u2019s kind of cool,\u201d she replied, glancing back at Kira, who was scrolling through her phone, her brow furrowed. The distance between them felt like an ocean.\n\nAt lunch, Jamie and Kira found themselves at their usual table, but the laughter that once flowed easily felt stilted. Kira poked at her salad, barely lifting her eyes. \u201cSo, how does it feel to be famous?\u201d she asked, her tone sharper than she intended.\n\n\u201cFamous? I wouldn\u2019t call it that,\u201d Jamie replied, trying to keep her voice light. \u201cIt\u2019s just a video!\u201d\n\n\u201cJust a video?\u201d Kira snapped, finally looking up. \u201cYou have hundreds of likes, Jamie! It\u2019s not just a video to everyone else.\u201d The words hung in the air heavy as a storm cloud.\n\nJamie\u2019s heart sank. \u201cKira, I didn\u2019t ask for this. I just want us to be okay. Can\u2019t we talk about this?\u201d \n\nJordan, who had been sitting nearby, cleared his throat. \u201cMaybe you both need to remember why you became friends in the first place,\u201d he suggested wisely. \u201cKira, you\u2019re an amazing artist. Have you thought about sharing your work online? You could gain followers too!\u201d\n\nKira\u2019s eyes softened, but the resentment still flickered beneath the surface. \u201cThat\u2019s the thing, Jordan. I don\u2019t want to be just known for my art. I want to be known for being me. And right now, I feel like I\u2019m just Jamie\u2019s sidekick.\u201d\n\nThe words stung, and Jamie felt a knot tightening in her chest. She could see the hurt in Kira\u2019s eyes, like a glass vase ready to shatter. \u201cYou\u2019re not my sidekick, Kira. You\u2019re my best friend. I don\u2019t care about the followers. I want to support you. How can we fix this?\u201d\n\nKira sighed, looking down at her tray. \u201cI guess I just didn\u2019t know how to tell you that I felt\u2026 left out,\u201d she admitted quietly. \u201cIt\u2019s hard watching you shine when I feel so invisible.\u201d\n\nIn that moment, the atmosphere shifted, like the first rays of sunlight breaking through the clouds. \u201cYou could never be invisible to me,\u201d Jamie said gently. \u201cLet me help you, Kira. Let\u2019s create something together, something that represents both of us.\u201d\n\nKira\u2019s face brightened, and for the first time in days, a smile crept back onto her lips. \u201cReally? You\u2019d want to do that?\u201d\n\n\u201cAbsolutely! Let\u2019s film a new video together\u2014one that shows off your art and my goofiness. We can share it on our page!\u201d Jamie suggested, her enthusiasm bubbling over.\n\nAs they talked about their new project, laughter bubbled between them once more, filling the cracks that social media had created. They made a plan to sketch ideas that weekend, and it felt like a breath of fresh air.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe tension had melted, leaving behind a warmth that felt both familiar and new. Jamie realized then that true fame was not about the number of likes, but about the people who stood by your side through it all.\n\nAs the bell rang, signaling the end of lunch, Jamie and Kira walked out together, their shoulders brushing, their spirits lifted. They were ready to face the world\u2014not as separate stars, but as a bright constellation, together.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What causes Kira to feel overshadowed?","options":["Her own art","Jamie\u2019s viral video","Jordan's popularity","The school's social media policy"],"correct_answer":"Jamie\u2019s viral video"},{"question":"What does Jordan suggest Kira do?","options":["Ignore social media","Create her own video","Help Jamie with her video","Draw more in private"],"correct_answer":"Create her own video"},{"question":"What realization does Jamie have by the end of the chapter?","options":["Popularity is everything","Friendship is more important than fame","She should go solo","Kira is not a good friend"],"correct_answer":"Friendship is more important than fame"},{"question":"How do Jamie and Kira plan to collaborate?","options":["By making separate videos","By creating a video together","By ignoring each other","By focusing on schoolwork"],"correct_answer":"By creating a video together"},{"question":"What is the main theme of this chapter?","options":["Competition","Envy","Friendship and communication","Technology"],"correct_answer":"Friendship and communication"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_300_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_300_ch5_img1.png","plot_300_ch5_img2.png","story_300_11-14_ch5_img1_1751269470.png","story_300_11-14_ch5_img2_1751269492.png"]},"word_count":683,"reading_level":"Builder"}
