   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_300_15_18","title":"The Social Media Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"The halls of Riverdale High buzzed with the electrifying hum of teenage energy, a ceaseless swirl of laughter, whispers, and the click of devices. Jamie Thompson, a vibrant whirlwind with a mane of curly auburn hair and a contagious laugh, floated through the throng, her phone capturing snippets of the day\u2019s excitement. She was the sun around which her friends orbited, her charisma amplifying their collective joy. With every step, she felt the familiar warmth of her best friend Kira just behind her, a steadier presence whose cool demeanor often balanced Jamie\u2019s exuberance.\n\n\u201cDid you see the likes on that video?\u201d Jamie exclaimed, pulling her phone from her pocket, her eyes sparkling with exhilaration. \u201cIt\u2019s at a thousand views and climbing!\u201d\n\nKira\u2019s smile faltered for a moment, hidden beneath her calm exterior. She had been there, filming Jamie\u2019s spontaneous dance routine at the school assembly, laughing at their shared silliness. But now, as Jamie basked in this unexpected fame, Kira felt a sharp pang of envy that she couldn\u2019t quite shake. \u201cThat\u2019s awesome, Jamie,\u201d she replied, forcing her voice to remain upbeat. \u201cYou deserve it.\u201d\n\nYet the words felt heavy, as if they were coated with a layer of resentment. Kira had always been the dependable one, the steady rock, while Jamie was the bright flame that drew attention. At that moment, she couldn\u2019t help but wonder if her own talents were overshadowed by Jamie\u2019s vibrant persona.\n\nAs they reached their lockers, Jamie\u2019s phone buzzed incessantly with notifications, each ping amplifying her excitement. \u201cI can\u2019t believe it! People are sharing it all over! Can you take another video of me? Maybe we could do a challenge?\u201d\n\nKira nodded absently, her mind drifting. \u201cSure, I guess\u2026\u201d \n\nThat evening, as Kira lay in bed, she scrolled through her feed, her heart sinking with each glance at Jamie\u2019s growing popularity. Friends had already started tagging her in screenshots of Jamie\u2019s video, their comments filled with enthusiasm. \u201cHow lucky is Kira to be friends with such a star?\u201d they wrote. The messages stung like tiny bee stings, each a reminder of her own perceived inadequacies.\n\nThe next day, Kira arrived at school, her heart heavier than usual. Jamie was already a whirlwind of energy, greeting classmates and filming snippets for her burgeoning social media presence. Kira felt her spirit dimming, watching Jamie thrive while she stood on the sidelines like a forgotten character in a story.\n\n\u201cHey, Kira!\u201d Jordan, their tech-savvy classmate, sidled up beside her. His messy hair and thick glasses gave him an endearing nerdiness, which Kira found comforting. \u201cAre you okay? You seem\u2026 off.\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2019m fine,\u201d Kira replied, her voice sharper than intended. \u201cJust tired, I guess.\u201d\n\nJordan raised an eyebrow, sensing the underlying tension. \u201cYou know, it\u2019s great that Jamie\u2019s getting attention, but don\u2019t forget your own strengths. You\u2019ve got the talent to be in the spotlight too.\u201d\n\nKira shrugged, her mind racing. \u201cYeah, but it\u2019s hard to compete with someone like her.\u201d\n\nJordan nodded, his brow furrowing in thought. \u201cHave you talked to her about it?\u201d\n\nKira opened her mouth to respond but hesitated. \u201cNot really. I mean, what would I say? \u2018Hey, I\u2019m jealous of you becoming famous?\u2019\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe just be honest? You might be surprised at how she feels.\u201d \n\nAs the day wore on, Kira found herself standing in the center of the cafeteria, a sea of faces engaged in conversations, all buzzing about Jamie\u2019s latest video. The bright fluorescent lights flickered above, amplifying the hum of teenage chatter. Her stomach twisted in knots, and she felt invisible. Kira spotted Jamie at the far end, surrounded by curious classmates, her laughter ringing out like a song. \n\nSuddenly, a thought struck Kira. What if she shot her own video? A way to express herself, reclaim her space beside Jamie without stepping into her shadow. She grabbed her phone, her heart racing as she approached Jordan for support. \u201cHey, let\u2019s do something together!\u201d she called out over the noise. \n\nJust then, a loud crash reverberated through the cafeteria, and Kira turned to see Jamie, her phone slipping from her fingers, a look of shock on her face as she watched her device smash against the tiled floor. \n\nThe crowd fell silent, and Kira felt the weight of expectation shift. This was the moment. Should she step up or retreat? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nAs Kira approached Jamie, the tension in the air thickened, and she felt the potential for change. Would she finally voice her feelings, or would the fear of rejection hold her back?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nKira reached Jamie just as the murmurs began to rise again, but the uncertainty in Jamie's eyes mirrored her own. This was more than just a moment of embarrassment; it was a chance for both of them to confront their fears.\n\n\u201cWhat should we do?\u201d Jamie's voice trembled, vulnerability breaking through her usual bravado. \n\nKira took a deep breath, ready to confront the new chapter that lay ahead in their friendship.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What is Jamie excited about at the beginning of the chapter?","options":["Her dance competition","A viral video","A school project","A new phone"],"correct_answer":"A viral video"},{"question":"How does Kira feel about Jamie's sudden fame?","options":["Indifferent","Proud","Envious","Happy"],"correct_answer":"Envious"},{"question":"What does Kira consider doing to express herself?","options":["Joining a new club","Shooting her own video","Changing schools","Ignoring Jamie"],"correct_answer":"Shooting her own video"},{"question":"What event causes a shift in the cafeteria?","options":["A food fight","Jamie\u2019s phone breaking","A surprise announcement","A fight between students"],"correct_answer":"Jamie\u2019s phone breaking"},{"question":"What advice does Jordan give Kira?","options":["To ignore her feelings","To talk to Jamie about her jealousy","To avoid Jamie","To focus on her studies"],"correct_answer":"To talk to Jamie about her jealousy"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_300_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_300_ch1_img1.png","plot_300_ch1_img2.png","story_300_15-18_ch1_img1_1751269127.png","story_300_15-18_ch1_img2_1751269449.png"]},"word_count":849,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
