   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_300_15_18","title":"The Social Media Showdown","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Friend Drama","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"The school bell rang loudly, reverberating through the bright, tech-savvy halls of Riverdale High as students jostled past each other, phones glued to their hands. Jamie Thompson, with her radiant smile and infectious laugh, stood at the entrance of the cafeteria, her heart racing with a mix of exhilaration and anxiety. The viral video of her spontaneous dance-off had ballooned her followers to almost a thousand overnight. Yet, the vibrant energy of the school felt muted as she scanned the room for her best friend, Kira.\n\nKira was seated at their usual table, a look of forced indifference marring her usually cheerful expression. A subtle pang of guilt struck Jamie. She knew this sudden fame had come at a cost, but their friendship felt like a fragile thread, stretched over the chasm of envy. With a deep breath, she approached.\n\n\"Hey, Kira! Did you see the views? It\u2019s insane!\" Jamie chirped, trying to mask her nerves.\n\nKira glanced up, her eyes betraying a mix of pride and resentment. \"Yeah, I saw. It\u2019s pretty... impressive,\" she replied, her tone flat. Jamie could sense the tension hanging in the air like a thick fog.\n\n\u201cCome on! You should be proud of me. We\u2019ve talked about this kind of opportunity!\u201d Jamie urged, her voice catching slightly as she clung to the hope that Kira would share in her excitement.\n\nKira shrugged, her gaze shifting to her phone, where a multitude of notifications chimed in rapid succession. \"Sure, I just thought we were in this together. Remember? You promised we\u2019d do everything together.\" The underlying hurt in her words was palpable, and Jamie's heart sank.\n\nSuddenly, the cafeteria door swung open, and Jordan, their tech-savvy classmate, strolled in, his eyes lighting up when he spotted Jamie. He navigated through the throng of students with ease, a laptop cradled in one arm.\n\n\"Jamie! You won\u2019t believe the analytics I pulled up for your video. It\u2019s going viral, like, really viral!\" he exclaimed, his enthusiasm infectious. He plopped down next to Kira without a second thought.\n\n\"That\u2019s amazing, right, Kira?\" Jamie said, turning to her friend, who remained silent, fingers tapping away on her phone. The contrast between Jordan's excitement and Kira's distant demeanor stung like a bee.\n\n\"It's like the whole school is talking about it,\" Jordan continued, oblivious to Kira's growing frustration. \"You could even monetize this if you wanted to.\"\n\n\"Monetize?\" Jamie's eyes widened with a mix of desire and unease. The thought of turning her fun into a job was thrilling yet daunting. As she opened her mouth to respond, Kira interjected.\n\n\"Or you could just think about what this is doing to your friendships,\" Kira snapped, her voice rising slightly above the din of the cafeteria.\n\nThe room fell into a hushed lull, all eyes on them. Jamie felt her cheeks heat up as she glanced around at their classmates, their whispers buzzing like wasps. \"Kira, I\u2019m not trying to replace you. This is still us!\" she pleaded, but Kira\u2019s expression had hardened.\n\n\"Is it? Because it feels like you\u2019ve moved on without me,\" Kira retorted, stabbing a chip into her salsa with unnecessary force. The hurt was evident, and Jamie felt a clamp of panic in her chest.\n\nRealizing the gravity of the situation, Jordan shifted uncomfortably. \"Hey, maybe we should talk about this later? It\u2019s not a big deal, right?\"\n\n\"But it is a big deal!\" Kira shot back, rising from her seat. \"Maybe I need to find out who I am outside of your shadow.\" And with that, she stormed out of the cafeteria, leaving Jamie stunned and Jordan looking awkwardly between them.\n\nThe cafeteria buzzed back to life, but Jamie felt like she had been plunged into chaos. She pushed her plate away, her appetite vanished. The exhilaration of her success now felt like a heavy burden. \u201cWhat just happened?\u201d she murmured, half to herself and half to Jordan, who looked equally bewildered.\n\n\u201cI think you two need to talk,\u201d he suggested cautiously, but Jamie was already grappling with the weight of Kira\u2019s words. Did her success really come at the expense of their friendship? \n\nAs Jamie picked up her phone, she noticed a new notification\u2014another wave of likes flooding in on her video. A strange bitterness rose in her throat. This was supposed to be fun, but all she felt was the gnawing anxiety of a rift growing between them. \n\nJust as she was about to reply to Kira, another notification pinged; it was a direct message from a popular influencer, asking if Jamie would collaborate. The excitement flickered, but it felt tainted now.\n\nHow could she balance her newfound fame and her friendship? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe vibrant cafeteria scene captured in a colorful, bustling atmosphere, filled with students animatedly interacting, some laughing, some absorbed in their phones. In the foreground, Jamie stands with a hopeful expression, while Kira sits with a conflicted look, her phone in hand, embodying the tension in their friendship.\n\nThe bell rang again, signaling the end of lunch, but Jamie remained seated, lost in thought. How could she mend what was fraying? She needed a plan\u2014something to bridge the chasm that now separated her and Kira. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nA close-up of Jamie\u2019s face, a mix of determination and anxiety, illuminated by the soft glow of her phone screen. The background blurs to symbolize her isolation, while her expression conveys the weight of choices ahead, hinting at the struggle to reconcile her digital success with her personal relationships.\n\nJamie took a deep breath, straightening her back as she resolved to talk to Kira again, to confront the growing distance, no matter the cost.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What triggers Kira's resentment towards Jamie?","options":["Jamie\u2019s academic achievements","Jamie\u2019s viral video success","Kira's own lack of popularity","Jordan's interference"],"correct_answer":"Jamie\u2019s viral video success"},{"question":"How does Jamie react to Kira's confrontation?","options":["She ignores Kira","She defends her success","She apologizes immediately","She laughs it off"],"correct_answer":"She defends her success"},{"question":"What does Jordan suggest to Jamie after Kira leaves?","options":["To ignore Kira","To talk to Kira","To focus solely on her fame","To stop making videos"],"correct_answer":"To talk to Kira"},{"question":"What does Jamie feel as she receives more likes on her video?","options":["Pure joy","Excitement mixed with anxiety","Indifference","Sadness"],"correct_answer":"Excitement mixed with anxiety"},{"question":"What internal conflict does Jamie experience in this chapter?","options":["She wants to be more famous","She struggles to balance fame with friendship","She dislikes social media","She wants to quit school"],"correct_answer":"She struggles to balance fame with friendship"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_300_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_300_ch2_img1.png","plot_300_ch2_img2.png","story_300_15-18_ch2_img1_1751269084.png","story_300_15-18_ch2_img2_1751269104.png"]},"word_count":956,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
