   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_291_7_10","title":"The Great Test Treasure Hunt","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Mia, Leo, and Ava met in the library after school. The shelves were tall and packed with books. Mia felt a thrill of excitement. \u201cToday is the day we crack the code!\u201d she declared.\n\n\u201cI can\u2019t wait to see what\u2019s next!\u201d Leo said, tapping on his tablet. \u201cLet\u2019s check the map again.\u201d \n\nMia spread the map across the table. It was full of strange symbols and drawings. \u201cThis looks like a puzzle,\u201d Ava said, adjusting her glasses. \u201cWe need to decode the next clue.\u201d\n\nSuddenly, a loud bell rang. \u201cOh no! We only have an hour before study hall!\u201d Mia exclaimed. They needed to hurry. \n\nAs they studied the map, Leo pointed to a spot marked with a big X. \u201cWhat if this X means the playground again?\u201d he suggested. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go, but we have to manage our time better!\u201d Mia said, glancing at her watch. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] \n\nThey rushed to the playground, where the sun shone bright. But when they arrived, they spotted something unusual. A group of older kids was gathered by the swings, laughing and teasing each other. \n\n\u201cDo you think they know about the treasure?\u201d Ava whispered, biting her lip.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s sneak closer!\u201d Mia said, her heart racing. They tiptoed in, hiding behind the slide. \n\nSuddenly, they heard one of the kids shout, \u201cWhoever finds the treasure first gets a pizza party!\u201d The words flew through Mia\u2019s mind like a lightning bolt. \u201cWe need to find it first!\u201d \n\nBut just then, Leo gasped. \u201cLook!\u201d he pointed to a hidden corner of the playground. A shiny object glinted in the grass. \n\n\u201cIs that\u2026?!\u201d Ava gasped. They dashed over, but the older kids turned and ran for it too!\n\n\u201cGet it, Mia!\u201d Leo yelled. The race was on. They sprinted, their hearts pounding. \n\nMia reached the shiny object first. She picked it up and gasped. \u201cIt\u2019s a compass!\u201d \n\nBut then, she heard a voice behind her. \u201cHey! That\u2019s ours!\u201d An older kid reached for the compass. \n\nMia pulled back. \u201cWait! We found it first!\u201d Tension hung in the air. Would they keep the compass, or would they lose it?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] \n\nMia\u2019s mind raced. They needed that compass for the treasure hunt. But with the older kids closing in, what would she do?\n\n\u201cMia!\u201d Leo shouted. \u201cWhat\u2019s the plan?\u201d\n\nMia took a deep breath. \u201cWe\u2019re not giving up!\u201d she said. \u201cWe\u2019ll use our brains. Let\u2019s think fast!\u201d \n\nBut as the older kids approached, she realized they had to make a choice: fight for the compass or find another way to win the treasure. And the exams were coming fast.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"Where did Mia and her friends find the compass?","options":["In the library","In the grass","In the classroom","In the cafeteria"],"correct_answer":"In the grass"},{"question":"What was the older kids' challenge for the treasure?","options":["A treasure map","A pizza party","A scavenger hunt","A riddle"],"correct_answer":"A pizza party"},{"question":"What did Mia feel when she saw the kids approaching?","options":["Happy","Excited","Nervous","Sleepy"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What did Leo suggest they check again?","options":["The map","The compass","The library","Their study notes"],"correct_answer":"The map"},{"question":"What choice did Mia have to make at the end of the chapter?","options":["Whether to run away","Whether to share the compass","Whether to keep the compass","Whether to keep studying"],"correct_answer":"Whether to keep the compass"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_291_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_291_ch3_img1.png","plot_291_ch3_img2.png","story_291_7-10_ch3_img1_1751268868.png","story_291_7-10_ch3_img2_1751268884.png"]},"word_count":444,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
