   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_291_7_10","title":"The Great Test Treasure Hunt","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":4,"chapter_name":"Chapter 4","content":"Mia sat on a bench in the schoolyard. The sun shone brightly, and the air was filled with laughter. Her heart raced as she unfolded the treasure map once more. \n\n\u201cOkay, team!\u201d she said, looking at Leo and Ava. \u201cWe need to be smart about this. We have tests soon, but we can\u2019t forget the treasure!\u201d\n\nLeo nodded. \u201cI think we can study and hunt at the same time. We just need a plan.\u201d \n\nAva adjusted her glasses. \u201cWe should follow the map during lunch. That way, we can still study in the evening!\u201d\n\nMia smiled. \u201cGreat idea, Ava! Let\u2019s start now!\u201d \n\nThey gathered around the map. The first clue was near the old oak tree by the library. They dashed over, excitement buzzing in the air. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nWhen they reached the oak tree, they looked around. \u201cWhere could the next clue be?\u201d Mia wondered aloud. \n\n\u201cWait! Look!\u201d Leo pointed at a small hollow in the trunk. \u201cIs that a piece of paper?\u201d\n\nAva gasped. \u201cIt is! Let\u2019s see what it says!\u201d \n\nMia reached in and pulled out the paper. It read: \u201cTo find the treasure, look where books fly high. In the library, the next clue lies.\u201d \n\n\u201cBooks fly high? What does that mean?\u201d Leo scratched his head. \n\nAva\u2019s eyes lit up. \u201cThe library has a reading corner with a big bookshelf! Maybe that\u2019s it!\u201d \n\nThey raced back to the library, hearts pounding with hope. Inside, they hurried to the reading corner. Mia looked up at the tall shelf. \u201cWe need to find the right book!\u201d\n\nLeo scanned the titles. \u201cWhat about this one?\u201d he said, pulling out a colorful book with a dragon on the cover. \n\n\u201cTry it!\u201d Mia encouraged. \n\nWhen Leo opened the book, a shiny envelope fell out! They all gasped. \n\n\u201cOpen it!\u201d Ava squealed. \n\nInside was a second clue and a shiny gold coin! \u201cWow! It\u2019s like treasure!\u201d Mia cheered. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s read the clue!\u201d Leo said, excited. The clue read: \u201cTo find the prize, the playground you must roam. Under the swings, you will find your next home.\u201d \n\nThey exchanged glances, their eyes wide with excitement. \u201cThe swings!\u201d Mia shouted. \u201cLet\u2019s go!\u201d \n\nWith their treasure hunt in full swing, they felt a rush of energy. Together, they could balance studying and adventuring. They were closer than ever to finding the treasure! \n\nAs they headed outside, Mia whispered, \u201cI know we can do this. We just have to keep working together!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia find at the oak tree?","options":["A shiny coin","A piece of paper","A key","A book"],"correct_answer":"A piece of paper"},{"question":"Where did they go after finding the clue at the oak tree?","options":["The library","The playground","The cafeteria","The gym"],"correct_answer":"The library"},{"question":"What did Leo pull off the shelf in the library?","options":["A map","A book","A dragon","A treasure"],"correct_answer":"A book"},{"question":"What did they find inside the book?","options":["A clue","A map","A test","A coin"],"correct_answer":"A clue"},{"question":"What is the next location they must search?","options":["The swings","The library","The classroom","The cafeteria"],"correct_answer":"The swings"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_291_ch4_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_291_ch4_img1.png","plot_291_ch4_img2.png","story_291_7-10_ch4_img1_1751268835.png","story_291_7-10_ch4_img2_1751268851.png"]},"word_count":416,"reading_level":"Explorer"}
