   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_291_11_14","title":"The Great Test Treasure Hunt","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the sun rose over Maplewood Middle School, Mia felt the familiar buzz of excitement mixed with anxiety in her stomach. It was test week, and the air was thick with the smell of freshly sharpened pencils and the faint, sweet scent of the cafeteria\u2019s famous cinnamon rolls. But today, after school, her adventure was just beginning. With Leo and Ava by her side, she felt invincible.\n\n\u201cAre you guys ready for the big hunt?\u201d Mia asked, her eyes sparkling with determination as they gathered outside the library.\n\n\u201cReady? I\u2019ve been waiting for this all week!\u201d Leo replied, his fingers twitching as if he were already typing up the clues on his imaginary laptop. He was the tech wizard of their group, always coming up with clever solutions. \n\nAva adjusted her glasses and peered at the treasure map, her brow furrowed with concentration. \u201cIf we follow this clue,\u201d she pointed to a scribbled note on the parchment, \u201cwe should head toward the old oak tree on the playground. But we can\u2019t forget about our studying! The history test on Friday is going to be brutal.\u201d\n\nMia bit her lip, torn between her desire for adventure and the looming weight of exams. \u201cWe can study tonight after we find the treasure. It\u2019ll be our reward!\u201d She clutched the map tightly, feeling its coarse edges and dreaming of the hidden prize.\n\nAs they made their way through the bustling hallways, filled with laughter and locker slams, Mia\u2019s heart raced. Just as they reached the library\u2019s entrance, Leo stopped in his tracks. \u201cWait! What\u2019s that?\u201d He pointed to a shimmering object lying beneath the library\u2019s front desk.\n\nMia and Ava exchanged glances before bending down to investigate. It was a key, old and ornate, with intricate designs carved into its surface. \n\n\u201cDo you think it\u2019s part of the treasure?!\u201d Ava exclaimed, her excitement bubbling over.\n\n\u201cMaybe it opens a hidden compartment somewhere!\u201d Leo added, his eyes gleaming with possibilities. They marveled at the unexpected find. \n\nSuddenly, the library door swung open, and Ms. Anderson, the librarian, appeared, her brow raised in curiosity. \u201cWhat are you three up to down there?\u201d she asked, her voice stern yet playful.\n\nMia quickly hid the key behind her back. \u201cUh, just\u2026 looking for books!\u201d she stammered.\n\nMs. Anderson\u2019s gaze narrowed, but then she chuckled softly. \u201cWell, remember, the library is for studying, especially this week. You can\u2019t afford distractions!\u201d\n\nAs she walked away, Mia felt a pang of guilt mixed with excitement. They had to keep the key a secret, but now the stakes felt higher. Testing their friendship, they knew they had to balance their time wisely.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s go to the oak tree before we forget about the treasure!\u201d Mia urged, clutching the map and the key tightly.\n\nThey raced outside, the sun shining brightly over the sprawling playground. Laughter echoed as students played games, filling the air with a sense of freedom that felt just out of reach.\n\nWhen they reached the old oak tree, its massive trunk stood like a guardian of secrets, its leaves whispering in the wind. Mia glanced at the map again. \u201cThe next clue should be hidden here, but what if someone else has already found it?\u201d\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s look around the base\u2014there could be something buried in the roots!\u201d Ava suggested, her eyes filled with excitement. \n\nAs they dug through the fallen leaves, a mysterious rustling sound came from behind them, making Mia freeze. \u201cDid you hear that?\u201d she whispered, glancing back.\n\nBefore they could react, a shadow loomed over them. It was Eric, the school\u2019s toughest bully, and he didn\u2019t look pleased. \u201cWhat are you losers doing? Looking for something? Better be careful; you might just end up in detention!\u201d he sneered, crossing his arms.\n\nAn electric tension filled the air. Mia\u2019s heart raced, not just from fear but from the determination to stand her ground. How could they continue their treasure hunt with Eric looming over them? \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s show him we\u2019re not afraid,\u201d Mia whispered to Leo and Ava. \u201cWe can\u2019t let him ruin our adventure!\u201d\n\nMia took a deep breath, ready to confront the bully. \u201cWe\u2019re just looking for something important! What\u2019s it to you?\u201d \n\nThe showdown had begun, and Mia\u2019s mind raced. Could they fend off Eric and continue their hunt?\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] Early in the chapter: A vibrant scene of Maplewood Middle School, with students bustling about. The sun shines down, illuminating the outdoor playground where Mia, Leo, and Ava stand together, looking determined and adventurous as they prepare for their treasure hunt.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2] Later in the chapter: A dramatic moment as Mia stands up to Eric, the bully, with her friends beside her. Mia\u2019s expression is a mix of bravery and resolve. In the background, the old oak tree towers, its leaves rustling ominously, while students nearby watch with wide eyes, sensing the tension.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What did Mia, Leo, and Ava find beneath the library desk?","options":["A treasure chest","An old book","A shiny key","A hidden map"],"correct_answer":"A shiny key"},{"question":"What did Ms. Anderson remind the kids about during their library visit?","options":["To keep secrets","To study hard","To play outside","To find the treasure"],"correct_answer":"To study hard"},{"question":"How did Mia react when Eric confronted them?","options":["She ran away","She ignored him","She stood her ground","She cried"],"correct_answer":"She stood her ground"},{"question":"What was the setting of the chapter?","options":["A forest","A mall","A middle school","A park"],"correct_answer":"A middle school"},{"question":"What dilemma did the friends face while planning their treasure hunt?","options":["Finding the treasure alone","Balancing studying and the hunt","Losing the map","Being friends with Eric"],"correct_answer":"Balancing studying and the hunt"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_291_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_291_ch2_img1.png","plot_291_ch2_img2.png","story_291_11-14_ch2_img1_1751268723.png","story_291_11-14_ch2_img2_1751268744.png"]},"word_count":839,"reading_level":"Builder"}
