   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_291_11_14","title":"The Great Test Treasure Hunt","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"As the clock ticked down to test week, the air in Crestwood Middle School felt charged with anticipation. Mia, Leo, and Ava gathered in the library, surrounded by towering shelves of dusty books. Sunlight filtered through the tall windows, casting a warm glow on their secret hideaway. Mia\u2019s heart raced as she unfolded the treasure map once more, her fingers tracing the faded ink. \n\n\u201cWhat if this really leads to something special?\u201d she murmured, half to herself and half to her friends, who were peering over her shoulder.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019ve got to decode these clues! But we also need to study for science\u2014our big test is in two days!\u201d Leo reminded them, adjusting his glasses. He always appeared calm, but his voice had a hint of urgency.\n\nAva bit her lip, clearly torn between her love for mysteries and her need to prepare. \u201cMaybe we can solve one clue tonight and study tomorrow? Just one clue!\u201d \n\nMia nodded, her determination surging. \u201cOkay! Let\u2019s start with the first clue.\u201d She cleared her throat and read aloud, \u201c\u2018Where knowledge sleeps and stories grow, beneath the tales that heroes know.\u2019\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe three friends exchanged glances. \u201cThe library has to be the place,\u201d Ava concluded, her eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cBut what do you think it means by \u2018beneath the tales\u2019?\u201d\n\n\u201cMaybe there\u2019s something hidden under a book?\u201d Leo suggested, tapping his chin thoughtfully.\n\n\u201cOr a secret compartment somewhere!\u201d Mia added, the thrill of adventure igniting her imagination.\n\nThey scoured the library, moving from shelf to shelf, popping open books and checking beneath them. Minutes turned into an hour, and the whispers of other students faded into a distant hum. Just as doubt began to creep in, Mia pulled out a hefty old book, its spine cracked and worn. \n\n\u201cLook at this one!\u201d she called, holding it up. \u201cIt\u2019s called \u2018Legends of the Lost.\u2019\u201d\n\n\u201cPerfect! Try flipping through it,\u201d Ava encouraged. \n\nAs Mia opened the book, a folded piece of paper slipped out and floated to the floor like a feather. She picked it up, her heart pounding in her chest. \u201cWhat is this?\u201d \n\nLeo leaned closer, joining Mia as she unfolded the paper. It was another clue: \u201cTo find what you seek, head to the place where the sun kisses the ground and laughter fills the air.\u201d \n\n\u201cIs that the playground?\u201d Ava exclaimed, her voice rising with excitement. \n\nBut just then, the door swung open with a bang, and in walked Eric, the school bully, flanked by his friends. \u201cWhat are you nerds doing?\u201d he sneered, crossing his arms and blocking their escape.\n\nMia felt a chill run down her spine. She exchanged worried glances with Leo and Ava. \u201cUh, we were just studying!\u201d she stammered, trying to mask her fear with bravado.\n\n\u201cStudying? In the library? Right.\u201d Eric took a step forward, his smug grin growing. \u201cWhat\u2019s that you\u2019re holding, Mia?\u201d\n\nThe map was still in her hands, but her fingers trembled around it. \u201cJust a project,\u201d she lied, her voice wavering.\n\nEric\u2019s eyes narrowed. \u201cLooks like a treasure map to me. You know, I\u2019ve always wanted to go on a treasure hunt. Maybe I should join you.\u201d\n\nThe tension in the air thickened, and Mia felt her heart race. \u201cNo way! We\u2019re doing this on our own!\u201d she declared, her voice more confident than she felt.\n\n\u201cSuit yourself,\u201d Eric replied, his smirk fading. \u201cBut if I find out what you\u2019re really up to, I won\u2019t let you have fun with it.\u201d\n\nAs he and his friends turned to leave, Mia felt a surge of determination. She couldn\u2019t let Eric ruin their quest. \u201cWe have to go to the playground!\u201d she whispered urgently to Leo and Ava. \u201cWe can\u2019t let him beat us to the treasure!\u201d\n\nWith a sense of urgency, they gathered their things and slipped out of the library, ready to chase down the next clue. The sun was setting, casting long shadows across the schoolyard. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s hurry,\u201d Leo urged, glancing back nervously. \n\n\u201cRight behind you!\u201d Mia said, her heart pounding with a mix of excitement and fear. What awaited them at the playground? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nBut just as they reached the swings, a loud bang echoed from behind them. Mia spun around, her stomach dropping. The school\u2019s back door had slammed shut, trapping them outside. \n\n\u201cUh-oh,\u201d Ava whispered, her eyes wide. \u201cWhat do we do now?\u201d\n\nMia\u2019s mind raced. They were running out of time\u2014not just for the treasure, but for the tests looming ahead. Would they face Eric again? Or would they find out something even more surprising?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What new clue do Mia and her friends discover?","options":["A treasure map","A folded piece of paper","A hidden key","A locked box"],"correct_answer":"A folded piece of paper"},{"question":"Who interrupts Mia and her friends in the library?","options":["Their teacher","A classmate","Eric, the bully","The librarian"],"correct_answer":"Eric, the bully"},{"question":"What place does the clue direct them to visit next?","options":["The library","The cafeteria","The playground","The gym"],"correct_answer":"The playground"},{"question":"What do Mia, Leo, and Ava struggle to balance during their treasure hunt?","options":["Their friendships","Studying for their tests","Finding the treasure","Keeping secrets"],"correct_answer":"Studying for their tests"},{"question":"How does the chapter end?","options":["With Eric leaving","With a new clue found","With them trapped outside","With a fight breaking out"],"correct_answer":"With them trapped outside"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_291_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_291_ch3_img1.png","plot_291_ch3_img2.png","story_291_11-14_ch3_img1_1751268683.png","story_291_11-14_ch3_img2_1751268706.png"]},"word_count":780,"reading_level":"Builder"}
