   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_291_15_18","title":"The Great Test Treasure Hunt","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"As the first light of dawn crept through the window of Crestwood Middle School, Mia Evans stood outside the doors, her heart racing with a mixture of excitement and trepidation. This wasn\u2019t just any ordinary day; it was the beginning of test week. The halls buzzed with anxious chatter, echoing the collective dread about the upcoming exams in English, Math, and History. But Mia, with her unruly chestnut curls and determined hazel eyes, had a plan\u2014one that involved a treasure map she had stumbled upon in the dusty corners of the library.\n\nThe ancient, leather-bound tome had caught her eye while she was searching for a book on Shakespeare. A slip of parchment had fluttered out, revealing hastily scrawled ink, promising a treasure hidden somewhere within the school's sprawling playground. Mia couldn\u2019t resist the allure of adventure, especially when her friends, Leo and Ava, would join her on this quest.\n\n\u201cAre you sure you want to do this today?\u201d Leo asked, his fingers tapping rhythmically on his phone, the screen glowing with the latest app he had been tinkering with. The tech-savvy boy was the brains behind many of their school projects and had a knack for figuring out things that left others perplexed. His dark hair fell over his brow as he squinted at the screen, contemplating the risks versus the rewards.\n\n\u201cAbsolutely,\u201d Mia replied, her voice tinged with determination. \u201cWe can study later. What's a treasure hunt without a little excitement?\u201d Leo raised an eyebrow but smiled, relenting to Mia\u2019s infectious enthusiasm. Ava, the quiet observer with her thick glasses perched precariously on her nose, looked up from her notebook, her expression a blend of curiosity and concern.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, guys. We have finals in two days,\u201d Ava said, adjusting her backpack to shift some of the weight. She was the quintessential bookworm, a puzzle aficionado who found comfort within the pages of fantasy novels, but the prospect of skipping study time for a treasure hunt made her uneasy. \u201cWhat if we don\u2019t have time to prepare?\u201d \n\nMia waved her hand dismissively. \u201cWe\u2019ll find the treasure, and then we\u2019ll study. It\u2019ll be fun. Just think about it, Ava! It\u2019s like an adventure in one of your books.\u201d She could see the spark of intrigue flicker in Ava\u2019s eyes, and it ignited a fire within Mia\u2019s heart.\n\nThey ambled towards the library, the sun casting playful shadows on the pavement. As they entered the library, the familiar scent of old books and polished wood enveloped them. [IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1] The library was their sanctuary, a collection of stories and knowledge that felt more like home than any other place in school. Rows of shelves reached towards the ceiling like ancient sentinels guarding secrets long forgotten.\n\nLeo pulled out a crumpled piece of parchment, its edges worn and yellowed with age. \u201cAlright, let\u2019s see what we have here.\u201d He spread it across a nearby table, squinting down at the scribbles with intense focus. \u201cThe first clue says something about the \u2018heart of learning,\u2019\u201d he read aloud, tapping his chin thoughtfully.\n\n\u201cIsn\u2019t that just a fancy way of saying the library?\u201d Mia suggested. Ava nodded slowly, her mind already racing through the possibilities. \u201cOr the main office? That\u2019s where the principal holds all the important meetings.\u201d\n\nMia grinned, fueled by adrenaline. \u201cThen let\u2019s check there first!\u201d \n\nAs they ventured through the library\u2019s maze-like corridors, Mia felt the weight of her decision quake beneath her. Was it wise to prioritize adventure over preparation? But the thrill of the hunt pushed her doubts aside. This treasure hunt could be the distraction they all needed from the looming stress of finals.\n\nSuddenly, a loud crash echoed behind them, interrupting their thoughts. They spun around, hearts pounding, only to find a group of students scrambling to pick up the scattered contents of their backpacks.\n\n\u201cAre you guys okay?\u201d Ava asked, her concern evident. \n\n\u201cYeah, just a little clumsy,\u201d one of the boys replied, rubbing the back of his neck sheepishly. \u201cBut you should be more careful. You\u2019ll forget about studying and end up failing.\u201d \n\nMia felt her stomach drop. The boy\u2019s words lingered in the air like a dark cloud. What if he was right? The pressure to perform weighed heavily on her shoulders, but she shook the thought away. She turned back to her friends, determination gleaming in her eyes. \u201cWe\u2019ll deal with the treasure first, then the tests. I promise!\u201d \n\nAs they emerged from the library, the sun now high in the sky, Mia felt exhilaration coursing through her veins. Little did they know, the hunt would take them to places they never imagined, testing their friendship and resolve in ways they could never foresee. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s head to the office!\u201d Mia exclaimed, her heart racing with a mix of fear and excitement. It was time to unlock the adventure that awaited them. \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nWith her friends at her side, Mia sprinted towards the main office, the promise of treasure overshadowing the cloud of tests looming ahead.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What do Mia and her friends find in the library?","options":["A treasure chest","A treasure map","A book on Shakespeare","An old diary"],"correct_answer":"A treasure map"},{"question":"What is Ava\u2019s main concern about the treasure hunt?","options":["It will be too dangerous","They won't have time to study","Mia might get lost","Leo might break his phone"],"correct_answer":"They won't have time to study"},{"question":"Which character is particularly tech-savvy?","options":["Mia","Ava","Leo","The principal"],"correct_answer":"Leo"},{"question":"What phrase does the first clue refer to?","options":["Heart of learning","Treasure of knowledge","Crestwood's secret","Missing puzzle piece"],"correct_answer":"Heart of learning"},{"question":"How does Mia feel about the idea of a treasure hunt?","options":["Indifferent","Excited","Anxious","Nervous"],"correct_answer":"Excited"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_291_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_291_ch1_img1.png","plot_291_ch1_img2.png","story_291_15-18_ch1_img1_1751268575.png","story_291_15-18_ch1_img2_1751268591.png"]},"word_count":855,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
