   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_291_15_18","title":"The Great Test Treasure Hunt","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":3,"chapter_name":"Chapter 3","content":"Mia sat at the long table in the library, the scent of old books swirling around her like a comforting blanket. The soft glow from the desk lamp cast shadows that danced upon the faded wooden shelves, creating a sense of intimacy amidst the towering stacks of knowledge. Leo was hunched over his laptop, fingers flying across the keys, while Ava scribbled notes furiously on a pad of graph paper, her brow furrowed in concentration.\n\n\u201cOkay, let\u2019s see what we have so far,\u201d Mia said, her voice barely above a whisper, as if the library itself might be listening. \n\nLeo looked up, pushing his glasses up the bridge of his nose. \u201cBased on the first clue, we need to find something related to the \u2018great oak\u2019,\u201d he said, his eyes sparkling with excitement. \u201cAnd I think I\u2019ve found a reference to it in the school\u2019s history section.\u201d\n\nAva nodded, her enthusiasm bubbling just beneath the surface. \u201cThe great oak is probably the one by the playground. Maybe there\u2019s something actually hidden there?\u201d \n\nAs they discussed the oak tree, the weight of their upcoming exams loomed over them, a spectral presence that turned their spirited debate into a tightrope walk between joy and anxiety. Mia felt a prickle of guilt at the thought. She was supposed to be studying for the biology test, not hunting for treasure.\n\n\u201cGuys,\u201d Mia interjected, \u201cwe have to keep our priorities straight. We can\u2019t let this treasure hunt distract us too much, especially with finals coming up.\u201d\n\n\u201cJust a little more time,\u201d Leo urged, his voice a mixture of pleading and excitement. \u201cWe can make this quick. Besides, think of the adrenaline rush! It\u2019s all part of the fun.\u201d \n\nMia bit her lip, caught in the crossfire of her own aspirations. She wanted the thrill of the hunt, but the thought of failing her exams gnawed at her conscience.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nSuddenly, the library doors creaked open, and in walked Ms. Thompson, the strict librarian with her cat-eye glasses balancing precariously on her nose. The tension in the room shifted palpably as they tried to appear absorbed in their tasks. Mia felt her heart quicken, a mix of anxiety and excitement. Would their secret be discovered?\n\n\u201cRemember, this library is a place for study, not for\u2026 other pursuits,\u201d Ms. Thompson said, her gaze piercing through each of them. \u201cI expect you all to be prepared for your exams.\u201d With that, she turned on her heel and walked away, leaving behind a silence thick with unspoken words.\n\n\u201cMaybe we should check out the oak tree after school,\u201d Ava suggested, her voice barely a whisper as if afraid of being overheard.\n\nThe tension that had been building inside Mia finally erupted. \u201cWhat if we get caught? What if we fail our exams? What\u2019s the point of treasure if we don\u2019t pass?\u201d Her voice shook, revealing her inner turmoil. \n\nLeo placed a hand on her shoulder, his expression softening. \u201cMia, I get it. But sometimes you have to take risks. This could be the adventure we need to break through the stress.\u201d\n\nMia's mind raced. The treasure map felt like a siren's call, pulling her toward the unknown, while the looming exams felt like chains, binding her to the mundane. \n\n\u201cAlright,\u201d she said finally, a mix of resolve and uncertainty in her tone. \u201cLet\u2019s do it. But we have to plan this carefully and make time for studying too.\u201d \n\nAs they gathered their things, the library felt less like a sanctuary and more like a battleground. The stakes had risen\u2014the treasure hunt was no longer just a fun distraction; it had become a race against time, against their own fears.\n\nLater that day, with the sun setting behind the school, they stood under the great oak, its branches twisting like ancient fingers reaching for the sky. The afternoon light danced across the leaves, casting dappled shadows on the ground. \n\n\u201cWhat now?\u201d Ava asked, glancing at the map that had become their guiding star.\n\nAs Mia prepared to read the next clue aloud, a sudden commotion erupted from the playground. They turned to see a group of older students gathered, their expressions a mixture of curiosity and mischief. \n\n\u201cHey! What are you doing over there?\u201d one of them shouted, narrowing his eyes.\n\nMia\u2019s heart dropped. They were about to be cornered, and the thrill of adventure suddenly felt perilous. The decision hung in the air\u2014stay and risk exposure, or run and hope for the best.\n\n\u201cRun!\u201d Mia shouted, adrenaline surging through her veins as they bolted for the trees, the map clutched tightly in her hands, their world spiraling into chaos.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\nThe path to the treasure had suddenly become a race against not only time but antagonizing peers. Each step was a heartbeat, echoing the uncertainty of what lay ahead.\n\nWould they even survive to decipher the next clue?","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What does Mia feel guilty about as they continue the treasure hunt?","options":["Not having enough fun","Failing her exams","Losing their map","Distracting her friends"],"correct_answer":"Failing her exams"},{"question":"What is the main setting of this chapter?","options":["The school cafeteria","The library","The playground","The sports field"],"correct_answer":"The library"},{"question":"How does Ms. Thompson react when she enters the library?","options":["She praises the students","She tells them to leave","She warns them to focus on studying","She joins their discussion"],"correct_answer":"She warns them to focus on studying"},{"question":"What decision do Mia and her friends face at the great oak?","options":["To reveal their treasure hunt","To confront the older students","To run away","To climb the tree"],"correct_answer":"To run away"},{"question":"What does the great oak represent in this chapter?","options":["A place for relaxation","A challenge to overcome","A fun gathering spot","An old school tradition"],"correct_answer":"A challenge to overcome"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_291_ch3_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_291_ch3_img1.png","plot_291_ch3_img2.png"]},"word_count":823,"reading_level":"Challenger"}
