   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_292_11_14","title":"The Test of Friendship","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":1,"chapter_name":"Chapter 1","content":"Chapter 1: The Countdown Begins\n\nJaden glanced around the cozy study room, the walls decorated with colorful posters about space, biology, and famous scientists. It buzzed with the chatter of students immersed in their books, some whispering tips, while others flipped nervously through their notes. Just days before the crucial science test, Jaden felt the tension in the air, like a balloon ready to pop.\n\n\u201cHey, Leo, are you ready?\u201d Jaden asked, trying to keep his voice light. His best friend, Leo, sat at a table piled high with neatly organized notes, colored highlighters, and a brand-new textbook. Leo looked up, adjusting his glasses, his expression serious. \n\n\u201cReady? I\u2019ve been preparing for weeks! I even made a study guide!\u201d Leo replied, tapping a pen against the table, his eyes wide with determination.\n\nJaden chuckled, trying to ease the pressure. \u201cCome on, man, you know you\u2019re the only one going all-out for this. I thought we could just kick back and study together.\u201d\n\nLeo raised an eyebrow, his lips thinning into a line. \u201cYou mean, you want to goof off instead of actually studying? We need to take this seriously!\u201d\n\nJaden shrugged, his easygoing demeanor a mask for the anxiety worming its way through his stomach. \u201cA little fun won\u2019t hurt, right? Science is all about curiosity!\u201d\n\nBefore Leo could respond, Ms. Wong, their science teacher, walked in, her presence commanding immediate attention. \u201cAlright, class! I hope you\u2019re all ready for the test next week. Remember, not just your grades are on the line\u2014so is your understanding of the material.\u201d \n\nJaden\u2019s heart raced. The last thing he wanted was to disappoint Ms. Wong. She had a way of making even the most complicated subjects intriguing, and he admired her for that. It was just that studying wasn't really his thing. \n\n\u201cLet\u2019s get started,\u201d Ms. Wong continued, her hands clasped together. \u201cI want you all to pair up for a study session. Jaden, Leo\u2014why don\u2019t you two work together?\u201d\n\nLeo\u2019s expression brightened, while Jaden\u2019s heart sank. \u201cSure, Ms. Wong,\u201d they both said in unison.\n\nAs Ms. Wong distributed worksheets, Jaden felt a sinking feeling in his stomach. He knew Leo would want to dive deep into the details, while he preferred to keep things relaxed and fun. They had worked together many times before, but never under this kind of pressure.\n\n\u201cLet\u2019s start with the basics,\u201d Leo suggested, pushing his glasses up his nose. \u201cYou know\u2014cell structure, the scientific method, and all that.\u201d\n\n\u201cSounds great, but how about we play a little quiz game instead?\u201d Jaden offered, hoping to lighten the mood. \u201cI\u2019ll ask the questions, and you can help me with the answers.\u201d\n\nLeo sighed, exasperated. \u201cThat\u2019s not how studying works, Jaden! We need to focus and\u2014\u201d\n\nSuddenly, Jaden leaned back in his chair, crossing his arms defiantly. \u201cWhy do we always have to do it your way? Sometimes I feel like I\u2019m not even part of this.\u201d\n\nThe room seemed to hold its breath, watching the two friends face off. Leo\u2019s eyes widened in surprise, and for a moment, tension crackled between them like static electricity. Jaden had never spoken to Leo this way before, and it felt strange, yet somehow exhilarating. \n\n\u201cMaybe we could find a middle ground?\u201d Leo suggested hesitantly, his voice softer now. \u201cI don\u2019t want to fight. I just want us to do well.\u201d\n\n\u201cMe too,\u201d Jaden replied, his heart beginning to soften. \u201cBut we need to figure out how to work together.\u201d\n\n\u201cOkay,\u201d Leo said, a small smile breaking through. \u201cLet\u2019s try both methods. A little fun and a little focus.\u201d\n\nJaden grinned, relieved. \u201cDeal! Now, let\u2019s get this test of friendship started!\u201d\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What subject are Jaden and Leo studying for?","options":["Math","English","History","Science"],"correct_answer":"Science"},{"question":"How does Jaden prefer to study?","options":["By making study guides","By having fun and playing quiz games","By reading textbooks","By memorizing facts"],"correct_answer":"By having fun and playing quiz games"},{"question":"What does Leo believe is important for studying?","options":["Having fun","Taking notes","Working together","Focusing and organizing"],"correct_answer":"Focusing and organizing"},{"question":"What does Ms. Wong want her students to understand?","options":["Science is boring","Their grades and understanding of the material are important","Group projects are mandatory","All tests are easy"],"correct_answer":"Their grades and understanding of the material are important"},{"question":"What does Jaden realize at the end of the chapter?","options":["He wants to study alone","He doesn\u2019t care about the test","They need to find a way to work together","Leo is too strict"],"correct_answer":"They need to find a way to work together"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_292_ch1_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_292_ch1_img1.png","plot_292_ch1_img2.png","story_292_11-14_ch1_img1_1751268224.png","story_292_11-14_ch1_img2_1751268244.png"]},"word_count":629,"reading_level":"Builder"}
