   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_292_11_14","title":"The Test of Friendship","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":2,"chapter_name":"Chapter 2","content":"As the sun dipped low in the sky, casting warm golden rays into the school\u2019s cozy study room, Jaden slumped into a beanbag chair, a lazy grin plastered across his face. The room was a riot of color, adorned with posters of famous scientists and motivational quotes. Students bustled around, some clutching textbooks, while others scribbled frantically on their notepads. Among them, Leo sat at a neat table, surrounded by an organized array of flashcards, diagrams, and highlighters. \n\n\u201cHey, Leo! You sure you don\u2019t need a relaxing beanbag, too?\u201d Jaden called, chuckling. \n\n\u201cVery funny,\u201d Leo replied, adjusting his glasses and not bothering to look up. \u201cI need to focus, Jaden. This test isn\u2019t going to ace itself!\u201d \n\nThe tension tugged at Jaden\u2019s stomach. He loved Leo's determination, but the pressure was starting to feel like a weight pressing down on his shoulders. \u201cC\u2019mon! We\u2019ve been studying for weeks. Let\u2019s just go through it together. It'll be fun!\u201d \n\nLeo sighed, his brows furrowing in frustration. \u201cFun? You think this is fun? We're talking about our grades here, Jaden!\u201d \n\nJaden\u2019s smile faded. Was it really just about grades? He could feel the friendship they shared beginning to fray at the edges. \n\nLeo then stood up and began pacing, his mind racing like a hamster on a wheel. \u201cI have a plan!\u201d he declared suddenly, his voice rising with a spark of enthusiasm. \u201cIf we divide the topics, we can quiz each other. You take the fun stuff\u2014like ecosystems and animals\u2014and I\u2019ll handle the complex stuff\u2014like chemical reactions.\u201d \n\n\u201cOr,\u201d Jaden countered, a playful glint in his eye, \u201cwe could flip a coin. Whoever loses does both.\u201d \n\nLeo shot him a sharp look, and for a moment, silence filled the room like a thick fog. The air crackled with unspoken thoughts. Then, Leo dropped his gaze, visibly deflating. \u201cYou\u2019re not taking this seriously, are you?\u201d \n\n\u201cOf course I am! I just think we can lighten up a bit.\u201d \n\nWith a deep breath, Leo turned back to his flashcards. \u201cMaybe that\u2019s the problem. I need to study hard, and you just want to joke around.\u201d \n\nBefore Jaden could respond, Ms. Wong entered the study room. Her presence instantly calmed the turbulent air like a gentle breeze. \u201cAlright, class! I hope everyone is ready for the big test. Remember, it\u2019s not just about knowledge; it\u2019s about how you use it.\u201d \n\nAs she spoke, Jaden felt a twist of anxiety in his stomach. Could he really use what he had learned, especially if Leo was going to insist on working separately? \n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nLater, as Ms. Wong began assigning study groups, Jaden and Leo exchanged worried glances. \u201cI can\u2019t believe we\u2019re being split up,\u201d Jaden whispered. \u201cWhat if I bomb the test without you?\u201d\n\n\u201cThat\u2019s the thing, Jaden!\u201d Leo said, his voice rising again. \u201cYou have to learn to stand on your own. I can\u2019t always be there to bail you out.\u201d \n\nJaden\u2019s heart sank. The truth of Leo's words stung, but they also ignited a flame of determination. He wasn\u2019t just going to sit back and let their friendship slip away. \u201cMaybe you\u2019re right,\u201d he said slowly, trying to mask the hurt. \u201cBut I don\u2019t want to lose what we have over a test.\u201d\n\nThe room buzzed around them, but the conversation felt like a bubble, isolating them from their chaotic surroundings. Jaden steeled himself, looking Leo squarely in the eyes. \u201cLet\u2019s find a way to study that works for both of us. We can make it happen even if it\u2019s hard.\u201d \n\nLeo\u2019s expression softened slightly, but before he could respond, Ms. Wong announced the group changes, and Jaden\u2019s heart raced. \n\n\u201cJaden, you will be with Carla and Amir. Leo, you\u2019re with Sam and Priya.\u201d \n\nThe words hung in the air like storm clouds, thick with uncertainty. Jaden\u2019s stomach twisted into a knot. Could he really manage this on his own? \n\nAs he set off to join his new group, he glanced back at Leo, who was already hunched over his materials, a look of concentration on his face. The tension wasn\u2019t just about studying anymore; it was a test of their friendship, too.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_2]\n\n\u201cWe\u2019ll figure it out,\u201d Jaden whispered to himself, as he took a deep breath and stepped forward into the unknown.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What study method does Leo prefer?","options":["Laid-back and casual","Organized and structured","Random and chaotic","Group-focused"],"correct_answer":"Organized and structured"},{"question":"What does Jaden suggest to lighten the mood?","options":["Joking around","Quiz each other","Playing games","Taking a break"],"correct_answer":"Joking around"},{"question":"What event causes further tension between Jaden and Leo?","options":["Ms. Wong assigns study groups","They take a break","They laugh together","They go outside"],"correct_answer":"Ms. Wong assigns study groups"},{"question":"How does Jaden feel about the upcoming test?","options":["Confident","Indifferent","Nervous","Excited"],"correct_answer":"Nervous"},{"question":"What challenge do Jaden and Leo face in this chapter?","options":["Dealing with a teacher","Studying for a test","Managing their friendship","All of the above"],"correct_answer":"All of the above"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_292_ch2_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_292_ch2_img1.png","plot_292_ch2_img2.png","story_292_11-14_ch2_img1_1751268188.png","story_292_11-14_ch2_img2_1751268207.png"]},"word_count":742,"reading_level":"Builder"}
