   [DEBUG] 📸 Book data: {"book_id":"school_life_292_11_14","title":"The Test of Friendship","genre":"School Life","sub_genre":"Test Stress","chapter_number":5,"chapter_name":"Chapter 5","content":"As the sun streamed through the large windows of the cozy study room, Jaden and Leo sat at their usual table, surrounded by a whirlwind of colorful posters and the buzz of students cramming for their science test. Jaden twirled a pencil between his fingers, a cheeky smirk plastered on his face, while Leo meticulously arranged his notes, ensuring every page was in perfect order. \n\n\u201cSeriously, Jaden, can you focus for just one second?\u201d Leo sighed, shaking his head at the scattered papers littering their table. \n\n\u201cYeah, yeah, I\u2019m focused. Just thinking of all those boring facts we have to memorize!\u201d Jaden chuckled, but inside, he felt the weight of the upcoming test pressing down on him. He wanted to impress Ms. Wong, who expected so much from them, but he also wanted to keep things light-hearted.\n\n[IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_1]\n\nThe study room was a haven for students like them, with its walls adorned with vibrant diagrams of the solar system and colorful charts about chemical reactions. It was buzzing with energy, but for Jaden, it felt a bit stifling. The pressure to perform was mounting, and he could sense Leo\u2019s frustration rising.\n\nAs they continued studying, Jaden decided to lighten the mood. \u201cHey, how about we do a little quiz battle? Winner gets to pick the pizza toppings for our post-test celebration!\u201d \n\nLeo raised an eyebrow, a hint of a smile breaking through his serious demeanor. \u201cOnly if you promise to take it seriously.\u201d\n\n\u201cDeal!\u201d Jaden grinned, excited that Leo was at least willing to have some fun. They took turns quizzing each other, and as they laughed over silly mistakes and the ridiculousness of some science terms, Jaden felt a shift in the air. It was as if the tension began to melt away, bit by bit.\n\nHours later, as the sun dipped lower in the sky, they reached a critical point in their study session. Leo had just explained the water cycle for the third time, and Jaden could see the exhaustion in his friend\u2019s eyes. \u201cLook, Leo, I really appreciate you being so organized, but can we mix it up a little? Maybe we can create a story about the water cycle instead of just memorizing it?\u201d\n\nLeo hesitated, his brow furrowing. \u201cYou mean like a\u2026 a skit?\u201d\n\n\u201cExactly! We can act it out! It\u2019ll be fun, and I promise it\u2019ll help with memorizing.\u201d Jaden\u2019s enthusiasm bubbled over, and he could tell Leo was considering it.\n\n\u201cOkay, let\u2019s give it a shot,\u201d Leo said slowly, a reluctant smile creeping across his face. \n\nAs they began crafting their skit, Jaden took on the role of the sun, bouncing around the room with exaggerated movements. Leo followed suit, becoming the rain, and soon enough, laughter filled the study room. Other students paused to watch the spectacle, some even cheering them on.\n\nJust when they were about to dive into the final part of their skit, Ms. Wong walked in. Her presence immediately quieted the room. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on here?\u201d she asked, a mix of curiosity and amusement in her eyes.\n\nJaden and Leo exchanged quick glances, their hearts racing. \u201cUh, just a little study break?\u201d Leo stammered, his cheeks flushed.\n\nMs. Wong crossed her arms, a smile tugging at her lips. \u201cWell, it looks like you two have found a creative way to study. I\u2019m impressed!\u201d \n\nWith a newfound sense of camaraderie and a shared laughter echoing in their minds, Jaden and Leo exchanged glances of relief. They weren\u2019t just studying anymore; they were working together, learning from each other. It was a small victory, but a victory nonetheless. \n\nAs they prepared for their test, Jaden felt a surge of gratitude wash over him. He realized that their friendship was far more important than any grade. Whether they aced the test or not, what mattered was that they had each other\u2019s backs. \n\n\u201cReady for this, Leo?\u201d Jaden asked.\n\n\u201cMore than ever,\u201d Leo replied, determination shining in his eyes.\n\nWith that, they walked out of the study room together, ready for whatever came next.","quiz":{"questions":[{"question":"What creative way do Jaden and Leo find to study for their test?","options":["A quiz battle","Creating a skit","Drawing diagrams","Reading textbooks"],"correct_answer":"Creating a skit"},{"question":"How does Leo initially feel about Jaden's suggestion to act out the water cycle?","options":["Excited","Reluctant","Angry","Indifferent"],"correct_answer":"Reluctant"},{"question":"What effect does Ms. Wong's arrival have on Jaden and Leo?","options":["They freeze in fear.","They stop having fun.","They feel proud of their creativity.","They become angry."],"correct_answer":"They feel proud of their creativity."},{"question":"What does Jaden learn about friendship in this chapter?","options":["It's about winning.","It's not important during tests.","It's about supporting each other.","It's about being serious."],"correct_answer":"It's about supporting each other."},{"question":"What is a major theme in Chapter 5?","options":["The importance of grades","The value of different study methods","The pressure of school","The joy of competition"],"correct_answer":"The value of different study methods"}]},"images":{"chapter_cover":"plot_292_ch5_img1.png","illustrations":["plot_292_ch5_img1.png","plot_292_ch5_img2.png","story_292_11-14_ch5_img1_1751268085.png","story_292_11-14_ch5_img2_1751268103.png"]},"word_count":685,"reading_level":"Builder"}
